/root/.codex/history.jsonl:986:{"session_id":"01a07b3b-c97a-7682-b907-31fc07ece643","ts":1788774875,"text":"Lavora in /opt.\n\nSTEP 3 — PREPARE WORM PRIVATE OTA/DOWNLOAD PATCH\n\nIMPORTANTE:\nQuesto step deve PREPARARE la patch ma NON applicarla alla produzione.\n\nStato confermato dall'audit:\n\n- Web server effettivo: Caddy.\n- Caddy è bindato a 10.90.20.10.\n- /releases/* serve attualmente /opt/Android/releases.\n- Questo espone installer ZIP, firmware ZIP, OTA e metadata.\n- worm.estixari.com serve il Web Installer.\n- worm.coffee.pm è previsto come endpoint privato WORM.\n- updater/config WORM OS punta a:\n    https://worm.coffee.pm/updates/\n- Area privata nuova:\n    /opt/worm/downloads/private/\n- WireGuard admin locale:\n    10.77.0.0/24\n  NON MODIFICARE.\n- Futuro WireGuard produzione worm-os:\n    worm-os 10.60.0.10/32\n        ->\n    OPNsense wg0 10.60.0.1/24\n        ->\n    server privato 10.90.20.10\n\nOBIETTIVO FINALE:\n\nInternet\n   |\n   +--> worm.estixari.com\n   |       Web Installer\n   |       NO ZIP\n   |       NO OTA\n   |       NO firmware\n   |\n   X--> /releases/*\n   X--> OTA pubblici\n\nworm-os\n   |\n   | WireGuard 10.60.0.0/24\n   v\nOPNsense\n   |\n   v\n10.90.20.10\n   |\n   +--> worm.coffee.pm/updates/\n   +--> downloads privati\n   +--> OTA\n   +--> metadata autorizzati\n\n\n1. BACKUP\n\nCrea:\n\n/opt/worm/backups/STEP-03/\n\nSalva copie, preservando path/metadata dove possibile, almeno di:\n\n- /etc/caddy/Caddyfile\n- /opt/Android/web-deploy/worm-installer/js/config.js\n- /opt/Android/web-deploy/worm-installer/scripts/publish-release.sh\n- /opt/Android/worm-os/config/private-endpoints.json\n\nRegistra SHA256 dei file originali.\n\nNON copiare private key o secret dentro /opt/worm.\n\n\n2. PREPARA AREA RELEASE PRIVATA\n\nCrea soltanto la struttura:\n\n/opt/worm/downloads/private/releases/\n/opt/worm/downloads/private/updates/\n/opt/worm/downloads/private/metadata/\n/opt/worm/downloads/staging/\n/opt/worm/downloads/archive/\n\nNON spostare ancora gli artifact di produzione.\nNON cancellare symlink esistenti.\n\n\n3. ANALIZZA CADDY\n\nPrepara una configurazione candidata che:\n\nA. mantenga funzionanti:\n   - worm.estixari.com\n   - autenticazione\n   - dashboard/status\n   - GitLab e gli altri host non correlati\n\nB. sul Web Installer pubblico:\n   - NON esponga /releases/*\n   - NON esponga /updates/*\n   - NON esponga ZIP/IMG/OTA\n\nC. preveda worm.coffee.pm come servizio PRIVATO.\n\nIl servizio privato deve essere raggiungibile solo tramite il percorso autorizzato OPNsense/WireGuard.\n\nNON assumere che il solo hostname renda privato il servizio.\n\nNon applicare ancora Caddyfile.\n\nSalva candidato in:\n\n/opt/worm/patches/STEP-03/Caddyfile.candidate\n\n\n4. DIRECTORY TRAVERSAL CHECK\n\nVerifica specificamente se:\n\nfile_server /opt/Android/releases\n\npuò rendere raggiungibile:\n\n/opt/Android/releases/staging\n\nattraverso URL come:\n\n/releases/staging/\n\nDocumenta risultato.\n\nNon modificare produzione.\n\n\n5. PUBLICATION PIPELINE\n\nPrepara versione candidata di:\n\npublish-release.sh\n\nin cui il default NON sia più:\n\n/var/www/worm-installer/releases\n\nIl nuovo target candidato deve essere:\n\n/opt/worm/downloads/private/releases\n\nNessuna release deve diventare pubblica automaticamente.\n\nNon sostituire ancora lo script originale.\n\n\n6. WEB INSTALLER\n\nAnalizza config.js.\n\nPrepara modifica candidata per eliminare la dipendenza pubblica da:\n\n/releases/frankel/latest.json\n\nIl Web Installer pubblico non deve poter recuperare automaticamente installer ZIP.\n\nIMPORTANTE:\nnon decidere arbitrariamente un nuovo URL pubblico.\n\nSe l'installer deve diventare WireGuard-only, documentalo esplicitamente.\n\n\n7. OTA\n\nMantieni come endpoint logico previsto:\n\nhttps://worm.coffee.pm/updates/\n\nPrepara mapping candidato:\n\n/updates/*\n    ->\n/opt/worm/downloads/private/updates/\n\nma NON attivarlo finché OPNsense/WireGuard 10.60.0.0/24 non è verificato.\n\nVerifica inoltre updater/App Store WORM OS e riferimenti a:\n\nPATCH-WORM-PRIVATE-ENDPOINT-V1\n\nNon applicare patch Android in questo step.\n\n\n8. WIREGUARD\n\nNON modificare:\n\n/etc/wireguard/wg0.conf\n10.77.0.0/24\nwg-quick@wg0\n\nQuello è WireGuard ADMIN.\n\nCerca e documenta solamente la configurazione candidata/legacy per:\n\n10.60.0.10/32 -> OPNsense 10.60.0.1/24 -> 10.90.20.10\n\nNon leggere/stampare private key.\n\nNon applicare configurazioni OPNsense.\n\n\n9. FIREHOL\n\nL'audit ha trovato:\n\nworm-firehol-blocklist-refresh.timer\n\nDato che la strategia prevista è lasciare OPNsense come firewall:\n\n- verifica cosa fa questo timer/service\n- NON disabilitarlo ancora\n- documenta se FireHOL è ancora attivo o se è soltanto rimasto il refresh timer\n- prepara eventuale rimozione/disabilitazione come patch separata\n\nNon mischiare questa modifica con OTA.\n\n\n10. TEST PLAN\n\nCrea test che, DOPO futura applicazione, verifichino:\n\nPUBLIC INTERNET:\n- Web Installer raggiungibile\n- /releases/* NON raggiungibile\n- /updates/* NON raggiungibile\n- installer ZIP NON scaricabile\n- OTA ZIP NON scaricabile\n- firmware ZIP NON scaricabile\n\nWIREGUARD WORM-OS:\n- 10.60.0.10 raggiunge 10.90.20.10\n- worm.coffee.pm risolve/raggiunge endpoint privato\n- /updates/ funziona\n- metadata funziona\n- OTA funziona solo dal percorso autorizzato\n\nADMIN WG:\n- 10.77.0.0/24 resta invariato e funzionante.\n\n\n11. ROLLBACK\n\nCrea:\n\n/opt/worm/patches/STEP-03/rollback.sh\n\nDeve essere preparato ma NON eseguito.\n\nDeve poter ripristinare esclusivamente i file che la futura patch modificherà.\n\n\n12. REPORT\n\nCrea:\n\n/opt/worm/patches/STEP-03/PLAN.md\n/opt/worm/patches/STEP-03/FILES.txt\n/opt/worm/patches/STEP-03/TEST-PLAN.md\n/opt/worm/patches/STEP-03/rollback.sh\n\nAlla fine esegui SOLO controlli read-only e mostra:\n\ncat /opt/worm/patches/STEP-03/PLAN.md\ncat /opt/worm/patches/STEP-03/FILES.txt\ncat /opt/worm/patches/STEP-03/TEST-PLAN.md\n\nNON:\n- reload Caddy\n- restart servizi\n- modificare OPNsense\n- modificare WireGuard\n- modificare firewall\n- spostare release\n- cancellare symlink\n- pubblicare artifact\n- applicare la patch\n\nFERMATI DOPO LA PREPARAZIONE.\nATTENDI APPROVAZIONE PER STEP 4."}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:987:{"session_id":"01a07b52-a5bf-7f21-9f6f-c47f0e9aa97a","ts":1788775413,"text":"Crea in /opt/worm la struttura OTA privata di worm-os.\n\nRequisiti:\n- release iniziale: 1.1.0\n- tutto OTA deve essere privato\n- directory:\n  /opt/worm/ota/releases/1.1.0\n  /opt/worm/ota/private-repo\n  /opt/worm/ota/signatures\n  /opt/worm/app-store\n  /opt/worm/augurri\n  /opt/worm/launcher\n  /opt/worm/updater\n  /opt/worm/fonts-private/PragmataPro\n  /opt/worm/security/signing\n  /opt/worm/security/device-keys\n\nPayload OTA:\n1. AUGURRI icon renderer\n2. PragmataPro come system font\n3. Worm Launcher aggiornato\n4. App Store originale con repository Worm privati e app:\n   - Proton\n   - Bitwarden\n   - AUGURRI-Update\n\nCrea:\n- manifest.json\n- pre-install.sh\n- install.sh\n- post-install.sh\n- rollback.sh\n- ota.conf\n- apps.json\n- repository.json\n- build-release.sh\n\nSicurezza:\n- no anonymous access\n- no public fallback\n- repository non pubblico\n- checksum SHA256\n- predisposizione per firma crittografica obbligatoria\n- permessi restrittivi\n- tutto root:root\n\nbuild-release.sh deve creare:\n /opt/worm/ota/private-repo/packages/worm-os-1.1.0.tar.gz\n e relativo .sha256\n\nNon modificare firewall, WireGuard o OPNsense.\nAlla fine mostrami i file creati con:\nfind /opt/worm/ota -maxdepth 4 -type f | sort"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:988:{"session_id":"01a07b52-a5bf-7f21-9f6f-c47f0e9aa97a","ts":1788776134,"text":"Continua il lavoro OTA in /opt/worm.\n\nImplementa firma e verifica crittografica della OTA 1.1.0.\n\nRequisiti:\n- usa Ed25519\n- genera la signing key privata in:\n  /opt/worm/security/signing/\n- permessi 600 sulla private key\n- esporta separatamente la public key\n- NON inserire mai la private key nel pacchetto OTA\n- firma manifest.json e SHA256SUMS\n- crea manifest.json.sig e SHA256SUMS.sig\n- modifica build-release.sh per firmare automaticamente ogni release\n- crea verify-release.sh\n- verifica PRIMA dell'installazione:\n  1. firma manifest\n  2. firma SHA256SUMS\n  3. checksum di tutti i payload\n- fail closed: qualsiasi errore deve bloccare l'installazione\n- install.sh non deve procedere senza verifica valida\n- mantieni OTA privata\n- non modificare firewall, WireGuard o OPNsense\n\nImportante:\nnon rigenerare automaticamente la signing key se esiste già.\n\nAlla fine esegui build + verifica della 1.1.0 e mostrami:\n- PASS/FAIL verifica\n- file .sig creati\n- percorso public key\n- permessi della private key"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:989:{"session_id":"01a07b52-a5bf-7f21-9f6f-c47f0e9aa97a","ts":1788776381,"text":"Continua worm-os OTA 1.1.0 in /opt/worm.\n\nOra prepara l'integrazione dei payload reali.\n\n1. Individua prima il Worm Launcher attualmente installato.\n2. Individua l'App Store originale attualmente installato e determina\n   quale package manager/repository system utilizza.\n3. NON sostituire l'App Store con uno store nuovo:\n   deve restare quello originale, con branding Worm e repository\n   Worm privati aggiuntivi.\n4. Prepara AUGURRI-Update come voce/app del catalogo.\n5. Prepara Proton e Bitwarden come voci del catalogo usando i\n   meccanismi supportati dall'App Store originale.\n6. Individua dove worm-os configura font di sistema e launcher,\n   ma NON installare ancora PragmataPro.\n7. Non inventare path o package manager: rilevali dal sistema.\n8. Non modificare firewall, WireGuard, OPNsense o networking.\n9. Non modificare ancora il sistema live: prepara tutto dentro\n   /opt/worm/ota/releases/1.1.0/payload/\n\nMantieni firma Ed25519 e verifica fail-closed esistenti.\n\nAlla fine mostrami:\n- App Store originale rilevato\n- package manager rilevato\n- Worm Launcher rilevato\n- path configurazione font\n- file aggiunti al payload\n- eventuali componenti che non hai potuto identificare"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:993:{"session_id":"01a07b52-a5bf-7f21-9f6f-c47f0e9aa97a","ts":1788778633,"text":"Prepara la pubblicazione privata di worm-os OTA 1.1.0.\n\n- usa il pacchetto già verificato:\n  /opt/worm/ota/private-repo/packages/worm-os-1.1.0.tar.gz\n- crea metadata/update manifest per AUGURRI-Update\n- includi versione, SHA256, dimensione, channel private-stable\n- includi riferimento alla firma Ed25519\n- configura endpoint OTA SOLO sulla rete privata Worm/WireGuard\n- nessun endpoint pubblico\n- nessun anonymous access\n- nessun public fallback\n- non esporre mai la signing private key\n- public key separata per verifica client\n- AUGURRI-Update deve fare:\n  check -> download -> verify signature -> verify SHA256 -> install\n- qualsiasi verifica fallita deve bloccare tutto\n- prepara rollback/recovery prima dell'installazione\n\nIMPORTANTE:\nnon installare OTA\nnon riavviare device\nnon modificare OPNsense\nnon modificare WireGuard\nnon aprire porte firewall\n\nAlla fine mostra:\nOTA VERSION\nPACKAGE\nSHA256\nUPDATE MANIFEST\nPRIVATE ENDPOINT\nAUTH MODE\nSIGNATURE VERIFY\nROLLBACK READY\nPUBLIC EXPOSURE\nREADY TO PUBLISH: YES/NO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1001:{"session_id":"01a07b52-a5bf-7f21-9f6f-c47f0e9aa97a","ts":1788780852,"text":"Diagnostica HEALTH FAIL della OTA 1.1.0.\n\nNON cancellare, spostare o modificare nulla.\nSOLO diagnosi read-only.\n\nPROBLEMA 1 — CLIENT PRIVATE KEY FOUND\n\nIdentifica esattamente:\n- path completo della private key trovata\n- hostname/macchina su cui si trova\n- se appartiene al SERVER OTA oppure al DEVICE CLIENT\n- quale processo/utente può leggerla\n\nLa signing key prevista sul SERVER è:\n/opt/worm/security/signing/worm-ota-signing.pem\n\nQuesta è corretta sul server e NON deve essere cancellata.\n\nIl device client deve possedere soltanto la public key necessaria\nalla verifica OTA.\n\nNon considerare la signing key del server come \"client key found\".\n\nPROBLEMA 2 — ROLLBACK 1.0.0 MISSING\n\nCerca read-only:\n- snapshot\n- backup\n- previous_version\n- previous_build\n- rollback metadata\n- rollback directory\n- OTA state/history\n\nControlla in:\n/opt/worm/ota/\n/opt/worm/ota/state/\n/opt/worm/ota/rollback/\n/opt/worm/ota/releases/\n\nVerifica anche perché durante installazione risultava:\nROLLBACK AVAILABLE: YES\n\ne ora:\nROLLBACK 1.0.0: MISSING\n\nNON creare un rollback fittizio.\n\nInfine correggi SOLO la logica dell'health-check se sta\nconfondendo server e client, ma non alterare lo stato OTA.\n\nOutput:\n\nPRIVATE KEY PATH:\nPRIVATE KEY LOCATION: SERVER/CLIENT\nPRIVATE KEY STATUS: SAFE/UNSAFE\n\nCLIENT HAS SIGNING PRIVATE KEY: YES/NO\nCLIENT HAS PUBLIC VERIFY KEY: YES/NO\n\nROLLBACK PREVIOUSLY RECORDED: YES/NO\nROLLBACK PATH:\nROLLBACK CONTENT VALID: YES/NO\nROLLBACK REASON:\n\nSYSTEM CHANGES: NONE\nHEALTH DIAGNOSIS: PASS/FAIL"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1002:{"session_id":"01a07b52-a5bf-7f21-9f6f-c47f0e9aa97a","ts":1788780934,"text":"Ripara la gestione rollback di worm-os OTA senza modificare\nl'installazione 1.1.0 attualmente funzionante.\n\nSituazione:\n- current = 1.1.0 build 1100\n- previous = 1.0.0\n- rollback esistente incompleto\n- signing private key è correttamente SERVER-ONLY\n- client possiede solo public verification key\n\n1. Correggi health-check:\n   - non considerare /opt/worm/security/signing/ del SERVER\n     come materiale client\n   - CLIENT SIGNING PRIVATE KEY deve risultare NO\n   - verifica separatamente server e client\n\n2. Ripara metadata rollback:\n   previous_version=1.0.0\n   previous_build=1000\n\n3. NON inventare file della 1.0.0.\n   Cerca nei source tree, build output, OTA precedenti e backup\n   locali i componenti originali 1.0.0 necessari.\n\n4. Il rollback deve coprire almeno tutti i componenti modificati\n   dalla 1.1.0:\n   - AUGURRI/framework changes\n   - PragmataPro/font configuration\n   - Worm Launcher\n   - App Store\n   - configurazione repository/update\n   - proprietà/versioning Worm\n\n5. Se non è possibile ricostruire esattamente lo stato 1.0.0,\n   NON dichiarare rollback READY.\n   In quel caso crea un report preciso di ciò che manca.\n\n6. Aggiungi per le OTA FUTURE una procedura transazionale:\n   PRE-INSTALL SNAPSHOT\n   -> verify snapshot\n   -> install\n   -> post-install health\n   -> retain rollback\n\n   L'installazione deve essere bloccata se lo snapshot precedente\n   non è completo e verificato.\n\n7. Non fare rollback adesso.\n   Non modificare i componenti funzionanti della 1.1.0.\n   Non riavviare.\n   Non modificare networking/OPNsense/WireGuard/firewall.\n\nAlla fine esegui health-check read-only e mostra:\n\nCURRENT: 1.1.0 build 1100\nCLIENT SIGNING PRIVATE KEY:\nCLIENT PUBLIC VERIFY KEY:\nROLLBACK VERSION:\nROLLBACK BUILD:\nROLLBACK AUGURRI:\nROLLBACK FONTS:\nROLLBACK LAUNCHER:\nROLLBACK APP STORE:\nROLLBACK CONFIG:\nROLLBACK VERIFIED:\nFUTURE SNAPSHOT GUARD:\nHEALTH:"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1016:{"session_id":"01a07b52-a5bf-7f21-9f6f-c47f0e9aa97a","ts":1788790921,"text":"Riorganizza la build GrapheneOS/worm-os sotto /opt/worm.\n\nTarget build tree:\n/opt/worm/build/grapheneos/\n\nUsa:\n- /opt/worm/build/grapheneos/source\n- /opt/worm/build/grapheneos/out\n- /opt/worm/build/grapheneos/prebuilts\n- /opt/worm/build/grapheneos/keys\n\nSe il source GrapheneOS attuale è in /opt/Android/worm-os:\n- NON cancellarlo\n- verifica dimensioni, git state, manifest e symlink\n- sposta o copia in modo sicuro dentro\n  /opt/worm/build/grapheneos/source\n- preferisci rsync preservando permessi, symlink e timestamp\n- verifica il tree dopo il trasferimento\n- non perdere modifiche locali Worm\n\nAggiorna gli script/config Worm affinché usino il nuovo BUILD_ROOT:\n/opt/worm/build/grapheneos/source\n\nMantieni separati:\n- OTA: /opt/worm/ota\n- PragmataPro: /opt/worm/fonts-private\n- security/signing: /opt/worm/security\n- launcher assets: /opt/worm/launcher\n- AUGURRI: /opt/worm/augurri\n\nNON fare ancora build completa.\nNON cancellare /opt/Android/worm-os finché il nuovo tree non è verificato.\n\nAlla fine mostra:\n\nOLD BUILD ROOT:\nNEW BUILD ROOT:\nSOURCE TREE: PASS/FAIL\nGIT STATE PRESERVED: YES/NO\nLOCAL WORM CHANGES PRESERVED: YES/NO\nSYMLINKS: PASS/FAIL\nBUILD CONFIG UPDATED: YES/NO\nOLD TREE REMOVED: NO\nREADY TO BUILD FROM /opt/worm: YES/NO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1017:{"session_id":"01a07b52-a5bf-7f21-9f6f-c47f0e9aa97a","ts":1788791671,"text":"Lavora nella build GrapheneOS/worm-os sotto:\n\n/opt/worm/build/grapheneos/source\n\nOBIETTIVO:\npreparare una build integrata con:\n- Worm Home come launcher predefinito\n- PragmataPro come font di sistema\n- AUGURRI integrato nel framework/system\n- App Store GrapheneOS con le nostre app aggiunte\n\nFASE 1 — AUDIT BUILD\n\nPrima identifica senza modificare:\n- device target\n- product/make target\n- build variant\n- launcher HOME attuale\n- modulo Worm Home\n- App Store source/prebuilt reale\n- font configuration\n- punti di integrazione AUGURRI\n- signing keys usate dalla build\n\nFASE 2 — WORM HOME\n\nIntegra Worm Home nella build:\n- usa package reale esistente\n- verifica intent MAIN/HOME/DEFAULT\n- imposta Worm Home come HOME predefinito\n- mantieni il launcher precedente nel sistema per recovery\n- non disinstallarlo\n\nFASE 3 — PRAGMATAPRO\n\nUsa i font reali presenti in:\n/opt/worm/fonts-private/PragmataPro\n\nIntegra nella build Android:\n- font system\n- fontconfig/fallback\n- conserva emoji\n- conserva fallback Unicode\n- nessun font pubblico\n\nFASE 4 — AUGURRI\n\nIntegra AUGURRI direttamente nel framework/system:\n- usa solo codice reale già presente nel progetto\n- niente patch runtime\n- niente placeholder\n- verifica che venga compilato nei moduli corretti\n\nFASE 5 — APP STORE\n\nMantieni:\napp.grapheneos.apps\n\nMantieni tutte le app GrapheneOS originali.\n\nAggiungi al catalogo realmente consumato dal client:\n- Worm Home\n- Proton\n- Bitwarden\n\nLe nostre app devono:\n- apparire nella stessa lista GrapheneOS\n- essere scrollabili normalmente con swipe up\n- essere aggiornabili\n- avere APK reali\n- versionCode/versionName reali\n- SHA256\n- firma APK valida\n\nNon creare secondo App Store.\nNon creare seconda UI.\nNon usare metadata che il client non legge.\n\nFASE 6 — BUILD TEST\n\nCompila prima solo i moduli interessati:\n- Worm Home\n- App Store\n- framework necessario AUGURRI\n- font/system config\n\nNon fare ancora full system build se i moduli falliscono.\n\nVerifica:\n- compile PASS\n- package names\n- signatures\n- HOME default\n- catalog parser reale\n- Worm Home visibile\n- Proton visibile\n- Bitwarden visibile\n\nNON creare ancora OTA.\nNON installare sul device.\nNON modificare rete, OPNsense, WireGuard o firewall.\n\nOUTPUT:\n\nBUILD ROOT:\nDEVICE TARGET:\nBUILD TARGET:\nCURRENT HOME:\nWORM HOME:\nDEFAULT HOME:\nPRAGMATAPRO:\nAUGURRI:\nAPP STORE:\nGRAPHENEOS APPS PRESERVED:\nWORM HOME CATALOG:\nPROTON CATALOG:\nBITWARDEN CATALOG:\nMODULE BUILD:\nREADY FOR FULL SYSTEM BUILD: YES/NO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1018:{"session_id":"01a07b52-a5bf-7f21-9f6f-c47f0e9aa97a","ts":1788793015,"text":"Migra l'intero ambiente di build GrapheneOS/Worm sotto /opt/worm.\n\nSOURCE PRINCIPALE ATTUALE:\n/opt/Android/grapheneos-frankel-17/\n\nTARGET:\n/opt/worm/build/grapheneos-frankel-17/\n\nPrima fai AUDIT COMPLETO di /opt/Android e individua TUTTE le directory\nnecessarie per compilare correttamente grapheneos-frankel-17.\n\nCerca e identifica almeno:\n- source tree GrapheneOS\n- repo metadata/.repo\n- local manifests\n- prebuilts\n- toolchains\n- clang\n- rust\n- java/jdk\n- build-tools\n- platform-tools\n- vendor trees\n- device trees\n- kernel trees\n- signing keys\n- AVB keys\n- release keys\n- app signing keys\n- ccache\n- build cache\n- out directories utili\n- scripts custom Worm\n- patch locali\n- AUGURRI sources\n- Worm Home sources\n- App Store sources\n- private font references\n- eventuali symlink verso /opt/Android\n\nIMPORTANTE:\n- non inventare directory\n- rileva quelle realmente usate dalla build\n- preserva git state\n- preserva .repo\n- preserva symlink\n- preserva permessi e timestamp\n- preserva file hidden\n- preserva modifiche locali non committate\n- NON cancellare nulla da /opt/Android in questa fase\n\nUsa rsync sicuro, ad esempio con:\n-aHAX --numeric-ids\ne gestisci correttamente symlink/hardlink se presenti.\n\nTarget organizzazione:\n\n/opt/worm/build/\n  grapheneos-frankel-17/\n  prebuilts/\n  toolchains/\n  cache/\n  ccache/\n  out/\n  keys/\n  scripts/\n\nLe chiavi PRIVATE devono restare in:\n  /opt/worm/security/\noppure\n  /opt/worm/build/keys/\ncon permessi restrittivi.\n\nPragmataPro deve restare in:\n  /opt/worm/fonts-private/PragmataPro/\n\nAggiorna eventuali script/config che contengono path assoluti\n/opt/Android/... affinché usino /opt/worm/...\n\nDopo la copia esegui VALIDAZIONE:\n\n1. confronta dimensione/file count source e target\n2. verifica .repo\n3. verifica git status nei repo modificati\n4. verifica local manifests\n5. verifica symlink rotti\n6. cerca riferimenti residui a /opt/Android\n7. verifica toolchain disponibili\n8. verifica signing keys\n9. verifica ccache\n10. esegui solo environment/setup build test:\n    source build/envsetup.sh\n    lunch del target corretto\n    ma NON lanciare ancora una full build\n\nNON cancellare:\n/opt/Android/grapheneos-frankel-17/\nné altre directory originali.\n\nAlla fine mostra:\n\nMAIN SOURCE OLD:\nMAIN SOURCE NEW:\nEXTRA BUILD DIRECTORIES FOUND:\nFILES COPIED:\nSIZE OLD:\nSIZE NEW:\n.REPO: PASS/FAIL\nLOCAL MANIFESTS: PASS/FAIL\nGIT STATE: PASS/FAIL\nLOCAL CHANGES PRESERVED: YES/NO\nSYMLINKS: PASS/FAIL\nTOOLCHAINS: PASS/FAIL\nSIGNING KEYS: PASS/FAIL\nCCACHE: PASS/FAIL\nRESIDUAL /opt/Android REFERENCES:\nENVSETUP: PASS/FAIL\nLUNCH: PASS/FAIL\nREADY TO BUILD FROM /opt/worm: YES/NO\nOLD TREE REMOVED: NO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1019:{"session_id":"01a07b52-a5bf-7f21-9f6f-c47f0e9aa97a","ts":1788794466,"text":"Completa la migrazione GrapheneOS rendendo /opt/worm autosufficiente.\n\nSITUAZIONE ATTUALE:\nOLD:\n/opt/Android/grapheneos-frankel-17/\n\nNEW:\n/opt/worm/build/grapheneos-frankel-17/\n\nProblemi rimasti:\n- SIGNING KEYS: FAIL\n- alcuni symlink intenzionali puntano ancora a /opt/Android\n- old size ~264G\n- new size ~3.8G\n\nOBIETTIVO:\nla build deve poter funzionare anche se /opt/Android non fosse montato.\n\n1. AUDIT SYMLINK\nTrova TUTTI i symlink sotto:\n/opt/worm/build/grapheneos-frankel-17\n\nche puntano a:\n/opt/Android\n\nPer ogni symlink:\n- identifica la directory/file reale\n- copia nel nuovo tree il target necessario\n- sostituisci il symlink con path interno /opt/worm\n  oppure con symlink relativo interno al nuovo tree\n\nNon lasciare dipendenze runtime/build verso /opt/Android.\n\n2. SIGNING KEYS\n\nIndividua tutte le chiavi realmente richieste dalla build:\n- platform\n- release\n- media\n- shared\n- networkstack\n- AVB\n- OTA\n- App Store\n- Worm Home\n- eventuali altre chiavi product/device\n\nNON stampare private key o secret.\n\nCopia/sposta in modo sicuro sotto:\n/opt/worm/security/android-signing/\n\noppure usa riferimenti sicuri da:\n/opt/worm/security/\n\nPermessi:\n- directory private 700\n- private keys 600\n- public cert secondo necessità\n\nAggiorna i riferimenti della build al nuovo path.\n\n3. OUT / CACHE / PREBUILTS\n\nDetermina quali directory grandi sotto /opt/Android sono\nnecessarie realmente:\n- out\n- prebuilts\n- toolchains\n- cache\n- ccache\n- vendor\n- kernel\n- device\n- external\n- hardware\n\nMigra ciò che serve nella struttura /opt/worm.\n\nNon duplicare inutilmente file se possono essere ricreati,\nma la build deve essere autonoma.\n\n4. VALIDAZIONE AUTONOMA\n\nEsegui un test simulando assenza del vecchio tree:\nNON cancellare /opt/Android.\n\nVerifica che nessun file necessario venga risolto da /opt/Android.\n\nEsegui:\n- source build/envsetup.sh\n- lunch target corretto\n- build di un piccolo modulo\n- verifica signing configuration\n\nNon fare ancora full build.\n\n5. NON cancellare /opt/Android.\n\nOUTPUT:\n\nEXTERNAL SYMLINKS BEFORE:\nEXTERNAL SYMLINKS AFTER:\nRESIDUAL /opt/Android DEPENDENCIES:\nSIGNING KEYS: PASS/FAIL\nAVB KEYS: PASS/FAIL\nOTA SIGNING: PASS/FAIL\nAPP STORE SIGNING: PASS/FAIL\nWORM HOME SIGNING: PASS/FAIL\nPREBUILTS: PASS/FAIL\nTOOLCHAINS: PASS/FAIL\nENVSETUP: PASS/FAIL\nLUNCH: PASS/FAIL\nTEST MODULE BUILD: PASS/FAIL\nSELF-CONTAINED /opt/worm: YES/NO\nSAFE TO ARCHIVE /opt/Android: YES/NO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1020:{"session_id":"01a07b52-a5bf-7f21-9f6f-c47f0e9aa97a","ts":1788795433,"text":"Il tree /opt/worm è autonomo nei path, ma NON è ancora build-complete.\n\nTEST MODULE BUILD fallisce con module types Soong mancanti:\n- aidl_interface\n- aidl_interface_defaults\n- hidl_package_root\n\nNON archiviare ancora /opt/Android.\n\nSOURCE OLD:\n/opt/Android/grapheneos-frankel-17/\n\nSOURCE NEW:\n/opt/worm/build/grapheneos-frankel-17/\n\nObiettivo:\nrendere NEW un mirror completo dei SORGENTI necessari alla build\nGrapheneOS, senza copiare inutilmente output/cache generati.\n\n1. Confronta OLD vs NEW usando .repo manifest/projects.\n\nTrova tutti i progetti AOSP/GrapheneOS mancanti nel NEW.\n\nControlla in particolare i provider Soong per:\n- aidl_interface\n- aidl_interface_defaults\n- hidl_package_root\n\ne relative dipendenze build.\n\nNon aggiungere workaround o definizioni finte.\n\n2. Completa il source tree dal OLD al NEW.\n\nCopia tutti i repository sorgente mancanti mantenendo:\n- .repo\n- git metadata\n- local changes\n- symlink\n- permissions\n- timestamps\n\nPreferisci un mirror completo del source tree.\n\nPuoi ESCLUDERE soltanto directory generate/ricreabili come:\n- out/\n- cache temporanee\n- .cache se non necessaria\n- log\n- artefatti build ricreabili\n\nNON escludere:\n- build/\n- system/\n- system/tools/\n- packages/\n- frameworks/\n- hardware/\n- external/\n- device/\n- vendor/\n- kernel/\n- prebuilts/\n- tools/\n- development/\n- trusty/\n- CTS/platform_testing se referenziati\n- qualunque progetto presente nel manifest\n\n3. Dopo la copia:\n\n- verifica che tutti i project path del repo manifest esistano\n- verifica Android.bp / Android.mk necessari\n- verifica Soong plugin/module type registration\n- verifica che non esistano symlink verso /opt/Android\n- verifica signing keys sotto /opt/worm\n\n4. Esegui dalla NUOVA root:\n\nsource build/envsetup.sh\nlunch frankel-cur-userdebug\n\nPoi build test progressivo:\n- un modulo semplice\n- Worm Home\n- App Store\n- un modulo framework che usa AIDL\n\nSe un test fallisce, diagnostica e correggi il SOURCE TREE.\nNon creare shim/fake module types.\n\nNON eseguire ancora full build.\nNON cancellare /opt/Android.\n\nOutput:\n\nMANIFEST PROJECTS OLD:\nMANIFEST PROJECTS NEW:\nMISSING PROJECTS BEFORE:\nMISSING PROJECTS AFTER:\nAIDL SOONG PROVIDER: PASS/FAIL\nHIDL SOONG PROVIDER: PASS/FAIL\nSOONG BOOTSTRAP: PASS/FAIL\nENVSETUP: PASS/FAIL\nLUNCH: PASS/FAIL\nSIMPLE MODULE: PASS/FAIL\nWORM HOME MODULE: PASS/FAIL\nAPP STORE MODULE: PASS/FAIL\nFRAMEWORK/AIDL MODULE: PASS/FAIL\nRESIDUAL /opt/Android DEPENDENCIES:\nBUILD-COMPLETE /opt/worm: YES/NO\nSAFE TO ARCHIVE /opt/Android: YES/NO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1021:{"session_id":"01a07b52-a5bf-7f21-9f6f-c47f0e9aa97a","ts":1788796770,"text":"Il tree /opt/worm è autonomo nei path, ma NON è ancora build-complete.\n\nTEST MODULE BUILD fallisce con module types Soong mancanti:\n- aidl_interface\n- aidl_interface_defaults\n- hidl_package_root\n\nNON archiviare ancora /opt/Android.\n\nSOURCE OLD:\n/opt/Android/grapheneos-frankel-17/\n\nSOURCE NEW:\n/opt/worm/build/grapheneos-frankel-17/\n\nObiettivo:\nrendere NEW un mirror completo dei SORGENTI necessari alla build\nGrapheneOS, senza copiare inutilmente output/cache generati.\n\n1. Confronta OLD vs NEW usando .repo manifest/projects.\n\nTrova tutti i progetti AOSP/GrapheneOS mancanti nel NEW.\n\nControlla in particolare i provider Soong per:\n- aidl_interface\n- aidl_interface_defaults\n- hidl_package_root\n\ne relative dipendenze build.\n\nNon aggiungere workaround o definizioni finte.\n\n2. Completa il source tree dal OLD al NEW.\n\nCopia tutti i repository sorgente mancanti mantenendo:\n- .repo\n- git metadata\n- local changes\n- symlink\n- permissions\n- timestamps\n\nPreferisci un mirror completo del source tree.\n\nPuoi ESCLUDERE soltanto directory generate/ricreabili come:\n- out/\n- cache temporanee\n- .cache se non necessaria\n- log\n- artefatti build ricreabili\n\nNON escludere:\n- build/\n- system/\n- system/tools/\n- packages/\n- frameworks/\n- hardware/\n- external/\n- device/\n- vendor/\n- kernel/\n- prebuilts/\n- tools/\n- development/\n- trusty/\n- CTS/platform_testing se referenziati\n- qualunque progetto presente nel manifest\n\n3. Dopo la copia:\n\n- verifica che tutti i project path del repo manifest esistano\n- verifica Android.bp / Android.mk necessari\n- verifica Soong plugin/module type registration\n- verifica che non esistano symlink verso /opt/Android\n- verifica signing keys sotto /opt/worm\n\n4. Esegui dalla NUOVA root:\n\nsource build/envsetup.sh\nlunch frankel-cur-userdebug\n\nPoi build test progressivo:\n- un modulo semplice\n- Worm Home\n- App Store\n- un modulo framework che usa AIDL\n\nSe un test fallisce, diagnostica e correggi il SOURCE TREE.\nNon creare shim/fake module types.\n\nNON eseguire ancora full build.\nNON cancellare /opt/Android.\n\nOutput:\n\nMANIFEST PROJECTS OLD:\nMANIFEST PROJECTS NEW:\nMISSING PROJECTS BEFORE:\nMISSING PROJECTS AFTER:\nAIDL SOONG PROVIDER: PASS/FAIL\nHIDL SOONG PROVIDER: PASS/FAIL\nSOONG BOOTSTRAP: PASS/FAIL\nENVSETUP: PASS/FAIL\nLUNCH: PASS/FAIL\nSIMPLE MODULE: PASS/FAIL\nWORM HOME MODULE: PASS/FAIL\nAPP STORE MODULE: PASS/FAIL\nFRAMEWORK/AIDL MODULE: PASS/FAIL\nRESIDUAL /opt/Android DEPENDENCIES:\nBUILD-COMPLETE /opt/worm: YES/NO\nSAFE TO ARCHIVE /opt/Android: YES/NO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1022:{"session_id":"01a07b52-a5bf-7f21-9f6f-c47f0e9aa97a","ts":1788799565,"text":"Crea il changelog/timeline pubblico di worm-os confrontando\nGrapheneOS originale con le nostre patch Worm.\n\nROOT:\n /opt/worm/build/grapheneos-frankel-17\n\nOBIETTIVO WEB:\n worm.estixari.com\n\nUI desiderata:\n\nTIMELINE\n│\n├── [data/versione]  TITOLO MODIFICA\n│                    [OPEN]\n│\n│   OPEN =>\n│   mostra changelog completo\n│\n├── [data/versione]  TITOLO MODIFICA\n│                    [OPEN]\n│\n└── ...\n\nFASE 1 — GIT AUDIT\n\nPer ogni repository modificato della build:\n\n- identifica remote/upstream GrapheneOS originale\n- identifica commit/base originale\n- identifica commit/modifiche Worm\n- usa git status, git log e git diff\n- includi anche patch locali non committate\n- NON modificare i repository\n\nConfronta almeno:\n- frameworks/base\n- frameworks/libs/systemui\n- packages/modules/Permission\n- App Store\n- Worm Home / launcher\n- system\n- vendor/worm\n- device/product config\n- font configuration\n- tutti gli altri repository che risultano modificati\n\nPer ogni modifica genera:\n\n- id\n- data\n- versione worm-os\n- build\n- titolo breve\n- componente\n- repository\n- upstream GrapheneOS commit\n- Worm commit, se presente\n- file modificati\n- summary\n- changelog dettagliato\n- tipo:\n  added\n  changed\n  fixed\n  security\n  removed\n- eventuale patch ID, ad esempio\n  PATCH-UPDATE-003\n\nNON pubblicare:\n- private keys\n- signing material\n- token\n- password\n- secret\n- contenuto PragmataPro\n- path sensibili non necessari\n\nFASE 2 — TIMELINE DATA\n\nGenera una sorgente dati strutturata:\n\n/opt/worm/changelog/timeline.json\n\nOrdine:\npiù recente -> più vecchio\n\nEsempio logico:\n\n{\n  \"version\": \"1.1.1\",\n  \"build\": 1110,\n  \"date\": \"...\",\n  \"title\": \"AUGURRI Icon Renderer\",\n  \"component\": \"SystemUI\",\n  \"type\": \"changed\",\n  \"summary\": \"...\",\n  \"changes\": [...],\n  \"upstream\": {...},\n  \"worm\": {...}\n}\n\nFASE 3 — WEBSITE\n\nIntegra la timeline nel sito:\n\nworm.estixari.com\n\nCrea pagina:\n /changelog\n\nDesign coerente con Worm.\n\nOgni elemento timeline deve mostrare inizialmente:\n\nDATA\nVERSIONE\nTITOLO\nOPEN\n\nPremendo OPEN:\n- espandi inline oppure modal\n- mostra changelog\n- summary\n- componente\n- file/moduli coinvolti\n- versione/build\n- upstream GrapheneOS\n- modifiche Worm\n\nNon mostrare diff sorgente completo.\nMostra una descrizione leggibile del cambiamento.\n\nSupporta:\n- mobile\n- desktop\n- dark/light theme se già presente nel sito\n- deep link per ogni entry, ad esempio:\n  /changelog#augurri-icon-renderer\n\nFASE 4 — VERSIONI\n\nRicostruisci anche la timeline storica disponibile dai git/patch:\n\n- 1.0.0 build 1000\n- 1.1.0 build 1100\n- 1.1.1 build 1110 se già presente nel tree\n\nNon inventare modifiche non dimostrabili dal git o dalle patch.\nSe una data/versione non è ricostruibile, marcala come unknown\nanziché inventarla.\n\nFASE 5 — AUTOMAZIONE\n\nCrea script:\n\n/opt/worm/tools/generate-changelog.sh\n\nLo script deve:\n- rieseguire audit git\n- rigenerare timeline.json\n- aggiornare la pagina changelog\n- non pubblicare secrets\n- essere idempotente\n\nSe il sito ha già un framework/build/deploy system,\nintegrati con quello esistente.\nNON creare un secondo sito parallelo.\n\nPrima di deploy:\n- valida JSON\n- build web\n- controlla link\n- controlla mobile\n- scansione secrets\n\nPoi pubblica su worm.estixari.com/changelog\nsolo se i test passano.\n\nOUTPUT FINALE:\n\nREPOSITORIES AUDITED:\nMODIFIED REPOSITORIES:\nPATCHES FOUND:\nTIMELINE ENTRIES:\nVERSIONS FOUND:\nCHANGELOG JSON:\nWEB PAGE:\nMOBILE TEST:\nSECRET SCAN:\nDEPLOY:\nURL:"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1024:{"session_id":"01a07b52-a5bf-7f21-9f6f-c47f0e9aa97a","ts":1788802425,"text":"Configura l’architettura Worm con separazione CONTROL / DISTRIBUTION.\n\nDOMINI:\n\n1. worm.estixari.com = CONTROL PLANE\n2. worm.coffee.pm   = DISTRIBUTION PLANE\n\nOBIETTIVO:\n\nworm.estixari.com deve ospitare:\n- dashboard Worm\n- timeline/changelog\n- stato infrastruttura\n- footer:\n  worm OS <=> OPNsense  ●\n- glyph verde/rosso in base a WireGuard + reachability OPNsense\n- nessun payload OTA\n- nessun APK\n- nessuna signing private key\n\nworm.coffee.pm deve ospitare:\n- API Worm\n- OTA private\n- distribuzione app Worm\n- metadata App Store\n- mirror/failover Hetzner\n- auth device\n- update check\n- download OTA\n- download APK\n\nSTRUTTURA SUGGERITA:\n\n/opt/worm/\n├── control/\n│   ├── dashboard/\n│   ├── changelog/\n│   └── api-status/\n│\n├── distribution/\n│   ├── api/\n│   ├── ota/\n│   ├── apps/\n│   ├── metadata/\n│   └── mirror/\n│\n├── build/\n│   └── grapheneos-frankel-17/\n│\n├── security/\n├── fonts-private/\n└── tools/\n\nCONTROL PLANE:\n\nworm.estixari.com\n\nIntegra:\n- /dashboard\n- /changelog\n- /api/status/network\n\n/api/status/network deve controllare SOLO read-only:\n- interfaccia WireGuard reale\n- handshake recente\n- route verso OPNsense\n- reachability OPNsense\n\nJSON esempio:\n\n{\n  \"status\": \"operational\",\n  \"wireguard\": true,\n  \"opnsense\": true,\n  \"interface\": \"...\",\n  \"last_check\": \"...\"\n}\n\nFooter:\n\nworm OS <=> OPNsense   ●\n\n● verde = tutto PASS\n● rosso = qualsiasi controllo FAIL\n\nNon esporre:\n- private key\n- peer secret\n- token\n- config WireGuard completa\n\nDISTRIBUTION PLANE:\n\nworm.coffee.pm\n\nEndpoint:\n\n/updates/\n  OTA private worm-os\n\n/apps/\n  APK Worm aggiornabili\n\n/apps/metadata.1.0.sjson\n  metadata consumabili dall’App Store Worm/GrapheneOS patchato\n\n/api/\n  device auth\n  update check\n  app metadata\n  health interno\n\nOTA:\n- auth obbligatoria\n- SHA256\n- Ed25519\n- private signing key SERVER ONLY\n- no anonymous access\n- no public fallback\n- no directory listing\n\nAPP DISTRIBUTION:\n- Worm Home\n- Proton\n- Bitwarden\n- future Worm apps\n- APK reali\n- versionCode/versionName\n- SHA256\n- firma APK verificata\n- metadata firmati\n\nMIRROR HETZNER:\n\nPrepara worm.coffee.pm per mirror/failover via Hetzner API.\n\nPrima fai audit read-only:\n- server Worm\n- robot\n- Primary IP\n- Floating IP\n- private network\n- firewall associations\n- location\n- volumes/snapshots\n\nNON spostare IP adesso.\n\nSe robot usa Floating IP:\n- prepara procedura di failover API\n- NON eseguirla\n\nSe robot usa Primary IP:\n- non tentare reassignment\n- prevedi IP pubblico dedicato al mirror\n\nDNS:\n\nworm.estixari.com\n-> control node\n\nworm.coffee.pm\n-> distribution/mirror node\n\nNon modificare DNS finché health-check non passa.\n\nSICUREZZA:\n\n- separa secrets CONTROL e DISTRIBUTION\n- signing private keys solo su distribution/server signing\n- nessuna private key nel frontend\n- permessi restrittivi\n- secret scan prima del deploy\n\nNON modificare:\n- OPNsense\n- WireGuard config\n- firewall rules\n- routing\n- IP assignment\nfinché non è terminato l’audit.\n\nAlla fine mostra:\n\nCONTROL ROOT:\nDISTRIBUTION ROOT:\n\nCONTROL DOMAIN:\nDISTRIBUTION DOMAIN:\n\nDASHBOARD:\nCHANGELOG:\nNETWORK STATUS API:\nWIREGUARD STATUS:\nOPNSENSE STATUS:\n\nOTA ENDPOINT:\nAPP ENDPOINT:\nAPP METADATA:\nDEVICE AUTH:\n\nHETZNER AUDIT:\nROBOT IP TYPE:\nMIRROR READY:\n\nPRIVATE KEYS EXPOSED: YES/NO\nPUBLIC ACCESS OTA: YES/NO\nPUBLIC ACCESS APPS: YES/NO\n\nCONTROL PLANE: PASS/FAIL\nDISTRIBUTION PLANE: PASS/FAIL\nREADY FOR DEPLOY: YES/NO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1026:{"session_id":"01a07774-da5a-7751-beb8-16e2ba629dff","ts":1788803383,"text":"Crea e applica una patch dedicata:\n\nPATCH-INFRA-004-opnsense-hetzner-audit\n\nROOT:\n/opt/worm\n\nSCOPO:\n1. correggere il rilevamento stato OPNsense\n2. completare audit Hetzner\n3. NON modificare configurazione infrastrutturale\n\n==================================================\nA. OPNsense HEALTH CHECK\n==================================================\n\nStato attuale:\nWIREGUARD STATUS: PASS\nOPNSENSE STATUS: FAIL\n\nEsegui audit READ-ONLY.\n\nRileva automaticamente:\n- interfaccia WireGuard reale\n- peer associato a OPNsense\n- ultimo handshake\n- route verso OPNsense\n- IP privato OPNsense\n- AllowedIPs effettivi\n\nNon assumere wg0 o IP hardcoded.\n\nDetermina perché OPNsense risulta FAIL.\n\nNon usare solamente ping/ICMP:\nOPNsense può bloccare ICMP.\n\nImplementa health-check a livelli:\n\n1. WireGuard interface UP\n2. peer configurato\n3. handshake recente\n4. route valida\n5. reachability OPNsense con check read-only sicuro\n\nSe ICMP è bloccato ma il percorso VPN è verificabile tramite\nun servizio/endpoint già esistente, considera quello.\n\nNON:\n- modificare OPNsense\n- aggiungere firewall rule\n- cambiare WireGuard\n- cambiare route\n- riavviare servizi di rete\n\nAggiorna:\n/opt/worm/control/api-status/\n\ne l'endpoint:\n/api/status/network\n\nFormato:\n\n{\n  \"status\": \"operational|offline\",\n  \"wireguard\": true,\n  \"opnsense\": true,\n  \"interface\": \"...\",\n  \"handshake\": \"...\",\n  \"last_check\": \"...\"\n}\n\nNon esporre:\n- IP pubblici completi se non necessari\n- private keys\n- preshared keys\n- peer secrets\n- token\n\nFooter dashboard/About/Changelog:\n\nworm OS <=> OPNsense  ●\n\nverde = operational\nrosso = offline\n\n==================================================\nB. HETZNER API AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nUsa la configurazione/API Hetzner già presente.\n\nREAD-ONLY.\n\nNON stampare token.\n\nRileva:\n\nSERVERS\n- robot\n- worm / distribution\n- server ID\n- status\n- location/datacenter\n\nNETWORK\n- private networks\n- private IP\n- subnet\n- association server/network\n\nPUBLIC IP\nPer robot determina:\n- IPv4\n- IPv6\n- Primary IP\n- Floating IP\n- server assignment\n\nMaschera gli IP nell'output umano.\n\nDetermina:\n\nROBOT IP TYPE:\nPRIMARY / FLOATING / UNKNOWN\n\nROBOT IP REASSIGNABLE:\nYES / NO\n\nFIREWALL\n- firewall associati\n- NON modificare rules\n\nSTORAGE\n- volumes\n- snapshots/images utili per mirror\n\n==================================================\nC. MIRROR PLAN\n==================================================\n\nNON creare ancora il mirror.\nNON spostare IP.\n\nSe robot IP = FLOATING:\nprepara solamente il piano API per failover.\n\nSe robot IP = PRIMARY:\nnon tentare reassignment.\nSegnala che il mirror necessita IP pubblico dedicato.\n\nworm.coffee.pm deve restare:\nDISTRIBUTION PLANE\n- OTA\n- Apps\n- API\n- future mirror/failover\n\nworm.estixari.com:\nCONTROL PLANE\n- dashboard\n- changelog\n- About\n- status\n\n==================================================\nD. PATCH ARTIFACT\n==================================================\n\nSalva documentazione e script della patch in:\n\n/opt/worm/patches/PATCH-INFRA-004-opnsense-hetzner-audit/\n\nCrea:\nREADME.md\naudit.sh\nverify.sh\nrevert.sh\n\nrevert.sh deve ripristinare SOLO eventuali modifiche al codice\nhealth-check/dashboard, non modificare infrastruttura.\n\nRegistra la patch nel changelog/timeline Worm.\n\nEsegui secret scan.\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nPATCH: PASS/FAIL\n\nWIREGUARD INTERFACE:\nWIREGUARD HANDSHAKE:\nOPNSENSE:\nOPNSENSE ROOT CAUSE:\nSTATUS API:\nFOOTER GLYPH:\n\nHETZNER API:\nROBOT:\nROBOT IP TYPE:\nROBOT IP REASSIGNABLE:\nPRIVATE NETWORK:\nFIREWALL AUDIT:\nSNAPSHOT/MIRROR SOURCE:\n\nMIRROR STRATEGY:\nINFRASTRUCTURE CHANGES: NONE\nSECRET SCAN:\nVERIFY:\nREADY FOR MIRROR STEP: YES/NO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1028:{"session_id":"01a07774-da5a-7751-beb8-16e2ba629dff","ts":1788804376,"text":"Finalizza PATCH-INFRA-004 e consolida il Control Plane sotto /opt/worm.\n\nSTATO:\n- PATCH-INFRA-004: PASS\n- OPNsense: PASS\n- /api/status/network: operational\n- Hetzner API: PASS\n- robot non presente nella Hetzner Cloud API interrogata\n- robot IP reassignment: NON consentito/non dimostrato\n- mirror step: non ancora pronto\n\n1. CONTROL PLANE PATH\n\nAudit:\n  /opt/Android/dashboard\n\nConfrontalo con:\n  /opt/worm/control/\n\nMigra sotto /opt/worm/control/ tutto ciò che serve realmente\na worm.estixari.com.\n\nDopo la migrazione:\n- nessun componente runtime del Control Plane deve dipendere da\n  /opt/Android/dashboard\n- preserva git history e modifiche Worm\n- NON cancellare ancora /opt/Android/dashboard\n\nAggiorna PATCH-INFRA-004 e gli script al path definitivo /opt/worm.\n\n2. ABOUT\n\nIntegra definitivamente:\n  WORM Network Architecture\n\nnella pagina:\n  worm.estixari.com/about\n\nCrea un asset path stabile, ad esempio:\n  /opt/worm/control/dashboard/public/assets/about/worm-network-architecture.png\n\nSe il file immagine non è disponibile localmente, crea esattamente\nquesto target e segnala COPY REQUIRED.\nNON ridisegnare l'immagine.\n\nUI:\n- responsive\n- aspect ratio originale\n- desktop large/full container\n- mobile width 100%\n- tap/click per visualizzazione grande\n\n3. FOOTER STATUS\n\nUsa esclusivamente:\n/api/status/network\n\nVisualizzazione:\n\nworm OS <=> OPNsense   ●\n\n● verde quando status=operational\n● rosso altrimenti\n\nNon mostrare IP nel footer.\n\n4. HETZNER\n\nRegistra il risultato dell'audit:\n\n- Hetzner API: PASS\n- worm-opnsense: presente\n- worm-private: presente\n- robot: non presente nella Cloud API interrogata\n- robot IP type: UNKNOWN\n- robot IP reassignment: NO\n\nNON tentare reassignment.\nNON creare mirror in questo passaggio.\n\n5. CHANGELOG\n\nAggiungi PATCH-INFRA-004 alla timeline/changelog:\n- OPNsense health-check corretto\n- HTTPS private-path health probe\n- Hetzner read-only audit\n- nessuna modifica firewall/networking\n\n6. VERIFY\n\nNon modificare:\n- OPNsense\n- WireGuard\n- firewall\n- routing\n- OTA\n- GrapheneOS build\n\nOutput:\n\nCONTROL ROOT:\nOLD DASHBOARD DEPENDENCY:\nABOUT IMAGE:\nABOUT PAGE:\nSTATUS API:\nFOOTER:\nFOOTER CURRENT STATE:\nPATCH-INFRA-004:\nCHANGELOG:\nHETZNER AUDIT:\nROBOT IP REASSIGNMENT:\nSECRET SCAN:\nREADY TO DEPLOY CONTROL PLANE:"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1040:{"session_id":"01a07d56-5707-7863-8688-12303e9def71","ts":1788811792,"text":"CODEX — APP STORE GENERATOR FIX\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nFix the broken worm OS app-repository generator path so the\napp-store mirror/rebuild workflow completes cleanly.\n\nCURRENT STATE\n\nAPP STORE UPDATE: PASS\nRELEASE VALIDATION: PASS\nNO-GMS: PASS\n\nKnown remaining issue:\n\nrebuild-worm-app-repo.sh generator path is broken.\n\nDO NOT modify the already-valid catalog contents unless required\nto fix generator consistency.\n\nDO NOT remove any currently integrated app.\n\nPRESERVE:\n\n- Proton VPN\n- Proton Mail\n- Proton Drive\n- Bitwarden\n- Signal\n- Firefox\n- Mullvad VPN\n- Thunderbird\n- VLC\n- Aegis\n\n==================================================\n1. REPRODUCE THE FAILURE\n==================================================\n\nRun the existing app-repository generator/rebuild command.\n\nCapture the exact failure.\n\nReport:\n\nSCRIPT\nFAILING LINE\nCURRENT PATH\nEXPECTED PATH\nMISSING FILE/DIRECTORY\nCALLER\n\nDo not guess the path.\n\n==================================================\n2. TRACE PATH RESOLUTION\n==================================================\n\nInspect:\n\nworm-os/scripts/rebuild-worm-app-repo.sh\n\nand every helper it invokes.\n\nDetermine whether paths are:\n\n- absolute\n- relative to current working directory\n- relative to script directory\n- relative to repository root\n\nIdentify the root cause.\n\n==================================================\n3. FIX ROBUSTLY\n==================================================\n\nPrefer script-directory/repository-root based path resolution.\n\nThe script must work regardless of the shell's current working\ndirectory.\n\nUse a robust pattern equivalent to:\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=<resolved directory of this script>\nREPO_ROOT=<resolved worm OS repository root>\n\nThen derive all paths from those variables.\n\nDo not hardcode machine-specific paths such as:\n\n/opt/worm/...\n/home/...\n/mnt/...\n\nunless the existing architecture explicitly requires them.\n\n==================================================\n4. PRESERVE SECURITY / SIGNING\n==================================================\n\nDo not change:\n\n- repository signing keys\n- signing algorithms\n- APK signatures\n- certificate pins\n- release verification policy\n- hash validation\n\nThe task is path/generator repair only.\n\n==================================================\n5. RUN FULL APP-REPO REBUILD\n==================================================\n\nAfter repair, run the actual generator.\n\nVerify generation of:\n\ncatalog metadata\nrepository metadata\nsignatures\nAPK sidecar metadata\nmirror/repository outputs\n\n==================================================\n6. VERIFY RELEASE 1.1.1\n==================================================\n\nRun existing validation:\n\nbuild-release.sh 1.1.1\nverify-release.sh 1.1.1\n\nBoth must pass.\n\nIf the generator rewrites deterministic metadata, ensure the\noutput is valid and expected.\n\n==================================================\n7. VERIFY APP CATALOG\n\nConfirm catalog still contains exactly the intended current\nentries.\n\nExplicitly verify:\n\nProton VPN\nProton Mail\nProton Drive\nBitwarden\nSignal\nFirefox\nMullvad VPN\nThunderbird\nVLC\nAegis\n\nNo Google Play Services package may appear.\n\n==================================================\n8. PORTABILITY TEST\n==================================================\n\nRun the rebuild script from at least:\n\n- repository root\n- another working directory\n\nThe generator must resolve its own paths correctly in both cases.\n\n==================================================\n9. OUTPUT\n\nAPP STORE GENERATOR FIX\n\nROOT CAUSE:\n...\n\nCHANGED FILES:\n...\n\nGENERATOR:\nPASS / FAIL\n\nBUILD RELEASE 1.1.1:\nPASS / FAIL\n\nVERIFY RELEASE 1.1.1:\nPASS / FAIL\n\nCATALOG:\nPASS / FAIL\n\nNO-GMS:\nPASS / FAIL\n\nPORTABILITY:\nPASS / FAIL\n\nFINAL STATUS:\nPASS / BLOCKED\n\nIf PASS, this closes the App Store maintenance checkpoint.\n\nDo not start another unrelated feature automatically.\nSTOP."}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1055:{"session_id":"01a07774-da5a-7751-beb8-16e2ba629dff","ts":1788885262,"text":"RESTRUCTURE WORM-OS PROJECT UNDER /opt/worm\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nMake /opt/worm the single canonical root for the entire WormOS project,\nincluding Android source, build outputs, patches, scripts, artifacts,\nprovenance and caches.\n\nDo NOT create or use /opt/Android anymore.\n\n============================================================\n1. CREATE DIRECTORY LAYOUT\n============================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android\n\n/opt/worm/build/out\n/opt/worm/build/target-files\n/opt/worm/build/ota\n/opt/worm/build/logs\n/opt/worm/build/tmp\n\n/opt/worm/patches/base\n/opt/worm/patches/material3\n/opt/worm/patches/app-store\n/opt/worm/patches/wireguard\n/opt/worm/patches/ota\n\n/opt/worm/vendor/wireguard\n\n/opt/worm/manifests/grapheneos\n/opt/worm/manifests/wormos\n\n/opt/worm/config/build\n/opt/worm/config/product\n/opt/worm/config/selinux\n/opt/worm/config/network\n\n/opt/worm/scripts/build\n/opt/worm/scripts/ota\n/opt/worm/scripts/storage\n/opt/worm/scripts/validation\n/opt/worm/scripts/maintenance\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/releases\n/opt/worm/artifacts/target-files\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports\n/opt/worm/artifacts/provenance\n\n/opt/worm/cache/repo\n/opt/worm/cache/ccache\n/opt/worm/cache/downloads\n\n/opt/worm/backup/metadata\n\n/opt/worm/docs\n\n============================================================\n2. DEFINE CANONICAL PATHS\n============================================================\n\nCanonical project paths:\n\nWORM_ROOT=/opt/worm\nANDROID_BUILD_TOP=/opt/worm/src/android\nOUT_DIR=/opt/worm/build/out\nTMPDIR=/opt/worm/build/tmp\nCCACHE_DIR=/opt/worm/cache/ccache\n\nDo not use /opt/Android.\n\nCreate a reusable environment file:\n\n/opt/worm/config/build/env.sh\n\ncontaining the canonical environment variables.\n\nDo not put secrets in env.sh.\n\n============================================================\n3. ORGANIZE EXISTING /opt/worm CONTENT\n============================================================\n\nAudit existing files under /opt/worm.\n\nMove only when safe and obvious:\n\nexisting patches\n    -> /opt/worm/patches/\n\nbuild scripts\n    -> /opt/worm/scripts/build/\n\nOTA scripts\n    -> /opt/worm/scripts/ota/\n\nStorage Box scripts\n    -> /opt/worm/scripts/storage/\n\nvalidation scripts\n    -> /opt/worm/scripts/validation/\n\nreports\n    -> /opt/worm/artifacts/reports/\n\nsource provenance\n    -> /opt/worm/artifacts/provenance/\n\nmanifests\n    -> /opt/worm/manifests/\n\nDo not silently move ambiguous files.\n\nFor ambiguous files, leave them in place and report them.\n\n============================================================\n4. STORAGE BOX POLICY\n============================================================\n\nThe previous Android project stored on Storage Box is an archive/reference.\n\nDo not use the Storage Box Android tree as the live build workspace.\n\nStorage Box may contain:\n\n- historical source backup\n- release artifacts\n- target-files archives\n- OTA archives\n- project backups\n\nLive builds must run locally under:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android\n/opt/worm/build\n\n============================================================\n5. ANDROID SOURCE LOCATION\n============================================================\n\nThe next clean GrapheneOS checkout must be created at:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android\n\nnot /opt/Android.\n\nKeep source separate from generated outputs by using:\n\nOUT_DIR=/opt/worm/build/out\n\nDo not place generated Android out/ directly inside the source tree unless\nthe Android build absolutely requires it.\n\n============================================================\n6. BUILD WRAPPER\n============================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/worm/scripts/build/worm-build.sh\n\nIt must:\n\n- source /opt/worm/config/build/env.sh\n- verify /opt/worm/src/android exists\n- verify free disk space\n- initialize the Android build environment\n- accept build targets as arguments\n- write logs under /opt/worm/build/logs\n- fail cleanly on errors\n\nDo not hardcode secrets.\n\n============================================================\n7. CLEANUP WRAPPER\n============================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/worm/scripts/maintenance/worm-clean.sh\n\nSupport safe cleanup modes:\n\nlogs\ntmp\nout\nota\ntarget-files\ncache\n\nNever delete:\n\n/opt/worm/src\n/opt/worm/patches\n/opt/worm/vendor\n/opt/worm/manifests\n/opt/worm/config\n/opt/worm/artifacts/provenance\n/opt/worm/scripts\n\nunless explicitly requested.\n\n============================================================\n8. STORAGE STATUS WRAPPER\n============================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/worm/scripts/maintenance/worm-disk.sh\n\nReport:\n\n- filesystem usage\n- /opt/worm/src size\n- /opt/worm/build size\n- /opt/worm/cache size\n- /opt/worm/artifacts size\n- largest directories\n- inode usage\n\n============================================================\n9. DOCUMENT STRUCTURE\n============================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/worm/docs/FILESYSTEM-LAYOUT.md\n\nDocument:\n\n/opt/worm/src         = source\n/opt/worm/build       = disposable build workspace\n/opt/worm/patches     = persistent WormOS patches\n/opt/worm/vendor      = pinned third-party source\n/opt/worm/config      = non-secret configuration\n/opt/worm/scripts     = project tooling\n/opt/worm/artifacts   = persistent outputs/reports\n/opt/worm/cache       = disposable caches\n/opt/worm/manifests   = source revision metadata\n\n============================================================\n10. DO NOT BUILD YET\n============================================================\n\nFor this task, do not start a GrapheneOS repo sync or full build.\n\nFirst establish and validate the filesystem/project structure.\n\nFINAL REPORT:\n\nWORM_ROOT=\nANDROID_BUILD_TOP=\nOUT_DIR=\nSTRUCTURE_CREATED=\nENV_FILE=\nBUILD_WRAPPER=\nCLEAN_WRAPPER=\nDISK_WRAPPER=\nFILESYSTEM_DOC=\nFILES_MOVED=\nAMBIGUOUS_FILES=\nOLD_OPT_ANDROID_REFERENCES=\nREADY_FOR_ANDROID_CHECKOUT="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1056:{"session_id":"01a07774-da5a-7751-beb8-16e2ba629dff","ts":1788885852,"text":"RESUME WORM-OS SOURCE STATE WITHOUT BUILD OR OTA\n\nCURRENT GOAL:\n\nReconstruct the previously accepted WormOS source state under /opt/worm.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\n- DO NOT build Android.\n- DO NOT build target-files.\n- DO NOT generate OTA.\n- DO NOT flash devices.\n- DO NOT modify OPNsense or server/network infrastructure.\n- DO NOT change the already-approved WireGuard architecture.\n- DO NOT introduce new features.\n- DO NOT redesign existing accepted patches.\n\nThis task is SOURCE RECONSTRUCTION ONLY.\n\nCanonical paths:\n\nWORM_ROOT=/opt/worm\nANDROID_SOURCE=/opt/worm/src/android\nPATCH_ROOT=/opt/worm/patches\nARTIFACT_ROOT=/opt/worm/artifacts\nVENDOR_ROOT=/opt/worm/vendor\n\n============================================================\n1. RESTORE BASE AND PRODUCT STATE\n============================================================\n\nRestore the previously accepted WormOS base/product changes.\n\nIdentify the exact patches or source modifications from:\n\n- /opt/worm persistent state\n- accepted patch artifacts\n- old Android backup on Storage Box, read-only if needed\n\nDo not restore generated build output.\n\nReport:\n\nWORMOS_BASE_PRODUCT=RESTORED|MISSING|PARTIAL\n\n============================================================\n2. MATERIAL 3 CHECKPOINT\n============================================================\n\nRestore the previously accepted Material 3 integration checkpoint.\n\nDo not extend or redesign Material 3.\n\nOnly restore the accepted state.\n\nReport:\n\nMATERIAL3=RESTORED|MISSING|PARTIAL\n\n============================================================\n3. WORMOS APP STORE\n============================================================\n\nRestore the accepted WormOS App Store modifications.\n\nInclude accepted app additions where previously present:\n\n- Proton\n- Bitwarden\n- Proton Drive\n\nDo not add new applications during this task.\n\nReport:\n\nAPP_STORE=RESTORED|MISSING|PARTIAL\nPROTON=RESTORED|NOT_PRESENT\nBITWARDEN=RESTORED|NOT_PRESENT\nPROTON_DRIVE=RESTORED|NOT_PRESENT\n\n============================================================\n4. WORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD\n============================================================\n\nRestore the accepted privileged/system-owned WormSystemWireGuard component.\n\nRequired architecture remains:\n\nAndroid VPN / lockdown\n        |\nWormSystemWireGuard\n        |\nVpnService TUN\n        |\nofficial WireGuard Android backend\n        |\nsource-built wireguard-go\n        |\nOPNsense peer\n\nDo not revert to the abandoned deep kernel/framework integration design.\n\nReport:\n\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD=RESTORED|MISSING|PARTIAL\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS|FAIL\n\n============================================================\n5. OFFICIAL WIREGUARD ANDROID BACKEND\n============================================================\n\nRestore the previously selected official WireGuard Android tunnel/backend\nintegration.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- source only\n- no user-facing WireGuard app dependency\n- no opaque binaries\n- no runtime download\n- no moving/unpinned upstream revision\n\nReport:\n\nWG_ANDROID_BACKEND=RESTORED|MISSING|PARTIAL\n\n============================================================\n6. SOURCE-BUILT WIREGUARD-GO\n============================================================\n\nRestore the source integration required to build wireguard-go.\n\nDo not build it in this task.\n\nVerify only that:\n\n- source is present\n- build files are present\n- integration references are present\n\nReport:\n\nWIREGUARD_GO_SOURCE=RESTORED|MISSING|PARTIAL\nWIREGUARD_GO_BUILD_INTEGRATION=RESTORED|MISSING|PARTIAL\n\n============================================================\n7. BACKEND PROVENANCE\n============================================================\n\nRestore and verify the exact previously pinned upstream backend provenance.\n\nRecover:\n\nUPSTREAM_REPOSITORY=\nUPSTREAM_COMMIT=\nUPSTREAM_COMMIT_DATE=\nLICENSE=\nPROVENANCE_FILE=\n\nDo not substitute HEAD/latest.\n\nIf exact upstream commit cannot be recovered, mark:\n\nBACKEND_PINNED=FAIL\n\nand STOP before modifying the backend source.\n\nReport:\n\nBACKEND_PROVENANCE=PASS|FAIL\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS|FAIL\n\n============================================================\n8. SELINUX\n============================================================\n\nRestore the previously accepted SELinux policy changes required by:\n\n- WormSystemWireGuard\n- WireGuard backend\n- related privileged integration\n\nDo not broaden policies.\n\nDo not add permissive rules.\n\nDo not bypass neverallow.\n\nThis task only restores source policy files; it does not compile policy.\n\nReport:\n\nSELINUX_SOURCE_CHANGES=RESTORED|MISSING|PARTIAL\n\n============================================================\n9. FAIL-CLOSED DESIGN / CONFIGURATION\n============================================================\n\nRestore the accepted fail-closed configuration/design artifacts.\n\nInclude source/configuration covering:\n\n- IPv4 protection\n- IPv6 protection\n- boot-time protection\n- Wi-Fi/cellular handover\n- backend crash behavior\n- peer unreachable behavior\n- DNS protection\n- private-route protection\n- prevention of ordinary app UID fallback to physical uplink\n\nDo not claim runtime validation.\n\nReport:\n\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE_DESIGN=RESTORED|MISSING|PARTIAL\nFAIL_CLOSED_RUNTIME=NOT_TESTED\n\n============================================================\n10. OLD STORAGE BOX BACKUP\n============================================================\n\nThe old /opt/Android backup on Storage Box may be used only as a read-only\nreference to recover accepted SOURCE files or patch artifacts that are\nmissing locally.\n\nRules:\n\n- do not restore old build output\n- do not restore old out/\n- do not restore old target-files\n- do not restore old OTA files\n- do not overwrite the backup\n- document every file recovered from it\n\nReport:\n\nFILES_RECOVERED_FROM_STORAGEBOX=\n\n============================================================\n11. SOURCE-ONLY VALIDATION\n============================================================\n\nPerform source/static validation only.\n\nAllowed:\n\n- file presence checks\n- git diff/status\n- patch applicability checks\n- provenance verification\n- manifest/revision verification\n- grep/static inspection\n- Android.bp / AndroidManifest.xml inspection\n- SELinux source inspection\n- secret scan\n- dependency/source audit\n\nNOT ALLOWED:\n\n- m\n- mm\n- mmm\n- ninja\n- target-files-package\n- OTA generation\n- emulator/device flashing\n\n============================================================\n12. ORGANIZE PERSISTENT STATE\n============================================================\n\nEnsure reconstructed persistent artifacts are organized under:\n\n/opt/worm/patches/base\n/opt/worm/patches/material3\n/opt/worm/patches/app-store\n/opt/worm/patches/wireguard\n/opt/worm/config\n/opt/worm/vendor/wireguard\n/opt/worm/artifacts/provenance\n/opt/worm/docs\n\nDo not move Android upstream source out of:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android\n\n============================================================\nFINAL REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWORMOS_BASE_PRODUCT=\nMATERIAL3=\nAPP_STORE=\nPROTON=\nBITWARDEN=\nPROTON_DRIVE=\n\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD=\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=\nWG_ANDROID_BACKEND=\nWIREGUARD_GO_SOURCE=\nWIREGUARD_GO_BUILD_INTEGRATION=\n\nBACKEND_PROVENANCE=\nBACKEND_PINNED=\nUPSTREAM_REPOSITORY=\nUPSTREAM_COMMIT=\nUPSTREAM_COMMIT_DATE=\nLICENSE=\nPROVENANCE_FILE=\n\nSELINUX_SOURCE_CHANGES=\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE_DESIGN=\nFAIL_CLOSED_RUNTIME=NOT_TESTED\n\nNO_SECRETS=\nFILES_RECOVERED_FROM_STORAGEBOX=\nFILES_CHANGED=\nMISSING_ARTIFACTS=\nBLOCKERS=\n\nSOURCE_STATE_READY=\nBUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN\nOTA_READY=NO\n\nSOURCE_STATE_READY=PASS only if every accepted source-side WormOS component\nlisted above has been restored or positively verified."}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1058:{"session_id":"01a07774-da5a-7751-beb8-16e2ba629dff","ts":1788887520,"text":"CREATE WORMOS IMPLEMENTATION CHECKPOINT TAG\n\nCurrent verified source state:\n\nSOURCE_STATE_READY=PASS\nBUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN\nBLOCKERS=None\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nThis task is GIT CHECKPOINT ONLY.\n\nDo NOT:\n- build\n- generate OTA\n- modify source implementation\n- add Bitwarden\n- add Proton Drive\n- change WireGuard\n- change Material 3\n- modify server/network infrastructure\n\n============================================================\n1. INSPECT CANONICAL GIT STATE\n============================================================\n\nWork from:\n\n/opt/worm\n\nIdentify the canonical WormOS Git repository and remote.\n\nVerify the remote belongs to the configured git.worm infrastructure.\n\nReport:\n\nGIT_ROOT=\nGIT_REMOTE=\nGIT_BRANCH=\nGIT_HEAD=\nGIT_STATUS=\n\nDo not change the remote.\n\n============================================================\n2. VERIFY CHECKPOINT CONTENT\n============================================================\n\nConfirm the checkpoint contains the recovered persistent state for:\n\n- WormOS base/product\n- Material 3\n- WormOS App Store\n- Proton\n- WormSystemWireGuard\n- official WireGuard Android backend\n- wireguard-go source/build integration\n- backend provenance\n- SELinux source changes\n- fail-closed source/design\n\nBitwarden and Proton Drive are explicitly NOT part of this checkpoint.\n\nDo not add generated build artifacts.\n\nEnsure .gitignore excludes at minimum appropriate generated content under:\n\n/opt/worm/build/\n/opt/worm/cache/\n\nand other disposable Android build outputs.\n\nDo not accidentally ignore persistent source, patches, manifests,\nprovenance or documentation.\n\n============================================================\n3. SECRET SCAN\n============================================================\n\nRun the existing WormOS secret scan over everything that will be committed.\n\nMust remain:\n\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nIf a genuine secret is detected:\n\nSTOP\n\nDo not commit.\nDo not push.\n\n============================================================\n4. CREATE CHECKPOINT COMMIT\n============================================================\n\nStage only the persistent reconstructed project/source state.\n\nCreate a commit with message:\n\nWormOS: recover pre-build WireGuard backend source state\n\nReport:\n\nCHECKPOINT_COMMIT=\n\n============================================================\n5. CREATE ANNOTATED IMPLEMENTATION TAG\n============================================================\n\nCreate exactly:\n\nwormos-prebuild-wg-backend-recovered\n\nas an ANNOTATED Git tag pointing to CHECKPOINT_COMMIT.\n\nTag message:\n\nWormOS pre-build WireGuard backend recovered checkpoint.\n\nRecovered and verified source state:\n- WormOS base/product\n- Material 3\n- WormOS App Store\n- Proton\n- system-owned WormSystemWireGuard\n- official WireGuard Android backend\n- source-built wireguard-go integration\n- pinned backend provenance\n- SELinux source changes\n- fail-closed source/design\n\nBitwarden and Proton Drive are not part of this checkpoint.\nBuild not run.\nOTA not generated.\nRuntime tests not performed.\n\nVerify:\n\ngit rev-parse wormos-prebuild-wg-backend-recovered^{commit}\n\nmust equal CHECKPOINT_COMMIT.\n\n============================================================\n6. PUSH CHECKPOINT\n============================================================\n\nPush the checkpoint commit using the existing safe WormOS branch strategy.\n\nPush the tag:\n\nwormos-prebuild-wg-backend-recovered\n\nDo NOT force push.\n\nDo NOT move/replace an existing tag.\n\nIf that tag already exists remotely, compare its target first.\n\nIf it already points to the exact checkpoint:\nTAG_PUSH=ALREADY_PRESENT_VALID\n\nIf it points somewhere else:\nSTOP\nTAG_CONFLICT=YES\n\nNever overwrite it.\n\n============================================================\n7. ESTABLISH PER-IMPLEMENTATION TAG POLICY\n============================================================\n\nCreate/update:\n\n/opt/worm/docs/GIT-TAG-POLICY.md\n\nPolicy:\n\nEvery accepted WormOS implementation gets its own immutable annotated tag.\n\nFormat:\n\nwormos-<implementation>\n\nor, where state matters:\n\nwormos-<implementation>-<state>\n\nExamples:\n\nwormos-base-product\nwormos-material3\nwormos-appstore\nwormos-appstore-bitwarden\nwormos-appstore-proton-drive\nwormos-system-wg\nwormos-wg-backend\nwormos-wg-failclosed\nwormos-prebuild-wg-backend-recovered\n\nRules:\n\n- annotated tags only\n- one accepted implementation/checkpoint per tag\n- never move an existing published tag\n- never force-update a tag\n- secret scan before tagging\n- tag exact verified commit\n- build status documented separately from source status\n\nDo NOT create the example tags retroactively in this task.\n\nOnly create:\n\nwormos-prebuild-wg-backend-recovered\n\n============================================================\nFINAL REPORT\n============================================================\n\nGIT_ROOT=\nGIT_REMOTE=\nGIT_BRANCH=\nCHECKPOINT_COMMIT=\n\nNO_SECRETS=\n\nIMPLEMENTATION_TAG=wormos-prebuild-wg-backend-recovered\nTAG_TYPE=\nTAG_TARGET=\nTAG_VERIFIED=\nTAG_PUSH=\nTAG_CONFLICT=\n\nDEFAULT_BRANCH_CHANGED=\nTAG_POLICY_CREATED=\n\nBUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN\nSOURCE_STATE_READY=PASS"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1059:{"session_id":"01a0824b-e5a1-7ed2-aacc-5eca7ff7c874","ts":1788892413,"text":"START WORMOS WIREGUARD-ONLY OTA CHECKPOINT\n\nGOAL:\n\nCreate a dedicated implementation checkpoint, tag, build and OTA containing\nONLY the accepted WireGuard-related WormOS implementation.\n\nBefore doing anything else, audit the entire:\n\n/opt/worm/*\n\nDo NOT build before the audit is complete.\n\nCanonical project root:\n\n/opt/worm\n\nExisting frozen checkpoint:\n\nwormos-prebuild-wg-backend-recovered\n\n============================================================\nPHASE 1 — FULL /opt/worm AUDIT\n============================================================\n\nInspect the complete directory tree under:\n\n/opt/worm/*\n\nincluding hidden files where relevant.\n\nAt minimum inspect and classify:\n\n/opt/worm/src\n/opt/worm/build\n/opt/worm/patches\n/opt/worm/vendor\n/opt/worm/manifests\n/opt/worm/config\n/opt/worm/scripts\n/opt/worm/artifacts\n/opt/worm/cache\n/opt/worm/backups\n/opt/worm/backup\n/opt/worm/worm-os\n/opt/worm/wireguard\n/opt/worm/app-store\n/opt/worm/ota\n/opt/worm/control\n/opt/worm/security\n/opt/worm/distribution\n/opt/worm/changelog\n/opt/worm/launcher\n/opt/worm/gradle\n/opt/worm/tools\n/opt/worm/updater\n/opt/worm/web-installer\n/opt/worm/augurri*\n/opt/worm/opnsense\n/opt/worm/worm-robot\n\nAlso inspect any other top-level directory not explicitly listed above.\n\nFor every top-level directory classify it as:\n\nWIREGUARD_REQUIRED\nWORMOS_BASE_REQUIRED\nUNRELATED_TO_WIREGUARD\nBUILD_ARTIFACT\nCACHE\nBACKUP\nSECURITY_SENSITIVE\nUNKNOWN\n\nProduce:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WIREGUARD-OTA-DIRECTORY-AUDIT.md\n\nThe audit must include:\n\nPATH=\nSIZE=\nTYPE=\nGIT_REPOSITORY=\nWIREGUARD_RELEVANCE=\nKEEP_FOR_BUILD=\nEXCLUDE_FROM_WG_CHECKPOINT=\nNOTES=\n\nDo not delete anything during this phase.\n\n============================================================\nPHASE 2 — GIT INVENTORY\n============================================================\n\nFind every Git repository under /opt/worm.\n\nDo not confuse Android repo-tool internals with WormOS repositories.\n\nFor each real project repository report:\n\nPATH=\nREMOTE=\nBRANCH=\nHEAD=\nDIRTY=\nRELEVANCE_TO_WIREGUARD=\n\nAt minimum inspect:\n\n/opt/worm/worm-os\n\nand the Android source repositories containing recovered WireGuard changes.\n\nVerify existing frozen tag:\n\nwormos-prebuild-wg-backend-recovered\n\nRecord its exact commit.\n\nDo not move or modify that tag.\n\n============================================================\nPHASE 3 — IDENTIFY EXACT WIREGUARD CHANGESET\n============================================================\n\nDetermine precisely which source files belong to the accepted WireGuard\nimplementation.\n\nExpected accepted WireGuard scope includes:\n\n- WormSystemWireGuard privileged/system component\n- Android VpnService integration\n- official WireGuard Android tunnel backend integration\n- source-built wireguard-go integration\n- exact pinned upstream source/provenance\n- WireGuard-related Android.bp / product packaging changes\n- required product makefile changes\n- WireGuard-specific SELinux changes\n- fail-closed source/configuration\n- protected DNS integration related to WireGuard\n- boot/autostart integration related to WireGuard\n- runtime/device validation scripts related to WireGuard\n- WireGuard implementation documentation/provenance\n\nRecover exact previously pinned upstream data:\n\nUPSTREAM_REPOSITORY=\nUPSTREAM_COMMIT=\nUPSTREAM_COMMIT_DATE=\nLICENSE=\n\nDo NOT include unrelated new application changes.\n\n============================================================\nPHASE 4 — EXCLUDE UNRELATED IMPLEMENTATIONS\n============================================================\n\nThe dedicated WireGuard checkpoint/OTA must NOT accidentally introduce new\nwork unrelated to WireGuard.\n\nIn particular:\n\n- do not add Bitwarden\n- do not add Proton Drive\n- do not add new App Store entries\n- do not expand Material 3\n- do not modify launcher features\n- do not modify Augurri\n- do not modify installer functionality\n- do not modify dashboard/control functionality\n- do not modify OPNsense\n- do not modify robot networking\n- do not add unrelated OTA features\n\nExisting WormOS base/product state that is required to boot the system may\nremain, but this checkpoint must introduce only the WireGuard implementation\nrelative to the accepted base.\n\nReport all unrelated differences detected before proceeding.\n\nIf unrelated uncommitted changes exist:\n\nSTOP before tagging/building.\n\n============================================================\nPHASE 5 — CREATE DEDICATED GIT BRANCH\n============================================================\n\nCreate a dedicated branch from the correct accepted base/checkpoint.\n\nPreferred:\n\npatch/PATCH-WIREGUARD-OTA\n\nDo not modify the existing frozen recovery tag.\n\nDo not force push.\n\nEnsure the branch contains the exact accepted WireGuard source state.\n\n============================================================\nPHASE 6 — SOURCE-ONLY VALIDATION\n============================================================\n\nBefore commit/build run:\n\n- source presence validation\n- Android.bp validation\n- product packaging validation\n- manifest validation\n- WireGuard backend provenance validation\n- exact pinned commit validation\n- SELinux source inspection\n- fail-closed source inspection\n- secret scan\n- dependency audit\n\nMust satisfy:\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nUPSTREAM_SOURCE_VERIFIED=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nDo not claim runtime PASS yet.\n\n============================================================\nPHASE 7 — CREATE IMPLEMENTATION COMMIT\n============================================================\n\nCommit only the WireGuard implementation checkpoint.\n\nSuggested commit message:\n\nWormOS: system WireGuard backend and fail-closed integration\n\nDo not include:\n\n- caches\n- build output\n- target-files\n- OTA packages\n- temporary files\n- unrelated application changes\n- secrets\n- signing private material\n\n============================================================\nPHASE 8 — CREATE WIREGUARD IMPLEMENTATION TAG\n============================================================\n\nCreate a new annotated tag:\n\nwormos-wg-backend-failclosed\n\nTag message:\n\nWormOS system WireGuard backend and fail-closed implementation checkpoint.\n\nIncludes:\n- privileged WormSystemWireGuard\n- Android VPN/lockdown integration\n- official pinned WireGuard Android backend\n- source-built wireguard-go integration\n- WireGuard SELinux integration\n- protected DNS/fail-closed source state\n- backend provenance\n\nThis tag represents the source implementation before the dedicated\nWireGuard OTA validation.\n\nDo not move this tag once published.\n\nVerify:\n\nTAG_TARGET == IMPLEMENTATION_COMMIT\n\n============================================================\nPHASE 9 — STORAGE CHECK\n============================================================\n\nBefore any build, inspect:\n\ndf -h\ndf -i\n\nand storage consumption under:\n\n/opt/worm/src\n/opt/worm/build\n/opt/worm/cache\n/opt/worm/artifacts\n\nDo not start the build unless enough space exists for:\n\n- Android build intermediates\n- target-files-package\n- OTA generation\n- temporary packaging overhead\n\nReport:\n\nSPACE_AVAILABLE=\nESTIMATED_REQUIRED=\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=\n\nIf BUILD_SPACE_OK=NO:\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\nPHASE 10 — CLEAN WIREGUARD BUILD\n============================================================\n\nUse canonical paths under /opt/worm.\n\nExpected:\n\nWORM_ROOT=/opt/worm\nANDROID_BUILD_TOP=/opt/worm/src/android\nOUT_DIR=/opt/worm/build/out\nTMPDIR=/opt/worm/build/tmp\n\nDo not recreate /opt/Android.\n\nBuild in this order:\n\n1. source-built wireguard-go backend\n2. WormSystemWireGuard\n3. affected product/system components\n4. target-files-package\n\nVerify actual output contains:\n\nWormSystemWireGuard.apk\nlibwg-go.so\nrequired WireGuard backend/runtime components\nWireGuard-related SELinux policy\nrequired product configuration\n\nDo not reuse old build PASS results.\n\n============================================================\nPHASE 11 — BUILD VALIDATION\n============================================================\n\nRun:\n\n- target-files inspection\n- backend source-build verification\n- provenance verification\n- license/NOTICE audit\n- dependency audit\n- secret scan\n- SELinux validation\n- packaging validation\n\nRequired source/build statuses:\n\nSOURCE_IMPLEMENTATION=PASS\nBUILD=PASS\nSELINUX=PASS\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND=PASS\nBACKEND_SOURCE_BUILD=PASS\nBACKEND_PACKAGED=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\n============================================================\nPHASE 12 — DEDICATED WIREGUARD OTA\n============================================================\n\nOnly after target-files-package succeeds, generate a dedicated WormOS OTA.\n\nThe OTA must correspond exactly to:\n\nwormos-wg-backend-failclosed\n\nRecord:\n\nSOURCE_COMMIT=\nSOURCE_TAG=\nTARGET_FILES=\nOTA_FILE=\nOTA_SHA256=\nBUILD_TIMESTAMP=\n\nStore persistent outputs under:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/target-files/\n/opt/worm/artifacts/releases/\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/\n/opt/worm/artifacts/provenance/\n\nDo not store final release artifacts only inside disposable build/out.\n\n============================================================\nPHASE 13 — OTA TAG\n============================================================\n\nAfter a successful OTA package is generated and verified, create a second\nannotated tag:\n\nwormos-wg-backend-failclosed-ota-built\n\nThis tag must point to the SAME source commit as:\n\nwormos-wg-backend-failclosed\n\nThe distinction is metadata/state:\n\nwormos-wg-backend-failclosed\n    = source implementation checkpoint\n\nwormos-wg-backend-failclosed-ota-built\n    = OTA successfully built from that exact source checkpoint\n\nDo not mark runtime/device validation as complete.\n\n============================================================\nPHASE 14 — DEVICE VALIDATION REMAINS SEPARATE\n============================================================\n\nOTA_READY FOR FLASH may be reported after successful package/build validation.\n\nBut security/runtime PASS requires actual physical-device testing for:\n\nAUTO_START\nWG_RUNTIME\nFAIL_CLOSED_IPV4\nFAIL_CLOSED_IPV6\nFAIL_CLOSED_BOOT\nFAIL_CLOSED_HANDOVER\nFAIL_CLOSED_BACKEND_CRASH\nFAIL_CLOSED_PEER_UNREACHABLE\nPROTECTED_DNS\nPRIVATE_ACCESS\nPUBLIC_IPV4\n\nUntil flashed/tested:\n\nDEVICE_RUNTIME_VALIDATION=NOT_RUN\n\nDo not create a runtime-pass tag yet.\n\nFuture tag after actual device validation:\n\nwormos-wg-backend-failclosed-runtime-pass\n\n============================================================\nINFRASTRUCTURE FREEZE\n============================================================\n\nDo NOT modify:\n\n- OPNsense\n- server WireGuard configuration\n- public IP configuration\n- firewall infrastructure\n- external DNS infrastructure\n\nSERVER_NETWORK=FROZEN_UNCHANGED\n\n============================================================\nFINAL REPORT\n============================================================\n\nDIRECTORY_AUDIT=\nGIT_REPOSITORIES_FOUND=\nUNRELATED_CHANGES_FOUND=\n\nBASE_COMMIT=\nIMPLEMENTATION_BRANCH=\nIMPLEMENTATION_COMMIT=\nIMPLEMENTATION_TAG=wormos-wg-backend-failclosed\nIMPLEMENTATION_TAG_TARGET=\n\nSOURCE_IMPLEMENTATION=\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=\nWG_BACKEND=\nBACKEND_SOURCE_BUILD=\nBACKEND_PACKAGED=\nBACKEND_PINNED=\nUPSTREAM_SOURCE_VERIFIED=\nSELINUX=\nNO_SECRETS=\n\nSPACE_AVAILABLE=\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=\n\nBUILD=\nTARGET_FILES=\nOTA_BUILD=\nOTA_FILE=\nOTA_SHA256=\n\nOTA_BUILD_TAG=wormos-wg-backend-failclosed-ota-built\nOTA_BUILD_TAG_TARGET=\n\nDEVICE_RUNTIME_VALIDATION=NOT_RUN\nSERVER_NETWORK=FROZEN_UNCHANGED\n\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1062:{"session_id":"01a0824b-e5a1-7ed2-aacc-5eca7ff7c874","ts":1788893166,"text":"RESUME WORMOS WIREGUARD-ONLY OTA\n\nThe full /opt/worm audit has completed.\n\nAuthoritative reports:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WIREGUARD-OTA-DIRECTORY-AUDIT.md\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WIREGUARD-OTA-BLOCKERS.md\n\nKnown blockers:\n\n1. Unrelated dirty work exists in Android projects and separate WormOS repos.\n2. /opt/worm/build currently consumes approximately 106G.\n3. Approximately 134G filesystem free space remains.\n\nUSER DECISION:\n\nPRESERVE ALL UNRELATED DIRTY WORK.\n\nDo NOT discard, reset, clean, stash, commit, or modify unrelated dirty work.\n\nWe will create an isolated WireGuard-only source/build state.\n\n============================================================\n1. PRESERVE CURRENT STATE\n============================================================\n\nTreat all existing unrelated dirty repositories as READ-ONLY for this task.\n\nDo not run:\n\ngit reset\ngit clean\ngit stash\ngit checkout -- .\ngit restore .\n\nagainst existing dirty work.\n\nDo not modify:\n\n/opt/worm/changelog\n/opt/worm/control/dashboard\n\nor unrelated dirty Android projects.\n\nRecord their current HEAD/status for provenance only.\n\n============================================================\n2. USE FROZEN WIREGUARD CHECKPOINT\n============================================================\n\nCanonical frozen checkpoint:\n\nwormos-prebuild-wg-backend-recovered\n\nCommit:\n\nf947156d418667ec6c9c654250b00f5aa32eb382\n\nUse this checkpoint as the authoritative WormOS WireGuard source state.\n\nDo not move or rewrite this tag.\n\n============================================================\n3. CREATE ISOLATED WIREGUARD WORKSPACE\n============================================================\n\nCreate an isolated workspace under:\n\n/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota\n\nand dedicated build directories:\n\n/opt/worm/build-wg/out\n/opt/worm/build-wg/tmp\n/opt/worm/build-wg/logs\n\nDo NOT use:\n\n/opt/Android\n\nDo NOT reuse:\n\n/opt/worm/build/out\n\nThe purpose is to prevent unrelated dirty source state or previous build\noutput from contaminating the WireGuard OTA.\n\n============================================================\n4. RECONSTRUCT ANDROID SOURCE STATE\n============================================================\n\nCreate the WireGuard OTA source state from the exact GrapheneOS/AOSP\nrevision represented by the recovered accepted checkpoint/provenance.\n\nReuse existing local repo objects/source data where safe to avoid unnecessary\nnetwork transfer, but the resulting checked-out source state must be clean\nand reproducible.\n\nApply ONLY the accepted source changes required for:\n\n- WormOS base/product boot integration\n- WormSystemWireGuard privileged component\n- official pinned WireGuard Android backend\n- source-built wireguard-go\n- WireGuard product packaging\n- WireGuard-specific SELinux changes\n- boot/autostart integration\n- VPN lockdown/fail-closed integration\n- protected DNS integration\n- required WireGuard provenance/build metadata\n\nDo NOT apply unrelated dirty changes.\n\n============================================================\n5. VERIFY CLEANNESS\n============================================================\n\nBefore building, verify every Android project participating in the\nWireGuard-only workspace.\n\nRequired:\n\nUNRELATED_DIRTY_CHANGES=0\n\nGenerate:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WIREGUARD-OTA-SOURCE-MANIFEST.md\n\ncontaining exact project revisions and WireGuard patches applied.\n\nIf unrelated changes remain:\n\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n6. BUILD OUTPUT CLEANUP\n============================================================\n\nThe existing:\n\n/opt/worm/build\n\nis old/disposable build output but DO NOT delete it automatically yet.\n\nFirst determine whether it contains any persistent artifact not already\nstored under:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts\n\nIf everything important is already preserved, report:\n\nOLD_BUILD_SAFE_TO_DELETE=YES\n\nThen STOP and report the exact reclaimable size before deleting.\n\nIf old build output contains unique target-files, OTA, provenance, reports,\nor other persistent artifacts:\n\ncopy those persistent artifacts into the appropriate /opt/worm/artifacts\nlocation first and verify hashes.\n\nOnly after preservation may old disposable build output be considered safe\nfor removal.\n\n============================================================\n7. STORAGE GATE\n============================================================\n\nCalculate space after potential removal of the old 106G build output.\n\nTarget layout:\n\n/opt/worm/build-wg = dedicated disposable WireGuard build\n\nRequire enough free space for:\n\n- full Android output\n- target-files\n- OTA packaging\n- temporary packaging overhead\n- safety margin\n\nReport:\n\nCURRENT_FREE_SPACE=\nOLD_BUILD_SIZE=\nOLD_BUILD_SAFE_TO_DELETE=\nPROJECTED_FREE_SPACE_AFTER_CLEANUP=\nESTIMATED_WG_BUILD_REQUIREMENT=\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=\n\nDo NOT start build until BUILD_SPACE_OK=YES.\n\n============================================================\n8. GIT CHECKPOINT\n============================================================\n\nPrepare dedicated branch:\n\npatch/PATCH-WIREGUARD-OTA\n\nThe WireGuard implementation tag will be:\n\nwormos-wg-backend-failclosed\n\nDo not create the tag until the isolated WireGuard source state is verified\nclean and complete.\n\nDo not modify:\n\nwormos-prebuild-wg-backend-recovered\n\n============================================================\n9. STOP BEFORE BUILD\n============================================================\n\nFor THIS continuation:\n\nDO NOT BUILD.\nDO NOT GENERATE OTA.\n\nComplete only:\n\n- isolation\n- reconstruction\n- cleanliness verification\n- preservation analysis of old build output\n- storage calculation\n- WireGuard-only source manifest\n\nFINAL REPORT:\n\nISOLATED_WORKSPACE=\nBASE_CHECKPOINT=\nBASE_COMMIT=\nANDROID_SOURCE_STATE=\nUNRELATED_DIRTY_CHANGES=\nWG_SOURCE_COMPLETE=\nOLD_BUILD_SIZE=\nOLD_BUILD_SAFE_TO_DELETE=\nPERSISTENT_ARTIFACTS_RECOVERED=\nCURRENT_FREE_SPACE=\nPROJECTED_FREE_SPACE_AFTER_CLEANUP=\nESTIMATED_WG_BUILD_REQUIREMENT=\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=\nIMPLEMENTATION_BRANCH=\nREADY_FOR_WG_BUILD=\nBLOCKERS=\n\nREADY_FOR_WG_BUILD=YES only when the isolated source state is clean,\nWireGuard-complete and sufficient build space can be guaranteed."}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1063:{"session_id":"01a0824b-e5a1-7ed2-aacc-5eca7ff7c874","ts":1788893483,"text":"RESUME WORMOS WIREGUARD-ONLY OTA PREPARATION\n\nEXPLICIT USER APPROVAL:\n\nThe old disposable build output identified by the previous audit is approved\nfor deletion.\n\nAuthoritative previous results:\n\nOLD_BUILD_SIZE=106G\nOLD_BUILD_SAFE_TO_DELETE=YES_FOR_WG_OTA_PURPOSE\nPERSISTENT_ARTIFACTS_RECOVERED=NONE_REQUIRED\nPROJECTED_FREE_SPACE_AFTER_CLEANUP=240G\nESTIMATED_WG_BUILD_REQUIREMENT=200G+\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES_AFTER_OLD_BUILD_CLEANUP\n\nBase checkpoint:\n\nwormos-prebuild-wg-backend-recovered\nf947156d418667ec6c9c654250b00f5aa32eb382\n\nDedicated branch:\n\npatch/PATCH-WIREGUARD-OTA\n\nDedicated WormOS worktree:\n\n/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/worm-os\n\n============================================================\n1. DELETE ONLY APPROVED OLD BUILD OUTPUT\n============================================================\n\nDelete ONLY the old disposable build output previously audited under:\n\n/opt/worm/build\n\nDo not delete or modify:\n\n/opt/worm/src\n/opt/worm/worktrees\n/opt/worm/patches\n/opt/worm/vendor\n/opt/worm/manifests\n/opt/worm/config\n/opt/worm/scripts\n/opt/worm/artifacts\n/opt/worm/worm-os\n/opt/worm/changelog\n/opt/worm/control\n/opt/worm/security\n/opt/worm/app-store\n/opt/worm/ota\n\nDo not touch Storage Box backups.\n\nAfter deletion run:\n\ndf -h\ndf -i\n\nReport:\n\nOLD_BUILD_DELETED=\nSPACE_RECLAIMED=\nFREE_SPACE_AFTER_CLEANUP=\n\nIf expected space is not reclaimed, investigate before continuing.\n\n============================================================\n2. PRESERVE DEDICATED BUILD ROOT\n============================================================\n\nUse only:\n\n/opt/worm/build-wg/out\n/opt/worm/build-wg/tmp\n/opt/worm/build-wg/logs\n\nfor the future WireGuard OTA build.\n\nDo NOT recreate /opt/worm/build for this build.\n\nDo NOT use /opt/Android.\n\n============================================================\n3. MATERIALIZE CLEAN ANDROID SOURCE\n============================================================\n\nThe previous phase generated a revision inventory but did NOT materialize\nthe full isolated Android checkout.\n\nNow create the complete isolated Android source tree required for the\nWireGuard OTA.\n\nPreferred location:\n\n/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/android\n\nUse the exact GrapheneOS/AOSP project revisions recorded in:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WIREGUARD-OTA-SOURCE-MANIFEST.md\n\nReuse local git/repo objects from /opt/worm/src/android where safe and\npossible to avoid unnecessary downloads.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe isolated checkout must NOT inherit dirty working-tree modifications from:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android\n\nUse clean Git objects/revisions, not filesystem copying of dirty source.\n\n============================================================\n4. RESTORE ONLY ACCEPTED WIREGUARD SOURCE STATE\n============================================================\n\nInto the isolated Android checkout restore/apply only the accepted state\nneeded for this WireGuard OTA:\n\n- required WormOS base/product integration\n- WormSystemWireGuard privileged system component\n- official pinned WireGuard Android backend\n- source-built wireguard-go source/build integration\n- WireGuard Android.bp integration\n- required product makefile integration\n- WireGuard-specific SELinux policy\n- boot/autostart integration\n- Android VPN/lockdown integration\n- fail-closed source/configuration\n- protected DNS integration\n- WireGuard provenance/build metadata\n\nDo NOT include unrelated dirty changes.\n\nDo NOT introduce:\n\n- Bitwarden\n- Proton Drive\n- new App Store work\n- additional Material 3 work\n- launcher changes\n- dashboard changes\n- changelog changes\n- Augurri changes\n- installer changes\n- unrelated OTA changes\n\nExisting base functionality strictly required by the selected WormOS source\ncheckpoint may remain.\n\n============================================================\n5. VERIFY PINNED BACKEND\n============================================================\n\nVerify the restored backend against the accepted provenance.\n\nExpected canonical upstream:\n\nhttps://git.zx2c4.com/wireguard-android\n\nExpected pinned commit from recovered state:\n\ne7b3a3c118836e112620b1302a8ba1873ad4daac\n\nDo not substitute another commit.\n\nVerify:\n\nBACKEND_SOURCE_PRESENT=\nBACKEND_COMMIT=\nBACKEND_PINNED=\nWIREGUARD_GO_SOURCE_PRESENT=\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=\n\nNo network upgrade to latest/HEAD.\n\n============================================================\n6. VERIFY COMPLETE ANDROID CHECKOUT\n============================================================\n\nRun source-only checks across the isolated Android tree.\n\nFor every participating repo/project verify:\n\n- expected revision\n- clean baseline\n- only approved WormOS/WireGuard modifications\n- no unrelated dirty files\n- no unresolved merge conflicts\n- no missing subprojects\n- repo manifest consistency\n\nGenerate:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WIREGUARD-OTA-ISOLATED-SOURCE-VERIFY.md\n\nReport:\n\nANDROID_CHECKOUT_MATERIALIZED=\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=\nUNRELATED_DIRTY_CHANGES=\nMERGE_CONFLICTS=\nMISSING_PROJECTS=\n\nRequired:\n\nUNRELATED_DIRTY_CHANGES=0\nMERGE_CONFLICTS=0\nMISSING_PROJECTS=0\n\n============================================================\n7. STATIC WIREGUARD VALIDATION\n============================================================\n\nWithout compiling, verify:\n\nWormSystemWireGuard source exists\nAndroidManifest integration exists\nprivileged/product integration exists\nWireGuard backend source exists\nwireguard-go build integration exists\nproduct packaging references exist\nSELinux source changes exist\nfail-closed configuration/source exists\nprotected DNS integration exists\nboot/autostart integration exists\n\nRun secret scan.\n\nRequired:\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nSELINUX_SOURCE=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\n============================================================\n8. STORAGE GATE AGAIN\n============================================================\n\nAfter source materialization, recalculate:\n\nFREE_SPACE=\nANDROID_SOURCE_SIZE=\nBUILD_WG_SIZE=\nESTIMATED_BUILD_REQUIREMENT=\nESTIMATED_POST_BUILD_MARGIN=\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=\n\nRequire a meaningful safety margin.\n\nIf materializing the isolated Android source consumes enough space that the\n200G+ build can no longer safely complete:\n\nSTOP.\n\nDo not begin compilation.\n\n============================================================\n9. DO NOT BUILD YET\n============================================================\n\nThis task ends at a clean, verified, isolated WireGuard source tree.\n\nDO NOT run:\n\nm\nmm\nmmm\nninja\ntarget-files-package\nOTA generation\n\nDo not create:\n\nwormos-wg-backend-failclosed\n\nyet.\n\nThe implementation tag will be created only after this isolated source state\nhas passed verification.\n\n============================================================\nFINAL REPORT\n============================================================\n\nOLD_BUILD_DELETED=\nSPACE_RECLAIMED=\nFREE_SPACE_AFTER_CLEANUP=\n\nISOLATED_WORMOS_WORKTREE=\nISOLATED_ANDROID_WORKSPACE=\nANDROID_CHECKOUT_MATERIALIZED=\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=\nUNRELATED_DIRTY_CHANGES=\nMERGE_CONFLICTS=\nMISSING_PROJECTS=\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=\nBACKEND_COMMIT=\nBACKEND_PINNED=\nWIREGUARD_GO_SOURCE_PRESENT=\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=\nSELINUX_SOURCE=\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=\nNO_SECRETS=\n\nANDROID_SOURCE_SIZE=\nFREE_SPACE=\nESTIMATED_BUILD_REQUIREMENT=\nESTIMATED_POST_BUILD_MARGIN=\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=\n\nIMPLEMENTATION_BRANCH=patch/PATCH-WIREGUARD-OTA\nIMPLEMENTATION_TAG=NOT_CREATED\nBUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN\n\nREADY_FOR_WG_BUILD=\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1065:{"session_id":"01a08261-44c5-7310-bd9f-ddc99926c922","ts":1788894989,"text":"Implement PATCH-WORM-MESH-TUI-V1.\n\nGOAL:\nCreate a modern terminal UI for the Worm Mesh Control Plane.\n\nLOCATION:\n/opt/worm/control-plane\n\nTECH:\nPython 3\nTextual\nRich\nSQLite\nPydantic\nPyYAML\n\nDo NOT modify:\n- OPNsense production WireGuard\n- network addressing\n- private backbone\n- worm-robot routing\n- FireHOL\n- OTA\n- worm-os Android source\n\nThis patch is CONTROL PLANE UI + LOCAL DATA MODEL only.\n\n==================================================\nFROZEN NETWORK REFERENCE\n==================================================\n\nOPNsense PUBLIC:\n2.28.34.27\n\nOPNsense WG:\n10.60.0.1/24\n\nWG endpoint:\n2.28.34.27:51823\n\nworm-os WG pool:\n10.60.0.0/24\n\nCurrent test device:\n10.60.0.10/32\n\nOPNsense PRIVATE:\n10.90.10.1\n\nworm-robot PRIVATE:\n10.90.20.10\n\nPrivate backbone:\n10.90.0.0/16\n\nDNS:\n10.60.0.1\n\n==================================================\n1. DIRECTORY STRUCTURE\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/worm/control-plane/\n├── wormctl.py\n├── pyproject.toml\n├── README.md\n├── wormmesh/\n│   ├── __init__.py\n│   ├── app.py\n│   ├── models.py\n│   ├── db.py\n│   ├── ipam.py\n│   ├── enrollment.py\n│   ├── dns.py\n│   ├── acl.py\n│   ├── opnsense.py\n│   ├── health.py\n│   ├── config.py\n│   └── screens/\n│       ├── __init__.py\n│       ├── dashboard.py\n│       ├── devices.py\n│       ├── enroll.py\n│       ├── device_detail.py\n│       ├── dns.py\n│       ├── acl.py\n│       ├── sync.py\n│       ├── health.py\n│       └── help.py\n├── data/\n│   └── .gitkeep\n└── config/\n    ├── acl.yaml\n    └── dns.yaml\n\nDo not store runtime DB in Git.\n\n==================================================\n2. UI STYLE\n==================================================\n\nBuild a modern Textual interface inspired by:\n- k9s\n- lazygit\n- modern terminal dashboards\n\nDo NOT create a numbered menu.\n\nMain layout:\n\n╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│ WORM MESH CONTROL PLANE                                     │\n│ OPNsense ●  WG ●  DNS ●  Backbone ●                        │\n├───────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ DEVICES               │ DETAILS                              │\n│                       │                                      │\n│ ● worm-001            │ Name        worm-001                 │\n│ ● worm-002            │ WG IP       10.60.0.10/32            │\n│ ○ worm-003 revoked    │ Public Key  GxW0...M38=              │\n│                       │ Policy      worm-standard             │\n│                       │ Last seen   12s ago                   │\n├───────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ [E] Enroll  [R] Revoke  [A] ACL  [D] DNS  [S] Sync  [?] Help│\n╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\nUse:\n- panels\n- tables\n- status badges\n- modal dialogs\n- confirmation dialogs\n- notifications\n- search/filter\n- keyboard shortcuts\n\n==================================================\n3. KEYBOARD UX\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nj / down      next item\nk / up        previous item\nenter         open device\ne             enroll\nr             revoke\na             ACL\nd             DNS\ns             sync\nh             health\n/             search\n?             help\nq             quit\n\nDo not require mouse.\n\n==================================================\n4. DEVICE MODEL\n==================================================\n\nCreate Pydantic model:\n\nDevice:\n- id\n- device_id\n- display_name\n- public_key\n- wg_ip\n- status\n- policy\n- groups\n- created_at\n- updated_at\n- last_seen\n- notes\n\nStatus:\nACTIVE\nREVOKED\nPENDING\n\nNever include:\nprivate_key\n\n==================================================\n5. SQLITE REGISTRY\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/worm/control-plane/data/wormmesh.db\n\nat runtime.\n\nTables:\n\ndevices\nip_allocations\npolicies\ndns_records\naudit_log\nsync_state\n\nUse migrations/version table.\n\nEnable:\nforeign_keys=ON\n\nUse transactions.\n\n==================================================\n6. IPAM\n==================================================\n\nPool:\n\n10.60.0.0/24\n\nReserve:\n\n10.60.0.1\nfor OPNsense\n\n10.60.0.2-9\nreserved infrastructure\n\nDevice pool begins:\n10.60.0.10\n\nAllocate /32 sequentially.\n\nDo not reuse an ACTIVE allocation.\n\nRevoked addresses may remain reserved by default.\n\nExpose:\n\nallocate_ip()\nrelease_ip()\nlist_allocations()\nis_available()\n\n==================================================\n7. ENROLLMENT SCREEN\n==================================================\n\nModern modal/form.\n\nFields:\n\nDisplay Name\nDevice ID\nPublic Key\nPolicy\nGroups\nNotes\n\nValidate WireGuard public key format.\n\nOn submit:\n\n1. validate\n2. allocate IP\n3. create device\n4. write audit entry\n5. show result\n\nDisplay:\n\nDEVICE ENROLLED\n\nDevice:\nworm-001\n\nWG IP:\n10.60.0.10/32\n\nDNS:\n10.60.0.1\n\nEndpoint:\n2.28.34.27:51823\n\nStatus:\nPENDING SYNC\n\nDo NOT ask for private key.\n\n==================================================\n8. DEVICE DETAIL\n==================================================\n\nShow:\n\nName\nDevice ID\nStatus\nWG IP\nPublic Key abbreviated\nPolicy\nGroups\nCreated\nLast Seen\nSync Status\n\nActions:\n\nRevoke\nEdit policy\nRotate public key\nCopy config values\nView audit history\n\nDo not display any secret material.\n\n==================================================\n9. REVOKE\n==================================================\n\nRequire confirmation modal:\n\nREVOKE DEVICE?\nworm-001\n10.60.0.10/32\n\nThis will block future network access after OPNsense sync.\n\n[Cancel]\n[Revoke]\n\nOn confirm:\nstatus=REVOKED\naudit entry\nsync status=PENDING\n\nDo not delete registry history.\n\n==================================================\n10. DNS\n==================================================\n\nDefault private records:\n\nopnsense.worm -> 10.60.0.1\nrobot.worm -> 10.90.20.10\ngit.worm -> 10.90.20.10\ndashboard.worm -> 10.90.20.10\nota.worm -> 10.90.20.10\n\nBuild DNS screen:\n- list\n- add\n- edit\n- disable\n- validate IP/hostname\n\nFor V1:\nLOCAL MODEL ONLY.\n\nDo not apply to OPNsense yet.\n\n==================================================\n11. ACL\n==================================================\n\nDefault policies:\n\nworm-standard\nworm-admin\nworm-restricted\n\nExample:\n\nworm-standard:\n- internet\n- ota\n- downloads\n- apps\n\nworm-admin:\n- internet\n- ota\n- downloads\n- apps\n- git\n- dashboard\n- robot-ssh\n- opnsense-management\n\nworm-restricted:\n- ota\n- downloads\n\nStore in config/acl.yaml.\n\nBuild ACL screen:\n- policy list\n- permissions\n- assigned devices\n\nV1:\nLOCAL MODEL ONLY.\n\n==================================================\n12. OPNsense ADAPTER\n==================================================\n\nCreate abstraction only.\n\nwormmesh/opnsense.py\n\nInterface methods:\n\nhealth()\nlist_peers()\ncreate_peer()\nupdate_peer()\ndelete_peer()\napply_dns()\napply_acl()\ndry_run()\n\nV1 MUST default to:\n\nDRY_RUN=True\n\nDo not modify production OPNsense.\n\nSync screen should clearly show:\n\nDRY RUN\n\nPending changes:\n+ peer worm-001 10.60.0.10/32\n- peer worm-003\n~ ACL worm-admin\n\n[Preview]\n[Apply]\n\nApply must be disabled in V1 unless explicitly enabled through config.\n\n==================================================\n13. HEALTH DASHBOARD\n==================================================\n\nTop status cards:\n\nOPNsense\nWireGuard\nPrivate DNS\nPrivate Backbone\nRegistry\nPending Sync\n\nHealth screen:\n\nOPNsense public: 2.28.34.27\nOPNsense private: 10.90.10.1\nWG gateway: 10.60.0.1\nWG endpoint: 2.28.34.27:51823\nRobot private: 10.90.20.10\nRobot public: 162.55.6.173\n\nFor V1:\nread from config/local checks only.\nDo not mutate anything.\n\n==================================================\n14. AUDIT LOG\n==================================================\n\nEvery action logs:\n\ntimestamp\nactor\naction\ndevice_id\ndetails\n\nNever log:\nprivate keys\npasswords\ntokens\n\nShow recent activity in dashboard.\n\n==================================================\n15. CONFIG\n==================================================\n\nCreate config loader.\n\nExample:\n\ncontrol_plane:\n  name: worm\n\nwireguard:\n  network: 10.60.0.0/24\n  gateway: 10.60.0.1\n  endpoint: 2.28.34.27:51823\n  dns: 10.60.0.1\n\nprivate:\n  opnsense: 10.90.10.1\n  robot: 10.90.20.10\n  backbone: 10.90.0.0/16\n\nopnsense:\n  dry_run: true\n\nDo not store credentials in YAML.\n\n==================================================\n16. START COMMAND\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\ncd /opt/worm/control-plane\npython3 wormctl.py\n\nAlso install:\n\n/usr/local/bin/wormctl\n\nwrapper/symlink if appropriate.\n\nThen:\n\nwormctl\n\nmust open the TUI.\n\n==================================================\n17. DEMO DATA\n==================================================\n\nDo not insert fake production devices automatically.\n\nProvide optional command:\n\nwormctl --demo\n\nwhich initializes temporary demo data.\n\nNormal startup must use real empty/local registry.\n\n==================================================\n18. TESTS\n==================================================\n\nAdd tests for:\n\n- DB initialization\n- IPAM allocation\n- duplicate public key rejection\n- duplicate device ID rejection\n- revoke flow\n- address collision\n- ACL loading\n- DNS validation\n- no private-key field\n- dry-run OPNsense adapter\n\nRun them.\n\n==================================================\n19. SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nPermissions:\n\ncontrol-plane directory:\nroot-owned or appropriate worm service owner\n\nDB:\nnot world-readable\n\nconfig:\nnot world-writable\n\nNo shell injection.\n\nNo unsafe YAML loader.\n\nNo secrets in logs.\n\nDo not run arbitrary commands from device fields.\n\n==================================================\n20. PATCH OUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nPATCH-WORM-MESH-TUI-V1/\n\nInclude:\n\nREADME.md\nARCHITECTURE.md\nUI.md\nDATABASE.md\nIPAM.md\nENROLLMENT.md\nDNS.md\nACL.md\nOPNSENSE-ADAPTER.md\nSECURITY.md\nTESTS.md\nROLLBACK.md\nmodified-files.txt\ntest-results.txt\n\n==================================================\nFINAL GATE\n==================================================\n\nPASS requires:\n\nPASS Textual TUI launches\nPASS dashboard\nPASS device list\nPASS enrollment modal\nPASS device detail\nPASS revoke flow\nPASS SQLite registry\nPASS IPAM\nPASS DNS model\nPASS ACL model\nPASS audit log\nPASS search\nPASS keyboard shortcuts\nPASS health screen\nPASS OPNsense adapter DRY-RUN\nPASS no production network changes\nPASS no secrets\nPASS tests\n\nFinal output:\n\nWORM MESH TUI V1:\nPASS / PARTIAL / FAIL\n\nTUI:\nPASS / FAIL\n\nREGISTRY:\nPASS / FAIL\n\nIPAM:\nPASS / FAIL\n\nDNS MODEL:\nPASS / FAIL\n\nACL MODEL:\nPASS / FAIL\n\nOPNSENSE:\nDRY-RUN / FAIL\n\nNETWORK:\nUNCHANGED / FAIL\n\nDo not enable live OPNsense synchronization automatically."}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1066:{"session_id":"01a0824b-e5a1-7ed2-aacc-5eca7ff7c874","ts":1788896609,"text":"RESUME WORMOS WIREGUARD-ONLY OTA PREPARATION\n\nCurrent verified state:\n\nANDROID_CHECKOUT_MATERIALIZED=YES\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108\nUNRELATED_DIRTY_CHANGES=0\nMERGE_CONFLICTS=0\nMISSING_PROJECTS=0\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nWIREGUARD_GO_SOURCE_PRESENT=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nCurrent blockers:\n\nSELINUX_SOURCE=FAIL\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=NO\n\nDO NOT BUILD OR GENERATE OTA YET.\n\n============================================================\n1. RESOLVE SELINUX SOURCE BLOCKER\n============================================================\n\nThe isolated checkout currently contains no explicit SELinux policy for\nWormSystemWireGuard / systemwg.\n\nFirst inspect the recovered historical source/patch artifacts under:\n\n/opt/worm/patches\n/opt/worm/artifacts\n/opt/worm/vendor\n/opt/worm/worm-os\n\nand, only if necessary, the preserved Storage Box historical Android backup.\n\nDetermine whether the previously accepted WireGuard implementation actually\ncontained SELinux source changes.\n\nDo NOT invent policy merely because the previous report expected it.\n\nClassify:\n\nA. SELinux policy existed previously but was omitted during reconstruction.\n   -> Recover the exact accepted policy.\n\nB. WormSystemWireGuard runs inside an existing Android SELinux domain and\n   requires no new policy.\n   -> Prove this by source/static inspection and document it.\n\nC. New SELinux policy is genuinely required but was never implemented.\n   -> Implement the minimum policy required for the accepted system-owned\n      WireGuard architecture.\n\nFor case C:\n\n- minimum permissions only\n- no permissive\n- no wildcard/broad allow rules\n- no neverallow bypass\n- no unrelated domain changes\n- no additional privilege beyond what WormSystemWireGuard requires\n\nInspect at minimum:\n\nAndroidManifest.xml\nprivileged app configuration\nprocess/UID assignment\nservice lifecycle\nVpnService interaction\nwireguard-go/native library execution model\nsocket/network access\nfiles/config accessed by the component\n\nGenerate:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WIREGUARD-OTA-SELINUX-AUDIT.md\n\nReport:\n\nSELINUX_EXECUTION_DOMAIN=\nSELINUX_NEW_POLICY_REQUIRED=\nSELINUX_POLICY_SOURCE=\nSELINUX_SOURCE=\n\nDo not claim compiled SELinux PASS yet.\nThis phase is source/static validation only.\n\n============================================================\n2. AUDIT DUPLICATE ANDROID SOURCE\n============================================================\n\nWe currently have approximately:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android                         ~ source tree\n/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/android            106G verified isolated tree\n\nThe isolated tree is the authoritative WireGuard OTA workspace.\n\nAudit /opt/worm/src/android before deleting anything.\n\nDetermine whether it contains any UNIQUE persistent WormOS source,\npatch, manifest, provenance or accepted implementation not already preserved\nunder:\n\n/opt/worm/patches\n/opt/worm/artifacts\n/opt/worm/manifests\n/opt/worm/vendor\n/opt/worm/worm-os\n/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/android\n\nDo NOT treat ordinary upstream Android source or regenerable repo objects as\nunique persistent project state.\n\nReport:\n\nOLD_ANDROID_SOURCE_SIZE=\nOLD_ANDROID_UNIQUE_FILES=\nOLD_ANDROID_UNIQUE_STATE_PRESERVED=\nOLD_ANDROID_SAFE_TO_DELETE=\n\n============================================================\n3. PRESERVE UNIQUE STATE\n============================================================\n\nIf unique accepted WormOS files are found in /opt/worm/src/android:\n\ncopy ONLY those persistent source/patch/provenance artifacts into the\nappropriate canonical /opt/worm persistent locations.\n\nRecord SHA256 hashes before and after preservation.\n\nDo not copy:\n\nout/\nbuild intermediates\nrepo caches\ntemporary files\nupstream source duplicated by the isolated checkout\n\nGenerate:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/OLD-ANDROID-SOURCE-PRESERVATION.md\n\n============================================================\n4. DELETE DUPLICATE SOURCE ONLY IF SAFE\n============================================================\n\nIf and only if:\n\nOLD_ANDROID_SAFE_TO_DELETE=YES\n\nthen explicit approval is granted to delete:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android\n\nDo NOT delete:\n\n/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/android\n/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/worm-os\n/opt/worm/patches\n/opt/worm/artifacts\n/opt/worm/manifests\n/opt/worm/vendor\n/opt/worm/config\n/opt/worm/scripts\n/opt/worm/worm-os\n\nAfter deletion:\n\ndf -h\ndf -i\n\nReport:\n\nOLD_ANDROID_DELETED=\nSPACE_RECLAIMED=\nFREE_SPACE_AFTER_SOURCE_CLEANUP=\n\n============================================================\n5. UPDATE CANONICAL BUILD PATH FOR THIS OTA\n============================================================\n\nFor this WireGuard-only OTA use:\n\nWORM_ROOT=/opt/worm\nANDROID_BUILD_TOP=/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/android\nOUT_DIR=/opt/worm/build-wg/out\nTMPDIR=/opt/worm/build-wg/tmp\n\nDo not recreate /opt/worm/src/android during this OTA.\n\nDo not use /opt/Android.\n\n============================================================\n6. STORAGE GATE\n============================================================\n\nRecalculate actual available space after cleanup.\n\nReport:\n\nFREE_SPACE=\nANDROID_SOURCE_SIZE=\nESTIMATED_BUILD_REQUIREMENT=\nESTIMATED_POST_BUILD_MARGIN=\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=\n\nRequire sufficient space for:\n\n- Android build output\n- target-files-package\n- OTA packaging\n- temporary packaging overhead\n- safety margin\n\nDo not use the previous 200G+ estimate blindly.\nRecalculate using historical WormOS/GrapheneOS build output sizes available\nin reports/backups where possible.\n\nIf BUILD_SPACE_OK=NO:\n\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n7. FINAL PREBUILD SOURCE VALIDATION\n============================================================\n\nVerify again:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=\nUNRELATED_DIRTY_CHANGES=0\nMERGE_CONFLICTS=0\nMISSING_PROJECTS=0\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=PASS\nSELINUX_SOURCE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\n============================================================\n8. NO BUILD YET\n============================================================\n\nDo not compile in this task.\n\nDo not create the implementation tag yet.\n\nFinal required gate:\n\nREADY_FOR_WG_BUILD=YES\n\n============================================================\nFINAL REPORT\n============================================================\n\nSELINUX_EXECUTION_DOMAIN=\nSELINUX_NEW_POLICY_REQUIRED=\nSELINUX_POLICY_SOURCE=\nSELINUX_SOURCE=\n\nOLD_ANDROID_SOURCE_SIZE=\nOLD_ANDROID_UNIQUE_FILES=\nOLD_ANDROID_UNIQUE_STATE_PRESERVED=\nOLD_ANDROID_SAFE_TO_DELETE=\nOLD_ANDROID_DELETED=\nSPACE_RECLAIMED=\n\nANDROID_BUILD_TOP=\nFREE_SPACE=\nESTIMATED_BUILD_REQUIREMENT=\nESTIMATED_POST_BUILD_MARGIN=\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=\nUNRELATED_DIRTY_CHANGES=\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=\nBACKEND_PINNED=\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=\nNO_SECRETS=\n\nBUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN\nREADY_FOR_WG_BUILD=\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1067:{"session_id":"01a0824b-e5a1-7ed2-aacc-5eca7ff7c874","ts":1788910950,"text":"START NEW TASK: REPAIR WORMOS WG-OTA ANDROID REPO CHECKOUT\n\nDo not resume the previous stalled goal.\n\nCurrent authoritative workspace:\n\n/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/android\n\nWireGuard WormOS worktree:\n\n/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/worm-os\n\nBranch:\n\npatch/PATCH-WIREGUARD-OTA\n\nBase checkpoint:\n\nwormos-prebuild-wg-backend-recovered\nf947156d418667ec6c9c654250b00f5aa32eb382\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM\n\nThe Android working files exist, but the isolated repo checkout was created\nwith Git object dependencies pointing into the now-deleted:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android/.repo/project-objects\n\nAs a result, many Android project repositories cannot resolve their Git\nobjects.\n\nThis is a REPO METADATA / OBJECT DATABASE repair task.\n\nDo not rebuild WormOS source from memory.\nDo not change Android versions.\nDo not change WireGuard implementation.\nDo not build or generate OTA yet.\n\n============================================================\n1. INSPECT ACTUAL CURRENT STATE\n============================================================\n\nIgnore stale previous status summaries.\n\nInspect the filesystem and Git metadata NOW.\n\nCheck:\n\n/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/android/.repo\n\nand all project .git metadata.\n\nCount:\n\nTOTAL_MANIFEST_PROJECTS=\nVALID_PROJECT_GIT_REPOS=\nBROKEN_PROJECT_GIT_REPOS=\nBROKEN_SYMLINKS=\nBROKEN_ALTERNATES=\nMERGE_CONFLICT_PROJECTS=\n\nList every merge-conflict project separately.\n\nDetermine whether the conflicts are genuine working-tree conflicts or only\nartifacts of missing Git objects.\n\nDo not modify files yet.\n\n============================================================\n2. INSPECT STORAGE BOX BACKUP FIRST\n============================================================\n\nUse the existing /opt/worm Storage Box tooling to locate the historical\nbackup of the former /opt/Android.\n\nREAD ONLY.\n\nSearch specifically for:\n\n.repo/project-objects\n.repo/projects\nmanifest.xml\nmanifests.git\n\nIf the backup contains the old .repo Git object stores, determine whether\nthey contain the exact objects required by the isolated checkout.\n\nPrefer recovering these exact objects over redownloading the complete\nAndroid source.\n\nDo not restore:\n\nout/\nbuild output\nOTA\ntarget-files\ntemporary files\n\nReport:\n\nSTORAGEBOX_REPO_OBJECTS_FOUND=\nSTORAGEBOX_PROJECTS_METADATA_FOUND=\nSTORAGEBOX_MANIFEST_FOUND=\nSTORAGEBOX_OBJECT_RESTORE_FEASIBLE=\n\n============================================================\n3. RESTORE REPO OBJECT DATABASE\n============================================================\n\nIf Storage Box contains the required object stores:\n\nrestore only the required .repo Git metadata into a NEW local persistent\nobject-cache location:\n\n/opt/worm/cache/android-repo\n\nDo NOT recreate /opt/worm/src/android.\n\nDo NOT make the WG OTA checkout dependent on Storage Box at runtime.\n\nAfter restoration, repair references inside:\n\n/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/android/.repo\n\nto use the local cache or self-contained local Git objects.\n\nIf Storage Box does not contain sufficient objects:\n\nuse the exact existing manifest and canonical upstream remotes to fetch\nmissing objects.\n\nNever substitute latest/HEAD.\n\nAll projects must remain at their recorded pinned revisions.\n\n============================================================\n4. REMOVE DEAD REFERENCES\n============================================================\n\nAfter object restoration, find every reference to:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android\n\ninside the isolated checkout metadata.\n\nRepair/remove those references appropriately.\n\nRequired final state:\n\nBROKEN_SYMLINKS=0\nBROKEN_ALTERNATES=0\nOLD_ANDROID_REFERENCES=0\n\nThe checkout must remain usable even though:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android\n\ndoes not exist.\n\n============================================================\n5. RESOLVE REPO METADATA BEFORE SOURCE CONFLICTS\n============================================================\n\nDo NOT resolve source merge conflicts while Git objects are still missing.\n\nFirst restore complete Git object visibility.\n\nThen rerun:\n\nrepo status\n\nand per-project Git status.\n\nIf a previously reported conflict disappears after object repair, classify\nit as:\n\nOBJECT_CACHE_ARTIFACT\n\nIf a real source conflict remains:\n\nSTOP for that project and report:\n\nPROJECT=\nFILES=\nBASE_REVISION=\nCURRENT_STATE=\n\nDo not automatically choose ours/theirs.\n\n============================================================\n6. VERIFY ALL PROJECTS\n============================================================\n\nUse the authoritative manifest/revision inventory already stored under:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/\n\nVerify every manifest project.\n\nFor every project require:\n\n- Git metadata readable\n- pinned revision object available\n- revision resolves\n- worktree readable\n- no missing object errors\n- no unexpected revision change\n\nExpected total from previous audit:\n\n1108\n\nRequired:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\n\n============================================================\n7. VERIFY APPROVED MODIFICATIONS\n============================================================\n\nAfter Git metadata is healthy, distinguish approved WormOS/WireGuard changes\nfrom unrelated dirty changes.\n\nApproved scope:\n\n- required WormOS base/product integration\n- WormSystemWireGuard\n- official pinned WireGuard Android backend\n- source-built wireguard-go integration\n- WireGuard build/product integration\n- existing priv_app SELinux-domain integration\n- fail-closed source\n- protected DNS / boot integration required by WireGuard\n\nNo unrelated modifications may enter the WG OTA.\n\nRequired:\n\nUNRELATED_DIRTY_CHANGES=0\n\n============================================================\n8. REVERIFY WIREGUARD\n============================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=PASS\n\nBACKEND_COMMIT must remain exactly:\n\ne7b3a3c118836e112620b1302a8ba1873ad4daac\n\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nWIREGUARD_GO_SOURCE_PRESENT=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=PASS\nSELINUX_SOURCE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\n============================================================\n9. STORAGE\n============================================================\n\nCurrent previous free-space measurement was approximately:\n\n290G\n\nAfter object restoration report actual:\n\nFREE_SPACE=\nANDROID_WORKSPACE_SIZE=\nANDROID_OBJECT_CACHE_SIZE=\nESTIMATED_BUILD_REQUIREMENT=\nESTIMATED_POST_BUILD_MARGIN=\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=\n\nDo not begin compilation.\n\n============================================================\n10. REPORTS\n============================================================\n\nUpdate/create:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WIREGUARD-OTA-REPO-OBJECT-REPAIR.md\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WIREGUARD-OTA-ISOLATED-SOURCE-VERIFY.md\n\nInclude exact object recovery method and project verification counts.\n\n============================================================\n11. STOP AT BUILD GATE\n============================================================\n\nBUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN\n\nDo NOT create the implementation tag yet.\n\nFinal required state:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nBROKEN_SYMLINKS=0\nBROKEN_ALTERNATES=0\nOLD_ANDROID_REFERENCES=0\nMERGE_CONFLICTS=0\nUNRELATED_DIRTY_CHANGES=0\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=PASS\nSELINUX_SOURCE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES\n\nThen:\n\nREADY_FOR_WG_BUILD=YES\n\nFINAL REPORT:\n\nTOTAL_MANIFEST_PROJECTS=\nVALID_PROJECT_GIT_REPOS=\nBROKEN_PROJECT_GIT_REPOS=\nSTORAGEBOX_REPO_OBJECTS_FOUND=\nSTORAGEBOX_OBJECT_RESTORE_FEASIBLE=\nOBJECTS_RECOVERED_FROM_STORAGEBOX=\nOBJECTS_FETCHED_FROM_UPSTREAM=\n\nBROKEN_SYMLINKS=\nBROKEN_ALTERNATES=\nOLD_ANDROID_REFERENCES=\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=\nMERGE_CONFLICTS=\nUNRELATED_DIRTY_CHANGES=\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=\nBACKEND_COMMIT=\nBACKEND_PINNED=\nWIREGUARD_GO_SOURCE_PRESENT=\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=\nSELINUX_SOURCE=\nNO_SECRETS=\n\nFREE_SPACE=\nANDROID_WORKSPACE_SIZE=\nANDROID_OBJECT_CACHE_SIZE=\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=\n\nBUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN\nREADY_FOR_WG_BUILD=\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1068:{"session_id":"01a08261-44c5-7310-bd9f-ddc99926c922","ts":1788911766,"text":"Polish PATCH-WORM-MESH-TUI-V1 before enabling live sync.\n\nDO NOT modify networking or OPNsense.\nKeep OPNsense DRY-RUN.\n\nFix and improve the existing Textual TUI in:\n/opt/worm/control-plane\n\n1. Fix literal escaped newlines.\nCurrent UI renders:\nDETAILS\\n\\nNo devices enrolled.\nIt must render real line breaks.\n\n2. Optimize responsive layout for narrow/mobile terminals.\n\nFor wide terminals:\nDEVICES | DETAILS side-by-side.\n\nFor narrow terminals:\nshow DEVICES full width.\nOpening/selecting a device shows DETAILS as a separate screen/panel.\n\nDo not squeeze both columns until text becomes unreadable.\n\n3. Improve header.\n\nWORM MESH\nControl Plane\n\nShow compact status badges:\nOPN ●\nWG ●\nDNS ●\nNET ●\nDRY-RUN\n\nUse available width intelligently.\n\n4. Empty state.\n\nInstead of a nearly empty screen show centered:\n\nNo Worm devices enrolled\n\nPress E to enroll your first device\n\nWG pool: 10.60.0.0/24\nNext IP: 10.60.0.10\n\n5. Bottom command bar.\n\nMake it responsive.\n\nNarrow:\n[E] Enroll   [/] Search   [?] Help   [Q] Quit\n\nOther actions should appear contextually.\n\nWide:\n[E] Enroll [R] Revoke [A] ACL [D] DNS [S] Sync [H] Health [?] Help [Q] Quit\n\nNever truncate action names into confusing fragments.\n\n6. Add navigation tabs/screens:\n\nDevices\nNetwork\nDNS\nACL\nAudit\n\nUse keyboard navigation.\n\n7. Network screen must display READ-ONLY frozen topology:\n\nWG Gateway       10.60.0.1\nWG Network       10.60.0.0/24\nEndpoint         2.28.34.27:51823\nProtected DNS    10.60.0.1\nOPNsense Private 10.90.10.1\nRobot Private    10.90.20.10\nRobot Public     162.55.6.173\nBackbone         10.90.0.0/16\n\nClearly mark:\nPRODUCTION NETWORK — READ ONLY\n\n8. Improve visual hierarchy using Textual CSS:\ntitles\nborders\nspacing\nstatus badges\nselected rows\nmodal dialogs\n\nKeep it professional and terminal-native.\nDo not add decorative clutter.\n\n9. Verify Android/Termux narrow-terminal rendering as far as automated\nTextual sizing tests permit.\n\nTest widths:\n60\n80\n120 columns\n\nTest heights:\n24\n32\n40 rows\n\nNo traceback.\nNo overlapping widgets.\nNo literal escape sequences.\nNo critical text truncation.\n\n10. Preserve all existing functionality and tests.\n\nRun full test suite and add responsive-layout tests.\n\nFinal:\n\nWORM MESH TUI POLISH=\nPASS / FAIL\n\nRESPONSIVE_60COL=\nPASS / FAIL\n\nRESPONSIVE_80COL=\nPASS / FAIL\n\nRESPONSIVE_120COL=\nPASS / FAIL\n\nNEWLINE_RENDERING=\nPASS / FAIL\n\nREGISTRY=\nPASS / FAIL\n\nIPAM=\nPASS / FAIL\n\nOPNSENSE=\nDRY-RUN\n\nNETWORK=\nUNCHANGED\n\nDo not start V1.1 automatically."}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1069:{"session_id":"01a0824b-e5a1-7ed2-aacc-5eca7ff7c874","ts":1788913036,"text":"START WORMOS WIREGUARD SYSTEM-STATE OTA ONLY\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nBuild one dedicated OTA containing ONLY the accepted WireGuard system-state\nimplementation required to make WormSystemWireGuard part of WormOS.\n\nDo not include unrelated WormOS feature work.\n\nCanonical root:\n\n/opt/worm\n\nWireGuard isolated Android workspace:\n\n/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/android\n\nWireGuard WormOS worktree:\n\n/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/worm-os\n\nDedicated build output:\n\n/opt/worm/build-wg\n\nBase checkpoint:\n\nwormos-prebuild-wg-backend-recovered\nf947156d418667ec6c9c654250b00f5aa32eb382\n\nDedicated branch:\n\npatch/PATCH-WIREGUARD-OTA\n\n============================================================\n1. DEFINE EXACT SYSTEM-STATE SCOPE\n============================================================\n\nThe OTA may contain only changes required for:\n\n- WormSystemWireGuard privileged/system app\n- product/package inclusion\n- required privileged permissions\n- Android VpnService integration\n- official pinned WireGuard Android tunnel backend\n- source-built wireguard-go\n- backend lifecycle\n- boot/autostart integration\n- Android VPN lockdown/fail-closed integration\n- IPv4 fail-closed source\n- IPv6 fail-closed source\n- protected DNS integration\n- private-network routing support required by WireGuard\n- underlying network handover logic required by WireGuard\n- backend crash / peer unreachable fail-closed logic\n- minimal existing SELinux domain integration\n- runtime non-secret configuration/provisioning interfaces\n- WireGuard provenance/build metadata\n- device validation scripts for this implementation\n\nExplicitly exclude new changes for:\n\n- Bitwarden\n- Proton Drive\n- Proton changes unrelated to existing base\n- App Store changes\n- Material 3 changes\n- launcher\n- dashboard\n- control\n- changelog\n- Augurri\n- web installer\n- unrelated updater/OTA features\n- OPNsense\n- server WireGuard\n- server firewall\n- public IP/network infrastructure\n\n============================================================\n2. REPAIR / VERIFY ANDROID CHECKOUT FIRST\n============================================================\n\nBefore build, the isolated Android repo metadata must be healthy.\n\nRepair the current blocker:\n\nISOLATED_ANDROID_REPO_OBJECT_CACHE_BROKEN\n\nUse:\n\n- Storage Box historical .repo/project-objects if available, or\n- canonical upstream fetches for exact pinned manifest revisions.\n\nDo not upgrade source revisions.\n\nDo not recreate /opt/worm/src/android.\n\nRequired before proceeding:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nBROKEN_SYMLINKS=0\nBROKEN_ALTERNATES=0\nOLD_ANDROID_REFERENCES=0\nMERGE_CONFLICTS=0\n\n============================================================\n3. VERIFY WIREGUARD SOURCE STATE\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=PASS\n\nBACKEND_COMMIT must remain exactly:\n\ne7b3a3c118836e112620b1302a8ba1873ad4daac\n\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nWIREGUARD_GO_SOURCE_PRESENT=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=PASS\nSELINUX_SOURCE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nNo source redesign in this phase unless required to fix a build blocker.\n\n============================================================\n4. VERIFY OTA DIFF IS WIREGUARD-ONLY\n============================================================\n\nBefore compiling, generate a complete source delta from the accepted base.\n\nProduce:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WIREGUARD-SYSTEM-STATE-OTA-DIFF.md\n\nFor every changed file classify:\n\nWIREGUARD_REQUIRED\nBASE_REQUIRED\nUNRELATED\n\nRequired:\n\nUNRELATED_FILES_INCLUDED=0\n\nIf any unrelated implementation would enter the image:\n\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n5. CREATE SOURCE IMPLEMENTATION CHECKPOINT\n============================================================\n\nOnce source verification passes, commit only the WireGuard system-state\nimplementation.\n\nCommit message:\n\nWormOS: WireGuard system-state integration\n\nCreate annotated tag:\n\nwormos-wg-system-state\n\nTag message:\n\nWormOS WireGuard system-state implementation.\n\nIncludes system-owned WormSystemWireGuard, official pinned WireGuard Android\nbackend, source-built wireguard-go, VPN lockdown/fail-closed, protected DNS,\nboot lifecycle and required system integration.\n\nBuild/runtime validation tracked separately.\n\nNever move this tag after publishing.\n\n============================================================\n6. STORAGE CHECK\n============================================================\n\nUse:\n\nANDROID_BUILD_TOP=/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/android\nOUT_DIR=/opt/worm/build-wg/out\nTMPDIR=/opt/worm/build-wg/tmp\n\nCheck actual disk space before build.\n\nRequired:\n\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES\n\nDo not use /opt/Android.\nDo not use /opt/worm/build.\n\n============================================================\n7. BUILD SYSTEM-STATE OTA\n============================================================\n\nBuild in this order:\n\n1. source-built wireguard-go\n2. WormSystemWireGuard\n3. required affected platform/product components\n4. target-files-package\n5. OTA package\n\nDo not add unrelated build targets unless required by dependency resolution.\n\n============================================================\n8. VERIFY RESULTING TARGET-FILES\n============================================================\n\nProve the generated target-files contain:\n\n- WormSystemWireGuard.apk\n- source-built libwg-go.so\n- WireGuard Android backend runtime pieces\n- required product package declarations\n- privileged permissions/config\n- boot/autostart integration\n- required fail-closed integration\n- protected DNS integration\n- required SELinux policy/domain mapping\n\nRequired:\n\nWG_BACKEND=PASS\nBACKEND_SOURCE_BUILD=PASS\nBACKEND_PACKAGED=PASS\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nSELINUX=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\n============================================================\n9. VERIFY NO UNRELATED OTA CONTENT\n============================================================\n\nCompare the produced target-files/image against the chosen base image/source\nstate.\n\nGenerate:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WIREGUARD-SYSTEM-STATE-OTA-CONTENT.md\n\nIdentify every changed package/config/system component.\n\nRequired:\n\nUNRELATED_OTA_CONTENT=0\n\nIf unrelated source or package modifications are detected:\n\nOTA_BUILD=FAIL_SCOPE_CONTAMINATION\n\nDo not publish the OTA.\n\n============================================================\n10. GENERATE OTA\n============================================================\n\nIf all build and scope gates pass, generate the dedicated OTA.\n\nStore persistent artifacts under:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/releases/wireguard-system-state/\n/opt/worm/artifacts/target-files/\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/\n/opt/worm/artifacts/provenance/\n\nRecord:\n\nSOURCE_COMMIT=\nSOURCE_TAG=wormos-wg-system-state\nTARGET_FILES=\nOTA_FILE=\nOTA_SHA256=\nBUILD_TIMESTAMP=\n\n============================================================\n11. OTA BUILD TAG\n============================================================\n\nAfter a successful package verification create:\n\nwormos-wg-system-state-ota-built\n\nas an annotated tag pointing to the same source commit as:\n\nwormos-wg-system-state\n\nDo not create a runtime-pass tag.\n\n============================================================\n12. DEVICE VALIDATION IS SEPARATE\n============================================================\n\nAfter OTA generation:\n\nBUILD=PASS\nOTA_BUILD=PASS\n\nbut:\n\nDEVICE_RUNTIME_VALIDATION=NOT_RUN\n\nPhysical device tests still required:\n\nAUTO_START\nWG_RUNTIME\nFAIL_CLOSED_IPV4\nFAIL_CLOSED_IPV6\nFAIL_CLOSED_BOOT\nFAIL_CLOSED_HANDOVER\nFAIL_CLOSED_BACKEND_CRASH\nFAIL_CLOSED_PEER_UNREACHABLE\nPROTECTED_DNS\nPRIVATE_ACCESS\nPUBLIC_IPV4\n\nDo not claim these PASS from build-time evidence.\n\n============================================================\nFINAL REPORT\n============================================================\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=\nBROKEN_SYMLINKS=\nBROKEN_ALTERNATES=\nMERGE_CONFLICTS=\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=\nBACKEND_COMMIT=\nBACKEND_PINNED=\nWIREGUARD_GO_SOURCE_PRESENT=\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=\nSELINUX_SOURCE=\nNO_SECRETS=\n\nUNRELATED_FILES_INCLUDED=\nSOURCE_COMMIT=\nSOURCE_TAG=wormos-wg-system-state\n\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=\nBUILD=\nWG_BACKEND=\nBACKEND_SOURCE_BUILD=\nBACKEND_PACKAGED=\nSELINUX=\n\nTARGET_FILES=\nOTA_BUILD=\nOTA_FILE=\nOTA_SHA256=\nUNRELATED_OTA_CONTENT=\n\nOTA_BUILD_TAG=wormos-wg-system-state-ota-built\nDEVICE_RUNTIME_VALIDATION=NOT_RUN\n\nSERVER_NETWORK=FROZEN_UNCHANGED\nBLOCKERS="}
