/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1071:{"session_id":"01a0824b-e5a1-7ed2-aacc-5eca7ff7c874","ts":1788914160,"text":"CONTINUE WORMOS WIREGUARD SYSTEM-STATE OTA\n\nGOAL:\n\nFinish materializing the clean Android checkout required for the\nWireGuard-system-state-only OTA.\n\nDo NOT build yet.\nDo NOT generate OTA yet.\nDo NOT modify WireGuard architecture.\nDo NOT restore unrelated WormOS customizations.\n\nCurrent authoritative state:\n\nANDROID_WORKSPACE=/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/android\nWORMOS_WORKTREE=/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/worm-os\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=535_OF_1108\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=PASS\nSELINUX_SOURCE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nOLD_ANDROID_REFERENCES=0\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES_STORAGE_ONLY\n\n============================================================\n1. MATERIALIZE THE REMAINING ANDROID PROJECTS\n============================================================\n\n571 manifest projects are still not fully materialized.\n\nUse the existing exact manifest/revision inventory and canonical upstream\nremotes to restore them.\n\nDo not change manifest revisions.\n\nDo not use latest/HEAD.\n\nFor every missing project:\n\n- identify canonical remote\n- identify exact required revision\n- fetch required objects\n- materialize project Git metadata\n- verify required commit resolves\n- verify checkout corresponds to recorded revision\n\nProcess all remaining projects rather than stopping after the first\nrecoverable fetch error.\n\nUse retries for transient network failures.\n\nMaintain a failure list for projects that remain unresolved.\n\n============================================================\n2. REPAIR external/scudo\n============================================================\n\nexternal/scudo was left incomplete by an interrupted exact-revision fetch.\n\nRepair it specifically.\n\nDetermine its exact manifest revision.\n\nFetch the required commit from its canonical remote.\n\nVerify:\n\ngit -C external/scudo rev-parse HEAD\ngit -C external/scudo cat-file -e <required-revision>^{commit}\n\nDo not substitute another revision.\n\nRequired:\n\nEXTERNAL_SCUDO=PASS\n\n============================================================\n3. REMOVE APPSTORE CUSTOMIZATION FROM THIS OTA\n============================================================\n\nexternal/AppStore currently points to:\n\n46afd57685afd18b99744ecbbf5e6c194c9005a3\n\nThis represents excluded App Store customization and MUST NOT enter the\nWireGuard-system-state-only OTA.\n\nDetermine the canonical GrapheneOS AppStore revision required by the exact\nAndroid manifest/base revision used for this checkout.\n\nRestore external/AppStore to that exact canonical revision.\n\nDo not guess.\nDo not use current upstream HEAD.\nDo not delete the project.\n\nRequired:\n\nAPPSTORE_SOURCE=CANONICAL_GRAPHENEOS_BASE\nAPPSTORE_CUSTOMIZATION_INCLUDED=NO\n\nDocument:\n\nAPPSTORE_PREVIOUS_REVISION=\nAPPSTORE_CANONICAL_REVISION=\nAPPSTORE_REMOTE=\n\n============================================================\n4. EXCLUDE ALL OTHER NON-WIREGUARD CUSTOMIZATIONS\n============================================================\n\nAudit the manifest/project state for other recovered WormOS customizations.\n\nFor this OTA, retain only:\n\n- minimum WormOS product/base integration required for the target\n- WormSystemWireGuard\n- official pinned WireGuard Android backend\n- source-built wireguard-go\n- WireGuard product/package integration\n- WireGuard boot/autostart integration\n- VPN lockdown/fail-closed integration\n- protected DNS integration\n- required existing SELinux-domain integration\n- WireGuard provenance\n\nExclude customization relating solely to:\n\n- AppStore\n- Proton\n- Bitwarden\n- Proton Drive\n- Material 3\n- launcher\n- dashboard/control\n- Augurri\n- installer\n- unrelated updater/OTA work\n- unrelated UI changes\n\nDo not remove upstream GrapheneOS functionality.\n\n============================================================\n5. VERIFY ALL 1108 PROJECTS\n============================================================\n\nAfter restoration, verify every manifest project.\n\nRequired:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_EXPECTED=1108\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nBROKEN_PROJECT_GIT_REPOS=0\nMISSING_PROJECTS=0\nBROKEN_SYMLINKS=0\nBROKEN_ALTERNATES=0\nOLD_ANDROID_REFERENCES=0\nMERGE_CONFLICTS=0\n\nDo not proceed if any project cannot resolve its exact required revision.\n\n============================================================\n6. WIREGUARD-ONLY DIFF GATE\n============================================================\n\nNow regenerate:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WIREGUARD-SYSTEM-STATE-OTA-DIFF.md\n\nCompare against the exact canonical GrapheneOS/WormOS base.\n\nClassify every non-upstream modification as:\n\nWIREGUARD_REQUIRED\nWORMOS_BASE_REQUIRED\nUNRELATED\n\nPrint every WORMOS_BASE_REQUIRED file explicitly.\n\nRequired:\n\nUNRELATED_FILES_INCLUDED=0\n\nIf any unrelated file remains, STOP and report it rather than silently\nincluding it.\n\n============================================================\n7. REVERIFY WIREGUARD STATE\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=PASS\n\nBACKEND_COMMIT=\ne7b3a3c118836e112620b1302a8ba1873ad4daac\n\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nWIREGUARD_GO_SOURCE_PRESENT=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=PASS\nSELINUX_SOURCE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\n============================================================\n8. STORAGE GATE\n============================================================\n\nAfter completing the repositories, recalculate actual disk usage.\n\nReport:\n\nFREE_SPACE=\nANDROID_WORKSPACE_SIZE=\nANDROID_REPO_OBJECTS_SIZE=\nESTIMATED_BUILD_REQUIREMENT=\nESTIMATED_POST_BUILD_MARGIN=\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=\n\nDo not compile if BUILD_SPACE_OK is no longer YES.\n\n============================================================\n9. PREPARE SOURCE CHECKPOINT — NO TAG YET\n============================================================\n\nBranch:\n\npatch/PATCH-WIREGUARD-OTA\n\nPlanned implementation tag:\n\nwormos-wg-system-state\n\nDo not create the tag yet.\n\nDo not commit until:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nUNRELATED_FILES_INCLUDED=0\n\n============================================================\n10. STOP AT BUILD GATE\n============================================================\n\nDO NOT RUN:\n\nm\nmm\nmmm\nninja\ntarget-files-package\nOTA generation\n\nFinal required result:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nEXTERNAL_SCUDO=PASS\nAPPSTORE_CUSTOMIZATION_INCLUDED=NO\nUNRELATED_FILES_INCLUDED=0\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=PASS\nSELINUX_SOURCE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES\n\nREADY_FOR_WG_SYSTEM_STATE_BUILD=YES\n\nFINAL REPORT:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_EXPECTED=\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=\nBROKEN_PROJECT_GIT_REPOS=\nMISSING_PROJECTS=\n\nEXTERNAL_SCUDO=\n\nAPPSTORE_PREVIOUS_REVISION=\nAPPSTORE_CANONICAL_REVISION=\nAPPSTORE_CUSTOMIZATION_INCLUDED=\n\nWIREGUARD_REQUIRED_FILES=\nWORMOS_BASE_REQUIRED_FILES=\nUNRELATED_FILES_INCLUDED=\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=\nBACKEND_COMMIT=\nBACKEND_PINNED=\nWIREGUARD_GO_SOURCE_PRESENT=\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=\nSELINUX_SOURCE=\nNO_SECRETS=\n\nFREE_SPACE=\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=\n\nBUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN\nREADY_FOR_WG_SYSTEM_STATE_BUILD=\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1073:{"session_id":"01a0824b-e5a1-7ed2-aacc-5eca7ff7c874","ts":1788933444,"text":"CONTINUE WORMOS WIREGUARD SYSTEM-STATE OTA\nUSING THE EXISTING ACCEPTED WORMOS BASELINE\n\nIMPORTANT CORRECTION:\n\nDo NOT reduce the source tree to vanilla GrapheneOS + WireGuard.\n\nThe existing WormOS baseline already contains accepted implementation state,\nincluding keys/config references and other accepted patches.\n\nThese accepted baseline changes must be preserved.\n\nThe goal of this OTA is:\n\nBASELINE = all previously accepted WormOS source state\nNEW IMPLEMENTATION DELTA = WireGuard system-state only\n\nDo not remove accepted baseline patches merely because they are unrelated to\nWireGuard.\n\n============================================================\n1. RECONSTRUCT THE ACCEPTED BASELINE\n============================================================\n\nUse the previously frozen/recovered WormOS checkpoint and accepted source\nstate as the baseline.\n\nAuthoritative checkpoint:\n\nwormos-prebuild-wg-backend-recovered\nf947156d418667ec6c9c654250b00f5aa32eb382\n\nInspect existing provenance/recovery reports under:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts\n/opt/worm/patches\n/opt/worm/worm-os\n/opt/worm/config\n/opt/worm/vendor\n\nDetermine exactly which changes were already accepted BEFORE this dedicated\nWireGuard OTA task.\n\nClassify each customization as:\n\nACCEPTED_BASELINE\nWIREGUARD_NEW_DELTA\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK\n\nDo not confuse ACCEPTED_BASELINE with unrelated dirty work.\n\n============================================================\n2. PRESERVE ACCEPTED KEYS / CONFIG INTEGRATION\n============================================================\n\nPreserve already accepted key/config integration and references required by\nWormOS.\n\nDo NOT expose or print secrets.\n\nDo NOT commit private key material if it is intentionally external/non-Git.\n\nVerify only the integration/reference state.\n\nClassify:\n\nKEY_CONFIG_INTEGRATION=ACCEPTED_BASELINE|MISSING|UNKNOWN\n\nDo not regenerate keys.\nDo not replace existing accepted keys/config.\nDo not copy secrets into source.\n\n============================================================\n3. PRESERVE OTHER ACCEPTED PATCHES\n============================================================\n\nPreserve accepted patches already part of the frozen WormOS baseline,\nincluding where previously accepted:\n\n- WormOS base/product changes\n- Material 3 checkpoint\n- WormOS App Store modifications\n- Proton integration\n- existing launcher/system changes\n- signing/config references\n- other already-tagged/accepted WormOS source modifications\n\nBitwarden / Proton Drive must only be present if they were already accepted\nin the frozen baseline.\n\nDo NOT revert accepted baseline modifications to upstream GrapheneOS merely\nto make the OTA \"WireGuard-only\".\n\n============================================================\n4. DEFINE WIREGUARD-ONLY DELTA CORRECTLY\n============================================================\n\nThe phrase \"WireGuard-only OTA\" means:\n\nthe NEW source implementation introduced by this checkpoint must be only the\nWireGuard system-state implementation.\n\nIt does NOT mean stripping previously accepted WormOS baseline features from\nthe image.\n\nWireGuard delta includes:\n\n- WormSystemWireGuard privileged/system component\n- official pinned WireGuard Android backend\n- source-built wireguard-go\n- Android VpnService integration\n- system lifecycle / boot autostart\n- lockdown / fail-closed\n- IPv4 / IPv6 protection\n- protected DNS integration\n- required routing / handover behavior\n- required product packaging\n- required privileged permissions\n- required SELinux integration\n- runtime provisioning interfaces\n- WireGuard provenance/build metadata\n\n============================================================\n5. REPAIR ANDROID REPO METADATA\n============================================================\n\nContinue repairing the isolated Android checkout:\n\n/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/android\n\nCurrent incomplete state must be brought to:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\n\nRestore exact Git objects/revisions without altering accepted baseline source\ncontent.\n\nUse Storage Box historical repo metadata/object stores where possible.\n\nCanonical upstream fetches are allowed for missing exact objects.\n\nDo not reset accepted baseline modifications.\n\n============================================================\n6. DO NOT REVERT ACCEPTED APPSTORE OR OTHER BASELINE PATCHES\n============================================================\n\nexternal/AppStore and other customized projects must be evaluated against the\nACCEPTED WORMOS BASELINE, not vanilla GrapheneOS.\n\nIf AppStore customization existed in the accepted baseline:\n\nAPPSTORE_CLASSIFICATION=ACCEPTED_BASELINE\n\nand it must remain.\n\nOnly classify AppStore as unrelated if evidence proves it was unaccepted\ndirty work.\n\nDo not automatically restore it to upstream.\n\n============================================================\n7. GENERATE TWO DIFFS\n============================================================\n\nGenerate:\n\nA. BASELINE DIFF\n   accepted WormOS baseline vs canonical GrapheneOS base\n\nB. WIREGUARD DELTA DIFF\n   WireGuard-system-state checkpoint vs accepted WormOS baseline\n\nReports:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WORMOS-ACCEPTED-BASELINE.md\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WIREGUARD-SYSTEM-STATE-DELTA.md\n\nFor every changed file classify:\n\nACCEPTED_BASELINE\nWIREGUARD_NEW_DELTA\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK\n\nRequired before build:\n\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\n\n============================================================\n8. VERIFY EXISTING TAG HISTORY\n============================================================\n\nInspect existing WormOS tags and commits.\n\nUse them as evidence for accepted implementations.\n\nDo not move any existing tag.\n\nReport:\n\nEXISTING_ACCEPTED_TAGS=\nBASELINE_COMMIT=\nBASELINE_TAG=\n\nThe dedicated new tag remains:\n\nwormos-wg-system-state\n\n============================================================\n9. SOURCE GATE\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\n\nACCEPTED_BASELINE_RECONSTRUCTED=PASS\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\n\nKEY_CONFIG_INTEGRATION=PASS\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nWIREGUARD_GO_SOURCE_PRESENT=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=PASS\nSELINUX_SOURCE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\n============================================================\n10. TAG ONLY THE WIREGUARD IMPLEMENTATION CHECKPOINT\n============================================================\n\nAfter source gate passes:\n\ncommit the resulting accepted baseline + WireGuard system-state source.\n\nCommit message:\n\nWormOS: add WireGuard system-state integration\n\nCreate annotated tag:\n\nwormos-wg-system-state\n\nThe tag means:\n\n\"accepted WormOS baseline plus newly completed WireGuard system-state\"\n\nIt does NOT mean the image contains only WireGuard and no other previously\naccepted WormOS features.\n\n============================================================\n11. BUILD / OTA\n============================================================\n\nOnly after source gate:\n\nBuild using:\n\nANDROID_BUILD_TOP=/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/android\nOUT_DIR=/opt/worm/build-wg/out\nTMPDIR=/opt/worm/build-wg/tmp\n\nBuild:\n\n1. wireguard-go\n2. WormSystemWireGuard\n3. affected platform/product components\n4. target-files-package\n5. OTA\n\n============================================================\n12. OTA VALIDATION\n============================================================\n\nVerify:\n\n- all accepted WormOS baseline features remain present\n- WireGuard system-state is newly included\n- no unaccepted dirty work entered the image\n- no secrets embedded\n- SELinux passes\n- backend packaged\n- target-files match source checkpoint\n\nCreate:\n\nwormos-wg-system-state-ota-built\n\npointing to the same source commit.\n\n============================================================\nFINAL REPORT\n============================================================\n\nACCEPTED_BASELINE_RECONSTRUCTED=\nBASELINE_COMMIT=\nBASELINE_TAG=\nEXISTING_ACCEPTED_TAGS=\n\nKEY_CONFIG_INTEGRATION=\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=\n\nACCEPTED_BASELINE_FILES=\nWIREGUARD_NEW_DELTA_FILES=\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=\nBACKEND_PINNED=\nWIREGUARD_GO_SOURCE_PRESENT=\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=\nSELINUX_SOURCE=\nNO_SECRETS=\n\nSOURCE_COMMIT=\nSOURCE_TAG=wormos-wg-system-state\n\nBUILD=\nTARGET_FILES=\nOTA_BUILD=\nOTA_FILE=\nOTA_SHA256=\n\nOTA_BUILD_TAG=wormos-wg-system-state-ota-built\nDEVICE_RUNTIME_VALIDATION=NOT_RUN\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1074:{"session_id":"01a0824b-e5a1-7ed2-aacc-5eca7ff7c874","ts":1788934715,"text":"START PREBUILD STORAGE OPTIMIZATION FOR WIREGUARD SYSTEM-STATE\n\nCURRENT SOURCE STATE IS VERIFIED AND MUST NOT BE RECONSTRUCTED AGAIN.\n\nAuthoritative state:\n\nACCEPTED_BASELINE_RECONSTRUCTED=PASS\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nBROKEN_PROJECT_GIT_REPOS=0\nMISSING_PROJECTS=0\nBROKEN_REPO_METADATA_SYMLINKS=0\nBROKEN_ALTERNATES=0\nOLD_ANDROID_REFERENCES=0\nMERGE_CONFLICTS=0\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nWIREGUARD_GO_SOURCE_PRESENT=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=PASS\nSELINUX_SOURCE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nCURRENT BLOCKER:\n\nFREE_SPACE=167G\nANDROID_WORKSPACE_SIZE=229G\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=NO\n\nDO NOT BUILD YET.\nDO NOT DELETE OR RECONSTRUCT THE VERIFIED ANDROID CHECKOUT.\n\n============================================================\n1. PROTECT VERIFIED SOURCE\n============================================================\n\nTreat as immutable for storage-cleanup purposes:\n\n/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/android\n/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/worm-os\n/opt/worm/patches\n/opt/worm/manifests\n/opt/worm/vendor\n/opt/worm/config\n/opt/worm/artifacts/provenance\n\nDo not delete repo objects from the verified Android checkout.\n\nDo not recreate /opt/worm/src/android.\n\n============================================================\n2. FULL STORAGE AUDIT\n============================================================\n\nAudit filesystem usage without deleting anything.\n\nInspect:\n\ndf -h\ndf -i\nfindmnt\n\ndu -xhd1 /opt/worm\ndu -xhd2 /opt/worm/build-wg\ndu -xhd2 /opt/worm/cache\ndu -xhd2 /opt/worm/backups\ndu -xhd2 /opt/worm/artifacts\ndu -xhd2 /opt/worm/worktrees\n\nAlso inspect:\n\n/tmp\n/var/tmp\n/var/cache\n/mnt/worm-build\n\nIdentify the largest reclaimable consumers.\n\nClassify each as:\n\nVERIFIED_SOURCE_DO_NOT_DELETE\nPERSISTENT_ARTIFACT\nDISPOSABLE_BUILD_OUTPUT\nCACHE_REGENERABLE\nTEMPORARY\nBACKUP\nUNKNOWN\n\nGenerate:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WIREGUARD-PREBUILD-STORAGE-AUDIT.md\n\n============================================================\n3. INSPECT /mnt/worm-build\n============================================================\n\nDetermine exactly what /mnt/worm-build is.\n\nReport:\n\nWORM_BUILD_MOUNT_TYPE=\nWORM_BUILD_FILESYSTEM=\nWORM_BUILD_SIZE=\nWORM_BUILD_FREE=\nWORM_BUILD_PERSISTENCE=\nWORM_BUILD_SAME_FILESYSTEM_AS_ROOT=\nWORM_BUILD_SUITABLE_FOR_OUT_DIR=\n\nCheck performance/permissions and whether it supports the filesystem\nsemantics required by Android builds.\n\nDo not assume it is suitable merely because it exists.\n\nIf it is tmpfs/RAM-backed, explicitly report that and DO NOT use it for the\nfull Android OUT_DIR unless capacity is genuinely sufficient.\n\n============================================================\n4. AUDIT build-wg\n============================================================\n\nInspect:\n\n/opt/worm/build-wg\n\nDetermine whether it contains build output from aborted/previous attempts.\n\nSince BUILD=NOT_RUN for the current verified source state, identify anything\ninside build-wg that is safely regenerable.\n\nReport:\n\nBUILD_WG_SIZE=\nBUILD_WG_DISPOSABLE_SIZE=\nBUILD_WG_SAFE_TO_CLEAN=\n\nDo not delete until classified.\n\n============================================================\n5. AUDIT DUPLICATE REPO OBJECT STORAGE\n============================================================\n\nThe Android workspace is 229G.\n\nDetermine how much is:\n\nWORKING_FILES=\nREPO_PROJECT_OBJECTS=\nREPO_PROJECTS_METADATA=\nDUPLICATE_OBJECTS=\nOTHER=\n\nCheck whether object storage exists redundantly under:\n\n/opt/worm/cache/android-repo\n/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/android/.repo/project-objects\n/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/android/.repo/projects\n\nDo NOT delete Git objects required by the verified checkout.\n\nIf exact duplicate object stores exist and one can be removed while leaving\nthe checkout completely self-contained and verifiable, document the safe\nstrategy first.\n\n============================================================\n6. SAFE CLEANUP\n============================================================\n\nAutomatically clean only items classified with high confidence as:\n\nTEMPORARY\nCACHE_REGENERABLE\nDISPOSABLE_BUILD_OUTPUT\n\nNever automatically delete:\n\nVERIFIED_SOURCE_DO_NOT_DELETE\nPERSISTENT_ARTIFACT\nBACKUP\nUNKNOWN\n\nPreserve reports/provenance.\n\nAfter cleanup run:\n\ndf -h\ndf -i\n\nReport:\n\nSPACE_BEFORE=\nSPACE_RECLAIMED=\nSPACE_AFTER=\nFILESYSTEM_FREE_AFTER=\n\n============================================================\n7. RECHECK SOURCE AFTER CLEANUP\n============================================================\n\nThis is mandatory.\n\nAfter any cleanup verify again:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nBROKEN_PROJECT_GIT_REPOS=0\nMISSING_PROJECTS=0\nBROKEN_ALTERNATES=0\nMERGE_CONFLICTS=0\n\nAlso verify:\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nIf source verification regresses:\n\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n8. RECALCULATE BUILD REQUIREMENT\n============================================================\n\nDo not simply reuse the previous generic \"200G+\" estimate.\n\nUse historical build information under /opt/worm reports/backups where\navailable and calculate:\n\nEXPECTED_OUT_DIR_PEAK=\nTARGET_FILES_OVERHEAD=\nOTA_OVERHEAD=\nTEMP_OVERHEAD=\nSAFETY_MARGIN=\nTOTAL_REQUIRED_FREE=\n\nThen report:\n\nFREE_SPACE=\nTOTAL_REQUIRED_FREE=\nESTIMATED_POST_BUILD_FREE=\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=\n\n============================================================\n9. PREBUILD GATE\n============================================================\n\nIf sufficient storage is available, rerun the complete mandatory pre-build\ncheck.\n\nRequired:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=PASS\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=PASS\nSELINUX_SOURCE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nBUILD_ENV=PASS\nGIT_STATE=PASS\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES\n\nThen:\n\nPREBUILD_GATE=PASS\n\nOtherwise:\n\nPREBUILD_GATE=FAIL\nBUILD=NOT_STARTED\n\n============================================================\n10. STOP BEFORE BUILD\n============================================================\n\nEven if PREBUILD_GATE=PASS, STOP at this point.\n\nDo NOT compile in this task.\n\nDo NOT generate target-files.\nDo NOT generate OTA.\n\nWe want explicit confirmation of PREBUILD_GATE=PASS before starting the\nexpensive build.\n\nFINAL REPORT:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=\n\nSPACE_BEFORE=\nSPACE_RECLAIMED=\nSPACE_AFTER=\n\nANDROID_WORKSPACE_SIZE=\nWORKING_FILES=\nREPO_PROJECT_OBJECTS=\nDUPLICATE_OBJECTS=\n\nWORM_BUILD_MOUNT_TYPE=\nWORM_BUILD_SIZE=\nWORM_BUILD_FREE=\nWORM_BUILD_SUITABLE_FOR_OUT_DIR=\n\nBUILD_WG_SIZE=\nBUILD_WG_DISPOSABLE_SIZE=\n\nEXPECTED_OUT_DIR_PEAK=\nTARGET_FILES_OVERHEAD=\nOTA_OVERHEAD=\nTEMP_OVERHEAD=\nSAFETY_MARGIN=\nTOTAL_REQUIRED_FREE=\nESTIMATED_POST_BUILD_FREE=\n\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=\nBUILD_ENV=\nGIT_STATE=\nPREBUILD_GATE=\n\nBUILD=NOT_STARTED\nOTA=NOT_STARTED\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1075:{"session_id":"01a084d5-062d-7302-868d-6ea30c803e46","ts":1788934952,"text":"NORMALIZE WORMOS TO SINGLE /opt/worm ROOT\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nUse /opt/worm as the single canonical root for all WormOS source, build,\nartifacts, caches and tooling.\n\nABSOLUTE RULE:\n\n/opt/Android must not exist or be referenced anywhere.\n\nDo NOT build yet.\n\n============================================================\n1. CANONICAL PATHS\n============================================================\n\nSet:\n\nWORM_ROOT=/opt/worm\nANDROID_BUILD_TOP=/opt/worm/src/android\nOUT_DIR=/opt/worm/build/out\nTMPDIR=/opt/worm/build/tmp\nBUILD_LOGS=/opt/worm/build/logs\nTARGET_FILES_DIR=/opt/worm/build/target-files\nOTA_DIR=/opt/worm/build/ota\nCACHE_DIR=/opt/worm/cache\nARTIFACT_DIR=/opt/worm/artifacts\n\n============================================================\n2. CONSOLIDATE VERIFIED ANDROID CHECKOUT\n============================================================\n\nCurrent verified WireGuard checkout:\n\n/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/android\n\nThis checkout is currently the authoritative verified Android source state.\n\nMove or relocate it safely to:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android\n\nDo not duplicate the 229G tree.\n\nPrefer filesystem rename/move on the same filesystem.\n\nBefore moving, verify:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nBROKEN_PROJECT_GIT_REPOS=0\nMISSING_PROJECTS=0\nBROKEN_ALTERNATES=0\nMERGE_CONFLICTS=0\n\nAfter moving, rerun the same checks.\n\n============================================================\n3. REMOVE OLD PATH REFERENCES\n============================================================\n\nSearch all of /opt/worm for references to:\n\n/opt/Android\n/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/android\n/opt/worm/src/android.old\n\nUpdate only project/tooling references that must point to the new canonical\npath:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android\n\nDo not modify historical reports merely to rewrite history unless they are\nactive configuration files.\n\nReport:\n\nOLD_OPT_ANDROID_REFERENCES=\nOLD_WG_ANDROID_PATH_REFERENCES=\n\nActive configuration references must be zero.\n\n============================================================\n4. BUILD DIRECTORY\n============================================================\n\nUse only:\n\n/opt/worm/build/out\n/opt/worm/build/tmp\n/opt/worm/build/logs\n/opt/worm/build/target-files\n/opt/worm/build/ota\n\nDo not use:\n\n/opt/worm/build-wg\n/mnt/worm-build\n\nunless explicitly approved later.\n\nAudit /opt/worm/build-wg.\n\nIf it contains no unique persistent artifacts, classify it as disposable.\n\nDo not delete until verified safe.\n\n============================================================\n5. ENVIRONMENT FILE\n============================================================\n\nCreate/update:\n\n/opt/worm/config/build/env.sh\n\nwith:\n\nexport WORM_ROOT=/opt/worm\nexport ANDROID_BUILD_TOP=/opt/worm/src/android\nexport OUT_DIR=/opt/worm/build/out\nexport TMPDIR=/opt/worm/build/tmp\n\nDo not include secrets.\n\n============================================================\n6. SCRIPTS\n============================================================\n\nUpdate active WormOS build/OTA/validation scripts under /opt/worm/scripts\nso they use only canonical /opt/worm paths.\n\nReject any active use of /opt/Android.\n\n============================================================\n7. VERIFY SINGLE ROOT\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\ntest ! -e /opt/Android\n\nAll active source/build paths must resolve under:\n\n/opt/worm\n\nReport:\n\nWORM_ROOT=\nANDROID_BUILD_TOP=\nOUT_DIR=\nTMPDIR=\nOPT_ANDROID_EXISTS=\nACTIVE_PATHS_OUTSIDE_WORM=\n\nRequired:\n\nOPT_ANDROID_EXISTS=NO\nACTIVE_PATHS_OUTSIDE_WORM=0\n\n============================================================\n8. REVERIFY WIREGUARD SOURCE\n============================================================\n\nAfter relocation verify:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=PASS\nSELINUX_SOURCE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\n============================================================\n9. STORAGE CHECK\n============================================================\n\nRun:\n\ndf -h\ndf -i\ndu -sh /opt/worm/src/android\ndu -sh /opt/worm/build\ndu -sh /opt/worm/cache\ndu -sh /opt/worm/artifacts\n\nReport:\n\nFREE_SPACE=\nANDROID_SOURCE_SIZE=\nBUILD_SIZE=\nCACHE_SIZE=\nARTIFACT_SIZE=\n\n============================================================\n10. NO BUILD\n============================================================\n\nBUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN\n\nFinal required state:\n\nSINGLE_WORM_ROOT=PASS\nANDROID_BUILD_TOP=/opt/worm/src/android\nOPT_ANDROID_EXISTS=NO\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nREADY_FOR_PREBUILD_CHECK=YES"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1076:{"session_id":"01a084d5-062d-7302-868d-6ea30c803e46","ts":1788935366,"text":"MANDATORY PRE-BUILD CHECK\n\nCondition to build:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=EXPECTED_TOTAL\nBROKEN_PROJECT_GIT_REPOS=0\nMISSING_PROJECTS=0\nBROKEN_SYMLINKS=0\nBROKEN_ALTERNATES=0\nMERGE_CONFLICTS=0\n\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=PASS\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=PASS\nSELINUX_SOURCE=PASS\n\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nBUILD_ENV=PASS\nGIT_STATE=PASS\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES\n\nWORM_ROOT=/opt/worm\nANDROID_BUILD_TOP=/opt/worm/src/android\nOUT_DIR=/opt/worm/build/out\nTMPDIR=/opt/worm/build/tmp\n\nOPT_ANDROID_EXISTS=NO\nACTIVE_PATHS_OUTSIDE_WORM=0\n\nONLY THEN:\n\nPREBUILD_GATE=PASS"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1077:{"session_id":"01a084d5-062d-7302-868d-6ea30c803e46","ts":1788935686,"text":"RESUME WORMOS WG SYSTEM-STATE PREBUILD\n\nMANDATORY PRE-BUILD GATE REMAINS ENFORCED.\n\nCurrent blocker:\n\nBROKEN_SYMLINKS=46\n\nEverything else currently passes.\n\nDO NOT BUILD.\nDO NOT GENERATE OTA.\nDO NOT RESET SOURCE.\nDO NOT DELETE ACCEPTED BASELINE FILES.\n\n============================================================\n1. INVENTORY ALL 46 SYMLINKS\n============================================================\n\nInspect every currently classified broken symlink under:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android\n\nFor every symlink record:\n\nPATH=\nTARGET=\nABSOLUTE_OR_RELATIVE=\nOWNER_PROJECT=\nTRACKED_BY_GIT=\nEXPECTED_BY_PROJECT_REVISION=\nREQUIRED_FOR_BUILD=\nCLASSIFICATION=\n\nClassification must be exactly one of:\n\nVALID_DANGLING_SOURCE_SYMLINK\nBROKEN_REPO_METADATA\nSTALE_OLD_PATH_REFERENCE\nMISSING_CHECKOUT_CONTENT\nBROKEN_WORMOS_INTEGRATION\nUNKNOWN\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/PREBUILD-BROKEN-SYMLINK-AUDIT.md\n\n============================================================\n2. DISTINGUISH VALID DANGLING SYMLINKS\n============================================================\n\nDo not assume every dangling symlink is a build blocker.\n\nFor Git-tracked symlinks, inspect the exact pinned project revision and\ndetermine whether the symlink itself is part of the canonical source tree.\n\nIf a dangling symlink is intentionally present in the exact accepted\nupstream/baseline revision and is not required to resolve during this build:\n\nCLASSIFICATION=VALID_DANGLING_SOURCE_SYMLINK\n\nSuch a link must NOT count as BROKEN_SYMLINKS in the pre-build gate.\n\nTrack separately:\n\nVALID_DANGLING_SYMLINKS=\n\n============================================================\n3. FIND STALE PATH REFERENCES\n============================================================\n\nPay particular attention to symlinks targeting old locations such as:\n\n/opt/Android\n/opt/worm/worktrees/wg-ota/android\n/opt/worm/src/android.old\ndeleted .repo/project-objects paths\ndeleted cache paths\n\nRequired:\n\nSTALE_OPT_ANDROID_SYMLINKS=0\nSTALE_WG_WORKTREE_SYMLINKS=0\n\nRepair stale metadata links only when the correct canonical target can be\nproven.\n\nCanonical source root is:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android\n\n============================================================\n4. CHECK .repo METADATA SEPARATELY\n============================================================\n\nAudit:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android/.repo/project-objects\n/opt/worm/src/android/.repo/projects\n\nand project Git metadata.\n\nVerify:\n\nBROKEN_REPO_METADATA_SYMLINKS=0\nBROKEN_ALTERNATES=0\nMISSING_GIT_OBJECTS=0\n\nDo not alter working source merely to repair repo metadata.\n\n============================================================\n5. REPAIR ONLY PROVEN BROKEN LINKS\n============================================================\n\nFor each genuinely broken symlink:\n\n- establish expected target from exact Git revision, manifest, accepted\n  baseline, or recovered provenance;\n- repair only when target is unambiguous;\n- do not invent targets;\n- do not replace symlinks with copied files unless the canonical source\n  explicitly requires that;\n- do not fetch latest/HEAD.\n\nIf required checkout content is missing, restore the exact pinned content.\n\nUNKNOWN links remain blockers.\n\n============================================================\n6. REVERIFY 1108 PROJECTS\n============================================================\n\nAfter repairs:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nBROKEN_PROJECT_GIT_REPOS=0\nMISSING_PROJECTS=0\nBROKEN_ALTERNATES=0\nMERGE_CONFLICTS=0\n\nAlso confirm:\n\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\n\nDo not count repair changes as accepted automatically.\nAny new source modification must be classified.\n\n============================================================\n7. REDEFINE SYMLINK PREBUILD METRIC CORRECTLY\n============================================================\n\nReport separately:\n\nTOTAL_DANGLING_SYMLINKS=\nVALID_DANGLING_SYMLINKS=\nGENUINELY_BROKEN_SYMLINKS=\nUNKNOWN_SYMLINKS=\n\nThe hard gate condition is:\n\nGENUINELY_BROKEN_SYMLINKS=0\nUNKNOWN_SYMLINKS=0\n\nDo not fail the build solely because an exact upstream source revision\ncontains an intentional dangling symlink.\n\n============================================================\n8. RERUN COMPLETE MANDATORY PREBUILD\n============================================================\n\nAfter symlink audit/repair rerun ALL gates, not just symlinks.\n\nRequired:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nBROKEN_PROJECT_GIT_REPOS=0\nMISSING_PROJECTS=0\nBROKEN_ALTERNATES=0\nMERGE_CONFLICTS=0\n\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=PASS\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=PASS\nSELINUX_SOURCE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nBUILD_ENV=PASS\nGIT_STATE=PASS\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES\n\nWORM_ROOT=/opt/worm\nANDROID_BUILD_TOP=/opt/worm/src/android\nOUT_DIR=/opt/worm/build/out\nTMPDIR=/opt/worm/build/tmp\n\nOPT_ANDROID_EXISTS=NO\nACTIVE_PATHS_OUTSIDE_WORM=0\n\nGENUINELY_BROKEN_SYMLINKS=0\nUNKNOWN_SYMLINKS=0\n\n============================================================\n9. HARD STOP\n============================================================\n\nIf every condition passes:\n\nPREBUILD_GATE=PASS\n\nbut STILL:\n\nBUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN\n\nStop and report PASS.\n\nIf anything fails:\n\nPREBUILD_GATE=FAIL\nBUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN\n\n============================================================\nFINAL REPORT\n============================================================\n\nTOTAL_DANGLING_SYMLINKS=\nVALID_DANGLING_SYMLINKS=\nGENUINELY_BROKEN_SYMLINKS=\nUNKNOWN_SYMLINKS=\n\nSTALE_OPT_ANDROID_SYMLINKS=\nSTALE_WG_WORKTREE_SYMLINKS=\nBROKEN_REPO_METADATA_SYMLINKS=\nBROKEN_ALTERNATES=\nMISSING_GIT_OBJECTS=\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=\nBACKEND_PINNED=\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=\nSELINUX_SOURCE=\nNO_SECRETS=\n\nBUILD_ENV=\nGIT_STATE=\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=\n\nOPT_ANDROID_EXISTS=\nACTIVE_PATHS_OUTSIDE_WORM=\n\nPREBUILD_GATE=\nBUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1078:{"session_id":"01a084d5-062d-7302-868d-6ea30c803e46","ts":1788936557,"text":"START WORMOS WG SYSTEM-STATE BUILD\n\nEXPLICIT AUTHORIZATION:\n\nThe mandatory pre-build gate has passed.\n\nCurrent authoritative result:\n\nPREBUILD_GATE=PASS\nBLOCKERS=NONE\n\nCanonical paths:\n\nWORM_ROOT=/opt/worm\nANDROID_BUILD_TOP=/opt/worm/src/android\nOUT_DIR=/opt/worm/build/out\nTMPDIR=/opt/worm/build/tmp\n\nABSOLUTE RULE:\n\n/opt/Android must not exist or be used.\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nBuild and package the accepted WormOS baseline plus the WireGuard\nsystem-state implementation.\n\nDo not introduce any additional implementation.\n\n============================================================\n0. PRE-BUILD CHECK IS MANDATORY BEFORE EVERY BUILD STAGE\n============================================================\n\nThe previous PASS authorizes entering the build workflow, but does NOT\ndisable subsequent gates.\n\nImmediately before EACH stage below rerun the mandatory pre-build check.\n\nStages:\n\nA. wireguard-go\nB. WormSystemWireGuard\nC. affected platform/product build\nD. target-files-package\nE. OTA generation\n\nFor every stage write a separate immutable report:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/PREBUILD-WG-<stage>-<timestamp>.md\n\nRequired every time:\n\nPREBUILD_GATE=PASS\n\nIf any stage returns anything other than PASS:\n\nSTOP\nBUILD_STAGE_NOT_STARTED\n\nDo not continue to the next stage.\n\n============================================================\n1. FREEZE SOURCE STATE\n============================================================\n\nBefore compiling record:\n\nSOURCE_BRANCH=\nSOURCE_HEAD=\nBASELINE_TAG=\nBACKEND_COMMIT=\n\nRecord complete approved dirty/baseline state.\n\nDo not reset the 17 accepted baseline files.\n\nDo not modify accepted baseline merely to obtain a clean git status.\n\nVerify again:\n\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\n\n============================================================\n2. CREATE WIREGUARD SOURCE CHECKPOINT\n============================================================\n\nCreate the implementation commit/tag only if doing so can preserve the\naccepted baseline correctly without accidentally committing secrets or\nunrelated state.\n\nTarget annotated tag:\n\nwormos-wg-system-state\n\nTag meaning:\n\naccepted WormOS baseline + WireGuard system-state source implementation.\n\nRun secret scan immediately before commit/tag.\n\nNever move an existing published tag.\n\nReport:\n\nSOURCE_COMMIT=\nSOURCE_TAG=\nTAG_TARGET=\n\n============================================================\n3. STAGE A — WIREGUARD-GO\n============================================================\n\nRERUN PREBUILD CHECK.\n\nOnly if PASS:\n\nBuild the pinned wireguard-go backend from source.\n\nExpected pinned backend revision:\n\ne7b3a3c118836e112620b1302a8ba1873ad4daac\n\nVerify resulting architecture/product artifact.\n\nRequired:\n\nWIREGUARD_GO_BUILD=PASS\n\nIf FAIL:\n\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n4. STAGE B — WormSystemWireGuard\n============================================================\n\nRERUN PREBUILD CHECK.\n\nThe pre-build checker must understand that expected generated output from\nStage A is not source contamination.\n\nOnly if PASS:\n\nBuild WormSystemWireGuard.\n\nVerify:\n\n- APK built\n- expected privileged/system packaging\n- libwg-go linkage/packaging\n- no user-facing WireGuard app dependency\n\nRequired:\n\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_BUILD=PASS\n\nIf FAIL:\n\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n5. STAGE C — AFFECTED PRODUCT/PLATFORM\n============================================================\n\nRERUN PREBUILD CHECK.\n\nExpected generated build output from A/B must not be classified as dirty\nsource.\n\nOnly if PASS:\n\nBuild the minimum affected product/platform targets required for the final\ntarget-files package.\n\nDo not introduce unrelated source changes.\n\nRequired:\n\nPRODUCT_BUILD=PASS\n\nIf FAIL:\n\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n6. STAGE D — TARGET-FILES\n============================================================\n\nRERUN PREBUILD CHECK.\n\nAlso check storage again because this stage may require substantial\ntemporary space.\n\nRequired before starting:\n\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES\n\nOnly if PASS:\n\nBuild target-files-package.\n\nAfter completion inspect target-files and prove presence of:\n\n- WormSystemWireGuard.apk\n- source-built libwg-go.so\n- required WireGuard backend components\n- privileged permissions/product declarations\n- boot/autostart integration\n- fail-closed integration\n- protected DNS integration\n- expected SELinux domain/policy state\n\nRequired:\n\nTARGET_FILES_BUILD=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_PACKAGED=PASS\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG_PACKAGED=PASS\nSELINUX=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nIf any fail:\n\nSTOP.\nDO NOT GENERATE OTA.\n\n============================================================\n7. TARGET-FILES SCOPE AUDIT\n============================================================\n\nBefore OTA generation compare the resulting target-files against the\naccepted baseline and WireGuard system-state scope.\n\nGenerate:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WIREGUARD-SYSTEM-STATE-TARGETFILES-AUDIT.md\n\nClassify changes:\n\nACCEPTED_BASELINE\nWIREGUARD_SYSTEM_STATE\nUNACCEPTED\n\nRequired:\n\nUNACCEPTED_TARGETFILES_CONTENT=0\n\nIf not zero:\n\nSTOP.\nDO NOT GENERATE OTA.\n\n============================================================\n8. STAGE E — OTA\n============================================================\n\nRERUN THE FULL PREBUILD CHECK AGAIN.\n\nAdditionally require:\n\nTARGET_FILES_BUILD=PASS\nUNACCEPTED_TARGETFILES_CONTENT=0\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES\n\nOnly then generate the OTA.\n\nStore final artifacts persistently under:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/releases/wireguard-system-state/\n/opt/worm/artifacts/target-files/\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/\n/opt/worm/artifacts/provenance/\n\nRecord:\n\nOTA_FILE=\nOTA_SHA256=\nOTA_SIZE=\nTARGET_FILES=\nBUILD_TIMESTAMP=\n\n============================================================\n9. OTA BUILD TAG\n============================================================\n\nOnly after OTA build + package verification passes create annotated tag:\n\nwormos-wg-system-state-ota-built\n\nIt must point to the exact same SOURCE_COMMIT as:\n\nwormos-wg-system-state\n\nVerify both peeled tag targets.\n\nDo not create runtime-pass tag.\n\n============================================================\n10. POST-BUILD VALIDATION\n============================================================\n\nRun:\n\n- secret scan\n- target-files inspection\n- OTA integrity/hash\n- provenance verification\n- backend revision verification\n- package presence verification\n- SELinux build result\n- source state verification\n\nRequired:\n\nBUILD=PASS\nTARGET_FILES_BUILD=PASS\nOTA_BUILD=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nPhysical-device tests remain:\n\nDEVICE_RUNTIME_VALIDATION=NOT_RUN\n\n============================================================\n11. NEVER AUTO-CLEAN ON FAILURE\n============================================================\n\nIf any build stage fails:\n\n- preserve logs\n- preserve exact source state\n- preserve OUT_DIR unless disk safety requires intervention\n- report the exact blocker\n- do not git reset\n- do not git clean\n- do not delete source\n- do not retry with changed source automatically\n\nFixes require a new mandatory PREBUILD_GATE before retry.\n\n============================================================\nFINAL REPORT\n============================================================\n\nSOURCE_BRANCH=\nSOURCE_COMMIT=\nSOURCE_TAG=wormos-wg-system-state\nTAG_TARGET=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_A=\nWIREGUARD_GO_BUILD=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_B=\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_BUILD=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_C=\nPRODUCT_BUILD=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_D=\nTARGET_FILES_BUILD=\nWG_BACKEND_PACKAGED=\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG_PACKAGED=\nSELINUX=\n\nUNACCEPTED_TARGETFILES_CONTENT=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_E=\nOTA_BUILD=\nOTA_FILE=\nOTA_SHA256=\nOTA_SIZE=\n\nOTA_BUILD_TAG=wormos-wg-system-state-ota-built\nOTA_BUILD_TAG_TARGET=\n\nNO_SECRETS=\nDEVICE_RUNTIME_VALIDATION=NOT_RUN\n\nBUILD=\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1079:{"session_id":"01a084d5-062d-7302-868d-6ea30c803e46","ts":1788936975,"text":"START FIX: WORMOS ANDROID GO PREBUILT FOR WG STAGE A\n\nCURRENT STATE\n\nMandatory pre-build policy remains active.\n\nPrevious result:\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_A=PASS\nWIREGUARD_GO_BUILD=FAIL\n\nExact blocker:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android/prebuilts/go/linux-x86/src\n\nis missing/incomplete.\n\nAndroid bootstrap fails because Go standard library source packages such as:\n\nbytes\nfmt\nos\ntime\n\ncannot be found.\n\nDO NOT run Stage B/C/D/E.\nDO NOT generate OTA.\nDO NOT install or substitute host/system Go.\nDO NOT use latest/HEAD.\nDO NOT change WireGuard source.\nDO NOT reset accepted WormOS baseline.\n\nCanonical root:\n\n/opt/worm\n\nAndroid source:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android\n\n============================================================\n1. AUDIT EXACT ANDROID GO PROJECT\n============================================================\n\nInspect:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android/prebuilts/go/linux-x86\n\nDetermine:\n\nPROJECT_PATH=\nMANIFEST_PROJECT=\nCANONICAL_REMOTE=\nPINNED_REVISION=\nCURRENT_HEAD=\nCURRENT_GIT_STATUS=\n\nVerify whether:\n\nsrc/\nbin/\npkg/\n\nexist and whether the checkout is complete for the exact pinned revision.\n\nRun equivalent Git object checks for the required revision.\n\nReport:\n\nGO_PROJECT_GIT_VALID=\nGO_PINNED_REVISION_PRESENT=\nGO_STDLIB_SRC_PRESENT=\nGO_STDLIB_SRC_COMPLETE=\n\nDo not modify anything yet.\n\n============================================================\n2. COMPARE AGAINST PINNED REVISION\n============================================================\n\nInspect the exact Git tree for the pinned commit.\n\nDetermine whether the pinned revision itself contains:\n\nsrc/bytes\nsrc/fmt\nsrc/os\nsrc/time\n\nand the rest of the Go standard library source required by Android bootstrap.\n\nIf the exact pinned commit contains these paths but the working checkout does\nnot:\n\nclassify:\n\nGO_PREBUILT_STATE=INCOMPLETE_CHECKOUT\n\nIf the required source is absent from the pinned commit itself:\n\nSTOP and report the manifest/toolchain inconsistency.\n\nDo NOT fetch a newer Go revision.\n\n============================================================\n3. RESTORE EXACT MISSING CONTENT\n============================================================\n\nIf incomplete checkout is confirmed, restore only the exact project content\nfrom its pinned revision.\n\nPreferred sources, in order:\n\n1. existing local Git objects;\n2. Storage Box historical Android backup, read-only;\n3. canonical Android/GrapheneOS remote for the exact pinned revision.\n\nDo not restore an entire old Android tree.\n\nDo not restore build output.\n\nDo not use another Go version.\n\nRequired result:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android/prebuilts/go/linux-x86/src\n\nmust correspond exactly to the pinned project revision.\n\n============================================================\n4. VERIFY GO TOOLCHAIN CONSISTENCY\n============================================================\n\nAfter restoration verify:\n\nGO_BIN_PRESENT=\nGO_VERSION=\nGO_ROOT=\nGO_STDLIB_SRC_PRESENT=\nGO_STDLIB_PACKAGES_CHECK=\n\nCheck at minimum:\n\nsrc/bytes\nsrc/fmt\nsrc/os\nsrc/time\nsrc/runtime\n\nVerify Android's expected bootstrap invocation can resolve std packages.\n\nDo not compile WireGuard yet.\n\n============================================================\n5. VERIFY REPAIR DID NOT CONTAMINATE SOURCE\n============================================================\n\nRerun project/source verification.\n\nRequired:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nBROKEN_PROJECT_GIT_REPOS=0\nMISSING_PROJECTS=0\nBROKEN_ALTERNATES=0\nMISSING_GIT_OBJECTS=0\nMERGE_CONFLICTS=0\n\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=PASS\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\n\nThe Go project repair must match its exact pinned revision and therefore must\nnot become an unaccepted source modification.\n\n============================================================\n6. RERUN COMPLETE MANDATORY PREBUILD\n============================================================\n\nBefore retrying Stage A, rerun the FULL mandatory pre-build check.\n\nRequired:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=PASS\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=PASS\nSELINUX_SOURCE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nBUILD_ENV=PASS\nGIT_STATE=PASS\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES\n\nOPT_ANDROID_EXISTS=NO\nACTIVE_PATHS_OUTSIDE_WORM=0\n\nGO_PREBUILT=PASS\n\nOnly then:\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_A_RETRY=PASS\n\n============================================================\n7. RETRY ONLY STAGE A\n============================================================\n\nOnly if:\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_A_RETRY=PASS\n\nretry:\n\nwireguard-go source build\n\nDo NOT automatically continue to Stage B.\n\nRequired result:\n\nWIREGUARD_GO_BUILD=PASS\n\nVerify the produced artifact corresponds to the pinned backend:\n\ne7b3a3c118836e112620b1302a8ba1873ad4daac\n\nReport produced library path and hash.\n\n============================================================\n8. HARD STOP AFTER STAGE A\n============================================================\n\nRegardless of Stage A result:\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_B=NOT_RUN\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nPRODUCT_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nTARGET_FILES_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA_BUILD=NOT_RUN\n\nWe want explicit confirmation that Stage A is repaired before continuing.\n\n============================================================\nREPORTS\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/GO-PREBUILT-REPAIR.md\n\nand a new immutable:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/PREBUILD-WG-wireguard-go-retry-<timestamp>.md\n\nFINAL REPORT:\n\nMANIFEST_PROJECT=\nCANONICAL_REMOTE=\nPINNED_REVISION=\nCURRENT_HEAD=\n\nGO_PREBUILT_STATE=\nGO_PROJECT_GIT_VALID=\nGO_STDLIB_SRC_PRESENT=\nGO_STDLIB_SRC_COMPLETE=\nGO_VERSION=\nGO_PREBUILT=\n\nOBJECTS_RECOVERED_LOCALLY=\nOBJECTS_RECOVERED_FROM_STORAGEBOX=\nOBJECTS_FETCHED_FROM_UPSTREAM=\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=\nNO_SECRETS=\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_A_RETRY=\nWIREGUARD_GO_BUILD=\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT=\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_SHA256=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_B=NOT_RUN\nBUILD=\nOTA=NOT_RUN\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1080:{"session_id":"01a084d5-062d-7302-868d-6ea30c803e46","ts":1788938199,"text":"DIAGNOSE GO TOOLCHAIN ONLY — NO BUILD\n\nDo not resume/retry Stage A.\n\nKnown facts:\n\nGO project:\nplatform/prebuilts/go/linux-x86\n\nPINNED_REVISION=\n05bc4bad6bdd9e5615c147c54e6f1a53bf04c375\n\nCURRENT_HEAD=\n05bc4bad6bdd9e5615c147c54e6f1a53bf04c375\n\nGO_VERSION=go1.25.4\nGO_STDLIB_SRC_PRESENT=PASS\nGO_STDLIB_SRC_COMPLETE=PASS\n\nBut the pinned bin/go reports packages including:\n\nbytes\nfmt\nos\ntime\nruntime\n\nas non-standard-library packages.\n\nDO NOT:\n- build wireguard-go\n- run Stage B/C/D/E\n- change source\n- fetch another Go revision\n- install host Go\n- change GOROOT permanently\n\n============================================================\n1. RUN PINNED GO FROM A COMPLETELY CLEAN ENVIRONMENT\n============================================================\n\nGO=/opt/worm/src/android/prebuilts/go/linux-x86/bin/go\n\nmkdir -p /opt/worm/build/tmp/go-neutral\n\nFrom /opt/worm/build/tmp/go-neutral run the equivalent of:\n\nenv -i \\\n  HOME=/tmp \\\n  PATH=/opt/worm/src/android/prebuilts/go/linux-x86/bin:/usr/bin:/bin \\\n  GOROOT=/opt/worm/src/android/prebuilts/go/linux-x86 \\\n  GOENV=off \\\n  GOTOOLCHAIN=local \\\n  \"$GO\" env\n\nThen:\n\n\"$GO\" env GOROOT GOVERSION GOMOD GOWORK GOPATH GOENV GOTOOLCHAIN\n\nand:\n\n\"$GO\" list std\n\"$GO\" list -json bytes\n\"$GO\" list -json runtime\n\nCapture stdout/stderr exactly.\n\nReport:\n\nNEUTRAL_GO_LIST_STD=\nNEUTRAL_BYTES_STANDARD=\nNEUTRAL_BYTES_GOROOT=\nNEUTRAL_BYTES_DIR=\nNEUTRAL_RUNTIME_STANDARD=\nNEUTRAL_RUNTIME_GOROOT=\nNEUTRAL_RUNTIME_DIR=\n\n============================================================\n2. INSPECT THE ACTUAL GO DISTRIBUTION\n============================================================\n\nInspect:\n\nprebuilts/go/linux-x86/VERSION\nprebuilts/go/linux-x86/go.env\nprebuilts/go/linux-x86/src/go.mod\nprebuilts/go/linux-x86/src/internal/goexperiment\nprebuilts/go/linux-x86/pkg/tool/linux_amd64\n\nRun:\n\ngit -C prebuilts/go/linux-x86 status --short\ngit -C prebuilts/go/linux-x86 ls-tree -r HEAD -- \\\n  VERSION go.env src/bytes src/fmt src/os src/time src/runtime pkg/tool\n\nDetermine whether bin/go, src and pkg/tool are all tracked by and belong to\nthe same pinned commit.\n\nReport:\n\nVERSION_CONTENT=\nSRC_GO_MOD=\nGO_BINARY_FROM_PINNED_TREE=\nGO_SRC_FROM_PINNED_TREE=\nGO_TOOLS_FROM_PINNED_TREE=\nGO_DISTRIBUTION_COHERENT=\n\n============================================================\n3. CHECK GO'S PACKAGE CLASSIFICATION LOGIC\n============================================================\n\nFor bytes and runtime capture:\n\nImportPath\nStandard\nGoroot\nDir\nRoot\nModule\nError\n\nusing go list -json.\n\nAlso check whether their resolved directories are actually underneath the\nGOROOT reported by the binary.\n\nReport:\n\nGOROOT_REPORTED=\nGOROOT_EXPECTED=\nGOROOT_MATCH=\nSTDLIB_PATH_RESOLUTION=\n\n============================================================\n4. FIND ANDROID'S REAL INVOCATION\n============================================================\n\nSearch the pinned Android source for references to:\n\nprebuilts/go/linux-x86/bin/go\nGOROOT\nGOTOOLCHAIN\nGOENV\n\nand determine how this exact GrapheneOS/AOSP revision expects Go to be\ninvoked.\n\nDo not modify anything.\n\nReport:\n\nANDROID_GO_WRAPPER=\nANDROID_GO_ENVIRONMENT=\nSTAGE_A_USED_EXPECTED_INVOCATION=\n\n============================================================\n5. ROOT CAUSE\n============================================================\n\nReturn exactly one:\n\nROOT_CAUSE=BUILD_ENV_CONTAMINATION\nROOT_CAUSE=GOROOT_LAYOUT_MISMATCH\nROOT_CAUSE=GO_DISTRIBUTION_INCOHERENT\nROOT_CAUSE=ANDROID_WRAPPER_REQUIRED\nROOT_CAUSE=STAGE_A_WRONG_INVOCATION\nROOT_CAUSE=OTHER_PROVEN:<description>\nROOT_CAUSE=UNKNOWN\n\nDo not apply a fix if UNKNOWN.\n\n============================================================\n6. NO BUILD\n============================================================\n\nPREBUILD_GATE remains unchanged.\n\nWIREGUARD_GO_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nPREBUILD_STAGE_B=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN\n\nFINAL REPORT:\n\nNEUTRAL_GO_LIST_STD=\nNEUTRAL_BYTES_STANDARD=\nNEUTRAL_RUNTIME_STANDARD=\n\nGOROOT_REPORTED=\nGOROOT_EXPECTED=\nGOROOT_MATCH=\n\nVERSION_CONTENT=\nGO_DISTRIBUTION_COHERENT=\n\nANDROID_GO_WRAPPER=\nANDROID_GO_ENVIRONMENT=\nSTAGE_A_USED_EXPECTED_INVOCATION=\n\nROOT_CAUSE=\nRECOMMENDED_MINIMUM_FIX=\n\nWIREGUARD_GO_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1081:{"session_id":"01a084d5-062d-7302-868d-6ea30c803e46","ts":1788938809,"text":"APPLY MINIMUM FIX FOR WG STAGE A GO CACHE\n\nAuthoritative diagnosis:\n\nROOT_CAUSE=BUILD_ENV_CONTAMINATION\n\nPinned Go distribution is coherent.\n\nThe failure reproduces only with:\n\nGOCACHE=/root/.cache/go-build\n\nand disappears with an isolated cache.\n\nDO NOT:\n- change Go source\n- change Go revision\n- install host Go\n- change WireGuard source\n- run Stage B/C/D/E\n- generate OTA\n\n============================================================\n1. DEFINE CANONICAL BUILD-OWNED GO CACHE\n============================================================\n\nUse:\n\nGOCACHE=/opt/worm/build/tmp/go-cache\nGOENV=off\nGOTOOLCHAIN=local\n\nEnsure:\n\nmkdir -p /opt/worm/build/tmp/go-cache\n\nPermissions must allow the build user to read/write it.\n\nDo not use:\n\n/root/.cache/go-build\n\n============================================================\n2. UPDATE ACTIVE WORM BUILD ENVIRONMENT\n============================================================\n\nUpdate only active WormOS build tooling so every Android/Go build under\n/opt/worm uses the isolated cache.\n\nPreferred locations:\n\n/opt/worm/config/build/env.sh\n/opt/worm/scripts/build/worm-build.sh\n\nDo not modify upstream Android Go source.\n\nDo not hardcode secrets.\n\nExpected effective environment:\n\nWORM_ROOT=/opt/worm\nANDROID_BUILD_TOP=/opt/worm/src/android\nOUT_DIR=/opt/worm/build/out\nTMPDIR=/opt/worm/build/tmp\nGOCACHE=/opt/worm/build/tmp/go-cache\nGOENV=off\nGOTOOLCHAIN=local\n\n============================================================\n3. CLEAN ONLY THE CONTAMINATED CACHE DEPENDENCY\n============================================================\n\nDo not delete source.\n\nDo not globally clear system caches.\n\nEnsure the retry does NOT read from:\n\n/root/.cache/go-build\n\nThe new cache may start empty.\n\n============================================================\n4. VERIFY FIX BEFORE BUILD\n============================================================\n\nUsing the exact pinned Go binary with the new effective Stage A environment,\nverify:\n\ngo env GOCACHE\ngo env GOROOT\ngo list std\ngo list bytes\ngo list runtime\n\nRequired:\n\nGOCACHE=/opt/worm/build/tmp/go-cache\nbytes Standard=true\nruntime Standard=true\n\nReport:\n\nGO_CACHE_ISOLATED=PASS\nGO_STDLIB_RESOLUTION=PASS\n\n============================================================\n5. MANDATORY FULL PREBUILD CHECK\n============================================================\n\nBefore retrying Stage A, rerun the COMPLETE mandatory pre-build gate.\n\nRequired:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=PASS\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=PASS\nSELINUX_SOURCE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nBUILD_ENV=PASS\nGIT_STATE=PASS\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES\n\nOPT_ANDROID_EXISTS=NO\nACTIVE_PATHS_OUTSIDE_WORM=0\n\nGO_CACHE_ISOLATED=PASS\nGO_STDLIB_RESOLUTION=PASS\n\nOnly then:\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_A_RETRY3=PASS\n\n============================================================\n6. RETRY ONLY STAGE A\n============================================================\n\nOnly if PREBUILD_STAGE_A_RETRY3=PASS:\n\nbuild only the pinned WireGuard Go backend.\n\nExpected backend commit:\n\ne7b3a3c118836e112620b1302a8ba1873ad4daac\n\nRequired:\n\nWIREGUARD_GO_BUILD=PASS\n\nRecord:\n\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT=\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_SHA256=\n\n============================================================\n7. STOP AFTER STAGE A\n============================================================\n\nRegardless of result:\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_B=NOT_RUN\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nPRODUCT_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nTARGET_FILES_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA_BUILD=NOT_RUN\n\nDo not automatically continue.\n\n============================================================\nFINAL REPORT\n============================================================\n\nGOCACHE=\nGO_CACHE_ISOLATED=\nGO_STDLIB_RESOLUTION=\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=\nNO_SECRETS=\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_A_RETRY3=\nWIREGUARD_GO_BUILD=\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT=\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_SHA256=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_B=NOT_RUN\nBUILD=\nOTA=NOT_RUN\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1082:{"session_id":"01a084d5-062d-7302-868d-6ea30c803e46","ts":1788939534,"text":"DIAGNOSE AND REPAIR SOONG/SISO main.star — STAGE A ONLY\n\nCURRENT VERIFIED STATE:\n\nWORM_ROOT=/opt/worm\nANDROID_BUILD_TOP=/opt/worm/src/android\nOUT_DIR=/opt/worm/build/out\nTMPDIR=/opt/worm/build/tmp\n\nGOCACHE=/opt/worm/build/tmp/go-cache\nGO_CACHE_ISOLATED=PASS\nGO_STDLIB_RESOLUTION=PASS\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=PASS\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES\n\nPrevious:\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_A_RETRY3=PASS\n\nGo stdlib/cache blocker is RESOLVED.\n\nCurrent blocker:\n\nSoong/Siso config load failure:\nfailed to load @config//main.star:\nopen main.star: no such file or directory\n\nDO NOT:\n- create a fake main.star\n- copy main.star from another Android version\n- update to latest/HEAD\n- modify WireGuard\n- modify accepted baseline\n- run Stage B/C/D/E\n- generate OTA\n\n============================================================\n1. CAPTURE EXACT FAILURE CONTEXT\n============================================================\n\nInspect the Stage A failure log and determine the exact command/process that\nattempted to load:\n\n@config//main.star\n\nRecord:\n\nFAILING_COMMAND=\nFAILING_BINARY=\nWORKING_DIRECTORY=\nSISO_CONFIG_DIR=\nSISO_CONFIG_REFERENCE=\nENVIRONMENT_RELEVANT_TO_SISO=\n\nDetermine whether the failure originates from:\n\nSoong\nSiso\nBlueprint\nNinja wrapper\nWormOS build wrapper\nenvironment configuration\n\n============================================================\n2. FIND ALL main.star FILES\n============================================================\n\nSearch the canonical tree:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android\n\nfor:\n\nmain.star\n*.star\n\nAlso search active build configuration under:\n\n/opt/worm/config\n/opt/worm/scripts\n\nDo not modify anything.\n\nReport:\n\nMAIN_STAR_FILES_FOUND=\nEXPECTED_MAIN_STAR_PATH=\nACTUAL_MAIN_STAR_PATH=\n\n============================================================\n3. DETERMINE PINNED SOURCE OWNER\n============================================================\n\nDetermine which exact manifest project is expected to provide the Siso\nconfiguration containing main.star.\n\nInspect relevant pinned projects, including as applicable:\n\nbuild/soong\nbuild/blueprint\nprebuilts/build-tools\nprebuilts/remoteexecution-client\nor the exact project referenced by this Android revision.\n\nFor the owning project report:\n\nPROJECT=\nREMOTE=\nPINNED_REVISION=\nCURRENT_HEAD=\nGIT_VALID=\nMAIN_STAR_TRACKED_AT_PINNED_REVISION=\n\nUse:\n\ngit ls-tree\n\nor equivalent against the exact pinned commit.\n\nDo not assume a missing working-tree file means it is absent upstream.\n\n============================================================\n4. DETERMINE WHETHER FILE IS MISSING OR PATH IS WRONG\n============================================================\n\nClassify exactly one:\n\nSISO_ROOT_CAUSE=MISSING_PINNED_CHECKOUT_CONTENT\nSISO_ROOT_CAUSE=INCORRECT_CONFIG_PATH\nSISO_ROOT_CAUSE=BUILD_ENV_CONTAMINATION\nSISO_ROOT_CAUSE=MISSING_MANIFEST_PROJECT\nSISO_ROOT_CAUSE=WRONG_STAGE_A_INVOCATION\nSISO_ROOT_CAUSE=OTHER_PROVEN:<description>\nSISO_ROOT_CAUSE=UNKNOWN\n\nIf UNKNOWN:\n\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n5. REPAIR ONLY IF PROVEN\n============================================================\n\nIf MISSING_PINNED_CHECKOUT_CONTENT:\n\nrestore the exact file/content from the project's exact pinned revision.\n\nPreferred:\n\n1. existing local Git objects\n2. Storage Box historical source/object backup\n3. canonical upstream exact pinned revision\n\nIf INCORRECT_CONFIG_PATH or BUILD_ENV_CONTAMINATION:\n\nfix only WormOS build environment/tooling under:\n\n/opt/worm/config\n/opt/worm/scripts\n\nIf WRONG_STAGE_A_INVOCATION:\n\nuse the exact invocation expected by this pinned Android/GrapheneOS tree.\n\nDO NOT fabricate Siso configuration.\n\n============================================================\n6. VERIFY SISO BEFORE BUILD\n============================================================\n\nWithout running Stage A yet, verify the exact Siso configuration can load.\n\nRequired:\n\nSISO_MAIN_STAR_PRESENT=PASS\nSISO_CONFIG_PATH=PASS\nSISO_CONFIG_LOAD=PASS\n\nAlso verify the repair did not damage source state:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=PASS\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\n============================================================\n7. MANDATORY PREBUILD AGAIN\n============================================================\n\nRun the COMPLETE mandatory pre-build check.\n\nRequired:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nBROKEN_PROJECT_GIT_REPOS=0\nMISSING_PROJECTS=0\nBROKEN_ALTERNATES=0\nMERGE_CONFLICTS=0\n\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=PASS\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=PASS\nSELINUX_SOURCE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nGO_CACHE_ISOLATED=PASS\nGO_STDLIB_RESOLUTION=PASS\n\nSISO_MAIN_STAR_PRESENT=PASS\nSISO_CONFIG_LOAD=PASS\n\nBUILD_ENV=PASS\nGIT_STATE=PASS\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES\n\nOPT_ANDROID_EXISTS=NO\nACTIVE_PATHS_OUTSIDE_WORM=0\n\nOnly then:\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_A_RETRY4=PASS\n\n============================================================\n8. RETRY STAGE A ONLY\n============================================================\n\nOnly if PREBUILD_STAGE_A_RETRY4=PASS:\n\nretry ONLY the pinned wireguard-go build.\n\nExpected backend commit:\n\ne7b3a3c118836e112620b1302a8ba1873ad4daac\n\nIf successful:\n\nWIREGUARD_GO_BUILD=PASS\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT=<exact path>\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_SHA256=<sha256>\n\nDo not automatically start Stage B.\n\n============================================================\n9. HARD STOP\n============================================================\n\nAfter Stage A:\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_B=NOT_RUN\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nPRODUCT_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nTARGET_FILES_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA_BUILD=NOT_RUN\n\n============================================================\nFINAL REPORT\n============================================================\n\nFAILING_COMMAND=\nFAILING_BINARY=\nSISO_CONFIG_REFERENCE=\n\nMAIN_STAR_FILES_FOUND=\nEXPECTED_MAIN_STAR_PATH=\nACTUAL_MAIN_STAR_PATH=\n\nSISO_OWNER_PROJECT=\nSISO_PINNED_REVISION=\nSISO_CURRENT_HEAD=\nMAIN_STAR_TRACKED_AT_PINNED_REVISION=\n\nSISO_ROOT_CAUSE=\nFIX_APPLIED=\n\nSISO_MAIN_STAR_PRESENT=\nSISO_CONFIG_PATH=\nSISO_CONFIG_LOAD=\n\nGO_CACHE_ISOLATED=\nGO_STDLIB_RESOLUTION=\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=\nNO_SECRETS=\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_A_RETRY4=\nWIREGUARD_GO_BUILD=\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT=\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_SHA256=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_B=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1083:{"session_id":"01a084d5-062d-7302-868d-6ea30c803e46","ts":1788940052,"text":"DIAGNOSE SOONG PATH VALIDATION — NO SOURCE WORKAROUND\n\nCURRENT STATE\n\nCanonical root:\n\nWORM_ROOT=/opt/worm\nANDROID_BUILD_TOP=/opt/worm/src/android\nOUT_DIR=/opt/worm/build/out\nTMPDIR=/opt/worm/build/tmp\n\nResolved previous blockers:\n\nGO_CACHE_ISOLATED=PASS\nGO_STDLIB_RESOLUTION=PASS\nSISO_MAIN_STAR_PRESENT=PASS\nSISO_CONFIG_PATH=PASS\nSISO_CONFIG_LOAD=PASS\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=PASS\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_A_RETRY4=PASS\n\nCurrent Stage A blocker:\n\nplatform_testing/Android.bp:255:1\n\ncontinuous_native_tests path validation failure:\n\n/opt/worm/build/out/host/linux-x86/framework/\nnet-tests-utils-host-common.jar\n\nis outside directory\n\nDO NOT:\n- modify platform_testing/Android.bp to bypass validation\n- disable path validation\n- copy the jar into the source tree\n- change WireGuard source\n- reset accepted baseline\n- use /opt/Android\n- run Stage B/C/D/E\n- generate OTA\n\n============================================================\n1. CAPTURE EXACT SOONG ERROR\n============================================================\n\nInspect the complete Stage A log.\n\nRecord:\n\nFAILING_MODULE=\nFAILING_BP_FILE=\nFAILING_BP_LINE=\nFAILING_PROPERTY=\nVALIDATED_PATH=\nEXPECTED_DIRECTORY=\nSOONG_ERROR_TEXT=\n\nInspect platform_testing/Android.bp around the failing definition and\ndetermine exactly which Soong module/property performs this validation.\n\nDo not edit it.\n\n============================================================\n2. DETERMINE PATH ORIGIN\n============================================================\n\nDetermine which module produces:\n\nnet-tests-utils-host-common.jar\n\nFind:\n\nPRODUCER_MODULE=\nPRODUCER_BP_FILE=\nPRODUCER_OUTPUT_PATH=\n\nDetermine how continuous_native_tests obtains/references that artifact.\n\nClassify whether the offending path originates from:\n\nSOURCE_PATH\nGENERATED_OUTPUT\nHOST_TOOL_OUTPUT\nOUT_DIR_EXPANSION\nABSOLUTE_PATH_EXPANSION\nOTHER\n\n============================================================\n3. AUDIT OUT_DIR SEMANTICS\n============================================================\n\nDetermine how this exact pinned Android/GrapheneOS revision expects OUT_DIR\nto be configured.\n\nInspect build/soong, build/make and relevant environment setup.\n\nCompare:\n\nOUT_DIR=/opt/worm/build/out\n\nagainst a source-relative representation which resolves to the SAME\ncanonical location under /opt/worm.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe canonical physical output location must remain:\n\n/opt/worm/build/out\n\nDo not move build output to /opt/Android.\n\nDetermine whether Soong requires OUT_DIR to be expressed relative to\nANDROID_BUILD_TOP rather than as an absolute path.\n\nReport:\n\nOUT_DIR_ABSOLUTE_SUPPORTED=\nOUT_DIR_EXPECTED_FORM=\nOUT_DIR_PATH_VALIDATION_EFFECT=\n\n============================================================\n4. CHECK EXISTING WORM BUILD WRAPPER\n============================================================\n\nInspect:\n\n/opt/worm/config/build/env.sh\n/opt/worm/scripts/build/worm-build.sh\n\nDetermine exactly how OUT_DIR is exported and passed into:\n\nSoong\nNinja\nSiso\n\nCheck for:\n\nrealpath\nreadlink\nabsolute path conversion\nPWD dependence\nTOP-relative path conversion\n\nDo not modify yet.\n\n============================================================\n5. REPRODUCE WITHOUT FULL BUILD\n============================================================\n\nUse the smallest safe Soong/bootstrap/path diagnostic possible.\n\nTest whether the error changes when OUT_DIR is represented in the exact form\nexpected by this Android revision while still resolving physically to:\n\n/opt/worm/build/out\n\nDo not start a full product build.\n\nDo not delete existing output.\n\n============================================================\n6. ROOT CAUSE\n============================================================\n\nReturn exactly one:\n\nSOONG_PATH_ROOT_CAUSE=ABSOLUTE_OUT_DIR_UNSUPPORTED\nSOONG_PATH_ROOT_CAUSE=OUT_DIR_NORMALIZATION_BUG\nSOONG_PATH_ROOT_CAUSE=STALE_GENERATED_PATH\nSOONG_PATH_ROOT_CAUSE=WRONG_BUILD_INVOCATION\nSOONG_PATH_ROOT_CAUSE=PINNED_SOURCE_INCONSISTENCY\nSOONG_PATH_ROOT_CAUSE=OTHER_PROVEN:<description>\nSOONG_PATH_ROOT_CAUSE=UNKNOWN\n\nIf UNKNOWN:\n\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n7. APPLY MINIMUM TOOLING FIX ONLY\n============================================================\n\nIf the problem is OUT_DIR representation or build invocation:\n\nmodify only WormOS tooling/configuration under:\n\n/opt/worm/config/build\n/opt/worm/scripts/build\n\nDo NOT modify Android upstream source.\n\nPhysical canonical requirements remain:\n\nWORM_ROOT=/opt/worm\nANDROID_BUILD_TOP=/opt/worm/src/android\n\nThe effective build output must resolve to:\n\n/opt/worm/build/out\n\nNo active path may use /opt/Android.\n\nIf a relative OUT_DIR is required, prove with realpath that it resolves\nexactly to /opt/worm/build/out.\n\n============================================================\n8. STALE OUTPUT CHECK\n============================================================\n\nBecause previous bootstrap attempts populated /opt/worm/build/out, determine\nwhether any generated Soong state embeds the old/incorrect path semantics.\n\nIdentify only regenerable bootstrap metadata affected by the path change.\n\nIf cleanup is required:\n\n- list exact paths first;\n- preserve build failure logs/reports;\n- delete only regenerable bootstrap metadata;\n- do not delete source;\n- do not indiscriminately wipe OUT_DIR unless proven necessary.\n\nReport:\n\nSTALE_OUTPUT_FOUND=\nSTALE_OUTPUT_CLEANED=\n\n============================================================\n9. MANDATORY PREBUILD\n============================================================\n\nAfter the proven fix, rerun the COMPLETE mandatory pre-build check.\n\nRequired:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=PASS\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=PASS\nSELINUX_SOURCE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nGO_CACHE_ISOLATED=PASS\nGO_STDLIB_RESOLUTION=PASS\nSISO_CONFIG_LOAD=PASS\n\nBUILD_ENV=PASS\nGIT_STATE=PASS\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES\n\nOPT_ANDROID_EXISTS=NO\nACTIVE_PATHS_OUTSIDE_WORM=0\n\nSOONG_PATH_VALIDATION=PASS\n\nOnly then:\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_A_RETRY5=PASS\n\n============================================================\n10. RETRY STAGE A ONLY\n============================================================\n\nOnly if:\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_A_RETRY5=PASS\n\nretry ONLY the WireGuard Go backend build.\n\nExpected backend commit:\n\ne7b3a3c118836e112620b1302a8ba1873ad4daac\n\nRequired:\n\nWIREGUARD_GO_BUILD=PASS\n\nRecord:\n\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT=\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_SHA256=\n\n============================================================\n11. STOP AFTER STAGE A\n============================================================\n\nDo NOT automatically proceed to Stage B.\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_B=NOT_RUN\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nPRODUCT_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nTARGET_FILES_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA_BUILD=NOT_RUN\n\n============================================================\nFINAL REPORT\n============================================================\n\nFAILING_MODULE=\nFAILING_PROPERTY=\nVALIDATED_PATH=\nEXPECTED_DIRECTORY=\n\nPRODUCER_MODULE=\nPRODUCER_OUTPUT_PATH=\n\nOUT_DIR_ABSOLUTE_SUPPORTED=\nOUT_DIR_EXPECTED_FORM=\nOUT_DIR_EFFECTIVE_REALPATH=\n\nSOONG_PATH_ROOT_CAUSE=\nFIX_APPLIED=\n\nSTALE_OUTPUT_FOUND=\nSTALE_OUTPUT_CLEANED=\nSOONG_PATH_VALIDATION=\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=\nNO_SECRETS=\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_A_RETRY5=\nWIREGUARD_GO_BUILD=\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT=\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_SHA256=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_B=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1084:{"session_id":"01a084d5-062d-7302-868d-6ea30c803e46","ts":1788941954,"text":"FIX WIREGUARD-GO SOONG SBOX PATH — STAGE A ONLY\n\nCURRENT VERIFIED STATE\n\nPrevious blockers resolved:\n\nGO_CACHE_ISOLATED=PASS\nGO_STDLIB_RESOLUTION=PASS\nSISO_CONFIG_LOAD=PASS\nSOONG_PATH_VALIDATION=PASS\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=PASS\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES\n\nCurrent blocker:\n\nworm-libwg-go-source-built fails inside Soong sbox because\nbuild-libwg-go.sh derives script_dir from its runtime location.\n\nInside sbox the script is copied/executed from a generated tools/out/bin\nlocation, so script_dir no longer identifies the Android source tree.\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nMake the WireGuard Go source-build integration hermetic and compatible with\nSoong sbox.\n\nDo not bypass sbox.\nDo not hardcode /opt/worm/src/android into Android source.\nDo not use /opt/Android.\nDo not weaken sandboxing.\n\n============================================================\n1. AUDIT CURRENT MODULE AND SCRIPT\n============================================================\n\nInspect the exact files implementing:\n\nworm-libwg-go-source-built\nbuild-libwg-go.sh\n\nIdentify:\n\nMODULE_BP_FILE=\nBUILD_SCRIPT_SOURCE=\nMODULE_TYPE=\nDECLARED_SRCS=\nDECLARED_TOOLS=\nDECLARED_OUT=\nSCRIPT_CURRENT_ROOT_DISCOVERY=\nSBOX_RUNTIME_SCRIPT_PATH=\n\nDetermine every source/config file required by build-libwg-go.sh.\n\nDo not edit yet.\n\n============================================================\n2. PROVE ROOT CAUSE\n============================================================\n\nConfirm that the failure occurs because logic equivalent to:\n\ndirname \"$0\"\n\nis being used to infer a source-tree location after Soong has staged the\nscript into sbox.\n\nReport:\n\nSBOX_ROOT_CAUSE=SCRIPT_LOCATION_USED_AS_SOURCE_ROOT\n\nIf this is not proven, STOP.\n\n============================================================\n3. DESIGN HERMETIC FIX\n============================================================\n\nUse Soong-declared inputs rather than runtime script location.\n\nPreferred architecture:\n\n- declare every required WireGuard Go source/input in Android.bp;\n- declare build-libwg-go.sh as a tool;\n- pass input locations explicitly through the generated command;\n- use Soong/genrule locations such as $(location ...) / $(locations ...)\n  where appropriate;\n- write output only to the declared $(out);\n- use the existing isolated Go cache/environment;\n- do not depend on absolute host source paths.\n\nThe build must work when the script is executed from an arbitrary sbox path.\n\nDo not rely on:\n\nPWD\ndirname \"$0\" as Android root\n/opt/worm/src/android literals\n/opt/Android\nundeclared filesystem traversal\n\n============================================================\n4. PRESERVE PINNED BACKEND\n============================================================\n\nBackend must remain exactly:\n\ne7b3a3c118836e112620b1302a8ba1873ad4daac\n\nDo not modify upstream WireGuard implementation merely to accommodate the\nbuild.\n\nChanges should be restricted to WormOS build integration unless an existing\nWormOS-owned wrapper itself requires correction.\n\nRequired:\n\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\n\n============================================================\n5. APPLY MINIMUM PATCH\n============================================================\n\nPatch only the WormOS WireGuard build integration necessary to make\nworm-libwg-go-source-built hermetic.\n\nDocument every modified file.\n\nDo not modify unrelated Android.bp files.\n\nDo not disable sbox.\n\nDo not introduce broad source globs without checking reproducibility and\ninput declaration correctness.\n\nGenerate:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WIREGUARD-GO-SBOX-PATH-FIX.md\n\nReport:\n\nFILES_MODIFIED=\nSBOX_ROOT_CAUSE=\nHERMETIC_INPUTS=\nHERMETIC_OUTPUT=\nABSOLUTE_SOURCE_PATH_DEPENDENCY=\n\nRequired:\n\nABSOLUTE_SOURCE_PATH_DEPENDENCY=NO\n\n============================================================\n6. STATIC SBOX VALIDATION\n============================================================\n\nBefore compiling, verify that the resulting command can run with the build\nscript located outside its source directory.\n\nVerify:\n\nSCRIPT_LOCATION_INDEPENDENT=PASS\nALL_REQUIRED_INPUTS_DECLARED=PASS\nOUTPUT_DECLARED=PASS\nSBOX_COMPATIBLE=PASS\n\nIf any is not PASS:\n\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n7. MANDATORY PRE-BUILD CHECK\n============================================================\n\nThe build integration changed, therefore run the FULL mandatory pre-build\ngate again.\n\nThe intentional WireGuard build-integration patch must be classified as:\n\nCURRENT_IMPLEMENTATION\n\nnot UNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK.\n\nRequired:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=PASS\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=PASS\nSELINUX_SOURCE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nGO_CACHE_ISOLATED=PASS\nGO_STDLIB_RESOLUTION=PASS\nSISO_CONFIG_LOAD=PASS\nSOONG_PATH_VALIDATION=PASS\nSBOX_COMPATIBLE=PASS\n\nBUILD_ENV=PASS\nGIT_STATE=PASS\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES\n\nOPT_ANDROID_EXISTS=NO\nACTIVE_PATHS_OUTSIDE_WORM=0\n\nOnly then:\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_A_RETRY6=PASS\n\n============================================================\n8. RETRY STAGE A ONLY\n============================================================\n\nOnly if:\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_A_RETRY6=PASS\n\nbuild ONLY:\n\nworm-libwg-go-source-built / required libwg-go target\n\nDo not request a broader product build.\n\nVerify resulting library is actually source-built from the pinned backend.\n\nRequired:\n\nWIREGUARD_GO_BUILD=PASS\nBACKEND_SOURCE_BUILD=PASS\n\nRecord:\n\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT=\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_SHA256=\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_ARCH=\n\n============================================================\n9. STOP AFTER STAGE A\n============================================================\n\nEven if Stage A passes:\n\nSTOP.\n\nDo not automatically start WormSystemWireGuard.\n\nRequired final state:\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_B=NOT_RUN\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nPRODUCT_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nTARGET_FILES_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA_BUILD=NOT_RUN\n\n============================================================\nFINAL REPORT\n============================================================\n\nMODULE_BP_FILE=\nBUILD_SCRIPT_SOURCE=\nMODULE_TYPE=\n\nSBOX_ROOT_CAUSE=\nFILES_MODIFIED=\n\nSCRIPT_LOCATION_INDEPENDENT=\nALL_REQUIRED_INPUTS_DECLARED=\nOUTPUT_DECLARED=\nABSOLUTE_SOURCE_PATH_DEPENDENCY=\nSBOX_COMPATIBLE=\n\nBACKEND_PINNED=\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=\nNO_SECRETS=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_A_RETRY6=\n\nWIREGUARD_GO_BUILD=\nBACKEND_SOURCE_BUILD=\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT=\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_SHA256=\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_ARCH=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_B=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN\nBLOCKERS="}
