/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1093:{"session_id":"01a084d5-062d-7302-868d-6ea30c803e46","ts":1788946706,"text":"FIX ACCEPTED BASELINE: AugurriIconRenderer.java TRUNCATED\n\nCURRENT STATE\n\nStage A:\nWIREGUARD_GO_BUILD=PASS\nBACKEND_SOURCE_BUILD=PASS\n\nStage B:\nPREBUILD_STAGE_B=PASS\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_BUILD=FAIL\n\nExact blocker:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android/frameworks/base/core/java/android/util/AugurriIconRenderer.java\n\nis truncated at line 142 and causes:\n\nframeworks/base:framework-minus-apex-headers\nunexpected end of input\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nAugurri is ACCEPTED_BASELINE.\n\nDo NOT remove Augurri.\nDo NOT revert frameworks/base to vanilla upstream.\nDo NOT touch WireGuard source.\nDo NOT run Stage C/D/E or OTA.\nDo NOT fabricate missing Java code.\n\n============================================================\n1. AUDIT THE FILE\n============================================================\n\nInspect:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android/frameworks/base/core/java/android/util/AugurriIconRenderer.java\n\nRecord:\n\nFILE_SIZE=\nLINE_COUNT=\nLAST_30_LINES=\nGIT_STATUS=\nOWNER_PROJECT=\nCURRENT_PROJECT_HEAD=\n\nDetermine whether the file ends mid-method/class.\n\nReport:\n\nTRUNCATION_CONFIRMED=\n\n============================================================\n2. FIND AUTHORITATIVE COMPLETE COPY\n============================================================\n\nSearch accepted WormOS sources and provenance under:\n\n/opt/worm/patches\n/opt/worm/artifacts\n/opt/worm/backups\n/opt/worm/worm-os\n/opt/worm/changelog\n\nand historical Storage Box backup if necessary.\n\nSearch by:\n\nAugurriIconRenderer.java\nclass AugurriIconRenderer\nunique method names from the existing file\n\nPrefer sources in this order:\n\n1. accepted WormOS patch/provenance artifact\n2. accepted Git commit/tag history\n3. Storage Box historical source backup\n4. other exact accepted local copy\n\nDo NOT use arbitrary internet/latest source.\n\nReport:\n\nAUTHORITATIVE_SOURCE_FOUND=\nAUTHORITATIVE_SOURCE_PATH=\nAUTHORITATIVE_SOURCE_COMMIT_OR_TAG=\nAUTHORITATIVE_SOURCE_SHA256=\n\n============================================================\n3. VERIFY IT BELONGS TO ACCEPTED BASELINE\n============================================================\n\nProve the recovered complete file belongs to the previously accepted\nAugurri/WormOS baseline.\n\nUse existing tags/reports/patch metadata.\n\nRequired:\n\nAUGURRI_BASELINE_PROVENANCE=PASS\n\nIf provenance cannot be proven:\n\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n4. RESTORE EXACT COMPLETE FILE\n============================================================\n\nReplace only the truncated file with the exact accepted complete copy.\n\nDo not alter unrelated frameworks/base files.\n\nAfter restoration:\n\n- verify Java structure is complete\n- verify braces/classes/methods close correctly\n- verify file hash\n- verify no merge markers\n- verify no secrets\n\nReport:\n\nAUGURRI_FILE_RESTORED=PASS\nRESTORED_SHA256=\n\n============================================================\n5. STATIC JAVA CHECK\n============================================================\n\nRun the smallest safe parser/static validation available for this source.\n\nDo not launch Stage B yet.\n\nRequired:\n\nJAVA_PARSE_CHECK=PASS\nUNEXPECTED_EOF=NO\n\n============================================================\n6. REVERIFY ACCEPTED BASELINE\n============================================================\n\nRerun source classification.\n\nThe restored file must remain:\n\nACCEPTED_BASELINE\n\nRequired:\n\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=PASS\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\n============================================================\n7. MANDATORY PREBUILD STAGE B RETRY\n============================================================\n\nBefore any Stage B retry, rerun the FULL mandatory pre-build gate.\n\nRequired:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nBROKEN_PROJECT_GIT_REPOS=0\nMISSING_PROJECTS=0\nBROKEN_ALTERNATES=0\nMERGE_CONFLICTS=0\n\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=PASS\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_SOURCE=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=PASS\nSELINUX_SOURCE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nGO_CACHE_ISOLATED=PASS\nGO_STDLIB_RESOLUTION=PASS\nSISO_CONFIG_LOAD=PASS\nSOONG_PATH_VALIDATION=PASS\nSBOX_COMPATIBLE=PASS\n\nSTAGE_A_ARTIFACT_PRESENT=PASS\nSTAGE_A_ARTIFACT_HASH_MATCH=PASS\n\nAUGURRI_FILE_RESTORED=PASS\nJAVA_PARSE_CHECK=PASS\n\nBUILD_ENV=PASS\nGIT_STATE=PASS\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES\n\nOPT_ANDROID_EXISTS=NO\nACTIVE_PATHS_OUTSIDE_WORM=0\n\nOnly then:\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_B_RETRY=PASS\n\n============================================================\n8. RETRY STAGE B ONLY\n============================================================\n\nOnly if PREBUILD_STAGE_B_RETRY=PASS:\n\nbuild only:\n\nWormSystemWireGuard\n\nand direct dependencies.\n\nDo not continue to Stage C.\n\nRequired:\n\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_BUILD=PASS\n\nRecord:\n\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK=\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK_SHA256=\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK_SIZE=\n\n============================================================\n9. HARD STOP AFTER STAGE B\n============================================================\n\nRegardless of result:\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_C=NOT_RUN\nPRODUCT_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nTARGET_FILES_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA_BUILD=NOT_RUN\n\n============================================================\nFINAL REPORT\n============================================================\n\nTRUNCATION_CONFIRMED=\nAUTHORITATIVE_SOURCE_FOUND=\nAUTHORITATIVE_SOURCE_PATH=\nAUTHORITATIVE_SOURCE_COMMIT_OR_TAG=\nAUGURRI_BASELINE_PROVENANCE=\n\nAUGURRI_FILE_RESTORED=\nRESTORED_SHA256=\nJAVA_PARSE_CHECK=\nUNEXPECTED_EOF=\n\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=\nNO_SECRETS=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_B_RETRY=\n\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_BUILD=\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK=\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK_SHA256=\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK_SIZE=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_C=NOT_RUN\nOTA_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1095:{"session_id":"01a08578-eb37-7001-a5ee-15bd637aa18e","ts":1788947315,"text":"CORRECT PERMANENT WORMOS WG KEY POLICY\n\nThe current policy incorrectly uses WORMOS_WG_KEY_GATE as a global\npre-build requirement.\n\nReplace it permanently with TWO independent gates:\n\n1. WORMOS_WG_BUILD_KEY_GATE\n2. WORMOS_WG_RUNTIME_KEY_GATE\n\nDo not build in this task.\n\n============================================================\nBUILD KEY GATE\n============================================================\n\nThis gate runs before every build.\n\nThe production device private key is runtime-provisioned and MUST NOT be\nrequired on the build host.\n\nRequired build-time checks:\n\nPRIVATE_KEY_PROVISIONING=RUNTIME_PROVISIONED\n\nPRIVATE_KEY_EMBEDDED_IN_SOURCE=NO\nPRIVATE_KEY_EMBEDDED_IN_BUILD_OUTPUT=NO\nPRIVATE_KEY_EMBEDDED_IN_APK=NO\n\nKEY_PROVISIONING_IMPLEMENTATION=PASS\nKEY_STORAGE_LOCATION_DESIGN=PASS\nKEY_FILE_PERMISSIONS_DESIGN=PASS\nPUBLIC_KEY_DERIVATION_IMPLEMENTATION=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_KEY_API_INTEGRATION=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_KEY_COMPATIBILITY=PASS\n\nIf all above pass:\n\nWORMOS_WG_BUILD_KEY_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\nRUNTIME KEY GATE\n============================================================\n\nThese checks require an installed device and must NOT be treated as build\nfailures:\n\nPRIVATE_KEY_PRESENT=NOT_TESTABLE_DEVICE_REQUIRED\nPRIVATE_KEY_PERMISSIONS=NOT_TESTABLE_DEVICE_REQUIRED\nPRIVATE_KEY_FORMAT=NOT_TESTABLE_DEVICE_REQUIRED\nPUBLIC_KEY_DERIVATION=NOT_TESTABLE_DEVICE_REQUIRED\nPUBLIC_KEY_MATCH=NOT_TESTABLE_DEVICE_REQUIRED\nWG_KEY_PARSE=NOT_TESTABLE_DEVICE_REQUIRED\nWIREGUARD_HANDSHAKE=NOT_TESTABLE_DEVICE_REQUIRED\n\nTherefore before device testing:\n\nWORMOS_WG_RUNTIME_KEY_GATE=NOT_RUN_DEVICE_REQUIRED\n\nNever convert NOT_TESTABLE_DEVICE_REQUIRED into FAIL merely because the\nproduction private key is intentionally absent from the build host.\n\n============================================================\nBUILD AUTHORIZATION\n============================================================\n\nThe permanent rule becomes:\n\nBUILD_ALLOWED <=>\nPREBUILD_GATE=PASS\nAND WORMOS_WG_BUILD_KEY_GATE=PASS\n\nWORMOS_WG_RUNTIME_KEY_GATE is NOT a prerequisite for building the OTA.\n\nIt IS mandatory before:\n\nWIREGUARD_RUNTIME_PASS=PASS\nPRODUCTION_READY=PASS\nwormos-wg-system-state-runtime-pass tag\n\n============================================================\nSECURITY INVARIANT\n============================================================\n\nA production private key appearing on the build host/source/APK/OTA is NOT a\nway to satisfy the runtime gate.\n\nIf a private key is unexpectedly found embedded:\n\nWORMOS_WG_BUILD_KEY_GATE=FAIL\nBUILD_ALLOWED=NO\n\nNever print private key material.\n\n============================================================\nUPDATE PERMANENT POLICY\n============================================================\n\nUpdate:\n\n/opt/worm/docs/WORMOS-INITIAL-BUILD-POLICY.md\n\nand active pre-build tooling/configuration so every future build uses:\n\nPREBUILD_GATE\nWORMOS_WG_BUILD_KEY_GATE\n\nDo not use WORMOS_WG_KEY_GATE as the build authorization gate anymore.\n\nPreserve historical reports unchanged.\n\nGenerate a new correction report under:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/\n\n============================================================\nVERIFY CURRENT STATE\n============================================================\n\nEvaluate the current source state against the corrected policy.\n\nReport:\n\nPREBUILD_GATE=\nPRIVATE_KEY_PROVISIONING=\n\nKEY_PROVISIONING_IMPLEMENTATION=\nKEY_STORAGE_LOCATION_DESIGN=\nKEY_FILE_PERMISSIONS_DESIGN=\nPUBLIC_KEY_DERIVATION_IMPLEMENTATION=\nWG_BACKEND_KEY_API_INTEGRATION=\nWG_BACKEND_KEY_COMPATIBILITY=\n\nPRIVATE_KEY_EMBEDDED_IN_SOURCE=\nPRIVATE_KEY_EMBEDDED_IN_BUILD_OUTPUT=\nPRIVATE_KEY_EMBEDDED_IN_APK=\n\nWORMOS_WG_BUILD_KEY_GATE=\nWORMOS_WG_RUNTIME_KEY_GATE=\n\nBUILD_ALLOWED=\n\n============================================================\nSTOP\n============================================================\n\nDo not start Stage B.\n\nRequired target state:\n\nPREBUILD_GATE=PASS\nWORMOS_WG_BUILD_KEY_GATE=PASS\nWORMOS_WG_RUNTIME_KEY_GATE=NOT_RUN_DEVICE_REQUIRED\nBUILD_ALLOWED=YES\n\nSTAGE_B=NOT_STARTED\nOTA=NOT_STARTED\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1098:{"session_id":"01a084d5-062d-7302-868d-6ea30c803e46","ts":1788947630,"text":"ADD ROBOT-WORM WIREGUARD CONFIG CHECK + ON/OFF POLICY\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nUse the existing accepted robot-worm configuration as the authoritative\nreference for WormOS WireGuard runtime configuration/state.\n\nDo not copy private keys or secrets into WormOS source, APK or OTA.\n\nCanonical root:\n\n/opt/worm\n\nInspect relevant accepted configuration under:\n\n/opt/worm/worm-robot\n/opt/worm/config\n/opt/worm/wireguard\n\nand other robot-worm paths found by the audit.\n\n============================================================\n1. FIND ROBOT-WORM WG CONFIG\n============================================================\n\nLocate the accepted robot-worm configuration describing:\n\n- WireGuard enabled/disabled state\n- device identity/reference\n- public key reference\n- peer/server endpoint references\n- assigned VPN IP\n- DNS configuration\n- allowed/private networks\n- autostart policy\n- fail-closed policy\n\nDo NOT print:\n\nprivate keys\nPSKs\npasswords\ntokens\n\nReport:\n\nROBOT_WORM_WG_CONFIG_FOUND=\nROBOT_WORM_WG_CONFIG_SOURCE=\nROBOT_WORM_WG_CONFIG_SCHEMA=\n\n============================================================\n2. DEFINE SYSTEM STATE SWITCH\n============================================================\n\nImplement/read a canonical boolean state such as:\n\nWIREGUARD_SYSTEM_STATE=ON|OFF\n\nPreferred canonical configuration under:\n\n/opt/worm/config/wireguard/\n\nDo not duplicate configuration if robot-worm already provides an accepted\nsingle source of truth.\n\nIf robot-worm is the source of truth, WormOS tooling should read/reference\nit rather than maintain an independent conflicting copy.\n\n============================================================\n3. ON STATE\n============================================================\n\nWhen:\n\nWIREGUARD_SYSTEM_STATE=ON\n\nrequire static/build-time validation of:\n\nROBOT_WORM_CONFIG=PASS\nWG_CONFIG_REFERENCES=PASS\nWG_PUBLIC_CONFIG_COMPLETE=PASS\nKEY_PROVISIONING_IMPLEMENTATION=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_KEY_API_INTEGRATION=PASS\n\nNo production private key is required on the build server.\n\nBuild-time result:\n\nWORMOS_WG_CONFIG_GATE=PASS\n\nRuntime checks remain device-required.\n\n============================================================\n4. OFF STATE\n============================================================\n\nWhen:\n\nWIREGUARD_SYSTEM_STATE=OFF\n\nverify:\n\n- WormSystemWireGuard will not auto-start\n- no runtime WireGuard tunnel is requested\n- fail-closed behavior does not accidentally block normal system networking\n  unless explicitly designed to do so\n- runtime key provisioning is not attempted\n\nReport:\n\nWG_AUTOSTART=OFF\nWG_RUNTIME_REQUESTED=NO\nWG_RUNTIME_KEY_REQUIRED=NO\n\nThe presence of WireGuard binaries/components in the image may remain if\nthat is the selected architecture.\n\nDo not remove source/backend merely because runtime state is OFF.\n\n============================================================\n5. CONFIG VALIDATION\n============================================================\n\nValidate robot-worm public/non-secret configuration fields.\n\nCheck:\n\nCONFIG_SYNTAX=\nDEVICE_ID_REFERENCE=\nPUBLIC_KEY_REFERENCE=\nVPN_ADDRESS=\nENDPOINT_REFERENCE=\nDNS_REFERENCE=\nALLOWED_NETWORKS=\nAUTOSTART_POLICY=\nFAIL_CLOSED_POLICY=\n\nDo not print secret values.\n\nClassify:\n\nPASS\nFAIL\nNOT_CONFIGURED\nRUNTIME_PROVISIONED\n\n============================================================\n6. BUILD POLICY\n============================================================\n\nBefore every build stage require:\n\nPREBUILD_GATE=PASS\nWORMOS_WG_BUILD_KEY_GATE=PASS\nWORMOS_WG_CONFIG_GATE=PASS\n\nIf WireGuard state is ON:\n\nWG_ON_CONFIG_VALID=PASS is mandatory.\n\nIf WireGuard state is OFF:\n\nWG_OFF_STATE_VALID=PASS is mandatory.\n\nThen:\n\nBUILD_ALLOWED=YES\n\nOtherwise:\n\nBUILD_ALLOWED=NO\n\n============================================================\n7. RUNTIME POLICY\n============================================================\n\nAfter device flash:\n\nIf WIREGUARD_SYSTEM_STATE=ON, test:\n\nPRIVATE_KEY_PRESENT\nPUBLIC_KEY_DERIVATION\nWG_KEY_PARSE\nWG_RUNTIME\nWIREGUARD_HANDSHAKE\nFAIL_CLOSED\nPROTECTED_DNS\n\nIf WIREGUARD_SYSTEM_STATE=OFF, test:\n\nWG_INTERFACE_INACTIVE\nWG_AUTOSTART_INACTIVE\nNO_UNEXPECTED_FAIL_CLOSED_BLOCK\n\n============================================================\n8. DO NOT BUILD\n============================================================\n\nThis task is configuration/policy implementation only.\n\nBUILD=NOT_STARTED\nOTA=NOT_STARTED\n\nFINAL REPORT:\n\nROBOT_WORM_WG_CONFIG_FOUND=\nROBOT_WORM_WG_CONFIG_SOURCE=\n\nWIREGUARD_SYSTEM_STATE=\n\nCONFIG_SYNTAX=\nDEVICE_ID_REFERENCE=\nPUBLIC_KEY_REFERENCE=\nVPN_ADDRESS=\nENDPOINT_REFERENCE=\nDNS_REFERENCE=\nALLOWED_NETWORKS=\nAUTOSTART_POLICY=\nFAIL_CLOSED_POLICY=\n\nWORMOS_WG_CONFIG_GATE=\nWORMOS_WG_BUILD_KEY_GATE=\nPREBUILD_GATE=\n\nWG_ON_CONFIG_VALID=\nWG_OFF_STATE_VALID=\n\nBUILD_ALLOWED=\nBUILD=NOT_STARTED\nOTA=NOT_STARTED\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1099:{"session_id":"01a084d5-062d-7302-868d-6ea30c803e46","ts":1788947967,"text":"START WORMOS COMPONENT-BY-COMPONENT VALIDATION\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nValidate every currently implemented WormOS feature independently before\ncontinuing the final WireGuard system-state OTA.\n\nCanonical root:\n\n/opt/worm\n\nANDROID_BUILD_TOP=/opt/worm/src/android\nOUT_DIR=/opt/worm/build/out\nTMPDIR=/opt/worm/build/tmp\n\nABSOLUTE RULES:\n\n- /opt/Android must not exist or be used.\n- Mandatory pre-build check before EVERY component build.\n- Test ONE component at a time.\n- Stop that component on first real failure.\n- Do not automatically repair unrelated components.\n- Do not run full product build.\n- Do not generate target-files.\n- Do not generate OTA.\n- Do not reset accepted baseline.\n- Never expose private keys/secrets.\n\n============================================================\n0. DISCOVER CURRENT COMPONENTS\n============================================================\n\nFirst use current source/provenance, not assumptions, to determine which\nfeatures are actually present.\n\nExpected candidates include:\n\n01 WormOS base/product\n02 Material 3\n03 WormLauncher\n04 WormOS App Store\n05 Proton\n06 Bitwarden\n07 Proton Drive\n08 PragmataPro\n09 Augurri\n10 key/config integration\n11 WormSystemWireGuard\n12 official WireGuard Android backend\n13 source-built wireguard-go\n14 fail-closed networking\n15 protected DNS\n16 boot/autostart\n17 WireGuard ON/OFF configuration\n18 updater/OTA integration\n19 web installer\n20 robot-worm integration\n\nAdd other CURRENT source components if discovered.\n\nDo not test OPNsense/server infrastructure as part of the Android build.\n\n============================================================\n1. CREATE TEST MATRIX\n============================================================\n\nFor every component assign:\n\nPRESENT\nNOT_PRESENT\nPARTIAL\nUNKNOWN\n\nThen, if PRESENT/PARTIAL:\n\nSOURCE_STATIC_TEST\nMODULE_BUILD_TEST\nINTEGRATION_TEST\nRUNTIME_DEVICE_REQUIRED\n\nNot every component needs every test.\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WORMOS-COMPONENT-TEST-MATRIX.md\n\n============================================================\n2. MANDATORY PREBUILD BEFORE EACH BUILD\n============================================================\n\nImmediately before ANY component compilation rerun the mandatory pre-build\ngate.\n\nRequired baseline conditions:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=PASS\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nBUILD_ENV=PASS\nGIT_STATE=PASS\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES\n\nOPT_ANDROID_EXISTS=NO\nACTIVE_PATHS_OUTSIDE_WORM=0\n\nGO_CACHE_ISOLATED=PASS\nGO_STDLIB_RESOLUTION=PASS\nSISO_CONFIG_LOAD=PASS\nSOONG_PATH_VALIDATION=PASS\n\nAlso run component-specific checks.\n\nIf any required check fails:\n\nCOMPONENT_PREBUILD=FAIL\nCOMPONENT_BUILD=NOT_STARTED\n\nContinue with another independent component only if doing so cannot be\naffected by the failed component.\n\n============================================================\n3. TEST BASE/PRODUCT\n============================================================\n\nValidate WormOS product definitions, makefiles, packages and target\nconfiguration.\n\nDo not perform a full product build.\n\nReport:\n\nWORMOS_BASE_SOURCE=\nWORMOS_PRODUCT_CONFIG=\nWORMOS_BASE_BUILD_CHECK=\n\n============================================================\n4. TEST MATERIAL 3\n============================================================\n\nIf present:\n\nidentify exact modified projects/modules.\n\nRun static validation first, then the smallest relevant module build.\n\nReport:\n\nMATERIAL3_SOURCE=\nMATERIAL3_PREBUILD=\nMATERIAL3_BUILD=\nMATERIAL3_RUNTIME_REQUIRED=\n\n============================================================\n5. TEST WORMLAUNCHER\n============================================================\n\nIf present:\n\nvalidate source/resources/manifest and build the launcher module only.\n\nReport:\n\nWORMLAUNCHER_SOURCE=\nWORMLAUNCHER_PREBUILD=\nWORMLAUNCHER_BUILD=\nWORMLAUNCHER_APK=\n\n============================================================\n6. TEST APP STORE\n============================================================\n\nIf accepted App Store customization is present:\n\nvalidate exact accepted revision/customization and build the minimum App\nStore target.\n\nReport:\n\nAPPSTORE_SOURCE=\nAPPSTORE_ACCEPTED_BASELINE=\nAPPSTORE_PREBUILD=\nAPPSTORE_BUILD=\n\n============================================================\n7. TEST PROTON / BITWARDEN / PROTON DRIVE\n============================================================\n\nTreat independently.\n\nDo not assume presence.\n\nFor each:\n\nSOURCE=\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=\nPREBUILD=\nBUILD=\n\nIf absent:\n\nSTATUS=NOT_PRESENT\n\nDo not install/add it during this validation.\n\n============================================================\n8. TEST PRAGMATAPRO\n============================================================\n\nValidate:\n\nfont files referenced correctly\nproduct/resource integration\nno broken references\nno secret/private font material copied into reports\n\nDo not expose font files.\n\nReport:\n\nPRAGMATAPRO_SOURCE=\nPRAGMATAPRO_INTEGRATION=\nPRAGMATAPRO_BUILD_CHECK=\n\n============================================================\n9. TEST AUGURRI\n============================================================\n\nThis is especially important because:\n\nAugurriIconRenderer.java previously caused Stage B failure.\n\nFirst verify the file is complete.\n\nRequired before any dependent build:\n\nAUGURRI_SOURCE_COMPLETE=PASS\nAUGURRI_JAVA_PARSE=PASS\n\nThen build the smallest relevant framework target capable of proving the\nsource compiles.\n\nReport:\n\nAUGURRI_SOURCE_COMPLETE=\nAUGURRI_JAVA_PARSE=\nAUGURRI_PREBUILD=\nAUGURRI_BUILD=\n\nIf Augurri fails:\n\ndo not attempt to hide/remove it.\nRecord the exact accepted-baseline blocker.\n\n============================================================\n10. TEST KEY/CONFIG INTEGRATION\n============================================================\n\nUse the corrected build/runtime distinction.\n\nBuild-time:\n\nPRIVATE_KEY_EMBEDDED_IN_SOURCE=NO\nPRIVATE_KEY_EMBEDDED_IN_BUILD_OUTPUT=NO\nKEY_PROVISIONING_IMPLEMENTATION=\nWG_BACKEND_KEY_API_INTEGRATION=\n\nNever print private key material.\n\nReport:\n\nWORMOS_WG_BUILD_KEY_GATE=\n\nRuntime key validation remains:\n\nWORMOS_WG_RUNTIME_KEY_GATE=NOT_RUN_DEVICE_REQUIRED\n\n============================================================\n11. TEST WIREGUARD-GO\n============================================================\n\nStage A already produced a valid artifact.\n\nFirst verify existing artifact/hash.\n\nDo not rebuild unnecessarily.\n\nRequired:\n\nWIREGUARD_GO_SOURCE=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_PRESENT=PASS\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_HASH_MATCH=PASS\n\nKnown successful architecture:\n\nAArch64\n\nReport:\n\nWIREGUARD_GO_BUILD=PASS_EXISTING_ARTIFACT\n\n============================================================\n12. TEST WormSystemWireGuard\n============================================================\n\nOnly after its mandatory prebuild passes.\n\nAugurri/framework dependencies must pass first.\n\nBuild ONLY WormSystemWireGuard and direct dependencies.\n\nReport:\n\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_PREBUILD=\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_BUILD=\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK=\nBACKEND_USED_BY_APP=\n\nDo not continue into product build.\n\n============================================================\n13. TEST FAIL-CLOSED\n============================================================\n\nSeparate static/build-time from runtime.\n\nVerify source/config integration for:\n\nIPv4\nIPv6\nboot\nhandover\nbackend crash\npeer unreachable\n\nReport:\n\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=\nFAIL_CLOSED_BUILD_INTEGRATION=\n\nActual behavior:\n\nFAIL_CLOSED_RUNTIME=NOT_RUN_DEVICE_REQUIRED\n\n============================================================\n14. TEST PROTECTED DNS\n============================================================\n\nVerify source/config integration independently.\n\nReport:\n\nPROTECTED_DNS_SOURCE=\nPROTECTED_DNS_BUILD_INTEGRATION=\nPROTECTED_DNS_RUNTIME=NOT_RUN_DEVICE_REQUIRED\n\n============================================================\n15. TEST BOOT/AUTOSTART\n============================================================\n\nVerify manifest/service/receiver/product integration.\n\nReport:\n\nBOOT_AUTOSTART_SOURCE=\nBOOT_AUTOSTART_BUILD_INTEGRATION=\nBOOT_AUTOSTART_RUNTIME=NOT_RUN_DEVICE_REQUIRED\n\n============================================================\n16. TEST WG ON/OFF CONFIG\n============================================================\n\nUse robot-worm configuration/reference if it is the accepted source of truth.\n\nTest both logical states without requiring a real tunnel:\n\nON:\nWG_ON_CONFIG_VALID=\nWG_AUTOSTART_EXPECTED=\n\nOFF:\nWG_OFF_CONFIG_VALID=\nWG_AUTOSTART_DISABLED=\nWG_KEY_PROVISIONING_DISABLED=\n\nDo not change OPNsense/server configuration.\n\n============================================================\n17. UPDATER / WEB INSTALLER / ROBOT-WORM\n============================================================\n\nTest each independently only if present.\n\nDo not modify production infrastructure.\n\nPrefer static/config/unit checks.\n\nReport separately:\n\nUPDATER=\nWEB_INSTALLER=\nROBOT_WORM=\n\n============================================================\n18. RESULTS CLASSIFICATION\n============================================================\n\nFor every component return exactly one overall state:\n\nPASS\nFAIL\nPARTIAL\nNOT_PRESENT\nRUNTIME_TEST_REQUIRED\nBLOCKED_BY_<component>\n\nA component must not be marked PASS solely because source files exist.\n\n============================================================\n19. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite individual reports under:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/components/\n\nand final:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WORMOS-COMPONENT-VALIDATION-SUMMARY.md\n\nFinal table:\n\nCOMPONENT | PRESENT | STATIC | PREBUILD | BUILD | RUNTIME | OVERALL\n\nThen summarize:\n\nCOMPONENTS_PASS=\nCOMPONENTS_FAIL=\nCOMPONENTS_PARTIAL=\nCOMPONENTS_NOT_PRESENT=\nCOMPONENTS_RUNTIME_REQUIRED=\n\nNEXT_BLOCKER=\n\n============================================================\n20. STOP\n============================================================\n\nDo NOT run:\n\nfull product build\ntarget-files-package\nOTA generation\n\nBUILD_FULL=NOT_RUN\nTARGET_FILES=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1102:{"session_id":"01a085a6-cfd1-7c01-8a04-fdc287459446","ts":1788948701,"text":"DEFINE GLOBAL WORMOS PRIVATE-NETWORK SERVICE POLICY\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nAll WormOS operational services must use the private network path through\nWireGuard and OPNsense unless a specific bootstrap exception is explicitly\ndocumented and approved.\n\nAUTHORITATIVE NETWORK PATH:\n\nWormOS\n  -> WireGuard\n  -> OPNsense\n  -> private services / routed Internet / DNS\n\nRobot\n  -> WireGuard\n  -> OPNsense\n\nOPNsense is the central routing, firewall and policy enforcement point.\n\n============================================================\n1. SERVICES IN SCOPE\n============================================================\n\nAudit and classify at minimum:\n\nOTA\nUPDATER\nWEB_INSTALLER\nAPP_STORE\nROBOT_CONTROL\nCONTROL_API\nPRIVATE_API\nDNS\nTELEMETRY_IF_PRESENT\nPACKAGE_DOWNLOADS\nPROVISIONING\nDEVICE_ENROLLMENT\nCONFIG_SYNC\nOTHER_WORMOS_SERVICES\n\nFor every service report:\n\nSERVICE=\nSOURCE_PATH=\nENDPOINT=\nPRIVATE_OR_PUBLIC=\nNETWORK_PATH=\nREQUIRES_WG=\nBOOTSTRAP_EXCEPTION=\nSTATUS=\n\n============================================================\n2. DEFAULT NETWORK POLICY\n============================================================\n\nDefault rule:\n\nALL_WORMOS_SERVICES_VIA_OPNSENSE=YES\n\nNo service may silently connect directly to a public endpoint while\nWireGuard/private networking is expected.\n\nRequired:\n\nDIRECT_SERVICE_BYPASS=0\n\n============================================================\n3. OTA\n============================================================\n\nOTA metadata and OTA package retrieval must use the approved private route.\n\nVerify:\n\nOTA_METADATA_VIA_OPNSENSE=\nOTA_PACKAGE_VIA_OPNSENSE=\nOTA_PRIVATE_ENDPOINT=\nOTA_PUBLIC_BYPASS=\n\nRequired:\n\nOTA_PUBLIC_BYPASS=NO\n\n============================================================\n4. WEB INSTALLER\n============================================================\n\nVerify WormOS web installer/update service uses the private/private-routed\nendpoint through OPNsense.\n\nRequired:\n\nWEB_INSTALLER_VIA_OPNSENSE=YES\n\nIf the installer is intentionally public before device enrollment, classify\nthat separately as:\n\nBOOTSTRAP_EXCEPTION\n\nand document exact scope.\n\n============================================================\n5. UPDATER / APP STORE\n============================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nUPDATER_VIA_OPNSENSE=YES\nAPPSTORE_VIA_OPNSENSE=YES\n\nNo direct uncontrolled endpoint bypass.\n\n============================================================\n6. ROBOT / CONTROL\n============================================================\n\nRobot/control traffic must traverse:\n\nRobot -> WireGuard -> OPNsense\n\nand WormOS control traffic:\n\nWormOS -> WireGuard -> OPNsense -> private control services\n\nRequired:\n\nROBOT_TRAFFIC_VIA_OPNSENSE=YES\nWORMOS_CONTROL_VIA_OPNSENSE=YES\n\n============================================================\n7. DNS\n============================================================\n\nAll WormOS service DNS resolution must follow approved DNS routing through\nthe private path.\n\nRequired:\n\nDNS_VIA_OPNSENSE=YES\nPUBLIC_DNS_BYPASS=NO\n\n============================================================\n8. FAIL-CLOSED\n============================================================\n\nIf WireGuard/private path is required and unavailable:\n\nservices classified PRIVATE_ONLY must not fall back directly to public\nnetworking.\n\nRequired:\n\nPRIVATE_SERVICE_FAIL_CLOSED=PASS\n\nAny approved bootstrap exception must be explicit and minimal.\n\n============================================================\n9. BOOTSTRAP EXCEPTIONS\n============================================================\n\nIdentify services that must work before WireGuard enrollment/handshake.\n\nFor each exception require:\n\nSERVICE=\nWHY_REQUIRED=\nPUBLIC_ENDPOINT=\nALLOWED_PORT=\nALLOWED_PROTOCOL=\nTIME_WINDOW_OR_STATE=\nFAIL_CLOSED_AFTER_ENROLLMENT=\n\nNo implicit exceptions.\n\n============================================================\n10. PREBUILD NETWORK GATE\n============================================================\n\nBefore every build require:\n\nWORMOS_WG_CONFIG_GATE=PASS\nOPNSENSE_PEER_CONFIG_MATCH=PASS\n\nALL_WORMOS_SERVICES_VIA_OPNSENSE=PASS\nDIRECT_SERVICE_BYPASS=0\nDNS_VIA_OPNSENSE=PASS\nPRIVATE_SERVICE_FAIL_CLOSED=PASS\n\nBOOTSTRAP_EXCEPTIONS_VALID=PASS\n\nThen:\n\nWORMOS_NETWORK_GATE=PASS\n\nIf not:\n\nBUILD_ALLOWED=NO\n\n============================================================\n11. RUNTIME TESTS\n============================================================\n\nAfter OTA/device flash verify individually:\n\nOTA_VIA_OPNSENSE\nUPDATER_VIA_OPNSENSE\nWEB_INSTALLER_VIA_OPNSENSE\nAPPSTORE_VIA_OPNSENSE\nROBOT_VIA_OPNSENSE\nCONTROL_API_VIA_OPNSENSE\nDNS_VIA_OPNSENSE\n\nand:\n\nNO_DIRECT_PUBLIC_BYPASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_PRIVATE_SERVICES\n\n============================================================\n12. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WORMOS-PRIVATE-NETWORK-SERVICE-AUDIT.md\n\nFinal:\n\nALL_WORMOS_SERVICES_VIA_OPNSENSE=\nOTA_VIA_OPNSENSE=\nUPDATER_VIA_OPNSENSE=\nWEB_INSTALLER_VIA_OPNSENSE=\nAPPSTORE_VIA_OPNSENSE=\nROBOT_VIA_OPNSENSE=\nCONTROL_API_VIA_OPNSENSE=\nDNS_VIA_OPNSENSE=\n\nDIRECT_SERVICE_BYPASS=\nBOOTSTRAP_EXCEPTIONS=\nBOOTSTRAP_EXCEPTIONS_VALID=\n\nPRIVATE_SERVICE_FAIL_CLOSED=\nWORMOS_NETWORK_GATE=\n\nBUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1104:{"session_id":"01a085a6-cfd1-7c01-8a04-fdc287459446","ts":1788949321,"text":"RESUME WORMOS WIREGUARD OTA — STAGE B\n\nUse the currently verified state as authoritative.\n\nDO NOT redo network architecture/configuration unless a check regresses.\n\nKnown PASS state:\n\nWIREGUARD_GO_BUILD=PASS\nBACKEND_SOURCE_BUILD=PASS\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_PRESENT=PASS\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_HASH_MATCH=PASS\n\nWORMOS_WG_CONFIG_GATE=PASS\nWORMOS_WG_BUILD_KEY_GATE=PASS\nOPNSENSE_PEER_CONFIG_MATCH=PASS\nWORMOS_NETWORK_GATE=PASS\n\nDIRECT_SERVICE_BYPASS=0\nPRIVATE_SERVICE_FAIL_CLOSED=PASS\n\nCanonical root:\n\nWORM_ROOT=/opt/worm\nANDROID_BUILD_TOP=/opt/worm/src/android\n\n/opt/Android must not exist.\n\n============================================================\n1. CHECK PREVIOUS STAGE-B BLOCKER FIRST\n============================================================\n\nPrevious Stage B failed because:\n\nframeworks/base/core/java/android/util/AugurriIconRenderer.java\n\nwas reported truncated, causing:\n\nframework-minus-apex-headers:\nunexpected end of input\n\nBefore attempting Stage B, verify this exact blocker.\n\nRequired:\n\nAUGURRI_SOURCE_COMPLETE=PASS\nAUGURRI_JAVA_PARSE=PASS\n\nIf still truncated:\n\nSTOP.\n\nRecover the exact accepted Augurri baseline source using existing accepted\nWormOS provenance/backups/history.\n\nDo not fabricate Java code.\nDo not remove Augurri.\nDo not revert the accepted customization.\n\nAfter any repair, rerun the complete pre-build gate before building.\n\n============================================================\n2. MANDATORY STAGE-B PREBUILD\n============================================================\n\nRequire:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=PASS\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nBUILD_ENV=PASS\nGIT_STATE=PASS\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES\n\nGO_CACHE_ISOLATED=PASS\nGO_STDLIB_RESOLUTION=PASS\nSISO_CONFIG_LOAD=PASS\nSOONG_PATH_VALIDATION=PASS\nSBOX_COMPATIBLE=PASS\n\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_PRESENT=PASS\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_HASH_MATCH=PASS\n\nWORMOS_WG_CONFIG_GATE=PASS\nWORMOS_WG_BUILD_KEY_GATE=PASS\nOPNSENSE_PEER_CONFIG_MATCH=PASS\nWORMOS_NETWORK_GATE=PASS\n\nDIRECT_SERVICE_BYPASS=0\nPRIVATE_SERVICE_FAIL_CLOSED=PASS\n\nAUGURRI_SOURCE_COMPLETE=PASS\nAUGURRI_JAVA_PARSE=PASS\n\nOPT_ANDROID_EXISTS=NO\nACTIVE_PATHS_OUTSIDE_WORM=0\n\nOnly then:\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_B=PASS\n\n============================================================\n3. BUILD STAGE B ONLY\n============================================================\n\nOnly if PREBUILD_STAGE_B=PASS:\n\nBuild WormSystemWireGuard and only the direct dependencies required by\nSoong.\n\nDo not start full product build.\nDo not generate target-files.\nDo not generate OTA.\n\nUse the existing source-built libwg-go artifact when valid.\n\n============================================================\n4. VERIFY RESULT\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_BUILD=PASS\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK_PRESENT=PASS\n\nRecord:\n\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK=\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK_SHA256=\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK_SIZE=\n\nVerify:\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG_PACKAGING=PASS\nBACKEND_USED_BY_STAGE_B=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\n\nWORMOS_WG_CONFIG_GATE=PASS\nWORMOS_NETWORK_GATE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nDo not claim runtime WireGuard PASS.\n\nRuntime remains:\n\nWORMOS_WG_RUNTIME_KEY_GATE=NOT_RUN_DEVICE_REQUIRED\nWG_HANDSHAKE=NOT_RUN_DEVICE_REQUIRED\n\n============================================================\n5. STOP AFTER STAGE B\n============================================================\n\nIf Stage B passes:\n\nSTOP.\n\nDo not automatically start Stage C.\n\nFinal:\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_B=\nAUGURRI_SOURCE_COMPLETE=\nAUGURRI_JAVA_PARSE=\n\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_HASH_MATCH=\n\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_BUILD=\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK_PRESENT=\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK=\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK_SHA256=\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG_PACKAGING=\nBACKEND_USED_BY_STAGE_B=\n\nWORMOS_WG_CONFIG_GATE=\nWORMOS_WG_BUILD_KEY_GATE=\nWORMOS_NETWORK_GATE=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_C=NOT_RUN\nPRODUCT_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nTARGET_FILES_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA_BUILD=NOT_RUN\n\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1105:{"session_id":"01a085a6-cfd1-7c01-8a04-fdc287459446","ts":1788951981,"text":"START WORMOS WG SYSTEM-STATE STAGE C — PRODUCT BUILD\n\nAUTHORITATIVE COMPLETED STATE:\n\nSTAGE_A=PASS\nWIREGUARD_GO_BUILD=PASS\nBACKEND_SOURCE_BUILD=PASS\n\nSTAGE_B=PASS\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_BUILD=PASS\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK_PRESENT=PASS\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG_PACKAGING=PASS\nBACKEND_USED_BY_STAGE_B=PASS\n\nWORMOS_WG_CONFIG_GATE=PASS\nWORMOS_WG_BUILD_KEY_GATE=PASS\nWORMOS_NETWORK_GATE=PASS\n\nBLOCKERS=NONE\n\nDo NOT rebuild or modify Stage A/B implementation unless dependency\nresolution naturally reuses/rebuilds required outputs.\n\nCanonical root:\n\nWORM_ROOT=/opt/worm\nANDROID_BUILD_TOP=/opt/worm/src/android\n\nPhysical output:\n\n/opt/worm/build/out\n\nAndroid build tools may use source-relative OUT_DIR=out where required,\nwith:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android/out -> ../../../build/out\n\n/opt/Android must never exist or be used.\n\n============================================================\n1. VERIFY STAGE A/B ARTIFACTS\n============================================================\n\nBefore Stage C verify:\n\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_PRESENT=PASS\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_HASH_MATCH=PASS\n\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK_PRESENT=PASS\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK_HASH_MATCH=PASS\n\nUse the previously recorded hashes as authority.\n\nIf either regresses:\n\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n2. CHECK SOONG EXECUTION ENVIRONMENT\n============================================================\n\nPrevious Stage B note:\n\nthe first sandboxed attempt encountered Soong path-interposer socket\npermission problems; the scoped build subsequently completed successfully.\n\nBefore product build determine whether the normal Stage C build user can\ncreate/access all required Soong/Siso/sbox/path-interposer sockets and\ntemporary paths.\n\nDo not disable sandboxing.\n\nDo not weaken system-wide permissions.\n\nRequired:\n\nSOONG_SOCKET_PERMISSIONS=PASS\nSBOX_RUNTIME=PASS\nSISO_RUNTIME=PASS\n\nIf an explicit build-user privilege model is required, document and use the\nminimum established configuration.\n\n============================================================\n3. MANDATORY PREBUILD STAGE C\n============================================================\n\nRun the COMPLETE pre-build check immediately before Stage C.\n\nRequired:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nBROKEN_PROJECT_GIT_REPOS=0\nMISSING_PROJECTS=0\nBROKEN_ALTERNATES=0\nMERGE_CONFLICTS=0\n\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=PASS\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nBUILD_ENV=PASS\nGIT_STATE=PASS\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES\n\nGO_CACHE_ISOLATED=PASS\nGO_STDLIB_RESOLUTION=PASS\nSISO_CONFIG_LOAD=PASS\nSOONG_PATH_VALIDATION=PASS\nSBOX_COMPATIBLE=PASS\n\nSOONG_SOCKET_PERMISSIONS=PASS\n\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_PRESENT=PASS\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_HASH_MATCH=PASS\n\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK_PRESENT=PASS\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK_HASH_MATCH=PASS\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nPROVENANCE_MATCH=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED_SOURCE=PASS\nSELINUX_SOURCE=PASS\n\nWORMOS_WG_CONFIG_GATE=PASS\nWORMOS_WG_BUILD_KEY_GATE=PASS\nOPNSENSE_PEER_CONFIG_MATCH=PASS\nWORMOS_NETWORK_GATE=PASS\n\nDIRECT_SERVICE_BYPASS=0\nPRIVATE_SERVICE_FAIL_CLOSED=PASS\n\nOPT_ANDROID_EXISTS=NO\nACTIVE_PATHS_OUTSIDE_WORM=0\n\nOnly then:\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_C=PASS\n\nOtherwise:\n\nPRODUCT_BUILD=NOT_STARTED\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n4. BUILD PRODUCT\n============================================================\n\nOnly if PREBUILD_STAGE_C=PASS:\n\nbuild the configured frankel WormOS product required for subsequent\ntarget-files generation.\n\nUse the existing canonical WormOS build wrapper/environment.\n\nDo not generate OTA in this stage.\n\nDo not introduce source modifications to fix build failures automatically.\n\nOn first genuine build failure:\n\nSTOP\nPRESERVE LOGS\nREPORT BLOCKER\n\n============================================================\n5. VERIFY PRODUCT OUTPUT\n============================================================\n\nAfter successful product build verify:\n\nPRODUCT_BUILD=PASS\n\nand confirm the resulting product contains:\n\nWormSystemWireGuard.apk\nsource-built libwg-go.so\nexpected privileged app placement\nexpected product package declarations\n\nRequired:\n\nWG_APK_IN_PRODUCT=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_IN_PRODUCT=PASS\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG_IN_PRODUCT=PASS\n\n============================================================\n6. SECURITY / SELINUX\n============================================================\n\nBecause this is now a product-level build, record actual compiled policy\nresult rather than source-only status.\n\nRequired:\n\nSELINUX_COMPILE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nDo not claim runtime fail-closed/handshake PASS.\n\nThose remain device tests.\n\n============================================================\n7. NETWORK POLICY PRESERVATION\n============================================================\n\nVerify generated product configuration still corresponds to:\n\nWORMOS_WG_CONFIG_GATE=PASS\nWORMOS_NETWORK_GATE=PASS\nDIRECT_SERVICE_BYPASS=0\n\nNo production private key may appear in generated product output.\n\nRequired:\n\nPRIVATE_KEY_EMBEDDED_IN_PRODUCT=NO\n\n============================================================\n8. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/PREBUILD-WG-product-<timestamp>.md\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WORMOS-WG-STAGE-C-PRODUCT-BUILD-<timestamp>.md\n\nRecord exact build log.\n\n============================================================\n9. HARD STOP AFTER STAGE C\n============================================================\n\nEven if product build succeeds:\n\nDO NOT generate target-files.\nDO NOT generate OTA.\n\nRequired:\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_D=NOT_RUN\nTARGET_FILES_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA_BUILD=NOT_RUN\n\n============================================================\nFINAL REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_PRESENT=\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_HASH_MATCH=\n\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK_PRESENT=\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK_HASH_MATCH=\n\nSOONG_SOCKET_PERMISSIONS=\nSBOX_RUNTIME=\nSISO_RUNTIME=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_C=\n\nPRODUCT_BUILD=\n\nWG_APK_IN_PRODUCT=\nWG_BACKEND_IN_PRODUCT=\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG_IN_PRODUCT=\n\nSELINUX_COMPILE=\nNO_SECRETS=\nPRIVATE_KEY_EMBEDDED_IN_PRODUCT=\n\nWORMOS_WG_CONFIG_GATE=\nWORMOS_NETWORK_GATE=\nDIRECT_SERVICE_BYPASS=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_D=NOT_RUN\nTARGET_FILES_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA_BUILD=NOT_RUN\n\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1106:{"session_id":"01a085a6-cfd1-7c01-8a04-fdc287459446","ts":1788953160,"text":"FIX ACCEPTED BASELINE: AugurriIconRenderer.kt TRUNCATED\n\nCURRENT STATE\n\nStage A:\nWIREGUARD_GO_BUILD=PASS\n\nStage B:\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_BUILD=PASS\n\nStage C:\nPREBUILD_STAGE_C=PASS\nPRODUCT_BUILD=FAIL\n\nExact blocker:\n\n/opt/worm/src/android/frameworks/libs/systemui/iconloaderlib/src/\ncom/android/launcher3/icons/AugurriIconRenderer.kt\n\nThe file is truncated/incomplete.\n\nObserved:\n\nLINE_COUNT=105\nfailure around lines 101-106\nfile ends inside Config(...) constructor\n\nDO NOT:\n\n- remove Augurri\n- replace with vanilla AOSP implementation\n- invent missing Kotlin\n- touch WireGuard\n- start Stage D\n- generate OTA\n\n============================================================\n1. AUDIT THE TRUNCATED FILE\n============================================================\n\nInspect the current file and record:\n\nFILE_SIZE=\nLINE_COUNT=\nCURRENT_SHA256=\nLAST_40_LINES=\nGIT_STATUS=\nOWNER_PROJECT=\nCURRENT_PROJECT_HEAD=\n\nConfirm:\n\nAUGURRI_KT_TRUNCATION_CONFIRMED=PASS|FAIL\n\n============================================================\n2. FIND AUTHORITATIVE COMPLETE COPY\n============================================================\n\nSearch accepted WormOS state and provenance under:\n\n/opt/worm/patches\n/opt/worm/artifacts\n/opt/worm/backups\n/opt/worm/worm-os\n/opt/worm/changelog\n/opt/worm/augurri\n\nAlso inspect accepted Git history/tags and Storage Box historical backup if\nneeded.\n\nSearch for:\n\nAugurriIconRenderer.kt\nclass AugurriIconRenderer\nunique symbols/methods from the current file\nConfig(\npalette\n\nPreferred source order:\n\n1. accepted WormOS provenance/artifact\n2. accepted Git tag/commit\n3. Storage Box historical source backup\n4. exact accepted local copy\n\nDo not use arbitrary internet/latest code.\n\nReport:\n\nAUTHORITATIVE_KT_SOURCE_FOUND=\nAUTHORITATIVE_KT_SOURCE_PATH=\nAUTHORITATIVE_KT_SOURCE_COMMIT_OR_TAG=\nAUTHORITATIVE_KT_SHA256=\n\n============================================================\n3. PROVE BASELINE PROVENANCE\n============================================================\n\nThe recovered file must belong to the accepted Augurri baseline.\n\nRequired:\n\nAUGURRI_KT_BASELINE_PROVENANCE=PASS\n\nIf provenance cannot be proven:\n\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n4. RESTORE EXACT FILE\n============================================================\n\nReplace only:\n\nAugurriIconRenderer.kt\n\nwith the complete accepted copy.\n\nDo not modify unrelated SystemUI/iconloader files.\n\nAfter restoration verify:\n\nAUGURRI_KT_RESTORED=PASS\nRESTORED_KT_SHA256=\nMERGE_MARKERS=0\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\n============================================================\n5. KOTLIN STATIC VALIDATION\n============================================================\n\nRun the smallest available Kotlin/source parser or affected module static\nvalidation.\n\nRequired:\n\nAUGURRI_KT_PARSE=PASS\nKOTLIN_UNEXPECTED_EOF=NO\n\nDo not launch full Stage C yet.\n\n============================================================\n6. RECHECK ALL AUGURRI BASELINE FILES\n============================================================\n\nBecause both Java and Kotlin Augurri files were found truncated, audit ALL\ncurrent Augurri-related source files before retrying product build.\n\nSearch current source tree for:\n\n*Augurri*\naugurri\n\nFor every source file report:\n\nPATH=\nLANGUAGE=\nLINE_COUNT=\nENDS_CLEANLY=\nPARSE_OR_STATIC_CHECK=\nBASELINE_PROVENANCE=\n\nRequired:\n\nAUGURRI_FILES_TOTAL=\nAUGURRI_FILES_VALID=\nAUGURRI_FILES_TRUNCATED=0\nAUGURRI_FILES_UNKNOWN=0\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/AUGURRI-BASELINE-COMPLETE-AUDIT.md\n\n============================================================\n7. REVERIFY ACCEPTED BASELINE\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=PASS\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nRestored accepted files must remain classified as baseline, not new\nunaccepted implementation.\n\n============================================================\n8. MANDATORY PREBUILD STAGE C RETRY\n============================================================\n\nBefore any product build retry rerun the COMPLETE mandatory gate.\n\nRequired:\n\nANDROID_PROJECTS_VERIFIED=1108_OF_1108\nBROKEN_PROJECT_GIT_REPOS=0\nMISSING_PROJECTS=0\nBROKEN_ALTERNATES=0\nMERGE_CONFLICTS=0\n\nACCEPTED_BASELINE=PASS\nUNACCEPTED_DIRTY_WORK=0\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nGO_CACHE_ISOLATED=PASS\nGO_STDLIB_RESOLUTION=PASS\nSISO_CONFIG_LOAD=PASS\nSOONG_PATH_VALIDATION=PASS\nSBOX_COMPATIBLE=PASS\nSOONG_SOCKET_PERMISSIONS=PASS\n\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_PRESENT=PASS\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_HASH_MATCH=PASS\n\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK_PRESENT=PASS\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK_HASH_MATCH=PASS\n\nWORMOS_WG_CONFIG_GATE=PASS\nWORMOS_WG_BUILD_KEY_GATE=PASS\nOPNSENSE_PEER_CONFIG_MATCH=PASS\nWORMOS_NETWORK_GATE=PASS\n\nAUGURRI_SOURCE_COMPLETE=PASS\nAUGURRI_JAVA_PARSE=PASS\nAUGURRI_KT_RESTORED=PASS\nAUGURRI_KT_PARSE=PASS\nAUGURRI_FILES_TRUNCATED=0\nAUGURRI_FILES_UNKNOWN=0\n\nBUILD_ENV=PASS\nGIT_STATE=PASS\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES\n\nOPT_ANDROID_EXISTS=NO\nACTIVE_PATHS_OUTSIDE_WORM=0\n\nOnly then:\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_C_RETRY=PASS\n\n============================================================\n9. RETRY STAGE C ONLY\n============================================================\n\nOnly if:\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_C_RETRY=PASS\n\nretry the frankel product build.\n\nDo not automatically proceed to target-files.\n\nIf successful require:\n\nPRODUCT_BUILD=PASS\nWG_APK_IN_PRODUCT=PASS\nWG_BACKEND_IN_PRODUCT=PASS\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG_IN_PRODUCT=PASS\nSELINUX_COMPILE=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\n============================================================\n10. STOP\n============================================================\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_D=NOT_RUN\nTARGET_FILES_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA_BUILD=NOT_RUN\n\nFINAL REPORT:\n\nAUGURRI_KT_TRUNCATION_CONFIRMED=\nAUTHORITATIVE_KT_SOURCE_FOUND=\nAUTHORITATIVE_KT_SOURCE_PATH=\nAUTHORITATIVE_KT_SOURCE_COMMIT_OR_TAG=\nAUGURRI_KT_BASELINE_PROVENANCE=\n\nAUGURRI_KT_RESTORED=\nRESTORED_KT_SHA256=\nAUGURRI_KT_PARSE=\nKOTLIN_UNEXPECTED_EOF=\n\nAUGURRI_FILES_TOTAL=\nAUGURRI_FILES_VALID=\nAUGURRI_FILES_TRUNCATED=\nAUGURRI_FILES_UNKNOWN=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_C_RETRY=\nPRODUCT_BUILD=\n\nWG_APK_IN_PRODUCT=\nWG_BACKEND_IN_PRODUCT=\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG_IN_PRODUCT=\nSELINUX_COMPILE=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_D=NOT_RUN\nOTA_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1113:{"session_id":"01a08677-3f76-7d13-b541-cc1429ce16b4","ts":1788962357,"text":"PATCH-CONTROL-FEATURE-REGISTRY-V1\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nImplement a central WormOS feature-control layer under:\n\n/opt/worm/control\n\nIt must become the authoritative place for:\n\n- feature inventory\n- ON/OFF state\n- source/build/network/runtime status\n- dependencies\n- update class\n- blockers\n- global feature gate\n- pre-build authorization\n\nDo NOT run product build.\nDo NOT generate target-files.\nDo NOT generate OTA.\n\nDo not modify feature implementations except where strictly required to\nexpose/read their current state.\n\n============================================================\n1. DIRECTORY LAYOUT\n============================================================\n\nCreate/ensure:\n\n/opt/worm/control/features/\n/opt/worm/control/state/\n/opt/worm/control/bin/\n/opt/worm/control/schema/\n/opt/worm/control/reports/\n\nSuggested files:\n\n/opt/worm/control/features/features.env\n/opt/worm/control/state/current.json\n/opt/worm/control/state/current.env\n/opt/worm/control/schema/features.schema.json\n/opt/worm/control/bin/worm-feature-control\n/opt/worm/control/bin/worm-feature-check\n\nDo not store secrets.\n\n============================================================\n2. FEATURE REGISTRY\n============================================================\n\nRegister at minimum:\n\nWORMOS_BASE\nMATERIAL3\nWORMLAUNCHER\nAPPSTORE\nPROTON\nBITWARDEN\nPROTON_DRIVE\nPRAGMATAPRO\nAUGURRI\n\nWIREGUARD_GO\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD\nWG_FAIL_CLOSED\nPROTECTED_DNS\nWG_AUTOSTART\nWG_ON_OFF\nWG_CONFIG\nOPNSENSE_NETWORK\n\nOTA\nUPDATER\nWEB_INSTALLER\nROBOT\nCONTROL_API\nPRIVATE_API\n\nAdd any other actual feature discovered in current /opt/worm state.\n\nEach feature must expose:\n\nFEATURE_ID=\nDISPLAY_NAME=\nENABLED=ON|OFF\nTOGGLEABLE=YES|NO\nPRESENT=YES|NO\n\nSOURCE_STATUS=PASS|FAIL|PARTIAL|UNKNOWN|NOT_APPLICABLE\nBUILD_STATUS=PASS|FAIL|NOT_RUN|NOT_APPLICABLE\nNETWORK_STATUS=PASS|FAIL|NOT_RUN|NOT_APPLICABLE\nRUNTIME_STATUS=PASS|FAIL|NOT_RUN|NOT_RUN_DEVICE_REQUIRED|NOT_APPLICABLE\n\nOVERALL_STATUS=\nBLOCKER=\n\nUPDATE_CLASS=OTA|SYSTEM_COMPONENT|APP|CONFIG|WEB|ROBOT|NONE\n\n============================================================\n3. ENABLED IS NOT PASS\n============================================================\n\nMandatory invariant:\n\nENABLED=ON\n\ndoes NOT imply:\n\nOVERALL_STATUS=PASS\n\nExamples:\n\nAUGURRI:\nENABLED=ON\nSOURCE_STATUS=FAIL\nOVERALL_STATUS=FAIL\n\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD:\nENABLED=ON\nSOURCE_STATUS=PASS\nBUILD_STATUS=PASS\nNETWORK_STATUS=PASS\nRUNTIME_STATUS=NOT_RUN_DEVICE_REQUIRED\nOVERALL_STATUS=PARTIAL\n\n============================================================\n4. UPDATE CLASS\n============================================================\n\nAssign the minimum valid update mechanism.\n\nExamples:\n\nWORMOS_BASE=OTA\nAUGURRI=OTA\nSELINUX/platform integration=OTA\n\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD=SYSTEM_COMPONENT\nif independently updateable by accepted architecture;\notherwise OTA.\n\nAPPSTORE=APP\nPROTON=APP\nBITWARDEN=APP\nPROTON_DRIVE=APP\n\nWG_CONFIG=CONFIG\nWG_ON_OFF=CONFIG\nOPNSENSE_NETWORK=CONFIG\n\nWEB_INSTALLER=WEB\nCONTROL_API=WEB or CONFIG according to actual implementation\n\nROBOT=ROBOT\n\nDo not classify a framework/system change as CONFIG merely to avoid OTA.\n\n============================================================\n5. DEPENDENCIES\n============================================================\n\nAdd explicit dependencies.\n\nAt minimum:\n\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD:\n  WIREGUARD_GO\n  WG_CONFIG\n  OPNSENSE_NETWORK\n\nWG_FAIL_CLOSED:\n  WORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD\n  OPNSENSE_NETWORK\n\nPROTECTED_DNS:\n  WORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD\n  OPNSENSE_NETWORK\n\nOTA:\n  WORMOS_BASE\n  FEATURE_CONTROL_GATE\n  WORMOS_NETWORK_GATE\n\nPRIVATE_API:\n  OPNSENSE_NETWORK\n\nROBOT:\n  OPNSENSE_NETWORK\n\nIf a required dependency fails:\n\nDEPENDENCY_GATE=FAIL\nOVERALL_STATUS cannot be PASS.\n\n============================================================\n6. IMPORT CURRENT VERIFIED STATE\n============================================================\n\nRead current evidence from:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/components\n\nPrefer current source plus latest valid report.\n\nDo not trust stale reports blindly.\n\nKnown current state to revalidate:\n\nWIREGUARD_GO:\nBUILD_STATUS=PASS\n\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD:\nBUILD_STATUS=PASS\n\nWG_CONFIG:\nNETWORK_STATUS=PASS\n\nOPNSENSE_NETWORK:\nNETWORK_STATUS=PASS\n\nWORMOS_NETWORK_GATE=PASS\n\nAUGURRI:\nknown recent product-build blocker due to incomplete\nAugurriIconRenderer.kt unless already repaired.\n\nDo not mark AUGURRI PASS without current validation.\n\n============================================================\n7. ON/OFF CONTROL\n============================================================\n\nImplement commands:\n\nworm-feature-control list\nworm-feature-control status <feature>\nworm-feature-control on <feature>\nworm-feature-control off <feature>\nworm-feature-control check\nworm-feature-control gate\n\nRules:\n\n- only TOGGLEABLE=YES may be changed\n- OFF must not delete source\n- OFF must not bypass security dependencies\n- mandatory security/network features may be TOGGLEABLE=NO\n\nFor WireGuard ON/OFF:\n\nON:\nWG_RUNTIME_REQUESTED=YES\n\nOFF:\nWG_RUNTIME_REQUESTED=NO\nWG_AUTOSTART=OFF\n\nDo not allow OFF to create uncontrolled public bypass.\n\n============================================================\n8. GLOBAL FEATURE GATE\n============================================================\n\nEvaluate all ENABLED build-critical features.\n\nProduce:\n\nFEATURES_DISCOVERED=\nFEATURES_ENABLED=\nFEATURES_DISABLED=\n\nFEATURES_PASS=\nFEATURES_FAIL=\nFEATURES_PARTIAL=\nFEATURES_RUNTIME_PENDING=\n\nFor each enabled feature required for product build:\n\nSOURCE_STATUS must not be FAIL/UNKNOWN\nrequired BUILD prerequisite must PASS\nrequired NETWORK prerequisite must PASS\n\nThen:\n\nFEATURE_CONTROL_GATE=PASS\n\nOtherwise:\n\nFEATURE_CONTROL_GATE=FAIL\n\n============================================================\n9. BUILD AUTHORIZATION\n============================================================\n\nPermanent rule:\n\nBUILD_ALLOWED <=>\nPREBUILD_GATE=PASS\nAND FEATURE_CONTROL_GATE=PASS\nAND WORMOS_NETWORK_GATE=PASS\n\nIf not:\n\nBUILD_ALLOWED=NO\n\nDo not auto-start a build.\n\n============================================================\n10. OUTPUT FORMAT\n============================================================\n\n`worm-feature-control list` should display:\n\nFEATURE                 ON/OFF  SOURCE   BUILD    NETWORK  RUNTIME   UPDATE\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWORMOS_BASE             ON      PASS     ...      N/A      N/A       OTA\nAUGURRI                 ON      FAIL     FAIL     N/A      N/A       OTA\nWIREGUARD_GO            ON      PASS     PASS     N/A      N/A       OTA\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD     ON      PASS     PASS     PASS     PENDING   SYSTEM_COMPONENT\nWG_CONFIG               ON      PASS     N/A      PASS     PENDING   CONFIG\nOPNSENSE_NETWORK        ON      PASS     N/A      PASS     PENDING   CONFIG\n\nInclude:\n\nOVERALL\nBLOCKER\n\nin detailed status.\n\n============================================================\n11. MACHINE-READABLE STATE\n============================================================\n\nGenerate atomically:\n\n/opt/worm/control/state/current.json\n/opt/worm/control/state/current.env\n\nDo not expose private keys, PSKs, passwords or tokens.\n\nState should include timestamp and evidence references.\n\n============================================================\n12. DASHBOARD\n============================================================\n\nIf:\n\n/opt/worm/control/dashboard\n\nalready exists, expose current.json to the existing dashboard without\nredesigning it.\n\nDesired dashboard fields:\n\nfeature\nON/OFF\nstatus\nblocker\nupdate class\nruntime pending\n\nNo unrelated frontend changes.\n\n============================================================\n13. PREBUILD INTEGRATION\n============================================================\n\nIntegrate:\n\n/opt/worm/control/bin/worm-feature-check\n\ninto the existing mandatory pre-build sequence.\n\nBefore any build:\n\nworm-feature-check\n\nRequired:\n\nFEATURE_CONTROL_GATE=PASS\n\nThe checker must exit non-zero if the gate fails.\n\n============================================================\n14. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/CONTROL-FEATURE-REGISTRY-V1.md\n\nFinal report:\n\nFEATURES_DISCOVERED=\nFEATURES_ENABLED=\nFEATURES_DISABLED=\n\nFEATURES_PASS=\nFEATURES_FAIL=\nFEATURES_PARTIAL=\nFEATURES_RUNTIME_PENDING=\n\nAUGURRI_STATUS=\nWIREGUARD_GO_STATUS=\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_STATUS=\nWG_CONFIG_STATUS=\nOPNSENSE_NETWORK_STATUS=\nOTA_STATUS=\n\nFEATURE_CONTROL_GATE=\nPREBUILD_GATE=\nWORMOS_NETWORK_GATE=\nBUILD_ALLOWED=\n\nFILES_CREATED=\nFILES_MODIFIED=\nBLOCKERS=\n\nBUILD=NOT_RUN\nTARGET_FILES=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1114:{"session_id":"01a0867d-9a26-79f2-8b11-b08c7c089d74","ts":1788962778,"text":"IMPLEMENT RAM-ONLY NETWORK STATE POLICY FOR WORMOS / ROBOT / ANTANI\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nApply the approved persistence policy:\n\nPERSISTENT_NETWORK_STATE=PRIVATE_IP_ONLY\n\nPersist only non-secret private IP / tunnel addressing required to identify\nnodes on the private network.\n\nAll sensitive WireGuard and runtime network state must remain RAM-only.\n\nCanonical root:\n\n/opt/worm\n\nDo NOT build.\nDo NOT generate OTA.\nDo NOT modify OPNsense infrastructure in this task.\nDo NOT print or persist secrets.\n\n============================================================\n1. DEFINE PROFILES\n============================================================\n\nCreate two control profiles:\n\nwormos-mobile\nrobot-antani\n\nFor both:\n\nPERSISTENT_NETWORK_STATE=PRIVATE_IP_ONLY\n\n============================================================\n2. PERSISTENT STATE\n============================================================\n\nAllowed to persist:\n\nWORMOS_PRIVATE_IP=\nROBOT_PRIVATE_IP=\nANTANI_PRIVATE_IP=\nPRIVATE_SERVICE_IPS=\n\nand only other non-secret private addressing/subnet identifiers that are\nstrictly required.\n\nDo NOT persist:\n\nWIREGUARD_PRIVATE_KEY\nWIREGUARD_PSK\nWIREGUARD_RUNTIME_CONFIG\nWIREGUARD_SESSION_STATE\nWIREGUARD_HANDSHAKE_STATE\nPEER_RUNTIME_STATE\nDNS_RUNTIME_STATE\nROUTING_RUNTIME_STATE\nTEMP_API_TOKENS\nTEMP_SESSION_TOKENS\n\nRequired:\n\nPERSIST_PRIVATE_IP=YES\nPERSIST_PRIVATE_KEY=NO\nPERSIST_PSK=NO\nPERSIST_RUNTIME_CONFIG=NO\nPERSIST_SESSION_STATE=NO\n\n============================================================\n3. WORMOS-MOBILE PROFILE\n============================================================\n\nFor WormOS:\n\nPersist only the assigned private/tunnel IP and required non-secret private\nnetwork identifiers.\n\nRuntime-sensitive material must live only in memory.\n\nUse a runtime location concept equivalent to:\n\n/run/worm/wireguard\n/run/worm/network\n\nor the Android-appropriate in-memory/runtime mechanism.\n\nDo not require plain-text private key persistence.\n\nReport:\n\nWORMOS_PRIVATE_IP_PERSISTENCE=\nWORMOS_SECRET_RUNTIME=RAM_ONLY\nWORMOS_RUNTIME_CONFIG=RAM_ONLY\n\n============================================================\n4. ROBOT-ANTANI PROFILE\n============================================================\n\nFor Robot/Antani use tmpfs/runtime paths under:\n\n/run/worm/\n\nCreate/ensure runtime layout:\n\n/run/worm/wireguard\n/run/worm/secrets\n/run/worm/network\n/run/worm/dns\n/run/worm/control\n/run/worm/sessions\n/run/worm/tmp\n\nAll these runtime directories must be RAM-backed/tmpfs.\n\nPersist only private IP/service IP configuration under the canonical\nnon-secret config area in /opt/worm.\n\nRequired:\n\nROBOT_RUNTIME_STATE=RAM_ONLY\nANTANI_NETWORK_STATE=RAM_ONLY\nRUNTIME_SECRETS_PATH=/run/worm/secrets\nRUNTIME_NETWORK_PATH=/run/worm/network\n\n============================================================\n5. ZEROIZATION / STOP POLICY\n============================================================\n\nOn:\n\nWireGuard OFF\nservice stop\nservice restart\nshutdown\nreboot\n\nremove runtime-sensitive material.\n\nRequired:\n\nZEROIZE_ON_STOP=YES\nZEROIZE_ON_WG_OFF=YES\nTMPFS_CLEARED_ON_BOOT=YES\n\nDo not delete persistent private IP configuration.\n\n============================================================\n6. CONTROL INTEGRATION\n============================================================\n\nUpdate the central feature/control registry so it exposes:\n\nPERSISTENT_NETWORK_STATE=\nPERSIST_PRIVATE_IP=\nPERSIST_PRIVATE_KEY=\nPERSIST_PSK=\nPERSIST_RUNTIME_CONFIG=\nPERSIST_SESSION_STATE=\n\nWORMOS_SECRET_RUNTIME=\nROBOT_RUNTIME_STATE=\nANTANI_NETWORK_STATE=\n\nZEROIZE_ON_STOP=\nZEROIZE_ON_WG_OFF=\nTMPFS_CLEARED_ON_BOOT=\n\nAdd control checks:\n\nworm-feature-control status network-state\nworm-feature-control check network-state\n\n============================================================\n7. SECURITY CHECK\n============================================================\n\nSearch current persistent project/config locations for accidental sensitive\nWireGuard persistence.\n\nDo NOT print matching secret values.\n\nCheck at minimum:\n\n/opt/worm/config\n/opt/worm/control\n/opt/worm/scripts\n/opt/worm/worm-os\n/opt/worm/worm-robot\n\nRequired:\n\nPERSISTED_PRIVATE_KEY_FOUND=NO\nPERSISTED_PSK_FOUND=NO\nPERSISTED_RUNTIME_SECRET_FOUND=NO\n\nIf a real secret is discovered:\n\nSTOP\nreport only file/path/category\ndo not print the secret\n\n============================================================\n8. PRIVATE IP CHECK\n============================================================\n\nVerify private IP configuration is:\n\n- non-secret\n- syntactically valid\n- unique where required\n- consistent with accepted OPNsense/WireGuard addressing\n- stored in the canonical persistent config\n\nDo not change OPNsense in this task.\n\nReport:\n\nWORMOS_PRIVATE_IP_STATUS=\nROBOT_PRIVATE_IP_STATUS=\nANTANI_PRIVATE_IP_STATUS=\nPRIVATE_IP_CONFLICTS=\n\n============================================================\n9. BOOT RECONSTRUCTION DESIGN\n============================================================\n\nVerify that after reboot:\n\n1. private IP config remains available\n2. /run/worm runtime state starts empty\n3. runtime WireGuard/network state is reconstructed\n4. secrets are loaded/generated only into RAM\n5. no runtime state falls back to persistent storage\n\nRequired:\n\nBOOT_RUNTIME_RECONSTRUCTION=PASS\n\nDo not claim live runtime PASS unless actually tested.\n\nIf device/runtime test is required:\n\nRUNTIME_TEST=NOT_RUN_DEVICE_REQUIRED\n\n============================================================\n10. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/RAM-ONLY-NETWORK-STATE-POLICY.md\n\nFinal report:\n\nPERSISTENT_NETWORK_STATE=\nPERSIST_PRIVATE_IP=\nPERSIST_PRIVATE_KEY=\nPERSIST_PSK=\nPERSIST_RUNTIME_CONFIG=\nPERSIST_SESSION_STATE=\n\nWORMOS_PRIVATE_IP_STATUS=\nROBOT_PRIVATE_IP_STATUS=\nANTANI_PRIVATE_IP_STATUS=\nPRIVATE_IP_CONFLICTS=\n\nWORMOS_SECRET_RUNTIME=\nROBOT_RUNTIME_STATE=\nANTANI_NETWORK_STATE=\n\nRUNTIME_SECRETS_PATH=\nRUNTIME_NETWORK_PATH=\n\nZEROIZE_ON_STOP=\nZEROIZE_ON_WG_OFF=\nTMPFS_CLEARED_ON_BOOT=\n\nPERSISTED_PRIVATE_KEY_FOUND=\nPERSISTED_PSK_FOUND=\nPERSISTED_RUNTIME_SECRET_FOUND=\n\nBOOT_RUNTIME_RECONSTRUCTION=\nRUNTIME_TEST=\n\nFILES_CREATED=\nFILES_MODIFIED=\nBLOCKERS=\n\nBUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1115:{"session_id":"01a08677-3f76-7d13-b541-cc1429ce16b4","ts":1788963067,"text":"PATCH CONTROL: GLOBAL OPNSENSE-ONLY EGRESS POLICY\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nMake OPNsense the mandatory network egress/policy gateway for:\n\n- WormOS / Android\n- Antani\n- Robot\n- WormOS operational services\n\nRequired topology:\n\nWormOS/Android -> WireGuard -> OPNsense -> Internet/private network\nAntani/Robot   -> WireGuard -> OPNsense -> Internet/private network\n\nAll Internet traffic must traverse OPNsense.\n\nDo not build or generate OTA in this task.\nDo not expose private keys or PSKs.\n\n============================================================\n1. CONTROL POLICY\n============================================================\n\nAdd to /opt/worm/control:\n\nINTERNET_EGRESS_POLICY=OPNSENSE_ONLY\n\nWORMOS_FULL_TUNNEL=YES\nANTANI_FULL_TUNNEL=YES\nROBOT_FULL_TUNNEL=YES\n\nWORMOS_DEFAULT_ROUTE_VIA_OPNSENSE=YES\nANTANI_DEFAULT_ROUTE_VIA_OPNSENSE=YES\nROBOT_DEFAULT_ROUTE_VIA_OPNSENSE=YES\n\nDNS_VIA_OPNSENSE=YES\nDIRECT_WAN_BYPASS=NO\nFAIL_CLOSED=YES\n\n============================================================\n2. FULL-TUNNEL CONFIG VALIDATION\n============================================================\n\nValidate the accepted WireGuard/OPNsense configuration.\n\nFor IPv4 full tunnel require the effective policy to cover:\n\n0.0.0.0/0\n\nFor IPv6, if IPv6 is enabled, require equivalent full-tunnel routing:\n\n::/0\n\nDo not blindly modify peer configuration.\n\nFirst compare current WormOS, Antani, Robot and OPNsense configuration.\n\nReport:\n\nWORMOS_IPV4_FULL_TUNNEL=\nWORMOS_IPV6_FULL_TUNNEL=\nANTANI_IPV4_FULL_TUNNEL=\nANTANI_IPV6_FULL_TUNNEL=\nROBOT_IPV4_FULL_TUNNEL=\nROBOT_IPV6_FULL_TUNNEL=\n\n============================================================\n3. DNS POLICY\n============================================================\n\nRequire DNS resolution through the approved OPNsense/private DNS path.\n\nRequired:\n\nWORMOS_DNS_VIA_OPNSENSE=PASS\nANTANI_DNS_VIA_OPNSENSE=PASS\nROBOT_DNS_VIA_OPNSENSE=PASS\n\nPUBLIC_DNS_BYPASS=NO\n\n============================================================\n4. BOOTSTRAP EXCEPTION\n============================================================\n\nAllow only the minimum traffic required to establish WireGuard with\nOPNsense before the tunnel exists.\n\nCurrent expected exception:\n\nOPNsense WireGuard endpoint\nUDP/51823\n\nVerify against current authoritative configuration; do not assume the port\nif configuration has changed.\n\nThe exception may reach ONLY the configured OPNsense WireGuard endpoint.\n\nIt must not become a general Internet bypass.\n\nReport:\n\nWG_BOOTSTRAP_EXCEPTION=PASS\nWG_BOOTSTRAP_DESTINATION_RESTRICTED=PASS\n\n============================================================\n5. FAIL-CLOSED / KILL-SWITCH\n============================================================\n\nIf the WireGuard tunnel is unavailable:\n\nWormOS must not fall back to direct Internet.\nAntani must not fall back to direct Internet.\nRobot must not fall back to direct Internet.\n\nThe bootstrap connection to the OPNsense WG endpoint remains permitted.\n\nRequired:\n\nWORMOS_FAIL_CLOSED=PASS\nANTANI_FAIL_CLOSED=PASS\nROBOT_FAIL_CLOSED=PASS\n\nDIRECT_FALLBACK_TO_WAN=NO\n\n============================================================\n6. SERVICE POLICY\n============================================================\n\nRevalidate:\n\nOTA\nUPDATER\nWEB_INSTALLER\nAPPSTORE\nROBOT_CONTROL\nCONTROL_API\nPRIVATE_API\nPACKAGE_DOWNLOADS\nCONFIG_SYNC\nDNS\n\nRequired for each applicable service:\n\nVIA_OPNSENSE=PASS\nDIRECT_PUBLIC_BYPASS=NO\n\n============================================================\n7. CONTROL GATE\n============================================================\n\nExtend worm-feature-check / control gate.\n\nRequired:\n\nOPNSENSE_EGRESS_GATE=PASS\n\nPASS requires:\n\nWORMOS_FULL_TUNNEL=YES\nANTANI_FULL_TUNNEL=YES\nROBOT_FULL_TUNNEL=YES\nDNS_VIA_OPNSENSE=YES\nDIRECT_WAN_BYPASS=NO\nDIRECT_FALLBACK_TO_WAN=NO\nWG_BOOTSTRAP_EXCEPTION=PASS\nFAIL_CLOSED=YES\n\nThen build authorization becomes:\n\nBUILD_ALLOWED <=>\nPREBUILD_GATE=PASS\nAND FEATURE_CONTROL_GATE=PASS\nAND WORMOS_NETWORK_GATE=PASS\nAND OPNSENSE_EGRESS_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n8. RAM POLICY COMPATIBILITY\n============================================================\n\nPreserve the previously selected model:\n\nPERSISTENT_NETWORK_STATE=PRIVATE_IP_ONLY\n\nDo not persist plaintext:\n\nWireGuard private key\nPSK\nruntime WG configuration\nsession state\n\nRuntime-sensitive state remains RAM-backed.\n\n============================================================\n9. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/OPNSENSE-ONLY-EGRESS-POLICY.md\n\nFinal:\n\nINTERNET_EGRESS_POLICY=\nWORMOS_FULL_TUNNEL=\nANTANI_FULL_TUNNEL=\nROBOT_FULL_TUNNEL=\n\nWORMOS_IPV4_FULL_TUNNEL=\nWORMOS_IPV6_FULL_TUNNEL=\nANTANI_IPV4_FULL_TUNNEL=\nANTANI_IPV6_FULL_TUNNEL=\nROBOT_IPV4_FULL_TUNNEL=\nROBOT_IPV6_FULL_TUNNEL=\n\nDNS_VIA_OPNSENSE=\nPUBLIC_DNS_BYPASS=\n\nWG_BOOTSTRAP_EXCEPTION=\nWG_BOOTSTRAP_DESTINATION_RESTRICTED=\n\nWORMOS_FAIL_CLOSED=\nANTANI_FAIL_CLOSED=\nROBOT_FAIL_CLOSED=\nDIRECT_FALLBACK_TO_WAN=\n\nDIRECT_WAN_BYPASS=\nOPNSENSE_EGRESS_GATE=\n\nFEATURE_CONTROL_GATE=\nPREBUILD_GATE=\nWORMOS_NETWORK_GATE=\nBUILD_ALLOWED=\n\nBLOCKERS=\n\nBUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1116:{"session_id":"01a0867d-9a26-79f2-8b11-b08c7c089d74","ts":1788963513,"text":"CLEAN CONTROL PYTHON CACHE BEFORE TAG\n\nCanonical root:\n/opt/worm\n\nDo NOT build.\nDo NOT generate OTA.\n\n1. Remove generated Python cache artifacts only:\n\nfind /opt/worm/control -type d -name __pycache__ -prune -exec rm -rf {} +\nfind /opt/worm/control -type f \\( -name '*.pyc' -o -name '*.pyo' \\) -delete\n\n2. Ensure the appropriate WormOS/control Git repository ignores:\n\n__pycache__/\n*.py[cod]\n\nDo not modify unrelated ignore rules.\n\n3. Verify no generated Python bytecode is tracked or included in the\ncurrent implementation/provenance file list.\n\nRequired:\n\nPYTHON_CACHE_FILES_PRESENT=0\nPYTHON_CACHE_FILES_TRACKED=0\nPYTHON_CACHE_IGNORED=PASS\n\n4. Re-run control gates:\n\nNETWORK_STATE_CHECK=PASS\nFEATURE_CONTROL_GATE=PASS\nPREBUILD_GATE=PASS\nWORMOS_NETWORK_GATE=PASS\nOPNSENSE_EGRESS_GATE=PASS\nBUILD_ALLOWED=YES\n\n5. Correct RAM-ONLY-NETWORK-STATE-POLICY.md if its FILES_MODIFIED field\nincorrectly records generated __pycache__/pyc files as implementation files.\n\nDo not rewrite historical facts other than removing generated cache from\nthe implementation file inventory.\n\nFinal:\n\nPYTHON_CACHE_FILES_PRESENT=\nPYTHON_CACHE_FILES_TRACKED=\nPYTHON_CACHE_IGNORED=\n\nNETWORK_STATE_CHECK=\nFEATURE_CONTROL_GATE=\nPREBUILD_GATE=\nWORMOS_NETWORK_GATE=\nOPNSENSE_EGRESS_GATE=\nBUILD_ALLOWED=\n\nBUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1117:{"session_id":"01a08662-abaa-7ee2-9647-8d125dd7492c","ts":1788963994,"text":"AUDIT REAL OPNSENSE CONFIG — READ ONLY — NO SECRETS\n\nCURRENT VERIFIED STATE\n\nOPNsense disk=/dev/sda\nZFS_POOL=zroot\nZFS_STATE=ONLINE\n\nREAD_ONLY_ROOT=/mnt/opnsense-ro/zroot\nCONFIG_XML=/mnt/opnsense-ro/zroot/conf/config.xml\n\nThe pool is currently imported READ-ONLY.\n\nABSOLUTE RULE:\n\nDO NOT remount/import read-write.\nDO NOT modify config.xml.\nDO NOT reboot OPNsense.\nDO NOT change Hetzner networking.\nDO NOT print private keys, PSKs, passwords, tokens, hashes or credentials.\n\n============================================================\n1. PARSE CONFIG.XML SAFELY\n============================================================\n\nParse config.xml locally.\n\nExtract only non-secret network/policy information required to validate:\n\n- WireGuard configuration presence\n- WireGuard listen port\n- interface assignments\n- tunnel/private addresses\n- peer presence/count\n- AllowedIPs/networks\n- gateways/routes\n- DNS configuration\n- firewall policy relevant to WG\n- NAT relevant to WG -> Internet\n- IPv4/IPv6 configuration\n- aliases relevant to WormOS/Robot/Antani\n\nFor key fields report only:\n\nPRIVATE_KEY_PRESENT=YES|NO\nPSK_PRESENT=YES|NO\n\nFor public keys:\n\ndo not print the full value unless necessary;\nprefer SHA256/fingerprint/reference.\n\nNever print secret XML nodes.\n\n============================================================\n2. VALIDATE HUB ROLE\n============================================================\n\nDetermine from actual OPNsense config whether it implements:\n\nOPNSENSE_ROLE=WG_HUB_GATEWAY\n\nVerify independently:\n\nWORMOS peer -> OPNsense\nRobot/Antani peer -> OPNsense\n\nReport:\n\nWG_CONFIG_PRESENT=\nWG_LISTEN_PORT=\nWG_PEER_COUNT=\n\nWORMOS_PEER_FOUND=\nROBOT_ANTANI_PEER_FOUND=\n\nOPNSENSE_WG_HUB_GATEWAY=\n\n============================================================\n3. VERIFY PRIVATE ADDRESSING\n============================================================\n\nCompare actual OPNsense private/WG addressing with:\n\n/opt/worm/config/wireguard/opnsense-hub.env\n/opt/worm/config/wireguard/robot-worm.env\n/opt/worm/config/wireguard/system-state.env\n/opt/worm/control/features/egress-policy.env\n\nDo not modify either side.\n\nReport:\n\nWORMOS_PRIVATE_IP_MATCH=\nROBOT_PRIVATE_IP_MATCH=\nANTANI_PRIVATE_IP_MATCH=\n\nWG_SUBNET_MATCH=\nPRIVATE_IP_CONFLICTS=\n\n============================================================\n4. VERIFY FULL-TUNNEL POLICY\n============================================================\n\nUsing actual OPNsense config, verify whether the intended architecture is\nsupported:\n\nWormOS -> WG -> OPNsense -> Internet\nRobot/Antani -> WG -> OPNsense -> Internet\n\nCheck routing/firewall/NAT evidence.\n\nReport separately:\n\nOPNSENSE_WG_TO_WAN_ROUTE=\nOPNSENSE_WG_TO_WAN_NAT=\nOPNSENSE_WG_FIREWALL_POLICY=\n\nWORMOS_FULL_TUNNEL_SUPPORTED=\nROBOT_ANTANI_FULL_TUNNEL_SUPPORTED=\n\nDo NOT infer PASS merely because AllowedIPs contains 0.0.0.0/0.\n\nRequire the necessary OPNsense routing + firewall + NAT evidence.\n\n============================================================\n5. DNS\n============================================================\n\nDetermine actual DNS path/policy.\n\nReport:\n\nOPNSENSE_DNS_SERVICE=\nWG_CLIENT_DNS_SUPPORTED=\nDNS_TO_PUBLIC_BYPASS_POLICY=\n\nCompare with:\n\nDNS_VIA_OPNSENSE=PASS\n\nIf actual configuration disagrees with /opt/worm control state:\n\nCONFIG_DRIFT=YES\n\nDo not silently change control to PASS.\n\n============================================================\n6. FAIL-CLOSED / BYPASS\n============================================================\n\nCheck whether current OPNsense configuration supports the intended policy.\n\nDistinguish:\n\nCLIENT_FAIL_CLOSED\nOPNSENSE_FIREWALL_ENFORCEMENT\n\nReport:\n\nOPNSENSE_POLICY_ENFORCEMENT=\nDIRECT_WAN_BYPASS_EVIDENCE=\n\nDo not claim that OPNsense alone guarantees WormOS client-side fail-closed.\n\n============================================================\n7. BOOTSTRAP ENDPOINT\n============================================================\n\nVerify the actual WireGuard listener.\n\nCompare against the currently recorded bootstrap exception:\n\nUDP/51823\n\nReport:\n\nACTUAL_WG_LISTEN_PORT=\nBOOTSTRAP_PORT_MATCH=\n\nDo not change firewall/networking.\n\n============================================================\n8. CONTROL DRIFT AUDIT\n============================================================\n\nCompare actual OPNsense state against current control claims:\n\nINTERNET_EGRESS_POLICY=OPNSENSE_ONLY\nWORMOS_IPV4_FULL_TUNNEL=PASS\nANTANI_IPV4_FULL_TUNNEL=PASS\nROBOT_IPV4_FULL_TUNNEL=PASS\nDNS_VIA_OPNSENSE=PASS\nWG_BOOTSTRAP_EXCEPTION=PASS\nDIRECT_WAN_BYPASS=NO\nDIRECT_FALLBACK_TO_WAN=NO\n\nFor each return:\n\nMATCH\nMISMATCH\nNOT_PROVABLE_FROM_OPNSENSE\nNOT_CONFIGURED\n\nThen:\n\nOPNSENSE_CONTROL_CONFIG_MATCH=PASS|FAIL|PARTIAL\n\nNever turn NOT_PROVABLE into PASS.\n\n============================================================\n9. SECURITY\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nCONFIG_READ_ONLY=PASS\nCONFIG_MODIFIED=NO\nZFS_WRITE_OCCURRED=NO\nSECRETS_PRINTED=NO\n\nDo not copy config.xml into /opt/worm artifacts.\n\nReports must contain sanitized findings only.\n\n============================================================\n10. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite sanitized report:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/OPNSENSE-REAL-CONFIG-AUDIT.md\n\nFinal:\n\nOPNSENSE_ROLE=\nWG_CONFIG_PRESENT=\nACTUAL_WG_LISTEN_PORT=\nWG_PEER_COUNT=\n\nWORMOS_PEER_FOUND=\nROBOT_ANTANI_PEER_FOUND=\n\nWORMOS_PRIVATE_IP_MATCH=\nROBOT_PRIVATE_IP_MATCH=\nANTANI_PRIVATE_IP_MATCH=\nWG_SUBNET_MATCH=\nPRIVATE_IP_CONFLICTS=\n\nOPNSENSE_WG_TO_WAN_ROUTE=\nOPNSENSE_WG_TO_WAN_NAT=\nOPNSENSE_WG_FIREWALL_POLICY=\n\nWORMOS_FULL_TUNNEL_SUPPORTED=\nROBOT_ANTANI_FULL_TUNNEL_SUPPORTED=\n\nWG_CLIENT_DNS_SUPPORTED=\nBOOTSTRAP_PORT_MATCH=\n\nCONFIG_DRIFT=\nOPNSENSE_CONTROL_CONFIG_MATCH=\n\nCONFIG_READ_ONLY=\nCONFIG_MODIFIED=\nZFS_WRITE_OCCURRED=\nSECRETS_PRINTED=\n\nRECOMMENDED_CHANGES=\nBLOCKERS=\n\nBUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1125:{"session_id":"01a086a9-150c-79a2-93c4-5e37a042ce1a","ts":1788967027,"text":"NEXT: installa il pilot Headscale su Antani.\n\nCONTESTO VERIFICATO:\n- Debian 13 x86_64\n- Antani private IP = 10.90.20.10\n- WAN = 162.55.6.173\n- WireGuard esistente:\n    wg0 = 10.77.0.1/24\n    UDP 51820\n- Docker NON installato\n- Caddy già presente su 10.90.20.10:80/443\n- /opt/worm esistente\n- NON modificare WireGuard wg0\n- NON modificare routing\n- NON modificare OPNsense\n- NON modificare firewall\n- NON esporre Headscale sulla WAN\n\nOBIETTIVO:\ninstallare Headscale nativamente come servizio systemd per un pilot WORM.\n\n1. Prima verifica la versione stabile corrente di Headscale compatibile\n   con Debian 13 amd64.\n\n2. Installa SOLO Headscale.\n   Non installare Docker.\n\n3. Crea struttura persistente:\n\n   /opt/worm/headscale/\n     config/\n     data/\n     logs/\n\n4. Configura Headscale con:\n\n   listen_addr: 10.90.20.10:8088\n\n   database SQLite persistente sotto:\n   /opt/worm/headscale/data/\n\n   log level:\n   info\n\n5. NON usare:\n   127.0.0.1 come unico listen address\n   perché successivamente dovremo raggiungere Headscale\n   da altri nodi della rete privata.\n\n6. Per il pilot NON configurare ancora:\n   - exit node\n   - subnet routes\n   - OPNsense routing\n   - ACL complesse\n   - Android\n   - robot\n   - DERP custom\n   - modifiche DNS globali\n\n7. IMPORTANTE:\n   Headscale è il CONTROL PLANE.\n   Non creare una seconda interfaccia WireGuard manualmente.\n   Non modificare wg0/51820.\n\n8. Crea/abilita il servizio systemd Headscale.\n\n9. Avvia Headscale.\n\n10. Verifica:\n\n   systemctl status headscale --no-pager\n   ss -lntp | grep 8088\n   curl -v http://10.90.20.10:8088/health\n\n11. Verifica esplicitamente che NON ascolti su:\n    162.55.6.173:8088\n\n12. Verifica che dopo l'installazione siano invariati:\n\n    wg show\n    ip route\n    ss -lunp | grep 51820\n\n13. NON creare ancora utenti/nodi/preauth key.\n\n14. Alla fine mostra:\n    - versione Headscale\n    - percorso binario\n    - percorso config\n    - percorso database\n    - stato systemd\n    - indirizzo/porta di ascolto\n    - risultato health check\n    - conferma wg0 invariato\n    - conferma routing invariato\n\nFERMATI dopo queste verifiche."}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1127:{"session_id":"01a085a6-cfd1-7c01-8a04-fdc287459446","ts":1788967487,"text":"STAGE D BUILD-SPACE RECOVERY AUDIT\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nRecover enough space for Stage D target-files without destroying the\nsuccessful Stage A/B/C state.\n\nCurrent blocker:\n\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=NO\nAVAILABLE_KIB=64267884\nREQUIRED_KIB=104857600\n\nNeed at least 100 GiB available according to the mandatory gate.\n\nCanonical root:\n/opt/worm\n\nDO NOT build.\nDO NOT generate target-files.\nDO NOT generate OTA.\nDO NOT delete anything until classified safe.\n\n============================================================\n1. DISK INVENTORY\n============================================================\n\nReport:\n\ndf -h\ndf -i\n\nMeasure largest directories under:\n\n/opt/worm/build\n/opt/worm/src\n/opt/worm/artifacts\n/opt/worm/cache\n/opt/worm/downloads\n/opt/worm/backups\n/opt/worm/worktrees\n/tmp\n/var/tmp\n\nUse same-filesystem measurements where appropriate.\n\nProduce top space consumers.\n\n============================================================\n2. PROTECT SUCCESSFUL BUILD STATE\n============================================================\n\nMust preserve:\n\ncurrent Stage C product output required for target-files\nWormSystemWireGuard.apk\nlibwg-go.so\nbuild configuration/ninja metadata required by Stage D\naccepted Android source tree\nAugurri restored baseline\nartifacts/provenance\nreports\ncontrol state\nGit repositories\n\nClassify these:\n\nPROTECTED_FROM_CLEANUP=YES\n\n============================================================\n3. FIND RECLAIMABLE BUILD DATA\n============================================================\n\nIdentify only safely regenerable/unneeded data, such as:\n\nstale build attempts\nobsolete logs\nold temporary files\nabandoned build directories\nold caches\nPython __pycache__\nstale extracted/intermediate artifacts not referenced by current build\nobsolete worktrees if provably unused\n\nFor every candidate report:\n\nPATH=\nSIZE=\nCATEGORY=\nCURRENT_BUILD_REQUIRED=YES|NO|UNKNOWN\nSAFE_TO_DELETE=YES|NO\nREASON=\n\nUNKNOWN must never be deleted automatically.\n\n============================================================\n4. CHECK /opt/worm/build CAREFULLY\n============================================================\n\nDetermine which portions of:\n\n/opt/worm/build/out\n\nare required for current successful Stage C and target-files generation.\n\nDo NOT run a generic:\n\nrm -rf /opt/worm/build/out\n\nDo NOT run installclean/clobber unless explicitly proven compatible with\npreserving the current Stage C state.\n\nIdentify stale outputs from previous failed builds separately.\n\n============================================================\n5. CALCULATE CLEANUP PLAN\n============================================================\n\nTarget:\n\nminimum free space after cleanup >= 110 GiB\n\nUse 110 GiB rather than exactly 100 GiB to preserve a safety margin.\n\nReport:\n\nCURRENT_FREE=\nSAFE_RECLAIMABLE=\nPROJECTED_FREE=\n\nIf PROJECTED_FREE < 110 GiB:\n\nCLEANUP_SUFFICIENT=NO\n\nand STOP without deleting anything.\n\n============================================================\n6. CLEAN ONLY IF PROVEN SAFE\n============================================================\n\nIf and only if:\n\nCLEANUP_SUFFICIENT=YES\n\ndelete only candidates explicitly classified SAFE_TO_DELETE=YES.\n\nNever delete:\n\nsource\nGit metadata\naccepted baseline\ncurrent product output\ncurrent target/product/frankel\ncurrent Soong/Ninja state required by Stage D\nWireGuard artifacts\nprovenance\ncontrol\nprivate-IP configuration\n\n============================================================\n7. POST-CLEANUP VALIDATION\n============================================================\n\nAfter cleanup verify:\n\nPRODUCT_OUTPUT_PRESENT=PASS\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK_PRESENT=PASS\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_PRESENT=PASS\n\nAUGURRI_FILES_TRUNCATED=0\n\nFEATURE_CONTROL_GATE=PASS\nWORMOS_NETWORK_GATE=PASS\nOPNSENSE_EGRESS_GATE=PASS\n\nThen measure:\n\nFREE_SPACE_AFTER_CLEANUP=\n\nRequired:\n\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=YES\n\n============================================================\n8. STOP\n============================================================\n\nDo not start Stage D.\n\nFinal:\n\nCURRENT_FREE=\nSAFE_RECLAIMABLE=\nSPACE_RECLAIMED=\nFREE_SPACE_AFTER_CLEANUP=\nBUILD_SPACE_OK=\n\nPRODUCT_OUTPUT_PRESENT=\nWORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD_APK_PRESENT=\nWIREGUARD_GO_ARTIFACT_PRESENT=\n\nCLEANUP_PATHS=\nPROTECTED_PATHS=\n\nPREBUILD_STAGE_D=NOT_RUN_AFTER_CLEANUP\nTARGET_FILES_BUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA_BUILD=NOT_RUN\n\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1128:{"session_id":"01a085a6-cfd1-7c01-8a04-fdc287459446","ts":1788967885,"text":"Do not delete anything and do not start a build.\n\nWe want to move the WORM OS build's disposable working data to RAM.\n\nAvailable RAM tmpfs:\n  /dev/shm = 32 GiB\n\nPersistent build state currently exists under:\n  /opt/worm/build\n  /opt/worm/src/android\n  /opt/worm/artifacts\n\nAudit the current Stage C/D build pipeline and determine exactly which\ntemporary/cache/intermediate paths can safely be redirected to:\n\n  /dev/shm/worm-build/tmp\n  /dev/shm/worm-build/cache\n  /dev/shm/worm-build/work\n\nRequirements:\n- preserve all current Stage C state\n- do not delete /opt/worm/build/out/soong/.intermediates\n- do not modify existing artifacts\n- do not build\n- do not run OTA\n- do not write persistent configuration yet\n- estimate worst-case RAM requirement for each proposed RAM path\n- reject any plan that could exceed the 32 GiB /dev/shm limit\n- identify which build paths MUST remain persistent/on SSD\n\nThen propose the minimal patch needed to enable a RAM-backed build workspace,\nbut DO NOT apply it.\n\nWrite the audit report under:\n  /opt/worm/artifacts/reports/"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1129:{"session_id":"01a086a9-150c-79a2-93c4-5e37a042ce1a","ts":1788967982,"text":"NEXT: collega Antani come PRIMO client al control plane Headscale locale.\n\nCONTESTO:\nHeadscale:\n- v0.29.3\n- server = 10.90.20.10:8088\n- service active\n- health OK\n- config = /opt/worm/headscale/config/config.yaml\n- database = /opt/worm/headscale/data/db.sqlite\n\nRete Antani:\n- private = 10.90.20.10/24\n- WAN = 162.55.6.173\n- wg0 = 10.77.0.1/24\n- WireGuard UDP 51820 esistente\n\nVINCOLI ASSOLUTI:\n- NON modificare wg0\n- NON modificare UDP 51820\n- NON modificare routing esistente manualmente\n- NON modificare firewall\n- NON modificare OPNsense\n- NON configurare exit node\n- NON annunciare subnet routes\n- NON abilitare accept-routes\n- NON modificare DNS di sistema\n- NON usare il control plane pubblico Tailscale\n\nFASE 1 — verifica server_url\n\nPrima di installare il client, mostra il valore attuale di:\n\nserver_url\n\nnel file:\n\n/opt/worm/headscale/config/config.yaml\n\nVerifica che sia utilizzabile dal client Tailscale.\n\nNON inventare DNS o certificati.\n\nSe il server_url attuale NON è adatto al pilot con\n10.90.20.10:8088, fermati e proponi la modifica minima necessaria.\n\nSe è adatto, continua.\n\nFASE 2 — installazione client\n\nInstalla il client Tailscale ufficiale compatibile con Debian 13 amd64.\n\nNON installare un secondo server Headscale.\n\nAbilita e avvia:\n\ntailscaled.service\n\nFASE 3 — namespace Headscale\n\nCrea un utente/namespace Headscale dedicato:\n\nworm\n\nMostra il risultato.\n\nFASE 4 — registrazione Antani\n\nRegistra Antani nel control plane Headscale locale.\n\nUsa come login server ESCLUSIVAMENTE il server_url configurato\nin Headscale.\n\nHostname nodo:\n\nantani\n\nConfigurazione client:\n\n- accept-routes=false\n- accept-dns=false\n- advertise-exit-node=false\n- nessuna advertise-route\n\nNon usare login.tailscale.com.\n\nFASE 5 — verifica\n\nMostra:\n\ntailscale status\ntailscale ip -4\nip -br addr show tailscale0\nheadscale nodes list\nsystemctl status tailscaled --no-pager\n\nPoi verifica nuovamente:\n\nwg show\nss -lunp | grep 51820\nip route\n\nConfronta con lo stato precedente.\n\nRISULTATO ATTESO:\n\nwg0:\n10.77.0.1/24\nINVARIATO\n\ntailscale0:\nnuovo IP overlay Headscale/Tailscale\n\nHeadscale:\nvede il nodo \"antani\"\n\nRouting infrastrutturale esistente:\nINVARIATO salvo le route strettamente create automaticamente\ndal client Tailscale per il proprio overlay.\n\nIMPORTANTE:\nnon creare preauth key persistenti se non necessarie.\nSe serve una chiave temporanea per completare automaticamente\nla registrazione, creala non-reusable e con scadenza breve e\nNON stamparla nell'output.\n\nFERMATI dopo la registrazione e le verifiche."}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1130:{"session_id":"01a086a9-150c-79a2-93c4-5e37a042ce1a","ts":1788968940,"text":"We need to configure Antani as a WireGuard peer to the existing OPNsense gateway in the WORM Hetzner network.\n\nGOAL:\n- Antani must use OPNsense as its WireGuard gateway.\n- Prefer full-tunnel Internet routing through OPNsense.\n- Keep Hetzner private networking working.\n- Do not break SSH access.\n- Do not disable the firewall.\n- Do not expose WireGuard private keys in output.\n- Make the minimum safe changes.\n- Before applying changes, audit the current networking and produce a plan.\n- Then apply only if the plan is safe.\n\nCURRENT WORM NETWORK CONTEXT:\n- OPNsense WAN: 2.28.34.27\n- OPNsense private LAN: 10.90.10.1\n- Hetzner private network: 10.90.10.0/24\n- Antani is on the Hetzner private network\n- We want a separate WireGuard subnet:\n  10.90.20.0/24\n- OPNsense WireGuard IP:\n  10.90.20.1/24\n- Antani WireGuard IP:\n  10.90.20.2/24\n\nTASKS:\n\n1. Audit Antani:\n   - ip -br addr\n   - ip route\n   - ip rule\n   - resolvectl status if available\n   - cat /etc/resolv.conf\n   - systemctl status systemd-networkd NetworkManager networking 2>/dev/null\n   - wg show\n   - ls -la /etc/wireguard\n   - determine the primary Hetzner private interface\n   - determine current default route\n   - determine whether wireguard-tools is installed\n   - determine whether wg-quick is available\n\n2. Do not print any WireGuard private key.\n\n3. If WireGuard is not installed:\n   - on Debian 13 install only the required package(s)\n   - do not upgrade unrelated packages\n\n4. Generate a dedicated Antani WireGuard keypair if one does not already exist:\n   - private key:\n     /etc/wireguard/antani.key\n   - public key:\n     /etc/wireguard/antani.pub\n   - chmod 600 private\n   - chmod 644 public\n   - never print the private key\n   - print only the public key\n\n5. Build the Antani peer config at:\n   /etc/wireguard/wg-worm.conf\n\n   Expected local config shape:\n\n   [Interface]\n   Address = 10.90.20.2/24\n   PrivateKey = <read from /etc/wireguard/antani.key>\n\n   [Peer]\n   PublicKey = <OPNSENSE_WG_PUBLIC_KEY>\n   Endpoint = 2.28.34.27:51820\n   AllowedIPs = 0.0.0.0/0\n   PersistentKeepalive = 25\n\n6. IMPORTANT ROUTING SAFETY:\n   - ensure the WireGuard endpoint 2.28.34.27 itself remains reachable outside the tunnel\n   - preserve access to the Hetzner private network 10.90.10.0/24 via the physical/private interface\n   - preserve SSH reachability on Antani\n   - do not create a routing loop\n   - use policy routing or explicit routes if required\n   - do not remove the existing default route until WireGuard is verified\n   - prefer wg-quick routing logic if safe, otherwise explicitly document the chosen route rules\n\n7. DNS:\n   - audit current DNS first\n   - do not overwrite resolv.conf blindly\n   - if OPNsense is intended to provide DNS, configure it safely only after the tunnel is verified\n   - otherwise preserve current DNS during the first test\n\n8. Create a pre-flight validation script:\n   /opt/worm/scripts/wireguard-preflight.sh\n\n   It must check:\n   - OPNsense private IP reachable: 10.90.10.1\n   - OPNsense WAN endpoint reachable: 2.28.34.27\n   - current SSH route is preserved\n   - wg-worm config syntax\n   - /dev/net/tun availability if relevant\n   - required kernel module/support\n   - no duplicate 10.90.20.0/24 route\n   - current public IPv4 before tunnel\n\n9. Create a post-up validation script:\n   /opt/worm/scripts/wireguard-status.sh\n\n   It must show:\n   - wg show wg-worm\n   - latest handshake\n   - transfer counters\n   - ip route\n   - ip rule\n   - route to 10.90.10.1\n   - route to 2.28.34.27\n   - public IPv4 after tunnel\n   - DNS status\n   - no private key output\n\n10. Before starting wg-worm:\n    - stop\n    - print the exact OPNsense peer data I must configure:\n      Antani public key\n      Allowed IP = 10.90.20.2/32\n    - ask for OPNSENSE_WG_PUBLIC_KEY if it is not already present somewhere under /opt/worm/config or /etc/wireguard\n\n11. Once the OPNsense public key is available and config is valid:\n    - run preflight\n    - start wg-worm\n    - verify handshake\n    - verify 10.90.10.1 remains reachable\n    - verify 2.28.34.27 route does not go through wg-worm\n    - verify Internet works\n    - verify the public IPv4 seen from Antani is the OPNsense egress IP\n    - verify SSH remains reachable\n\n12. Persistence:\n    - enable wg-quick@wg-worm only after successful validation\n    - do not enable persistence before successful handshake + routing test\n\n13. Rollback:\n    create:\n    /opt/worm/scripts/wireguard-rollback.sh\n\n    Rollback must:\n    - disable wg-quick@wg-worm\n    - bring wg-worm down\n    - remove only routes/rules created by this setup\n    - preserve existing Hetzner networking\n    - preserve the WireGuard key files\n    - preserve logs/config for debugging\n\n14. Logging:\n    write a report to:\n    /opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WIREGUARD-ANTANI-SETUP-<timestamp>.md\n\n    Include:\n    - pre-state\n    - applied changes\n    - public key only\n    - routing rules\n    - verification results\n    - rollback command\n    - no private keys or secrets\n\nDO NOT:\n- disable firewall\n- flush iptables/nftables\n- delete existing routes blindly\n- modify OPNsense remotely unless credentials/API are explicitly available\n- change SSH configuration\n- reboot\n- expose private keys\n\nStart with the audit and plan."}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1132:{"session_id":"01a085a6-cfd1-7c01-8a04-fdc287459446","ts":1788969560,"text":"Apply the minimal RAM workspace patch proposed in your\nWORMOS-STAGE-D-RAM-WORKSPACE-AUDIT report.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- RAM workspace is opt-in via:\n  WORM_RAM_BUILD_WORKSPACE=1\n\n- Use RAM ONLY for:\n  TMPDIR\n  TMP\n  TEMP\n  GOCACHE\n\n- Keep persistent/on SSD:\n  OUT_DIR\n  soong/.intermediates\n  product output\n  target-files\n  artifacts\n  source\n  Git metadata\n  host tools\n  ccache\n\n- Use:\n  /dev/shm/worm-build/tmp\n  /dev/shm/worm-build/cache/go-cache\n\n- Keep parallel build configuration at 12 jobs where supported.\n\n- Do not start Stage D.\n- Do not build target-files.\n- Do not build OTA.\n- Do not delete existing build state.\n\nAfter applying the patch:\n\n1. initialize the RAM workspace\n2. validate permissions\n3. validate environment variables\n4. show df -h /dev/shm\n5. show free -h\n6. show swapon --show\n7. run no build\n8. write a report under /opt/worm/artifacts/reports/\n\nAlso remove/disable any WORM RAM configuration we created today that\nredirects ccache, OUT_DIR, generic cache, artifacts, source, or build\nintermediates into /dev/shm.\n\nPreserve the existing ccache installation; only remove its RAM redirection.\n\nDo not modify WireGuard/network configuration as part of this task."}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1138:{"session_id":"01a086f1-133d-75e2-9e82-3af63aa28a1f","ts":1788970920,"text":"echo \"===== ACTIVE BUILD / REPO =====\"\nps -eo pid,etime,cmd | grep -E \\\n'repo (sync|forall)|git (fetch|pack-objects|index-pack)|ninja|soong|make|gradle' \\\n| grep -v grep || true\n\necho\necho \"===== BUILD OUT =====\"\ndu -sh /opt/worm/build/out 2>/dev/null\nfind /opt/worm/build/out -maxdepth 2 -type f \\\n  \\( -name '*.img' -o -name '*.zip' -o -name '*.apk' \\) \\\n  -printf '%s %p\\n' 2>/dev/null \\\n  | sort -nr | head -30 \\\n  | numfmt --field=1 --to=iec-i --suffix=B\n\necho\necho \"===== REPO TMP PACKS =====\"\nfind /opt/worm/src/android/.repo -type f -name 'tmp_pack_*' \\\n  -printf '%s %TY-%Tm-%Td %TH:%TM %p\\n' 2>/dev/null \\\n  | sort -nr \\\n  | numfmt --field=1 --to=iec-i --suffix=B\n\necho\necho \"===== TOTAL TMP PACKS =====\"\nfind /opt/worm/src/android/.repo -type f -name 'tmp_pack_*' \\\n  -printf '%s\\n' 2>/dev/null \\\n  | awk '{s+=$1} END {printf \"%.2f GiB\\n\",s/1073741824}'"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1139:{"session_id":"01a086f1-133d-75e2-9e82-3af63aa28a1f","ts":1788970990,"text":"echo \"===== BEFORE =====\"\ndf -h /opt/worm\nfind /opt/worm/src/android/.repo -type f -name 'tmp_pack_*' -printf '%s\\n' 2>/dev/null \\\n | awk '{s+=$1;n++} END {printf \"tmp_pack: %d files, %.2f GiB\\n\",n,s/1073741824}'\n\necho \"===== DELETE STALE TMP PACKS =====\"\nfind /opt/worm/src/android/.repo -type f -name 'tmp_pack_*' -delete\n\necho \"===== VERIFY =====\"\nfind /opt/worm/src/android/.repo -type f -name 'tmp_pack_*' -print 2>/dev/null\ndf -h /opt/worm\ndu -sh /opt/worm/src/android/.repo 2>/dev/null"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1140:{"session_id":"01a08704-2ef8-7c71-a57f-de1bfe18d8d7","ts":1788971603,"text":"WORM NETWORK ARCHITECTURE — AUTHORITATIVE CROSS-LAYER AUDIT\n\nMODE:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> MINIMAL CHANGE -> VERIFY\n\nTHIS TASK IS AUDIT + GATE ONLY.\n\nDO NOT modify networking.\nDO NOT start wg-worm.\nDO NOT change routes.\nDO NOT change firewall.\nDO NOT change Hetzner network/VLAN.\nDO NOT modify OPNsense.\nDO NOT enable persistence.\nDO NOT build WormOS.\nDO NOT generate OTA.\nDO NOT print private keys/PSKs.\n\n============================================================\nOBJECTIVE\n============================================================\n\nResolve the complete network architecture across:\n\n1. Hetzner public network\n2. Hetzner Private Network / VLAN\n3. OPNsense VPS\n4. Antani\n5. Robot\n6. existing admin WireGuard wg0\n7. new WORM WireGuard wg-worm\n8. WormOS\n9. DNS\n10. Internet egress\n\nDo not validate components independently.\n\nValidate the complete packet paths end-to-end.\n\n============================================================\nA. DISCOVER PHYSICAL / HETZNER LAYER\n============================================================\n\nOn Antani discover without modification:\n\nip -br link\nip -br addr\nip route\nip rule\n\nIdentify:\n\nANTANI_PUBLIC_INTERFACE=\nANTANI_PUBLIC_IP=\nANTANI_DEFAULT_GATEWAY=\n\nANTANI_PRIVATE_INTERFACE=\nANTANI_PRIVATE_VLAN_ID=\nANTANI_PRIVATE_IP=\nANTANI_PRIVATE_PREFIX=\n\nVerify current expected private state:\n\nANTANI_PRIVATE_IP=10.90.20.10/24\n\nDetermine whether the private interface is:\n\nphysical\nVLAN subinterface\nHetzner private-network interface\n\nReport actual state, do not assume.\n\n============================================================\nB. OPNsense PHYSICAL MODEL\n============================================================\n\nUsing currently available evidence/reports only:\n\nOPNSENSE_WAN_IP=\nOPNSENSE_WAN_INTERFACE_IF_KNOWN=\n\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_IP=\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_PREFIX=\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_INTERFACE_IF_KNOWN=\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_VLAN_ID_IF_KNOWN=\n\nCurrent expected model:\n\nOPNSENSE_WAN_IP=2.28.34.27\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_IP=10.90.20.1/24\n\nMark every field:\n\nVERIFIED\nEVIDENCE_ONLY\nNOT_VERIFIED\n\nDo not invent live state.\n\n============================================================\nC. PRIVATE VLAN CONNECTIVITY\n============================================================\n\nValidate the intended server transport:\n\nAntani 10.90.20.10\n        <- Hetzner Private Network/VLAN ->\nOPNsense 10.90.20.1\n\nRequired architecture:\n\nPRIVATE_TRANSPORT_SUBNET=10.90.20.0/24\n\nCheck route only.\n\nDo not change anything.\n\nReport:\n\nANTANI_TO_OPNSENSE_PRIVATE_ROUTE=\nPRIVATE_VLAN_MODEL=\nPRIVATE_VLAN_GATE=\n\n============================================================\nD. PRESERVE ADMIN WIREGUARD\n============================================================\n\nExisting wg0 is management infrastructure and MUST remain separate.\n\nExpected:\n\nADMIN_WG_INTERFACE=wg0\nADMIN_WG_SUBNET=10.77.0.0/24\nADMIN_WG_LOCAL=10.77.0.1/24\nADMIN_WG_PEER=10.77.0.2/32\nADMIN_WG_PORT=51820\n\nVerify current state.\n\nRequired:\n\nADMIN_WG_PRESERVED=PASS\nADMIN_WG_OVERLAP_WITH_WORM=NO\n\nDo not reuse 10.77.0.0/24 for WormOS.\n\n============================================================\nE. WORM OVERLAY NETWORK\n============================================================\n\nAuthoritative intended overlay:\n\nWORM_WG_INTERFACE=wg-worm\nWORM_WG_SUBNET=10.90.30.0/24\n\nOPNSENSE_WORM_WG_IP=10.90.30.1\nANTANI_WORM_WG_IP=10.90.30.2\n\nWormOS devices must receive unique addresses from the same accepted\nWORM overlay or an explicitly defined child subnet.\n\nDo not assign addresses now.\n\nReport:\n\nWORM_WG_SUBNET_CONFLICT=\nWORM_WG_VLAN_OVERLAP=\nWORM_WG_ADMIN_OVERLAP=\n\nRequired all NO.\n\n============================================================\nF. DEFINE ROLES\n============================================================\n\nRequired architecture:\n\nOPNSENSE_ROLE=\n  EDGE_FIREWALL\n  WORM_WG_HUB\n  PRIVATE_NETWORK_ROUTER\n  DNS_POLICY_POINT\n  INTERNET_EGRESS_GATEWAY\n\nANTANI_ROLE=\n  PRIVATE_VLAN_NODE\n  WORM_WG_PEER\n  ROBOT_HOST\n\nROBOT_ROLE=\n  SERVICE_ON_ANTANI\n  TRAFFIC_POLICY_VIA_OPNSENSE\n\nWORMOS_ROLE=\n  MOBILE_WORM_WG_PEER\n  FULL_TUNNEL_CLIENT\n\nADMIN_WG_ROLE=\n  SEPARATE_MANAGEMENT_PLANE\n\nVerify that current configuration/evidence does not contradict these roles.\n\n============================================================\nG. AUTHORITATIVE PACKET PATHS\n============================================================\n\nDefine and validate each intended path separately.\n\nPATH 1 — Antani private management:\n\nAntani\n -> 10.90.20.0/24 private VLAN\n -> OPNsense 10.90.20.1\n\nPATH 2 — Antani WORM overlay:\n\nAntani 10.90.30.2\n -> wg-worm\n -> OPNsense 10.90.30.1\n\nPATH 3 — Antani Internet after full-tunnel activation:\n\nAntani\n -> wg-worm\n -> OPNsense\n -> firewall/NAT\n -> Internet\n\nPATH 4 — Robot:\n\nRobot process\n -> Antani\n -> wg-worm\n -> OPNsense\n -> destination\n\nPATH 5 — WormOS:\n\nWormOS\n -> WireGuard\n -> OPNsense\n -> private services OR Internet\n\nPATH 6 — WormOS to Robot:\n\nWormOS\n -> WG\n -> OPNsense\n -> WG/private routed path\n -> Antani/Robot\n\nPATH 7 — Admin:\n\nadmin peer\n -> wg0\n -> Antani\n\nThis path must remain independent of wg-worm.\n\nFor each:\n\nROUTE_DESIGN=\nFIREWALL_REQUIREMENT=\nNAT_REQUIREMENT=\nCURRENTLY_PROVABLE=\nBLOCKER=\n\n============================================================\nH. ROUTING OWNERSHIP\n============================================================\n\nRequired principle:\n\nOPNsense owns WORM routing policy.\n\nAntani must NOT become an accidental router bypassing OPNsense.\n\nCheck for:\n\nIP forwarding\npolicy routing\nextra routing tables\nNAT/masquerade\nDocker/container routes if relevant\nTailscale routes\nwg0 routes\nwg-worm planned routes\n\nReport:\n\nANTANI_UNINTENDED_ROUTER=\nROUTE_CONFLICTS=\nPOLICY_ROUTING_CONFLICTS=\nTAILSCALE_CONFLICTS=\nWG0_CONFLICTS=\n\nDo not disable anything.\n\n============================================================\nI. FULL-TUNNEL DESIGN\n============================================================\n\nDo not activate it.\n\nDetermine exact route model required so that:\n\nWormOS Internet -> OPNsense\nRobot Internet -> OPNsense\nAntani Internet -> OPNsense\n\nwhile preserving the physical path needed to reach the OPNsense WG\nendpoint itself.\n\nCritical invariant:\n\nThe route to the OPNsense WireGuard endpoint must remain outside the\nnew default WG route, otherwise the tunnel can route itself into itself.\n\nVerify expected endpoint:\n\n2.28.34.27:51820\n\nReport:\n\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_PIN_REQUIRED=\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_CURRENT=\nFULL_TUNNEL_ROUTE_LOOP_RISK=\n\nRequired:\n\nFULL_TUNNEL_ROUTE_LOOP_RISK=NO\n\nbefore activation.\n\n============================================================\nJ. DNS\n============================================================\n\nDefine intended DNS:\n\nWormOS -> WG -> OPNsense DNS\nAntani/Robot -> WG -> OPNsense DNS\n\nReport:\n\nDNS_PRIVATE_ENDPOINT=\nDNS_ROUTE_DESIGN=\nDNS_BYPASS_RISK=\n\nDo not change resolv.conf/systemd-resolved.\n\n============================================================\nK. RAM-ONLY SECRET POLICY\n============================================================\n\nCurrent policy:\n\nPERSISTENT_NETWORK_STATE=PRIVATE_IP_ONLY\n\nAudit new Antani files.\n\nSpecifically check:\n\n/etc/wireguard/antani.key\n/etc/wireguard/antani.pub\n/etc/wireguard/wg-worm.conf\n\nDo not print contents.\n\nReport:\n\nPERSISTENT_PRIVATE_KEY_FOUND=\nPERSISTENT_WG_SECRET_FOUND=\nWG_CONF_CONTAINS_SECRET=\n\nIf /etc/wireguard/antani.key contains the actual private key:\n\nRAM_ONLY_POLICY_GATE=FAIL\n\nDo not delete it in this audit.\n\nDefine the minimal remediation:\n\nruntime secrets -> /run/worm/secrets\n\nPersistent private IP/non-secret metadata may remain under /opt/worm.\n\n============================================================\nL. CROSS-LAYER ADDRESS TABLE\n============================================================\n\nProduce one authoritative table:\n\nNODE       PLANE       INTERFACE   ADDRESS          GATEWAY/PEER\nOPNsense   WAN         ...         2.28.34.27       Hetzner\nOPNsense   PRIVATE     ...         10.90.20.1/24    -\nAntani     PUBLIC      ...         actual           Hetzner\nAntani     PRIVATE     ...         10.90.20.10/24   OPNsense\nOPNsense   WORM_WG     wg-worm     10.90.30.1/24    -\nAntani     WORM_WG     wg-worm     10.90.30.2/24    OPNsense\nAntani     ADMIN_WG    wg0         10.77.0.1/24     admin-01\nWormOS     WORM_WG     future      RESERVED/PLAN    OPNsense\n\nDo not fill unknown fields by guessing.\n\n============================================================\nM. FINAL ARCHITECTURE GATE\n============================================================\n\nRequired before ANY wg-worm activation:\n\nPRIVATE_VLAN_GATE=PASS\nADDRESS_PLAN_GATE=PASS\nADMIN_WG_PRESERVED=PASS\nROUTE_CONFLICT_GATE=PASS\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_GATE=PASS\nRAM_ONLY_POLICY_GATE=PASS\n\nThen:\n\nWORM_NETWORK_ARCHITECTURE_GATE=PASS\n\nOtherwise:\n\nWORM_NETWORK_ARCHITECTURE_GATE=FAIL\nWG_WORM_ACTIVATION_ALLOWED=NO\n\n============================================================\nREPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WORM-NETWORK-ARCHITECTURE-AUDIT.md\n\nFinal:\n\nPRIVATE_TRANSPORT_SUBNET=\nWORM_WG_SUBNET=\nADMIN_WG_SUBNET=\n\nOPNSENSE_WAN_IP=\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_IP=\nANTANI_PRIVATE_IP=\n\nPRIVATE_VLAN_GATE=\nADDRESS_PLAN_GATE=\nADMIN_WG_PRESERVED=\nROUTE_CONFLICT_GATE=\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_GATE=\nRAM_ONLY_POLICY_GATE=\n\nWORM_NETWORK_ARCHITECTURE_GATE=\nWG_WORM_ACTIVATION_ALLOWED=\n\nOPNSENSE_LIVE_CONFIG_GATE=\nBLOCKERS=\n\nCHANGES_MADE=NONE\nWG_WORM_STARTED=NO\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_CHANGED=NO\nFIREWALL_CHANGED=NO\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1142:{"session_id":"01a08704-2ef8-7c71-a57f-de1bfe18d8d7","ts":1788972249,"text":"WORM NETWORK — MINIMAL CHANGE 1\nRAM-ONLY WIREGUARD SECRET/CONFIG MIGRATION\n\nMODE:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> MINIMAL CHANGE -> VERIFY\n\nCURRENT FINDING:\n\nANTANI_PRIVATE_KEY_PERSISTENT=YES\nWG_WORM_CONF_PERSISTENT=YES\nWG_WORM_CONF_CONTAINS_PRIVATE_KEY=YES\nRAM_ONLY_POLICY_GATE=FAIL\n\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE=RAM-only key/config correction\n\nCanonical root:\n/opt/worm\n\nABSOLUTE RULES:\n\nDO NOT print private key.\nDO NOT print PSK.\nDO NOT regenerate/change WireGuard identity unless unavoidable.\nDO NOT start wg-worm.\nDO NOT modify wg0.\nDO NOT change routes.\nDO NOT change default route.\nDO NOT change firewall.\nDO NOT modify OPNsense.\nDO NOT modify Hetzner networking.\n\n============================================================\n1. PRE-MIGRATION IDENTITY CHECK\n============================================================\n\nWithout printing key material:\n\nverify:\n\n/etc/wireguard/antani.key\n/etc/wireguard/antani.pub\n/etc/wireguard/wg-worm.conf\n\nDerive the public key from the existing private key in memory/pipe only and\ncompare it with antani.pub.\n\nReport only:\n\nPRIVATE_KEY_PRESENT=\nPUBLIC_KEY_PRESENT=\nPRIVATE_PUBLIC_KEY_MATCH=\n\nRecord fingerprints/hashes only if needed.\n\nRequired:\n\nPRIVATE_PUBLIC_KEY_MATCH=PASS\n\nIf FAIL:\n\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n2. PREPARE RAM RUNTIME\n============================================================\n\nRequired runtime paths:\n\n/run/worm/secrets\n/run/worm/wireguard\n\nVerify these paths are actually RAM-backed/tmpfs.\n\nSet restrictive permissions appropriate for secret runtime state.\n\nRequired:\n\nRUNTIME_PATH_RAM_BACKED=PASS\nRUNTIME_SECRET_PERMISSIONS=PASS\n\n============================================================\n3. MIGRATE EXISTING IDENTITY WITHOUT ROTATION\n============================================================\n\nPreserve the CURRENT WireGuard identity.\n\nMove/copy the existing private-key material into:\n\n/run/worm/secrets/antani.key\n\nwithout displaying it.\n\nGenerate runtime wg-worm configuration under:\n\n/run/worm/wireguard/wg-worm.conf\n\nusing the same current identity and accepted non-secret configuration.\n\nThe runtime config may reference the runtime secret or otherwise consume it\nwithout creating another persistent copy.\n\nRequired:\n\nWG_IDENTITY_ROTATED=NO\n\n============================================================\n4. REMOVE PERSISTENT SECRET MATERIAL\n============================================================\n\nOnly AFTER runtime identity verification succeeds:\n\nremove persistent plaintext private-key material from:\n\n/etc/wireguard/antani.key\n\nRemove/replace:\n\n/etc/wireguard/wg-worm.conf\n\nif it contains PrivateKey or other runtime secret material.\n\nDo NOT delete antani.pub merely because it is persistent; public key is not\nsecret.\n\nPersistent Worm configuration may contain ONLY accepted non-secret\nmetadata such as:\n\nprivate IP\nsubnet\nendpoint address/port\npublic-key reference/fingerprint\nfeature/policy state\n\n============================================================\n5. BOOT/RUNTIME GENERATION\n============================================================\n\nUpdate Worm tooling so wg-worm runtime configuration is created under\n/run/worm/wireguard rather than /etc/wireguard.\n\nDo not embed a private key into persistent scripts/config.\n\nDo not solve reboot provisioning by persisting plaintext private key.\n\nIf the existing architecture cannot reconstruct/retrieve the same identity\nafter reboot without persistent plaintext secret material:\n\nBOOT_REPROVISIONING_GATE=NOT_IMPLEMENTED\n\nDo NOT invent a provisioning mechanism.\n\n============================================================\n6. VERIFY NO PERSISTENT SECRET\n============================================================\n\nPerform a scoped secret-persistence scan.\n\nDo not print matches containing secret values.\n\nCheck relevant persistent locations including:\n\n/etc/wireguard\n/opt/worm/config\n/opt/worm/control\n/opt/worm/scripts\n\nReport path/category only if a secret is found.\n\nRequired:\n\nPERSISTENT_PRIVATE_KEY_FOUND=NO\nPERSISTENT_PSK_FOUND=NO\nPERSISTENT_WG_RUNTIME_SECRET_FOUND=NO\n\n============================================================\n7. VERIFY RUNTIME IDENTITY\n============================================================\n\nWithout starting wg-worm:\n\nderive the public key from the RAM-only private key.\n\nCompare against the original antani.pub.\n\nRequired:\n\nRAM_PRIVATE_KEY_PRESENT=YES\nRAM_PUBLIC_KEY_MATCH=PASS\nWG_IDENTITY_ROTATED=NO\n\n============================================================\n8. RAM-ONLY GATE\n============================================================\n\nPASS requires:\n\nRUNTIME_PATH_RAM_BACKED=PASS\nRAM_PRIVATE_KEY_PRESENT=YES\nRAM_PUBLIC_KEY_MATCH=PASS\nPERSISTENT_PRIVATE_KEY_FOUND=NO\nPERSISTENT_PSK_FOUND=NO\nPERSISTENT_WG_RUNTIME_SECRET_FOUND=NO\nWG_IDENTITY_ROTATED=NO\n\nThen:\n\nRAM_ONLY_POLICY_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n9. DO NOT TOUCH OTHER FAILED GATES\n============================================================\n\nDo not attempt to repair:\n\nADDRESS_PLAN_GATE\nROUTE_CONFLICT_GATE\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_GATE\nOPNSENSE_LIVE_CONFIG_GATE\n\nThey remain separate subsequent steps.\n\n============================================================\n10. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nUpdate/write sanitized report:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WORM-WG-RAM-ONLY-MIGRATION.md\n\nFinal:\n\nPRIVATE_PUBLIC_KEY_MATCH=\n\nRUNTIME_PATH_RAM_BACKED=\nRUNTIME_SECRET_PERMISSIONS=\n\nRAM_PRIVATE_KEY_PRESENT=\nRAM_PUBLIC_KEY_MATCH=\nWG_IDENTITY_ROTATED=\n\nPERSISTENT_PRIVATE_KEY_FOUND=\nPERSISTENT_PSK_FOUND=\nPERSISTENT_WG_RUNTIME_SECRET_FOUND=\n\nBOOT_REPROVISIONING_GATE=\nRAM_ONLY_POLICY_GATE=\n\nADDRESS_PLAN_GATE=UNCHANGED\nROUTE_CONFLICT_GATE=UNCHANGED\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_GATE=UNCHANGED\nOPNSENSE_LIVE_CONFIG_GATE=NOT_VERIFIED\n\nWG_WORM_STARTED=NO\nWG0_MODIFIED=NO\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_CHANGED=NO\nROUTES_CHANGED=NO\nFIREWALL_CHANGED=NO\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1143:{"session_id":"01a08704-2ef8-7c71-a57f-de1bfe18d8d7","ts":1788972483,"text":"WORM NETWORK — MINIMAL CHANGE 2\nRETIRE LEGACY 10.60.0.0/24 WORM ADDRESS REFERENCES\n\nMODE:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> MINIMAL CHANGE -> VERIFY\n\nCURRENT STATE:\n\nWORM wg-worm runtime migration=PASS\nWORM_WG_RAM_ONLY_GATE=PASS\nADMIN wg0=LEGACY / OUT OF SCOPE\nBOOT_REPROVISIONING_GATE=NOT_IMPLEMENTED\n\nADDRESS_PLAN_GATE=FAIL because stale WORM references remain.\n\nAUTHORITATIVE ADDRESS PLAN:\n\nPRIVATE_TRANSPORT_SUBNET=10.90.20.0/24\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_IP=10.90.20.1\nANTANI_PRIVATE_IP=10.90.20.10\n\nWORM_WG_SUBNET=10.90.30.0/24\nOPNSENSE_WORM_WG_IP=10.90.30.1\nANTANI_WORM_WG_IP=10.90.30.2\n\nADMIN_WG_SUBNET=10.77.0.0/24\n\nLegacy WORM values to retire:\n\n10.60.0.0/24\n10.60.0.1\n10.60.0.10\n\nCanonical root:\n/opt/worm\n\nABSOLUTE RULES:\n\nDO NOT start wg-worm.\nDO NOT modify wg0.\nDO NOT change live routes.\nDO NOT change default route.\nDO NOT change ip_forward.\nDO NOT change firewall.\nDO NOT modify OPNsense.\nDO NOT modify Hetzner networking.\nDO NOT print secrets.\nDO NOT build.\nDO NOT generate OTA.\n\n============================================================\n1. AUDIT ALL LEGACY REFERENCES\n============================================================\n\nSearch /opt/worm for references to:\n\n10.60.0.0/24\n10.60.0.1\n10.60.0.10\n\nClassify every match:\n\nACTIVE_CONFIG\nSOURCE_CONFIG\nGENERATED_STATE\nHISTORICAL_REPORT\nDOCUMENTATION\nBUILD_OUTPUT\nUNKNOWN\n\nDo not modify historical reports merely because they record old state.\n\nReport:\n\nLEGACY_REFERENCES_TOTAL=\nLEGACY_ACTIVE_CONFIG=\nLEGACY_SOURCE_CONFIG=\nLEGACY_HISTORICAL_ONLY=\nLEGACY_UNKNOWN=\n\nUNKNOWN => STOP before modification.\n\n============================================================\n2. AUTHORITATIVE SOURCE CORRECTION\n============================================================\n\nCorrect only ACTIVE_CONFIG and SOURCE_CONFIG that still define the old\nWORM topology.\n\nKnown candidates from previous audit include:\n\n/opt/worm/config/network/network-state-policy.env\n/opt/worm/config/network/profiles/wormos-mobile.env\n/opt/worm/src/android/vendor/worm/WormSystemWireGuard/res/values/worm_network.xml\n\nAlso inspect current authoritative WireGuard/control configuration.\n\nMap semantically, not by blind global replacement:\n\nold WORM subnet:\n10.60.0.0/24\n->\n10.90.30.0/24\n\nold OPNsense WORM address:\n10.60.0.1\n->\n10.90.30.1\n\nold Antani/WORM client address:\n10.60.0.10\n->\nuse the correct node-specific address.\n\nFor Antani wg-worm this is:\n10.90.30.2\n\nDo NOT blindly replace 10.60.0.10 with an Antani address inside WormOS\ndevice configuration if that field represents a WormOS client address.\n\nIf semantic ownership is ambiguous:\n\nSTOP and report the file/field.\n\n============================================================\n3. DO NOT ALTER ACCEPTED HISTORICAL EVIDENCE\n============================================================\n\nReports/provenance describing the previous 10.60.x configuration must\nremain historical evidence.\n\nDo not rewrite old reports to make history appear different.\n\nCurrent state/report generators may be updated to the new authoritative\nplan.\n\n============================================================\n4. VERIFY ADDRESS PLAN\n============================================================\n\nAfter correction, scan active/source configuration again.\n\nRequired:\n\nACTIVE_LEGACY_WORM_REFERENCES=0\nUNKNOWN_LEGACY_WORM_REFERENCES=0\n\nVerify:\n\nPRIVATE_TRANSPORT_SUBNET=10.90.20.0/24\nWORM_WG_SUBNET=10.90.30.0/24\nADMIN_WG_SUBNET=10.77.0.0/24\n\nSUBNET_OVERLAPS=NO\nADDRESS_DUPLICATES=NO\n\nThen:\n\nADDRESS_PLAN_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n5. VERIFY NO NETWORK STATE CHANGED\n============================================================\n\nCompare before/after live state:\n\nip -br addr\nip route\nip rule\nwg show\n\nRequired:\n\nWG_WORM_STARTED=NO\nWG0_MODIFIED=NO\nLIVE_ADDRESSES_CHANGED=NO\nROUTES_CHANGED=NO\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_CHANGED=NO\nIP_FORWARD_CHANGED=NO\nFIREWALL_CHANGED=NO\n\n============================================================\n6. PRESERVE RAM-ONLY WORM STATE\n============================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nRAM_PRIVATE_KEY_PRESENT=YES\nRAM_PUBLIC_KEY_MATCH=PASS\n\nPERSISTENT_WORM_PRIVATE_KEY_FOUND=NO\nPERSISTENT_WORM_PSK_FOUND=NO\n\nDo not include legacy admin wg0 in the WORM-specific gate.\n\nReport separately:\n\nWORM_WG_RAM_ONLY_GATE=PASS\nADMIN_WG_RAM_ONLY_GATE=FAIL_LEGACY\nGLOBAL_RAM_ONLY_STATUS=PARTIAL\n\n============================================================\n7. DO NOT FIX NEXT GATES\n============================================================\n\nDo NOT repair yet:\n\nROUTE_CONFLICT_GATE\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_GATE\nOPNSENSE_LIVE_CONFIG_GATE\nBOOT_REPROVISIONING_GATE\n\n============================================================\n8. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WORM-ADDRESS-PLAN-MIGRATION.md\n\nFinal:\n\nLEGACY_REFERENCES_TOTAL=\nLEGACY_ACTIVE_CONFIG=\nLEGACY_SOURCE_CONFIG=\nLEGACY_HISTORICAL_ONLY=\nLEGACY_UNKNOWN=\n\nACTIVE_LEGACY_WORM_REFERENCES=\nUNKNOWN_LEGACY_WORM_REFERENCES=\n\nPRIVATE_TRANSPORT_SUBNET=\nWORM_WG_SUBNET=\nADMIN_WG_SUBNET=\n\nSUBNET_OVERLAPS=\nADDRESS_DUPLICATES=\nADDRESS_PLAN_GATE=\n\nWORM_WG_RAM_ONLY_GATE=\nADMIN_WG_RAM_ONLY_GATE=\nGLOBAL_RAM_ONLY_STATUS=\n\nROUTE_CONFLICT_GATE=UNCHANGED\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_GATE=UNCHANGED\nOPNSENSE_LIVE_CONFIG_GATE=NOT_VERIFIED\nBOOT_REPROVISIONING_GATE=NOT_IMPLEMENTED\n\nWG_WORM_STARTED=NO\nWG0_MODIFIED=NO\nLIVE_ADDRESSES_CHANGED=NO\nROUTES_CHANGED=NO\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_CHANGED=NO\nIP_FORWARD_CHANGED=NO\nFIREWALL_CHANGED=NO\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1144:{"session_id":"01a08704-2ef8-7c71-a57f-de1bfe18d8d7","ts":1788972854,"text":"NEXT NETWORK COMPONENT: OPNSENSE DNS\n\nMODE:\nAUDIT ONLY\n\nDo not install Pi-hole.\nDo not modify Unbound.\nDo not modify firewall.\nDo not modify OPNsense.\nDo not modify WormOS.\nDo not change DNS.\n\nDetermine from existing OPNsense evidence:\n\nUNBOUND_PRESENT=\nUNBOUND_ENABLED=\nUNBOUND_LISTEN_INTERFACES=\nUNBOUND_PRIVATE_NETWORK_ACCESS=\n\nDNS_BLOCKLIST_SUPPORT=\nDNSSEC_STATUS=\nDNS_OVER_TLS_STATUS=\n\nDetermine desired reachability from:\n\n10.90.20.0/24\n10.90.30.0/24\n10.77.0.0/24\n\nDefine target architecture:\n\nDNS_POLICY=OPNSENSE_ONLY\nDNS_RESOLVER=UNBOUND\n\nWORMOS_DNS_VIA_OPNSENSE=REQUIRED\nANTANI_DNS_VIA_OPNSENSE=REQUIRED\nROBOT_DNS_VIA_OPNSENSE=REQUIRED\n\nAssess:\n\nDIRECT_DNS_BYPASS_RISK=\nANDROID_PRIVATE_DNS_BYPASS_RISK=\nDOH_BYPASS_RISK=\nDOT_BYPASS_RISK=\n\nCompare options:\n\nA = OPNsense Unbound only\nB = OPNsense Unbound + blocklists\nC = Pi-hole separate service behind OPNsense\n\nRecommend the minimum architecture satisfying:\n- private DNS\n- filtering\n- DNSSEC\n- no direct DNS bypass\n- compatibility with WireGuard full tunnel\n- minimal additional infrastructure\n\nWrite:\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/OPNSENSE-DNS-ARCHITECTURE-AUDIT.md\n\nCHANGES_MADE=NONE"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1146:{"session_id":"01a08704-2ef8-7c71-a57f-de1bfe18d8d7","ts":1788973236,"text":"WORM NETWORK — MINIMAL CHANGE 3\nWG ENDPOINT PHYSICAL HOST-ROUTE PROTECTION\n\nMODE:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> MINIMAL CHANGE -> VERIFY\n\nCURRENT AUTHORITATIVE STATE:\n\nADDRESS_PLAN_GATE=PASS\n\nPRIVATE_TRANSPORT_SUBNET=10.90.20.0/24\nWORM_WG_SUBNET=10.90.30.0/24\nADMIN_WG_SUBNET=10.77.0.0/24\n\nOPNSENSE_WAN_ENDPOINT=2.28.34.27\nOPNSENSE_WG_PORT=51820\n\nPrevious route discovery:\n\n2.28.34.27 via 162.55.6.129 dev enp9s0 src 162.55.6.173\n\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE=WG endpoint host-route protection\n\nABSOLUTE RULES:\n\nDO NOT start wg-worm.\nDO NOT modify wg0.\nDO NOT change default route.\nDO NOT change ip_forward.\nDO NOT change firewall.\nDO NOT modify OPNsense.\nDO NOT modify Hetzner networking.\nDO NOT enable full tunnel.\nDO NOT build.\nDO NOT generate OTA.\n\n============================================================\n1. AUDIT CURRENT ENDPOINT ROUTE\n============================================================\n\nCapture:\n\nip route get 2.28.34.27\nip route show\nip rule show\n\nVerify actual:\n\nendpoint\ngateway\nphysical interface\nsource address\n\nRequired expected physical path:\n\nENDPOINT=2.28.34.27\nGATEWAY=162.55.6.129\nINTERFACE=enp9s0\nSOURCE=162.55.6.173\n\nIf actual values differ:\n\nSTOP.\n\nDo not install a route using stale values.\n\n============================================================\n2. CONFLICT CHECK\n============================================================\n\nBefore modification verify that:\n\n2.28.34.27 is NOT routed through:\n- wg0\n- wg-worm\n- tailscale0\n- 10.90.20.1\n- another policy-routing table\n\nCheck all relevant policy tables.\n\nReport:\n\nENDPOINT_ROUTE_CONFLICT=\nENDPOINT_POLICY_RULE_CONFLICT=\n\nIf either is YES:\n\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n3. MINIMAL HOST ROUTE\n============================================================\n\nOnly after audit PASS:\n\ninstall one explicit IPv4 /32 route protecting the OPNsense WireGuard\nendpoint over the currently verified physical public path.\n\nTarget semantic route:\n\n2.28.34.27/32\nvia 162.55.6.129\ndev enp9s0\nsrc 162.55.6.173\n\nDo NOT alter the default route.\n\nDo NOT alter 10.90.20.0/24.\nDo NOT alter 10.90.30.0/24.\nDo NOT alter 10.77.0.0/24.\n\n============================================================\n4. VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nAfter installation:\n\nip route get 2.28.34.27\n\nRequired:\n\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_GATE=PASS\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_PREFIX=/32\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_INTERFACE=enp9s0\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_GATEWAY=162.55.6.129\n\nVerify:\n\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_CHANGED=NO\nWG0_ROUTE_CHANGED=NO\nPRIVATE_VLAN_ROUTE_CHANGED=NO\n\n============================================================\n5. PERSISTENCE — DO NOT APPLY YET\n============================================================\n\nDetermine how this host-route SHOULD eventually survive reboot using the\nexisting Antani network management mechanism.\n\nDo not persist it yet.\n\nReport:\n\nHOST_ROUTE_RUNTIME_INSTALLED=YES\nHOST_ROUTE_PERSISTENCE=NOT_APPLIED\nHOST_ROUTE_PERSISTENCE_METHOD=\n\nWe first validate the runtime architecture.\n\n============================================================\n6. CONNECTIVITY SAFETY\n============================================================\n\nVerify route resolution for:\n\n2.28.34.27\n10.90.20.1\ncurrent SSH/admin path\n\nDo not send destructive traffic.\n\nRequired:\n\nOPNSENSE_ENDPOINT_REACHABILITY_PATH=PHYSICAL\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_ROUTE_PRESERVED=PASS\nADMIN_ACCESS_ROUTE_PRESERVED=PASS\n\n============================================================\n7. RECHECK CURRENT GATES\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nADDRESS_PLAN_GATE=PASS\nWORM_WG_RAM_ONLY_GATE=PASS\n\nLeave unchanged:\n\nROUTE_CONFLICT_GATE\nOPNSENSE_LIVE_CONFIG_GATE\nBOOT_REPROVISIONING_GATE\n\nDo not start wg-worm.\n\n============================================================\n8. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WORM-WG-ENDPOINT-HOST-ROUTE.md\n\nFinal:\n\nWG_ENDPOINT=\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_PREFIX=\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_INTERFACE=\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_GATEWAY=\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_SOURCE=\n\nENDPOINT_ROUTE_CONFLICT=\nENDPOINT_POLICY_RULE_CONFLICT=\n\nHOST_ROUTE_RUNTIME_INSTALLED=\nHOST_ROUTE_PERSISTENCE=\nHOST_ROUTE_PERSISTENCE_METHOD=\n\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_GATE=\n\nADDRESS_PLAN_GATE=\nWORM_WG_RAM_ONLY_GATE=\nROUTE_CONFLICT_GATE=UNCHANGED\nOPNSENSE_LIVE_CONFIG_GATE=NOT_VERIFIED\nBOOT_REPROVISIONING_GATE=NOT_IMPLEMENTED\n\nWG_WORM_STARTED=NO\nFULL_TUNNEL_ENABLED=NO\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_CHANGED=NO\nWG0_MODIFIED=NO\nIP_FORWARD_CHANGED=NO\nFIREWALL_CHANGED=NO\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1149:{"session_id":"01a08704-2ef8-7c71-a57f-de1bfe18d8d7","ts":1788973855,"text":"WORM NETWORK — MINIMAL CHANGE 4B\nRETIRE LEGACY 10.60.0.0/24 ROUTE ONLY\n\nMODE:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> MINIMAL CHANGE -> VERIFY\n\nAUTHORITATIVE FINDINGS:\n\nROUTE_10_90_0_16_OWNER=ifupdown:/etc/network/interfaces.d/worm-vswitch\nROUTE_10_90_0_16_REQUIRED=YES\nROUTE_10_90_0_16_ACTUAL_CONFLICT=NO\n\nROUTE_10_90_30_MORE_SPECIFIC_WINS=YES\n\nLegacy persistent route still exists:\n\n10.60.0.0/24\n\nand is created by:\n\n/etc/network/interfaces.d/worm-vswitch\n\nCURRENT GATES:\n\nADDRESS_PLAN_GATE=PASS\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_GATE=PASS\nWORM_WG_RAM_ONLY_GATE=PASS\nROUTE_CONFLICT_GATE=FAIL\n\nGOAL:\n\nRetire ONLY the obsolete 10.60.0.0/24 route.\n\nDo NOT solve forwarding in this task.\n\nABSOLUTE RULES:\n\nDO NOT modify 10.90.0.0/16.\nDO NOT modify 10.90.20.0/24.\nDO NOT modify 10.90.30.0/24.\nDO NOT modify 10.77.0.0/24.\n\nDO NOT change ip_forward.\nDO NOT modify nftables.\nDO NOT modify firewall.\nDO NOT modify Tailscale.\nDO NOT modify wg0.\nDO NOT start wg-worm.\nDO NOT change default route.\nDO NOT modify OPNsense.\nDO NOT modify Hetzner.\nDO NOT build.\nDO NOT generate OTA.\n\n============================================================\n1. AUDIT EXACT LEGACY DEFINITION\n============================================================\n\nInspect:\n\n/etc/network/interfaces.d/worm-vswitch\n\nIdentify only directives responsible for:\n\n10.60.0.0/24\n\nDo not print unrelated sensitive configuration.\n\nReport:\n\nLEGACY_ROUTE_CONFIG_FOUND=\nLEGACY_ROUTE_CONFIG_FILE=\nLEGACY_ROUTE_CONFIG_DIRECTIVE=\nLEGACY_ROUTE_REQUIRED=YES|NO\n\nRequired before modification:\n\nLEGACY_ROUTE_REQUIRED=NO\n\nIf not provably obsolete:\n\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n2. BACKUP MINIMUM CONFIG\n============================================================\n\nBefore editing, create a local timestamped backup of ONLY:\n\n/etc/network/interfaces.d/worm-vswitch\n\nDo not backup secrets unnecessarily.\n\nReport:\n\nCONFIG_BACKUP_CREATED=\nCONFIG_BACKUP_PATH=\n\n============================================================\n3. MINIMAL PERSISTENT CHANGE\n============================================================\n\nRemove/disable ONLY the directive that recreates:\n\n10.60.0.0/24\n\nPreserve:\n\n10.90.0.0/16 via 10.90.20.1\n10.90.20.x private transport configuration\nVLAN 4000 configuration\nall unrelated interface configuration\n\nDo not restart networking.\n\n============================================================\n4. REMOVE LIVE LEGACY ROUTE\n============================================================\n\nReconfirm live route exists.\n\nIf present and still exactly the obsolete:\n\n10.60.0.0/24\n\nremove ONLY that live route.\n\nDo not flush route tables.\n\nDo not restart interfaces.\n\n============================================================\n5. VERIFY PROTECTED ROUTES\n============================================================\n\nRequired after modification:\n\nLEGACY_10_60_ROUTE_PRESENT=NO\n\nROUTE_10_90_0_16_PRESENT=YES\nPRIVATE_10_90_20_ROUTE_PRESENT=YES\n\nVerify:\n\nip route get 2.28.34.27\n\nmust still resolve through protected physical path:\n\n2.28.34.27/32\nvia 162.55.6.129\ndev enp9s0\n\nRequired:\n\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_GATE=PASS\n\nVerify admin wg0 route unchanged.\n\n============================================================\n6. VERIFY PERSISTENCE SOURCE\n============================================================\n\nSearch active network configuration again.\n\nRequired:\n\nPERSISTENT_LEGACY_10_60_ROUTE_REFERENCES=0\n\nHistorical reports/provenance may still contain 10.60.x and MUST NOT be\nrewritten.\n\n============================================================\n7. GATES\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nADDRESS_PLAN_GATE=PASS\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_GATE=PASS\nWORM_WG_RAM_ONLY_GATE=PASS\nADMIN_WG_PRESERVED=PASS\n\nDo NOT mark ROUTE_CONFLICT_GATE=PASS yet because forwarding policy remains\na separate blocker.\n\nReturn:\n\nROUTE_CONFLICT_GATE=PARTIAL_FORWARDING_POLICY_REMAINS\n\n============================================================\n8. NETWORK SAFETY\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nWG_WORM_STARTED=NO\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_CHANGED=NO\nIP_FORWARD_CHANGED=NO\nNFTABLES_CHANGED=NO\nFIREWALL_CHANGED=NO\nTAILSCALE_CHANGED=NO\nWG0_MODIFIED=NO\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_CHANGED=NO\n\n============================================================\n9. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WORM-LEGACY-ROUTE-RETIREMENT.md\n\nFinal:\n\nLEGACY_ROUTE_CONFIG_FOUND=\nLEGACY_ROUTE_REQUIRED=\nCONFIG_BACKUP_CREATED=\n\nLEGACY_10_60_ROUTE_REMOVED=\nLEGACY_10_60_ROUTE_PRESENT=\nPERSISTENT_LEGACY_10_60_ROUTE_REFERENCES=\n\nROUTE_10_90_0_16_PRESENT=\nPRIVATE_10_90_20_ROUTE_PRESENT=\n\nADDRESS_PLAN_GATE=\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_GATE=\nWORM_WG_RAM_ONLY_GATE=\nADMIN_WG_PRESERVED=\n\nROUTE_CONFLICT_GATE=PARTIAL_FORWARDING_POLICY_REMAINS\n\nIP_FORWARD_CURRENT=\nNFT_FORWARD_POLICY=\n\nWG_WORM_STARTED=NO\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_CHANGED=NO\nIP_FORWARD_CHANGED=NO\nNFTABLES_CHANGED=NO\nWG0_MODIFIED=NO\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=Antani forwarding policy still requires fail-closed WORM rules\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE=Antani WORM forwarding fail-closed policy"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1155:{"session_id":"01a08704-2ef8-7c71-a57f-de1bfe18d8d7","ts":1788975665,"text":"OPNSENSE — MINIMAL CHANGE 7C\nRESCUE READ-ONLY CONFIG RECOVERY\n\nMODE:\nAUDIT ONLY\n\nThe OPNsense VPS is now authorized to be inspected from Hetzner Rescue.\n\nABSOLUTE RULES:\n\nREAD ONLY.\nDO NOT modify config.xml.\nDO NOT import ZFS read-write.\nDO NOT change firewall.\nDO NOT change interfaces.\nDO NOT change WireGuard.\nDO NOT install packages.\nDO NOT print passwords, private keys, PSKs or other secrets.\nDO NOT build WormOS.\nDO NOT modify Antani.\n\nKnown previous disk layout:\n\nOPNsense disk=/dev/sda\nZFS pool=zroot\nroot dataset=zroot/ROOT/default\n\nPrevious successful read-only method used:\n\nzpool import -f -N -o readonly=on -o cachefile=none \\\n  -R /mnt/opnsense-ro/zroot zroot\n\n============================================================\n1. DISCOVER AGAIN — DO NOT ASSUME\n============================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nlsblk\nblkid\nzpool import\n\nDetermine actual OPNsense disk and ZFS pool.\n\nReport:\n\nOPNSENSE_DISK=\nZFS_POOL=\nZFS_POOL_STATE=\n\nIf different from previous evidence:\nSTOP and report.\n\n============================================================\n2. IMPORT STRICTLY READ-ONLY\n============================================================\n\nImport zroot read-only.\n\nVerify:\n\nZFS_READONLY=ON\n\nMount/read the OPNsense root dataset without enabling writes.\n\nLocate:\n\n/conf/config.xml\n\nReport:\n\nCONFIG_XML_PRESENT=\nCONFIG_XML_SIZE=\nCONFIG_XML_SHA256=\n\nDo not print config.xml.\n\n============================================================\n3. SANITIZED CONFIG PARSE\n============================================================\n\nParse config.xml locally.\n\nNEVER output:\n\npassword hashes\nprivate keys\nPSKs\nAPI keys\ncert private material\ntokens\nsecrets\n\nExtract only non-secret networking metadata.\n\n============================================================\n4. INTERFACES\n============================================================\n\nDetermine:\n\nWAN_INTERFACE=\nWAN_IP=\n\nPRIVATE_INTERFACE=\nPRIVATE_IP=\nPRIVATE_PREFIX=\n\nVLAN_ID=\nVLAN_PARENT=\n\nCompare against target:\n\nWAN=2.28.34.27\nPRIVATE=10.90.20.1/24\n\nReturn:\n\nWAN_CONFIG_GATE=\nPRIVATE_CONFIG_GATE=\n\n============================================================\n5. WEBGUI / SSH\n============================================================\n\nDetermine configured:\n\nWEBGUI_PROTOCOL=\nWEBGUI_PORT=\nWEBGUI_LISTEN_INTERFACES=\n\nSSHD_ENABLED=\nSSHD_PORT=\nSSHD_LISTEN_POLICY=\n\nDetermine whether configuration explains:\n\n10.90.20.1:443 TIMEOUT\n10.90.20.1:22 TIMEOUT\n\nReturn:\n\nPRIVATE_WEBGUI_CONFIG_GATE=\nPRIVATE_SSH_CONFIG_GATE=\n\n============================================================\n6. WIREGUARD\n============================================================\n\nExtract sanitized WireGuard metadata only.\n\nDetermine:\n\nWG_ENABLED=\nWG_INSTANCE_COUNT=\nWG_LISTEN_PORT=\nWG_INTERFACE_ADDRESS=\nWG_PEER_COUNT=\n\nTarget:\n\nWG subnet=10.90.30.0/24\nOPNsense WG=10.90.30.1/24\nlisten UDP=51820\n\nDetermine presence of peer definitions corresponding to:\n\nAntani AllowedIP=10.90.30.2/32\nWormOS AllowedIP=10.90.30.3/32\n\nDo NOT print keys.\n\nReturn:\n\nANTANI_PEER_PRESENT=\nWORMOS_PEER_PRESENT=\nWIREGUARD_CONFIG_GATE=\n\n============================================================\n7. FIREWALL\n============================================================\n\nParse rules relevant only to:\n\nWAN UDP/51820\nPRIVATE -> OPNsense TCP/443\nPRIVATE -> OPNsense TCP/22\nWORM 10.90.30.0/24\n\nDetermine:\n\nWAN_WG_51820_CONFIGURED=\nPRIVATE_WEBGUI_ALLOWED=\nPRIVATE_SSH_ALLOWED=\nWORM_INTERFACE_RULES_PRESENT=\n\n============================================================\n8. NAT\n============================================================\n\nDetermine whether configuration contains outbound NAT/policy for:\n\n10.90.30.0/24 -> WAN\n\nReturn:\n\nWORM_OUTBOUND_NAT_CONFIGURED=\nWORM_EGRESS_CONFIG_GATE=\n\n============================================================\n9. UNBOUND / DNS\n============================================================\n\nTarget architecture:\n\nWormOS\n -> WireGuard\n -> OPNsense\n -> Unbound\n -> upstream DoT\n -> Internet\n\nDetermine:\n\nUNBOUND_ENABLED=\nUNBOUND_LISTEN_NETWORKS=\nWORM_SUBNET_DNS_ALLOWED=\nDNSSEC_CONFIGURED=\nUPSTREAM_DOT_CONFIGURED=\n\nReturn:\n\nOPNSENSE_DNS_CONFIG_GATE=\n\n============================================================\n10. CONFIG DRIFT\n============================================================\n\nCompare config.xml against authoritative target:\n\nPRIVATE=10.90.20.1/24\n\nWORM_WG_SUBNET=10.90.30.0/24\nOPNSENSE_WG=10.90.30.1\nANTANI_WG=10.90.30.2\nWORMOS_WG=10.90.30.3\nWG_PORT=51820\n\nReport exact non-secret differences:\n\nCONFIG_DRIFT=\nCONFIG_DRIFT_FIELDS=\n\n============================================================\n11. EXPORT NOTHING SECRET\n============================================================\n\nWrite ONLY sanitized report:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/OPNSENSE-RESCUE-CONFIG-AUDIT.md\n\nIf /opt/worm is not available inside Rescue, write the sanitized report\nto an explicitly temporary location for later retrieval.\n\nNever copy config.xml into /opt/worm.\n\n============================================================\n12. CLEAN EXIT\n============================================================\n\nUnmount/export read-only ZFS cleanly.\n\nRequired:\n\nCONFIG_MODIFIED=NO\nZFS_WRITE_OCCURRED=NO\nSECRETS_PRINTED=NO\n\n============================================================\nFINAL\n============================================================\n\nCONFIG_XML_PRESENT=\nZFS_READONLY=\n\nWAN_INTERFACE=\nWAN_IP=\nPRIVATE_INTERFACE=\nPRIVATE_IP=\nVLAN_ID=\n\nWEBGUI_PORT=\nWEBGUI_LISTEN_INTERFACES=\nSSHD_ENABLED=\n\nWG_ENABLED=\nWG_LISTEN_PORT=\nWG_INTERFACE_ADDRESS=\nANTANI_PEER_PRESENT=\nWORMOS_PEER_PRESENT=\n\nWAN_WG_51820_CONFIGURED=\nPRIVATE_WEBGUI_ALLOWED=\n\nWORM_OUTBOUND_NAT_CONFIGURED=\n\nUNBOUND_ENABLED=\nWORM_SUBNET_DNS_ALLOWED=\nDNSSEC_CONFIGURED=\nUPSTREAM_DOT_CONFIGURED=\n\nCONFIG_DRIFT=\nCONFIG_DRIFT_FIELDS=\n\nCONFIG_MODIFIED=NO\nZFS_WRITE_OCCURRED=NO\nSECRETS_PRINTED=NO\n\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE=\nBLOCKERS="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1157:{"session_id":"01a08704-2ef8-7c71-a57f-de1bfe18d8d7","ts":1788976311,"text":"OPNSENSE / HETZNER — LEVEL PRO\nRESCUE API -> READ-ONLY ZFS CONFIG AUDIT\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> MINIMAL CHANGE -> VERIFY\n\nWORK ROOT:\n/opt/worm\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nUse the already configured Hetzner API/access available on this server to:\n\n1. identify the authoritative OPNsense VPS\n2. verify its identity before any action\n3. enable Hetzner Rescue ONLY for OPNsense\n4. reboot ONLY OPNsense into Rescue\n5. obtain Rescue SSH access through the authorized mechanism\n6. discover the OPNsense disk/ZFS layout\n7. import ZFS STRICTLY READ-ONLY\n8. parse /conf/config.xml without printing secrets\n9. export zroot cleanly\n10. leave a sanitized report under /opt/worm\n\nThis is NOT an OPNsense configuration-change task.\n\n============================================================\nABSOLUTE SAFETY RULES\n============================================================\n\nNEVER print:\n\n- Hetzner API tokens\n- Rescue passwords\n- SSH private keys\n- OPNsense passwords/hashes\n- WireGuard private keys\n- WireGuard PSKs\n- API credentials\n- certificate private keys\n- secrets from config.xml\n\nDO NOT:\n\n- modify Antani\n- reboot Antani\n- modify WormOS\n- modify /opt/worm source/build state\n- modify OPNsense config.xml\n- import ZFS read-write\n- run pfctl -d\n- modify firewall\n- modify NAT\n- modify interfaces\n- modify WireGuard\n- start wg-worm\n- enable full tunnel\n- generate OTA\n- build Android\n\nOnly OPNsense VPS may be rebooted.\n\n============================================================\nA. DISCOVER HETZNER API CAPABILITY\n============================================================\n\nFind the existing Hetzner API tooling/configuration already available on\nthe server.\n\nDo not print credential values.\n\nDetermine:\n\nHETZNER_API_AVAILABLE=\nHETZNER_API_AUTH=PASS|FAIL\nHETZNER_API_SCOPE=\n\nList server metadata sufficient to identify OPNsense without exposing\nunnecessary account information.\n\nExpected OPNsense public IP:\n\n2.28.34.27\n\nRequired:\n\nOPNSENSE_SERVER_FOUND=YES\nOPNSENSE_PRIMARY_IPV4=2.28.34.27\n\nRecord:\n\nOPNSENSE_SERVER_ID=\nOPNSENSE_SERVER_NAME=\nOPNSENSE_SERVER_STATUS=\n\nIf more than one server could match:\n\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\nB. PRE-REBOOT IDENTITY GATE\n============================================================\n\nBefore any Rescue/reboot operation verify:\n\nTARGET_PRIMARY_IPV4=2.28.34.27\nTARGET_IS_NOT_ANTANI=PASS\nTARGET_IS_OPNSENSE=PASS\n\nAlso record Antani identity independently if available so there is no\npossibility of rebooting the wrong VPS.\n\nRequired:\n\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE=PASS\n\nIf FAIL:\n\nSTOP WITHOUT ACTION.\n\n============================================================\nC. RECORD PRE-RESCUE STATE\n============================================================\n\nUsing API/read-only probes record:\n\nSERVER_STATUS=\nRESCUE_ENABLED_BEFORE=\nPUBLIC_IP=\nDATACENTER=\nSERVER_TYPE=\n\nFrom Antani preserve current network evidence:\n\nip route get 2.28.34.27\n\nExpected protected route:\n\n2.28.34.27 via 162.55.6.129 dev enp9s0 src 162.55.6.173\n\nRequired:\n\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\nD. ENABLE RESCUE\n============================================================\n\nOnly after TARGET_IDENTITY_GATE=PASS:\n\nEnable Linux Rescue on the OPNsense VPS through the existing authorized\nHetzner API.\n\nUse the existing authorized SSH key mechanism if supported/preconfigured.\n\nDo NOT print Rescue credentials.\n\nReport only:\n\nRESCUE_ENABLE_REQUEST=SUCCESS|FAIL\nRESCUE_TYPE=\nRESCUE_SSH_KEY_AUTH_REQUESTED=YES|NO\n\nIf Rescue enable fails:\n\nSTOP.\nDO NOT reboot.\n\n============================================================\nE. REBOOT ONLY OPNSENSE\n============================================================\n\nAfter Rescue enable SUCCESS:\n\nreboot ONLY the verified OPNsense VPS.\n\nUse the least disruptive Hetzner-supported reboot/reset method that\nactually boots the enabled Rescue system.\n\nNever target Antani.\n\nReport:\n\nOPNSENSE_REBOOT_REQUESTED=YES\nANTANI_REBOOT_REQUESTED=NO\n\nWait/retry safely for SSH availability.\n\nDo not continuously hammer the endpoint.\n\n============================================================\nF. VERIFY RESCUE HOST\n============================================================\n\nConnect to the Rescue environment using authorized credentials/key.\n\nImmediately verify that this is Rescue and not Antani.\n\nCollect:\n\nhostname\nuname -a\nlsblk\nblkid\nzpool import\n\nDo not modify disks.\n\nRequired:\n\nCURRENT_HOST=OPNSENSE_RESCUE\nRESCUE_BOOT_GATE=PASS\n\nIf identity is uncertain:\n\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\nG. DISCOVER DISK / ZFS\n============================================================\n\nPrevious historical evidence suggested:\n\ndisk=/dev/sda\npool=zroot\nroot dataset=zroot/ROOT/default\n\nDO NOT assume these values.\n\nDiscover actual state.\n\nReport:\n\nOPNSENSE_DISK=\nPARTITION_LAYOUT=\nZFS_POOL=\nZFS_POOL_STATE=\n\nRequired:\n\nZFS_POOL_FOUND=PASS\n\n============================================================\nH. STRICT READ-ONLY ZFS IMPORT\n============================================================\n\nImport the discovered OPNsense pool strictly read-only.\n\nEquivalent safety properties required:\n\nreadonly=on\ncachefile=none\nalternate root under /mnt/opnsense-ro\nno persistent pool changes\n\nExample only if actual pool is confirmed zroot:\n\nzpool import -f -N \\\n  -o readonly=on \\\n  -o cachefile=none \\\n  -R /mnt/opnsense-ro \\\n  zroot\n\nThen mount/read only the required root dataset.\n\nVerify:\n\nZFS_READONLY=ON\nZFS_WRITE_OCCURRED=NO\n\n============================================================\nI. LOCATE CONFIG.XML\n============================================================\n\nLocate authoritative OPNsense:\n\n/conf/config.xml\n\nPossible mounted path may resemble:\n\n/mnt/opnsense-ro/.../conf/config.xml\n\nReport:\n\nCONFIG_XML_PRESENT=\nCONFIG_XML_PATH=\nCONFIG_XML_SIZE=\nCONFIG_XML_SHA256=\n\nDO NOT copy config.xml to /opt/worm.\n\nDO NOT print its raw contents.\n\n============================================================\nJ. SANITIZED OPNsense PARSER\n============================================================\n\nParse config.xml programmatically.\n\nNever emit secret-valued XML nodes.\n\nExtract ONLY non-secret network configuration.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nJ1. WAN\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nWAN_INTERFACE=\nWAN_IP=\nWAN_GATEWAY=\n\nExpected WAN IP:\n\n2.28.34.27\n\nWAN_CONFIG_GATE=\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nJ2. PRIVATE / VLAN\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nExtract:\n\nPRIVATE_INTERFACE=\nPRIVATE_IP=\nPRIVATE_PREFIX=\n\nVLAN_PRESENT=\nVLAN_ID=\nVLAN_PARENT=\n\nTarget:\n\nPRIVATE_SUBNET=10.90.20.0/24\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_IP=10.90.20.1/24\n\nPRIVATE_CONFIG_GATE=\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nJ3. WEBGUI\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nExtract:\n\nWEBGUI_PROTOCOL=\nWEBGUI_PORT=\nWEBGUI_LISTEN_INTERFACES=\n\nDetermine whether static config explains why:\n\n10.90.20.1:443\n10.90.20.1:80\n\ncurrently time out.\n\nPRIVATE_WEBGUI_CONFIG_GATE=\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nJ4. SSH\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nExtract sanitized SSH configuration:\n\nSSHD_ENABLED=\nSSHD_PORT=\nSSHD_INTERFACE_POLICY=\n\nDo not print authorized keys.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nJ5. WIREGUARD\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nExtract only metadata:\n\nWG_ENABLED=\nWG_INSTANCE_COUNT=\nWG_LISTEN_PORT=\nWG_INTERFACE_ADDRESS=\nWG_PEER_COUNT=\n\nTARGET:\n\nWG_INTERFACE_ADDRESS=10.90.30.1/24\nWG_LISTEN_PORT=51820\n\nCheck peers semantically without printing keys:\n\nAntani:\nAllowedIP=10.90.30.2/32\n\nWormOS:\nAllowedIP=10.90.30.3/32\n\nReport:\n\nANTANI_PEER_PRESENT=\nWORMOS_PEER_PRESENT=\nWIREGUARD_CONFIG_GATE=\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nJ6. FIREWALL\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nInspect only rules relevant to:\n\nWAN UDP 51820 -> OPNsense\n\nPRIVATE 10.90.20.10 -> OPNsense TCP 443\n\nPRIVATE 10.90.20.10 -> OPNsense TCP 22\n\nWORM 10.90.30.0/24\n\nReport:\n\nWAN_WG_51820_CONFIGURED=\nPRIVATE_WEBGUI_ALLOWED=\nPRIVATE_SSH_ALLOWED=\nWORM_FIREWALL_RULES_PRESENT=\n\nDo not modify PF configuration.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nJ7. NAT\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nDetermine whether:\n\n10.90.30.0/24 -> WAN\n\nis represented in outbound NAT/policy.\n\nReport:\n\nWORM_OUTBOUND_NAT_CONFIGURED=\nWORM_EGRESS_CONFIG_GATE=\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nJ8. DNS / UNBOUND\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nTarget architecture:\n\nWormOS\n -> WireGuard\n -> OPNsense\n -> Unbound\n -> upstream DoT\n -> Internet\n\nExtract:\n\nUNBOUND_ENABLED=\nUNBOUND_LISTEN_INTERFACES=\nWORM_SUBNET_DNS_ALLOWED=\nDNSSEC_CONFIGURED=\nUPSTREAM_DOT_CONFIGURED=\n\nAlso identify whether config currently supports client DNS policy through\nOPNsense.\n\nOPNSENSE_DNS_CONFIG_GATE=\n\n============================================================\nK. CONFIG DRIFT\n============================================================\n\nCompare actual config.xml to authoritative Worm design:\n\nPRIVATE:\n10.90.20.0/24\nOPNsense=10.90.20.1\n\nWORM WG:\n10.90.30.0/24\nOPNsense=10.90.30.1\nAntani=10.90.30.2\nWormOS=10.90.30.3/32\n\nWG UDP:\n51820\n\nDNS target:\nOPNsense Unbound -> upstream DoT\n\nReport exactly:\n\nCONFIG_DRIFT=YES|NO\nCONFIG_DRIFT_FIELDS=\n\nDo not alter anything.\n\n============================================================\nL. GATES\n============================================================\n\nReturn separately:\n\nWAN_CONFIG_GATE=\nPRIVATE_CONFIG_GATE=\nPRIVATE_WEBGUI_CONFIG_GATE=\n\nWIREGUARD_CONFIG_GATE=\nWIREGUARD_FIREWALL_GATE=\n\nWORM_EGRESS_CONFIG_GATE=\nOPNSENSE_DNS_CONFIG_GATE=\n\nOPNSENSE_HANDSHAKE_READY_GATE=\nOPNSENSE_FULL_TUNNEL_READY_GATE=\nOPNSENSE_DNS_READY_GATE=\n\nThese are CONFIG gates based on the offline authoritative config.\n\nDo not claim live service PASS from offline config alone.\n\n============================================================\nM. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nCreate a SANITIZED report on Antani under:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/OPNSENSE-RESCUE-AUTHORITATIVE-AUDIT.md\n\nIf direct report transfer from Rescue to Antani is used, transfer only\nthe sanitized generated report.\n\nNever transfer config.xml itself.\n\nFinal report must include:\n\nHETZNER_API_AVAILABLE=\nHETZNER_API_AUTH=\n\nOPNSENSE_SERVER_ID=\nOPNSENSE_SERVER_NAME=\nOPNSENSE_PRIMARY_IPV4=\n\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE=\n\nRESCUE_ENABLE_REQUEST=\nOPNSENSE_REBOOT_REQUESTED=\nRESCUE_BOOT_GATE=\n\nOPNSENSE_DISK=\nZFS_POOL=\nZFS_READONLY=\n\nCONFIG_XML_PRESENT=\nCONFIG_XML_SHA256=\n\nWAN_INTERFACE=\nWAN_IP=\n\nPRIVATE_INTERFACE=\nPRIVATE_IP=\nVLAN_ID=\n\nWEBGUI_PORT=\nWEBGUI_LISTEN_INTERFACES=\nSSHD_ENABLED=\n\nWG_ENABLED=\nWG_LISTEN_PORT=\nWG_INTERFACE_ADDRESS=\nANTANI_PEER_PRESENT=\nWORMOS_PEER_PRESENT=\n\nWAN_WG_51820_CONFIGURED=\nPRIVATE_WEBGUI_ALLOWED=\nWORM_OUTBOUND_NAT_CONFIGURED=\n\nUNBOUND_ENABLED=\nWORM_SUBNET_DNS_ALLOWED=\nDNSSEC_CONFIGURED=\nUPSTREAM_DOT_CONFIGURED=\n\nCONFIG_DRIFT=\nCONFIG_DRIFT_FIELDS=\n\nOPNSENSE_HANDSHAKE_READY_GATE=\nOPNSENSE_FULL_TUNNEL_READY_GATE=\nOPNSENSE_DNS_READY_GATE=\n\nCONFIG_MODIFIED=NO\nZFS_WRITE_OCCURRED=NO\nSECRETS_PRINTED=NO\n\n============================================================\nN. CLEAN EXIT\n============================================================\n\nCleanly unmount/export the OPNsense pool.\n\nRequired:\n\nzpool export <actual_pool>\n\nVerify no OPNsense filesystem remains mounted.\n\nDo NOT modify boot config.\n\nDo NOT reboot back to normal automatically in this task unless explicitly\nrequired to exit Rescue safely and the target identity is revalidated.\n\nPrefer STOP after clean ZFS export.\n\n============================================================\nFINAL CONTROL STATE\n============================================================\n\nANTANI_CHANGED=NO\nWORMOS_CHANGED=NO\nOPNSENSE_CONFIG_CHANGED=NO\nOPNSENSE_FIREWALL_CHANGED=NO\nOPNSENSE_WG_CHANGED=NO\n\nWG_WORM_STARTED=NO\nFULL_TUNNEL_ENABLED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1158:{"session_id":"01a08704-2ef8-7c71-a57f-de1bfe18d8d7","ts":1788976672,"text":"OPNSENSE — MINIMAL CHANGE 7E\nTEMPORARY RESCUE OPENZFS TOOLING + READ-ONLY AUDIT\n\nMODE:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> MINIMAL CHANGE -> VERIFY\n\nCURRENT VERIFIED STATE:\n\nHETZNER_API_AUTH=PASS\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE=PASS\nRESCUE_BOOT_GATE=PASS\n\nCURRENT_HOST=OPNSENSE_RESCUE\nOPNSENSE_DISK=/dev/sda\nZFS_PARTITION=/dev/sda4\nZFS_POOL_LABEL=zroot\n\nOPNSENSE_CONFIG_CHANGED=NO\nZFS_WRITE_OCCURRED=NO\n\nBLOCKER:\nHetzner Rescue currently lacks active OpenZFS support.\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nMake OpenZFS tooling available TEMPORARILY in the Rescue OS only,\nthen import OPNsense zroot STRICTLY READ-ONLY and perform the previously\nrequested sanitized config.xml audit.\n\nABSOLUTE RULES:\n\nDO NOT install anything into /dev/sda.\nDO NOT mount the OPNsense root read-write.\nDO NOT modify config.xml.\nDO NOT run zpool upgrade.\nDO NOT run zpool scrub.\nDO NOT run zpool clear.\nDO NOT run zfs set on the OPNsense pool.\nDO NOT modify bootloader/EFI.\nDO NOT modify PF/firewall/WireGuard.\nDO NOT print secrets.\n\nAny package/tool installation must affect only the ephemeral Hetzner\nRescue environment.\n\n============================================================\n1. RESCUE ENVIRONMENT GATE\n============================================================\n\nVerify again:\n\nhostname\nuname -a\nfindmnt /\nlsblk\n\nProve that the running root filesystem is the Hetzner Rescue environment\nand NOT /dev/sda4.\n\nReport:\n\nRESCUE_ROOT_VERIFIED=\nOPNSENSE_DISK_NOT_ROOT=\n\nRequired both PASS.\n\nOtherwise STOP.\n\n============================================================\n2. OPENZFS CAPABILITY AUDIT\n============================================================\n\nDetermine:\n\nRESCUE_DISTRO=\nKERNEL_VERSION=\nZPOOL_BINARY_PRESENT=\nZFS_BINARY_PRESENT=\nZFS_KERNEL_MODULE_PRESENT=\nZFS_KERNEL_MODULE_LOADED=\n\nCheck whether existing binaries merely lack the kernel module.\n\nAttempt only safe module discovery/load if the matching module already\nexists.\n\nDo not compile anything yet.\n\n============================================================\n3. TEMPORARY TOOLING\n============================================================\n\nIf matching OpenZFS support can be installed through the Rescue OS package\nmanager without touching /dev/sda:\n\ninstall only the minimum required Rescue packages/modules.\n\nBefore installation verify package targets belong to the Rescue root.\n\nRequired:\n\nPACKAGE_TARGET=RESCUE_ROOT_ONLY\n\nDo not add repositories to OPNsense disk.\nDo not chroot into OPNsense.\nDo not install packages into OPNsense.\n\nIf the available packages require kernel replacement, reboot, DKMS build\nagainst unavailable headers, or modification of /dev/sda:\n\nSTOP.\n\nReport:\n\nTEMP_ZFS_TOOLING_INSTALLED=\nZFS_MODULE_AVAILABLE=\nZFS_MODULE_LOADED=\n\n============================================================\n4. READ-ONLY POOL DISCOVERY\n============================================================\n\nRun:\n\nzpool import\n\nDiscover actual pool identity.\n\nDo not import yet.\n\nRequired:\n\nPOOL_FOUND=YES\nPOOL_NAME=zroot\n\nRecord pool GUID if useful.\n\n============================================================\n5. STRICT READ-ONLY IMPORT\n============================================================\n\nImport with read-only safety properties:\n\nreadonly=on\ncachefile=none\nalternate root=/mnt/opnsense-ro\n\nEquivalent intended operation:\n\nzpool import -f -N \\\n  -o readonly=on \\\n  -o cachefile=none \\\n  -R /mnt/opnsense-ro \\\n  zroot\n\nImmediately verify:\n\nzpool get readonly zroot\nzpool get cachefile zroot\n\nRequired:\n\nZFS_READONLY=ON\nCACHEFILE=NONE\n\nIf not:\nexport immediately and STOP.\n\n============================================================\n6. LOCATE ROOT DATASET\n============================================================\n\nInspect datasets read-only.\n\nExpected historical root:\n\nzroot/ROOT/default\n\nDo not assume.\n\nFind the actual mounted/root dataset and expose it only under:\n\n/mnt/opnsense-ro\n\nLocate:\n\nconf/config.xml\n\nRequired:\n\nCONFIG_XML_PRESENT=YES\n\nDo NOT cat the raw file.\n\n============================================================\n7. SANITIZED CONFIG AUDIT\n============================================================\n\nRun the complete sanitized parser from the previous OPNsense audit.\n\nExtract ONLY:\n\nWAN interface/IP\nPrivate interface/IP/VLAN\nWebGUI port/listen interfaces\nSSH enabled/listen policy\n\nWireGuard:\n- enabled\n- interface/address\n- listen port\n- peer count\n- Antani 10.90.30.2/32 presence\n- WormOS 10.90.30.3/32 presence\n\nFirewall:\n- WAN UDP/51820\n- private WebGUI access\n- WORM rules\n\nNAT:\n- 10.90.30.0/24 outbound policy\n\nUnbound:\n- enabled\n- WORM subnet access\n- DNSSEC\n- upstream DoT\n\nNEVER output:\n\nprivate keys\nPSKs\npassword hashes\nAPI keys\ntokens\ncertificate private material\n\n============================================================\n8. TARGET COMPARISON\n============================================================\n\nCompare against:\n\nPRIVATE_SUBNET=10.90.20.0/24\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_IP=10.90.20.1\n\nWORM_WG_SUBNET=10.90.30.0/24\nOPNSENSE_WG_IP=10.90.30.1\nANTANI_WG_IP=10.90.30.2\nWORMOS_WG_IP=10.90.30.3/32\n\nWG_PORT=51820\n\nDNS_TARGET:\nWormOS -> WG -> OPNsense -> Unbound -> upstream DoT -> Internet\n\nReturn:\n\nCONFIG_DRIFT=\nCONFIG_DRIFT_FIELDS=\n\n============================================================\n9. CLEAN EXPORT\n============================================================\n\nAfter audit:\n\nunmount any explicitly mounted datasets if necessary\nzpool export zroot\n\nVerify:\n\nZPOOL_EXPORTED=PASS\nOPNSENSE_FILESYSTEM_MOUNTED=NO\n\nDo not reboot yet.\n\n============================================================\n10. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nTransfer/write ONLY the sanitized report to:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/OPNSENSE-RESCUE-AUTHORITATIVE-AUDIT.md\n\nNever transfer config.xml.\n\nFinal:\n\nRESCUE_ROOT_VERIFIED=\nOPNSENSE_DISK_NOT_ROOT=\n\nTEMP_ZFS_TOOLING_INSTALLED=\nZFS_MODULE_AVAILABLE=\nZFS_MODULE_LOADED=\n\nPOOL_FOUND=\nZFS_READONLY=\nCONFIG_XML_PRESENT=\nCONFIG_XML_SHA256=\n\nWAN_INTERFACE=\nWAN_IP=\n\nPRIVATE_INTERFACE=\nPRIVATE_IP=\nVLAN_ID=\n\nWEBGUI_PORT=\nWEBGUI_LISTEN_INTERFACES=\nSSHD_ENABLED=\n\nWG_ENABLED=\nWG_LISTEN_PORT=\nWG_INTERFACE_ADDRESS=\nANTANI_PEER_PRESENT=\nWORMOS_PEER_PRESENT=\n\nWAN_WG_51820_CONFIGURED=\nPRIVATE_WEBGUI_ALLOWED=\nWORM_OUTBOUND_NAT_CONFIGURED=\n\nUNBOUND_ENABLED=\nWORM_SUBNET_DNS_ALLOWED=\nDNSSEC_CONFIGURED=\nUPSTREAM_DOT_CONFIGURED=\n\nCONFIG_DRIFT=\nCONFIG_DRIFT_FIELDS=\n\nOPNSENSE_HANDSHAKE_READY_GATE=\nOPNSENSE_FULL_TUNNEL_READY_GATE=\nOPNSENSE_DNS_READY_GATE=\n\nCONFIG_MODIFIED=NO\nZFS_WRITE_OCCURRED=NO\nSECRETS_PRINTED=NO\nZPOOL_EXPORTED=\n\nOPNSENSE_REBOOTED_TO_NORMAL=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1159:{"session_id":"01a08755-ba69-7880-9b5d-d39bb21288b8","ts":1788976941,"text":"LEVEL PRO — WORM / ANTANI / OPNSENSE\n\nFrom this point operate in PRO mode.\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> MINIMAL CHANGE -> VERIFY\n\nROOT:\n/opt/worm\n\nPRINCIPLES:\n\n- Inspect real state before assumptions.\n- Prefer authoritative live evidence over historical reports.\n- Never declare PASS without verification.\n- Never combine unrelated fixes.\n- One blocker -> one minimal change -> verification.\n- Preserve working infrastructure.\n- Fail closed on ambiguity.\n- Stop before destructive or high-impact actions unless explicitly authorized.\n- Never print secrets, passwords, API tokens, private keys, PSKs or credentials.\n- Keep sanitized reports under /opt/worm/artifacts/reports/.\n- Record exact files/commands/state changed.\n- Preserve rollback information before persistent modifications.\n- Do not rewrite historical provenance to match current desired state.\n\nNETWORK ARCHITECTURE:\n\nOPNsense = authoritative firewall/router/WireGuard hub/DNS/Internet gateway.\n\nPRIVATE TRANSPORT:\n10.90.20.0/24\nOPNsense = 10.90.20.1\nAntani = 10.90.20.10\n\nWORM WG:\n10.90.30.0/24\nOPNsense = 10.90.30.1\nAntani = 10.90.30.2\nWormOS primary = 10.90.30.3/32\n\nADMIN WG:\n10.77.0.0/24\nwg0 must remain isolated and preserved.\n\nWORM traffic policy:\nWormOS / Robot / Antani WORM traffic\n-> WireGuard\n-> OPNsense\n-> firewall/NAT\n-> Internet\n\nNo direct WORM Internet bypass through Antani WAN.\n\nDNS target:\nWormOS\n-> WG\n-> OPNsense\n-> Unbound\n-> upstream DoT\n-> Internet\n\nRUNTIME SECURITY:\n\nWORM WireGuard private secrets = RAM-only.\nPersistent network state = non-secret metadata/private IP only.\nNever embed WG private keys in ROM/source/build outputs.\n\nBUILD POLICY:\n\nMandatory pre-build gate before every build.\nNo build when any required gate is FAIL.\nNo OTA unless all OTA-specific gates PASS.\n\nCURRENT OPERATING RULE:\n\nDo not start wg-worm or enable full tunnel until:\nADDRESS_PLAN_GATE=PASS\nWG_ENDPOINT_ROUTE_GATE=PASS\nWORM_WG_RAM_ONLY_GATE=PASS\nROUTE_CONFLICT_GATE=PASS\nOPNSENSE_HANDSHAKE_READY_GATE=PASS\n\nOUTPUT STYLE:\n\nAt the end of every task print:\n\nAUDIT=\nGATE=\nCHANGE=\nVERIFY=\n\nCHANGES_MADE=\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE=\n\nIf nothing was changed:\nCHANGES_MADE=NONE\n\nIf a requested action could interrupt SSH, routing, firewall, OPNsense,\nAntani, or production services:\nSTOP and request explicit authorization first.\n\nLEVEL_PRO=ACTIVE"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1160:{"session_id":"01a08704-2ef8-7c71-a57f-de1bfe18d8d7","ts":1788977281,"text":"OPNSENSE — LEVEL PRO\nRECOVERY AUDIT: CURRENT CONFIG + LOCAL BACKUP CANDIDATE\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> MINIMAL CHANGE -> VERIFY\n\nCURRENT STATE:\n\nHETZNER_API_AUTH=PASS\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE=PASS\nRESCUE_BOOT_GATE=PASS\n\nCURRENT_HOST=OPNSENSE_RESCUE\nOPNSENSE_DISK=/dev/sda\nZFS_PARTITION=/dev/sda4\nZFS_POOL_LABEL=zroot\n\nOPNSENSE_CONFIG_CHANGED=NO\nZFS_WRITE_OCCURRED=NO\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\n1. enable OpenZFS tooling only inside ephemeral Rescue\n2. import OPNsense zroot STRICTLY read-only\n3. audit current /conf/config.xml\n4. enumerate /conf/backup safely\n5. identify the most recent plausible working configuration\n6. compare current vs candidate\n7. STOP before any restore\n\nABSOLUTE RULES:\n\nDO NOT restore config.xml.\nDO NOT overwrite any file on OPNsense disk.\nDO NOT import ZFS read-write.\nDO NOT run zpool upgrade.\nDO NOT run zfs set on OPNsense datasets.\nDO NOT modify bootloader.\nDO NOT reboot back to normal.\nDO NOT modify PF/firewall.\nDO NOT modify WireGuard.\nDO NOT modify interfaces.\nDO NOT print secrets/password hashes/private keys/PSKs/API credentials.\nDO NOT copy raw config.xml or backup XML files into /opt/worm.\n\n============================================================\n1. VERIFY RESCUE ROOT\n============================================================\n\nProve current root filesystem is Rescue and not OPNsense disk.\n\nCollect:\n\nhostname\nuname -a\nfindmnt /\nlsblk\n\nReport:\n\nRESCUE_ROOT_VERIFIED=\nOPNSENSE_DISK_NOT_ROOT=\n\nRequired both PASS.\n\nOtherwise STOP.\n\n============================================================\n2. TEMPORARY OPENZFS TOOLING\n============================================================\n\nAudit:\n\nRESCUE_DISTRO=\nKERNEL_VERSION=\nZPOOL_BINARY_PRESENT=\nZFS_BINARY_PRESENT=\nZFS_MODULE_PRESENT=\nZFS_MODULE_LOADED=\n\nIf OpenZFS support is missing, install/load the minimum required tooling\nONLY into the Rescue environment.\n\nBefore package installation verify:\n\nPACKAGE_TARGET=RESCUE_ROOT_ONLY\n\nDo not chroot into OPNsense.\n\nIf installation requires modifying /dev/sda, replacing Rescue kernel,\nor writing into OPNsense root:\n\nSTOP.\n\nReport:\n\nTEMP_ZFS_TOOLING_INSTALLED=\nZFS_MODULE_AVAILABLE=\nZFS_MODULE_LOADED=\n\n============================================================\n3. DISCOVER POOL\n============================================================\n\nRun read-only discovery:\n\nzpool import\n\nDetermine:\n\nPOOL_FOUND=\nPOOL_NAME=\nPOOL_GUID=\nPOOL_STATE=\n\nExpected pool name:\n\nzroot\n\nDo not assume if actual discovery differs.\n\n============================================================\n4. IMPORT STRICTLY READ-ONLY\n============================================================\n\nImport with:\n\nreadonly=on\ncachefile=none\nalternate root=/mnt/opnsense-ro\n\nEquivalent safe form:\n\nzpool import -f -N \\\n  -o readonly=on \\\n  -o cachefile=none \\\n  -R /mnt/opnsense-ro \\\n  zroot\n\nVerify immediately:\n\nZFS_READONLY=ON\nCACHEFILE=NONE\n\nIf not:\n\nexport pool immediately\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n5. LOCATE OPNsense ROOT\n============================================================\n\nEnumerate datasets read-only.\n\nFind actual root dataset.\n\nLocate:\n\n/conf/config.xml\n/conf/backup/\n\nDo not assume zroot/ROOT/default if discovery says otherwise.\n\nReport:\n\nROOT_DATASET=\nCONFIG_XML_PRESENT=\nBACKUP_DIR_PRESENT=\n\n============================================================\n6. CURRENT CONFIG FINGERPRINT\n============================================================\n\nFor current config.xml collect only metadata:\n\nCURRENT_CONFIG_PATH=\nCURRENT_CONFIG_SIZE=\nCURRENT_CONFIG_SHA256=\nCURRENT_CONFIG_MTIME=\n\nDo not print raw XML.\n\nParse sanitized network metadata only:\n\nCURRENT_WAN_IP=\nCURRENT_PRIVATE_IP=\nCURRENT_WG_SUBNET=\nCURRENT_WG_ADDRESS=\nCURRENT_WG_PORT=\nCURRENT_WEBGUI_PORT=\n\nNever output secrets.\n\n============================================================\n7. ENUMERATE LOCAL BACKUPS\n============================================================\n\nEnumerate /conf/backup without printing file contents.\n\nFor every candidate collect:\n\nfilename\nmtime\nsize\nsha256\n\nParse sanitized metadata only:\n\nWAN IP\nprivate IP\nWG subnet/address/port\nWebGUI port/listen policy\n\nLimit detailed comparison to the newest reasonable candidates.\n\nDo not treat a newer backup as automatically better.\n\nReport:\n\nBACKUP_COUNT=\nBACKUP_CANDIDATES_ANALYZED=\n\n============================================================\n8. FIND LAST PLAUSIBLE WORKING CONFIG\n============================================================\n\nTarget known-good architecture:\n\nWAN=2.28.34.27\n\nPRIVATE:\n10.90.20.0/24\nOPNsense=10.90.20.1\n\nWORM WG:\n10.90.30.0/24\nOPNsense=10.90.30.1\nAntani=10.90.30.2\nWormOS=10.90.30.3/32\n\nWG_PORT=51820\n\nBut also consider prior known live evidence/history.\n\nSelect candidate only when evidence supports it.\n\nFor each promising backup classify:\n\nCANDIDATE_PRIVATE_NETWORK_MATCH=\nCANDIDATE_WEBGUI_ACCESS_MATCH=\nCANDIDATE_WG_CONFIG_MATCH=\nCANDIDATE_FIREWALL_MATCH=\nCANDIDATE_OVERALL_CONFIDENCE=\n\nDo not select a candidate solely because it matches the desired future\n10.90.x design if it was never known to boot successfully.\n\n============================================================\n9. CURRENT VS CANDIDATE DIFF\n============================================================\n\nIf a plausible candidate exists, produce a SANITIZED semantic diff.\n\nCompare only:\n\ninterfaces\nIP assignments\nVLAN\nWebGUI listen/port\nSSH enable/listen\nWireGuard enable/address/port/peers\nWAN UDP 51820 rule\nprivate management rule\noutbound NAT\nUnbound/DNS settings\n\nDo not print secret nodes.\n\nReport:\n\nRECOVERY_CANDIDATE_FOUND=\nRECOVERY_CANDIDATE_FILE=\nRECOVERY_CANDIDATE_SHA256=\n\nDIFF_INTERFACE=\nDIFF_PRIVATE_IP=\nDIFF_WEBGUI=\nDIFF_WIREGUARD=\nDIFF_FIREWALL=\nDIFF_NAT=\nDIFF_DNS=\n\n============================================================\n10. RECOVERY GATE\n============================================================\n\nPASS only if one candidate is demonstrably safer/more plausible than the\ncurrent config.\n\nReturn:\n\nRECOVERY_CANDIDATE_GATE=PASS|FAIL|AMBIGUOUS\n\nIf PASS:\n\nRESTORE_ALLOWED=NO_NOT_YET_AUTHORIZED\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE=Restore selected config.xml candidate after explicit authorization\n\nIf AMBIGUOUS:\n\nRESTORE_ALLOWED=NO\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE=Manual candidate review\n\nIf FAIL:\n\nRESTORE_ALLOWED=NO\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE=Use OPNsense importer/reinstall recovery plan\n\n============================================================\n11. CLEAN EXIT\n============================================================\n\nDo not change any OPNsense file.\n\nExport:\n\nzpool export zroot\n\nVerify:\n\nZPOOL_EXPORTED=PASS\nOPNSENSE_FILESYSTEM_MOUNTED=NO\n\n============================================================\n12. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite ONLY sanitized report to:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/OPNSENSE-RECOVERY-CANDIDATE-AUDIT.md\n\nFinal:\n\nRESCUE_ROOT_VERIFIED=\nTEMP_ZFS_TOOLING_INSTALLED=\nZFS_MODULE_LOADED=\n\nPOOL_FOUND=\nZFS_READONLY=\nROOT_DATASET=\n\nCONFIG_XML_PRESENT=\nCURRENT_CONFIG_SHA256=\n\nBACKUP_DIR_PRESENT=\nBACKUP_COUNT=\nBACKUP_CANDIDATES_ANALYZED=\n\nRECOVERY_CANDIDATE_FOUND=\nRECOVERY_CANDIDATE_FILE=\nRECOVERY_CANDIDATE_SHA256=\nRECOVERY_CANDIDATE_GATE=\n\nCURRENT_PRIVATE_IP=\nCANDIDATE_PRIVATE_IP=\n\nCURRENT_WEBGUI_PORT=\nCANDIDATE_WEBGUI_PORT=\n\nCURRENT_WG_ADDRESS=\nCANDIDATE_WG_ADDRESS=\n\nCURRENT_WG_PORT=\nCANDIDATE_WG_PORT=\n\nCONFIG_MODIFIED=NO\nRESTORE_PERFORMED=NO\nZFS_WRITE_OCCURRED=NO\nSECRETS_PRINTED=NO\nZPOOL_EXPORTED=\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1163:{"session_id":"01a08704-2ef8-7c71-a57f-de1bfe18d8d7","ts":1788978436,"text":"CONTINUATION — SAME AUTHORIZED OPNsense STAGE 1 TASK\n\nThis is the missing continuation of the previous Stage 1 instruction.\n\nThe authorization remains:\n\nAUTHORIZED_WRITE=YES\nAUTHORIZED_SCOPE=STAGE_1_ONLY\n\nDo not expand scope beyond the already specified:\n- private/LAN 10.90.10.1/24 -> 10.90.20.1/24\n- removal/neutralization of ONLY the conflicting 10.90.20.0/24 static route\n\nAll previous safety constraints remain in force.\n\n============================================================\n9. LIVE MANAGEMENT VERIFICATION\n============================================================\n\nAfter the already specified config backup, minimal Stage-1 edit,\nXML verification, clean zpool export, and normal OPNsense boot:\n\nFrom Antani verify:\n\nip route get 10.90.20.1\n\nThen verify private L2/neighbour reachability for:\n\n10.90.20.1\n\nTest HTTPS:\n\nhttps://10.90.20.1:443\n\nUse a short timeout.\n\nA TLS certificate warning/self-signed certificate is acceptable.\nWe are testing transport/service reachability, not certificate trust.\n\nDo NOT log into WebGUI.\nDo NOT change WebGUI configuration.\n\nReport:\n\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_ROUTE=\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_L2=\nOPNSENSE_WEBGUI_HTTPS=\n\nRequired success:\n\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_ROUTE=PASS\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_L2=PASS\nOPNSENSE_WEBGUI_HTTPS=PASS\n\nICMP is NOT required.\n\n============================================================\n10. FAILURE / ROLLBACK POLICY\n============================================================\n\nIf normal OPNsense boot fails, or HTTPS on 10.90.20.1:443 is not\nreachable:\n\nDO NOT perform additional speculative fixes.\n\nDO NOT modify:\n- firewall\n- WAN\n- WireGuard\n- NAT\n- DNS\n- SSH\n- Hetzner network configuration\n- Antani network configuration\n\nPreserve the verified Stage-1 recovery backup.\n\nDo NOT automatically restore it unless separately authorized.\n\nReturn:\n\nPRIVATE_MANAGEMENT_RECOVERY_GATE=FAIL\n\nand provide the exact observed blocker.\n\n============================================================\n11. FINAL GATE\n============================================================\n\nIf normal boot succeeds and HTTPS 10.90.20.1:443 is reachable from\nAntani:\n\nPRIVATE_MANAGEMENT_RECOVERY_GATE=PASS\n\nOtherwise:\n\nPRIVATE_MANAGEMENT_RECOVERY_GATE=FAIL\n\nDo NOT mark WireGuard ready merely because private management works.\n\nKeep:\n\nWG_CHANGE_DEFERRED=YES\nNAT_CHANGE_DEFERRED=YES\nDNS_CHANGE_DEFERRED=YES\n\n============================================================\n12. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite sanitized report:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/OPNSENSE-STAGE1-PRIVATE-MANAGEMENT-RECOVERY.md\n\nFinal report MUST contain:\n\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE=\n\nBACKUP_CREATED=\nBACKUP_HASH_MATCH=\nORIGINAL_CONFIG_SHA256=\nRECOVERY_BACKUP_SHA256=\nNEW_CONFIG_SHA256=\n\nOLD_PRIVATE_IP=\nNEW_PRIVATE_IP=\n\nSTATIC_ROUTE_CONFLICT_CONFIRMED=\nOBSOLETE_10_90_20_STATIC_ROUTE_PRESENT=\n\nXML_VALID=\nUNEXPECTED_CONFIG_CHANGES=\n\nWAN_CONFIG_UNCHANGED=\nWG_CONFIG_UNCHANGED=\nNAT_CONFIG_UNCHANGED=\nDNS_CONFIG_UNCHANGED=\n\nZPOOL_EXPORTED=\n\nNORMAL_BOOT_REQUESTED=\nNORMAL_BOOT_REACHED=\n\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_ROUTE=\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_L2=\nOPNSENSE_WEBGUI_HTTPS=\n\nPRIVATE_MANAGEMENT_RECOVERY_GATE=\n\nWG_CHANGE_DEFERRED=YES\nNAT_CHANGE_DEFERRED=YES\nDNS_CHANGE_DEFERRED=YES\n\nANTANI_CHANGED=NO\nWORMOS_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE=\n\n============================================================\n13. NEXT STEP DECISION\n============================================================\n\nIf:\n\nPRIVATE_MANAGEMENT_RECOVERY_GATE=PASS\n\nthen:\n\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE=Stage 2 live OPNsense verification through restored private management path\n\nIf FAIL:\n\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE=Diagnose Stage 1 failure using current evidence and recovery backup; no automatic additional changes\n\n============================================================\nFINAL CONTROL\n============================================================\n\nDo not start wg-worm.\nDo not enable full tunnel.\nDo not configure 10.90.30.0/24 yet.\nDo not change UDP 51823/51820 yet.\nDo not configure NAT yet.\nDo not configure Unbound/DoT yet.\n\nContinue execution of the SAME Stage-1 task now."}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1165:{"session_id":"01a08704-2ef8-7c71-a57f-de1bfe18d8d7","ts":1788979954,"text":"OPNSENSE — LEVEL PRO\nSTAGE 1C — NORMAL BOOT + LIVE RUNTIME DIAGNOSIS\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> MINIMAL CHANGE -> VERIFY\n\nCURRENT STATE:\n\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE=PASS\n\nOFFLINE CONFIG VERIFIED:\n\nPRIVATE_IP=10.90.20.1/24\nPRIVATE_INTERFACE=lan\nPRIVATE_DEVICE=vtnet1\n\nWEBGUI_PROTOCOL=https\nWEBGUI_PORT=443\nWEBGUI_BIND_GATE=PASS\n\nPRIVATE_HTTPS_PASS_RULE_PRESENT=YES\nPRIVATE_HTTPS_EARLIER_BLOCK=NO\nPRIVATE_HTTPS_FIREWALL_GATE=PASS\n\nCONFIG_XML_REPAIR_JUSTIFIED=NO\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nOPNsense is currently in Hetzner Rescue after the read-only audit.\nzroot was exported cleanly.\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\n1. boot the verified OPNsense VPS back into normal installed OPNsense\n2. verify normal boot\n3. diagnose LIVE runtime state\n4. make NO OPNsense configuration changes\n\nABSOLUTE RULES:\n\nDO NOT edit config.xml.\nDO NOT rollback Stage 1.\nDO NOT disable PF.\nDO NOT change firewall.\nDO NOT change WebGUI configuration.\nDO NOT change WAN/LAN.\nDO NOT change WireGuard.\nDO NOT change NAT/DNS.\nDO NOT change Hetzner networking.\nDO NOT change Antani.\nDO NOT start wg-worm.\n\n============================================================\n1. TARGET GATE\n============================================================\n\nUsing existing Hetzner API access verify:\n\nSERVER_ID=164649753\nSERVER_NAME=worm-opnsense\nPRIMARY_IPV4=2.28.34.27\n\nRequired:\n\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE=PASS\n\nOtherwise STOP.\n\n============================================================\n2. CLEAN RESCUE STATE\n============================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nzroot is exported\nno OPNsense filesystem remains mounted\nno pending disk operation exists\n\nRequired:\n\nZPOOL_EXPORTED=PASS\nOPNSENSE_FILESYSTEM_MOUNTED=NO\n\n============================================================\n3. BOOT NORMAL OPNsense\n============================================================\n\nExit/disable Rescue according to the Hetzner boot mechanism and reboot\nONLY worm-opnsense.\n\nDo not reboot Antani.\n\nWait for API server state and network availability.\n\nRequired:\n\nRESCUE_ENABLED_AFTER=NO\nNORMAL_BOOT_REQUESTED=YES\n\n============================================================\n4. PROVE NORMAL BOOT\n============================================================\n\nDo NOT infer normal boot only from ICMP.\n\nUse available evidence to distinguish installed OPNsense from Rescue.\n\nReport:\n\nSERVER_API_RUNNING=\nPUBLIC_ICMP=\nPUBLIC_TCP22=\n\nIf an authorized live access method becomes available, verify OS identity.\n\nReturn:\n\nNORMAL_BOOT_REACHED=YES|NO|UNVERIFIED\n\nIf NO:\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n5. PRIVATE PATH RECHECK\n============================================================\n\nFrom Antani:\n\nip route get 10.90.20.1\nip neigh show 10.90.20.1\n\nProbe:\n\n10.90.20.1:443\n10.90.20.1:80\n10.90.20.1:22\n\nReport:\n\nPRIVATE_ROUTE=\nPRIVATE_L2=\nPRIVATE_443=\nPRIVATE_80=\nPRIVATE_22=\n\n============================================================\n6. LIVE PACKET ARRIVAL TEST\n============================================================\n\nIf an authorized mechanism exists to observe OPNsense runtime without\nchanging configuration:\n\nobserve vtnet1 while Antani performs ONE short TCP/443 connection test.\n\nDetermine:\n\nANTANI_SYN_SENT=\nOPNSENSE_VTNET1_SYN_SEEN=\n\nDo not capture payload.\nDo not record credentials.\nMetadata only.\n\nIf runtime capture is unavailable:\n\nOPNSENSE_VTNET1_SYN_SEEN=NOT_VERIFIED\n\n============================================================\n7. LIVE WEBGUI LISTENER\n============================================================\n\nIf authorized runtime inspection is available, determine whether TCP/443\nis actually listening on OPNsense.\n\nReport:\n\nWEBGUI_PROCESS_RUNNING=\nTCP443_LISTENER_PRESENT=\nTCP443_LISTENER_ADDRESS=\n\nDo not restart WebGUI.\n\n============================================================\n8. LIVE PF STATE\n============================================================\n\nRead only.\n\nDetermine:\n\nPF_ENABLED=\nPF_RULESET_LOADED=\nPRIVATE_HTTPS_RUNTIME_RULE_PRESENT=\n\nDo not run pfctl -d.\nDo not reload PF.\n\nIf possible inspect whether the Antani TCP/443 attempt is passed or\nblocked.\n\nReport:\n\nPRIVATE_HTTPS_RUNTIME_ACTION=\n\n============================================================\n9. FAILURE CLASSIFICATION\n============================================================\n\nClassify using LIVE evidence:\n\nA:\nSYN_NOT_REACHING_OPNSENSE\n\nB:\nSYN_REACHES_OPNSENSE_NO_443_LISTENER\n\nC:\nSYN_REACHES_OPNSENSE_PF_BLOCKS\n\nD:\n443_LISTENER_AND_PF_PASS_BUT_NO_RESPONSE\n\nE:\nRUNTIME_ACCESS_INSUFFICIENT\n\nReturn:\n\nWEBGUI_RUNTIME_FAILURE_CLASS=\n\n============================================================\n10. GATE\n============================================================\n\nIf 443 becomes reachable:\n\nPRIVATE_MANAGEMENT_RECOVERY_GATE=PASS\n\nIf still timeout:\n\nPRIVATE_MANAGEMENT_RECOVERY_GATE=FAIL\n\nDo not make the repair automatically.\n\nDetermine exactly ONE next minimal repair from live evidence.\n\n============================================================\n11. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/OPNSENSE-STAGE1C-LIVE-RUNTIME-DIAGNOSIS.md\n\nFinal:\n\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE=\n\nRESCUE_ENABLED_AFTER=\nNORMAL_BOOT_REQUESTED=\nNORMAL_BOOT_REACHED=\n\nPRIVATE_ROUTE=\nPRIVATE_L2=\nPRIVATE_443=\nPRIVATE_80=\nPRIVATE_22=\n\nANTANI_SYN_SENT=\nOPNSENSE_VTNET1_SYN_SEEN=\n\nWEBGUI_PROCESS_RUNNING=\nTCP443_LISTENER_PRESENT=\nTCP443_LISTENER_ADDRESS=\n\nPF_ENABLED=\nPF_RULESET_LOADED=\nPRIVATE_HTTPS_RUNTIME_RULE_PRESENT=\nPRIVATE_HTTPS_RUNTIME_ACTION=\n\nWEBGUI_RUNTIME_FAILURE_CLASS=\n\nPRIVATE_MANAGEMENT_RECOVERY_GATE=\n\nCONFIG_CHANGED=NO\nPF_CHANGED=NO\nWEBGUI_CHANGED=NO\nWAN_CHANGED=NO\nLAN_CHANGED=NO\nWG_CHANGED=NO\nANTANI_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1167:{"session_id":"01a08704-2ef8-7c71-a57f-de1bfe18d8d7","ts":1788980492,"text":"OPNSENSE — LEVEL PRO\nPRIVATE ADMIN ACCESS RECOVERY\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> MINIMAL CHANGE -> VERIFY\n\nEXPLICIT AUTHORIZATION:\n\nAUTHORIZED_WRITE=YES\nAUTHORIZED_SCOPE=PRIVATE_ADMIN_ACCESS_ONLY\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nMake OPNsense administratively reachable ONLY from Antani over the\nprivate network:\n\nANTANI=10.90.20.10\nOPNSENSE=10.90.20.1\n\nRequired:\n\nhttps://10.90.20.1:443\n\nand preferably:\n\nssh -> 10.90.20.1:22\n\nNO WAN ADMIN ACCESS.\n\nCURRENT VERIFIED:\n\nPRIVATE_ROUTE=PASS\nPRIVATE_L2=PASS\n\nPRIVATE_443=TIMEOUT\nPRIVATE_22=TIMEOUT\n\nOPNsense private interface:\nlan / vtnet1 / 10.90.20.1/24\n\n============================================================\nAUDIT\n============================================================\n\nUse the established Hetzner Rescue + ZFS workflow.\n\nBefore writing:\n\n1. verify target identity\n2. backup /conf/config.xml\n3. verify backup hash\n4. structurally parse config.xml\n\nAudit ONLY:\n\n- WebGUI enabled state\n- WebGUI HTTPS port\n- WebGUI listen/bind configuration\n- SSH enabled state\n- SSH listen configuration\n- LAN/private firewall rules\n- anti-lockout configuration\n\nDo not print credentials, hashes or private keys.\n\n============================================================\nGATE\n============================================================\n\nRequired target policy:\n\nWEBGUI_ENABLED=YES\nWEBGUI_PROTOCOL=HTTPS\nWEBGUI_PORT=443\n\nPRIVATE_WEBGUI_SOURCE=10.90.20.10\nPRIVATE_WEBGUI_DESTINATION=10.90.20.1\nPRIVATE_WEBGUI_PORT=443\n\nSSH_ENABLED=YES\n\nPRIVATE_SSH_SOURCE=10.90.20.10\nPRIVATE_SSH_DESTINATION=10.90.20.1\nPRIVATE_SSH_PORT=22\n\nWAN_WEBGUI_ACCESS=NO\nWAN_SSH_ACCESS=NO\n\nIf this cannot be implemented without exposing management on WAN:\n\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\nMODIFICA MINIMA\n============================================================\n\nModify ONLY what is necessary to guarantee private management.\n\n1. Ensure WebGUI is enabled on HTTPS/443 and available on the private\n   LAN interface owning 10.90.20.1.\n\n2. Ensure SSH daemon is enabled for private administration.\n\n3. Ensure LAN/private firewall contains narrowly scoped PASS rules:\n\n   source      10.90.20.10\n   destination 10.90.20.1\n   TCP          443\n\nand:\n\n   source      10.90.20.10\n   destination 10.90.20.1\n   TCP          22\n\n4. Ensure no earlier private-interface block defeats these rules.\n\n5. Do NOT create equivalent WAN rules.\n\n6. Prefer public-key SSH authentication.\n   Do not enable unnecessary password authentication.\n\nDO NOT:\n\n- pfctl -d\n- disable firewall\n- create allow-any rules\n- expose WebGUI on WAN\n- expose SSH on WAN\n- modify WAN\n- modify WireGuard\n- modify NAT\n- modify DNS\n- modify Antani\n- modify Hetzner networking\n\n============================================================\nOFFLINE VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nBefore reboot:\n\nXML_VALID=PASS\n\nPRIVATE_IP=10.90.20.1/24\n\nWEBGUI_HTTPS_PRIVATE_CONFIGURED=PASS\nSSH_PRIVATE_CONFIGURED=PASS\n\nPRIVATE_443_PASS_RULE=PASS\nPRIVATE_22_PASS_RULE=PASS\n\nWAN_443_PASS_RULE_CREATED=NO\nWAN_22_PASS_RULE_CREATED=NO\n\nWAN_CONFIG_UNCHANGED=PASS\nWG_CONFIG_UNCHANGED=PASS\nNAT_CONFIG_UNCHANGED=PASS\nDNS_CONFIG_UNCHANGED=PASS\n\nUNEXPECTED_CONFIG_CHANGES=0\n\nThen cleanly export ZFS.\n\n============================================================\nNORMAL BOOT\n============================================================\n\nBoot ONLY worm-opnsense normally.\n\nDo not reboot Antani.\n\nWait for private L2 reachability.\n\n============================================================\nLIVE VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nFrom Antani test:\n\n10.90.20.1:443\n10.90.20.1:22\n\nRequired:\n\nPRIVATE_HTTPS_443=OPEN\nPRIVATE_SSH_22=OPEN\n\nA TLS certificate warning is acceptable.\n\nDo not require successful SSH login if no authorized key exists yet;\nTCP/22 OPEN is sufficient to prove sshd/private firewall reachability.\n\nAlso verify that public management was NOT exposed.\n\nDo not attempt authentication against WAN.\n\n============================================================\nFINAL GATE\n============================================================\n\nPRIVATE_ADMIN_NETWORK_GATE=PASS only if:\n\nPRIVATE_HTTPS_443=OPEN\nAND\nWAN_WEBGUI_ACCESS_CREATED=NO\n\nSSH is additional:\n\nPRIVATE_SSH_22=OPEN|AUTH_PENDING\n\n============================================================\nREPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/OPNSENSE-PRIVATE-ADMIN-RECOVERY.md\n\nFinal:\n\nPRIVATE_IP=\n\nWEBGUI_ENABLED=\nWEBGUI_PROTOCOL=\nWEBGUI_PORT=\n\nSSH_ENABLED=\nSSH_PORT=\n\nPRIVATE_443_PASS_RULE=\nPRIVATE_22_PASS_RULE=\n\nWAN_WEBGUI_ACCESS_CREATED=\nWAN_SSH_ACCESS_CREATED=\n\nPRIVATE_HTTPS_443=\nPRIVATE_SSH_22=\n\nPRIVATE_ADMIN_NETWORK_GATE=\n\nWAN_CONFIG_UNCHANGED=\nWG_CONFIG_UNCHANGED=\nNAT_CONFIG_UNCHANGED=\nDNS_CONFIG_UNCHANGED=\n\nBACKUP_CREATED=\nXML_VALID=\nUNEXPECTED_CONFIG_CHANGES=\n\nANTANI_CHANGED=NO\nWORMOS_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1172:{"session_id":"01a08704-2ef8-7c71-a57f-de1bfe18d8d7","ts":1788983254,"text":"LEVEL PRO — HEADSCALE ADMIN SUBNET ROUTE\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> MINIMAL CHANGE -> VERIFY\n\nABSOLUTE FREEZE:\n\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_CHANGED=NO\nWG0_CHANGED=NO\nWG_WORM_CHANGED=NO\n\nDO NOT TOUCH OPNsense.\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nProvide remote administrative routing:\n\nAuthorized Admin Device\n        |\nTailscale\n        |\nHeadscale self-hosted\n        |\nAntani tailscale0\n        |\nenp9s0.4000\n        |\n10.90.20.0/24\n\nAdvertise ONLY:\n\n10.90.20.0/24\n\nDO NOT advertise:\n\n0.0.0.0/0\n10.90.30.0/24\n10.77.0.0/24\n\nDO NOT configure Antani as exit node.\n\n============================================================\nAUDIT\n============================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nHEADSCALE_CONNECTED=YES\nTAILSCALE_INTERFACE=tailscale0\n\nANTANI_PRIVATE_INTERFACE=enp9s0.4000\nANTANI_PRIVATE_IP=10.90.20.10/24\n\nPRIVATE_ROUTE_TO_10_90_20_1=PASS\nPRIVATE_L2_TO_10_90_20_1=PASS\n\nDiscover the actual existing Headscale server/control tooling.\n\nDo not print:\n- auth keys\n- API tokens\n- private keys\n- credentials\n\nDetermine:\n\nANTANI_HEADSCALE_NODE=\nANTANI_NODE_ONLINE=\nCURRENT_ADVERTISED_ROUTES=\nCURRENT_APPROVED_ROUTES=\nEXIT_NODE_ENABLED=\n\n============================================================\nGATE\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nHEADSCALE_CONNECTED=YES\nANTANI_NODE_ONLINE=YES\nPRIVATE_ROUTE_GATE=PASS\nPRIVATE_L2_GATE=PASS\nEXIT_NODE_ENABLED=NO\n\nConfirm no route conflict for:\n\n10.90.20.0/24\n\ninside the existing Tailnet.\n\nReturn:\n\nADMIN_SUBNET_ROUTE_GATE=\n\nIf conflict exists:\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\nMINIMAL CHANGE\n============================================================\n\nOn Antani advertise ONLY:\n\n10.90.20.0/24\n\nusing the existing Tailscale configuration.\n\nPreserve all existing Tailscale preferences.\n\nDo NOT replace/reset existing configuration.\n\nDo NOT advertise an exit node.\n\nThen, using the existing authorized Headscale administration mechanism,\napprove ONLY:\n\n10.90.20.0/24\n\nfor the Antani node.\n\nDo not approve unrelated pending routes.\n\n============================================================\nFORWARDING\n============================================================\n\nAudit current forwarding/firewall ownership first.\n\nExisting FireHOL/nftables policy must be preserved.\n\nAllow only the forwarding required between:\n\ntailscale0\n<->\nenp9s0.4000 / 10.90.20.0/24\n\nDo NOT allow tailscale0 -> Antani public WAN forwarding.\n\nDo NOT flush nftables.\n\nDo NOT disable FireHOL.\n\nDo NOT blindly change ip_forward if already enabled.\n\nIf a FireHOL change is required:\n\nmake the smallest persistent FireHOL-native change.\n\n============================================================\nVERIFY HEADSCALE\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nROUTE_10_90_20_ADVERTISED=YES\nROUTE_10_90_20_APPROVED=YES\n\nEXIT_NODE_ENABLED=NO\n\nVerify existing routes remain unchanged.\n\n============================================================\nVERIFY ROUTING\n============================================================\n\nFrom an already connected authorized Headscale/Tailscale admin node,\nif available, verify route resolution for:\n\n10.90.20.1\n\nReport:\n\nREMOTE_ROUTE_10_90_20_1=\n\nThen test:\n\nTCP/443 -> 10.90.20.1\nTCP/22  -> 10.90.20.1\n\nImportant:\n\nIf routing works but 443/22 still timeout:\n\nADMIN_SUBNET_ROUTE_GATE=PASS\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_ADMIN_GATE=FAIL\n\nDo NOT treat this as Headscale failure.\n\nOPNsense is known to currently provide no TCP response from the private\ninterface and remains OUT OF SCOPE.\n\n============================================================\nSECURITY VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nROUTE_0_0_0_0_ADVERTISED=NO\nROUTE_10_90_30_ADVERTISED=NO\nROUTE_10_77_ADVERTISED=NO\n\nANTANI_EXIT_NODE=NO\nPUBLIC_WAN_FORWARD_FROM_TAILSCALE=NO\n\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_CHANGED=NO\nWG0_CHANGED=NO\nWG_WORM_CHANGED=NO\n\n============================================================\nREPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/HEADSCALE-ADMIN-SUBNET-10.90.20.md\n\nFinal:\n\nHEADSCALE_CONNECTED=\nANTANI_HEADSCALE_NODE=\nANTANI_NODE_ONLINE=\n\nROUTE_10_90_20_ADVERTISED=\nROUTE_10_90_20_APPROVED=\n\nTAILSCALE_TO_PRIVATE_FORWARD=\nPRIVATE_TO_TAILSCALE_RETURN=\n\nEXIT_NODE_ENABLED=\n\nREMOTE_ROUTE_10_90_20_1=\nREMOTE_HTTPS_10_90_20_1=\nREMOTE_SSH_10_90_20_1=\n\nADMIN_SUBNET_ROUTE_GATE=\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_ADMIN_GATE=\n\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_CHANGED=NO\nWG0_CHANGED=NO\nWG_WORM_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1173:{"session_id":"01a08704-2ef8-7c71-a57f-de1bfe18d8d7","ts":1788983807,"text":"LEVEL PRO — ROBOT ANTANI SERVICE AUDIT\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> NO CHANGE -> VERIFY\n\nSCOPE:\nANTANI / ROBOT SERVICES ONLY\n\nABSOLUTE RULES:\n\nDO NOT modify OPNsense.\nDO NOT modify Hetzner networking.\nDO NOT modify Headscale/Tailscale.\nDO NOT modify WireGuard.\nDO NOT restart services.\nDO NOT enable/disable services.\nDO NOT change firewall.\nDO NOT build WormOS.\nDO NOT generate OTA.\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nDetermine which Robot/Antani services are:\n\n- installed\n- enabled\n- running\n- listening\n- reachable\n- healthy\n- exposed through the expected private/control interfaces\n\n============================================================\n1. DISCOVER SERVICES\n============================================================\n\nAudit systemd and existing service definitions.\n\nSearch for relevant units containing names such as:\n\nworm\nrobot\nantani\ncontrol\ndashboard\napi\nota\nupdater\ninstaller\nappstore\nheadscale\ntailscale\nwireguard\n\nUse:\n\nsystemctl list-unit-files\nsystemctl list-units --type=service --all\n\nReport only relevant services.\n\nFor each:\n\nSERVICE_NAME=\nINSTALLED=\nENABLED=\nACTIVE=\nSUBSTATE=\nPID=\n\n============================================================\n2. PROCESS AUDIT\n============================================================\n\nAudit relevant running processes.\n\nDetermine:\n\nROBOT_PROCESS_PRESENT=\nWORM_CONTROL_PROCESS_PRESENT=\nDASHBOARD_PROCESS_PRESENT=\nAPI_PROCESS_PRESENT=\nOTA_PROCESS_PRESENT=\nUPDATER_PROCESS_PRESENT=\n\nDo not kill/restart anything.\n\n============================================================\n3. LISTENING PORTS\n============================================================\n\nAudit:\n\nss -lntup\n\nMap relevant listeners to services.\n\nFor each relevant service:\n\nLISTEN_ADDRESS=\nLISTEN_PORT=\nPROCESS=\n\nClassify exposure:\n\nLOOPBACK_ONLY\nPRIVATE_ONLY\nTAILSCALE_ONLY\nPUBLIC_WAN\nALL_INTERFACES\n\nFlag unexpected PUBLIC_WAN exposure.\n\n============================================================\n4. DASHBOARD AUDIT\n============================================================\n\nSpecifically inspect existing Worm dashboard/control implementation.\n\nExpected historical path:\n\n/opt/worm/control/dashboard\n\nCheck:\n\nfiles present\nservice/unit present\nprocess running\nlistener present\n\nVerify API endpoint if locally reachable:\n\n/api/status/features\n\nDo not modify anything.\n\nReport:\n\nDASHBOARD_PRESENT=\nDASHBOARD_SERVICE=\nDASHBOARD_RUNNING=\nDASHBOARD_LISTEN_ADDRESS=\nDASHBOARD_LISTEN_PORT=\nDASHBOARD_API_STATUS_FEATURES=\n\n============================================================\n5. ROBOT CONTROL / API\n============================================================\n\nAudit existing Robot control services and APIs.\n\nDetermine:\n\nROBOT_CONTROL_SERVICE=\nROBOT_CONTROL_RUNNING=\nROBOT_CONTROL_PORT=\nROBOT_CONTROL_BIND=\n\nCONTROL_API_SERVICE=\nCONTROL_API_RUNNING=\nCONTROL_API_PORT=\nCONTROL_API_BIND=\n\n============================================================\n6. OTA / UPDATE SERVICES\n============================================================\n\nAudit only.\n\nDetermine:\n\nOTA_SERVICE_PRESENT=\nOTA_SERVICE_RUNNING=\nOTA_LISTEN_PORT=\n\nUPDATER_SERVICE_PRESENT=\nUPDATER_SERVICE_RUNNING=\n\nWEB_INSTALLER_SERVICE_PRESENT=\nAPPSTORE_SERVICE_PRESENT=\n\nDo not trigger update or OTA.\n\n============================================================\n7. NETWORK PATH POLICY\n============================================================\n\nFor each discovered service determine whether current bind/exposure\nmatches intended architecture.\n\nPreferred:\n\nmanagement/control:\nprivate / Headscale / local only\n\nWORM production traffic:\nthrough OPNsense/WireGuard when implemented\n\nReport:\n\nSERVICE_PUBLIC_BYPASS_FOUND=\nPUBLICLY_EXPOSED_SERVICES=\n\nDo not change exposure.\n\n============================================================\n8. HEALTH CHECKS\n============================================================\n\nFor services with local health/status endpoints, perform read-only checks.\n\nUse localhost/private endpoint only.\n\nDo not authenticate using secrets unless already available through an\nexisting safe mechanism.\n\nReport:\n\nSERVICE_HEALTH_PASS=\nSERVICE_HEALTH_FAIL=\n\n============================================================\n9. LOG AUDIT\n============================================================\n\nFor relevant failed/inactive services inspect recent logs only:\n\njournalctl -u <service> -n 100 --no-pager\n\nSanitize secrets.\n\nReport concise failure reasons only.\n\n============================================================\n10. GATE\n============================================================\n\nReturn:\n\nROBOT_SERVICES_GATE=\nDASHBOARD_GATE=\nCONTROL_API_GATE=\nOTA_SERVICE_GATE=\nSERVICE_NETWORK_POLICY_GATE=\n\nDo not require services that are intentionally deferred.\n\n============================================================\n11. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/ROBOT-ANTANI-SERVICE-AUDIT.md\n\nFinal:\n\nSERVICES_DISCOVERED=\n\nROBOT_CONTROL_SERVICE=\nROBOT_CONTROL_RUNNING=\n\nDASHBOARD_PRESENT=\nDASHBOARD_RUNNING=\nDASHBOARD_LISTEN_ADDRESS=\nDASHBOARD_LISTEN_PORT=\nDASHBOARD_API_STATUS_FEATURES=\n\nCONTROL_API_RUNNING=\n\nOTA_SERVICE_PRESENT=\nOTA_SERVICE_RUNNING=\n\nUPDATER_SERVICE_PRESENT=\nUPDATER_SERVICE_RUNNING=\n\nPUBLICLY_EXPOSED_SERVICES=\nSERVICE_PUBLIC_BYPASS_FOUND=\n\nROBOT_SERVICES_GATE=\nDASHBOARD_GATE=\nCONTROL_API_GATE=\nOTA_SERVICE_GATE=\nSERVICE_NETWORK_POLICY_GATE=\n\nCHANGES_MADE=NONE\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1174:{"session_id":"01a08704-2ef8-7c71-a57f-de1bfe18d8d7","ts":1788984255,"text":"LEVEL PRO — ROBOT/ANTANI DASHBOARD\nMOBILE-ONLY UI + EMAIL AUTH-CODE\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> MINIMAL CHANGE -> VERIFY\n\nROOT:\n/opt/worm\n\nSCOPE:\nWORM CONTROL / ROBOT ANTANI DASHBOARD ONLY\n\nABSOLUTE RULES:\n\nDO NOT modify OPNsense.\nDO NOT modify Hetzner networking.\nDO NOT modify Headscale routing.\nDO NOT modify WireGuard.\nDO NOT expose dashboard publicly on WAN.\nDO NOT print SMTP passwords/API keys.\nDO NOT commit SMTP secrets into Git.\nDO NOT store auth codes plaintext.\nDO NOT build WormOS.\nDO NOT generate OTA.\n\nTARGET AUTH EMAIL:\n\nwill@unit.estixari.com\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\n1. dashboard usable from mobile browsers only\n2. desktop browsers receive an access-denied page\n3. dashboard requires one-time email auth-code\n4. auth-code sent by SMTP\n5. successful session stored securely\n6. dashboard remains on private/admin network only\n\n============================================================\nAUDIT\n============================================================\n\nDiscover current dashboard implementation.\n\nExpected historical path:\n\n/opt/worm/control/dashboard\n\nDetermine:\n\nDASHBOARD_FRAMEWORK=\nDASHBOARD_ENTRYPOINT=\nDASHBOARD_SERVICE=\nDASHBOARD_LISTEN_ADDRESS=\nDASHBOARD_PORT=\n\nLocate existing:\n\nauthentication\nsessions\nmiddleware\nroutes\ntemplates/static UI\nSMTP configuration\nfeature-control integration\n\nSearch for existing secrets only by metadata/path.\n\nNEVER print secret values.\n\nReport:\n\nDASHBOARD_PRESENT=\nAUTH_PRESENT=\nSESSION_SUPPORT_PRESENT=\nSMTP_SUPPORT_PRESENT=\nMOBILE_DETECTION_PRESENT=\n\n============================================================\nGATE\n============================================================\n\nRequired before change:\n\nDASHBOARD_NOT_PUBLIC_WAN=PASS\nSMTP_SECRET_IN_SOURCE=NO\nSMTP_SECRET_IN_GIT=NO\n\nRequired target:\n\nAUTH_EMAIL=will@unit.estixari.com\nAUTH_CODE_SINGLE_USE=YES\nAUTH_CODE_EXPIRING=YES\nAUTH_CODE_RATE_LIMITED=YES\n\nDESKTOP_UI_ALLOWED=NO\nMOBILE_UI_ALLOWED=YES\n\nIf dashboard is currently bound directly to public WAN:\n\nSTOP and report.\n\n============================================================\nMOBILE ACCESS POLICY\n============================================================\n\nImplement application-level mobile gate.\n\nAllow mobile/tablet browser classes.\n\nBlock desktop-class browsers before dashboard rendering.\n\nDesktop response should be a simple page:\n\n\"Dashboard available from authorized mobile devices only.\"\n\nDo not expose internal details.\n\nImplement detection centrally in middleware, not separately in every\nroute.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nUser-Agent/device-class detection is UX/access policy, NOT the security\nboundary.\n\nAuthentication remains mandatory even for mobile.\n\nAllow an explicit development/test override only when:\n\n- disabled by default\n- localhost/private admin only\n- clearly marked non-production\n\n============================================================\nAUTH-CODE FLOW\n============================================================\n\nUnauthenticated mobile user:\n\nGET /login\n\nUser requests code.\n\nServer generates cryptographically secure numeric or short alphanumeric\none-time code.\n\nRecommended properties:\n\nAUTH_CODE_TTL=10 minutes\nAUTH_CODE_MAX_ATTEMPTS=5\nAUTH_CODE_SINGLE_USE=YES\n\nDo not store raw code persistently.\n\nStore only:\n\ncode hash\ncreated timestamp\nexpiry\nattempt count\nconsumed state\nrequest metadata necessary for abuse control\n\nDestination email is fixed:\n\nwill@unit.estixari.com\n\nDo NOT let the public login form choose arbitrary recipient addresses.\n\n============================================================\nSMTP\n============================================================\n\nUse configurable SMTP environment variables, for example:\n\nWORM_SMTP_HOST\nWORM_SMTP_PORT\nWORM_SMTP_USERNAME\nWORM_SMTP_PASSWORD\nWORM_SMTP_FROM\nWORM_SMTP_TLS\n\nRecipient:\n\nWORM_DASHBOARD_AUTH_EMAIL=will@unit.estixari.com\n\nSMTP credentials MUST come from an existing secret mechanism or protected\nruntime environment.\n\nNever put SMTP password into:\n\nsource\nGit\ncurrent.json\nreports\nlogs\n\nPrefer TLS.\n\nFail closed if SMTP is unavailable.\n\nReport only:\n\nSMTP_CONFIG_PRESENT=\nSMTP_TLS_ENABLED=\nSMTP_AUTH_AVAILABLE=\n\nNever print credentials.\n\n============================================================\nLOGIN ENDPOINTS\n============================================================\n\nImplement minimal endpoints:\n\nGET  /login\nPOST /auth/request-code\nPOST /auth/verify-code\nPOST /logout\n\nFlow:\n\nmobile device\n -> request code\n -> SMTP\n -> will@unit.estixari.com\n -> enter code\n -> verify\n -> create authenticated session\n -> dashboard\n\n============================================================\nSESSION SECURITY\n============================================================\n\nUse server-side or securely signed sessions.\n\nRequired cookie properties where applicable:\n\nHttpOnly=YES\nSecure=YES\nSameSite=Strict or appropriate equivalent\n\nSet reasonable session expiration.\n\nRegenerate session identity after successful login.\n\nLogout invalidates session.\n\nDo not persist auth-code after consumption.\n\n============================================================\nRATE LIMITING\n============================================================\n\nImplement limits for:\n\ncode requests\ncode verification attempts\n\nSuggested baseline:\n\nmax 3 code requests / 15 minutes / client\nmax 5 attempts per generated code\n\nDo not permanently lock account/device from transient failures.\n\n============================================================\nDASHBOARD ROUTE PROTECTION\n============================================================\n\nAll dashboard/API routes except health/login/auth static resources must\nrequire BOTH:\n\nMOBILE_POLICY=PASS\nAUTH_SESSION=PASS\n\nProtect existing API such as:\n\n/api/status/features\n\nUnauthenticated access:\n\n401\n\nDesktop access:\n\n403\n\nAuthenticated mobile access:\n\n200\n\n============================================================\nNETWORK POLICY\n============================================================\n\nPreserve existing private/admin-only binding.\n\nPreferred access:\n\nauthorized phone\n -> Headscale/Tailscale\n -> Antani\n -> dashboard\n\nDo NOT create:\n\npublic WAN listener\npublic reverse proxy\nWAN firewall rule\n\nReturn:\n\nDASHBOARD_PRIVATE_ONLY=\n\n============================================================\nMODIFICA MINIMA\n============================================================\n\nImplement ONLY:\n\n- mobile middleware\n- login/auth-code endpoints\n- SMTP mail sender\n- session middleware\n- protected dashboard/API routes\n- minimal mobile login/error UI\n\nDo not redesign unrelated dashboard features.\n\n============================================================\nVERIFY\n============================================================\n\nUse safe test configuration.\n\nRequired tests:\n\nMOBILE_UNAUTHENTICATED_DASHBOARD=401_OR_LOGIN\nMOBILE_CODE_REQUEST=PASS\nSMTP_SEND_ATTEMPT=PASS\nAUTH_CODE_WRONG=REJECTED\nAUTH_CODE_VALID=PASS\nAUTH_CODE_REUSE=REJECTED\nAUTH_CODE_EXPIRED=REJECTED\n\nMOBILE_AUTHENTICATED_DASHBOARD=PASS\n\nDESKTOP_LOGIN_OR_DASHBOARD=403\nDESKTOP_DASHBOARD_RENDERED=NO\n\nAPI_UNAUTHENTICATED=401\nAPI_AUTHENTICATED_MOBILE=200\n\nSESSION_COOKIE_HTTPONLY=PASS\nSESSION_COOKIE_SECURE=PASS\n\nSMTP_SECRET_IN_SOURCE=NO\nSMTP_SECRET_IN_REPORT=NO\n\nDASHBOARD_PUBLIC_WAN_EXPOSURE=NO\n\n============================================================\nREPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite sanitized report:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/ROBOT-DASHBOARD-MOBILE-AUTH-CODE.md\n\nFinal:\n\nDASHBOARD_PRESENT=\nDASHBOARD_SERVICE=\nDASHBOARD_LISTEN_ADDRESS=\nDASHBOARD_PORT=\n\nMOBILE_POLICY_IMPLEMENTED=\nDESKTOP_ACCESS_BLOCKED=\n\nAUTH_CODE_IMPLEMENTED=\nAUTH_CODE_TTL=\nAUTH_CODE_SINGLE_USE=\nAUTH_CODE_RATE_LIMITED=\n\nAUTH_EMAIL=will@unit.estixari.com\n\nSMTP_CONFIG_PRESENT=\nSMTP_TLS_ENABLED=\nSMTP_SEND_TEST=\n\nSESSION_SECURITY_GATE=\n\nAPI_AUTH_GATE=\nMOBILE_DASHBOARD_GATE=\nDESKTOP_BLOCK_GATE=\n\nDASHBOARD_PRIVATE_ONLY=\nDASHBOARD_PUBLIC_WAN_EXPOSURE=NO\n\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_CHANGED=NO\nHEADSCALE_CHANGED=NO\nWG_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1177:{"session_id":"01a08755-ba69-7880-9b5d-d39bb21288b8","ts":1788986788,"text":"AUDIT ONLY — NON MODIFICARE FILE, NON ESEGUIRE SYNC, NON FARE RETE.\n\nTarget:\n  /opt/worm/scripts/storage_sync.py\n\nObiettivo:\nverificare se lo script ha bug o comportamenti pericolosi, in particolare perché\n`python3 storage_sync.py --help`\nha avviato un sync reale invece di mostrare l'help.\n\nProcedura obbligatoria:\n1. Leggi integralmente lo script.\n2. Non eseguire lo script.\n3. Non lanciare rsync/ssh/scp.\n4. Non modificare file.\n5. Non usare --help sullo script target.\n6. Analizza staticamente:\n\n- parsing CLI / sys.argv / argparse\n- comportamento con argomenti sconosciuti\n- comportamento senza argomenti\n- presenza o assenza di --help\n- distinzione sync / restore\n- source e destination\n- eventuale inversione source/destination\n- uso di --delete / delete-after / remove-source-files\n- rmtree / unlink / remove\n- subprocess.run / Popen / shell=True\n- check=True / returncode / gestione errori\n- timeout\n- gestione ssh\n- dry-run\n- report finali\n- exit code\n- idempotenza\n- race condition evidenti\n- rischio di sync avviato accidentalmente\n- rischio di cancellazione locale/remota\n- rischio che eccezioni vengano ignorate\n\nOutput richiesto:\n\n=== AUDIT storage_sync.py ===\n\nSEVERITY:\n- CRITICAL:\n- HIGH:\n- MEDIUM:\n- LOW:\n\nCLI:\n- ...\nSYNC SAFETY:\n- ...\nRESTORE SAFETY:\n- ...\nDELETE SAFETY:\n- ...\nERROR HANDLING:\n- ...\nREPORTING:\n- ...\n\nBUG CONFERMATI:\n1. ...\n\nBUG POTENZIALI:\n1. ...\n\nGATE:\nSAFE_TO_RUN=YES|NO\nSAFE_TO_USE_FOR_RESTORE=YES|NO\nSAFE_TO_USE_FOR_SYNC=YES|NO\n\nPATCH_RECOMMENDED=YES|NO\n\nSe PATCH_RECOMMENDED=YES:\nmostra SOLO una patch proposta in unified diff,\nma NON applicarla.\n\nVincolo:\nnessuna modifica, nessun comando distruttivo, nessun trasferimento di rete."}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1178:{"session_id":"01a08755-ba69-7880-9b5d-d39bb21288b8","ts":1788987162,"text":"Applica la patch minima a:\n\n/opt/worm/scripts/storage_sync.py\n\nSCOPO:\nrendere il comando sync fail-closed e sicuro.\nNON implementare ancora restore.\nNON eseguire alcun trasferimento reale.\n\nREQUISITI OBBLIGATORI:\n\n1. argparse obbligatorio.\n2. Il sync deve poter partire SOLO con:\n   python3 /opt/worm/scripts/storage_sync.py sync\n\n3. Devono essere non distruttivi:\n   --help\n   -h\n   nessun argomento\n   argomento sconosciuto\n\n4. Implementare:\n   sync --dry-run\n\n5. `--dry-run` deve aggiungere `--dry-run` al comando rsync.\n\n6. Nessun:\n   --delete\n   --delete-after\n   --remove-source-files\n\n7. SOURCE deve restare:\n   /opt/worm/\n\n8. DESTINATION deve restare esplicitamente il target Storage Box\n   attualmente configurato.\n\n9. Spostare i report sotto:\n   /opt/worm/artifacts/reports/storage-sync/\n\n10. Nessuna directory/report deve essere creata durante import del modulo.\n\n11. Non aggiungere restore in questa patch.\n\n12. Non eseguire rsync/ssh/scp reale durante la modifica o i test.\n\nVERIFICA STATICA + TEST LOCALI:\n\n- python3 storage_sync.py --help\n  -> exit 0, nessun sync\n\n- python3 storage_sync.py\n  -> exit non-zero, nessun sync\n\n- python3 storage_sync.py nonsense\n  -> exit non-zero, nessun sync\n\n- python3 storage_sync.py sync --help\n  -> exit 0, nessun sync\n\n- verificare tramite mock che:\n  storage_sync.py sync --dry-run\n  costruisca rsync con --dry-run\n\n- verificare tramite mock che:\n  storage_sync.py sync\n  sia l'unico percorso che può raggiungere l'esecuzione rsync\n\n- py_compile\n\n- controllare assenza di:\n  --delete\n  --delete-after\n  --remove-source-files\n  rmtree\n  unlink\n\nIMPORTANTE:\nnon usare il vero comando `sync` durante i test.\nMockare subprocess/Popen o il runner.\n\nScrivere report sanitizzato:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/STORAGE-SYNC-CLI-SAFETY.md\n\nOUTPUT FINALE:\n\nSTORAGE_SYNC_CLI_GATE=PASS|FAIL\nHELP_SAFE=YES|NO\nNO_ARGS_SAFE=YES|NO\nUNKNOWN_ARGS_SAFE=YES|NO\nDRY_RUN_IMPLEMENTED=YES|NO\nREAL_SYNC_EXPLICIT_ONLY=YES|NO\nDELETE_FLAGS_PRESENT=YES|NO\nNETWORK_USED_DURING_TESTS=YES|NO\nPY_COMPILE=PASS|FAIL\n\nSe tutti i gate passano:\nSAFE_TO_USE_FOR_SYNC=YES\nSAFE_TO_IMPLEMENT_RESTORE=YES\n\nAltrimenti:\nSAFE_TO_USE_FOR_SYNC=NO\nSAFE_TO_IMPLEMENT_RESTORE=NO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1179:{"session_id":"01a08755-ba69-7880-9b5d-d39bb21288b8","ts":1788987309,"text":"MODIFICA MINIMA — IMPLEMENTA SOLO RESTORE SICURO.\n\nTarget:\n  /opt/worm/scripts/storage_sync.py\n\nStato attuale:\n- CLI safety gate PASS\n- sync esplicito\n- dry-run presente\n- nessun delete flag\n- nessuna rete usata nei test\n\nObiettivo:\naggiungere un subcommand restore separato, sicuro e fail-closed.\n\nREQUISITI:\n\n1. Aggiungere:\n   storage_sync.py restore --source <remote-subpath> --dest <local-path> --dry-run\n\n2. Restore deve essere SEMPRE:\n   REMOTE -> LOCAL\n\n3. Vietare:\n   local -> remote nel percorso restore\n\n4. Nessun restore senza subcommand esplicito.\n\n5. Nessun restore senza:\n   --source\n   --dest\n\n6. --source deve essere interpretato come sottopercorso sotto il REMOTE_PATH configurato.\n   Non permettere path assoluti remoti arbitrari.\n\n7. --dest deve essere path locale assoluto.\n\n8. Prima di eseguire:\n   - normalizzare source\n   - normalizzare dest\n   - rifiutare traversal `..`\n   - rifiutare source vuoto\n   - rifiutare dest `/`\n   - rifiutare dest `/opt`\n   - rifiutare destinazioni fuori dal perimetro previsto senza flag esplicito\n\n9. Per questa prima implementazione permettere restore SOLO sotto:\n   /opt/Android/\n\n10. Non creare /opt/Android automaticamente durante dry-run.\n\n11. Implementare:\n   restore --dry-run\n\n12. Nessun:\n   --delete\n   --delete-after\n   --remove-source-files\n\n13. Prima del restore reale:\n   verificare che la directory remota esista tramite comando read-only.\n   Se manca: FAIL.\n\n14. Non usare shell=True.\n\n15. Propagare exit code rsync.\n\n16. Scrivere report sanitizzato sotto:\n   /opt/worm/artifacts/reports/storage-sync/\n\n17. NON eseguire restore reale durante i test.\n\nTEST OBBLIGATORI SOLO MOCK/STATICI:\n\n- restore --help -> safe\n- restore senza args -> fail closed\n- restore con source mancante -> fail\n- restore con dest mancante -> fail\n- restore source con .. -> fail\n- restore dest=/ -> fail\n- restore dest=/opt -> fail\n- restore dest fuori /opt/Android -> fail\n- restore --dry-run costruisce rsync REMOTE -> LOCAL\n- confermare che il comando non contenga delete flags\n- confermare che sync resti LOCAL -> REMOTE\n- py_compile\n\nOutput finale:\n\nSTORAGE_RESTORE_GATE=PASS|FAIL\nRESTORE_EXPLICIT_ONLY=YES|NO\nRESTORE_DIRECTION_REMOTE_TO_LOCAL=YES|NO\nRESTORE_DRY_RUN=YES|NO\nRESTORE_PATH_GUARDS=PASS|FAIL\nDELETE_FLAGS_PRESENT=YES|NO\nSYNC_DIRECTION_UNCHANGED=YES|NO\nNETWORK_USED_DURING_TESTS=YES|NO\nPY_COMPILE=PASS|FAIL\n\nSe tutto passa:\nSAFE_TO_DRY_RUN_RESTORE=YES\nSAFE_TO_REAL_RESTORE=NO\n\nImportante:\nanche se i test passano, NON eseguire restore reale."}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1180:{"session_id":"01a08755-ba69-7880-9b5d-d39bb21288b8","ts":1788987625,"text":"LEVEL PRO — FINAL PUBLIC IP ROLE SPLIT\nSERVICE PLANE + WEB PLANE\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> MINIMAL CHANGE -> VERIFY\n\nROOT:\n/opt/worm\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nSeparate public exposure into two authoritative roles:\n\nPUBLIC_IP_SERVICE\n  -> API/service backend\n  -> machine-to-machine endpoints\n  -> provisioning/control services\n\nPUBLIC_IP_WEB\n  -> Caddy\n  -> worm.coffee.pm\n  -> worm.estixari.com\n  -> dashboard web\n\nNo role mixing.\n\n============================================================\n1. DISCOVER AUTHORITATIVE PUBLIC IPS\n============================================================\n\nDetermine:\n\nPUBLIC_IP_SERVICE=\nPUBLIC_IP_WEB=\n\nFor both:\n\nOWNER_HOST=\nBOUND_INTERFACES=\nCURRENT_LISTENERS=\nCURRENT_DNS=\n\nRequired:\n\nPUBLIC_IP_SERVICE_IDENTIFIED=PASS\nPUBLIC_IP_WEB_IDENTIFIED=PASS\nPUBLIC_IPS_DISTINCT=YES\n\nDo not guess.\n\n============================================================\n2. SERVICE PLANE\n============================================================\n\nPUBLIC_IP_SERVICE_ROLE=SERVICES_ONLY\n\nInventory all intended service endpoints.\n\nInclude as applicable:\n\nCONTROL_API\nROBOT_API\nPROVISIONING_API\nAUTH_CODE_API\nIPAM\nWORMOS_ENROLLMENT\nOTA_METADATA_API\nMACHINE_TO_MACHINE_ENDPOINTS\n\nFor each:\n\nSERVICE=\nHOSTNAME=\nPORT=\nPROTOCOL=\nAUTH=\nPUBLIC_REQUIRED=\nSTATUS=\n\nDo not expose dashboard UI on PUBLIC_IP_SERVICE.\n\nRequired:\n\nSERVICE_IP_DASHBOARD_EXPOSURE=NO\n\n============================================================\n3. WEB PLANE\n============================================================\n\nPUBLIC_IP_WEB_ROLE=WEB_ONLY\n\nTarget hostnames:\n\nworm.coffee.pm\nworm.estixari.com\n\nBoth must terminate at Caddy on PUBLIC_IP_WEB.\n\nCaddy then reverse-proxies to the private dashboard origin.\n\nExpected origin where applicable:\n\n127.0.0.1:8765\n\nRequired:\n\nCADDY_WEB_ONLY=PASS\nDASHBOARD_BACKEND_PUBLIC=NO\n\n============================================================\n4. CADDY VHOSTS\n============================================================\n\nConfigure/verify two independent HTTPS hostnames:\n\nworm.coffee.pm\nworm.estixari.com\n\nBoth may proxy to the same authoritative dashboard application.\n\nPreserve:\n\nHost\nX-Forwarded-For\nX-Forwarded-Proto\n\nDo not trust arbitrary external forwarding headers.\n\nCaddy admin API must remain private.\n\nRequired:\n\nCADDY_ADMIN_PUBLIC=NO\n\n============================================================\n5. DASHBOARD AUTH POLICY\n============================================================\n\nPreserve existing application policy:\n\nDESKTOP_ACCESS=DENY_ALL\n\nMOBILE:\n  predefined password\n  ->\n  SMTP auth-code\n  ->\n  will@unit.estixari.com\n  ->\n  authenticated session\n  ->\n  dashboard\n\nRequired:\n\nDESKTOP_ZERO_ACCESS_POLICY_PRESERVED=PASS\nPASSWORD_AUTH_PRESERVED=PASS\nAUTH_CODE_PRESERVED=PASS\n\nBoth web hostnames must enforce the same backend auth state.\n\n============================================================\n6. DNS\n============================================================\n\nTarget:\n\nworm.coffee.pm    -> PUBLIC_IP_WEB\nworm.estixari.com -> PUBLIC_IP_WEB\n\nService/API hostnames must resolve to:\n\nPUBLIC_IP_SERVICE\n\nonly where explicitly intended.\n\nDo not point dashboard hostnames to PUBLIC_IP_SERVICE.\n\nReport:\n\nWORM_COFFEE_DNS=\nWORM_ESTIXARI_DNS=\nSERVICE_DNS_RECORDS=\n\n============================================================\n7. WEB EXPOSURE POLICY\n============================================================\n\nPUBLIC_IP_WEB should expose only intended web ports:\n\nTCP/80\nTCP/443\n\nFlag anything else:\n\nWEB_IP_UNEXPECTED_PORTS=\n\nDo not expose:\n\n8765\nservice API ports\ndatabase ports\ninternal control ports\n\nunless explicitly justified.\n\n============================================================\n8. SERVICE EXPOSURE POLICY\n============================================================\n\nPUBLIC_IP_SERVICE exposes only approved service/API ports.\n\nFlag:\n\nSERVICE_IP_UNEXPECTED_PORTS=\nSERVICE_IP_WEB_UI_EXPOSURE=\n\nRequired:\n\nSERVICE_IP_WEB_UI_EXPOSURE=NO\n\n============================================================\n9. CROSS-PLANE ISOLATION\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nWEB_TO_SERVICE_ROLE_MIXING=NO\nSERVICE_TO_WEB_ROLE_MIXING=NO\n\nDashboard web traffic must not terminate on SERVICE IP.\n\nMachine-to-machine API traffic must not depend on the dashboard web edge.\n\n============================================================\n10. NETWORK FREEZE\n============================================================\n\nDo not modify:\n\nOPNsense\nHeadscale\nWireGuard\nWormOS\nprivate VLAN\n\n============================================================\n11. GATE\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nPUBLIC_IP_SERVICE_IDENTIFIED=PASS\nPUBLIC_IP_WEB_IDENTIFIED=PASS\n\nWEB_ROLE_GATE=PASS\nSERVICE_ROLE_GATE=PASS\nDNS_ROLE_GATE=PASS\nCROSS_PLANE_ISOLATION_GATE=PASS\n\nThen:\n\nPUBLIC_IP_ROLE_SPLIT_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n12. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/PUBLIC-IP-FINAL-ROLE-SPLIT.md\n\nFinal:\n\nPUBLIC_IP_SERVICE=\nPUBLIC_IP_WEB=\n\nPUBLIC_IP_SERVICE_ROLE=SERVICES_ONLY\nPUBLIC_IP_WEB_ROLE=WEB_ONLY\n\nWORM_COFFEE_DNS=\nWORM_ESTIXARI_DNS=\nSERVICE_DNS_RECORDS=\n\nCADDY_WEB_ONLY=\nCADDY_ADMIN_PUBLIC=\n\nDASHBOARD_BACKEND_PUBLIC=\nSERVICE_IP_DASHBOARD_EXPOSURE=\n\nWEB_IP_UNEXPECTED_PORTS=\nSERVICE_IP_UNEXPECTED_PORTS=\n\nDESKTOP_ZERO_ACCESS_POLICY_PRESERVED=\nPASSWORD_AUTH_PRESERVED=\nAUTH_CODE_PRESERVED=\n\nWEB_TO_SERVICE_ROLE_MIXING=\nSERVICE_TO_WEB_ROLE_MIXING=\n\nPUBLIC_IP_ROLE_SPLIT_GATE=\n\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHEADSCALE_CHANGED=NO\nWG_CHANGED=NO\nWORMOS_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
