 .. -> fail\n- restore dest=/ -> fail\n- restore dest=/opt -> fail\n- restore dest fuori /opt/Android -> fail\n- restore --dry-run costruisce rsync REMOTE -> LOCAL\n- confermare che il comando non contenga delete flags\n- confermare che sync resti LOCAL -> REMOTE\n- py_compile\n\nOutput finale:\n\nSTORAGE_RESTORE_GATE=PASS|FAIL\nRESTORE_EXPLICIT_ONLY=YES|NO\nRESTORE_DIRECTION_REMOTE_TO_LOCAL=YES|NO\nRESTORE_DRY_RUN=YES|NO\nRESTORE_PATH_GUARDS=PASS|FAIL\nDELETE_FLAGS_PRESENT=YES|NO\nSYNC_DIRECTION_UNCHANGED=YES|NO\nNETWORK_USED_DURING_TESTS=YES|NO\nPY_COMPILE=PASS|FAIL\n\nSe tutto passa:\nSAFE_TO_DRY_RUN_RESTORE=YES\nSAFE_TO_REAL_RESTORE=NO\n\nImportante:\nanche se i test passano, NON eseguire restore reale."}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1183:{"session_id":"01a08a11-711a-78f0-b0e1-d1ad89d7af01","ts":1789022798,"text":"LEVEL PRO — DASHBOARD HTTP 500 ROOT-CAUSE AUDIT\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> NO CHANGE\n\nROOT=/opt/worm\n\nABSOLUTE FREEZE:\n\nDO NOT modify Caddy.\nDO NOT modify DNS.\nDO NOT modify firewall/networking.\nDO NOT modify OPNsense.\nDO NOT modify Headscale.\nDO NOT modify WireGuard.\nDO NOT restart anything.\n\nCURRENT EVIDENCE:\n\nworm-dashboard.service is listening:\n127.0.0.1:8765\n\nGET http://127.0.0.1:8765/\nreturns:\nHTTP 500 Internal Server Error\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nFind the exact exception causing dashboard HTTP 500.\n\n1. Inspect:\n\nsystemctl status worm-dashboard.service --no-pager -l\njournalctl -u worm-dashboard.service -n 200 --no-pager\n\n2. Inspect service definition and drop-ins:\n\nsystemctl cat worm-dashboard.service\n\n3. Determine presence ONLY, never values, of:\n\nWORM_DASHBOARD_PASSWORD_HASH\nWORM_DASHBOARD_PASSWORD_HASH_FILE\n\nWORM_SMTP_HOST\nWORM_SMTP_PORT\nWORM_SMTP_USERNAME\nWORM_SMTP_PASSWORD\nWORM_SMTP_FROM\nWORM_SMTP_TLS\n\nNever print secret values.\n\n4. Inspect application traceback associated with one controlled request:\n\ncurl http://127.0.0.1:8765/\n\nCorrelate the request with journal output.\n\n5. Classify:\n\nDASHBOARD_500_CLASS=\n\nAllowed classifications:\n\nPASSWORD_RUNTIME_SECRET_MISSING\nSMTP_RUNTIME_CONFIG_MISSING\nSESSION_SECRET_MISSING\nAPPLICATION_EXCEPTION\nTEMPLATE_EXCEPTION\nMIDDLEWARE_EXCEPTION\nCONFIG_EXCEPTION\nOTHER\n\n6. Report:\n\nDASHBOARD_SERVICE_ACTIVE=\nDASHBOARD_LISTENER=127.0.0.1:8765\nLOCAL_HTTP_STATUS=\n\nPASSWORD_HASH_PRESENT=\nPASSWORD_HASH_FILE_PRESENT=\n\nSMTP_HOST_PRESENT=\nSMTP_USERNAME_PRESENT=\nSMTP_PASSWORD_PRESENT=\nSMTP_FROM_PRESENT=\n\nEXCEPTION_TYPE=\nEXCEPTION_SOURCE_FILE=\nEXCEPTION_SOURCE_LINE=\n\nDo NOT include secret values or full sensitive traceback data.\n\n7. Determine exactly one minimal repair:\n\nMINIMAL_REPAIR=\n\nCHANGES_MADE=NONE\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/DASHBOARD-HTTP500-ROOT-CAUSE.md\n\nFINAL:\n\nDASHBOARD_500_CLASS=\nDASHBOARD_SERVICE_ACTIVE=\nLOCAL_HTTP_STATUS=\n\nPASSWORD_RUNTIME_GATE=\nSMTP_RUNTIME_GATE=\n\nMINIMAL_REPAIR=\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1184:{"session_id":"01a08a11-711a-78f0-b0e1-d1ad89d7af01","ts":1789022990,"text":"LEVEL PRO — WORM WEB RECOVERY\nDASHBOARD 500 + CADDY WEB IP FIX\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> MINIMAL CHANGE -> VERIFY\n\nROOT=/opt/worm\n\nAUTHORITATIVE ROLE SPLIT:\n\nPUBLIC_IP_SERVICE=162.55.6.173\nPUBLIC_IP_WEB=162.55.6.147\nOPNSENSE_WAN=2.28.34.27\n\nTARGET WEB HOSTS:\n\nworm.coffee.pm\nworm.estixari.com\n\nTARGET DASHBOARD ORIGIN:\n\n127.0.0.1:8765\n\nABSOLUTE FREEZE:\n\nDO NOT modify OPNsense.\nDO NOT modify Headscale.\nDO NOT modify WireGuard.\nDO NOT modify private VLAN.\nDO NOT move service-plane listeners to PUBLIC_IP_WEB.\nDO NOT move web-plane listeners to PUBLIC_IP_SERVICE.\nDO NOT expose port 8765 publicly.\nDO NOT print SMTP/password/private-key secrets.\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nRestore:\n\nhttps://worm.coffee.pm\nhttps://worm.estixari.com\n\nthrough:\n\nPUBLIC_IP_WEB=162.55.6.147\n -> Caddy\n -> 127.0.0.1:8765\n\nwhile keeping:\n\nPUBLIC_IP_SERVICE=162.55.6.173\nfor service/API traffic only.\n\n============================================================\n1. AUDIT CURRENT LOCAL WEB STATE\n============================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nsystemctl is-active caddy\nsystemctl is-active worm-dashboard.service\n\nss -lntp\n\ncurl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\\n' http://127.0.0.1:8765/\n\nRecord:\n\nCADDY_RUNNING=\nDASHBOARD_RUNNING=\nLOCAL_DASHBOARD_HTTP_STATUS=\n\nIf dashboard returns 500, inspect:\n\njournalctl -u worm-dashboard.service -n 200 --no-pager\nsystemctl cat worm-dashboard.service\n\nFind exact root cause.\n\nDo not print secret values.\n\n============================================================\n2. FIX DASHBOARD 500 FIRST\n============================================================\n\nKnown implementation requirements:\n\nWORM_DASHBOARD_PASSWORD_HASH\nor\nWORM_DASHBOARD_PASSWORD_HASH_FILE\n\nSMTP runtime variables\n\nsession/auth runtime configuration\n\nDetermine which required runtime items are missing.\n\nIf only protected runtime configuration is missing, create the minimum\nprotected runtime environment/drop-in required by worm-dashboard.service.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- secrets outside Git/source\n- root-owned\n- mode 0600 or stricter\n- no plaintext secret in reports/logs\n- no frontend exposure\n\nDo NOT invent a password.\n\nIf password secret is unavailable:\nSTOP with PASSWORD_SECRET_REQUIRED=YES.\n\nIf SMTP runtime secret is unavailable:\nSTOP with SMTP_SECRET_REQUIRED=YES.\n\nIf all required secrets already exist:\napply only the minimal runtime fix.\n\nRestart ONLY:\n\nworm-dashboard.service\n\nThen verify:\n\ncurl http://127.0.0.1:8765/\n\nExpected acceptable statuses:\n\n200\n302\n401\n403\n\n500 is NOT acceptable.\n\nRequired:\n\nLOCAL_DASHBOARD_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n3. AUDIT PUBLIC IP OWNERSHIP/BINDING\n============================================================\n\nVerify locally:\n\nip -br addr\nip route\n\nDetermine whether:\n\n162.55.6.173\n162.55.6.147\n\nare actually bound or routed to this host.\n\nReturn:\n\nSERVICE_IP_LOCAL=\nWEB_IP_LOCAL=\n\nIf 162.55.6.147 is not local but is routed/forwarded to this host via\nprovider/network configuration, prove that path from existing\nauthoritative evidence.\n\nIf ownership/routing cannot be proven:\nSTOP before changing bind/firewall.\n\n============================================================\n4. CADDY ROLE SPLIT\n============================================================\n\nAudit:\n\n/etc/caddy/Caddyfile\n\nTarget:\n\nPUBLIC_IP_WEB=162.55.6.147\nPUBLIC_IP_SERVICE=162.55.6.173\n\nCaddy WEB vhosts:\n\nworm.coffee.pm\nworm.estixari.com\n\nBoth must reverse_proxy to:\n\n127.0.0.1:8765\n\nDo not route dashboard/API web frontend through 162.55.6.173.\n\nPreserve service-plane listeners on 162.55.6.173.\n\nCaddy admin API must remain non-public.\n\n============================================================\n5. MINIMAL CADDY CHANGE\n============================================================\n\nApply only if required.\n\nEnsure Caddy serves:\n\nworm.coffee.pm\nworm.estixari.com\n\non the WEB role.\n\nPreferred public exposure:\n\n162.55.6.147:80\n162.55.6.147:443\n\nDo not expose:\n\n162.55.6.147:8765\n\nDo not create dashboard listener on:\n\n162.55.6.173:443\n\nunless an existing unrelated service explicitly owns it.\n\nValidate:\n\ncaddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile\n\nThen reload ONLY Caddy:\n\nsystemctl reload caddy\n\nDo not restart networking.\n\n============================================================\n6. DNS GATE\n============================================================\n\nAudit:\n\ndig +short A worm.coffee.pm\ndig +short A worm.estixari.com\n\nTarget:\n\nworm.coffee.pm    -> 162.55.6.147\nworm.estixari.com -> 162.55.6.147\n\nIf either hostname points elsewhere, and an already-authorized DNS API/\nconfiguration mechanism exists, update ONLY these A records.\n\nDo not alter unrelated DNS.\n\nIf no authorized DNS write mechanism exists:\nreport DNS_CHANGE_REQUIRED=YES and STOP before inventing credentials.\n\n============================================================\n7. FIREWALL / PORT VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nVerify WEB IP only requires:\n\nTCP/80\nTCP/443\n\nDo not disable firewall.\n\nDo not flush nftables/iptables/FireHOL.\n\nIf current host firewall blocks 80/443 specifically on WEB IP, apply the\nsmallest native persistent rule required for Caddy only.\n\nPreserve service IP policy.\n\nRequired:\n\nWEB_80_REACHABLE=\nWEB_443_REACHABLE=\n\n============================================================\n8. END-TO-END VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nVerify locally with SNI/Host as appropriate and externally where possible:\n\nhttps://worm.coffee.pm/\nhttps://worm.estixari.com/\n\nRequired:\n\nWORM_COFFEE_HTTPS_STATUS=\nWORM_ESTIXARI_HTTPS_STATUS=\n\nAcceptable application-level results include:\n\n200\n302\n401\n403\n\ndepending on mobile/auth state.\n\nDo NOT accept:\n\ntimeout\nconnection refused\n500\n502\n503\n\n============================================================\n9. SECURITY VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nPUBLIC_IP_SERVICE=162.55.6.173\nPUBLIC_IP_WEB=162.55.6.147\n\nSERVICE_IP_ROLE=SERVICES_ONLY\nWEB_IP_ROLE=WEB_ONLY\n\nDASHBOARD_BACKEND=127.0.0.1:8765\nPUBLIC_8765=NO\n\nDESKTOP_ZERO_ACCESS_POLICY_PRESERVED=PASS\nPASSWORD_AUTH_PRESERVED=PASS\nAUTH_CODE_PRESERVED=PASS\n\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHEADSCALE_CHANGED=NO\nWG_CHANGED=NO\n\n============================================================\n10. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WORM-WEB-RECOVERY.md\n\nFinal:\n\nPUBLIC_IP_SERVICE=\nPUBLIC_IP_WEB=\n\nSERVICE_IP_LOCAL=\nWEB_IP_LOCAL=\n\nCADDY_RUNNING=\nCADDY_CONFIG_VALID=\n\nDASHBOARD_RUNNING=\nLOCAL_DASHBOARD_HTTP_STATUS=\nLOCAL_DASHBOARD_GATE=\n\nPASSWORD_RUNTIME_GATE=\nSMTP_RUNTIME_GATE=\n\nWORM_COFFEE_A=\nWORM_ESTIXARI_A=\n\nWEB_80_REACHABLE=\nWEB_443_REACHABLE=\n\nWORM_COFFEE_HTTPS_STATUS=\nWORM_ESTIXARI_HTTPS_STATUS=\n\nPUBLIC_8765=NO\n\nSERVICE_IP_ROLE=\nWEB_IP_ROLE=\n\nDESKTOP_ZERO_ACCESS_POLICY_PRESERVED=\nPASSWORD_AUTH_PRESERVED=\nAUTH_CODE_PRESERVED=\n\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHEADSCALE_CHANGED=NO\nWG_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1185:{"session_id":"01a08a11-711a-78f0-b0e1-d1ad89d7af01","ts":1789023880,"text":"LEVEL PRO — GIT WEB REACHABILITY AUDIT\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> NO CHANGE\n\nROOT=/opt/worm\n\nABSOLUTE FREEZE:\n\nDO NOT modify DNS.\nDO NOT modify Caddy.\nDO NOT modify GitLab.\nDO NOT restart services.\nDO NOT modify firewall.\nDO NOT modify networking.\nDO NOT modify OPNsense.\nDO NOT modify Headscale/WireGuard.\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nDetermine why the Git web endpoint is unreachable.\n\nTest BOTH names because user reported:\n\ngit.worn.estixari.com\n\nand expected naming may be:\n\ngit.worm.estixari.com\n\n============================================================\n1. DNS\n============================================================\n\nRun:\n\ndig +short A git.worn.estixari.com\ndig +short AAAA git.worn.estixari.com\n\ndig +short A git.worm.estixari.com\ndig +short AAAA git.worm.estixari.com\n\nReport:\n\nGIT_WORN_A=\nGIT_WORN_AAAA=\n\nGIT_WORM_A=\nGIT_WORM_AAAA=\n\nDetermine authoritative configured hostname from local GitLab/Caddy\nconfiguration.\n\nGIT_AUTHORITATIVE_HOSTNAME=\n\n============================================================\n2. LOCAL GITLAB\n============================================================\n\nAudit:\n\nsystemctl status gitlab-runsvdir --no-pager\ngitlab-ctl status\n\nDo not restart.\n\nInspect listeners:\n\nss -lntp\n\nDetermine:\n\nGITLAB_RUNNING=\nGITLAB_WEB_LISTENER=\nGITLAB_WEB_PORT=\n\n============================================================\n3. LOCAL HTTP TEST\n============================================================\n\nDetermine actual local GitLab web upstream from existing configuration.\n\nTest it locally without authentication.\n\nReport:\n\nGITLAB_LOCAL_HTTP_STATUS=\n\nAccept:\n\n200\n301\n302\n401\n403\n\nReject:\n\n000\n500\n502\n503\n\n============================================================\n4. CADDY\n============================================================\n\nRead:\n\n/etc/caddy/Caddyfile\n\nDetermine whether either hostname exists:\n\ngit.worn.estixari.com\ngit.worm.estixari.com\n\nReport:\n\nGIT_CADDY_VHOST=\nGIT_CADDY_UPSTREAM=\n\nRun:\n\ncaddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile\n\nReport:\n\nCADDY_CONFIG_VALID=\n\n============================================================\n5. PUBLIC ROLE\n============================================================\n\nCurrent intended architecture:\n\nPUBLIC_IP_SERVICE=162.55.6.173\nPUBLIC_IP_WEB=162.55.6.147\n\nDetermine which plane Git web currently uses.\n\nReport:\n\nGIT_CURRENT_PUBLIC_IP=\nGIT_CURRENT_PLANE=\n\nClassify intended role separately:\n\nGit Web UI -> WEB\nGit SSH/service endpoint -> SERVICE where explicitly designed\n\nDo not change either.\n\n============================================================\n6. EXTERNAL HTTPS\n============================================================\n\nRun short safe probes against the authoritative hostname:\n\ncurl -4 -vkI --connect-timeout 5 https://<AUTHORITATIVE_HOSTNAME>/\n\nReport:\n\nGIT_PUBLIC_HTTPS_STATUS=\n\nClassify:\n\nDNS_MISSING\nDNS_WRONG\nPUBLIC_IP_UNREACHABLE\nCADDY_VHOST_MISSING\nCADDY_UPSTREAM_WRONG\nGITLAB_DOWN\nGITLAB_LOCAL_WEB_FAILURE\nTLS_FAILURE\nFIREWALL_OR_ROUTING\nHOSTNAME_TYPO\nOTHER\n\nGIT_WEB_FAILURE_CLASS=\n\n============================================================\n7. FINAL\n============================================================\n\nGIT_AUTHORITATIVE_HOSTNAME=\n\nGIT_WORN_A=\nGIT_WORM_A=\n\nGITLAB_RUNNING=\nGITLAB_LOCAL_HTTP_STATUS=\n\nGIT_CADDY_VHOST=\nGIT_CADDY_UPSTREAM=\nCADDY_CONFIG_VALID=\n\nGIT_CURRENT_PUBLIC_IP=\nGIT_CURRENT_PLANE=\n\nGIT_PUBLIC_HTTPS_STATUS=\nGIT_WEB_FAILURE_CLASS=\n\nCHANGES_MADE=NONE\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE=\n\nWrite:\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/GIT-WEB-REACHABILITY-AUDIT.md"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1186:{"session_id":"01a08a11-711a-78f0-b0e1-d1ad89d7af01","ts":1789024240,"text":"LEVEL PRO — WORM WEB DUAL-HOST RECOVERY\nworm.estixari.com + worm.coffee.pm\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> MINIMAL CHANGE -> VERIFY\n\nAUTHORITATIVE ROLES:\n\nPUBLIC_IP_SERVICE=162.55.6.173\nPUBLIC_IP_WEB=162.55.6.147\nOPNSENSE_WAN=2.28.34.27\n\nPRIMARY_WEB=worm.estixari.com\nMIRROR_WEB=worm.coffee.pm\n\nDASHBOARD_ORIGIN=127.0.0.1:8765\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nMake BOTH:\n\nhttps://worm.estixari.com\nhttps://worm.coffee.pm\n\nserve the SAME Worm dashboard through:\n\n162.55.6.147\n -> Caddy\n -> 127.0.0.1:8765\n\nworm.coffee.pm is an alias/mirror.\nDo NOT create a second dashboard instance.\n\n============================================================\nABSOLUTE FREEZE\n============================================================\n\nDO NOT modify:\n\nOPNsense\nHeadscale\nWireGuard\nprivate VLAN\nPUBLIC_IP_SERVICE role\nservice/API endpoints\n\nDO NOT expose 8765 publicly.\n\nDO NOT duplicate:\n\ndashboard process\npassword database\nauth-code state\nsession state\n\n============================================================\n1. DASHBOARD ORIGIN GATE\n============================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nsystemctl is-active worm-dashboard.service\n\nss -lntp\n\ncurl locally:\n\nhttp://127.0.0.1:8765/\n\nRequired acceptable HTTP status:\n\n200\n302\n401\n403\n\n500 is FAIL.\n\nReturn:\n\nDASHBOARD_RUNNING=\nDASHBOARD_ORIGIN_STATUS=\nDASHBOARD_ORIGIN_GATE=\n\nIf origin returns 500:\n\nSTOP before DNS/Caddy production changes.\n\nReport exact blocker.\n\n============================================================\n2. DNS AUDIT\n============================================================\n\nResolve:\n\nworm.estixari.com\nworm.coffee.pm\n\nReturn:\n\nWORM_ESTIXARI_A=\nWORM_ESTIXARI_AAAA=\n\nWORM_COFFEE_A=\nWORM_COFFEE_AAAA=\n\nTARGET:\n\nworm.estixari.com -> 162.55.6.147\nworm.coffee.pm    -> 162.55.6.147\n\n============================================================\n3. WEB IP GATE\n============================================================\n\nProve that:\n\nPUBLIC_IP_WEB=162.55.6.147\n\nis owned/routed by authorized infrastructure and can terminate Caddy\ntraffic.\n\nReturn:\n\nWEB_IP_OWNER_VERIFIED=\nWEB_IP_ROUTE_TO_CADDY_VERIFIED=\nWEB_IP_80_READY=\nWEB_IP_443_READY=\n\nIf routing/ownership cannot be proven:\n\nSTOP.\n\nDo NOT substitute:\n\n162.55.6.173\n\nPUBLIC_IP_SERVICE must remain SERVICES_ONLY.\n\n============================================================\n4. CADDY AUDIT\n============================================================\n\nInspect existing:\n\n/etc/caddy/Caddyfile\n\nDetermine current configuration for:\n\nworm.estixari.com\nworm.coffee.pm\n\nReturn:\n\nPRIMARY_WEB_VHOST_PRESENT=\nMIRROR_WEB_VHOST_PRESENT=\n\nPRIMARY_WEB_UPSTREAM=\nMIRROR_WEB_UPSTREAM=\n\nValidate:\n\ncaddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile\n\nRequired:\n\nCADDY_CONFIG_VALID=PASS\n\n============================================================\n5. MINIMAL CADDY CHANGE\n============================================================\n\nOnly after origin + WEB IP gates PASS.\n\nConfigure:\n\nworm.estixari.com {\n    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8765\n}\n\nworm.coffee.pm {\n    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8765\n}\n\nEquivalent existing Caddy structure is acceptable.\n\nBoth MUST use the SAME origin.\n\nPreserve required proxy metadata.\n\nDo not trust arbitrary external forwarded headers.\n\nCaddy admin API must remain private.\n\nValidate configuration BEFORE reload.\n\nThen reload ONLY:\n\ncaddy\n\nDo not restart networking.\n\n============================================================\n6. DNS MINIMAL CHANGE\n============================================================\n\nOnly using an existing authorized DNS management mechanism.\n\nTarget A records:\n\nworm.estixari.com -> 162.55.6.147\nworm.coffee.pm    -> 162.55.6.147\n\nDo NOT alter unrelated DNS.\n\nDo NOT point either web hostname to:\n\n162.55.6.173\n\nIf DNS write authorization is unavailable:\n\nSTOP with:\n\nDNS_CHANGE_REQUIRED=YES\n\n============================================================\n7. AUTH MUST BE SHARED\n============================================================\n\nBoth hostnames use the SAME dashboard application.\n\nRequired policy:\n\nDESKTOP -> DENY ALL\n\nMOBILE:\n -> predefined password\n -> SMTP auth-code\n -> will@unit.estixari.com\n -> authenticated session\n -> dashboard\n\nRequired:\n\nSAME_DASHBOARD_ORIGIN=PASS\nSAME_PASSWORD_AUTH=PASS\nSAME_AUTH_CODE_BACKEND=PASS\nSAME_SESSION_BACKEND=PASS\n\nDo NOT implement separate auth state per hostname.\n\n============================================================\n8. HOST / COOKIE VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nAudit session-cookie behavior for both HTTPS hostnames.\n\nEnsure authentication does not accidentally bypass because requests\narrive through a different Host header.\n\nRequired:\n\nPRIMARY_AUTH_GATE=PASS\nMIRROR_AUTH_GATE=PASS\n\nDESKTOP_PRIMARY=403\nDESKTOP_MIRROR=403\n\nUNKNOWN_DEVICE_PRIMARY=403\nUNKNOWN_DEVICE_MIRROR=403\n\nMobile authentication must remain required on both.\n\nDo NOT weaken SameSite/Secure/HttpOnly cookie policy.\n\n============================================================\n9. END-TO-END VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nTest independently:\n\nhttps://worm.estixari.com/\nhttps://worm.coffee.pm/\n\nAccept application responses:\n\n200\n302\n401\n403\n\nReject:\n\ntimeout\nconnection refused\n500\n502\n503\n\nReturn:\n\nWORM_ESTIXARI_HTTPS=\nWORM_COFFEE_HTTPS=\n\nVerify:\n\nSAME_DASHBOARD_ORIGIN=PASS\n\n============================================================\n10. PUBLIC EXPOSURE VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nPUBLIC_IP_WEB=162.55.6.147\nPUBLIC_IP_SERVICE=162.55.6.173\n\nWEB_IP_ROLE=WEB_ONLY\nSERVICE_IP_ROLE=SERVICES_ONLY\n\nPUBLIC_8765=NO\nCADDY_ADMIN_PUBLIC=NO\n\nworm.estixari.com -> WEB IP\nworm.coffee.pm -> WEB IP\n\nNo dashboard WebUI on SERVICE IP.\n\n============================================================\n11. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WORM-WEB-DUAL-HOST-RECOVERY.md\n\nFinal:\n\nPRIMARY_WEB=worm.estixari.com\nMIRROR_WEB=worm.coffee.pm\n\nPUBLIC_IP_WEB=\nPUBLIC_IP_SERVICE=\n\nWORM_ESTIXARI_A=\nWORM_COFFEE_A=\n\nDASHBOARD_RUNNING=\nDASHBOARD_ORIGIN_STATUS=\nDASHBOARD_ORIGIN_GATE=\n\nWEB_IP_OWNER_VERIFIED=\nWEB_IP_ROUTE_TO_CADDY_VERIFIED=\n\nCADDY_CONFIG_VALID=\n\nPRIMARY_WEB_UPSTREAM=\nMIRROR_WEB_UPSTREAM=\n\nWORM_ESTIXARI_HTTPS=\nWORM_COFFEE_HTTPS=\n\nSAME_DASHBOARD_ORIGIN=\nSAME_PASSWORD_AUTH=\nSAME_AUTH_CODE_BACKEND=\nSAME_SESSION_BACKEND=\n\nDESKTOP_PRIMARY=\nDESKTOP_MIRROR=\n\nPUBLIC_8765=NO\nCADDY_ADMIN_PUBLIC=NO\n\nWEB_IP_ROLE=WEB_ONLY\nSERVICE_IP_ROLE=SERVICES_ONLY\n\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHEADSCALE_CHANGED=NO\nWG_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1188:{"session_id":"01a08a11-711a-78f0-b0e1-d1ad89d7af01","ts":1789026783,"text":"LEVEL PRO — RETIRE GITLAB + git.worm.estixari.com\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> BACKUP -> GATE -> REMOVE -> VERIFY\n\nROOT=/opt/worm\n\nAUTHORIZED DESTRUCTIVE CHANGE=YES\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nCompletely retire the local GitLab installation and remove the DNS record\nfor:\n\ngit.worm.estixari.com\n\nDo NOT remove or modify:\n\ngit.coffee.pm\n\nunless explicitly required to remove a stale Caddy upstream pointing to\nthe retired GitLab.\n\nABSOLUTE FREEZE:\n\nDO NOT modify OPNsense.\nDO NOT modify Headscale.\nDO NOT modify WireGuard.\nDO NOT modify WORM dashboard.\nDO NOT modify PUBLIC_IP_SERVICE/PUBLIC_IP_WEB addressing.\nDO NOT delete Git repositories before verified backup.\nDO NOT delete GitHub remotes/repositories.\n\n============================================================\n1. AUDIT GITLAB\n============================================================\n\nDiscover authoritative GitLab installation:\n\npackages\nservices\nsystemd units\ngitlab-ctl state\nconfiguration\ndata directories\nrepositories\nCaddy vhosts\nDNS records\n\nDetermine:\n\nGITLAB_INSTALLED=\nGITLAB_RUNNING=\nGITLAB_VERSION=\n\nGITLAB_DATA_PATH=\nGITLAB_CONFIG_PATH=\nGITLAB_LOG_PATH=\n\nGIT_REPOSITORY_COUNT=\n\nGIT_WORM_DNS_CURRENT=\nGIT_COFFEE_DNS_CURRENT=\n\nFind repositories whose ONLY authoritative copy is local GitLab.\n\nReturn:\n\nLOCAL_ONLY_REPOSITORIES=\nREMOTE_BACKED_REPOSITORIES=\n\n============================================================\n2. BACKUP GATE — MANDATORY\n============================================================\n\nBefore deleting anything:\n\ncreate a complete recovery backup of GitLab configuration and repository\ndata using the safest existing GitLab/native mechanism.\n\nAlso inventory repository remotes.\n\nStore backup under an appropriate protected backup location outside the\nGitLab directories that will be removed.\n\nGenerate SHA256 manifest.\n\nRequired:\n\nBACKUP_CREATED=YES\nBACKUP_HASH_MANIFEST=PASS\nBACKUP_READABLE=PASS\n\nIf any repository is LOCAL_ONLY and not included in verified backup:\n\nSTOP.\n\nGITLAB_REMOVAL_GATE=FAIL\n\nDo not delete anything.\n\n============================================================\n3. CADDY AUDIT\n============================================================\n\nFind references to:\n\ngit.worm.estixari.com\ngit.coffee.pm\n127.0.0.1:8181\nGitLab\n\nDetermine:\n\nGIT_WORM_CADDY_VHOST=\nGIT_COFFEE_CADDY_VHOST=\n\nDo NOT remove git.coffee.pm itself.\n\nIf git.coffee.pm currently proxies exclusively to GitLab, mark:\n\nGIT_COFFEE_UPSTREAM_RETIRE_REQUIRED=YES\n\nbut preserve the hostname for future use.\n\n============================================================\n4. DNS GATE\n============================================================\n\nDiscover the existing authorized DNS management mechanism.\n\nTarget deletion ONLY:\n\ngit.worm.estixari.com\n\nRemove its A/AAAA/CNAME records as applicable.\n\nDO NOT remove:\n\ngit.coffee.pm\nworm.coffee.pm\nworm.estixari.com\n\nDo not modify unrelated DNS.\n\nIf DNS write authorization is unavailable:\n\nSTOP before uninstalling GitLab.\n\nRequired:\n\nDNS_WRITE_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n5. REMOVE GITLAB\n============================================================\n\nOnly after:\n\nBACKUP_CREATED=YES\nBACKUP_HASH_MANIFEST=PASS\nDNS_WRITE_GATE=PASS\n\nGracefully stop GitLab.\n\nDisable its services.\n\nRemove GitLab packages using the installed distribution's native package\nmanager.\n\nRemove obsolete GitLab runtime/service configuration only after package\nremoval.\n\nDo NOT blindly rm -rf unknown directories.\n\nFor each remaining GitLab path:\n\nclassify before deletion as:\n\nCONFIG\nDATA\nLOG\nCACHE\nBACKUP\nUNKNOWN\n\nNever delete the verified recovery backup.\n\nRemove obsolete local GitLab listeners.\n\n============================================================\n6. CADDY CLEANUP\n============================================================\n\nRemove ONLY the obsolete Caddy vhost for:\n\ngit.worm.estixari.com\n\nIf git.coffee.pm currently points to retired GitLab:\n\nremove/disable only its obsolete GitLab reverse_proxy mapping while\npreserving the hostname for future configuration.\n\nDo not redirect git.coffee.pm somewhere else automatically.\n\nValidate:\n\ncaddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile\n\nThen reload ONLY Caddy if configuration changed.\n\n============================================================\n7. DNS REMOVE\n============================================================\n\nDelete authoritative DNS records for:\n\ngit.worm.estixari.com\n\nVerify:\n\ndig +short A git.worm.estixari.com\ndig +short AAAA git.worm.estixari.com\ndig +short CNAME git.worm.estixari.com\n\nExpected after authoritative propagation:\n\nNO RECORD\n\nPreserve:\n\ngit.coffee.pm\n\n============================================================\n8. VERIFY SERVER\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nGITLAB_INSTALLED=NO\nGITLAB_RUNNING=NO\nGITLAB_LISTENER_PRESENT=NO\n\nVerify no remaining unexpected GitLab listeners.\n\nVerify:\n\ngitlab-ctl no longer active/installed as appropriate.\n\nCheck disk usage recovered:\n\nDISK_BEFORE=\nDISK_AFTER=\nDISK_RECLAIMED=\n\n============================================================\n9. PRESERVE GIT CLIENT DATA\n============================================================\n\nDo NOT rewrite existing /opt/worm Git remotes automatically.\n\nAudit them and report any remote still referencing:\n\ngit.worm.estixari.com\n\nReturn:\n\nSTALE_GIT_REMOTES=\n\nThese will be migrated separately.\n\n============================================================\n10. FINAL\n============================================================\n\nGITLAB_BACKUP_CREATED=\nGITLAB_BACKUP_HASH_MANIFEST=\nGITLAB_BACKUP_PATH=\n\nGITLAB_REMOVAL_GATE=\n\nGITLAB_INSTALLED=\nGITLAB_RUNNING=\nGITLAB_LISTENER_PRESENT=\n\nGIT_WORM_DNS_REMOVED=\nGIT_WORM_A=\nGIT_WORM_AAAA=\nGIT_WORM_CNAME=\n\nGIT_COFFEE_PRESERVED=YES\n\nGIT_WORM_CADDY_REMOVED=\nGIT_COFFEE_UPSTREAM_RETIRE_REQUIRED=\n\nSTALE_GIT_REMOTES=\n\nDISK_RECLAIMED=\n\nDASHBOARD_CHANGED=NO\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHEADSCALE_CHANGED=NO\nWG_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE=\n\nWrite report:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/GITLAB-RETIREMENT.md"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1189:{"session_id":"01a08a55-04e7-7063-bd04-03e246305f05","ts":1789027267,"text":"LEVEL PRO — RETIRE GITLAB + git.worm.estixari.com\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> BACKUP -> GATE -> REMOVE -> VERIFY\n\nROOT=/opt/worm\n\nAUTHORIZED DESTRUCTIVE CHANGE=YES\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nCompletely retire the local GitLab installation and remove the DNS record\nfor:\n\ngit.worm.estixari.com\n\nDo NOT remove or modify:\n\ngit.coffee.pm\n\nunless explicitly required to remove a stale Caddy upstream pointing to\nthe retired GitLab.\n\nABSOLUTE FREEZE:\n\nDO NOT modify OPNsense.\nDO NOT modify Headscale.\nDO NOT modify WireGuard.\nDO NOT modify WORM dashboard.\nDO NOT modify PUBLIC_IP_SERVICE/PUBLIC_IP_WEB addressing.\nDO NOT delete Git repositories before verified backup.\nDO NOT delete GitHub remotes/repositories.\n\n============================================================\n1. AUDIT GITLAB\n============================================================\n\nDiscover authoritative GitLab installation:\n\npackages\nservices\nsystemd units\ngitlab-ctl state\nconfiguration\ndata directories\nrepositories\nCaddy vhosts\nDNS records\n\nDetermine:\n\nGITLAB_INSTALLED=\nGITLAB_RUNNING=\nGITLAB_VERSION=\n\nGITLAB_DATA_PATH=\nGITLAB_CONFIG_PATH=\nGITLAB_LOG_PATH=\n\nGIT_REPOSITORY_COUNT=\n\nGIT_WORM_DNS_CURRENT=\nGIT_COFFEE_DNS_CURRENT=\n\nFind repositories whose ONLY authoritative copy is local GitLab.\n\nReturn:\n\nLOCAL_ONLY_REPOSITORIES=\nREMOTE_BACKED_REPOSITORIES=\n\n============================================================\n2. BACKUP GATE — MANDATORY\n============================================================\n\nBefore deleting anything:\n\ncreate a complete recovery backup of GitLab configuration and repository\ndata using the safest existing GitLab/native mechanism.\n\nAlso inventory repository remotes.\n\nStore backup under an appropriate protected backup location outside the\nGitLab directories that will be removed.\n\nGenerate SHA256 manifest.\n\nRequired:\n\nBACKUP_CREATED=YES\nBACKUP_HASH_MANIFEST=PASS\nBACKUP_READABLE=PASS\n\nIf any repository is LOCAL_ONLY and not included in verified backup:\n\nSTOP.\n\nGITLAB_REMOVAL_GATE=FAIL\n\nDo not delete anything.\n\n============================================================\n3. CADDY AUDIT\n============================================================\n\nFind references to:\n\ngit.worm.estixari.com\ngit.coffee.pm\n127.0.0.1:8181\nGitLab\n\nDetermine:\n\nGIT_WORM_CADDY_VHOST=\nGIT_COFFEE_CADDY_VHOST=\n\nDo NOT remove git.coffee.pm itself.\n\nIf git.coffee.pm currently proxies exclusively to GitLab, mark:\n\nGIT_COFFEE_UPSTREAM_RETIRE_REQUIRED=YES\n\nbut preserve the hostname for future use.\n\n============================================================\n4. DNS GATE\n============================================================\n\nDiscover the existing authorized DNS management mechanism.\n\nTarget deletion ONLY:\n\ngit.worm.estixari.com\n\nRemove its A/AAAA/CNAME records as applicable.\n\nDO NOT remove:\n\ngit.coffee.pm\nworm.coffee.pm\nworm.estixari.com\n\nDo not modify unrelated DNS.\n\nIf DNS write authorization is unavailable:\n\nSTOP before uninstalling GitLab.\n\nRequired:\n\nDNS_WRITE_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n5. REMOVE GITLAB\n============================================================\n\nOnly after:\n\nBACKUP_CREATED=YES\nBACKUP_HASH_MANIFEST=PASS\nDNS_WRITE_GATE=PASS\n\nGracefully stop GitLab.\n\nDisable its services.\n\nRemove GitLab packages using the installed distribution's native package\nmanager.\n\nRemove obsolete GitLab runtime/service configuration only after package\nremoval.\n\nDo NOT blindly rm -rf unknown directories.\n\nFor each remaining GitLab path:\n\nclassify before deletion as:\n\nCONFIG\nDATA\nLOG\nCACHE\nBACKUP\nUNKNOWN\n\nNever delete the verified recovery backup.\n\nRemove obsolete local GitLab listeners.\n\n============================================================\n6. CADDY CLEANUP\n============================================================\n\nRemove ONLY the obsolete Caddy vhost for:\n\ngit.worm.estixari.com\n\nIf git.coffee.pm currently points to retired GitLab:\n\nremove/disable only its obsolete GitLab reverse_proxy mapping while\npreserving the hostname for future configuration.\n\nDo not redirect git.coffee.pm somewhere else automatically.\n\nValidate:\n\ncaddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile\n\nThen reload ONLY Caddy if configuration changed.\n\n============================================================\n7. DNS REMOVE\n============================================================\n\nDelete authoritative DNS records for:\n\ngit.worm.estixari.com\n\nVerify:\n\ndig +short A git.worm.estixari.com\ndig +short AAAA git.worm.estixari.com\ndig +short CNAME git.worm.estixari.com\n\nExpected after authoritative propagation:\n\nNO RECORD\n\nPreserve:\n\ngit.coffee.pm\n\n============================================================\n8. VERIFY SERVER\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nGITLAB_INSTALLED=NO\nGITLAB_RUNNING=NO\nGITLAB_LISTENER_PRESENT=NO\n\nVerify no remaining unexpected GitLab listeners.\n\nVerify:\n\ngitlab-ctl no longer active/installed as appropriate.\n\nCheck disk usage recovered:\n\nDISK_BEFORE=\nDISK_AFTER=\nDISK_RECLAIMED=\n\n============================================================\n9. PRESERVE GIT CLIENT DATA\n============================================================\n\nDo NOT rewrite existing /opt/worm Git remotes automatically.\n\nAudit them and report any remote still referencing:\n\ngit.worm.estixari.com\n\nReturn:\n\nSTALE_GIT_REMOTES=\n\nThese will be migrated separately.\n\n============================================================\n10. FINAL\n============================================================\n\nGITLAB_BACKUP_CREATED=\nGITLAB_BACKUP_HASH_MANIFEST=\nGITLAB_BACKUP_PATH=\n\nGITLAB_REMOVAL_GATE=\n\nGITLAB_INSTALLED=\nGITLAB_RUNNING=\nGITLAB_LISTENER_PRESENT=\n\nGIT_WORM_DNS_REMOVED=\nGIT_WORM_A=\nGIT_WORM_AAAA=\nGIT_WORM_CNAME=\n\nGIT_COFFEE_PRESERVED=YES\n\nGIT_WORM_CADDY_REMOVED=\nGIT_COFFEE_UPSTREAM_RETIRE_REQUIRED=\n\nSTALE_GIT_REMOTES=\n\nDISK_RECLAIMED=\n\nDASHBOARD_CHANGED=NO\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHEADSCALE_CHANGED=NO\nWG_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE=\n\nWrite report:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/GITLAB-RETIREMENT.md"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1190:{"session_id":"01a08a57-750a-7b02-93df-b0700dbe6831","ts":1789027385,"text":"LEVEL PRO — RETIRE ALL WEB, PRESERVE SMTP ONLY\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> BACKUP -> MINIMAL REMOVAL -> VERIFY\n\nAUTHORIZED_DESTRUCTIVE_CHANGE=YES\n\nTARGET STATE:\n\nSERVER_ROLE=SMTP_ONLY\n\nREMOVE/RETIRE:\n- Caddy\n- all HTTP/HTTPS vhosts\n- Worm dashboard web service\n- GitLab and GitLab Web\n- web reverse proxies\n- web dashboards/UIs\n- web-only monitoring endpoints\n- HTTP/HTTPS public listeners\n- obsolete web DNS records\n\nPRESERVE:\n- SMTP\n- Postfix\n- OpenDKIM\n- mail TLS/certificates required by SMTP\n- mail DNS\n- MX\n- SPF\n- DKIM\n- DMARC\n- required SMTP submission/relay services\n\nABSOLUTE FREEZE:\n\nDO NOT modify OPNsense.\nDO NOT modify Headscale/Tailscale.\nDO NOT modify WireGuard.\nDO NOT modify Hetzner networking.\nDO NOT modify private VLAN.\nDO NOT change public IP addressing.\nDO NOT delete mail certificates/keys.\nDO NOT delete mail queues.\nDO NOT delete mailboxes/mail data.\nDO NOT expose new ports.\n\n============================================================\n1. COMPLETE SERVICE AUDIT\n============================================================\n\nInventory:\n\nsystemctl list-units --type=service --all\nsystemctl list-unit-files\nss -lntup\n\nClassify every relevant listener/service:\n\nSMTP_REQUIRED\nMAIL_REQUIRED\nWEB_ONLY\nSHARED_DEPENDENCY\nUNRELATED\nUNKNOWN\n\nExplicitly audit:\n\npostfix\ndovecot\nopendkim\nrspamd\nspamassassin\nclamav\ncaddy\nnginx\napache\ngitlab\nworm-dashboard\nprometheus\ngrafana\nalertmanager\nexporters\nuvicorn/python web services\n\nDo NOT remove UNKNOWN or SHARED_DEPENDENCY services.\n\nReturn:\n\nSMTP_SERVICES=\nMAIL_DEPENDENCIES=\nWEB_SERVICES=\nSHARED_DEPENDENCIES=\nUNKNOWN_SERVICES=\n\n============================================================\n2. SMTP BASELINE GATE\n============================================================\n\nBefore removing anything, prove current mail configuration.\n\nDetermine without printing secrets:\n\nSMTP_HOSTNAME=\nSMTP_LISTEN_ADDRESSES=\nSMTP_PORTS=\n\nAudit expected mail ports actually in use, such as:\n\n25\n465\n587\n\nDo not enable a port merely because it is listed here.\n\nDetermine:\n\nPOSTFIX_RUNNING=\nDOVECOT_REQUIRED=\nOPENDKIM_RUNNING=\nMAIL_TLS_PRESENT=\nMAIL_QUEUE_STATE=\n\nAudit DNS read-only:\n\nMX\nSPF\nDKIM\nDMARC\n\nRequired:\n\nSMTP_BASELINE_GATE=PASS\n\nIf SMTP dependency ownership is ambiguous:\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n3. BACKUP\n============================================================\n\nCreate protected backup of configuration/data necessary for recovery of\ncomponents being retired.\n\nFor GitLab specifically:\n\ninventory repositories first.\n\nIf repositories contain data without another verified copy, preserve them\nin backup before removal.\n\nCreate SHA256 manifest.\n\nRequired:\n\nRETIREMENT_BACKUP_CREATED=YES\nBACKUP_HASH_MANIFEST=PASS\n\nNever place SMTP private keys/secrets into reports.\n\n============================================================\n4. WEB DNS AUDIT\n============================================================\n\nAudit existing DNS records for:\n\nworm.estixari.com\nworm.coffee.pm\ngit.worm.estixari.com\ngit.coffee.pm\n\nand discover any other WEB-only hostnames.\n\nClassify every record:\n\nWEB_ONLY\nMAIL_REQUIRED\nSHARED\nUNKNOWN\n\nNEVER remove:\n\nMX records\nmail host A/AAAA required by MX\nSPF TXT\nDKIM TXT\nDMARC TXT\nSMTP-related PTR dependencies\n\nPrepare:\n\nWEB_DNS_RECORDS_TO_REMOVE=\n\n============================================================\n5. RETIRE APPLICATION WEB SERVICES\n============================================================\n\nStop and disable only confirmed WEB_ONLY services.\n\nTarget retirement includes, where confirmed:\n\nworm-dashboard.service\nCaddy\nGitLab Web/GitLab installation\nother dedicated web-only application services\n\nFor GitLab:\n\nuse native shutdown/package removal.\n\nDo NOT blindly rm -rf application/data directories.\n\nPreserve verified backups.\n\n============================================================\n6. CADDY / HTTP RETIREMENT\n============================================================\n\nRemove/disable all Caddy web serving.\n\nTarget:\n\nPUBLIC_HTTP_80=NO\nPUBLIC_HTTPS_443=NO\n\nDisable Caddy after confirming no SMTP/mail dependency uses it.\n\nCADDY_RUNNING=NO\n\nDo not delete certificates required by SMTP.\n\n============================================================\n7. WEB MONITORING RETIREMENT\n============================================================\n\nFor Prometheus/Grafana/Alertmanager/exporters:\n\ndetermine whether they are required for SMTP monitoring.\n\nIf WEB_ONLY:\nretire.\n\nIf required internally for SMTP operations:\nkeep loopback/private only.\n\nDo NOT expose their HTTP interfaces publicly.\n\n============================================================\n8. DNS MINIMAL REMOVAL\n============================================================\n\nUsing ONLY existing authorized DNS management:\n\nremove confirmed WEB_ONLY records.\n\nExpected candidates, only if confirmed web-only:\n\nworm.estixari.com\nworm.coffee.pm\ngit.worm.estixari.com\ngit.coffee.pm\n\nDo not remove a hostname if it is required by SMTP/mail.\n\nPreserve all mail DNS.\n\nIf DNS write access is unavailable:\n\nreport DNS_WEB_CLEANUP_PENDING=YES\n\nbut continue only with local web retirement where safe.\n\n============================================================\n9. PACKAGE / FILE CLEANUP\n============================================================\n\nRemove packages belonging exclusively to retired web applications where\ndependency analysis proves they are not required by SMTP.\n\nClean obsolete:\n\nweb configs\nweb service units\nweb caches\nweb application trees\n\nDo NOT delete:\n\nmail config\nmail queues\nmailboxes\nDKIM keys\nSMTP TLS keys/certificates\nmail logs needed operationally\nshared system dependencies\n\nFor every destructive directory removal:\n\nCLASSIFY_FIRST=MANDATORY\n\n============================================================\n10. LISTENER VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nAfter retirement run:\n\nss -lntup\n\nRequired:\n\nTCP_80_LISTENER=NO\nTCP_443_LISTENER=NO\nPUBLIC_WEB_LISTENERS=NONE\n\nSMTP listeners must remain according to the pre-change baseline.\n\nReturn:\n\nSMTP_LISTENERS_AFTER=\n\nCompare before/after.\n\nRequired:\n\nSMTP_LISTENER_REGRESSION=NO\n\n============================================================\n11. SMTP FUNCTIONAL VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nVerify locally without sending spam or exposing credentials:\n\nPostfix configuration syntax\nOpenDKIM status/config where applicable\nTLS configuration presence\nmail queue accessibility\nSMTP banner/listener\n\nPerform a safe SMTP protocol connection test locally.\n\nDo not send external mail unless an existing test mechanism is explicitly\nconfigured for that purpose.\n\nRequired:\n\nPOSTFIX_RUNNING_AFTER=YES\nOPENDKIM_RUNNING_AFTER=YES if previously required\nSMTP_LOCAL_TEST=PASS\nSMTP_TLS_GATE=PASS\nMAIL_DNS_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n12. SECURITY VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nRequired final architecture:\n\nPUBLIC_IP_SERVICE -> SMTP/mail only as required\n\nPUBLIC_IP_WEB -> NO WEB SERVICE\n\nNo:\n\nHTTP\nHTTPS\nCaddy\ndashboard\nGitLab Web\npublic monitoring UI\n\nReturn:\n\nWEB_PLANE_RETIRED=PASS\nSMTP_PRESERVED=PASS\n\n============================================================\n13. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WEB-RETIREMENT-SMTP-ONLY.md\n\nFinal:\n\nSERVER_ROLE=SMTP_ONLY\n\nPOSTFIX_RUNNING=\nOPENDKIM_RUNNING=\nDOVECOT_RUNNING=\nSMTP_PORTS=\n\nSMTP_BASELINE_GATE=\nSMTP_LOCAL_TEST=\nSMTP_TLS_GATE=\nMAIL_DNS_GATE=\n\nCADDY_RUNNING=\nDASHBOARD_RUNNING=\nGITLAB_RUNNING=\n\nTCP_80_LISTENER=\nTCP_443_LISTENER=\nPUBLIC_WEB_LISTENERS=\n\nWEB_DNS_RECORDS_REMOVED=\nMAIL_DNS_PRESERVED=\n\nRETIREMENT_BACKUP_CREATED=\nBACKUP_HASH_MANIFEST=\n\nSMTP_LISTENER_REGRESSION=\n\nWEB_PLANE_RETIRED=\nSMTP_PRESERVED=\n\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHEADSCALE_CHANGED=NO\nWG_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_NETWORK_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
