ion.\n\nDetermine without printing secrets:\n\nSMTP_HOSTNAME=\nSMTP_LISTEN_ADDRESSES=\nSMTP_PORTS=\n\nAudit expected mail ports actually in use, such as:\n\n25\n465\n587\n\nDo not enable a port merely because it is listed here.\n\nDetermine:\n\nPOSTFIX_RUNNING=\nDOVECOT_REQUIRED=\nOPENDKIM_RUNNING=\nMAIL_TLS_PRESENT=\nMAIL_QUEUE_STATE=\n\nAudit DNS read-only:\n\nMX\nSPF\nDKIM\nDMARC\n\nRequired:\n\nSMTP_BASELINE_GATE=PASS\n\nIf SMTP dependency ownership is ambiguous:\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n3. BACKUP\n============================================================\n\nCreate protected backup of configuration/data necessary for recovery of\ncomponents being retired.\n\nFor GitLab specifically:\n\ninventory repositories first.\n\nIf repositories contain data without another verified copy, preserve them\nin backup before removal.\n\nCreate SHA256 manifest.\n\nRequired:\n\nRETIREMENT_BACKUP_CREATED=YES\nBACKUP_HASH_MANIFEST=PASS\n\nNever place SMTP private keys/secrets into reports.\n\n============================================================\n4. WEB DNS AUDIT\n============================================================\n\nAudit existing DNS records for:\n\nworm.estixari.com\nworm.coffee.pm\ngit.worm.estixari.com\ngit.coffee.pm\n\nand discover any other WEB-only hostnames.\n\nClassify every record:\n\nWEB_ONLY\nMAIL_REQUIRED\nSHARED\nUNKNOWN\n\nNEVER remove:\n\nMX records\nmail host A/AAAA required by MX\nSPF TXT\nDKIM TXT\nDMARC TXT\nSMTP-related PTR dependencies\n\nPrepare:\n\nWEB_DNS_RECORDS_TO_REMOVE=\n\n============================================================\n5. RETIRE APPLICATION WEB SERVICES\n============================================================\n\nStop and disable only confirmed WEB_ONLY services.\n\nTarget retirement includes, where confirmed:\n\nworm-dashboard.service\nCaddy\nGitLab Web/GitLab installation\nother dedicated web-only application services\n\nFor GitLab:\n\nuse native shutdown/package removal.\n\nDo NOT blindly rm -rf application/data directories.\n\nPreserve verified backups.\n\n============================================================\n6. CADDY / HTTP RETIREMENT\n============================================================\n\nRemove/disable all Caddy web serving.\n\nTarget:\n\nPUBLIC_HTTP_80=NO\nPUBLIC_HTTPS_443=NO\n\nDisable Caddy after confirming no SMTP/mail dependency uses it.\n\nCADDY_RUNNING=NO\n\nDo not delete certificates required by SMTP.\n\n============================================================\n7. WEB MONITORING RETIREMENT\n============================================================\n\nFor Prometheus/Grafana/Alertmanager/exporters:\n\ndetermine whether they are required for SMTP monitoring.\n\nIf WEB_ONLY:\nretire.\n\nIf required internally for SMTP operations:\nkeep loopback/private only.\n\nDo NOT expose their HTTP interfaces publicly.\n\n============================================================\n8. DNS MINIMAL REMOVAL\n============================================================\n\nUsing ONLY existing authorized DNS management:\n\nremove confirmed WEB_ONLY records.\n\nExpected candidates, only if confirmed web-only:\n\nworm.estixari.com\nworm.coffee.pm\ngit.worm.estixari.com\ngit.coffee.pm\n\nDo not remove a hostname if it is required by SMTP/mail.\n\nPreserve all mail DNS.\n\nIf DNS write access is unavailable:\n\nreport DNS_WEB_CLEANUP_PENDING=YES\n\nbut continue only with local web retirement where safe.\n\n============================================================\n9. PACKAGE / FILE CLEANUP\n============================================================\n\nRemove packages belonging exclusively to retired web applications where\ndependency analysis proves they are not required by SMTP.\n\nClean obsolete:\n\nweb configs\nweb service units\nweb caches\nweb application trees\n\nDo NOT delete:\n\nmail config\nmail queues\nmailboxes\nDKIM keys\nSMTP TLS keys/certificates\nmail logs needed operationally\nshared system dependencies\n\nFor every destructive directory removal:\n\nCLASSIFY_FIRST=MANDATORY\n\n============================================================\n10. LISTENER VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nAfter retirement run:\n\nss -lntup\n\nRequired:\n\nTCP_80_LISTENER=NO\nTCP_443_LISTENER=NO\nPUBLIC_WEB_LISTENERS=NONE\n\nSMTP listeners must remain according to the pre-change baseline.\n\nReturn:\n\nSMTP_LISTENERS_AFTER=\n\nCompare before/after.\n\nRequired:\n\nSMTP_LISTENER_REGRESSION=NO\n\n============================================================\n11. SMTP FUNCTIONAL VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nVerify locally without sending spam or exposing credentials:\n\nPostfix configuration syntax\nOpenDKIM status/config where applicable\nTLS configuration presence\nmail queue accessibility\nSMTP banner/listener\n\nPerform a safe SMTP protocol connection test locally.\n\nDo not send external mail unless an existing test mechanism is explicitly\nconfigured for that purpose.\n\nRequired:\n\nPOSTFIX_RUNNING_AFTER=YES\nOPENDKIM_RUNNING_AFTER=YES if previously required\nSMTP_LOCAL_TEST=PASS\nSMTP_TLS_GATE=PASS\nMAIL_DNS_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n12. SECURITY VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nRequired final architecture:\n\nPUBLIC_IP_SERVICE -> SMTP/mail only as required\n\nPUBLIC_IP_WEB -> NO WEB SERVICE\n\nNo:\n\nHTTP\nHTTPS\nCaddy\ndashboard\nGitLab Web\npublic monitoring UI\n\nReturn:\n\nWEB_PLANE_RETIRED=PASS\nSMTP_PRESERVED=PASS\n\n============================================================\n13. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WEB-RETIREMENT-SMTP-ONLY.md\n\nFinal:\n\nSERVER_ROLE=SMTP_ONLY\n\nPOSTFIX_RUNNING=\nOPENDKIM_RUNNING=\nDOVECOT_RUNNING=\nSMTP_PORTS=\n\nSMTP_BASELINE_GATE=\nSMTP_LOCAL_TEST=\nSMTP_TLS_GATE=\nMAIL_DNS_GATE=\n\nCADDY_RUNNING=\nDASHBOARD_RUNNING=\nGITLAB_RUNNING=\n\nTCP_80_LISTENER=\nTCP_443_LISTENER=\nPUBLIC_WEB_LISTENERS=\n\nWEB_DNS_RECORDS_REMOVED=\nMAIL_DNS_PRESERVED=\n\nRETIREMENT_BACKUP_CREATED=\nBACKUP_HASH_MANIFEST=\n\nSMTP_LISTENER_REGRESSION=\n\nWEB_PLANE_RETIRED=\nSMTP_PRESERVED=\n\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHEADSCALE_CHANGED=NO\nWG_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_NETWORK_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1192:{"session_id":"01a08a5a-dfec-7512-a7e0-91c36caf66be","ts":1789033241,"text":"LEVEL PRO — REMOVE HEADSCALE + TAILSCALE\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> BACKUP -> MINIMAL REMOVAL -> VERIFY\n\nROOT=/opt/worm\n\nAUTHORIZED_DESTRUCTIVE_CHANGE=YES\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nCompletely retire:\n\n- Headscale\n- Tailscale\n- tailscaled\n- tailscale0\n- Headscale subnet routes\n- Headscale/Tailscale service units\n- Headscale/Tailscale-specific firewall rules\n- Headscale/Tailscale-specific configuration/state\n\nPRESERVE:\n\n- SMTP/mail services\n- OPNsense\n- Hetzner networking\n- wg0 admin WireGuard\n- wg-worm\n- FireHOL except Headscale/Tailscale-specific rules\n- Antani public/private interfaces\n- /opt/worm\n- WormOS build/source\n- Git data/backups not related to Headscale\n\nABSOLUTE RULES:\n\nDO NOT modify OPNsense.\nDO NOT reboot OPNsense.\nDO NOT modify Hetzner networks/IP assignments.\nDO NOT modify wg0.\nDO NOT modify wg-worm.\nDO NOT change default route unless removing a route owned exclusively by Tailscale.\nDO NOT flush nftables.\nDO NOT disable FireHOL.\nDO NOT remove shared packages without dependency proof.\nDO NOT print auth keys/tokens/secrets.\n\n============================================================\n1. ACCESS SAFETY AUDIT\n============================================================\n\nBefore removal determine whether the CURRENT Codex/SSH/admin session depends\non Tailscale/Headscale.\n\nCollect:\n\nwho\nss -tnp\nip route get <current_admin_source_if_known>\n\nDetermine:\n\nCURRENT_SESSION_VIA_TAILSCALE=YES|NO|UNKNOWN\nTAILSCALE_REMOVAL_WILL_DROP_ADMIN_ACCESS=YES|NO|UNKNOWN\n\nIf YES or UNKNOWN:\n\nSTOP before removal.\n\nDo not cut the active administrative path.\n\n============================================================\n2. INVENTORY\n============================================================\n\nAudit:\n\nsystemctl status tailscaled --no-pager\nsystemctl status headscale --no-pager\n\nsystemctl list-unit-files | grep -Ei 'tailscale|headscale'\nsystemctl list-units --all | grep -Ei 'tailscale|headscale'\n\ntailscale status\ntailscale ip\n\nip -br addr\nip route show table all\nip rule show\n\nss -lntup\n\nFind:\n\nTAILSCALE_INSTALLED=\nTAILSCALED_RUNNING=\nTAILSCALE_INTERFACE=\nTAILSCALE_IPS=\n\nHEADSCALE_INSTALLED=\nHEADSCALE_RUNNING=\nHEADSCALE_LISTENERS=\n\nHEADSCALE_CONFIG_PATHS=\nHEADSCALE_DATA_PATHS=\nTAILSCALE_STATE_PATHS=\n\n============================================================\n3. ROUTE OWNERSHIP\n============================================================\n\nIdentify all routes/rules owned exclusively by Tailscale/Headscale.\n\nEspecially audit:\n\n10.90.20.0/24 advertisement\ntable 52 or other Tailscale policy tables\ntailscale0 routes\nsubnet-router state\nexit-node state\n\nReport:\n\nTAILSCALE_OWNED_ROUTES=\nTAILSCALE_OWNED_RULES=\n\nRequired:\n\nNON_TAILSCALE_ROUTES_IDENTIFIED=PASS\n\nDo not remove:\n\n10.90.20.0/24 private transport route if owned by normal Antani networking\n10.90.0.0/16\n10.77.0.0/24 wg0\n2.28.34.27/32 protected OPNsense endpoint\ndefault route\n\n============================================================\n4. FIREWALL OWNERSHIP\n============================================================\n\nAudit FireHOL/nftables for rules referencing:\n\ntailscale0\n100.64.0.0/10\nHeadscale-specific paths\n10.90.20.0/24 rules created solely for Tailscale forwarding\n\nClassify:\n\nTAILSCALE_FIREWALL_RULES=\nSHARED_FIREWALL_RULES=\nUNKNOWN_FIREWALL_RULES=\n\nUNKNOWN => STOP before firewall cleanup.\n\n============================================================\n5. BACKUP\n============================================================\n\nBefore deleting persistent state, create a recovery backup of:\n\nHeadscale config\nHeadscale database/state\nTailscale config/state metadata\nrelevant service unit/drop-ins\nrelevant FireHOL configuration\n\nDo NOT put auth keys/tokens into the report.\n\nStore backup outside directories being removed.\n\nCreate SHA256 manifest.\n\nRequired:\n\nBACKUP_CREATED=YES\nBACKUP_HASH_MANIFEST=PASS\n\n============================================================\n6. PRE-REMOVAL GATE\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nCURRENT_SESSION_VIA_TAILSCALE=NO\nTAILSCALE_REMOVAL_WILL_DROP_ADMIN_ACCESS=NO\n\nBACKUP_CREATED=YES\nBACKUP_HASH_MANIFEST=PASS\n\nWG0_PRESERVATION_GATE=PASS\nWG_WORM_PRESERVATION_GATE=PASS\nSMTP_PRESERVATION_GATE=PASS\n\nThen:\n\nHEADSCALE_TAILSCALE_REMOVAL_GATE=PASS\n\nOtherwise STOP.\n\n============================================================\n7. STOP SERVICES\n============================================================\n\nOnly if removal gate PASS:\n\nstop and disable:\n\ntailscaled\nheadscale\n\nand only other units proven to belong exclusively to them.\n\nDo not stop networking.\n\nDo not restart FireHOL yet.\n\n============================================================\n8. REMOVE TAILSCALE RUNTIME STATE\n============================================================\n\nRemove only Tailscale-owned runtime networking:\n\ntailscale0\nTailscale policy rules\nTailscale routes\nsubnet advertisement state\n\nUse supported Tailscale shutdown/logout mechanism where applicable.\n\nDo NOT remove unrelated Linux routes.\n\nRequired after:\n\nTAILSCALE_INTERFACE_PRESENT=NO\nTAILSCALE_POLICY_ROUTES_PRESENT=NO\n\n============================================================\n9. REMOVE PACKAGES\n============================================================\n\nUse native package manager to remove:\n\ntailscale\nheadscale\n\nonly if package ownership is confirmed.\n\nDo not autoremove shared dependencies blindly.\n\nReport:\n\nTAILSCALE_PACKAGE_REMOVED=\nHEADSCALE_PACKAGE_REMOVED=\n\n============================================================\n10. REMOVE PERSISTENT CONFIG/STATE\n============================================================\n\nAfter package/service removal classify remaining paths before deletion.\n\nRemove confirmed Headscale/Tailscale-only:\n\nconfig\ndatabase/state\nruntime cache\nservice drop-ins\n\nDo not delete the recovery backup.\n\nDo not delete generic TLS/mail certs shared with SMTP.\n\n============================================================\n11. FIREHOL CLEANUP\n============================================================\n\nRemove only rules/includes created exclusively for Headscale/Tailscale.\n\nPreserve:\n\nWORM fail-closed policy\nwg0 policy\nwg-worm policy\nSMTP policy\nnormal Antani private/public policy\n\nValidate FireHOL configuration before reload.\n\nRequired:\n\nFIREHOL_CONFIG_VALID=PASS\n\nReload FireHOL only if its config changed.\n\n============================================================\n12. VERIFY CORE NETWORK\n============================================================\n\nVerify unchanged:\n\nANTANI_PUBLIC_INTERFACE=\nANTANI_PUBLIC_IP=\n\nANTANI_PRIVATE_INTERFACE=\nANTANI_PRIVATE_IP=10.90.20.10/24\n\nDEFAULT_ROUTE=\nOPNSENSE_ENDPOINT_ROUTE=\n\nwg0:\nPRESENT\nUNCHANGED\n\nwg-worm:\nstate/config unchanged\n\nRequired:\n\nWG0_PRESERVED=PASS\nWG_WORM_PRESERVED=PASS\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_PRESERVED=PASS\nPRIVATE_NETWORK_PRESERVED=PASS\n\n============================================================\n13. SMTP VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nVerify mail services remain healthy.\n\nAt minimum:\n\npostfix status\nopendkim status if required\nSMTP listeners\n\nRequired:\n\nSMTP_PRESERVED=PASS\n\nDo not send external test mail unless already approved.\n\n============================================================\n14. FINAL HEADSCALE/TAILSCALE CHECK\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nHEADSCALE_RUNNING=NO\nTAILSCALED_RUNNING=NO\n\nTAILSCALE_INTERFACE_PRESENT=NO\n\nHEADSCALE_LISTENERS=NONE\nTAILSCALE_LISTENERS=NONE\n\nHEADSCALE_SERVICE_ENABLED=NO\nTAILSCALE_SERVICE_ENABLED=NO\n\nHEADSCALE_TAILSCALE_RETIRED=PASS\n\n============================================================\n15. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/HEADSCALE-TAILSCALE-RETIREMENT.md\n\nFinal:\n\nCURRENT_SESSION_VIA_TAILSCALE=\nTAILSCALE_REMOVAL_WILL_DROP_ADMIN_ACCESS=\n\nBACKUP_CREATED=\nBACKUP_HASH_MANIFEST=\n\nHEADSCALE_PACKAGE_REMOVED=\nTAILSCALE_PACKAGE_REMOVED=\n\nHEADSCALE_RUNNING=\nTAILSCALED_RUNNING=\nTAILSCALE_INTERFACE_PRESENT=\n\nHEADSCALE_LISTENERS=\nTAILSCALE_LISTENERS=\n\nWG0_PRESERVED=\nWG_WORM_PRESERVED=\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_PRESERVED=\nPRIVATE_NETWORK_PRESERVED=\n\nSMTP_PRESERVED=\nFIREHOL_CONFIG_VALID=\n\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_NETWORK_CHANGED=NO\n\nHEADSCALE_TAILSCALE_RETIRED=\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1193:{"session_id":"01a08abd-a56a-7773-9aa9-ff51183b9712","ts":1789034084,"text":"LEVEL PRO — HETZNER PRIVATE NETWORK / OPNSENSE ROUTER DESIGN\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> MINIMAL CHANGE -> VERIFY\n\nMODE:\nAUDIT + PLAN ONLY\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nBuild the authoritative Hetzner-supported private routing architecture\nbetween:\n\nOPNsense Cloud VPS\nHetzner Cloud Network\nRobot vSwitch\nAntani dedicated server\n\nOPNsense must be the router/gateway for WORM traffic.\n\nDo NOT assume that OPNsense and Antani are directly attached to the same\nLayer-2 subnet.\n\nABSOLUTE RULES:\n\nDO NOT modify OPNsense.\nDO NOT modify Hetzner resources.\nDO NOT modify Antani networking.\nDO NOT modify routes.\nDO NOT modify VLAN.\nDO NOT modify firewall.\nDO NOT reboot anything.\nDO NOT print Hetzner API credentials.\n\n============================================================\n1. HETZNER AUTHORITATIVE INVENTORY\n============================================================\n\nUsing existing authorized Hetzner API access, inventory:\n\nCloud Networks\nCloud Network subnets\nCloud Network routes\nattached Cloud Servers\nvSwitch-connected subnets\nroute exposure to vSwitch\n\nIdentify:\n\nOPNSENSE_SERVER_ID=\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_NETWORK=\nOPNSENSE_ASSIGNED_PRIVATE_IP=\n\nNETWORK_CIDR=\nCLOUD_SUBNET_CIDR=\nCLOUD_SUBNET_GATEWAY=\n\nVSWITCH_SUBNET_CIDR=\nVSWITCH_GATEWAY=\nVSWITCH_ID=\nVSWITCH_VLAN_ID=\n\nEXPOSE_ROUTES_TO_VSWITCH=\n\nDo not infer values from old /opt/worm configuration.\n\n============================================================\n2. ANTANI / ROBOT AUDIT\n============================================================\n\nRead only:\n\nip -br link\nip -br addr\nip route\nip rule\nip neigh\n\nDetermine:\n\nANTANI_PUBLIC_INTERFACE=\nANTANI_VSWITCH_INTERFACE=\nANTANI_VSWITCH_VLAN_ID=\nANTANI_PRIVATE_IP=\nANTANI_PRIVATE_PREFIX=\nANTANI_PRIVATE_MTU=\n\nExpected VLAN from historical configuration may be:\n\n4000\n\nbut verify rather than assume.\n\n============================================================\n3. VALIDATE HETZNER MODEL\n============================================================\n\nRequired architecture:\n\nANTANI\n  ->\nvSwitch VLAN\n  ->\nvSwitch Gateway\n  ->\nHetzner Cloud Network Gateway\n  ->\nOPNsense private Cloud IP\n\nDo not require direct ARP between Antani and OPNsense when they are on\ndifferent Hetzner subnet types.\n\nReport:\n\nPRIVATE_NETWORK_MODEL=\nDIRECT_L2_EXPECTED=YES|NO\nHETZNER_GATEWAY_REQUIRED=YES|NO\n\n============================================================\n4. OPNsense ROUTER ROLE\n============================================================\n\nDesign OPNsense as:\n\nOPNSENSE_ROLE=PRIVATE_NETWORK_ROUTER\n\nDetermine its actual Hetzner-assigned private IP.\n\nDo NOT force:\n\n10.90.20.1\n\nunless Hetzner API proves that this is the assigned Cloud Network IP.\n\nHetzner Cloud Network interface configuration should use the actual\nprovider-assigned address/gateway model.\n\nReport:\n\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_IP_AUTHORITATIVE=\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_GATEWAY=\n\n============================================================\n5. PRIVATE ADDRESS PLAN\n============================================================\n\nCompare current desired Worm addressing against Hetzner-assigned\naddressing.\n\nCurrent Worm intent:\n\nANTANI_PRIVATE=10.90.20.10\nWORM_WG=10.90.30.0/24\n\nDetermine whether:\n\n10.90.20.0/24\n\nbelongs to:\n\nCLOUD_SUBNET\nVSWITCH_SUBNET\nNEITHER\n\nDo not use one subnet for two incompatible Hetzner subnet roles.\n\nReturn:\n\nADDRESS_PLAN_COMPATIBLE=\nADDRESS_PLAN_CONFLICTS=\n\n============================================================\n6. ROUTING THROUGH OPNsense\n============================================================\n\nDesign the required Hetzner Network route so private clients can use\nOPNsense as router.\n\nFor Internet/full-tunnel design evaluate:\n\nDestination:\n0.0.0.0/0\n\nGateway:\nOPNsense private Cloud IP\n\nDo NOT create the route.\n\nHetzner requires a Cloud Server to be the gateway for Cloud Network\nroutes.\n\nRequired:\n\nOPNSENSE_CAN_BE_HETZNER_GATEWAY=YES\n\nAlso determine whether:\n\nEXPOSE_ROUTES_TO_VSWITCH=YES\n\nis required so Antani receives the intended routed topology.\n\n============================================================\n7. ANTANI ROUTING PLAN\n============================================================\n\nDetermine exact future route required on Antani.\n\nDo not blindly set:\n\ndefault via OPNsense\n\nInstead derive:\n\nVSWITCH_GATEWAY=\nCLOUD_NETWORK_ROUTE=\n\nfrom authoritative Hetzner configuration.\n\nPreserve the public route needed to reach the OPNsense WireGuard endpoint\nbefore any future default-route change.\n\n============================================================\n8. MTU\n============================================================\n\nHetzner Cloud private networking commonly uses a lower MTU than the public\nnetwork.\n\nDetermine actual:\n\nCLOUD_PRIVATE_MTU=\nANTANI_VSWITCH_MTU=\n\nCompare with WireGuard overhead.\n\nReturn:\n\nWG_SAFE_MTU=\n\nDo not change MTU yet.\n\n============================================================\n9. WIREGUARD OVERLAY\n============================================================\n\nKeep WORM overlay separate:\n\nWORM_WG_SUBNET=10.90.30.0/24\n\nOPNsense WG=10.90.30.1\nAntani WG=10.90.30.2\nWormOS=10.90.30.3\n\nVerify:\n\nWG_OVERLAPS_HETZNER_PRIVATE_NETWORK=NO\n\nWireGuard is an overlay above the Hetzner transport network, not a\nreplacement for correct Hetzner private routing.\n\n============================================================\n10. AUTHORITATIVE DIAGRAM\n============================================================\n\nGenerate:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/HETZNER-OPNSENSE-PRIVATE-NETWORK-DESIGN.md\n\nInclude:\n\nInternet\n  |\nOPNsense WAN\n  |\nOPNsense private Cloud IP\n  |\nHetzner Cloud Network Gateway\n  |\nvSwitch Gateway\n  |\nVLAN 4000\n  |\nAntani private IP\n  |\nRobot\n\nand separately:\n\nWormOS/Antani\n  |\nWireGuard 10.90.30.0/24\n  |\nOPNsense\n  |\nInternet/private services\n\n============================================================\n11. GATE\n============================================================\n\nReturn:\n\nHETZNER_NETWORK_DISCOVERY_GATE=\nVSWITCH_DISCOVERY_GATE=\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_IP_GATE=\nADDRESS_PLAN_GATE=\nROUTING_DESIGN_GATE=\nMTU_DESIGN_GATE=\n\nThen:\n\nHETZNER_OPNSENSE_ARCHITECTURE_GATE=\n\nNo configuration changes.\n\n============================================================\nFINAL\n============================================================\n\nNETWORK_CIDR=\nCLOUD_SUBNET_CIDR=\nCLOUD_SUBNET_GATEWAY=\n\nVSWITCH_SUBNET_CIDR=\nVSWITCH_GATEWAY=\nVSWITCH_VLAN_ID=\n\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_IP_AUTHORITATIVE=\nANTANI_PRIVATE_IP_AUTHORITATIVE=\n\nEXPOSE_ROUTES_TO_VSWITCH=\n\nOPNSENSE_CAN_BE_HETZNER_GATEWAY=\n\nWORM_WG_SUBNET=\nWG_OVERLAPS_HETZNER_PRIVATE_NETWORK=\nWG_SAFE_MTU=\n\nHETZNER_OPNSENSE_ARCHITECTURE_GATE=\n\nCHANGES_MADE=NONE\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nANTANI_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1194:{"session_id":"01a08abd-a56a-7773-9aa9-ff51183b9712","ts":1789034433,"text":"LEVEL PRO — WORM WG ADDRESS PLAN CORRECTION\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> MINIMAL CHANGE -> VERIFY\n\nAUTHORITATIVE HETZNER STATE:\n\nHETZNER_NETWORK=10.90.0.0/16\n\nCLOUD_SUBNET=10.90.10.0/24\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_IP=10.90.10.1\n\nVSWITCH_SUBNET=10.90.20.0/24\nVSWITCH_GATEWAY=10.90.20.1\nVSWITCH_VLAN=4000\nANTANI_PRIVATE_IP=10.90.20.10\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\n10.90.20.1 IS HETZNER VSWITCH GATEWAY.\nIT IS NOT OPNSENSE.\n\nTARGET WIREGUARD OVERLAY:\n\nWORM_WG_SUBNET=10.91.30.0/24\nOPNSENSE_WG_IP=10.91.30.1\nANTANI_WG_IP=10.91.30.2\nWORMOS_WG_IP=10.91.30.3\n\n============================================================\nABSOLUTE FREEZE\n============================================================\n\nDO NOT modify OPNsense live configuration.\nDO NOT modify Hetzner Network.\nDO NOT modify VLAN 4000.\nDO NOT modify Antani live routes.\nDO NOT start wg-worm.\nDO NOT change wg0 admin WireGuard.\nDO NOT change default route.\n\nThis step corrects authoritative WORM source/config only.\n\n============================================================\n1. AUDIT\n============================================================\n\nSearch active/source WORM configuration for:\n\n10.90.30.0/24\n10.90.30.1\n10.90.30.2\n10.90.30.3\n\nClassify every occurrence:\n\nACTIVE_SOURCE\nGENERATED_CONFIG\nTEST\nDOCUMENTATION\nHISTORICAL_REPORT\nPROVENANCE\n\nDo NOT modify historical reports/provenance.\n\nReturn:\n\nACTIVE_10_90_30_REFERENCES=\nHISTORICAL_10_90_30_REFERENCES=\n\n============================================================\n2. COLLISION GATE\n============================================================\n\nVerify 10.91.30.0/24 against:\n\nip route\nip rule\nall local interfaces\nDocker/Podman networks if present\nwg0\nHetzner 10.90.0.0/16\nknown private networks\n\nRequired:\n\n10_91_30_COLLISION=NO\n10_91_30_OVERLAPS_HETZNER=NO\n\n============================================================\n3. MINIMAL CHANGE\n============================================================\n\nUpdate ONLY active/source WORM definitions:\n\n10.90.30.0/24 -> 10.91.30.0/24\n10.90.30.1    -> 10.91.30.1\n10.90.30.2    -> 10.91.30.2\n10.90.30.3    -> 10.91.30.3\n\nPreserve:\n\nOPNsense private = 10.90.10.1\nAntani private   = 10.90.20.10\nvSwitch gateway  = 10.90.20.1\nVLAN             = 4000\n\nDo not rewrite historical audit reports.\n\n============================================================\n4. ROUTING MODEL\n============================================================\n\nUpdate source assumptions so the model is:\n\nAntani 10.90.20.10\n        |\ngateway 10.90.20.1\n        |\nHetzner routed Network\n        |\nOPNsense 10.90.10.1\n\nNOT:\n\nAntani 10.90.20.10\n        |\ndirect L2\n        |\nOPNsense 10.90.20.1\n\nSearch active code/config for stale assumptions that identify\n10.90.20.1 as OPNsense.\n\nRequired:\n\nACTIVE_OPNSENSE_10_90_20_1_REFERENCES=0\n\n============================================================\n5. WIREGUARD MODEL\n============================================================\n\nTarget:\n\nTRANSPORT:\n10.90.0.0/16 Hetzner\n\nOVERLAY:\n10.91.30.0/24 WireGuard\n\nRequired:\n\nWG_OVERLAPS_HETZNER_PRIVATE_NETWORK=NO\n\nWG_SAFE_MTU=1340\n\nUpdate active WORM WireGuard templates/config metadata accordingly.\n\nDo NOT activate WireGuard.\n\n============================================================\n6. VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nADDRESS_PLAN_GATE=PASS\n\nHETZNER_NETWORK=10.90.0.0/16\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_IP=10.90.10.1\nANTANI_PRIVATE_IP=10.90.20.10\nVSWITCH_GATEWAY=10.90.20.1\n\nWORM_WG_SUBNET=10.91.30.0/24\nOPNSENSE_WG_IP=10.91.30.1\nANTANI_WG_IP=10.91.30.2\nWORMOS_WG_IP=10.91.30.3\n\nWG_OVERLAPS_HETZNER_PRIVATE_NETWORK=NO\n\nWG_WORM_STARTED=NO\nLIVE_ROUTES_CHANGED=NO\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_CHANGED=NO\n\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_CHANGED=NO\nANTANI_LIVE_NETWORK_CHANGED=NO\n\n============================================================\n7. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/WORM-WG-ADDRESS-PLAN-10.91.30.md\n\nFinal:\n\nHETZNER_NETWORK=\nCLOUD_SUBNET=\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_IP=\n\nVSWITCH_SUBNET=\nVSWITCH_GATEWAY=\nANTANI_PRIVATE_IP=\n\nOLD_WORM_WG_SUBNET=10.90.30.0/24\nNEW_WORM_WG_SUBNET=10.91.30.0/24\n\nOPNSENSE_WG_IP=\nANTANI_WG_IP=\nWORMOS_WG_IP=\n\nACTIVE_LEGACY_WG_REFERENCES=\nACTIVE_OPNSENSE_10_90_20_1_REFERENCES=\n\nWG_OVERLAPS_HETZNER_PRIVATE_NETWORK=\nADDRESS_PLAN_GATE=\n\nCHANGES_MADE=\nWG_WORM_STARTED=NO\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE=Verify routed Antani 10.90.20.10 -> OPNsense 10.90.10.1 transport"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1196:{"session_id":"01a08abd-a56a-7773-9aa9-ff51183b9712","ts":1789034780,"text":"LEVEL PRO — HETZNER ROUTED TRANSPORT VERIFY\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> NO CHANGE -> VERIFY\n\nAUTHORITATIVE:\n\nHETZNER_NETWORK=10.90.0.0/16\n\nCLOUD_SUBNET=10.90.10.0/24\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_IP=10.90.10.1\n\nVSWITCH_SUBNET=10.90.20.0/24\nVSWITCH_GATEWAY=10.90.20.1\nANTANI_PRIVATE_IP=10.90.20.10\nVLAN_ID=4000\n\nWORM_WG_SUBNET=10.91.30.0/24\n\nABSOLUTE RULE:\n\nREAD ONLY.\n\nDO NOT:\n- modify OPNsense\n- modify Hetzner\n- modify Antani networking\n- modify routes\n- modify firewall\n- start WireGuard\n- change default route\n\n============================================================\n1. ANTANI ROUTE AUDIT\n============================================================\n\nRun:\n\nip -br addr\nip route\nip rule\n\nip route get 10.90.20.1\nip route get 10.90.10.1\n\nReport:\n\nROUTE_TO_VSWITCH_GATEWAY=\nROUTE_TO_OPNSENSE=\nROUTE_TO_OPNSENSE_INTERFACE=\nROUTE_TO_OPNSENSE_SOURCE=\nROUTE_TO_OPNSENSE_GATEWAY=\n\nExpected source:\n\n10.90.20.10\n\n============================================================\n2. VSWITCH GATEWAY VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nVerify:\n\n10.90.20.1\n\nis reachable as the Hetzner vSwitch gateway.\n\nUse read-only:\n\nip neigh\nping where permitted\n\nReport:\n\nVSWITCH_GATEWAY_ROUTE=\nVSWITCH_GATEWAY_NEIGH=\nVSWITCH_GATEWAY_ICMP=\n\nICMP failure alone must not fail the gate.\n\n============================================================\n3. OPNSENSE TRANSPORT VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nTarget:\n\n10.90.10.1\n\nTest route and transport.\n\nUse safe probes:\n\nping if permitted\n\nTCP:\n22\n443\n\nDo NOT authenticate.\n\nReport:\n\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_ICMP=\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_TCP22=\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_TCP443=\n\nA closed management port does NOT automatically mean routing failure.\n\n============================================================\n4. PACKET PATH\n============================================================\n\nUse a safe route/path diagnostic where available.\n\nDetermine whether traffic to:\n\n10.90.10.1\n\nis sent:\n\nAntani\n -> enp9s0.4000\n -> 10.90.20.1\n -> Hetzner routed Network\n -> 10.90.10.1\n\nDo not require direct ARP for 10.90.10.1.\n\nRequired:\n\nDIRECT_ARP_TO_OPNSENSE_EXPECTED=NO\n\n============================================================\n5. SOURCE ADDRESS VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nOPNSENSE_TRANSPORT_SOURCE=10.90.20.10\n\nEnsure traffic is NOT sourced from:\n\n162.55.6.173\n10.77.x.x\n10.91.30.x\n\nReport:\n\nSOURCE_SELECTION_GATE=\n\n============================================================\n6. RETURN-PATH DIAGNOSIS\n============================================================\n\nIf packets leave correctly but no response returns, classify:\n\nANTANI_ROUTE_FAILURE\nVSWITCH_FAILURE\nHETZNER_NETWORK_ROUTE_FAILURE\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_INTERFACE_FAILURE\nOPNSENSE_FIREWALL\nRETURN_ROUTE_FAILURE\nPORT_CLOSED\nUNKNOWN\n\nDo NOT fix anything.\n\nReturn:\n\nTRANSPORT_FAILURE_CLASS=\n\n============================================================\n7. GATE\n============================================================\n\nEvaluate independently:\n\nANTANI_VSWITCH_GATE=\nHETZNER_ROUTED_PATH_GATE=\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_TRANSPORT_GATE=\n\nDo not require WebGUI/SSH to be open for basic routing PASS if other\nevidence proves bidirectional transport.\n\nFinal:\n\nHETZNER_TRANSPORT_GATE=\n\n============================================================\n8. WIREGUARD PRECONDITION\n============================================================\n\nOnly if:\n\nHETZNER_TRANSPORT_GATE=PASS\n\nreturn:\n\nWG_TRANSPORT_PRECONDITION=PASS\n\nOtherwise:\n\nWG_TRANSPORT_PRECONDITION=FAIL\n\nDO NOT start wg-worm.\n\n============================================================\n9. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/HETZNER-ANTANI-OPNSENSE-TRANSPORT.md\n\nFinal:\n\nANTANI_PRIVATE_IP=\nVSWITCH_GATEWAY=\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_IP=\n\nROUTE_TO_OPNSENSE=\nROUTE_TO_OPNSENSE_INTERFACE=\nROUTE_TO_OPNSENSE_SOURCE=\nROUTE_TO_OPNSENSE_GATEWAY=\n\nVSWITCH_GATEWAY_NEIGH=\nVSWITCH_GATEWAY_ICMP=\n\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_ICMP=\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_TCP22=\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_TCP443=\n\nDIRECT_ARP_TO_OPNSENSE_EXPECTED=NO\nSOURCE_SELECTION_GATE=\n\nANTANI_VSWITCH_GATE=\nHETZNER_ROUTED_PATH_GATE=\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_TRANSPORT_GATE=\nHETZNER_TRANSPORT_GATE=\n\nTRANSPORT_FAILURE_CLASS=\n\nWG_TRANSPORT_PRECONDITION=\n\nCHANGES_MADE=NONE\nWG_WORM_STARTED=NO\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_CHANGED=NO\nANTANI_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1197:{"session_id":"01a08abd-a56a-7773-9aa9-ff51183b9712","ts":1789035056,"text":"LEVEL PRO — OPNSENSE PRIVATE TRANSPORT ROOT-CAUSE\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> NO CHANGE\n\nCURRENT VERIFIED:\n\nANTANI_PRIVATE=10.90.20.10\nVSWITCH_GATEWAY=10.90.20.1\nOPNSENSE_EXPECTED_PRIVATE=10.90.10.1\n\nANTANI_ROUTE=PASS\nANTANI_SOURCE_SELECTION=PASS\nANTANI_VSWITCH_GATE=PASS\n\nOPNSENSE_ICMP=NO_REPLY\nOPNSENSE_TCP22=TIMEOUT\nOPNSENSE_TCP443=TIMEOUT\n\nABSOLUTE RULE:\n\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nANTANI_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_CHANGED=NO\nWG_WORM_STARTED=NO\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nDetermine whether failure is:\n\n1. OPNsense private interface/address\n2. missing Hetzner return route\n3. OPNsense firewall\n4. Hetzner Cloud Network/vSwitch routing\n\n============================================================\n1. HETZNER NETWORK ROUTES\n============================================================\n\nUsing existing authorized Hetzner Cloud API read-only access,\ninspect the authoritative Network containing:\n\n10.90.0.0/16\n\nReturn:\n\nNETWORK_ID=\nNETWORK_CIDR=\n\nCLOUD_SUBNET=\nCLOUD_SUBNET_GATEWAY=\n\nVSWITCH_SUBNET=\nVSWITCH_GATEWAY=\n\nROUTES=\n\nEXPOSE_ROUTES_TO_VSWITCH=\n\nDetermine specifically whether routing exists for:\n\n10.90.20.0/24 <-> 10.90.10.0/24\n\nReturn:\n\nHETZNER_INTERSUBNET_ROUTE_GATE=\n\nDo not modify anything.\n\n============================================================\n2. OPNSENSE ATTACHMENT\n\nFrom Hetzner API determine:\n\nOPNSENSE_SERVER_ID=\nOPNSENSE_NETWORK_ATTACHED=\nOPNSENSE_ASSIGNED_PRIVATE_IP=\n\nRequired expected:\n\nOPNSENSE_ASSIGNED_PRIVATE_IP=10.90.10.1\n\nReturn:\n\nOPNSENSE_ATTACHMENT_GATE=\n\n============================================================\n3. RETURN PATH\n\nDetermine authoritative provider route expected for packets:\n\n10.90.10.1 -> 10.90.20.10\n\nReturn:\n\nEXPECTED_RETURN_GATEWAY=\nRETURN_PATH_PROVIDER_GATE=\n\nIf Hetzner Network configuration itself provides inter-subnet\nrouting, state that explicitly.\n\n============================================================\n4. AVAILABLE OPNSENSE EVIDENCE\n\nDo NOT modify OPNsense.\n\nUse only already-authorized/read-only evidence available from:\n\nexisting reports\nprevious config.xml audit\nHetzner metadata\nexisting saved configuration evidence\n\nDetermine:\n\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_INTERFACE=\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_CONFIGURED_IP=\n\nOPNSENSE_ROUTE_TO_10_90_20=\nOPNSENSE_FIREWALL_10_90_20=\n\nMark UNKNOWN where live evidence is unavailable.\n\nDo not infer PASS.\n\n============================================================\n5. CLASSIFY FAILURE\n\nReturn exactly the strongest supported classification:\n\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_IP_MISMATCH\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_INTERFACE_DOWN\nOPNSENSE_RETURN_ROUTE_MISSING\nOPNSENSE_FIREWALL_BLOCK\nHETZNER_NETWORK_ROUTE_MISSING\nHETZNER_VSWITCH_ROUTE_EXPOSURE_MISSING\nPROVIDER_PATH_OK_OPNSENSE_RUNTIME_UNKNOWN\nUNKNOWN\n\nTRANSPORT_FAILURE_CLASS=\n\n============================================================\n6. FINAL\n\nANTANI_VSWITCH_GATE=PASS\n\nHETZNER_NETWORK_GATE=\nOPNSENSE_ATTACHMENT_GATE=\nHETZNER_INTERSUBNET_ROUTE_GATE=\nRETURN_PATH_PROVIDER_GATE=\n\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_CONFIGURED_IP=\nOPNSENSE_ROUTE_TO_10_90_20=\nOPNSENSE_FIREWALL_10_90_20=\n\nTRANSPORT_FAILURE_CLASS=\n\nWG_TRANSPORT_PRECONDITION=FAIL\n\nCHANGES_MADE=NONE\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nANTANI_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_CHANGED=NO\nWG_WORM_STARTED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE=\n\nWrite:\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/OPNSENSE-HETZNER-PRIVATE-ROOT-CAUSE.md"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1198:{"session_id":"01a08abd-a56a-7773-9aa9-ff51183b9712","ts":1789035785,"text":"LEVEL PRO — OPNSENSE WAN WEBGUI RECOVERY DIAGNOSIS\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> NO CHANGE\n\nTARGET:\nOPNSENSE_WAN=2.28.34.27\nWEBGUI=https://2.28.34.27:443\n\nKNOWN HISTORY:\nWAN WebGUI previously worked from approved admin IP.\nOPNsense normal boot previously succeeded.\n\nABSOLUTE RULE:\nNO OPNsense config changes.\nNO reboot/rescue.\nNO Hetzner changes.\nNO firewall changes.\nNO WireGuard changes.\n\n1. VERIFY TARGET\n\nUsing Hetzner API read-only:\n\nconfirm server identity\nconfirm 2.28.34.27 assignment\nconfirm server status\nconfirm rescue=false\n\nReturn:\n\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE=\nSERVER_RUNNING=\nWAN_IP_GATE=\n\n2. EXTERNAL PROBES\n\nFrom Antani test separately:\n\nICMP 2.28.34.27\nTCP/443\nTCP/80\nTCP/22\n\nUse short timeouts.\n\nReturn:\n\nWAN_ICMP=\nWAN_TCP443=\nWAN_TCP80=\nWAN_TCP22=\n\nClassify TCP/443 specifically:\n\nOPEN\nREFUSED\nTIMEOUT\n\n3. ROUTING\n\nRun read-only:\n\nip route get 2.28.34.27\n\nVerify traffic uses Antani public interface/default gateway and NOT:\n\n10.90.20.0/24\ntailscale\nWireGuard\n\nReturn:\n\nWAN_PROBE_ROUTE=\nWAN_PROBE_SOURCE=\nWAN_ROUTE_GATE=\n\n4. APPROVED SOURCE\n\nAudit current Antani public IPv4.\n\nCompare against the historical OPNsense WAN HTTPS rule:\n\n78.212.130.109/32\n\nIMPORTANT:\nAntani is NOT expected to match this rule.\n\nTherefore failure from Antani alone does not prove WebGUI failure.\n\nReturn:\n\nANTANI_PUBLIC_IP=\nWAN_HTTPS_ALLOWED_SOURCE_HISTORICAL=78.212.130.109/32\n\n5. USER-SIDE POSSIBILITY\n\nDetermine whether the user's current mobile public IP may have changed\nsince the rule was created.\n\nDo not modify OPNsense.\n\nReturn:\n\nADMIN_SOURCE_IP_CHANGE_POSSIBLE=YES\n\n6. CLASSIFY\n\nChoose strongest supported:\n\nADMIN_SOURCE_IP_CHANGED\nOPNSENSE_WEBGUI_NOT_LISTENING\nOPNSENSE_WAN_RULE_MISSING\nOPNSENSE_RUNTIME_FAILURE\nOPNSENSE_HOST_UNREACHABLE\nANTANI_EXPECTEDLY_BLOCKED\nUNKNOWN\n\nWAN_WEBGUI_FAILURE_CLASS=\n\n7. REPORT\n\nWrite:\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/OPNSENSE-WAN-WEBGUI-ACCESS-AUDIT.md\n\nFinal:\n\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE=\nSERVER_RUNNING=\nWAN_IP_GATE=\n\nWAN_ICMP=\nWAN_TCP443=\nWAN_TCP80=\nWAN_TCP22=\n\nWAN_PROBE_ROUTE=\nWAN_PROBE_SOURCE=\n\nWAN_HTTPS_ALLOWED_SOURCE_HISTORICAL=78.212.130.109/32\n\nADMIN_SOURCE_IP_CHANGE_POSSIBLE=\nWAN_WEBGUI_FAILURE_CLASS=\n\nCHANGES_MADE=NONE\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1199:{"session_id":"01a08abd-a56a-7773-9aa9-ff51183b9712","ts":1789036072,"text":"LEVEL PRO — OPNSENSE WAN BREAKS AFTER PRIVATE LAN\nROOT CAUSE AUDIT\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> COMPARE -> GATE -> NO CHANGE\n\nKNOWN:\n\nOPNSENSE_WAN_IP=2.28.34.27\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_IP=10.90.10.1\nHETZNER_NETWORK=10.90.0.0/16\nANTANI_PRIVATE=10.90.20.10\n\nSYMPTOM:\n\nWAN WebGUI works before private/LAN activation.\nAfter private/LAN is configured, WAN access stops working.\n\nABSOLUTE RULE:\n\nREAD ONLY.\n\nDO NOT:\n- modify OPNsense\n- modify Hetzner\n- modify firewall\n- modify routes\n- reboot\n- enable Rescue\n- start WireGuard\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nDetermine whether enabling OPNsense private interface changes:\n\n- default route\n- WAN gateway\n- return path\n- policy routing\n- interface gateway assignment\n- reply-to behavior\n- PF state/rules\n- source-address selection\n\n============================================================\n1. AUTHORITATIVE WAN STATE\n============================================================\n\nUsing existing configuration evidence determine:\n\nWAN_INTERFACE=\nWAN_IP=\nWAN_GATEWAY=\nWAN_DEFAULT_ROUTE=\n\nExpected WAN IP:\n\n2.28.34.27\n\nReturn:\n\nWAN_GATEWAY_PRESENT=\nWAN_DEFAULT_ROUTE_PRESENT=\n\n============================================================\n2. PRIVATE INTERFACE\n============================================================\n\nExpected:\n\nPRIVATE_INTERFACE=vtnet1\nPRIVATE_IP=10.90.10.1\n\nThe private interface MUST NOT become the Internet default gateway.\n\nReturn:\n\nPRIVATE_GATEWAY_SETTING=\nPRIVATE_DEFAULT_ROUTE_CREATED=\nPRIVATE_INTERFACE_GATEWAY_ASSIGNED=\n\n============================================================\n3. DEFAULT ROUTE CONFLICT\n============================================================\n\nCheck whether activation of vtnet1 causes:\n\ndefault -> private interface\n\nor installs a gateway with higher priority than WAN.\n\nRequired target:\n\nDEFAULT_ROUTE -> WAN\n\nReturn:\n\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_OWNER=\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_GATE=\n\nIf default route is private:\n\nWAN_FAILURE_CLASS=PRIVATE_INTERFACE_STOLE_DEFAULT_ROUTE\n\n============================================================\n4. HETZNER PRIVATE ROUTING\n============================================================\n\nPrivate network should handle only intended private prefixes.\n\nExpected:\n\n10.90.0.0/16 -> Hetzner private path\n\nInternet:\n\n0.0.0.0/0 -> WAN\n\nReturn:\n\nPRIVATE_ROUTE_SCOPE=\nPRIVATE_ROUTE_GATE=\n\nDo not create a private default route.\n\n============================================================\n5. RETURN PATH\n============================================================\n\nModel an incoming connection:\n\nADMIN_PUBLIC_IP\n    ->\n2.28.34.27:443\n    ->\nOPNsense\n\nDetermine expected reply route to ADMIN_PUBLIC_IP.\n\nRequired:\n\nREPLY_INTERFACE=WAN\nREPLY_SOURCE=2.28.34.27\n\nReturn:\n\nWAN_REPLY_ROUTE=\nWAN_REPLY_INTERFACE=\nWAN_REPLY_SOURCE=\n\nWAN_RETURN_PATH_GATE=\n\n============================================================\n6. PF / REPLY-TO\n============================================================\n\nAudit OPNsense PF behavior for the WAN WebGUI rule.\n\nDetermine whether the WAN rule has correct gateway/reply-to semantics.\n\nReturn:\n\nWAN_RULE_PRESENT=\nWAN_RULE_GATEWAY=\nWAN_RULE_REPLY_TO=\nWAN_RULE_RETURN_PATH_GATE=\n\nCheck whether private-interface activation changes or invalidates the\nexpected reply path.\n\n============================================================\n7. INTERFACE OPTIONS\n============================================================\n\nAudit private interface configuration for inappropriate settings such as:\n\ngateway assignment\nupstream gateway semantics\ndefault gateway selection\n\nThe Hetzner private interface must be treated as internal/private\ntransport, not WAN/upstream Internet.\n\nReturn:\n\nPRIVATE_INTERFACE_ROLE=\nPRIVATE_INTERFACE_UPSTREAM_GATEWAY=\nPRIVATE_INTERFACE_CONFIGURATION_GATE=\n\n============================================================\n8. CLASSIFY\n\nChoose strongest supported cause:\n\nPRIVATE_INTERFACE_STOLE_DEFAULT_ROUTE\nPRIVATE_GATEWAY_MISASSIGNED\nWAN_DEFAULT_GATEWAY_LOST\nWAN_RETURN_PATH_ASYMMETRIC\nPF_REPLY_TO_FAILURE\nWAN_RULE_FAILURE\nINTERFACE_CONFIGURATION_CONFLICT\nUNKNOWN\n\nWAN_AFTER_LAN_FAILURE_CLASS=\n\n============================================================\n9. REPORT\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/OPNSENSE-WAN-AFTER-LAN-ROOT-CAUSE.md\n\nFinal:\n\nWAN_IP=\nWAN_GATEWAY=\nWAN_DEFAULT_ROUTE=\n\nPRIVATE_INTERFACE=\nPRIVATE_IP=\nPRIVATE_GATEWAY_SETTING=\n\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_OWNER=\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_GATE=\n\nWAN_REPLY_INTERFACE=\nWAN_REPLY_SOURCE=\nWAN_RETURN_PATH_GATE=\n\nWAN_RULE_PRESENT=\nWAN_RULE_REPLY_TO=\n\nPRIVATE_INTERFACE_CONFIGURATION_GATE=\n\nWAN_AFTER_LAN_FAILURE_CLASS=\n\nCHANGES_MADE=NONE\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1200:{"session_id":"01a08abd-a56a-7773-9aa9-ff51183b9712","ts":1789051149,"text":"LEVEL PRO — OPNSENSE WEBGUI RUNTIME ROOT-CAUSE\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> NO CHANGE\n\nTARGET:\nWAN=vtnet0\nWAN_IP=2.28.34.27\nWAN_GATEWAY=172.31.1.1\n\nPRIVATE=vtnet1\nPRIVATE_IP=10.90.10.1\nPRIVATE_GATEWAY=10.90.0.1\n\nKNOWN:\nDEFAULT_ROUTE=WAN\nWAN_RETURN_PATH=PASS\n\nABSOLUTE RULE:\nREAD ONLY.\nDO NOT modify config.xml.\nDO NOT reload PF.\nDO NOT restart WebGUI.\nDO NOT reboot.\nDO NOT modify interfaces/routes/gateways.\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nDetermine exactly why TCP/443 is unreachable after vtnet1/private\ninterface configuration.\n\n============================================================\n1. RUNTIME INTERFACES\n============================================================\n\nOn OPNsense runtime inspect read-only:\n\nifconfig vtnet0\nifconfig vtnet1\nnetstat -rn\n\nReturn:\n\nVTNET0_UP=\nVTNET0_IPV4=\nVTNET1_UP=\nVTNET1_IPV4=\nDEFAULT_ROUTE=\nPRIVATE_ROUTE=\n\nRequired expected:\n\nvtnet0 = 2.28.34.27\nvtnet1 = 10.90.10.1\ndefault -> 172.31.1.1 via vtnet0\n\n============================================================\n2. WEBGUI PROCESS / SOCKET\n============================================================\n\nInspect WebGUI process and listeners.\n\nUse appropriate FreeBSD read-only tools:\n\nsockstat -4 -6 -l\nps aux\n\nDetermine:\n\nWEBGUI_PROCESS_RUNNING=\nWEBGUI_PORT=\nWEBGUI_LISTEN_ADDRESSES=\n\nExplicitly determine whether 443 listens on:\n\n2.28.34.27\n10.90.10.1\n0.0.0.0 / *\nloopback only\nnothing\n\nReturn:\n\nWEBGUI_WAN_LISTEN=\nWEBGUI_PRIVATE_LISTEN=\n\n============================================================\n3. CONFIGURED WEBGUI BIND\n============================================================\n\nRead config.xml WITHOUT modification.\n\nInspect WebGUI configuration only.\n\nDetermine:\n\nWEBGUI_PROTOCOL=\nWEBGUI_CONFIGURED_PORT=\nWEBGUI_CONFIGURED_INTERFACES=\n\nCompare configured interfaces with runtime listeners.\n\nReturn:\n\nWEBGUI_BIND_CONFIG_GATE=\n\n============================================================\n4. PF RUNTIME\n============================================================\n\nRead only:\n\npfctl -si\npfctl -sr\npfctl -sn\n\nDo NOT reload PF.\n\nDetermine whether WAN TCP/443 has a runtime PASS rule.\n\nReturn:\n\nPF_RUNNING=\nWAN_443_PASS_RULE_PRESENT=\nWAN_443_PASS_SOURCE=\nWAN_443_BLOCK_BEFORE_PASS=\nWAN_443_REPLY_TO=\n\nDo not print unrelated sensitive rule details.\n\n============================================================\n5. LOCAL SOCKET TEST\n============================================================\n\nFrom OPNsense itself perform safe probes:\n\n127.0.0.1:443\n2.28.34.27:443\n10.90.10.1:443\n\nDo not authenticate.\n\nReturn:\n\nLOCAL_443_LOOPBACK=\nLOCAL_443_WAN=\nLOCAL_443_PRIVATE=\n\n============================================================\n6. PACKET ARRIVAL\n============================================================\n\nDuring ONE external TCP/443 probe, observe vtnet0 read-only with tcpdump.\n\nFilter only:\n\ntcp port 443\n\nDetermine:\n\nWAN_443_SYN_ARRIVES=\nWAN_443_SYNACK_LEAVES=\nWAN_443_RST_LEAVES=\n\nDo not capture payload.\n\n============================================================\n7. CLASSIFY ROOT CAUSE\n============================================================\n\nChoose exactly one strongest-supported class:\n\nWEBGUI_PROCESS_DOWN\nWEBGUI_NOT_BOUND_TO_WAN\nWEBGUI_BOUND_PRIVATE_ONLY\nWAN_443_PASS_RULE_MISSING\nWAN_443_BLOCKED_BY_PF\nWAN_443_SOURCE_RESTRICTION\nPF_REPLY_TO_FAILURE\nPACKETS_NOT_REACHING_WAN\nRUNTIME_CONFIG_MISMATCH\nUNKNOWN\n\nWAN_WEBGUI_ROOT_CAUSE=\n\n============================================================\n8. GATE\n============================================================\n\nReturn:\n\nWAN_INTERFACE_GATE=\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_GATE=\nWEBGUI_PROCESS_GATE=\nWEBGUI_WAN_BIND_GATE=\nPF_WAN_443_GATE=\nWAN_PACKET_ARRIVAL_GATE=\n\nCHANGES_MADE=NONE\nOPNSENSE_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE=\n\nWrite:\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/OPNSENSE-WEBGUI-RUNTIME-ROOT-CAUSE.md"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1203:{"session_id":"01a08abd-a56a-7773-9aa9-ff51183b9712","ts":1789051730,"text":"LEVEL PRO — OPNSENSE CONFIG RESET\nWAN-ONLY RESTORE\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> BACKUP -> RESTORE -> VERIFY\n\nTARGET STATE:\n\nvtnet0 = WAN ONLY\nvtnet1 = UNASSIGNED / DISABLED\n\nWAN_IP=2.28.34.27\nWAN_GATEWAY=172.31.1.1\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nRestore the known-good OPNsense configuration that preserves WAN access\nand removes the private/LAN assignment.\n\nABSOLUTE RULES:\n\nDO NOT modify Hetzner resources.\nDO NOT modify Antani.\nDO NOT modify WireGuard.\nDO NOT modify SMTP.\nDO NOT alter DNS.\nDO NOT invent a new config.xml.\n\n============================================================\n1. FIND RESTORE CANDIDATE\n============================================================\n\nAudit existing OPNsense config backups and prior known-good snapshots.\n\nSearch for configs where:\n\nWAN=vtnet0\nWAN_IP=2.28.34.27\nWAN_GATEWAY=172.31.1.1\n\nand:\n\nvtnet1 is not assigned as LAN/private\nor private/LAN configuration predates the failure.\n\nReturn:\n\nCURRENT_CONFIG_SHA256=\nRESTORE_CANDIDATES=\n\nFor each candidate:\n\nFILE=\nSHA256=\nWAN_INTERFACE=\nWAN_IP=\nWAN_GATEWAY=\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=\nWEBGUI_PORT=\nWEBGUI_WAN_ACCESS_PRESENT=\n\nDo not print secrets/private keys.\n\n============================================================\n2. RESTORE GATE\n============================================================\n\nChoose ONLY a candidate that satisfies:\n\nWAN_INTERFACE=vtnet0\nWAN_IP=2.28.34.27\nWAN_GATEWAY=172.31.1.1\nDEFAULT_ROUTE=WAN\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=NO\n\nand preserves known WAN WebGUI access.\n\nIf no exact candidate exists:\n\nSTOP.\n\nDo not synthesize configuration.\n\nReturn:\n\nRESTORE_CANDIDATE=\nRESTORE_GATE=PASS|FAIL\n\n============================================================\n3. BACKUP CURRENT CONFIG\n============================================================\n\nBefore restore:\n\ncreate an immutable/current recovery copy of the existing config.xml.\n\nGenerate SHA256.\n\nRequired:\n\nCURRENT_BACKUP_CREATED=YES\nCURRENT_BACKUP_HASH=PASS\n\n============================================================\n4. RESTORE\n============================================================\n\nOnly if RESTORE_GATE=PASS:\n\nrestore the selected known-good config.xml using the normal OPNsense\nconfiguration restore mechanism.\n\nDo not manually merge unrelated settings.\n\nDo not modify Hetzner networking.\n\n============================================================\n5. BOOT / APPLY\n============================================================\n\nApply the restored configuration using the safest native OPNsense method.\n\nIf a reboot is required for clean restore:\n\nreboot ONLY OPNsense.\n\nDo not reboot Antani.\n\n============================================================\n6. VERIFY WAN\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nVTNET0_UP=YES\nVTNET0_IP=2.28.34.27\nDEFAULT_ROUTE=172.31.1.1\n\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=NO\nVTNET1_ENABLED=NO\n\nVerify:\n\nTCP/443 WAN\nWebGUI WAN\nWAN return path\n\nRequired:\n\nWAN_WEBGUI_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n7. VERIFY NO PRIVATE LAN\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE_IP_10_90_10_1=ABSENT\nVTNET1_PRIVATE_ROUTE=ABSENT\nPRIVATE_LAN_FIREWALL_BIND=ABSENT\n\nDo not remove Hetzner Network itself.\n\n============================================================\n8. FINAL\n============================================================\n\nRESTORE_CANDIDATE=\nRESTORE_GATE=\n\nCURRENT_BACKUP_CREATED=\nCURRENT_BACKUP_HASH=\n\nWAN_INTERFACE=\nWAN_IP=\nWAN_GATEWAY=\nDEFAULT_ROUTE=\n\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=\nVTNET1_ENABLED=\n\nWAN_WEBGUI_GATE=\n\nOPNSENSE_WAN_ONLY_MODE=PASS\n\nANTANI_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_CHANGED=NO\nWG_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE=\n\nWrite report:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/OPNSENSE-WAN-ONLY-CONFIG-RESTORE.md"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1205:{"session_id":"01a08abd-a56a-7773-9aa9-ff51183b9712","ts":1789051925,"text":"LEVEL PRO — OPNSENSE EXISTING CONFIG RESET VIA HETZNER API\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> BACKUP -> RESET -> NORMAL BOOT -> VERIFY\n\nAUTHORIZED ACTIONS:\n- Hetzner API Rescue/reboot for OPNsense\n- read/write OPNsense config ONLY to restore an EXISTING known-good config\n- reboot OPNsense\n\nDO NOT:\n- create a new config.xml\n- synthesize WAN/LAN configuration\n- modify Antani\n- modify Hetzner Network/vSwitch\n- modify WireGuard\n- modify DNS\n\nTARGET:\n\nSERVER_NAME=worm-opnsense\nWAN_IP=2.28.34.27\nWAN_INTERFACE=vtnet0\n\n============================================================\n1. VERIFY TARGET VIA HETZNER API\n============================================================\n\nUsing existing authorized Hetzner API credentials:\n\nidentify worm-opnsense.\n\nVerify:\n\nSERVER_ID=\nSERVER_NAME=\nPRIMARY_IPV4=2.28.34.27\nSERVER_STATUS=\n\nRequired:\n\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE=PASS\n\nDo not print API credentials.\n\n============================================================\n2. ENABLE RESCUE + REBOOT\n============================================================\n\nVia Hetzner API:\n\nenable Rescue for worm-opnsense\nrequest reboot\n\nWAIT until Rescue SSH becomes reachable.\n\nDo NOT touch Antani.\n\nReturn:\n\nRESCUE_ENABLE=PASS\nRESCUE_REBOOT=PASS\nRESCUE_SSH=PASS\n\n============================================================\n3. IMPORT ZFS READ-ONLY FIRST\n============================================================\n\nDiscover OPNsense ZFS pool.\n\nExpected historical:\n\nPOOL=zroot\n\nImport/mount READ-ONLY first.\n\nLocate installed OPNsense root dataset and:\n\n/conf/config.xml\n/conf/backup/\n\nDo not modify anything yet.\n\nReturn:\n\nZROOT_FOUND=\nOPNSENSE_ROOT_FOUND=\nCURRENT_CONFIG_FOUND=\nBACKUP_DIR_FOUND=\n\n============================================================\n4. FIND EXISTING KNOWN-GOOD CONFIG\n============================================================\n\nInspect EXISTING OPNsense backups only.\n\nFind the most recent known-good config satisfying:\n\nWAN=vtnet0\nWAN_IP/configuration appropriate for 2.28.34.27\nvtnet1 NOT assigned as LAN/private\nWebGUI WAN configuration present\n\nDo NOT create a replacement configuration.\n\nDo NOT infer missing XML.\n\nReturn:\n\nKNOWN_GOOD_CONFIG_FOUND=\nKNOWN_GOOD_CONFIG_FILE=\nKNOWN_GOOD_CONFIG_SHA256=\n\nSanitize secrets from output.\n\nIf none exists:\n\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n5. BACKUP CURRENT CONFIG\n============================================================\n\nBefore restoring:\n\ncopy current /conf/config.xml to a protected timestamped recovery file.\n\nCalculate SHA256 before and after copy.\n\nRequired:\n\nCURRENT_CONFIG_BACKUP=PASS\nCURRENT_CONFIG_BACKUP_HASH_MATCH=PASS\n\n============================================================\n6. RESTORE EXISTING CONFIG\n============================================================\n\nOnly after all gates PASS:\n\nremount/import only as required for the minimal write.\n\nReplace:\n\n/conf/config.xml\n\nwith the selected EXISTING known-good backup.\n\nPreserve correct ownership and permissions.\n\nDo NOT edit XML contents.\n\nVerify:\n\nRESTORED_SHA256 == KNOWN_GOOD_CONFIG_SHA256\n\nRequired:\n\nCONFIG_RESTORE_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n7. CLEAN EXPORT\n============================================================\n\nsync\n\ncleanly unmount/export OPNsense ZFS.\n\nRequired:\n\nZPOOL_EXPORT=PASS\n\n============================================================\n8. DISABLE RESCUE + NORMAL BOOT\n============================================================\n\nUsing Hetzner API:\n\nensure Rescue is disabled for next boot\nreboot worm-opnsense\n\nWAIT for normal OPNsense boot.\n\nRequired:\n\nNORMAL_BOOT_REQUESTED=YES\nRESCUE_ENABLED_AFTER=NO\n\n============================================================\n9. VERIFY WAN ONLY\n============================================================\n\nFrom external network verify:\n\n2.28.34.27 reachable\n\nTCP/443 test\n\nDo not authenticate automatically.\n\nExpected configuration:\n\nWAN_INTERFACE=vtnet0\nWAN_IP=2.28.34.27\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=NO\n\nReturn:\n\nNORMAL_BOOT_REACHED=\nWAN_443=\nWAN_WEBGUI_GATE=\n\n============================================================\n10. STOP CONDITIONS\n============================================================\n\nSTOP immediately if:\n\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE != PASS\nZROOT_FOUND != YES\nKNOWN_GOOD_CONFIG_FOUND != YES\nCURRENT_CONFIG_BACKUP != PASS\nCURRENT_CONFIG_BACKUP_HASH_MATCH != PASS\n\nNever improvise a replacement config.\n\n============================================================\n11. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/OPNSENSE-EXISTING-CONFIG-API-RESET.md\n\nFinal:\n\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE=\nSERVER_ID=\nPRIMARY_IPV4=\n\nRESCUE_ENABLE=\nRESCUE_SSH=\n\nZROOT_FOUND=\nCURRENT_CONFIG_FOUND=\n\nKNOWN_GOOD_CONFIG_FOUND=\nKNOWN_GOOD_CONFIG_FILE=\nKNOWN_GOOD_CONFIG_SHA256=\n\nCURRENT_CONFIG_BACKUP=\nCURRENT_CONFIG_BACKUP_HASH_MATCH=\n\nCONFIG_RESTORE_GATE=\nZPOOL_EXPORT=\n\nNORMAL_BOOT_REQUESTED=\nNORMAL_BOOT_REACHED=\nRESCUE_ENABLED_AFTER=\n\nWAN_443=\nWAN_WEBGUI_GATE=\n\nCONFIG_SYNTHESIZED=NO\nANTANI_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_NETWORK_CHANGED=NO\nWG_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1206:{"session_id":"01a08abd-a56a-7773-9aa9-ff51183b9712","ts":1789053188,"text":"LEVEL PRO — OPNSENSE WAN-ONLY CONFIG\nVTNET0 ONLY / REMOVE VTNET1\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> BACKUP -> GATE -> MINIMAL CONFIG CHANGE -> VERIFY\n\nAUTHORIZED CHANGE=YES\n\nTARGET:\n\nWAN_INTERFACE=vtnet0\nWAN_IP=2.28.34.27\n\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=NO\nVTNET1_ENABLED=NO\nLAN_INTERFACE=NONE\nPRIVATE_INTERFACE=NONE\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nConfigure OPNsense with ONLY vtnet0 as the active assigned interface.\n\nRemove all vtnet1/LAN/private assignment from OPNsense configuration.\n\nABSOLUTE FREEZE:\n\nDO NOT modify Hetzner Cloud Network.\nDO NOT modify Hetzner vSwitch.\nDO NOT modify Antani.\nDO NOT modify WireGuard.\nDO NOT modify DNS.\nDO NOT modify SMTP.\nDO NOT invent unrelated firewall/NAT configuration.\n\n============================================================\n1. TARGET IDENTITY\n============================================================\n\nVia existing authorized Hetzner API verify:\n\nSERVER_NAME=worm-opnsense\nPRIMARY_IPV4=2.28.34.27\n\nRequired:\n\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n2. RESCUE\n============================================================\n\nIf normal OPNsense runtime cannot be accessed:\n\nenable Hetzner Rescue for worm-opnsense\nreboot ONLY worm-opnsense\nwait for Rescue SSH\n\nMount/import the installed OPNsense filesystem using the previously\nvalidated ZFS procedure.\n\nDo not touch Antani.\n\n============================================================\n3. BACKUP CURRENT CONFIG\n============================================================\n\nLocate:\n\n/conf/config.xml\n\nBefore changing anything:\n\ncreate timestamped backup\ncalculate SHA256\nverify copied backup hash\n\nRequired:\n\nCURRENT_CONFIG_BACKUP=PASS\nCURRENT_CONFIG_BACKUP_HASH_MATCH=PASS\n\n============================================================\n4. AUDIT EXISTING CONFIG\n============================================================\n\nParse config.xml.\n\nDetermine:\n\nCURRENT_WAN_INTERFACE=\nCURRENT_WAN_CONFIG=\n\nCURRENT_LAN_INTERFACE=\nCURRENT_PRIVATE_INTERFACE=\n\nVTNET1_REFERENCES=\n\nFind all configuration objects whose existence depends exclusively on\nvtnet1, including:\n\n- interface assignment\n- LAN/private interface address\n- vtnet1 gateway\n- static routes tied to vtnet1\n- firewall rules on the removed interface\n- DHCP server tied to the removed interface\n- interface groups referencing removed assignment\n\nDo NOT remove unrelated objects.\n\n============================================================\n5. WAN PRESERVATION GATE\n============================================================\n\nRequired before editing:\n\nWAN_INTERFACE=vtnet0\n\nPreserve the existing working WAN IPv4 configuration exactly.\n\nDo NOT change:\n\nWAN addressing mode\nWAN gateway semantics\ndefault route\nMAC\nMTU\nprovider-specific WAN configuration\n\nWAN target public address remains:\n\n2.28.34.27\n\nRequired:\n\nWAN_PRESERVATION_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n6. MINIMAL CONFIG CHANGE\n============================================================\n\nModify the EXISTING config.xml.\n\nDo NOT generate a new config.xml from scratch.\n\nTarget assignments:\n\nvtnet0 -> WAN\n\nNo other assigned network interface.\n\nRemove/unassign:\n\nvtnet1\nLAN\nPRIVATE\n\nTarget:\n\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=NO\nLAN_ASSIGNED=NO\nPRIVATE_ASSIGNED=NO\n\nRemove the vtnet1 IPv4 configuration.\n\nRemove only gateway/routes/rules that reference the removed\nvtnet1/LAN/private assignment.\n\n============================================================\n7. WEBGUI WAN ACCESS\n============================================================\n\nThe system must remain administrable from WAN.\n\nEnsure WebGUI configuration permits HTTPS on WAN.\n\nWEBGUI_PROTOCOL=https\nWEBGUI_PORT=443\nWEBGUI_WAN=YES\n\nPreserve the existing approved-source security policy where possible.\n\nDo NOT expose SSH publicly.\n\nTarget:\n\nWAN_HTTPS=YES\nWAN_SSH=NO\n\n============================================================\n8. CONFIG VALIDATION\n============================================================\n\nBefore boot:\n\nvalidate XML syntax.\n\nVerify:\n\nvtnet0 reference exists\nWAN assignment exists\nvtnet1 assignment does NOT exist\nLAN assignment does NOT exist\n\nSearch entire active configuration for active vtnet1 interface\ndependencies.\n\nRequired:\n\nXML_VALID=PASS\nWAN_ASSIGNMENT_GATE=PASS\nVTNET1_REMOVAL_GATE=PASS\n\nDo not count historical backups.\n\n============================================================\n9. WRITE + VERIFY HASH\n============================================================\n\nWrite the minimally edited config.xml.\n\nImmediately read it back.\n\nVerify:\n\nCONFIG_WRITE_GATE=PASS\nXML_VALID_AFTER_WRITE=PASS\n\nDo NOT perform additional edits.\n\n============================================================\n10. CLEAN ZFS EXPORT\n============================================================\n\nsync\ncleanly unmount/export zroot\n\nRequired:\n\nZPOOL_EXPORT_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n11. NORMAL BOOT\n============================================================\n\nDisable Rescue for next boot.\n\nReboot ONLY worm-opnsense into installed OPNsense.\n\nWait for normal boot.\n\n============================================================\n12. WAN VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nVerify externally:\n\n2.28.34.27\n\nTest:\n\nTCP/443\n\nRequired:\n\nWAN_TCP443=OPEN\n\nThen verify WebGUI HTTPS responds.\n\nAccept:\n\nHTTP/TLS application response\n\nReject:\n\ntimeout\nconnection refused\n\nReturn:\n\nWAN_WEBGUI_GATE=\n\n============================================================\n13. FINAL NETWORK STATE\n============================================================\n\nTarget final state:\n\nVTNET0_ROLE=WAN\nVTNET0_IP=2.28.34.27\n\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=NO\nVTNET1_ENABLED=NO\n\nLAN_ASSIGNED=NO\nPRIVATE_ASSIGNED=NO\n\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_OWNER=WAN\n\nNo:\n\n10.90.10.1 interface address\n10.90.20.0/24 OPNsense private route\nvtnet1 firewall interface\nvtnet1 gateway\n\n============================================================\n14. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/OPNSENSE-VTNET0-WAN-ONLY.md\n\nFinal:\n\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE=\n\nCURRENT_CONFIG_BACKUP=\nCURRENT_CONFIG_BACKUP_HASH_MATCH=\n\nWAN_INTERFACE=\nWAN_IP=\nWAN_PRESERVATION_GATE=\n\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=\nLAN_ASSIGNED=\nPRIVATE_ASSIGNED=\n\nXML_VALID=\nVTNET1_REMOVAL_GATE=\n\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_OWNER=\n\nWAN_TCP443=\nWAN_WEBGUI_GATE=\n\nOPNSENSE_WAN_ONLY_GATE=\n\nANTANI_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_NETWORK_CHANGED=NO\nWG_CHANGED=NO\nSMTP_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1207:{"session_id":"01a08abd-a56a-7773-9aa9-ff51183b9712","ts":1789054791,"text":"LEVEL PRO — OPNsense CLEAN REINSTALL + WAN-ONLY RESTORE\n\nMETHOD:\nIDENTITY -> BACKUP -> INSTALL -> RESTORE -> REBOOT -> VERIFY\n\nAUTHORIZED DESTRUCTIVE CHANGE=YES\nTARGET=worm-opnsense\n\nFINAL TARGET:\n\nOPNsense fresh install\n    |\n    └── vtnet0 = WAN\n         ├── public IPv4 = 2.28.34.27\n         ├── default gateway = WAN\n         └── WebGUI HTTPS :443\n\nvtnet1 = UNASSIGNED\nLAN    = NONE\nOPT    = NONE\nPRIVATE= NONE\n\n============================================================\nABSOLUTE SAFETY\n============================================================\n\nTHIS TASK MAY ERASE THE OPNsense SYSTEM DISK.\n\nBefore ANY destructive command prove:\n\nSERVER_NAME=worm-opnsense\nPRIMARY_IPV4=2.28.34.27\nSERVER_ID=<authoritative Hetzner ID>\nTARGET_DISK=<authoritatively discovered OPNsense disk>\n\nIf any identity field is ambiguous:\n\nSTOP.\n\nNEVER touch Antani disks.\n\nDO NOT modify:\n\nAntani\nHetzner Network\nvSwitch\nDNS\nSMTP\nWireGuard\nWormOS\n\n============================================================\n1. PRESERVE CURRENT KNOWN-GOOD CONFIG\n============================================================\n\nThe currently validated configuration is:\n\nWAN_INTERFACE=vtnet0\nWAN_IP=2.28.34.27\n\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=NO\nVTNET1_ENABLED=NO\nLAN_ASSIGNED=NO\nPRIVATE_ASSIGNED=NO\n\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_OWNER=WAN\nWAN_TCP443=OPEN\nWAN_WEBGUI_GATE=PASS\nOPNSENSE_WAN_ONLY_GATE=PASS\n\nLocate the exact current:\n\n/conf/config.xml\n\nCreate TWO recovery copies outside the filesystem that will be erased.\n\nCalculate SHA256.\n\nReturn:\n\nWAN_ONLY_CONFIG_FOUND=\nWAN_ONLY_CONFIG_SHA256=\n\nBACKUP_COPY_1=\nBACKUP_COPY_2=\n\nBACKUP_COPY_1_HASH_MATCH=\nBACKUP_COPY_2_HASH_MATCH=\n\nRequired:\n\nCONFIG_BACKUP_GATE=PASS\n\nDo NOT proceed otherwise.\n\n============================================================\n2. SANITIZED CONFIG AUDIT\n============================================================\n\nParse the saved config.xml.\n\nVerify:\n\nWAN=vtnet0\nVTNET1_ASSIGNMENT=ABSENT\nLAN_ASSIGNMENT=ABSENT\nOPT_ASSIGNMENTS=ABSENT\n\nVerify no active interface address:\n\n10.90.10.1\n\nVerify no active vtnet1-specific gateway/route/firewall dependency.\n\nDo NOT print:\n\npassword hashes\nprivate keys\ncert private material\nAPI secrets\n\nRequired:\n\nWAN_ONLY_CONFIG_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n3. HETZNER TARGET IDENTITY\n============================================================\n\nUsing existing authorized Hetzner API:\n\nverify target server again immediately before reinstall.\n\nReturn:\n\nTARGET_SERVER_ID=\nTARGET_SERVER_NAME=\nTARGET_PRIMARY_IPV4=\nTARGET_STATUS=\n\nRequired:\n\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n4. ENTER INSTALL/RESCUE ENVIRONMENT\n============================================================\n\nUse the existing authorized Hetzner recovery/install mechanism.\n\nReboot ONLY:\n\nworm-opnsense\n\nDo not reboot Antani.\n\nVerify the environment is the intended OPNsense server before touching\nany disk.\n\nReturn:\n\nRECOVERY_ENVIRONMENT_GATE=\n\n============================================================\n5. DISK DISCOVERY\n============================================================\n\nDiscover disks.\n\nIdentify the existing OPNsense system disk from:\n\ndevice identity\npartition layout\nexisting OPNsense/ZFS evidence\n\nReturn:\n\nTARGET_DISK=\n\nExplicitly prove:\n\nTARGET_DISK_BELONGS_TO_OPNSENSE=YES\n\nIf more than one plausible target exists:\n\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n6. FRESH OPNsense INSTALL\n============================================================\n\nInstall the approved/current OPNsense release using the established\ninstallation mechanism for this server.\n\nDo not create an experimental network architecture.\n\nFresh installation target is the verified OPNsense system disk only.\n\nRequired:\n\nINSTALL_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n7. RESTORE WAN-ONLY CONFIG\n============================================================\n\nBefore first production boot, restore the exact previously backed-up\nWAN-only config.xml into the installed OPNsense configuration location.\n\nDo NOT regenerate it.\n\nDo NOT add LAN.\n\nDo NOT add vtnet1.\n\nDo NOT run interface assignment logic that introduces a LAN.\n\nAfter copy:\n\ncalculate SHA256.\n\nRequired:\n\nRESTORED_CONFIG_SHA256 == WAN_ONLY_CONFIG_SHA256\n\nReturn:\n\nCONFIG_RESTORE_GATE=\n\n============================================================\n8. PRE-BOOT CONFIG GATE\n============================================================\n\nParse restored config again.\n\nRequired:\n\nWAN_INTERFACE=vtnet0\n\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=NO\nLAN_ASSIGNED=NO\nOPT_ASSIGNED=NO\nPRIVATE_ASSIGNED=NO\n\nWEBGUI_PROTOCOL=https\nWEBGUI_PORT=443\n\nXML_VALID=PASS\n\nIf any fails:\n\nDO NOT NORMAL BOOT.\n\n============================================================\n9. NORMAL BOOT\n============================================================\n\nCleanly unmount/export filesystems.\n\nDisable Rescue/install boot.\n\nReboot ONLY worm-opnsense.\n\nWait for normal OPNsense startup.\n\nReturn:\n\nNORMAL_BOOT_REQUESTED=\nNORMAL_BOOT_REACHED=\n\n============================================================\n10. NETWORK VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nVerify externally:\n\n2.28.34.27\n\nRequired:\n\nWAN_REACHABLE=\nWAN_TCP443=OPEN\n\nVerify TLS/application response from:\n\nhttps://2.28.34.27/\n\nDo not require successful authentication for transport verification.\n\nAccept:\n\nHTTP application response including expected 200/302/401/403.\n\nReject:\n\ntimeout\nconnection refused\n5xx\n\nReturn:\n\nWAN_WEBGUI_TRANSPORT_GATE=\n\n============================================================\n11. INTERFACE VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nVerify final runtime where safely observable:\n\nVTNET0_PRESENT=YES\nVTNET0_ROLE=WAN\n\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=NO\nLAN_ASSIGNED=NO\nPRIVATE_ASSIGNED=NO\n\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_OWNER=WAN\n\nRequired:\n\nWAN_ONLY_RUNTIME_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n12. SECURITY VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nWAN SSH was NOT accidentally exposed.\n\nWAN_SSH_EXPOSED=NO\n\nWebGUI WAN access must preserve the intended restricted administration\npolicy from the restored known-good configuration.\n\nDo NOT broaden :443 to arbitrary sources merely to make verification\npass.\n\n============================================================\n13. FINAL GATE\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nFRESH_INSTALL_GATE=PASS\nCONFIG_RESTORE_GATE=PASS\nWAN_ONLY_RUNTIME_GATE=PASS\nWAN_WEBGUI_TRANSPORT_GATE=PASS\n\nThen:\n\nOPNSENSE_FRESH_WAN_ONLY_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n14. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/OPNSENSE-FRESH-INSTALL-WAN-ONLY.md\n\nFinal:\n\nTARGET_SERVER_ID=\nTARGET_PRIMARY_IPV4=\n\nTARGET_DISK=\nTARGET_DISK_BELONGS_TO_OPNSENSE=\n\nWAN_ONLY_CONFIG_SHA256=\nCONFIG_BACKUP_GATE=\n\nINSTALL_GATE=\nCONFIG_RESTORE_GATE=\n\nNORMAL_BOOT_REACHED=\n\nWAN_INTERFACE=\nWAN_IP=2.28.34.27\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_OWNER=\n\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=\nLAN_ASSIGNED=\nOPT_ASSIGNED=\nPRIVATE_ASSIGNED=\n\nWAN_TCP443=\nWAN_WEBGUI_TRANSPORT_GATE=\nWAN_SSH_EXPOSED=\n\nOPNSENSE_FRESH_WAN_ONLY_GATE=\n\nANTANI_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_NETWORK_CHANGED=NO\nVSWITCH_CHANGED=NO\nWG_CHANGED=NO\nSMTP_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1208:{"session_id":"01a08abd-a56a-7773-9aa9-ff51183b9712","ts":1789054914,"text":"LEVEL PRO — POST-INSTALL WAN BASELINE + GOLDEN BACKUP\n\nRun this stage ONLY after the fresh OPNsense installation has booted\nwith the WAN-only config.\n\nTARGET:\n\nWAN_INTERFACE=vtnet0\nWAN_IP=2.28.34.27\n\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=NO\nLAN_ASSIGNED=NO\nPRIVATE_ASSIGNED=NO\n\n============================================================\n1. NORMAL BOOT GATE\n============================================================\n\nVerify OPNsense is running from the installed system, NOT Rescue.\n\nRequired:\n\nNORMAL_BOOT_REACHED=YES\nRESCUE_ENABLED=NO\n\n============================================================\n2. WAN RUNTIME VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nvtnet0=UP\nWAN_IP=2.28.34.27\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_OWNER=WAN\n\nRequired:\n\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=NO\nLAN_ASSIGNED=NO\nPRIVATE_ASSIGNED=NO\n\nDo not change configuration during verification.\n\n============================================================\n3. EXTERNAL WAN TEST\n============================================================\n\nTest the public WAN from an external host.\n\nTarget:\n\n2.28.34.27\n\nVerify:\n\nWAN_IP_REACHABLE=\nWAN_TCP443=\n\nThen test:\n\nhttps://2.28.34.27/\n\nAccept an OPNsense application/TLS response.\n\nAcceptable application status where appropriate:\n\n200\n302\n401\n403\n\nReject:\n\ntimeout\nconnection refused\n500\n502\n503\n\nRequired:\n\nWAN_WEBGUI_TRANSPORT_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n4. ADMIN SOURCE TEST\n============================================================\n\nFrom the intended authorized administration source, verify actual WebGUI\naccess.\n\nRequired:\n\nWAN_WEBGUI_ADMIN_GATE=PASS\n\nDo not broaden the WAN firewall merely to make the test pass.\n\nSSH must remain non-public unless separately authorized.\n\nRequired:\n\nWAN_SSH_EXPOSED=NO\n\n============================================================\n5. STABILITY CHECK\n============================================================\n\nAfter initial PASS, verify again that:\n\nWAN remains reachable\ndefault route remains WAN\nWebGUI remains reachable\nno vtnet1/LAN assignment appeared\n\nRequired:\n\nWAN_STABILITY_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n6. GOLDEN BACKUP GATE\n============================================================\n\nONLY if all are PASS:\n\nNORMAL_BOOT_REACHED\nWAN_WEBGUI_TRANSPORT_GATE\nWAN_WEBGUI_ADMIN_GATE\nWAN_STABILITY_GATE\n\ncreate the post-install baseline backup.\n\nIf any gate fails:\n\nBACKUP_GOLDEN_CREATED=NO\n\nSTOP and diagnose.\n\nDo NOT mark a broken installation as golden.\n\n============================================================\n7. BACKUP CONFIG.XML\n============================================================\n\nBack up the exact live validated:\n\n/conf/config.xml\n\nUse a descriptive immutable name such as:\n\nOPNSENSE-WAN-ONLY-GOLDEN-<timestamp>.xml\n\nStore a recovery copy OUTSIDE the OPNsense system disk as well.\n\nCalculate:\n\nSHA256\n\nVerify copied file hash equals live config hash.\n\nRequired:\n\nGOLDEN_CONFIG_BACKUP=PASS\nGOLDEN_CONFIG_HASH_MATCH=PASS\n\n============================================================\n8. OPTIONAL SYSTEM RECOVERY METADATA\n============================================================\n\nRecord sanitized recovery metadata:\n\nOPNsense version\nFreeBSD version\nWAN interface\nWAN public IP\ndefault gateway\nconfig SHA256\nbackup timestamp\n\nNever include:\n\npassword hashes\nprivate keys\nAPI tokens\ncertificate private keys\n\n============================================================\n9. GOLDEN BASELINE\n============================================================\n\nMark this backup as the authoritative baseline only after verification.\n\nTarget:\n\nBASELINE_NAME=OPNSENSE_WAN_ONLY_GOLDEN\n\nProperties:\n\nWAN=vtnet0\nWAN_IP=2.28.34.27\nVTNET1=NONE\nLAN=NONE\nPRIVATE=NONE\nWAN_443=PASS\nWEBGUI=PASS\n\n============================================================\n10. REPORT\n============================================================\n\nWrite:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/OPNSENSE-WAN-ONLY-GOLDEN-BASELINE.md\n\nFinal:\n\nNORMAL_BOOT_REACHED=\n\nWAN_INTERFACE=\nWAN_IP=\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_OWNER=\n\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=\nLAN_ASSIGNED=\nPRIVATE_ASSIGNED=\n\nWAN_TCP443=\nWAN_WEBGUI_TRANSPORT_GATE=\nWAN_WEBGUI_ADMIN_GATE=\nWAN_SSH_EXPOSED=\n\nWAN_STABILITY_GATE=\n\nGOLDEN_CONFIG_BACKUP=\nGOLDEN_CONFIG_BACKUP_PATH=\nGOLDEN_CONFIG_SHA256=\nGOLDEN_CONFIG_HASH_MATCH=\n\nBASELINE_NAME=OPNSENSE_WAN_ONLY_GOLDEN\nGOLDEN_BASELINE_GATE=\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1210:{"session_id":"01a08abd-a56a-7773-9aa9-ff51183b9712","ts":1789055215,"text":"LEVEL PRO — PREPARE OPNsense FAT32 CONFIG IMPORT VOLUME\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> GATE -> MINIMAL CHANGE -> VERIFY\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nCreate a dedicated FAT32 configuration-import volume containing the\nalready validated OPNsense WAN-only config.xml.\n\nTHIS TASK DOES NOT REINSTALL OPNsense.\nTHIS TASK DOES NOT REBOOT OPNsense.\n\n============================================================\n1. SOURCE CONFIG\n============================================================\n\nLocate the authoritative validated WAN-only config.xml.\n\nRequired semantic state:\n\nWAN_INTERFACE=vtnet0\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=NO\nLAN_ASSIGNED=NO\nOPT_ASSIGNED=NO\nPRIVATE_ASSIGNED=NO\n\nWEBGUI_PROTOCOL=https\nWEBGUI_PORT=443\n\nDo not print XML secrets.\n\nCalculate:\n\nSOURCE_CONFIG_SHA256=\n\nRequired:\n\nSOURCE_CONFIG_FOUND=YES\nSOURCE_CONFIG_XML_VALID=PASS\nSOURCE_CONFIG_WAN_ONLY_GATE=PASS\n\nSTOP otherwise.\n\n============================================================\n2. BACKUP SOURCE\n============================================================\n\nBefore preparing media, preserve the source config outside OPNsense:\n\n/opt/worm/backups/opnsense/wan-only/config.xml\n\nand:\n\n/opt/worm/backups/opnsense/wan-only/config.xml.sha256\n\nVerify:\n\nSOURCE_BACKUP_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n3. CREATE IMPORT IMAGE\n============================================================\n\nCreate a small disk-image FILE first.\n\nDO NOT touch any block device.\n\nTarget:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/opnsense/opnsense-config-import-fat32.img\n\nSuggested size:\n\n64 MiB\n\nCreate FAT32 filesystem on the IMAGE FILE.\n\nUse a clear filesystem label such as:\n\nOPNSENSECFG\n\n============================================================\n4. SAFETY\n============================================================\n\nABSOLUTE RULE:\n\nDO NOT run mkfs against:\n\n/dev/sda\n/dev/sdb\n/dev/nvme*\nor any physical/block device.\n\nmkfs.vfat is permitted ONLY against the newly created image file.\n\nRequired:\n\nIMPORT_TARGET_TYPE=REGULAR_FILE\n\nOtherwise STOP.\n\n============================================================\n5. POPULATE\n============================================================\n\nMount the image through a temporary loop device/mountpoint.\n\nCreate exactly:\n\n/conf/\n\nCopy the authoritative config to:\n\n/conf/config.xml\n\nDo not modify its contents.\n\nNo other configuration is required on the FAT32 image.\n\n============================================================\n6. VERIFY CONTENT\n============================================================\n\nCalculate SHA256 of:\n\nsource config.xml\n\nand:\n\nFAT32 /conf/config.xml\n\nRequired:\n\nIMPORT_CONFIG_SHA256=\nSOURCE_CONFIG_SHA256=\n\nIMPORT_CONFIG_HASH_MATCH=PASS\n\nParse the copied XML again without printing secrets.\n\nRequired:\n\nIMPORT_CONFIG_XML_VALID=PASS\nIMPORT_CONFIG_WAN_ONLY_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n7. VERIFY FILESYSTEM\n============================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nFILESYSTEM=FAT32\nLABEL=OPNSENSECFG\n\nRequired path:\n\n/conf/config.xml\n\nReturn:\n\nIMPORT_MEDIA_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n8. CLEAN UNMOUNT\n============================================================\n\nsync\n\nUnmount the FAT32 image cleanly.\n\nDetach loop device.\n\nVerify:\n\nIMPORT_IMAGE_MOUNTED=NO\nLOOP_DEVICE_ATTACHED=NO\n\n============================================================\n9. IMAGE HASH\n============================================================\n\nCalculate:\n\nIMPORT_IMAGE_SHA256=\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/opnsense/opnsense-config-import-fat32.img.sha256\n\n============================================================\n10. DO NOT INSTALL YET\n============================================================\n\nDo NOT:\n\nenable Rescue\nreboot OPNsense\nerase OPNsense\nattach/write the image to an unknown disk\nstart installer\nmodify Hetzner resources\n\nThe next task will determine the safe mechanism for presenting this FAT32\nimage to the OPNsense Configuration Importer.\n\n============================================================\nFINAL\n============================================================\n\nSOURCE_CONFIG=\nSOURCE_CONFIG_SHA256=\nSOURCE_CONFIG_WAN_ONLY_GATE=\n\nIMPORT_IMAGE=/opt/worm/artifacts/opnsense/opnsense-config-import-fat32.img\nIMPORT_IMAGE_SHA256=\n\nIMPORT_FILESYSTEM=FAT32\nIMPORT_LABEL=OPNSENSECFG\nIMPORT_CONFIG_PATH=/conf/config.xml\n\nIMPORT_CONFIG_SHA256=\nIMPORT_CONFIG_HASH_MATCH=\nIMPORT_CONFIG_XML_VALID=\nIMPORT_CONFIG_WAN_ONLY_GATE=\n\nIMPORT_TARGET_TYPE=REGULAR_FILE\nPHYSICAL_DISKS_MODIFIED=NO\n\nIMPORT_MEDIA_GATE=\n\nREINSTALL_STARTED=NO\nOPNSENSE_REBOOTED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE=Determine how to present FAT32 config media to OPNsense Full Image importer"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1213:{"session_id":"01a08abd-a56a-7773-9aa9-ff51183b9712","ts":1789056290,"text":"LEVEL PRO — OPNsense FRESH INSTALL WITH VERIFIED CONFIG IMPORT\n\nMETHOD:\nIDENTITY -> BACKUP -> INSTALL MEDIA -> CONFIG IMPORT -> INSTALL -> BOOT -> WAN TEST -> GOLDEN BACKUP\n\nAUTHORIZED_DESTRUCTIVE_CHANGE=YES\n\nTARGET:\nworm-opnsense\nPUBLIC_IPV4=2.28.34.27\n\nVERIFIED IMPORT MEDIA:\n/opt/worm/artifacts/opnsense/opnsense-config-import-fat32.img\n\nVERIFIED CONFIG SHA256:\n56bf1a564ba7273fad4fb687890dca5d1c9ed168af50967d853207ffe0a8cc55\n\nTARGET CONFIGURATION:\n\nASSIGNED_INTERFACE_COUNT=1\nWAN=vtnet0\n\nvtnet1=NONE\nLAN=NONE\nOPT=NONE\nPRIVATE=NONE\nWG=NONE\n\n============================================================\n1. TARGET IDENTITY GATE\n============================================================\n\nUsing existing authorized Hetzner API credentials verify:\n\nSERVER_NAME=worm-opnsense\nPRIMARY_IPV4=2.28.34.27\nSERVER_ID=\nSTATUS=\n\nRequired:\n\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE=PASS\n\nImmediately STOP on ambiguity.\n\n============================================================\n2. FINAL BACKUP\n============================================================\n\nBefore destructive installation preserve:\n\n- current working OPNsense config.xml\n- verified WAN-only config.xml\n- FAT32 importer image\n\nStore copies outside the OPNsense VPS/system disk.\n\nCalculate and verify SHA256.\n\nRequired:\n\nPREINSTALL_BACKUP_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n3. DETERMINE IMPORT-MEDIA DELIVERY METHOD\n============================================================\n\nDetermine the REAL supported mechanism available in this Hetzner\nenvironment for presenting the verified FAT32 media to the OPNsense Full\nImage Configuration Importer.\n\nPossible result classifications:\n\nATTACHABLE_VOLUME\nVIRTUAL_MEDIA\nRESCUE_LOOP_DEVICE_VISIBLE_TO_INSTALLER\nINSTALL_ENVIRONMENT_STAGING\nOTHER_SUPPORTED_METHOD\nNOT_AVAILABLE\n\nReturn:\n\nIMPORT_MEDIA_DELIVERY_METHOD=\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nDo not assume that the local .img file is visible to the OPNsense VPS.\n\nDo not create fictitious Hetzner API capabilities.\n\nIf the Configuration Importer cannot actually access this media:\n\nSTOP before erasing OPNsense.\n\nReturn:\n\nCONFIG_IMPORT_MEDIA_ACCESS_GATE=FAIL\n\n============================================================\n4. VERIFY OPNsense INSTALL IMAGE\n============================================================\n\nUse the approved OPNsense Full Image.\n\nVerify official checksum/signature.\n\nRequired:\n\nOPNSENSE_IMAGE_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n5. DESTRUCTIVE INSTALL GATE\n============================================================\n\nIdentify the OPNsense target disk.\n\nRequired simultaneously:\n\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE=PASS\nPREINSTALL_BACKUP_GATE=PASS\nCONFIG_IMPORT_MEDIA_ACCESS_GATE=PASS\nOPNSENSE_IMAGE_GATE=PASS\n\nTARGET_DISK=\nTARGET_DISK_IS_OPNSENSE=YES\n\nOnly then:\n\nDESTRUCTIVE_INSTALL_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n6. CONFIGURATION IMPORTER\n============================================================\n\nBoot the OPNsense Full Image with the configuration media available.\n\nInvoke Configuration Importer.\n\nImporter must find:\n\n/conf/config.xml\n\nVerify imported configuration:\n\nASSIGNED_INTERFACE_COUNT=1\nWAN=vtnet0\n\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=NO\nLAN_ASSIGNED=NO\nOPT_ASSIGNED=NO\nPRIVATE_ASSIGNED=NO\n\nRequired:\n\nCONFIG_IMPORTER_GATE=PASS\n\nIf the installer proposes automatic LAN assignment:\n\nSTOP.\n\n============================================================\n7. FRESH INSTALL\n============================================================\n\nInstall OPNsense only to the verified target system disk.\n\nDo not modify Antani.\n\nDo not modify Hetzner Network/vSwitch.\n\nRequired:\n\nFRESH_INSTALL_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n8. INSTALLED CONFIG VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nBefore normal production boot verify installed:\n\n/conf/config.xml\n\nSHA256 must equal:\n\n56bf1a564ba7273fad4fb687890dca5d1c9ed168af50967d853207ffe0a8cc55\n\nRequired:\n\nINSTALLED_CONFIG_HASH_MATCH=PASS\n\nParse again:\n\nWAN=vtnet0\nASSIGNED_INTERFACE_COUNT=1\n\nvtnet1=NONE\nLAN=NONE\nOPT=NONE\nPRIVATE=NONE\n\nRequired:\n\nINSTALLED_WAN_ONLY_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n9. NORMAL BOOT\n============================================================\n\nRemove installer/import media from boot path.\n\nBoot installed OPNsense normally.\n\nRequired:\n\nNORMAL_BOOT_REACHED=YES\nRESCUE_MODE=NO\n\n============================================================\n10. REAL WAN TEST\n============================================================\n\nTest externally:\n\n2.28.34.27:443\n\nRequired:\n\nWAN_TCP443=OPEN\n\nTest:\n\nhttps://2.28.34.27/\n\nAccept OPNsense TLS/application response.\n\nRequired:\n\nWAN_WEBGUI_TRANSPORT_GATE=PASS\n\nThen verify from authorized admin source:\n\nWAN_WEBGUI_ADMIN_GATE=PASS\n\nWAN SSH must remain closed.\n\nWAN_SSH_EXPOSED=NO\n\n============================================================\n11. RUNTIME WAN-ONLY GATE\n============================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nWAN_INTERFACE=vtnet0\nASSIGNED_INTERFACE_COUNT=1\n\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=NO\nLAN_ASSIGNED=NO\nOPT_ASSIGNED=NO\nPRIVATE_ASSIGNED=NO\n\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_OWNER=WAN\n\nRequired:\n\nRUNTIME_WAN_ONLY_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n12. GOLDEN BACKUP\n============================================================\n\nONLY after:\n\nWAN_TCP443=OPEN\nWAN_WEBGUI_TRANSPORT_GATE=PASS\nWAN_WEBGUI_ADMIN_GATE=PASS\nRUNTIME_WAN_ONLY_GATE=PASS\n\ncreate a NEW post-install backup of live:\n\n/conf/config.xml\n\nStore outside the OPNsense VPS.\n\nCalculate SHA256 and verify.\n\nBASELINE_NAME=OPNSENSE_FRESH_WAN_ONLY_GOLDEN\n\nRequired:\n\nPOSTINSTALL_GOLDEN_BACKUP=PASS\nGOLDEN_BACKUP_HASH_MATCH=PASS\n\n============================================================\n13. FINAL\n============================================================\n\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE=\nPREINSTALL_BACKUP_GATE=\n\nIMPORT_MEDIA_DELIVERY_METHOD=\nCONFIG_IMPORT_MEDIA_ACCESS_GATE=\n\nOPNSENSE_IMAGE_GATE=\nDESTRUCTIVE_INSTALL_GATE=\n\nCONFIG_IMPORTER_GATE=\nFRESH_INSTALL_GATE=\nINSTALLED_CONFIG_HASH_MATCH=\n\nNORMAL_BOOT_REACHED=\n\nWAN_TCP443=\nWAN_WEBGUI_TRANSPORT_GATE=\nWAN_WEBGUI_ADMIN_GATE=\nWAN_SSH_EXPOSED=\n\nASSIGNED_INTERFACE_COUNT=\nWAN_INTERFACE=\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=\nLAN_ASSIGNED=\nOPT_ASSIGNED=\nPRIVATE_ASSIGNED=\n\nRUNTIME_WAN_ONLY_GATE=\n\nPOSTINSTALL_GOLDEN_BACKUP=\nGOLDEN_BACKUP_HASH_MATCH=\n\nOPNSENSE_FRESH_WAN_ONLY_GATE=\n\nANTANI_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_NETWORK_CHANGED=NO\nVSWITCH_CHANGED=NO\nWG_CHANGED=NO\nSMTP_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE="}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1214:{"session_id":"01a08abd-a56a-7773-9aa9-ff51183b9712","ts":1789056465,"text":"LEVEL PRO — OPNsense CONFIG IMPORT VOLUME DELIVERY\n\nMETHOD:\nAUDIT -> CREATE -> VERIFY -> STOP\n\nAUTHORIZED:\nCreate ONE temporary dedicated Hetzner Volume for OPNsense configuration\nimport media, but ONLY if the Hetzner platform supports attaching it to\nworm-opnsense in a form visible to the OPNsense Full ISO environment.\n\nDO NOT reinstall yet.\nDO NOT erase OPNsense.\nDO NOT reboot yet.\n\nTARGET:\nworm-opnsense\nWAN=2.28.34.27\n\nSOURCE IMAGE:\n/opt/worm/artifacts/opnsense/opnsense-config-import-fat32.img\n\nSOURCE CONFIG SHA256:\n56bf1a564ba7273fad4fb687890dca5d1c9ed168af50967d853207ffe0a8cc55\n\n============================================================\n1. VERIFY HETZNER CAPABILITY\n============================================================\n\nUsing existing authorized Hetzner API and available provider metadata,\ndetermine whether a Hetzner Volume attached to worm-opnsense:\n\n- appears as an additional block device\n- remains visible while booted from the OPNsense Full ISO\n- can contain a raw FAT32 filesystem\n- can be selected/read by OPNsense Configuration Importer\n\nReturn:\n\nHETZNER_VOLUME_ATTACH_SUPPORTED=\nVOLUME_VISIBLE_FROM_ISO_BOOT=\nRAW_FAT32_VOLUME_SUPPORTED=\nOPNSENSE_IMPORTER_CAN_READ_VOLUME=\n\nIf any required capability cannot be proven:\n\nSTOP.\n\nDo NOT create the Volume.\n\n============================================================\n2. CREATE TEMPORARY VOLUME\n============================================================\n\nOnly if capability gate PASS:\n\ncreate ONE smallest suitable temporary Hetzner Volume.\n\nName:\n\nopnsense-config-import\n\nAttach ONLY to:\n\nworm-opnsense\n\nDo not format automatically using provider filesystem provisioning.\n\nReturn:\n\nCONFIG_VOLUME_ID=\nCONFIG_VOLUME_DEVICE=\n\nRequired:\n\nCONFIG_VOLUME_ATTACHED=YES\n\n============================================================\n3. IDENTITY SAFETY\n============================================================\n\nProve the attached device is the NEW temporary Volume.\n\nRecord:\n\nDEVICE=\nSIZE=\nSERIAL=\nVOLUME_ID=\n\nRequired:\n\nCONFIG_VOLUME_IDENTITY_GATE=PASS\n\nNever use the OPNsense system disk.\n\n============================================================\n4. WRITE FAT32 IMAGE\n============================================================\n\nWrite the VERIFIED FAT32 image byte-for-byte to ONLY the temporary\nconfiguration Volume.\n\nSource:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/opnsense/opnsense-config-import-fat32.img\n\nDestination:\n\nverified CONFIG_VOLUME_DEVICE\n\nBefore writing require:\n\nCONFIG_VOLUME_IDENTITY_GATE=PASS\n\nThen write and sync.\n\n============================================================\n5. READ-BACK VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nRead the Volume back.\n\nVerify:\n\nFILESYSTEM=FAT32\nLABEL=OPNSENSECFG\nPATH=/conf/config.xml\n\nCalculate config SHA256.\n\nRequired:\n\nCONFIG_SHA256=\n56bf1a564ba7273fad4fb687890dca5d1c9ed168af50967d853207ffe0a8cc55\n\nCONFIG_HASH_MATCH=PASS\n\nParse sanitized XML.\n\nRequired:\n\nASSIGNED_INTERFACE_COUNT=1\nWAN_INTERFACE=vtnet0\n\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=NO\nLAN_ASSIGNED=NO\nOPT_ASSIGNED=NO\nPRIVATE_ASSIGNED=NO\n\nCONFIG_VOLUME_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n6. STOP BEFORE REINSTALL\n============================================================\n\nDo NOT:\n\nboot ISO\nstart Configuration Importer\nerase system disk\ninstall OPNsense\nreboot\n\nThis stage ends when the config Volume is attached and verified.\n\nFINAL:\n\nHETZNER_VOLUME_ATTACH_SUPPORTED=\nVOLUME_VISIBLE_FROM_ISO_BOOT=\nRAW_FAT32_VOLUME_SUPPORTED=\nOPNSENSE_IMPORTER_CAN_READ_VOLUME=\n\nCONFIG_VOLUME_ID=\nCONFIG_VOLUME_DEVICE=\nCONFIG_VOLUME_ATTACHED=\nCONFIG_VOLUME_IDENTITY_GATE=\n\nFILESYSTEM=\nCONFIG_HASH_MATCH=\nASSIGNED_INTERFACE_COUNT=\nWAN_INTERFACE=\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=\nLAN_ASSIGNED=\n\nCONFIG_VOLUME_GATE=\n\nREINSTALL_STARTED=NO\nSYSTEM_DISK_MODIFIED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE=Boot OPNsense Full ISO and run Configuration Importer"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1215:{"session_id":"01a08abd-a56a-7773-9aa9-ff51183b9712","ts":1789056540,"text":"LEVEL PRO — PROVE HETZNER VOLUME AS OPNsense IMPORT MEDIA\n\nMETHOD:\nCREATE -> ATTACH -> ISO BOOT -> DISCOVER -> VERIFY -> STOP\n\nAUTHORIZED CHANGES:\n\n- create one temporary Hetzner Volume\n- attach it ONLY to worm-opnsense\n- write verified FAT32 import media to that Volume\n- boot worm-opnsense temporarily from OPNsense Full ISO\n- reboot worm-opnsense as required for this test\n\nNOT AUTHORIZED:\n\n- OPNsense installation\n- system disk formatting\n- partition changes\n- installer execution\n- config import into system disk\n- Antani changes\n- Hetzner Network/vSwitch changes\n\nTARGET:\n\nSERVER=worm-opnsense\nWAN=2.28.34.27\n\nISO:\nOPNsense-25.7-dvd-amd64.iso\n\nSOURCE FAT32 IMAGE:\n/opt/worm/artifacts/opnsense/opnsense-config-import-fat32.img\n\nCONFIG SHA256:\n56bf1a564ba7273fad4fb687890dca5d1c9ed168af50967d853207ffe0a8cc55\n\n============================================================\n1. TARGET IDENTITY\n============================================================\n\nVia Hetzner API verify:\n\nSERVER_ID=\nSERVER_NAME=worm-opnsense\nPRIMARY_IPV4=2.28.34.27\n\nRequired:\n\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n2. CREATE CONFIG VOLUME\n============================================================\n\nCreate the smallest suitable temporary Hetzner Volume:\n\nNAME=opnsense-config-import\n\nAttach ONLY to worm-opnsense.\n\nDo NOT request automatic filesystem formatting.\n\nReturn:\n\nCONFIG_VOLUME_ID=\nCONFIG_VOLUME_SIZE=\nCONFIG_VOLUME_ATTACHED=\n\n============================================================\n3. DISCOVER DEVICE IN CURRENT OS\n============================================================\n\nBefore writing anything, discover the newly attached device.\n\nMatch using Hetzner Volume identity/serial.\n\nReturn:\n\nCONFIG_VOLUME_DEVICE=\nCONFIG_VOLUME_SERIAL=\n\nRequired:\n\nCONFIG_VOLUME_IDENTITY_GATE=PASS\n\nExplicitly identify separately:\n\nOPNSENSE_SYSTEM_DISK=\n\nRequired:\n\nCONFIG_VOLUME_DEVICE != OPNSENSE_SYSTEM_DISK\n\n============================================================\n4. WRITE VERIFIED FAT32 MEDIA\n============================================================\n\nONLY after identity gate PASS:\n\nwrite byte-for-byte:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/opnsense/opnsense-config-import-fat32.img\n\nto:\n\nCONFIG_VOLUME_DEVICE\n\nsync.\n\nDo not write to any other block device.\n\n============================================================\n5. READ-BACK VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nMount/read the configuration Volume.\n\nRequired:\n\nFILESYSTEM=FAT32\nLABEL=OPNSENSECFG\nCONFIG_PATH=/conf/config.xml\n\nCalculate SHA256 of config.xml.\n\nRequired:\n\nCONFIG_SHA256=\n56bf1a564ba7273fad4fb687890dca5d1c9ed168af50967d853207ffe0a8cc55\n\nCONFIG_HASH_MATCH=PASS\n\nVerify sanitized:\n\nASSIGNED_INTERFACE_COUNT=1\nWAN=vtnet0\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=NO\nLAN_ASSIGNED=NO\n\nUnmount cleanly.\n\n============================================================\n6. BOOT FULL ISO\n============================================================\n\nUsing authorized Hetzner ISO mechanism:\n\nmount/select:\n\nOPNsense-25.7-dvd-amd64.iso\n\nReboot ONLY worm-opnsense into the Full ISO.\n\nDO NOT START INSTALLER.\n\nRequired:\n\nOPNSENSE_FULL_ISO_BOOTED=YES\n\n============================================================\n7. FREEBSD DEVICE DISCOVERY\n============================================================\n\nFrom OPNsense Full ISO / Live environment perform READ-ONLY device\ndiscovery.\n\nUse appropriate FreeBSD tools such as:\n\ncamcontrol devlist\ngeom disk list\ngpart show\nmount\nfstyp\n\nDo NOT partition or format anything.\n\nIdentify:\n\nSYSTEM_DISK_DEVICE=\nISO_DEVICE=\nCONFIG_VOLUME_DEVICE_FROM_ISO=\n\nMatch the configuration device using:\n\nsize\nprovider identity\nserial/Volume ID where available\nFAT filesystem\nlabel OPNSENSECFG\n\nRequired:\n\nCONFIG_VOLUME_VISIBLE_FROM_ISO=YES\n\n============================================================\n8. READ IMPORT MEDIA FROM ISO ENVIRONMENT\n============================================================\n\nMount ONLY the proven FAT32 config Volume read-only.\n\nVerify:\n\n/conf/config.xml\n\nCalculate SHA256.\n\nRequired:\n\nISO_CONFIG_SHA256=\n56bf1a564ba7273fad4fb687890dca5d1c9ed168af50967d853207ffe0a8cc55\n\nISO_CONFIG_HASH_MATCH=PASS\n\nRequired:\n\nFAT32_READABLE_FROM_OPNSENSE_ISO=PASS\n\nUnmount.\n\n============================================================\n9. IMPORTER DISCOVERY TEST\n============================================================\n\nDetermine whether OPNsense Configuration Importer enumerates/detects\nthis FAT32 device as a valid configuration source.\n\nDO NOT proceed into installation.\n\nDo not write to system disk.\n\nReturn:\n\nIMPORTER_DEVICE_DETECTED=\nIMPORTER_CONFIG_FOUND=\n\nIf importer can select/read /conf/config.xml:\n\nOPNSENSE_IMPORTER_VOLUME_GATE=PASS\n\nOtherwise:\n\nOPNSENSE_IMPORTER_VOLUME_GATE=FAIL\n\n============================================================\n10. STOP\n============================================================\n\nSTOP after importer/media verification.\n\nDO NOT:\n\nrun installer\nerase system disk\ninstall OPNsense\nwrite imported config to system disk\n\nSYSTEM_DISK_MODIFIED=NO\nINSTALL_STARTED=NO\n\n============================================================\n11. RETURN TO NORMAL BOOT\n============================================================\n\nExit Live/ISO environment safely.\n\nDetach ISO from boot path.\n\nReboot installed OPNsense normally.\n\nDo NOT detach/delete the config Volume yet if:\n\nOPNSENSE_IMPORTER_VOLUME_GATE=PASS\n\nVerify existing installation returns:\n\nWAN_TCP443=OPEN\n\n============================================================\n12. FINAL\n============================================================\n\nCONFIG_VOLUME_ID=\nCONFIG_VOLUME_DEVICE=\n\nCONFIG_VOLUME_IDENTITY_GATE=\nCONFIG_HASH_MATCH=\n\nOPNSENSE_FULL_ISO_BOOTED=\n\nCONFIG_VOLUME_VISIBLE_FROM_ISO=\nFAT32_READABLE_FROM_OPNSENSE_ISO=\n\nIMPORTER_DEVICE_DETECTED=\nIMPORTER_CONFIG_FOUND=\nOPNSENSE_IMPORTER_VOLUME_GATE=\n\nSYSTEM_DISK_MODIFIED=NO\nINSTALL_STARTED=NO\n\nNORMAL_BOOT_RESTORED=\nWAN_TCP443=\n\nBLOCKERS=\n\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE=\nIf OPNSENSE_IMPORTER_VOLUME_GATE=PASS:\nperform fresh install using the already verified importer Volume."}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1216:{"session_id":"01a08abd-a56a-7773-9aa9-ff51183b9712","ts":1789057166,"text":"LEVEL PRO — OPNsense NATIVE IMPORTER FRESH REINSTALL\nEXISTING DISK -> LIVE TEST -> INSTALL -> GOLDEN\n\nMETHOD:\nIDENTITY -> BACKUP -> ISO -> IMPORT -> LIVE TEST -> DESTRUCTIVE GATE\n-> INSTALL -> WAN TEST -> GOLDEN BACKUP\n\nAUTHORIZED_DESTRUCTIVE_CHANGE=YES\nBUT ONLY AFTER LIVE_WAN_ONLY_GATE=PASS\n\nTARGET:\n\nSERVER=worm-opnsense\nPUBLIC_IPV4=2.28.34.27\n\nFINAL CONFIG:\n\nvtnet0 = WAN ONLY\n\nvtnet1 = UNASSIGNED\nLAN = NONE\nOPT = NONE\nPRIVATE = NONE\nWG = NONE\n\nWEBGUI=https:443\n\n============================================================\n0. ABSOLUTE SAFETY\n============================================================\n\nDO NOT modify Antani.\nDO NOT modify Hetzner Network/vSwitch.\nDO NOT modify SMTP.\nDO NOT modify WireGuard.\nDO NOT erase the OPNsense disk before LIVE_WAN_ONLY_GATE=PASS.\n\nUse the existing verified WAN-only config.xml.\n\nDo NOT synthesize another config.\n\n============================================================\n1. TARGET IDENTITY\n============================================================\n\nUsing existing authorized Hetzner API verify:\n\nSERVER_NAME=worm-opnsense\nPRIMARY_IPV4=2.28.34.27\nSERVER_ID=\nSTATUS=\n\nRequired:\n\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n2. PRESERVE CONFIG BEFORE ISO BOOT\n============================================================\n\nPreserve externally the already verified WAN-only config.xml.\n\nExpected SHA256:\n\n56bf1a564ba7273fad4fb687890dca5d1c9ed168af50967d853207ffe0a8cc55\n\nVerify:\n\nWAN=vtnet0\nASSIGNED_INTERFACE_COUNT=1\n\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=NO\nLAN_ASSIGNED=NO\nOPT_ASSIGNED=NO\nPRIVATE_ASSIGNED=NO\n\nCreate at least one verified copy outside the OPNsense system disk.\n\nRequired:\n\nPREINSTALL_CONFIG_BACKUP=PASS\nPREINSTALL_CONFIG_HASH_MATCH=PASS\n\n============================================================\n3. BOOT OFFICIAL FULL ISO\n============================================================\n\nUse the available official Full ISO:\n\nOPNsense-25.7-dvd-amd64.iso\n\nVerify target identity again.\n\nAttach/select ISO using authorized Hetzner mechanism.\n\nReboot ONLY worm-opnsense into the ISO.\n\nRequired:\n\nFULL_ISO_BOOTED=YES\n\nDO NOT START INSTALLER YET.\n\n============================================================\n4. CONFIGURATION IMPORTER\n============================================================\n\nInvoke the native OPNsense Configuration Importer.\n\nDiscover the EXISTING installed OPNsense disk.\n\nImporter source must be the existing OPNsense installation containing:\n\n/conf/config.xml\n\nDo NOT use:\n\nAntani disk\nunknown disk\nnew empty FAT volume\ngenerated config\n\nRequired:\n\nEXISTING_OPNSENSE_DISK_FOUND=YES\nEXISTING_CONFIG_FOUND=YES\n\nBefore import calculate/read the config SHA256 if possible.\n\nRequired:\n\nEXISTING_CONFIG_SHA256=\n56bf1a564ba7273fad4fb687890dca5d1c9ed168af50967d853207ffe0a8cc55\n\nIMPORT_SOURCE_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n5. IMPORT INTO LIVE ENVIRONMENT\n============================================================\n\nImport the existing configuration using Configuration Importer.\n\nThis step must NOT erase the existing installation.\n\nVerify imported semantics:\n\nASSIGNED_INTERFACE_COUNT=1\n\nWAN_INTERFACE=vtnet0\n\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=NO\nLAN_ASSIGNED=NO\nOPT_ASSIGNED=NO\nPRIVATE_ASSIGNED=NO\nWG_INTERFACE_ASSIGNED=NO\n\nRequired:\n\nCONFIG_IMPORT_GATE=PASS\nLIVE_STRICT_WAN_ONLY_GATE=PASS\n\nIf OPNsense introduces a LAN automatically:\n\nSTOP.\n\nINSTALL_STARTED=NO\n\n============================================================\n6. LIVE ENVIRONMENT WAN TEST\n============================================================\n\nBoot/continue into OPNsense Live Environment with imported config.\n\nVerify runtime:\n\nvtnet0=UP\n\nvtnet1 has NO OPNsense assignment.\n\nDefault route belongs to WAN.\n\nTest externally:\n\n2.28.34.27:443\n\nRequired:\n\nLIVE_WAN_TCP443=OPEN\n\nVerify HTTPS application response:\n\nhttps://2.28.34.27/\n\nAccept appropriate OPNsense application/TLS response.\n\nThen verify from authorized admin source.\n\nRequired:\n\nLIVE_WEBGUI_TRANSPORT_GATE=PASS\nLIVE_WEBGUI_ADMIN_GATE=PASS\n\nWAN SSH must remain closed.\n\nRequired:\n\nLIVE_WAN_SSH_EXPOSED=NO\n\n============================================================\n7. DESTRUCTIVE INSTALL GATE\n============================================================\n\nONLY proceed if ALL are PASS:\n\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE\nPREINSTALL_CONFIG_BACKUP\nPREINSTALL_CONFIG_HASH_MATCH\nIMPORT_SOURCE_GATE\nCONFIG_IMPORT_GATE\nLIVE_STRICT_WAN_ONLY_GATE\nLIVE_WEBGUI_TRANSPORT_GATE\nLIVE_WEBGUI_ADMIN_GATE\n\nThen:\n\nLIVE_WAN_ONLY_GATE=PASS\nDESTRUCTIVE_INSTALL_GATE=PASS\n\nOtherwise:\n\nSTOP.\n\nDO NOT FORMAT SYSTEM DISK.\n\n============================================================\n8. IDENTIFY INSTALL TARGET\n============================================================\n\nImmediately before installation identify:\n\nISO_DEVICE=\nOPNSENSE_SYSTEM_DISK=\n\nProve:\n\nTARGET_DISK_IS_EXISTING_OPNSENSE_DISK=YES\n\nRequired:\n\nTARGET_DISK_IDENTITY_GATE=PASS\n\nNo other disk may be selected.\n\n============================================================\n9. FRESH INSTALL\n============================================================\n\nRun native OPNsense Installer.\n\nInstall ONLY onto:\n\nOPNSENSE_SYSTEM_DISK\n\nPreserve/import the configuration already loaded through the supported\nOPNsense installation workflow.\n\nDo NOT perform manual interface assignment.\n\nDo NOT create LAN.\n\nRequired:\n\nFRESH_INSTALL_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n10. PRE-FIRST-BOOT VERIFY\n============================================================\n\nBefore normal production boot verify installed configuration.\n\nRequired semantics:\n\nWAN=vtnet0\nASSIGNED_INTERFACE_COUNT=1\n\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=NO\nLAN_ASSIGNED=NO\nOPT_ASSIGNED=NO\nPRIVATE_ASSIGNED=NO\n\nWEBGUI=https:443\n\nRequired:\n\nINSTALLED_STRICT_WAN_ONLY_GATE=PASS\n\nIf installed config can be hashed safely:\n\nINSTALLED_CONFIG_SHA256=\n\nCompare against source where byte-for-byte preservation is expected.\n\n============================================================\n11. NORMAL BOOT\n============================================================\n\nDetach ISO from boot path.\n\nBoot installed OPNsense.\n\nRequired:\n\nNORMAL_BOOT_REACHED=YES\nLIVE_ISO_MODE=NO\n\n============================================================\n12. POST-INSTALL WAN TEST\n============================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nWAN_INTERFACE=vtnet0\nWAN_IP=2.28.34.27\nDEFAULT_ROUTE_OWNER=WAN\n\nASSIGNED_INTERFACE_COUNT=1\n\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=NO\nLAN_ASSIGNED=NO\nOPT_ASSIGNED=NO\nPRIVATE_ASSIGNED=NO\n\nTest externally:\n\n2.28.34.27:443\n\nRequired:\n\nPOSTINSTALL_WAN_TCP443=OPEN\nPOSTINSTALL_WEBGUI_TRANSPORT_GATE=PASS\n\nVerify actual WebGUI login from authorized admin source.\n\nRequired:\n\nPOSTINSTALL_WEBGUI_ADMIN_GATE=PASS\n\nVerify:\n\nWAN_SSH_EXPOSED=NO\n\n============================================================\n13. STABILITY TEST\n============================================================\n\nAfter initial success, repeat:\n\nWAN route\nWAN :443\nWebGUI\ninterface assignment count\n\nRequired:\n\nPOSTINSTALL_STABILITY_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n14. GOLDEN BACKUP\n============================================================\n\nONLY after all post-install gates PASS:\n\nbackup the LIVE installed:\n\n/conf/config.xml\n\nto protected storage outside worm-opnsense.\n\nName baseline:\n\nOPNSENSE_FRESH_WAN_ONLY_GOLDEN\n\nCalculate SHA256 and verify backup.\n\nRequired:\n\nGOLDEN_BACKUP_CREATED=YES\nGOLDEN_BACKUP_HASH_MATCH=PASS\nGOLDEN_BASELINE_GATE=PASS\n\n============================================================\n15. FINAL\n============================================================\n\nTARGET_IDENTITY_GATE=\n\nPREINSTALL_CONFIG_BACKUP=\nPREINSTALL_CONFIG_HASH_MATCH=\n\nFULL_ISO_BOOTED=\n\nEXISTING_OPNSENSE_DISK_FOUND=\nEXISTING_CONFIG_FOUND=\nIMPORT_SOURCE_GATE=\n\nCONFIG_IMPORT_GATE=\nLIVE_STRICT_WAN_ONLY_GATE=\n\nLIVE_WAN_TCP443=\nLIVE_WEBGUI_TRANSPORT_GATE=\nLIVE_WEBGUI_ADMIN_GATE=\nLIVE_WAN_SSH_EXPOSED=\n\nLIVE_WAN_ONLY_GATE=\nDESTRUCTIVE_INSTALL_GATE=\n\nTARGET_DISK_IDENTITY_GATE=\nFRESH_INSTALL_GATE=\n\nNORMAL_BOOT_REACHED=\n\nWAN_INTERFACE=\nWAN_IP=\nASSIGNED_INTERFACE_COUNT=\n\nVTNET1_ASSIGNED=\nLAN_ASSIGNED=\nOPT_ASSIGNED=\nPRIVATE_ASSIGNED=\n\nPOSTINSTALL_WAN_TCP443=\nPOSTINSTALL_WEBGUI_TRANSPORT_GATE=\nPOSTINSTALL_WEBGUI_ADMIN_GATE=\nPOSTINSTALL_STABILITY_GATE=\n\nGOLDEN_BACKUP_CREATED=\nGOLDEN_BACKUP_HASH_MATCH=\nGOLDEN_BASELINE_GATE=\n\nOPNSENSE_FRESH_WAN_ONLY_GATE=\n\nANTANI_CHANGED=NO\nHETZNER_NETWORK_CHANGED=NO\nVSWITCH_CHANGED=NO\nWG_CHANGED=NO\nSMTP_CHANGED=NO\n\nBLOCKERS=\nNEXT_MINIMAL_CHANGE=\n\nWrite report:\n\n/opt/worm/artifacts/reports/OPNSENSE-NATIVE-IMPORTER-FRESH-WAN-ONLY.md"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:1230:{"session_id":"01a0a1a4-46d1-7b43-b876-0feab5383bbe","ts":1789421689,"text":"TASK: complete PATCH-005 Worm App Store integration and produce a signed Worm OS update/release for Pixel 10 (frankel).\n\nENVIRONMENT\n\nGrapheneOS / Worm OS tree:\n  /opt/worm/grapheneos\n\nWorm patch repository:\n  /opt/worm/wormos/repo\n\nAndroid build output:\n  /opt/worm/build/out\n\nLogical build output symlink:\n  /opt/worm/grapheneos/worm-out -> ../build/out\n\nPrevious preserved output:\n  /opt/worm-old/build/out\n\nWorm Apps source:\n  /opt/worm/apps/AppStore\n\nWorm Apps repository source:\n  /opt/worm/apps-repo-src\n\nPublished Worm Apps repository:\n  /var/www/apps.coffee.pm\n\nRepository URL:\n  https://apps.coffee.pm\n\nWorm Apps repository signing keys:\n  /opt/worm-apps-keys/\n\nWorm OS release keys:\n  /opt/worm-release-keys/\n\nGrapheneOS release-key link:\n  /opt/worm/grapheneos/keys/frankel\n\nDEVICE:\n  frankel\n\nTARGET RELEASE:\n  cp2a\n\nBUILD VARIANT:\n  user\n\nFACTORY BUILD ID:\n  CP2A.260805.005\n\nNEW BUILD NUMBER:\n  2026091400\n\nFIXED BUILD_DATETIME:\n  1789407749\n\n\nIMPORTANT SAFETY RULES\n\n1. NEVER delete or regenerate:\n   /opt/worm-release-keys\n   /opt/worm-apps-keys\n\n2. NEVER rotate signing keys.\n\n3. NEVER delete:\n   /opt/worm/build/out\n   /opt/worm-old/build/out\n\n4. Do not run repo sync.\n\n5. Do not reset the GrapheneOS tree.\n\n6. Do not overwrite existing Worm patches.\n\n7. PATCH-005 must remain a separate patch.\n\n8. Before every destructive operation, abort instead of guessing.\n\n9. Preserve existing OTA / AVB identity so installed Worm OS devices can receive updates.\n\n10. Use the existing frankel release keys through:\n    /opt/worm/grapheneos/keys/frankel\n\n\nCURRENT PATCH-005 STATE\n\nWorm Apps APK is already built:\n\n  /opt/worm/apps/AppStore/app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release.apk\n\nIt has already replaced:\n\n  /opt/worm/grapheneos/external/AppStore/prebuilt/app-release.apk\n\nExpected SHA256 for both files:\n\n  ee9047b3fb286f91aa3956220507a92c4cc78f1fe5866935dc53e5f91061f3c3\n\nWorm Apps contains:\n\n  REPO_BASE_URL=https://apps.coffee.pm\n  REPO_KEY_VERSION=0\n\nRepository metadata is already generated and signed.\n\nHTTPS repository has already passed byte-identical verification against:\n\n  /opt/worm/apps-repo-src/apps/metadata.1.0.sjson\n\n\nPHASE 1 — AUDIT\n\nRun and print results:\n\ncd /opt/worm/grapheneos\n\ngit status --short\n\nreadlink -f keys/frankel\nreadlink -f worm-out\n\nsha256sum \\\n  external/AppStore/prebuilt/app-release.apk \\\n  /opt/worm/apps/AppStore/app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release.apk\n\ndf -h /opt/worm /\n\ntest -d /opt/worm/build/out\ntest -d /opt/worm-old/build/out\ntest -f /opt/worm/build/out/siso_config/main.star\ntest -f /opt/worm/build/out/siso_config/main/main.star\n\nDo not continue if the APK hashes differ or keys/frankel does not resolve under /opt/worm-release-keys.\n\n\nPHASE 2 — FIX SISO BOOTSTRAP SAFELY\n\nThe current blocker is:\n\n  failed to load @config//main.star:\n  open main.star: no such file or directory\n\nHowever these files exist:\n\n  /opt/worm/build/out/siso_config/main.star\n  /opt/worm/build/out/siso_config/main/main.star\n\nand:\n\n  /opt/worm/build/out/siso_config/main\n\nmust point to:\n\n  /opt/worm/grapheneos/build/soong/siso_config\n\nDo NOT blindly delete siso_config.\n\nFirst inspect the last SISO command line:\n\ngrep -h 'commandline' \\\n  /opt/worm/build/out/soong/siso*.INFO \\\n  2>/dev/null | tail -10\n\nAlso inspect:\n\nrealpath /opt/worm/build/out/siso_config\nrealpath /opt/worm/build/out/siso_config/main\nls -la /opt/worm/build/out/siso_config\ncat /opt/worm/build/out/siso_config/main.star\n\nDetermine exactly what value is passed to:\n\n  --config_repo_dir\n\nSISO expects @config//main.star to resolve relative to that directory.\n\nFix the path/layout rather than patching SISO itself.\n\nPreferred correct layout:\n\n  /opt/worm/build/out/siso_config/main.star\n  /opt/worm/build/out/siso_config/main -> /opt/worm/grapheneos/build/soong/siso_config\n\nOwnership:\n\n  wormbuild:wormbuild\n\nmain.star permissions:\n\n  0644\n\nIf current main.star is stale or malformed, compare with:\n\n  /opt/worm-old/build/out/siso_config/main.star\n\nDo not change hard-coded variables unless needed.\n\nAfter repair, perform a direct SISO dry test using the SAME flags/config_repo_dir discovered from the latest Soong log.\n\nDo not continue until SISO can load @config//main.star.\n\n\nPHASE 3 — INCREMENTAL BUILD\n\nUse the logical output path used by the original successful build:\n\ncd /opt/worm/grapheneos\n\nsudo -u wormbuild -H bash -lc '\nset -euo pipefail\n\ncd /opt/worm/grapheneos\n\nexport OUT_DIR=worm-out\nexport BUILD_NUMBER=2026091400\nexport BUILD_DATETIME=1789407749\n\nsource build/envsetup.sh\nsource vendor/google_devices/frankel/cmds-for-envsetup.sh\n\nlunch frankel cp2a user\n\necho \"=== WORM OS PATCH-005 BUILD ===\"\necho \"OUT_DIR=$OUT_DIR\"\necho \"REAL_OUT=$(readlink -f \"$OUT_DIR\")\"\necho \"BUILD_NUMBER=$BUILD_NUMBER\"\necho \"BUILD_DATETIME=$BUILD_DATETIME\"\necho \"BUILD_ID_frankel=$BUILD_ID_frankel\"\necho \"TARGET_PRODUCT=$TARGET_PRODUCT\"\necho \"TARGET_RELEASE=$TARGET_RELEASE\"\necho \"TARGET_BUILD_VARIANT=$TARGET_BUILD_VARIANT\"\n\nm -j\"$(nproc)\" target-files-package otatools-package\n'\n\nDo NOT use a new output directory.\n\nReuse /opt/worm/build/out.\n\n\nPHASE 4 — VERIFY NEW BUILD ARTIFACTS\n\nFind the newly generated target-files and real otatools archive.\n\nExpected target-files shape:\n\n  /opt/worm/build/out/target/product/frankel/obj/PACKAGING/target_files_intermediates/frankel-target_files.zip\n\nFor otatools, DO NOT select the tiny script/otatools_files zip.\n\nSelect the real archive matching:\n\n  */build/make/tools/otatools_package/*/gen/otatools.zip\n\nValidate it contains:\n\n  device/common/clear-factory-images-variables.sh\n\nExample validation:\n\nunzip -l \"$OTATOOLS\" | grep \\\n  'device/common/clear-factory-images-variables.sh'\n\n\nPHASE 5 — PREPARE RELEASE INPUT\n\ncd /opt/worm/grapheneos\n\nmkdir -p releases/2026091400\n\ncp -f \\\n  /opt/worm/build/out/target/product/frankel/obj/PACKAGING/target_files_intermediates/frankel-target_files.zip \\\n  releases/2026091400/frankel-target_files.zip\n\nCopy the validated real otatools archive to:\n\n  releases/2026091400/frankel-otatools.zip\n\nPrint:\n\nls -lh \\\n  releases/2026091400/frankel-target_files.zip \\\n  releases/2026091400/frankel-otatools.zip\n\n\nPHASE 6 — RELEASE SIGNING\n\nVerify before release:\n\nreadlink -f keys/frankel\n\nRequired files must exist:\n\n  releasekey.pk8\n  releasekey.x509.pem\n  avb.pem\n  avb_pkmd.bin\n\nDo not print key contents.\n\nThen run:\n\ncd /opt/worm/grapheneos\n\nscript/generate-release.sh frankel 2026091400\n\nUse the EXISTING Worm OS keys.\n\nDo not create new keys.\n\n\nPHASE 7 — VERIFY RELEASE\n\nExpected directory:\n\n  releases/2026091400/release-frankel-2026091400\n\nExpected outputs include:\n\n  frankel-target_files.zip\n  frankel-ota_update-2026091400.zip\n  frankel-img-2026091400.zip\n  frankel-factory-2026091400.zip\n  frankel-install-2026091400.zip\n\nVerify install package contains:\n\n  avb_pkmd.bin\n  vbmeta.img\n  boot.img\n  init_boot.img\n  vendor_boot.img\n  flash-all.sh\n  flash-all.bat\n\nAlso verify flash-all.sh contains:\n\n  fastboot erase avb_custom_key\n  fastboot flash avb_custom_key avb_pkmd.bin\n\nGenerate SHA256SUMS for all final release ZIP files.\n\n\nPHASE 8 — PATCH-005 VERIFY\n\nVerify again:\n\nsha256sum \\\n  /opt/worm/grapheneos/external/AppStore/prebuilt/app-release.apk \\\n  /opt/worm/apps/AppStore/app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release.apk\n\nVerify embedded repository:\n\nstrings from classes.dex must contain:\n\n  https://apps.coffee.pm/metadata.1.0.sjson\n  https://apps.coffee.pm/packages/\n\nVerify live repository:\n\ncurl -fsS https://apps.coffee.pm/metadata.1.0.sjson \\\n  -o /tmp/worm-metadata-live.sjson\n\ncmp \\\n  /opt/worm/apps-repo-src/apps/metadata.1.0.sjson \\\n  /tmp/worm-metadata-live.sjson\n\nVerify APK URL returns HTTP 200:\n\nhttps://apps.coffee.pm/packages/app.grapheneos.apps/36/base.apk\n\n\nPHASE 9 — FINAL REPORT\n\nPrint a compact report containing:\n\n- PATCH-005 status\n- App Store APK SHA256\n- Worm Apps repository URL\n- build number\n- target device\n- target release\n- target-files size + SHA256\n- OTA size + SHA256\n- install.zip size + SHA256\n- img.zip size + SHA256\n- factory.zip size + SHA256\n- release signing key directory resolved path\n- AVB custom key presence\n- disk free space\n\nDo not modify unrelated files.\n\nIf any step fails, STOP and show:\n- failing command\n- exit code\n- last 80 relevant log lines\n- exact paths involved\n\nDo not attempt broad automatic cleanup."}
