9BYGi-_y6HxNSoSwqFHwqy4ooafmRn2QV98vIKcjUq5sBgKo8FFChJgCCB8qVpPZa9b3IbDkbg1KB8o7asQyPO3rnpUxeA9jRiVZuG0WR_eYXznB55Lj-cw96RLfPUCmOl6mVtpLJFXeI9fhN8MlJHDJ6iifFuJdmIXWA5wTWbOhrRK6J0yIipDPBHRmbaP203cvjtr5gCTJE2fN_ibyIohQJFynYKceXIi8sItRRNOZ0VyxEYkNmjhrZNh8ylTRCSqddELijM7ylw9SyNv1cA83R85TyCeyKDZuoMYGcjq4YJWiGZ5Do3MALS2yb6Qya0RZ3B_VTlE0tCH7nf7m9XybEx0FJwwy_cdFyLeeRblEQCe-tllAm1B8VOjA-mGLKlKMkkAHNrc6IPxFP-xehroBWqRc-XU99a50_jAP3VTuzQkF_D5nCC8WQ5i29UAFG_KXd817QxZiRut2MYhFEn0laWPm37SXqgZfoZYRB806vKsVPECszasIfWY3sThDOisX-42Td8qy9SxNcf8PVRZu0u5UUg-V-ihTSzh5rUW0AzIHvrINngowPCAAeirsbQFUgA2ZU2WOTN1t-AD6gevcFcwpxk4pEcEvJkCpy2wDtVMIvvtZDvA_EYFfRgFBV4Z4_mR0FVYMH1RqSD1ZWAi6pHGddwwjo=","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07d19-2774-7f13-8196-1f548029d2a3"}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_0d4d71abca8c0b20016a9f0812335c87d2b1c632151844add8","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Mentre il build continua, preparo gli artefatti della patch con stato onesto: sorgente implementato e compilazione in corso; runtime device rimane pending finché non viene flashato/testato."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07d19-2774-7f13-8196-1f548029d2a3","create_time":1788807183.755166,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0d4d71abca8c0b20016a9f081331c887d2869c998557ecf1be","status":"completed","call_id":"call_slp5l45k9KG5ISqcGHf9B31Q","name":"apply_patch","input":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/00-SUMMARY.md\n+# PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1\n+\n+Status: PARTIAL.\n+\n+This patch adds a native Worm system WireGuard/fail-closed foundation in\n+the worm-os GrapheneOS tree. It is client/system source work only.\n+\n+Implemented:\n+\n+- New privileged product app: `WormSystemWireGuard`.\n+- Boot and package-replaced autostart receiver.\n+- `VpnService` fail-closed TUN establishment for IPv4 and IPv6.\n+- Always-on VPN lockdown request using Android `VpnManager`.\n+- Public production server parameters only.\n+- No WireGuard private key, PSK, SSH key, Hetzner token, or signing key.\n+\n+Not implemented in this V1:\n+\n+- Userspace/kernel WireGuard packet engine inside the system app.\n+- Device runtime validation after flashing.\n+- Handover/crash/boot leak tests on the real device.\n+\n+Server/network state was not modified.\n*** Add File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/01-ARCHITECTURE.md\n+# Architecture\n+\n+Relevant Android components found in the source tree:\n+\n+- `frameworks/base/core/java/android/net/VpnService.java`\n+- `frameworks/base/core/java/android/net/VpnManager.java`\n+- `frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Vpn.java`\n+- `frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/VpnManagerService.java`\n+- `packages/modules/NetworkStack`\n+- `system/netd`\n+\n+V1 implementation point:\n+\n+- `vendor/worm/WormSystemWireGuard`\n+\n+The V1 avoids framework/netd modifications and uses the existing Android\n+VPN and lockdown primitives. This keeps the implementation auditable and\n+preserves GrapheneOS security boundaries.\n+\n+State model:\n+\n+- `EARLY_BOOT` -> `BLOCKED`\n+- `NETWORK_AVAILABLE` -> `BLOCKED`\n+- `WG_STARTING` -> `BLOCKED`\n+- `WG_READY` -> pending backend implementation\n+- `WG_FAILURE` -> `BLOCKED`\n+- `NETWORK_CHANGE` -> `BLOCKED`\n*** Add File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/02-UPSTREAM-DIFF.md\n+# Upstream Diff\n+\n+Files added under Worm vendor ownership:\n+\n+- `vendor/worm/WormSystemWireGuard/Android.bp`\n+- `vendor/worm/WormSystemWireGuard/AndroidManifest.xml`\n+- `vendor/worm/WormSystemWireGuard/privapp-permissions-com.worm.systemwg.xml`\n+- `vendor/worm/WormSystemWireGuard/res/values/strings.xml`\n+- `vendor/worm/WormSystemWireGuard/res/values/worm_network.xml`\n+- `vendor/worm/WormSystemWireGuard/src/com/worm/systemwg/WormBootReceiver.java`\n+- `vendor/worm/WormSystemWireGuard/src/com/worm/systemwg/WormNetworkState.java`\n+- `vendor/worm/WormSystemWireGuard/src/com/worm/systemwg/WormSystemWireGuardService.java`\n+\n+Product integration:\n+\n+- `vendor/google_devices/frankel/frankel.mk` adds\n+  `WormSystemWireGuard` to `PRODUCT_PACKAGES`.\n+\n+No framework, netd, NetworkStack, SELinux, OPNsense, FireHOL, NAT, DNS,\n+routing, or server configuration was changed.\n*** Add File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/03-SYSTEM-WG.md\n+# System WireGuard\n+\n+Implemented source foundation:\n+\n+- A direct-boot-aware privileged `VpnService`.\n+- Boot receiver starts the service at locked boot and normal boot.\n+- The service requests always-on VPN lockdown for its package.\n+- The service creates a blocking TUN covering:\n+  - IPv4 default route\n+  - IPv6 default route\n+  - protected DNS target\n+\n+Frozen public server parameters included:\n+\n+- Endpoint host: `2.28.34.27`\n+- Endpoint port: `51823`\n+- Client address: `10.60.0.10/32`\n+- DNS: `10.60.0.1`\n+- Keepalive: `25`\n+- PSK: none\n+\n+The server public key is included as public material only.\n+\n+Pending:\n+\n+- WireGuard packet engine integration.\n+- Bootstrap UDP socket protection for `2.28.34.27:51823`.\n+- Transition from `BLOCKED` to `PROTECTED` after authenticated handshake.\n*** Add File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/04-KEY-LIFECYCLE.md\n+# Key Lifecycle\n+\n+Private keys are not embedded in this patch.\n+\n+Required production lifecycle:\n+\n+- Generate the Worm OS client private key on device.\n+- Store it in device-protected app storage or Keystore-backed encrypted\n+  storage after backend selection.\n+- Exclude it from backup.\n+- Never log it.\n+- Never expose it through dumpsys or bugreports.\n+- Export only the public key for OPNsense peer provisioning.\n+- Support per-device `/32` assignment.\n+- Support individual revocation by removing one peer server-side.\n+- Factory reset deletes the device identity.\n+\n+Current V1 contains no private key and no PSK.\n*** Add File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/05-FAIL-CLOSED.md\n+# Fail Closed\n+\n+Implemented:\n+\n+- The service establishes a VPN TUN with `0.0.0.0/0` and `::/0`.\n+- No packets are forwarded by V1 without a WireGuard backend.\n+- Underlying network changes re-enter `BLOCKED`.\n+- Service restart re-enters `BLOCKED`.\n+\n+Security result for V1:\n+\n+- Direct IPv4 fallback is blocked when this VPN is active.\n+- Direct IPv6 fallback is blocked when this VPN is active.\n+- Production traffic is not allowed until the backend can prove the\n+  WireGuard tunnel is authenticated and protected.\n+\n+Pending:\n+\n+- Runtime proof on a flashed device.\n+- Explicit endpoint bootstrap socket using `VpnService.protect()`.\n+- Handover and crash tests.\n*** Add File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/06-BOOT.md\n+# Boot\n+\n+Implemented boot hooks:\n+\n+- `LOCKED_BOOT_COMPLETED`\n+- `BOOT_COMPLETED`\n+- `MY_PACKAGE_REPLACED`\n+\n+The service is direct-boot-aware and starts as a foreground VPN service.\n+\n+Expected V1 behavior:\n+\n+- Before user unlock: establish `BLOCKED` VPN where Android permits it.\n+- After user unlock: remain `BLOCKED` until backend implementation can\n+  authenticate WireGuard.\n+\n+Pending:\n+\n+- Real-device boot-before-unlock validation.\n+- Verification that no Worm OTA/apps/download traffic starts before the\n+  protected network state.\n*** Add File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/07-DNS.md\n+# DNS\n+\n+Configured production DNS target:\n+\n+- `10.60.0.1`\n+\n+V1 behavior:\n+\n+- The fail-closed VPN advertises `10.60.0.1` as DNS once the VPN TUN is\n+  established.\n+- There is no public fallback DNS configured by this module.\n+\n+Pending:\n+\n+- WireGuard backend must carry DNS traffic through the tunnel.\n+- Runtime verification for UDP/53 and TCP/53 from the device.\n+- Private DNS / DoT behavior must be tested on device.\n*** Add File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/08-IPV6.md\n+# IPv6\n+\n+Production policy until tunneled IPv6 is designed:\n+\n+- No direct IPv6 bypass.\n+\n+V1 implementation:\n+\n+- Adds `::/0` to the VPN TUN.\n+- Calls `allowFamily(AF_INET6)`.\n+- Does not configure a direct IPv6 fallback path.\n+\n+Pending:\n+\n+- Device proof that IPv6 cannot bypass during boot, network transition,\n+  tunnel failure, and service restart.\n*** Add File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/09-HANDOVER.md\n+# Handover\n+\n+The service registers a default network callback and returns to\n+`BLOCKED` on network availability/loss events.\n+\n+Required tests after flashing:\n+\n+- 5G to Wi-Fi.\n+- Wi-Fi to 5G.\n+- Wi-Fi AP change.\n+- Temporary signal loss.\n+- Airplane mode transition.\n+\n+Expected:\n+\n+- Either protected tunnel reconnects or networking remains blocked.\n+- Never direct Internet.\n*** Add File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/10-SELINUX.md\n+# SELinux\n+\n+No SELinux policy changes were made in V1.\n+\n+Reason:\n+\n+- The implementation uses an Android app-level `VpnService` and existing\n+  framework permissions.\n+- No new native daemon, socket context, file context, or netd extension\n+  was introduced.\n+\n+Pending:\n+\n+- Full build/neverallow validation.\n+- Runtime denials audit after flashing.\n+\n+SELinux must remain enforcing.\n*** Add File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/11-OTA.md\n+# OTA\n+\n+The system app is included through product packages and is expected to\n+survive OTA like other product apps.\n+\n+Private key policy:\n+\n+- Private key is not included in the image.\n+- Private key is not included in OTA payloads.\n+- Normal OTA must preserve on-device identity storage once implemented.\n+- Factory reset must delete identity storage.\n+\n+OTA integration tests are pending.\n*** Add File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/12-TEST-MATRIX.md\n+# Test Matrix\n+\n+Build:\n+\n+- Target: `frankel-cur-userdebug`\n+- Module: `WormSystemWireGuard`\n+- Status: see `test-results.txt`\n+\n+Runtime pending until flashed:\n+\n+- `SYSTEM_OWNED_WG`\n+- `AUTO_START`\n+- `WG_HANDSHAKE`\n+- public IPv4 observation\n+- protected DNS\n+- private OPNsense access\n+- private robot access\n+- direct IPv4 leak test\n+- direct IPv6 leak test\n+- boot fail-closed\n+- handover fail-closed\n+- crash/failure tests\n*** Add File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/13-SECURITY.md\n+# Security\n+\n+No secret material was added.\n+\n+Allowed public material:\n+\n+- OPNsense public endpoint.\n+- OPNsense public WireGuard key.\n+- Non-secret client address.\n+- Non-secret DNS address.\n+\n+Security constraints preserved:\n+\n+- No OPNsense changes.\n+- No Hetzner changes.\n+- No worm-robot changes.\n+- No FireHOL changes.\n+- No route/NAT/DNS server changes.\n+- No private key or PSK committed.\n+\n+V1 intentionally fails closed until a WireGuard backend is implemented\n+and tested.\n*** Add File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/14-ROLLBACK.md\n+# Rollback\n+\n+Rollback is source-only:\n+\n+1. Remove `WormSystemWireGuard` from `PRODUCT_PACKAGES` in\n+   `vendor/google_devices/frankel/frankel.mk`.\n+2. Remove `vendor/worm/WormSystemWireGuard/`.\n+3. Rebuild affected product/module.\n+\n+No server, network, firewall, NAT, DNS, route, OPNsense, Hetzner, or\n+worm-robot rollback is required because this patch did not modify them.\n*** Add File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/15-BACKLOG.md\n+# Backlog\n+\n+P1-WG-BACKEND-001:\n+\n+- Component: WormSystemWireGuard\n+- Evidence: V1 has fail-closed VPN shell but no WireGuard packet engine.\n+- Risk: device remains blocked instead of protected.\n+- Remediation: integrate audited WireGuard backend and protect only the\n+  bootstrap UDP socket.\n+- Blocks production: yes.\n+\n+P1-RUNTIME-DEVICE-001:\n+\n+- Component: device validation\n+- Evidence: not flashed/tested in this patch.\n+- Risk: boot/handover/lockdown behavior not proven.\n+- Remediation: run real-device test matrix.\n+- Blocks production: yes.\n+\n+P2-SELINUX-RUNTIME-001:\n+\n+- Component: SELinux\n+- Evidence: no policy changes; runtime AVC state unknown.\n+- Risk: service may require narrower policy after backend integration.\n+- Remediation: keep SELinux enforcing and audit AVCs on device.\n+- Blocks production if unresolved after backend: yes.\n*** Add File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/findings.json\n+{\n+  \"patch\": \"PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1\",\n+  \"status\": \"PARTIAL\",\n+  \"findings\": [\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"P1-WG-BACKEND-001\",\n+      \"severity\": \"P1\",\n+      \"component\": \"WormSystemWireGuard\",\n+      \"evidence\": \"V1 establishes a fail-closed VPN TUN but does not yet implement WireGuard packet encryption/transport.\",\n+      \"risk\": \"Device networking remains blocked rather than protected.\",\n+      \"remediation\": \"Integrate an audited WireGuard backend and bootstrap socket protection.\",\n+      \"blocks_production\": true\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"P1-RUNTIME-DEVICE-001\",\n+      \"severity\": \"P1\",\n+      \"component\": \"Real device validation\",\n+      \"evidence\": \"The image has not been flashed and runtime tests have not been performed.\",\n+      \"risk\": \"System-owned autostart, lockdown, handover, DNS, IPv6 and failure behavior are unproven.\",\n+      \"remediation\": \"Run the real-device runtime gate after backend integration.\",\n+      \"blocks_production\": true\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}\n*** Add File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/modified-files.txt\n+/opt/Android/grapheneos-frankel-17/vendor/google_devices/frankel/frankel.mk\n+/opt/Android/grapheneos-frankel-17/vendor/worm/WormSystemWireGuard/Android.bp\n+/opt/Android/grapheneos-frankel-17/vendor/worm/WormSystemWireGuard/AndroidManifest.xml\n+/opt/Android/grapheneos-frankel-17/vendor/worm/WormSystemWireGuard/privapp-permissions-com.worm.systemwg.xm