:"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"SOURCE_IMPLEMENTATION=PARTIAL  \nBUILD=PASS  \nSELINUX=PASS  \nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS  \nAUTO_START=DEVICE_TEST_REQUIRED  \nWG_RUNTIME=BLOCKED_WG_BACKEND_MISSING  \nFAIL_CLOSED_IPV4=DEVICE_TEST_REQUIRED  \nFAIL_CLOSED_IPV6=DEVICE_TEST_REQUIRED  \nFAIL_CLOSED_BOOT=DEVICE_TEST_REQUIRED  \nFAIL_CLOSED_HANDOVER=DEVICE_TEST_REQUIRED  \nPROTECTED_DNS=DEVICE_TEST_REQUIRED  \nPRIVATE_ACCESS=BLOCKED_WG_BACKEND_MISSING  \nPUBLIC_IPV4=BLOCKED_WG_BACKEND_MISSING  \nNO_SECRETS=PASS  \nSERVER_NETWORK=FROZEN_UNCHANGED  \nWORM_OS_SYSTEM_NETWORK=PARTIAL  \n\nFILES_CHANGED=11 source/report files plus 2 validation scripts  \nTESTS_EXECUTED=local-validate PASS; WormSystemWireGuard module build PASS; target-files-package PASS; findings.json parse PASS; secret scan PASS  \nDEVICE_TESTS_REQUIRED=AUTO_START, fail-closed IPv4/IPv6, boot leak, handover leak, protected DNS, private access, public IPv4, real WireGuard runtime  \nBLOCKERS=P1-WG-BACKEND-001: no WireGuard packet backend yet; P1-RUNTIME-DEVICE-001: image not flashed/runtime-tested  \nOTA_READY=NO"}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07f78-3e99-7e03-a9dd-f83b026f1b4e","create_time":1788845483.147961,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a07f80-cd3c-7e73-a33b-70e930e733eb","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"CONTINUE PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1.\n\nCurrent confirmed state:\n\nBUILD=PASS\nSELINUX=PASS\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\nSERVER_NETWORK=FROZEN_UNCHANGED\n\nPrimary blocker:\nP1-WG-BACKEND-001 — WormSystemWireGuard has no real WireGuard packet backend.\n\nDO NOT mark the OTA ready.\nDO NOT work around the missing backend with fake/mock connectivity.\nDO NOT install or depend on the user-facing WireGuard app.\nDO NOT modify OPNsense or external/server infrastructure.\nDO NOT add production secrets.\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nImplement the actual system-owned WireGuard packet/data-plane backend required\nby WormSystemWireGuard, using the existing GrapheneOS/AOSP networking stack\nand the safest maintainable integration available in the current source tree.\n\nFIRST: inspect the existing GrapheneOS kernel/userspace/network stack.\n\nDetermine exactly which usable WireGuard implementation is already available:\n\n- kernel WireGuard support/module, if present;\n- existing userspace WireGuard implementation;\n- Android VPN/WireGuard libraries already present in the tree;\n- existing GrapheneOS/AOSP VPN plumbing that can safely host the backend.\n\nDo not assume which backend exists.\nProve it from the checked-out source/config/build artifacts.\n\nPREFERRED IMPLEMENTATION ORDER:\n\n1. Existing native/kernel WireGuard backend already supported by this target.\n2. Existing trusted in-tree WireGuard userspace backend.\n3. Minimal system-owned integration of an appropriate existing backend.\n\nDo NOT download arbitrary binaries.\nDo NOT introduce a new external dependency unless absolutely required.\nIf a new dependency would be required, STOP and report it instead.\n\nREQUIREMENTS:\n\nA. REAL DATA PLANE\n\nWormSystemWireGuard must create a genuine WireGuard tunnel and route packets\nthrough it.\n\nIt must not merely expose configuration/status APIs.\n\nB. SYSTEM OWNERSHIP\n\nKeep:\n\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\n\nNo dependency on a user-installed WireGuard application.\n\nC. ANDROID NETWORK INTEGRATION\n\nIntegrate the backend correctly with Android networking.\n\nEnsure the design supports:\n\n- boot initialization;\n- network availability changes;\n- Wi-Fi/cellular handover;\n- IPv4;\n- IPv6;\n- DNS through the protected path;\n- private tunnel destinations;\n- Internet traffic through WireGuard.\n\nD. FAIL-CLOSED ARCHITECTURE\n\nImplement fail-closed enforcement independently from reconnect logic.\n\nNo ordinary application traffic may use the physical uplink outside the\nprotected WireGuard path when protection is enabled.\n\nAccount for:\n\n- tunnel not established;\n- tunnel failure;\n- boot;\n- backend crash/restart;\n- Wi-Fi -> cellular;\n- cellular -> Wi-Fi;\n- IPv4;\n- IPv6;\n- DNS.\n\nDo not weaken GrapheneOS/AOSP networking security to achieve this.\n\nE. SELINUX\n\nAdd only the minimum SELinux permissions genuinely required.\n\nNever use:\n\npermissive\nbroad allow rules\ndisable_neverallow\nSELinux bypasses\n\nSELINUX must remain PASS.\n\nF. SECRETS\n\nArchitecture must allow runtime provisioning of WireGuard secrets without\nembedding them in:\n\n- source;\n- APK;\n- product image;\n- target-files;\n- logs;\n- reports.\n\nNO_SECRETS must remain PASS.\n\nG. BUILD\n\nAfter implementation:\n\n1. build WormSystemWireGuard;\n2. build every affected Android/native component;\n3. build target-files-package;\n4. run local validation;\n5. run secret scan;\n6. inspect resulting target image/package to prove backend inclusion.\n\nH. DEVICE VALIDATION\n\nDo NOT claim runtime PASS from build-time evidence.\n\nPrepare/update an executable device-validation procedure for:\n\nAUTO_START\nWG_RUNTIME\nFAIL_CLOSED_IPV4\nFAIL_CLOSED_IPV6\nFAIL_CLOSED_BOOT\nFAIL_CLOSED_HANDOVER\nPROTECTED_DNS\nPRIVATE_ACCESS\nPUBLIC_IPV4\n\nIf the image has not actually been flashed and tested, report:\n\nDEVICE_TEST_REQUIRED\n\nrather than PASS.\n\nI. SERVER FREEZE\n\nOPNsense/server/public-IP/WireGuard-server configuration remains untouched:\n\nSERVER_NETWORK=FROZEN_UNCHANGED\n\nFINAL REPORT:\n\nSOURCE_IMPLEMENTATION=\nBUILD=\nSELINUX=\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=\nWG_BACKEND=\nAUTO_START=\nWG_RUNTIME=\nFAIL_CLOSED_IPV4=\nFAIL_CLOSED_IPV6=\nFAIL_CLOSED_BOOT=\nFAIL_CLOSED_HANDOVER=\nPROTECTED_DNS=\nPRIVATE_ACCESS=\nPUBLIC_IPV4=\nNO_SECRETS=\nSERVER_NETWORK=\nWORM_OS_SYSTEM_NETWORK=\n\nBACKEND_SELECTED=\nBACKEND_EVIDENCE=\nFILES_CHANGED=\nTESTS_EXECUTED=\nDEVICE_TESTS_REQUIRED=\nBLOCKERS=\nOTA_READY=\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nWG_BACKEND=PASS only if an actual packet/data-plane backend has been built\ninto the resulting system image.\n\nSOURCE_IMPLEMENTATION=PASS only when the complete source-side implementation\nexists.\n\nOTA_READY=PASS only after all security-critical runtime/device tests have\nactually passed.\n\nIf source implementation is complete but physical-device validation remains,\nuse:\n\nSOURCE_IMPLEMENTATION=PASS\nOTA_READY=NO"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07f80-cd17-7cf0-8ea8-11f559b49fc3","create_time":1788845542.7161188,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_0d4d71abca8c0b20016a9f9de882c887d2a12b280591f39568","summary":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqn53pVk4xYHpgvp3JLSgNQaDnQwaJY1p3IoouA9yvpzLd36yJconqNzI9cjsMJj-j_RRdtNHhXziv1sRUOTqKRWzgaKadn-9aPFiDE54LF7vqr7mWWxjdjmy-ptc-GgUCBReojNh8ktZnufWcDzQW1bkMZCvMuxNd-ZsiGaJL8vFghSFpYP5Hu3g5ho0D87bID8BK31TTPWI0CLU1kIvya3fw36J8hNscKGBFWb8yrEDhJ_-yKu6zZ0Bq4Yg9Jd-_x5hpeyddNxaNmCb1QpSkWcM8UfL580UGJIhz_RbhVTnK5z2oGKmKfSmt8tiYRD0yM8DoZ4p3R6gg4VR8HHRx2Xs6LwMl4ilhJ9QATtGzHEtStNdUJWCT9jDmFQuv0mSjfOA5usmg1BU0uEK4LrOwQwSBN-khrLkvDBiYNU10-i2EnLSa3ovzLzfJ2cdnleq4_expM5QR30wUxqitvDc9NhznexjgSZmFV1W66bw4WFhgqIZ8hAq-Fd3kUvJaLBmijIDnE1oa8uPNewpLS3t87txGcv_lyRGA9uFBYiTzya3GuBsnVDZeelPyzvzEgNlY9rX-_UhamIgd07cKgm0flJyspF5RWKKCcsFaUeObIfZLa9_qs4xW3QMCIzwjTwl4TnL64-UPP0pdNn5VgRyRkojV4CxpmiRiisAIsk9l8rgPt9dwqiGgVID42jgqHd8CUQ0E7szKg1Len2Nx492XxSItjb_jtffL6NDJ6c2v-KZUUpIEsZu2QdClYKGYpcUogIhY5AL3Mhx_m7HcBVrdnXHQtJcWre04iFfySGL9PwUguwpdAo0n6lETZsc9hEw3pO-C3RZsbKO7mPqmF_K1dbNonH9v4aS4LH0IfAW9eknBu2UmIDJbB-kn2w_m60kM53ITam129XPAeruOkaRkpSSVL46ovouKs11pm54_b_GUBGsf4BtS9mKTUwyb5GEz5Pl9-mTxet7A0a_ijx7Lt8Z3bkDxR92yndJ8ORn-WU__0BBNSUCUHS5Z7aXHymgPCe-BKUfdP7Z7L07tLtOU42R9d42Jx_fxnFZlMha9MoHIpkzmCjedKlrJ6fOIwNTuqnYcHiS3EeuHxKHh3Y7YOxAsQdqmkaw7_5shXsnLf-hOQ_fuxFUWNz7oRPQ89t96yz9tzbqh7D6y4DnIME4iRRQ_dl-57kY87G1frf-XVOxVgeA--4R-h7HrOO-b7QJm8Qd6TuLu5To8l8WKN-AV6Iy7uUoYzYfnRzn_28xNV3x2m1ialXA9VbvJ9-LReSPdFhvpTOWiKObaMpxjVE7pILI28X53aDSb_YqwBO9Ve05eKmw1G_RjXLW2T8v9u1ttEn8ZCkJgki313dhnbQpoD9OF8mcYnjnBrdfQzhovrhRkYV2Q0kSfM-E265Uj2l5NCj4NKQAt