ntly uses `VpnService` to enforce fail-closed\n+  routing for IPv4 and IPv6.\n+- A kernel `wg` interface configured independently through netlink would not\n+  consume packets from the `VpnService` TUN.\n+- Ordinary app traffic would remain captured by the fail-closed VPN TUN unless\n+  a real userspace WireGuard backend reads that TUN and forwards encrypted\n+  packets through a protected bootstrap socket.\n+- Bypassing `VpnService` with raw kernel routes would require deeper Android\n+  ConnectivityService/netd integration to preserve always-on lockdown semantics.\n+\n+Safe conclusion:\n+\n+- Existing kernel support is useful but not by itself a complete Android\n+  system-owned WireGuard runtime.\n+- Completing the data plane requires either:\n+  - importing/auditing a trusted userspace WireGuard backend, or\n+  - adding a deeper framework/netd integration for kernel WireGuard.\n+- No arbitrary dependency was downloaded or added in this patch.\n*** Update File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/test-results.txt\n@@\n SOURCE_IMPLEMENTATION=PARTIAL\n BUILD=PASS\n SELINUX=PASS\n NEVERALLOW=PASS\n SYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\n+WG_BACKEND=BLOCKED_NO_USABLE_IN_TREE_ANDROID_WG_BACKEND\n AUTO_START=DEVICE_TEST_REQUIRED\n WG_RUNTIME=BLOCKED_WG_BACKEND_MISSING\n@@\n WORM_OS_SYSTEM_NETWORK=PARTIAL\n*** Update File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/00-SUMMARY.md\n@@\n Not implemented in this V1:\n \n - Userspace/kernel WireGuard packet engine inside the system app.\n - Device runtime validation after flashing.\n - Handover/crash/boot leak tests on the real device.\n+\n+Continuation backend audit:\n+\n+- Kernel WireGuard support is present for the target kernel as built-in code.\n+- No production userspace WireGuard backend or Android WireGuard library is\n+  present in the checked-out tree.\n+- Kernel WireGuard alone cannot satisfy the current `VpnService` fail-closed\n+  architecture because app traffic is captured by the Android VPN TUN.\n+- No external dependency was downloaded or added.\n \n Server/network state was not modified.\n*** Update File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/03-SYSTEM-WG.md\n@@\n Pending:\n \n - WireGuard packet engine integration.\n - Bootstrap UDP socket protection for `2.28.34.27:51823`.\n - Transition from `BLOCKED` to `PROTECTED` after authenticated handshake.\n - Real-device proof that Android accepts the package as always-on/lockdown\n   before ordinary app traffic can leave.\n+\n+Backend audit:\n+\n+- Target kernel includes WireGuard symbols.\n+- No in-tree production Android WireGuard userspace backend was found.\n+- A root/netlink kernel WireGuard controller would not by itself integrate\n+  with the current Android `VpnService` TUN and always-on lockdown model.\n*** Update File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/12-TEST-MATRIX.md\n@@\n System-owned evidence:\n@@\n - Privapp permission grant file: PASS\n - No dependency on user-installed WireGuard app: PASS\n+\n+Backend evidence:\n+\n+- Kernel WireGuard symbol `wg_mod_init`: PRESENT\n+- WireGuard UAPI header: PRESENT\n+- Production `wg`/`wg-quick`/`wireguard-go`: NOT FOUND\n+- In-tree Android WireGuard userspace backend: NOT FOUND\n+- `WG_BACKEND`: BLOCKED\n \n Runtime pending until flashed or backend integration:\n@@\n - Device checklist:\n   - `/opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/device-validation.sh`\n*** Update File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/15-BACKLOG.md\n@@\n P1-WG-BACKEND-001:\n \n - Component: WormSystemWireGuard\n - Evidence: V1 has fail-closed VPN shell and system ownership scaffolding\n-  but no WireGuard packet engine.\n+  but no WireGuard packet engine. Backend audit found kernel WireGuard\n+  symbols and UAPI headers, but no production Android userspace WireGuard\n+  backend or existing GrapheneOS/AOSP WireGuard VPN runtime in-tree.\n - Risk: device remains blocked instead of protected.\n-- Remediation: integrate audited WireGuard backend and protect only the\n-  bootstrap UDP socket.\n+- Remediation: integrate an audited userspace WireGuard backend compatible\n+  with Android `VpnService`, or implement deeper ConnectivityService/netd\n+  integration for kernel WireGuard without weakening lockdown semantics.\n - Blocks production: yes.\n@@\n - VPN revoke handling added.\n+- Backend audit documented in `16-BACKEND-AUDIT.md`.\n*** Update File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/modified-files.txt\n@@\n /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/local-validate.sh\n /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/device-validation.sh\n+/opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/16-BACKEND-AUDIT.md\n*** Update File: /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-FAILCLOSED-V1/findings.json\n@@\n-      \"evidence\": \"V1 establishes a fail-closed VPN TUN and system ownership scaffolding but does not yet implement WireGuard packet encryption/transport.\",\n+      \"evidence\": \"V1 establishes a fail-closed VPN TUN and system ownership scaffolding but does not yet implement WireGuard packet encryption/transport. Kernel WireGuard symbols and UAPI headers are present, but no production in-tree Android WireGuard userspace backend or existing GrapheneOS/AOSP WireGuard VPN runtime was found.\",\n       \"risk\": \"Device networking remains blocked rather than protected.\",\n-      \"remediation\": \"Integrate an audited WireGuard backend and bootstrap socket protection.\",\n+      \"remediation\": \"Integrate an audited userspace WireGuard backend compatible with Android VpnService, or implement deeper ConnectivityService/netd integration for kernel WireGuard without weakening lockdown semantics.\",\n       \"blocks_production\": true\n*** End Patch\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07f80-cd17-7cf0-8ea8-11f559b49fc3","create_time":1788845607.286333}},{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a07f82-c038-7d83-a9f8-4be3829b44e6","call_id":"call_QYUPr84PrAxyBIinO