mands were truncated]\n The writable roots are `/opt/Android`, `/tmp`.\n</permissions instructions>"},{"type":"input_text","text":"<collaboration_mode># Collaboration Mode: Default\n\nYou are now in Default mode. Any previous instructions for other modes (e.g. Plan mode) are no longer active.\n\nYour active mode changes only when new developer instructions with a different `<collaboration_mode>...</collaboration_mode>` change it; user requests or tool descriptions do not change mode by themselves. Known mode names are Default and Plan.\n\n## request_user_input availability\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only when it is listed in the available tools for this turn.\n\nIn Default mode, strongly prefer making reasonable assumptions and executing the user's request rather than stopping to ask questions.\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only for optional questions where the answer would materially improve the quality of the work.\n\nIf `request_user_input` returns no answers, continue with best judgment instead of asking again or treating the turn as blocked.\n\nNever use the `request_user_input` tool for permission requests or permission-related escalations.\n\nIf explicit user input is required for another reason before progress can safely continue, do not use the `request_user_input` tool. Ask the user directly with one concise plain-text question instead. Never write a multiple choice question as a textual assistant message.\n</collaboration_mode>"},{"type":"input_text","text":"<apps_instructions>\n## Apps (Connectors)\nApps (Connectors) can be explicitly triggered in user messages in the format `[$app-name](app://{connector_id})`. Apps can also be implicitly triggered as long as the context suggests usage of available apps.\nAn app is equivalent to a set of MCP tools within the `codex_apps` MCP.\nAn installed app's MCP tools are either provided to you already, or can be lazy-loaded through the `tool_search` tool. If `tool_search` is available, the apps that are searchable by `tools_search` will be listed by it.\nDo not additionally call list_mcp_resources or list_mcp_resource_templates for apps.\n</apps_instructions>"},{"type":"input_text","text":"<plugins_instructions>\n## Plugins\nA plugin is a local bundle of skills, MCP servers, and apps.\n### How to use plugins\n- Skill naming: If a plugin contributes skills, those skill entries are prefixed with `plugin_name:` in the Skills list.\n- MCP naming: Plugin-provided MCP tools keep standard MCP identifiers such as `mcp__server__tool`; use tool provenance to tell which plugin they come from.\n- Trigger rules: If the user explicitly names a plugin, prefer capabilities associated with that plugin for that turn.\n- Relationship to capabilities: Plugins are not invoked directly. Use their underlying skills, MCP tools, and app tools to help solve the task.\n- Relevance: Determine what a plugin can help with from explicit user mention or from the plugin-associated skills, MCP tools, and apps exposed elsewhere in this turn.\n- Missing/blocked: If the user requests a plugin that does not have relevant callable capabilities for the task, say so briefly and continue with the best fallback.\n</plugins_instructions>"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07f9a-4db3-7512-bae2-e83dc8203e75","content_item_kinds":["host_skills.instructions","permissions.instructions","collaboration_mode.instructions","apps.instructions","plugins.usage_instructions"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a07f9b-7fe2-7c21-b888-52f71ea5c368","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"<environment_context>\n  <cwd>/opt/Android</cwd>\n  <shell>bash</shell>\n  <current_date>2026-09-08</current_date>\n  <timezone>Europe/Berlin</timezone>\n  <filesystem><workspace_roots><root>/opt/Android</root></workspace_roots><permission_profile type=\"managed\"><file_system type=\"restricted\"><entry access=\"read\"><special>:root</special></entry><entry access=\"write\"><path>/opt/Android</path></entry><entry access=\"write\"><special>:slash_tmp</special></entry><entry access=\"write\"><special>:tmpdir</special></entry><entry access=\"read\"><path>/opt/Android/.git</path></entry><entry access=\"read\"><path>/opt/Android/.agents</path></entry><entry access=\"read\"><path>/opt/Android/.codex</path></entry></file_system></permission_profile></filesystem>\n</environment_context>"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07f9a-4db3-7512-bae2-e83dc8203e75","content_item_kinds":["environments.environment_context"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a07f9a-4dd2-7051-8cf7-bb4e96c7d5df","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"CONTINUE PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3\n\nThe backend architecture decision is now APPROVED:\n\nBACKEND_SELECTED=official WireGuard Android tunnel backend + source-built\nwireguard-go\n\nThe previous phase intentionally stopped because the upstream source was not\nlocally present and no exact revision had been pinned.\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nResolve:\n\nP1-BACKEND-SOURCE-IMPORT-001\n\nby performing a controlled, reproducible source import of the official\nWireGuard backend required for WormSystemWireGuard.\n\nThis is no longer an architecture-selection task.\n\n============================================================\n1. VERIFY OFFICIAL UPSTREAM\n============================================================\n\nLocate the canonical official WireGuard Android source repository using the\nofficial WireGuard project references.\n\nBefore importing anything, record:\n\nUPSTREAM_REPOSITORY=\nUPSTREAM_COMMIT=\nUPSTREAM_COMMIT_DATE=\nUPSTREAM_LICENSE=\nUPSTREAM_SOURCE_VERIFIED=\n\nDo not use:\n\n- random GitHub forks;\n- mirrors as authoritative source;\n- prebuilt APKs;\n- downloaded native binaries;\n- unofficial Maven artifacts;\n- unpinned branches.\n\nUse an exact immutable commit hash.\n\nIf canonical upstream identity cannot be established with high confidence:\n\nSTOP\nUPSTREAM_SOURCE_VERIFIED=NO\nOTA_READY=NO\n\n============================================================\n2. PIN SOURCE\n============================================================\n\nPin the exact upstream commit.\n\nCreate provenance documentation containing at minimum:\n\n- canonical repository;\n- exact commit SHA;\n- retrieval date;\n- relevant license;\n- imported directories/files;\n- excluded directories/files;\n- reason for every major exclusion;\n- integrity/hash information sufficient to reproduce the import.\n\nNever track a moving branch as the WormOS production dependency.\n\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS only after the exact revision is recorded in the patch\nand build metadata.\n\n============================================================\n3. MINIMAL SOURCE IMPORT\n============================================================\n\nImport ONLY the components required to implement the WireGuard data plane.\n\nExpected scope:\n\n- Android tunnel/backend pieces required for TUN operation;\n- WireGuard configuration/parser pieces genuinely required;\n- crypto/native/backend pieces genuinely required;\n- source required to build wireguard-go for the target.\n\nExplicitly exclude unless technically required:\n\n- WireGuard user-facing application UI;\n- activities/screens;\n- launcher integration;\n- unrelated preferences;\n- application branding;\n- update mechanisms;\n- analytics;\n- sample/demo/test applications;\n- unnecessary resources.\n\nWormOS must NOT ship the normal user-facing WireGuard application as a\ndependency.\n\n============================================================\n4. REPRODUCIBLE SOURCE BUILD\n============================================================\n\nIntegrate the imported backend into the existing Android/GrapheneOS build.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- build backend from source;\n- no opaque prebuilts;\n- no runtime downloads;\n- no Play Services;\n- no external package manager required on device;\n- deterministic/pinned inputs;\n- appropriate Android target architecture(s).\n\nProve the produced target-files package contains the resulting backend built\nfrom the pinned source.\n\nReport:\n\nBACKEND_SOURCE_BUILD=\nBACKEND_PACKAGED=\n\n============================================================\n5. CONNECT WORMSYSTEMWIREGUARD\n============================================================\n\nReplace the current placeholder/mock backend boundary with the real backend.\n\nData path must become:\n\nApp traffic\n    |\nAndroid VPN lockdown\n    |\nVpnService TUN\n    |\nWormSystemWireGuard\n    |\nsource-built WireGuard backend\n    |\nprotected transport socket\n    |\nunderlying network\n    |\nOPNsense WireGuard peer\n\nWormSystemWireGuard remains privileged/system-owned.\n\nThe normal WireGuard app must not be installed or required.\n\n============================================================\n6. UNDERLYING SOCKET / LOCKDOWN\n============================================================\n\nPay special attention to the WireGuard UDP transport socket.\n\nIt must be able to reach the configured peer without creating a generic\napplication bypass around VPN lockdown.\n\nAudit the exact VpnService/protect()/network binding behavior used by the\nbackend.\n\nDocument exactly:\n\n- which socket escapes the VPN route;\n- why it must escape;\n- how its scope is limited;\n- why ordinary application UIDs cannot use the same bypass.\n\nDo not weaken lockdown globally.\n\n============================================================\n7. SECRETS\n============================================================\n\nDo NOT add real production credentials during this phase.\n\nNo:\n\n- private WireGuard key;\n- preshared key;\n- production secret;\n- token;\n- password.\n\nRuntime provisioning remains separate.\n\nRun a secret scan after import because upstream test/example files may\ncontain key-looking fixtures.\n\nExclude unnecessary fixtures from production packaging.\n\nNO_SECRETS must remain PASS.\n\n============================================================\n8. SELINUX / PRIVILEGE\n============================================================\n\nAdd only permissions actually required by the backend integration.\n\nNo:\n\n- permissive domains;\n- broad wildcard allows;\n- neverallow bypass;\n- unnecessary root shell;\n- excessive Linux capabilities.\n\nRun SELinux/build validation after changes.\n\n============================================================\n9. BUILD GATES\n============================================================\n\nExecute:\n\nA. backend source build\nB. WormSystemWireGuard module build\nC. affected dependency builds\nD. target-files-package build\nE. findings.json validation\nF. source provenance validation\nG. license/NOTICE validation\nH. dependency audit\nI. secret scan\nJ. resulting target-files inspection\n\nDo not reuse PREVIOUS_PASS for BUILD or SELINUX after source import.\n\nThey must actually be rerun.\n\n============================================================\n10. DEVICE TEST BOUNDARY\n============================================================\n\nDo NOT attempt to convert device-only requirements into build-time PASS.\n\nAfter successful source integration these may remain:\n\nDEVICE_TEST_REQUIRED\n\nfor:\n\nAUTO_START\nWG_RUNTIME\nFAIL_CLOSED_IPV4\nFAIL_CLOSED_IPV6\nFAIL_CLOSED_BOOT\nFAIL_CLOSED_HANDOVER\nFAIL_CLOSED_BACKEND_CRASH\nFAIL_CLOSED_PEER_UNREACHABLE\nPROTECTED_DNS\nPRIVATE_ACCESS\nPUBLIC_IPV4\n\nThat is acceptable.\n\nThe objective of THIS checkpoint is to reach:\n\nSOURCE_IMPLEMENTATION=PASS\nBUILD=PASS\nSELINUX=PASS\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\nWG_BACKEND=PASS\nBACKEND_SOURCE_BUILD=PASS\nBACKEND_PINNED=PASS\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nwhile:\n\nOTA_READY=NO\n\nuntil physical-device runtime validation is completed.\n\n============================================================\n11. INFRASTRUCTURE FREEZE\n============================================================\n\nDo not modify:\n\n- OPNsense;\n- WireGuard server;\n- server firewall;\n- public IP configuration;\n- DNS server infrastructure;\n- external networking.\n\nSERVER_NETWORK=FROZEN_UNCHANGED\n\n============================================================\nFINAL REPORT\n============================================================\n\nSOURCE_IMPLEMENTATION=\nBUILD=\nSELINUX=\nSYSTEM_OWNED_WG=\nWG_BACKEND=\nBACKEND_SOURCE_BUILD=\nBACKEND_PACKAGED=\nBACKEND_PINNED=\nUPSTREAM_SOURCE_VERIFIED=\nLOCKDOWN_INTEGRATION=\nAUTO_START=\nWG_RUNTIME=\nFAIL_CLOSED_IPV4=\nFAIL_CLOSED_IPV6=\nFAIL_CLOSED_BOOT=\nFAIL_CLOSED_HANDOVER=\nFAIL_CLOSED_BACKEND_CRASH=\nFAIL_CLOSED_PEER_UNREACHABLE=\nPROTECTED_DNS=\nPRIVATE_ACCESS=\nPUBLIC_IPV4=\nNO_SECRETS=\nSERVER_NETWORK=\nWORM_OS_SYSTEM_NETWORK=\n\nBACKEND_SELECTED=\nUPSTREAM_REPOSITORY=\nUPSTREAM_COMMIT=\nUPSTREAM_COMMIT_DATE=\nLICENSE_STATUS=\nDEPENDENCY_AUDIT=\nPROVENANCE_FILE=\nFILES_CHANGED=\nTESTS_EXECUTED=\nDEVICE_TESTS_REQUIRED=\nBLOCKERS=\nOTA_READY=\n\nSTOP CONDITIONS:\n\nIf official upstream cannot be verified:\nSTOP.\n\nIf importing requires an opaque prebuilt:\nSTOP.\n\nIf integration requires weakening GrapheneOS security:\nSTOP.\n\nIf build requires embedding production secrets:\nSTOP.\n\nOtherwise complete the source import, integration and builds.\n\nOTA_READY=NO until physical-device runtime validation."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07f9a-4db3-7512-bae2-e83dc8203e75","create_time":1788847214.0345445,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},{"type":"compaction","id":"cmp_0d4d71abca8c0b20016a9fa486056087d2923fbf5b5c828cd5","encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqn6S8G0M_K2cgnWz-oe0h-EJaG8G9SNXoxBE1STDJwjrhex9ish7p6jqHoe5NhO6sjGYAnVwoZMh7XutqFos0qMhM3OZG_OhaGBuIxi8forxRtC8ivEilIv24CO827fg_9zYQ25qTAjgu0Qzb3PYKGKWZJmnAALWJ_fBVL59pEgB6KXfhRNbChgrhJ1-RgcpjzUYXcEajq1XCJeDDKo6bC3BX3A9sef_zWQ8drqSCai3775gjv6ziLgAzbiZePTu4CxvrfFQPVmr6nMn3Luy8z8Mjx7xrEKUeU0VuLFm3-KlpnTpWZpvXbimV143P3GD-X3-StgD4EacuA5fxWN90yif_6BS7-8jSZFzCzJNCe9yjTx3JYNEMJ42QQnLfSf0CW_Y95AZkYIOb2JJEsX0ESHNa687ECRLKR0VZaaQj-72gQaZtgrDZAi_3VuY0e1273kgpTHQvhRy0_kVW_3Pc