01a07f88-2c06-7a33-aff8-360d194a2a72"}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_0d4d71abca8c0b20016a9fa05a18b887d28a645f98cd15b1ac","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"I’m stopping before source implementation for this V2 because the audited path is not a small app-level change. The kernel backend exists, but Android needs new trusted plumbing to create/configure the interface and make ConnectivityService/netd treat it as the secure VPN network with UID lockdown and DNS semantics."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07f88-2c06-7a33-aff8-360d194a2a72","create_time":1788846165.655531,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0d4d71abca8c0b20016a9fa05b856487d2bd12362b4b17334b","name":"exec_command","arguments":"{\"cmd\":\"mkdir -p /opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-NATIVE-KERNEL-WIREGUARD-V2\",\"workdir\":\"/opt/Android\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":2000}","call_id":"call_5E8vIiPIyNtDjWMYhRCtdg2V","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07f88-2c06-7a33-aff8-360d194a2a72","create_time":1788846165.655531}},{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a07f8a-693e-7543-a592-c9b8ee773ce8","call_id":"call_5E8vIiPIyNtDjWMYhRCtdg2V","output":"Chunk ID: dd2229\nWall time: 0.0000 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 0\nOutput:\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07f88-2c06-7a33-aff8-360d194a2a72","create_time":1788846172.47889}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_0d4d71abca8c0b20016a9fa05fb26487d2903e3fc35f4b6670","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"I’m writing the V2 audit artifact now: evidence, feasibility decision, minimal future change set, and the explicit reason no source implementation was applied in this pass."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07f88-2c06-7a33-aff8-360d194a2a72","create_time":1788846173.337868,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0d4d71abca8c0b20016a9fa060a65c87d2b09d37eb1ec0a605","status":"completed","call_id":"call_hARNFRHM7GvBOteUjaLHwLUb","name":"apply_patch","input":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: PATCH-WORMOS-NATIVE-KERNEL-WIREGUARD-V2/README.md\n+# PATCH-WORMOS-NATIVE-KERNEL-WIREGUARD-V2\n+\n+Status: AUDIT COMPLETE / STOPPED BEFORE IMPLEMENTATION.\n+\n+This patch evaluates replacing the previous `VpnService` userspace data-plane\n+assumption with direct integration of the target kernel's built-in WireGuard\n+implementation.\n+\n+Decision:\n+\n+`KERNEL_WG_FRAMEWORK_INTEGRATION=NOT_FEASIBLE`\n+\n+Meaning: not feasible as a minimum safe source patch using only the current\n+app-level WormSystemWireGuard component and existing in-tree Android APIs. The\n+kernel WireGuard data plane exists, but Android does not currently expose a\n+complete system-owned WireGuard VPN type that creates/configures a kernel WG\n+interface and registers it as the secure Android VPN network with lockdown\n+semantics.\n+\n+No OPNsense, server, WireGuard server, NAT, DNS, FireHOL, Hetzner, or public IP\n+configuration was modified.\n+\n*** Add File: PATCH-WORMOS-NATIVE-KERNEL-WIREGUARD-V2/01-ARCHITECTURE-AUDIT.md\n+# Architecture Audit\n+\n+Kernel WireGuard:\n+\n+- Present for the target kernel as built-in code.\n+- Evidence: `device/google/laguna-kernels/6.6/grapheneos/muzel/System.map`\n+  contains `wg_mod_init` and WireGuard init symbols.\n+- No standalone `wireguard.ko` was found in the frankel target output,\n+  consistent with built-in kernel support.\n+\n+WireGuard UAPI:\n+\n+- Present at `bionic/libc/kernel/uapi/linux/wireguard.h`.\n+- Exposes `WG_GENL_NAME`, `WG_CMD_SET_DEVICE`, peer attributes, allowed IP\n+  attributes, and device private/public key attributes.\n+\n+Generic netlink/rtnetlink:\n+\n+- In-tree userspace has netlink examples and libraries, including external\n+  `libnl` and Rust rtnetlink crates.\n+- No production Android system component currently uses them to configure\n+  kernel WireGuard for a VPN Network.\n+\n+Android VPN/Network model:\n+\n+- `frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Vpn.java`\n+  owns Android VPN lifecycle for VpnService and platform VPNs.\n+- `VpnService.establish()` creates a TUN fd through native `jniCreate()`.\n+- `Vpn.agentConnect()` registers a `NetworkAgent` with `TRANSPORT_VPN`.\n+- Existing platform VPN support is IKEv2/IPsec, not WireGuard.\n+\n+netd routing/lockdown:\n+\n+- `system/netd/server/VirtualNetwork.h` documents secure VPN semantics.\n+- `system/netd/server/NetdNativeService.cpp` exposes virtual network creation\n+  through `networkCreateVpn()` / `networkCreate()`.\n+- `system/netd/server/RouteController.cpp` installs high-priority secure VPN\n+  UID routing and prohibit-non-VPN rules.\n+- `Vpn.setVpnForcedLocked()` calls `ConnectivityManager.setRequireVpnForUids()`\n+  to enforce lockdown.\n+\n+Current WormSystemWireGuard:\n+\n+- System-owned privileged app exists.\n+- It currently uses `VpnService` to create a blocking fail-closed TUN.\n+- It does not own a packet backend and cannot hand TUN packets to kernel\n+  WireGuard.\n+\n*** Add File: PATCH-WORMOS-NATIVE-KERNEL-WIREGUARD-V2/02-FEASIBILITY.md\n+# Feasibility Decision\n+\n+`KERNEL_WG_FRAMEWORK_INTEGRATION=NOT_FEASIBLE`\n+\n+The kernel WireGuard backend can encrypt/decrypt packets for a kernel network\n+interface, but the current Android integration path is incomplete:\n+\n+- A kernel WG interface must be created via rtnetlink.\n+- Peer/device configuration must be applied via WireGuard generic netlink.\n+- Tunnel addresses, routes, DNS, UID ownership, and network validation must be\n+  represented through Android ConnectivityService/netd.\n+- Always-on lockdown must block application traffic when the protected network\n+  is absent or broken.\n+- Bootstrap traffic for `2.28.34.27:51823` must bypass the protected network\n+  without allowing general physical-uplink traffic.\n+\n+Existing AOSP/GrapheneOS primitives can support parts of this, but there is no\n+single existing in-tree WireGuard platform VPN runner equivalent to the IKEv2\n+runner. Adding one safely is a framework/netd feature, not a small app-only\n+patch.\n+\n+Smallest credible future implementation:\n+\n+1. Add a platform WireGuard profile/type or Worm-specific system service in\n+   system_server.\n+2. Add a native helper/controller for rtnetlink interface creation and\n+   WireGuard generic-netlink configuration.\n+3. Register the resulting `wg` interface as a secure netd virtual network.\n+4. Attach protected UID ranges through existing secure VPN routing rules.\n+5. Configure protected DNS on that VPN netId.\n+6. Use `protectFromVpn()` only for the numeric endpoint bootstrap UDP socket.\n+7. Recreate the kernel interface on underlying network changes.\n+8. Tear down or mark the VPN unavailable on handshake/runtime failure.\n+9. Keep lockdown/prohibit rules active whenever the protected network is not\n+   proven ready.\n+\n+This is feasible as a larger framework integration project, but not feasible as\n+the requested minimum implementation using only existing in-tree backend code.\n+\n*** Add File: PATCH-WORMOS-NATIVE-KERNEL-WIREGUARD-V2/03-LOCKDOWN.md\n+# Lockdown Compatibility\n+\n+Existing lockdown semantics are tied to Android VPN ownership:\n+\n+- `Vpn.setVpnForcedLocked()` computes UID ranges and calls\n+  `ConnectivityManager.setRequireVpnForUids()`.\n+- netd installs `RULE_PRIORITY_PROHIBIT_NON_VPN` prohibit rules for UIDs that\n+  must not use non-protected sockets.\n+- Secure virtual networks install high-priority UID routing rules using the\n+  protected VPN interface route table.\n+\n+Kernel WireGuard can be compatible only if the kernel WG interface is attached\n+to this same secure VPN model.\n+\n+An app-level privileged component cannot safely claim equivalent semantics just\n+by creating routes. Direct kernel routes without ConnectivityService/netd VPN\n+ownership risk app UID traffic using physical networks during boot, reconnect,\n+DNS failure, or interface loss.\n+\n+Conclusion:\n+\n+- Existing lockdown can be reused only if framework/netd represents kernel WG\n+  as the active secure VPN network.\n+- The current `VpnService` TUN model cannot use kernel WG without a userspace\n+  packet pump.\n+\n*** Add File: PATCH-WORMOS-NATIVE-KERNEL-WIREGUARD-V2/04-DESIGN-OPTIONS.md\n+# Remaining Architecture Options\n+\n+Option A: audited userspace WireGuard backend behind `VpnService`\n+\n+- Keeps current WormSystemWireGuard shape.\n+- Reuses Android VPN lockdown semantics directly.\n+- Requires importing and auditing a real userspace WireGuard backend.\n+- Lower framework blast radius.\n+- More CPU cost than kernel WG.\n+\n+Option B: deeper framework/netd kernel WireGuard integration\n+\n+- Uses existing kernel WireGuard data plane.\n+- Requires new trusted platform VPN runner/service and native netlink control.\n+- Must add Android NetworkAgent/netd integration for the kernel interface.\n+- Must preserve secure VPN UID routing, protected DNS, bootstrap-only endpoint\n+  exception, and handover behavior.\n+- Higher framework and SELinux blast radius.\n+\n+No option was implemented in this patch because the current tree does not\n+contain a complete kernel-backed WireGuard Android Network integration.\n+\n*** Add File: PATCH-WORMOS-NATIVE-KERNEL-WIREGUARD-V2/05-SECURITY-INVARIANTS.md\n+# Security Invariants\n+\n+Required invariants for any future implementation:\n+\n+- No application UID traffic may use the physical uplink while Worm protected\n+  networking is enabled unless that UID is explicitly excluded by policy.\n+- The only bootstrap exception is UDP to `2.28.34.27:51823`.\n+- Bootstrap must not require public DNS.\n+- Protected DNS is `10.60.0.1` after the tunnel is ready.\n+- IPv4 and IPv6 must both be either protected or blocked.\n+- If the WG interface, peer configuration, route, DNS, or handshake fails,\n+  application networking must remain blocked.\n+- Underlying network changes must leave traffic protected or blocked, never\n+  direct.\n+- WireGuard private keys and PSKs must never be embedded in source, images,\n+  target-files, logs, or reports.\n+- SELinux must remain enforcing with no permissive domains or broad allow rules.\n+\n*** Add File: PATCH-WORMOS-NATIVE-KERNEL-WIREGUARD-V2/06-FILES-REQUIRING-CHANGE.md\n+# Files Requiring Change For A Future Kernel-WG Implementation\n+\n+Likely framework/system files:\n+\n+- `frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Vpn.java`\n+- `frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/VpnManagerService.java`\n+- `frameworks/base/core/java/android/net/VpnManager.java`\n+- `frameworks/base/core/java/android/net/PlatformVpnProfile.java`\n+- `frameworks/base/core/java/com/android/internal/net/VpnProfile.java`\n+\n+Likely netd/native files:\n+\n+- `system/netd/server/NetdNativeService.cpp`\n+- `system/netd/server/NetworkController.cpp`\n+- `system/netd/server/RouteController.cpp`\n+- New native controller for rtnetlink and WireGuard generic netlink.\n+\n+Likely API/AIDL files:\n+\n+- `packages/modules/Connectivity/framework/src/android/net/IConnectivityManager.aidl`\n+- netd AIDL only if new explicit WireGuard operations are exposed through netd.\n+\n+Likely SELinux files:\n+\n+- `system/sepolicy/private/system_server.te`\n+- `system/sepolicy/private/netd.te`\n+- `system/sepolicy/private/service.te`\n+- file/service contexts for any new native helper.\n+\n+Current Worm app files likely become state/UX/provisioning only, or are removed\n+from data-plane ownership after platform integration:\n+\n+- `vendor/worm/WormSystemWireGuard/`\n+\n*** Add File: PATCH-WORMOS-NATIVE-KERNEL-WIREGUARD-V2/test-results.txt\n+KERNEL_WG_PRESENT=PASS\n+WG_UAPI_AVAILABLE=PASS\n+GENL_CONTROL_PATH=PARTIAL_HEADERS_PRESENT_NO_WG_CONTROLLER\n+ANDROID_NETWORK_INTEGRATION=NOT_AVAILABLE_FOR_KERNEL_WG\n+UID_ROUTING_INTEGRATION=REQUIRES_FRAMEWORK_NETD_VIRTUAL_NETWORK_INTEGRATION\n+LOCKDOWN_COMPATIBILITY=NOT_COMPATIBLE_APP_ONLY\n+DNS_INTEGRATION=REQUIRES_CONNECTIVITY_NETD_VPN_NETID\n+UNDERLYING_NETWORK_HANDOVER=REQUIRES_PLATFORM_RUNNER_OR_SYSTEM_SERVER_SERVICE\n+BOOT_FAIL_CLOSED_DESIGN=DESIGN_IDENTIFIED_NOT_IMPLEMENTED\n+IPV4_FAIL_CLOSED_DESIGN=DESIGN_IDENTIFIED_NOT_IMPLEMENTED\n+IPV6_FAIL_CLOSED_DESIGN=DESIGN_IDENTIFIED_NOT_IMPLEMENTED\n+SELINUX_DESIGN=REQUIRES_NEW_MINIMAL_POLICY_AFTER_CONTROLLER_SELECTION\n+KERNEL_WG_FRAMEWORK_INTEGRATION=NOT_FEASIBLE\n+IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS=STOPPED_AT_DECISION_GATE\n+BUILD_STATUS=NOT_RUN_DOCS_ONLY\n+DEVICE_TESTS_REQUIRED=YES\n+OTA_READY=NO\n+\n*** Add File: PATCH-WORMOS-NATIVE-KERNEL-WIREGUARD-V2/findings.json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"id\": \"P1-KERNELWG-FRAMEWORK-001\",\n+    \"severity\": \"P1\",\n+    \"component\": \"Android framework/netd\",\n+    \"evidence\": \"Kernel WireGuard symbols and UAPI are present, but no existing Android platform WireGuard VPN runner or complete kernel-WG NetworkAgent/netd integration was found.\",\n+    \"risk\": \"A kernel wg interface configured outside Android secure VPN ownership can leak app traffic during boot, failure, handover, DNS failure, or interface loss.\",\n+    \"remediation\": \"Implement a platform WireGuard VPN runner/service with native rtnetlink and WireGuard generic-netlink control, attach wg to a secure netd virtual network, and reuse lockdown UID prohibit semantics.\",\n+    \"blocks_source_pass\": true,\n+    \"blocks_ota\": true\n+  },\n+  {\n+    \"id\": \"P1-WG-BACKEND-001\",\n+    \"severity\": \"P1\",\n+    \"component\": \"WormSystemWireGuard\",\n+    \"evidence\": \"Current WormSystemWireGuard owns fail-closed VpnService scaffolding but has no packet backend. Kernel WG cannot consume VpnService TUN packets without a userspace backend.\",\n+    \"risk\": \"Device remains blocked or can only be made to work by weakening fail-closed semantics.\",\n+    \"remediation\": \"Choose either audited userspace backend behind 