KVeZYivpPUnWKv6mRFSDKFZYVeGzZCUqKwMBPcfr3Gsq2Qcj-BLTZJWOT577OgQJgV8RlS-3djrgJ1zCuyHC4padz1xW2sA4YwM_wxpO34HtYXpjMx6mK7M6GjjYK9Gg6goF7rd586DJ7KiCxD6173l7wYEE_0Y-pOra_4SR9-S2KxHdXLvfA==","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07f96-c499-7022-94d2-12be5639010e"}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_0d4d71abca8c0b20016a9fa3bd969c87d2b1506158029b1fc4","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"I’m creating the V3 artifact as a decision record with backend recommendation and the exact stop condition. The recommendation is source-vendoring the official WireGuard Android tunnel components plus `wireguard-go`, but I’m not importing source in this step because the audit phase had to complete first and no pinned source bundle is present locally."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07f96-c499-7022-94d2-12be5639010e","create_time":1788847029.717068,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0d4d71abca8c0b20016a9fa3bf013887d299ac3d7a4f573f35","status":"completed","call_id":"call_YYE4PkMz6mCb5pmkoGGAr8ig","name":"apply_patch","input":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3/README.md\n+# PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3\n+\n+Status: BACKEND SELECTION AUDIT COMPLETE / SOURCE INTEGRATION NOT STARTED.\n+\n+This patch evaluates source-built userspace WireGuard backends for completing\n+`WormSystemWireGuard` behind Android `VpnService` while preserving existing\n+Android VPN lockdown semantics.\n+\n+Decision:\n+\n+- `BACKEND_RECOMMENDATION=wireguard-android tunnel library with source-built wireguard-go`\n+- `IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS=BLOCKED_PENDING_SOURCE_VENDOR_IMPORT`\n+- `OTA_READY=NO`\n+\n+No OPNsense, server WireGuard, NAT, DNS, FireHOL, public IP, private backbone,\n+or external infrastructure configuration was modified.\n+\n*** Add File: PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3/01-BACKEND-SELECTION.md\n+# Backend Selection Audit\n+\n+## Recommendation\n+\n+`BACKEND_RECOMMENDATION=official WireGuard Android tunnel backend`\n+\n+Use the official WireGuard Android tunnel backend components, source-vendored\n+from `wireguard-android`, together with the source-built userspace\n+`wireguard-go` backend used by that project.\n+\n+Do not vendor the full user-facing WireGuard app UI. Import only backend,\n+configuration, crypto, and JNI/native pieces needed to run the tunnel from the\n+system-owned Worm service.\n+\n+## Upstream\n+\n+- Project: WireGuard Android\n+- Upstream source: `https://git.zx2c4.com/wireguard-android`\n+- Backend: Android `GoBackend` / tunnel library using `wireguard-go`\n+- Maintainer status: official WireGuard project, listed as Complete.\n+\n+## Version / Commit Policy\n+\n+Pin an exact upstream git commit before import.\n+\n+Record:\n+\n+- upstream remote URL\n+- commit hash\n+- source archive or git tree checksum\n+- license files\n+- local import diff\n+\n+No floating branch dependency is acceptable for production.\n+\n+## License\n+\n+- WireGuard Android tunnel library: Apache-2.0.\n+- `wireguard-go`: official WireGuard userspace implementation; license must be\n+  preserved from the pinned source tree during import.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+Expected source dependencies:\n+\n+- Java/Kotlin tunnel/config code from official WireGuard Android.\n+- JNI/native bridge used by the Android tunnel backend.\n+- Go toolchain for building `wireguard-go`.\n+- Android NDK integration for producing the backend shared library.\n+\n+Local tree evidence:\n+\n+- `/opt/Android/grapheneos-frankel-17/prebuilts/go/linux-x86/bin/go` exists.\n+- No `wireguard-go`, `wg`, `wg-quick`, or WireGuard Android tunnel source is\n+  currently vendored in the tree.\n+\n+## Rationale\n+\n+This is the smallest maintained path aligned with Android `VpnService`:\n+\n+- It keeps Android VPN lockdown semantics.\n+- It works with a TUN file descriptor.\n+- It avoids a deep framework/netd kernel WireGuard rewrite.\n+- It does not require the user-facing WireGuard app.\n+- It can be built from source and packaged as part of WormOS.\n+\n*** Add File: PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3/02-CANDIDATES.md\n+# Candidate Matrix\n+\n+## Official WireGuard Android Tunnel\n+\n+- Upstream project: `wireguard-android`\n+- Language: Java/Kotlin plus native Go backend\n+- Android compatibility: native Android project\n+- TUN compatibility: yes, designed for Android `VpnService`\n+- Maintenance: official WireGuard project, Complete\n+- Source-build requirements: Android build integration, Go toolchain, NDK/JNI\n+- Dependency footprint: backend/config/crypto/tunnel components only\n+- License: Apache-2.0 for Android tunnel library; preserve bundled backend\n+  licenses from source import\n+- Integration complexity: medium\n+- Security implications: best match for Android lockdown because it sits behind\n+  `VpnService`\n+\n+## wireguard-go Direct\n+\n+- Upstream project: `wireguard-go`\n+- Language: Go\n+- Android compatibility: possible, but Android TUN and service lifecycle glue\n+  must be supplied\n+- TUN compatibility: yes at userspace-WireGuard layer\n+- Maintenance: official WireGuard project, Complete^{}\n+- Source-build requirements: Go cross-build, JNI/control wrapper, Android\n+  service integration\n+- Dependency footprint: lower than full Android project but more custom glue\n+- License: preserve from pinned upstream source\n+- Integration complexity: high without WireGuard Android tunnel glue\n+- Security implications: more custom code around TUN ownership, socket protect,\n+  lifecycle, and configuration parsing\n+\n+## wireguard-rs\n+\n+- Upstream project: official WireGuard repositories list includes `wireguard-rs`\n+- Language: Rust\n+- Android compatibility: not established in this tree\n+- TUN compatibility: userspace implementation goal\n+- Maintenance: Active, not listed Complete\n+- Source-build requirements: Rust cross-build and Android service integration\n+- Dependency footprint: unknown for this tree\n+- License: must be verified before any import\n+- Integration complexity: high\n+- Security implications: larger unproven integration path for Android\n+\n+## BoringTun\n+\n+- Upstream project: Cloudflare BoringTun\n+- Language: Rust\n+- Android compatibility: not validated in this tree\n+- TUN compatibility: userspace WireGuard implementation\n+- Maintenance: auditable but not an official WireGuard project\n+- Source-build requirements: Rust/Cargo integration\n+- Dependency footprint: separate Rust dependency graph\n+- License: must be preserved from upstream\n+- Integration complexity: high\n+- Security implications: less aligned with official Android WireGuard path\n+\n+## Selected\n+\n+`BACKEND_SELECTED=wireguard-android tunnel + wireguard-go`\n+\n*** Add File: PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3/03-INTEGRATION-PLAN.md\n+# Integration Plan\n+\n+Source integration should proceed only after a pinned upstream revision is\n+selected and reviewed.\n+\n+Minimum source-vendored import:\n+\n+1. Import official WireGuard Android tunnel/config/crypto backend code.\n+2. Import `wireguard-go` source required by the Android backend.\n+3. Exclude UI, import/export activities, settings screens, QR scanners, and\n+   user-facing app code.\n+4. Add Android.bp/Soong integration or a reviewed build wrapper that compiles\n+   the backend from source using the in-tree Go toolchain.\n+5. Produce a source-built backend library/binary in the WormOS product image.\n+6. Link or load that backend only from the privileged Worm system component.\n+7. Connect `WormSystemWireGuardService` TUN fd to the real backend.\n+8. Use `VpnService.protect()` or equivalent protected socket handling only for\n+   the WireGuard endpoint transport socket.\n+9. Keep always-on lockdown active with no app bypass allowlist.\n+10. Store private device identity only through runtime provisioning.\n+\n+This patch does not perform the import because no pinned source revision or\n+source bundle is present locally yet.\n+\n*** Add File: PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3/04-FAIL-CLOSED.md\n+# Fail-Closed Design\n+\n+The selected userspace backend preserves the current fail-closed direction:\n+\n+- Android app UID traffic is routed into the `VpnService` TUN.\n+- Android lockdown blocks app UID traffic when the VPN is absent.\n+- The WireGuard backend reads packets from the TUN.\n+- Only the backend's protected transport socket may use the underlying\n+  physical network to reach `2.28.34.27:51823`.\n+- DNS is configured to `10.60.0.1` through the VPN network after establishment.\n+\n+Required runtime states:\n+\n+- Startup before backend ready: blocked.\n+- Backend crash: blocked.\n+- Peer unreachable: blocked or protected retry, never direct.\n+- Handover: protected or blocked.\n+- IPv4: protected or blocked.\n+- IPv6: protected or blocked.\n+- DNS failure: no direct resolver fallback.\n+\n+Device validation is required before any runtime PASS.\n+\n*** Add File: PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3/05-SECURITY.md\n+# Security\n+\n+No secrets were added.\n+\n+The backend import must preserve:\n+\n+- source build only;\n+- no opaque binaries;\n+- no runtime downloads;\n+- no Play Services dependency;\n+- no user-installed WireGuard app dependency;\n+- no private keys or PSKs in source, APK, product image, target-files, logs, or\n+  reports;\n+- SELinux enforcing;\n+- no permissive domains;\n+- no broad wildcard allow rules;\n+- no neverallow bypass.\n+\n+Runtime provisioning remains required for the device private key.\n+\n*** Add File: PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3/06-BUILD-VALIDATION.md\n+# Build Validation\n+\n+Not run for V3 because source integration was not started.\n+\n+Reason:\n+\n+- The selected backend is not currently vendored in the tree.\n+- A pinned upstream source revision must be selected and imported before build\n+  validation is meaningful.\n+\n+Previous V1 state remains:\n+\n+- WormSystemWireGuard scaffolding build: PASS.\n+- target-files-package build: PASS.\n+- SELinux: PASS.\n+- no secrets: PASS.\n+\n+Those results do not prove WG backend runtime.\n+\n*** Add File: PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3/07-DEVICE-TESTS.md\n+# Device Test Package\n+\n+Required after source backend integration and flashing:\n+\n+- AUTO_START\n+- WG_RUNTIME\n+- FAIL_CLOSED_IPV4\n+- FAIL_CLOSED_IPV6\n+- FAIL_CLOSED_BOOT\n+- FAIL_CLOSED_HANDOVER\n+- FAIL_CLOSED_BACKEND_CRASH\n+- FAIL_CLOSED_PEER_UNREACHABLE\n+- PROTECTED_DNS\n+- PRIVATE_ACCESS\n+- PUBLIC_IPV4\n+\n+Each test must be performed on a physical WormOS device.\n+\n+Until then:\n+\n+`DEVICE_TESTS_REQUIRED=YES`\n+\n*** Add File: PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3/test-results.txt\n+SOURCE_IMPLEMENTATION=PARTIAL\n+BUILD=NOT_RUN\n+SELINUX=PREVIOUS_PASS_NOT_RERUN\n+SYSTEM_OWNED_WG=PASS\n+WG_BACKEND=NOT_IMPLEMENTED\n+BACKEND_SOURCE_BUILD=NOT_RUN\n+BACKEND_PINNED=NO\n+LOCKDOWN_INTEGRATION=DESIGN_IDENTIFIED\n+AUTO_START=DEVICE_TEST_REQUIRED\n+WG_RUNTIME=BLOCKED_PENDING_BACKEND_IMPORT\n+FAIL_CLOSED_IPV4=DEVICE_TEST_REQUIRED\n+FAIL_CLOSED_IPV6=DEVICE_TEST_REQUIRED\n+FAIL_CLOSED_BOOT=DEVICE_TEST_REQUIRED\n+FAIL_CLOSED_HANDOVER=DEVICE_TEST_REQUIRED\n+FAIL_CLOSED_BACKEND_CRASH=DEVICE_TEST_REQUIRED\n+FAIL_CLOSED_PEER_UNREACHABLE=DEVICE_TEST_REQUIRED\n+PROTECTED_DNS=DEVICE_TEST_REQUIRED\n+PRIVATE_ACCESS=DEVICE_TEST_REQUIRED\n+PUBLIC_IPV4=DEVICE_TEST_REQUIRED\n+NO_SECRETS=PASS\n+SERVER_NETWORK=FROZEN_UNCHANGED\n+WORM_OS_SYSTEM_NETWORK=PARTIAL\n+BACKEND_SELECTED=wireguard-android-tunnel-plus-wireguard-go\n+UPSTREAM_REVISION=NOT_PINNED\n+LICENSE_STATUS=PRELIMINARY_OK_REQUIRES_PINNED_SOURCE_NOTICE_REVIEW\n+DEPENDENCY_AUDIT=PRELIMINARY_OK_REQUIRES_PINNED_SOURCE_REVIEW\n+OTA_READY=NO\n+\n*** Add File: PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3/findings.json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"id\": \"P1-BACKEND-SOURCE-IMPORT-001\",\n+    \"severity\": \"P1\",\n+    \"component\": \"WormSystemWireGuard backend\",\n+    \"evidence\": \"Official WireGuard Android tunnel plus wireguard-go is the recommended backend, but no pinned upstream source is currently vendored in the tree.\",\n+    \"risk\": \"WormSystemWireGuard still cannot pass packets through a real WireGuard tunnel.\",\n+    \"remediation\": \"Pin and vendor the minimum official WireGuard Android tunnel and wireguard-go source, integrate source build into Soong, and connect it to the WormSystemWireGuard VpnService TUN.\",\n+    \"blocks_source_pass\": true,\n+    \"blocks_ota\": true\n+  },\n+  {\n+    \"id\": \"P1-DEVICE-RUNTIME-001\",\n+    \"severity\": \"P1\",\n+    \"component\": \"device validation\",\n+    \"evidence\": \"No flashed image with source-built backend has been tested.\",\n+    \"risk\": \"Fail-closed, protected DNS, handover, and runtime WireGuard behavior are unproven.\",\n+    \"remediation\": \"After backend integration and build, flash a physical device and run the V3 runtime test package.\",\n+    \"blocks_source_pass\": false,\n+    \"blocks_ota\": true\n+  }\n+]\n+\n*** Add File: PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3/modified-files.txt\n+/opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3/README.md\n+/opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3/01-BACKEND-SELECTION.md\n+/opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3/02-CANDIDATES.md\n+/opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3/03-INTEGRATION-PLAN.md\n+/opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3/04-FAIL-CLOSED.md\n+/opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3/05-SECURITY.md\n+/opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3/06-BUILD-VALIDATION.md\n+/opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3/07-DEVICE-TESTS.md\n+/opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3/test-results.txt\n+/opt/Android/PATCH-WORMOS-SYSTEM-WG-BACKEND-V3/findings.json\n+\n*** End Patch\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07f96-c499-7022-94d2-12be5639010e","create_time":1788847029.717068}},{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a07f98-8235-70b2-b39c-124376451450","call_id":"call_YYE4PkMz6mCb5pmkoGGAr8ig","output":"Exit code: 0\nWall time: 1.1 secon