ypair\n- 10.60.0.1/24\n- UDP/51821\n- PF\n- NAT\n- DNS\n- FireHOL\n- routing\n- public IPs\n- private IPs\n\nCurrent problem:\nwg0 is UP but has ZERO peers.\n\nProvision persistently the existing Android peer:\n\nName:\nworm-os-test-01\n\nPublicKey:\njxZ2fEyoynXMrhNPZitfKY1kqMZBZ/6bYLbyZb6XCXM=\n\nAllowedIP:\n10.60.0.10/32\n\nIMPORTANT:\nThis must be written to the authoritative persistent OPNsense\nconfiguration, not only applied with `wg set`.\n\nNever print any private key.\n\nAfter applying/reloading safely verify:\n\nwg show wg0\nwg show wg0 peers\nwg show wg0 allowed-ips\n\nExpected:\n\nPEER_PRESENT=YES\nANDROID_PUBLIC_KEY=\njxZ2fEyoynXMrhNPZitfKY1kqMZBZ/6bYLbyZb6XCXM=\n\nALLOWED_IP=\n10.60.0.10/32\n\nThen verify the authoritative OPNsense configuration contains the peer\nand that it will survive service restart/reboot.\n\nSTOP after peer provisioning and print:\n\nPEER RESTORED - ENABLE ANDROID WIREGUARD NOW\n\nThen monitor for 90 seconds:\n\n- wg show wg0\n- WAN UDP/51821\n- handshake\n- RX/TX\n\nAndroid is currently using SPLIT TUNNEL:\n\nAddress:\n10.60.0.10/32\n\nAllowedIPs:\n10.60.0.0/24,10.90.0.0/16\n\nDNS:\n1.1.1.1\n\nEndpoint:\n2.28.34.27:51821\n\nDo NOT change Android configuration during this test.\n\nIf handshake becomes RECENT:\n\ntest sequentially:\n\n10.60.0.1\n10.90.10.1\n10.90.20.10\n10.90.20.10:22\n\nThen test real private SSH.\n\nFinal report:\n\nPEER_PERSISTENT=\nHANDSHAKE=\nRX=\nTX=\nOPNSENSE_WG=\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE=\nWORM_ROBOT_PRIVATE=\nWORM_ROBOT_SSH=\nPRIVATE_WORM_FOUNDATION=\n\nDo not start full-tunnel work."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a078d9-1344-7c62-a6a1-55e72d5a92d8","create_time":1788733887.3266647,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a078dd-4800-7550-ae75-7ca0fdf5f511","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"ll"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a078dd-47e8-7e20-bfb7-72cf2715cba3","create_time":1788734162.9444172,"content_item_