/root/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T18-02-21-01a07774-da5a-7751-beb8-16e2ba629dff.jsonl:17851:{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T16:49:51.543Z","ordinal":17849,"type":"compacted","payload":{"message":"","replacement_history":[{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a07893-2ca1-72e2-8e01-3b6ed8688cf1","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Implement PATCH-NET-007-PRIVATE-NETWORK-HARDENING.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nThe frozen Worm network architecture MUST NOT change.\n\nFROZEN TOPOLOGY:\n\nworm-robot PUBLIC:\n162.55.6.173\n\nworm-robot PRIVATE:\n10.90.20.10\n\nOPNsense PUBLIC / worm-os egress:\n2.28.34.27\n\nOPNsense PRIVATE:\n10.90.10.1\n\nOPNsense WireGuard:\n10.60.0.1/24\n\nworm-os:\n10.60.0.x/32\n\nHetzner private backbone:\n10.90.0.0/16\n\nADMIN WireGuard:\n10.77.0.0/24\n\nvSwitch:\n85469\n\nVLAN:\n40…2170 tokens truncated…n worm-robot\nPASS public Web disabled\nPASS public OTA/download denied\nPASS private Worm routing\nPASS DNS protected\nPASS IPv6 leak protection\nPASS no public fallback\nPASS reboot persistence or explicitly documented PENDING blocker\nPASS no secrets\n\nFinal output:\n\nPATCH-NET-007 STATUS:\nPASS / PARTIAL / BLOCKED\n\nThen rerun:\n\nWORM PRE-CHECK AUDIT\n\nExpected final gate:\n\nWORM PRE-CHECK: PASS\n\nDo not start another patch automatically."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07893-2c86-7791-9c14-76b5631ce08a","create_time":1788729306.2736113,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a07893-b122-7192-919e-0c1fe0fc832f","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Perform FINAL WORM INFRASTRUCTURE AUDIT before enabling\nWireGuard as a native/system component of worm-os.\n\nAUDIT ONLY.\n\nDO NOT:\n- modify networking\n- modify OPNsense\n- modify FireHOL\n- reload firewall\n- change NAT\n- change DNS\n- change WireGuard keys\n- recreate peers\n- restart services unless strictly required for a read-only test\n- reboot\n- modify Android/ex-graphene\n- start the system WireGuard implementation\n\n==================================================\nPURPOSE\n==================================================\n\nDetermine whether the current infrastructure is safe and ready for:\n\nWORM-OS SYSTEM WIREGUARD\n\nThe final decision MUST be exactly:\n\nREADY FOR WORM-OS SYSTEM WIREGUARD\n\nor:\n\nNOT READY FOR WORM-OS SYSTEM WIREGUARD\n\n==================================================\nFROZEN ARCHITECTURE\n==================================================\n\nINTERNET\n\nworm-robot PUBLIC:\n162.55.6.173\n\nworm-robot PRIVATE:\n10.90.20.10\n\nOPNsense PUBLIC / worm-os dedicated egress:\n2.28.34.27\n\nOPNsense PRIVATE:\n10.90.10.1\n\nOPNsense WireGuard:\n10.60.0.1/24\n\nworm-os peers:\n10.60.0.x/32\n\nHetzner private backbone:\n10.90.0.0/16\n\nADMIN WireGuard:\n10.77.0.0/24\n\nvSwitch:\n85469\n\nVLAN:\n4000\n\nThis topology is FROZEN.\n\n==================================================\n1. VERIFY PATCH STATE\n==================================================\n\nAudit all existing relevant patches:\n\nPATCH-NET-001-OPNSENSE-PRIVATE-IP\nPATCH-NET-002-WORM-ROBOT-PRIVATE-IP\nPATCH-NET-003-WORM-OS-PRIVATE-IP\nPATCH-NET-004-WORM-OS-PUBLIC-EGRESS\nPATCH-NET-004B-OPNSENSE-WORMOS-MANAGEMENT\nPATCH-NET-005-DISABLE-PUBLIC-WEB\nPATCH-NET-006-WORM-PRIVATE-OTA-DOWNLOADS\nPATCH-NET-007-PRIVATE-NETWORK-HARDENING\n\nFor each report:\n\nPASS\nPARTIAL\nPENDING\nFAIL\nNOT IMPLEMENTED\n\nA P0/P1 unresolved networking/security issue blocks system integration.\n\n==================================================\n2. REAL WIREGUARD CLIENT\n==================================================\n\nVerify the existing real Android test peer.\n\nExpected client:\n10.60.0.10/32\n\nVerify:\n- peer exists\n- public key matches provisioned peer\n- AllowedIP exactly 10.60.0.10/32\n- latest handshake RECENT while client is connected\n- RX > 0\n- TX > 0\n- UDP/51821 operational\n\nNever print private keys.\n\n==================================================\n3. FULL-TUNNEL INTERNET\n==================================================\n\nWith real Android client connected:\n\nAllowedIPs:\n0.0.0.0/0\n\nVerify actual Internet access.\n\nVerify using at least two independent HTTPS observations that:\n\nPUBLIC_EGRESS_IPV4=2.28.34.27\n\nThe test MUST be performed from the client path.\nDo not infer PASS merely from NAT configuration.\n\nVerify:\n- HTTPS works\n- normal TCP works\n- DNS works\n- network transitions do not immediately break tunnel\n\n==================================================\n4. DNS\n==================================================\n\nExpected protected resolver:\n10.60.0.1\n\nVerify from real worm-os test client:\n- UDP/53 works\n- TCP/53 works where appropriate\n- ordinary hostname resolution works\n- resolver is not exposed publicly on WAN\n- no underlying mobile/Wi-Fi DNS fallback during protected mode\n\nReport:\nDNS_PROTECTED=PASS/FAIL\n\n==================================================\n5. IPV6 LEAK\n==================================================\n\nCritical gate.\n\nVerify whether the Android client has native IPv6 from 5G/Wi-Fi.\n\nWhile full-tunnel WireGuard is enabled:\n- verify IPv6 cannot bypass OPNsense\n- verify external IPv6 is either tunneled according to an explicit design\n  or unavailable by deliberate policy\n\nDo not mark PASS merely because IPv4 works.\n\nReport:\nIPV6_LEAK=NONE/DETECTED/UNTESTED\n\nUNTESTED blocks production system-WireGuard activation.\n\n==================================================\n6. FAIL-CLOSED REQUIREMENT\n==================================================\n\nThis is critical for native worm-os integration.\n\nVerify infrastructure supports:\n\nWireGuard available:\nWorm private services reachable through protected route.\n\nWireGuard unavailable:\nWorm private services NOT reachable through public fallback.\n\nCheck:\n- OTA\n- image.zip\n- update metadata\n- update payloads\n- Worm downloads\n- Apps private distribution\n- backup/private APIs where implemented\n\nVerify no client configuration points to a public fallback.\n\nReport:\nPRIVATE_SERVICES_FAIL_CLOSED=PASS/FAIL/PENDING\n\nFAIL blocks system integration.\nPENDING blocks production activation if the corresponding service is\nalready expected to ship.\n\n==================================================\n7. OPNsense MANAGEMENT POLICY\n==================================================\n\nFrozen policy:\n\nworm-os 10.60.0.0/24\n        ->\nOPNsense 10.60.0.1\n\nRequired:\nTCP/22  ALLOW\nTCP/80  ALLOW\nTCP/443 ALLOW\n\nVerify from real WireGuard client.\n\nWAN must remain:\n\n2.28.34.27:22  CLOSED/FILTERED\n2.28.34.27:80  CLOSED/FILTERED\n2.28.34.27:443 CLOSED/FILTERED\n\nUDP/51821:\nAVAILABLE\n\nVerify IPv6 does not bypass WAN management restrictions.\n\n==================================================\n8. WORM-ROBOT PRIVATE PATH\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nworm-os\n10.60.0.x\n ->\nOPNsense\n ->\n10.90.20.10\n\nConfirm permitted Worm private service traffic works.\n\nConfirm worm-os cannot reach worm-robot SSH unless explicitly allowed\nby frozen policy.\n\nConfirm worm-os cannot reach:\n10.77.0.0/24 ADMIN\n\n==================================================\n9. WORM-ROBOT\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nPUBLIC:\n162.55.6.173\n\nPRIVATE:\n10.90.20.10\n\nVLAN:\n4000\n\nMTU:\n1400\n\nPRIVATE ROUTE:\n10.90.0.0/16 via expected private path\n\nVerify:\nnet.ipv4.ip_forward=0\n\nworm-robot MUST NOT become a router for worm-os.\n\n==================================================\n10. FIREHOL\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n- installed\n- enabled\n- active\n- configuration valid\n- public default deny\n- SSH policy correct\n- ADMIN WireGuard policy correct\n- blocklist mechanism status\n- private interface not trusted-any\n- no broad forwarding\n- IPv4 filtering\n- IPv6 filtering\n\nRecord wildcard listeners separately.\n\nReview especially:\n*:9094\n*:5353\nand any other wildcard socket.\n\nA wildcard listener protected correctly by FireHOL may be WARN,\nbut an unintended publicly reachable service is FAIL.\n\n==================================================\n11. PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION\n==================================================\n\nVerify public Internet CANNOT retrieve:\n\n- Web Installer\n- WebUSB\n- image.zip\n- OTA metadata\n- OTA payloads\n- Worm downloads\n- private Apps content\n\nTest:\n- hostname\n- direct IPv4\n- IPv6\n- alternate Host header where relevant\n- TCP/80\n- TCP/443\n- UDP/443/HTTP3\n\nExpected:\nPUBLIC_WORM_DISTRIBUTION=DENIED\n\n==================================================\n12. PRIVATE OTA / DOWNLOADS\n==================================================\n\nVerify intended private path:\n\nworm-os\n ->\nWireGuard\n ->\nOPNsense\n ->\nworm-robot 10.90.20.10\n\nWhere implemented verify:\n- metadata\n- payload\n- image.zip\n- downloads\n\nVerify OTA signature/integrity verification remains unchanged.\n\nWireGuard transport MUST NOT replace Android OTA cryptographic\nverification.\n\n==================================================\n13. STALE RULES\n==================================================\n\nAudit:\n- iptables\n- nftables\n- PF\n- NAT\n- FORWARD\n\nIdentify stale troubleshooting rules from previous recovery work.\n\nNo unexplained broad forwarding/NAT rule may remain.\n\nDo not delete anything during this audit.\n\n==================================================\n14. REBOOT/PERSISTENCE STATUS\n==================================================\n\nReport persistence status for:\n\nOPNsense:\n- private interface\n- WireGuard\n- peer\n- NAT\n- firewall\n- DNS\n\nworm-robot:\n- VLAN 4000\n- 10.90.20.10\n- route\n- FireHOL\n- ADMIN WG\n- ip_forward=0\n\nIf reboot persistence has already been tested, record PASS.\n\nIf not:\nPENDING REBOOT VALIDATION\n\nDetermine whether this is blocking based on whether the exact persistent\nconfiguration has otherwise been verified.\n\n==================================================\n15. SYSTEM-WIREGUARD PREREQUISITES\n==================================================\n\nAudit ex-graphene/Worm OS source READ-ONLY.\n\nDetermine:\n\n- kernel WireGuard support\n- userspace/platform WireGuard support\n- Android VPN framework capabilities\n- always-on VPN facilities\n- lockdown/fail-closed facilities\n- boot lifecycle hooks\n- ConnectivityService integration points\n- NetworkStack/netd implications\n- Android Keystore options\n- SELinux implications\n- backup exclusion mechanisms\n- OTA integration points\n- Wi-Fi/5G handover support\n\nDO NOT modify source.\n\n==================================================\n16. KEY MANAGEMENT GATE\n==================================================\n\nConfirm proposed system design can satisfy:\n\n- unique keypair per device\n- private key generated on device\n- private key never in source tree\n- private key never in factory image\n- private key never in OTA\n- private key excluded from backup\n- no private key in logs\n- no private key in dumpsys\n- public-key enrollment supported\n- per-device /32 assignment\n- individual peer revocation\n- OPNsense public-key rotation support\n\nAny design requiring one shared private key across Worm OS devices:\nP0 FAIL.\n\n==================================================\n17. SYSTEM PRIVACY POLICY GATE\n==================================================\n\nConfirm intended production policy:\n\nBOOT\n ->\nnetwork available\n ->\nsystem WireGuard\n ->\nhandshake\n ->\nprotected networking available\n ->\nWorm private services enabled\n\nNo race where OTA/apps/downloads contact public endpoints before\nWireGuard is ready.\n\nProduction target:\n\nAllowedIPs:\n0.0.0.0/0\n\nNo ordinary application can disable the Worm system tunnel.\n\nNetwork transitions:\nWi-Fi -> 5G\n5G -> Wi-Fi\nreconnect\nairplane mode\ntemporary loss\n\nmust have a viable recovery design.\n\n==================================================\n18. SECRET SCAN\n==================================================\n\nScan patch and audit documentation for:\n\nPrivateKey\nPresharedKey\npassword\nHetzner token\nSSH private key\nsigning private key\nbackup encryption key\n\nNever print secret values.\n\nPublic WireGuard keys are allowed.\n\n==================================================\n19. FINDING SEVERITY\n==================================================\n\nClassify every finding:\n\nP0 CRITICAL\nP1 HIGH\nP2 MEDIUM\nP3 LOW\nINFO\n\nFor every P0/P1 include:\n- component\n- evidence\n- risk\n- required remediation\n- whether it blocks system WireGuard\n\n==================================================\n20. OUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/root/WORM-SYSTEM-WIREGUARD-FINAL-AUDIT/\n\nInclude:\n\n00-EXECUTIVE-SUMMARY.md\n01-FROZEN-ARCHITECTURE.md\n02-PATCH-STATE.md\n03-WIREGUARD-LIVE.md\n04-FULL-TUNNEL.md\n05-DNS.md\n06-IPV6-LEAK.md\n07-FAIL-CLOSED.md\n08-OPNSENSE.md\n09-WORM-ROBOT.md\n10-FIREHOL.md\n11-PUBLIC-DISTRIBUTION.md\n12-PRIVATE-OTA.md\n13-PERSISTENCE.md\n14-ANDROID-PREREQUISITES.md\n15-KEY-MANAGEMENT.md\n16-SELINUX.md\n17-THREAT-MODEL.md\n18-SECRET-SCAN.md\n19-FINDINGS.md\n20-READINESS.md\n\nAlso:\nfindings.json\n\n==================================================\nFINAL GATE\n==================================================\n\nREADY requires at minimum:\n\nPASS frozen topology\nPASS real WireGuard handshake\nPASS RX/TX\nPASS full-tunnel Internet\nPASS public IPv4 = 2.28.34.27\nPASS protected DNS\nPASS no IPv6 leak\nPASS OPNsense WG management policy\nPASS OPNsense WAN management denied\nPASS private routing\nPASS ADMIN isolation\nPASS worm-robot ip_forward=0\nPASS FireHOL\nPASS public WebUSB/Web disabled\nPASS public OTA/download denied\nPASS private service fail-closed\nPASS per-device key-management design\nPASS no shared device private key\nPASS no critical secret leak\nPASS Android integration path identified\nPASS SELinux can remain enforcing\n\nIf any P0/P1 remains unresolved:\n\nNOT READY FOR WORM-OS SYSTEM WIREGUARD\n\nOtherwise:\n\nREADY FOR WORM-OS SYSTEM WIREGUARD\n\nDo not implement WireGuard in Android during this audit.\nDo not remediate automatically."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07893-b107-7692-bf60-95f72743a1fd","create_time":1788729340.1944475,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a0789d-93a6-7900-8d8a-6ca498738866","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Reclassify the final WireGuard audit into two separate gates.\n\nDO NOT modify infrastructure.\nDO NOT modify Android source yet.\n\nGATE A:\nREADY FOR WORM-OS SYSTEM WIREGUARD DEVELOPMENT\n\nGATE B:\nREADY FOR WORM-OS SYSTEM WIREGUARD PRODUCTION\n\nThe previous audit incorrectly treated the absence of the component\nwe intend to develop as a blocker to beginning its development.\n\nReclassify:\n\nP1-ANDROID-SYSTEMWG-001\n\"No completed native/system WireGuard component\"\n\nThis MUST NOT block DEVELOPMENT.\nIt MUST block PRODUCTION until implementation and device tests pass.\n\nP1-FAILCLOSED-001:\nNative fail-closed behavior is part of the system-WireGuard\nimplementation.\n\nIt MUST NOT block DEVELOPMENT.\nIt MUST block PRODUCTION until implemented and tested.\n\nThe following infrastructure/live-client findings remain prerequisites\nthat should be resolved or explicitly validated:\n\nP1-WG-LIVE-001\nP1-FULLTUNNEL-001\nP1-DNS-CLIENT-001\nP1-IPV6-LEAK-001\n\nNow perform a focused live-client validation using the real Android\nWireGuard client.\n\nImportant known correction:\nOPNsense actual public key starts with lowercase \"v\":\n\nvJtONCHbxMj3d7SAsPD5OFkTD7NcAoNgjIfmTcinE04=\n\nAndroid client peer configuration must use exactly that key.\n\nExpected client:\n10.60.0.10/32\n\nEndpoint:\n2.28.34.27:51821\n\nAllowedIPs:\n0.0.0.0/0\n\nDNS:\n10.60.0.1\n\nWhile the Android tunnel is enabled verify:\n\n1. recent WireGuard handshake\n2. RX > 0\n3. TX > 0\n4. Internet connectivity\n5. public IPv4 exactly 2.28.34.27\n6. DNS through 10.60.0.1\n7. IPv6 leak behavior\n8. 10.60.0.1 management reachability according to frozen policy\n9. private routing toward 10.90.0.0/16\n10. ADMIN 10.77.0.0/24 isolation\n\nDo not change keys, NAT, DNS or firewall merely because a test fails.\nIdentify the exact failing layer first.\n\nUpdate:\n/root/WORM-SYSTEM-WIREGUARD-FINAL-AUDIT/20-READINESS.md\n/root/WORM-SYSTEM-WIREGUARD-FINAL-AUDIT/19-FINDINGS.md\n/root/WORM-SYSTEM-WIREGUARD-FINAL-AUDIT/findings.json\n\nFinal output MUST contain TWO decisions:\n\nDEVELOPMENT GATE:\nREADY FOR WORM-OS SYSTEM WIREGUARD DEVELOPMENT\nor\nNOT READY FOR WORM-OS SYSTEM WIREGUARD DEVELOPMENT\n\nPRODUCTION GATE:\nREADY FOR WORM-OS SYSTEM WIREGUARD PRODUCTION\nor\nNOT READY FOR WORM-OS SYSTEM WIREGUARD PRODUCTION\n\nDo not implement the Android component yet."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0789d-935d-71f0-a318-73535221f6ad","create_time":1788729988.0068915,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a078a3-c179-7bf2-8723-4e192db548ab","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Perform WORM-OS SYSTEM WIREGUARD DEVELOPMENT GATE.\n\nAUDIT ONLY.\n\nDO NOT:\n- modify OPNsense\n- modify worm-robot\n- modify FireHOL\n- change NAT\n- change DNS\n- change WireGuard keys\n- recreate peers\n- reboot\n- modify ex-graphene/Worm OS source yet\n- start implementation\n\n==================================================\nGOAL\n==================================================\n\nDecide only whether we can START DEVELOPMENT of native/system WireGuard\ninside worm-os.\n\nThis is NOT the production-release gate.\n\nFinal decision must be exactly:\n\nREADY FOR WORM-OS SYSTEM WIREGUARD DEVELOPMENT\n\nor:\n\nNOT READY FOR WORM-OS SYSTEM WIREGUARD DEVELOPMENT\n\n==================================================\nFROZEN TOPOLOGY\n==================================================\n\nworm-robot PUBLIC:\n162.55.6.173\n\nworm-robot PRIVATE:\n10.90.20.10\n\nOPNsense PUBLIC / worm-os egress:\n2.28.34.27\n\nOPNsense PRIVATE:\n10.90.10.1\n\nOPNsense WireGuard:\n10.60.0.1/24\n\nworm-os peers:\n10.60.0.x/32\n\nHetzner private backbone:\n10.90.0.0/16\n\nADMIN WireGuard:\n10.77.0.0/24\n\nvSwitch:\n85469\n\nVLAN:\n4000\n\nTopology is frozen.\n\n==================================================\n1. SERVER-SIDE READINESS\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n\n- OPNsense server running\n- WAN = 2.28.34.27\n- PRIVATE = 10.90.10.1\n- WG = 10.60.0.1/24\n- UDP/51821 listening\n- real Android peer exists\n- peer AllowedIP = 10.60.0.10/32\n- worm-robot PRIVATE = 10.90.20.10\n- worm-robot FireHOL active\n- worm-robot net.ipv4.ip_forward = 0\n- ADMIN network 10.77.0.0/24 unchanged\n\nNever print private keys.\n\n==================================================\n2. REAL CLIENT WIREGUARD VALIDATION\n==================================================\n\nKnown Android client:\n\nAddress:\n10.60.0.10/32\n\nEndpoint:\n2.28.34.27:51821\n\nOPNsense actual public key:\nvJtONCHbxMj3d7SAsPD5OFkTD7NcAoNgjIfmTcinE04=\n\nAllowedIPs:\n0.0.0.0/0\n\nDNS:\n10.60.0.1\n\nWith Android tunnel enabled, verify:\n\n- latest handshake RECENT\n- RX > 0\n- TX > 0\n\nIf no recent handshake:\nDEVELOPMENT GATE = FAIL\n\n==================================================\n3. FULL-TUNNEL VALIDATION\n==================================================\n\nWith real Android client connected verify:\n\n- Internet works\n- public IPv4 = 2.28.34.27\n- HTTPS works\n\nUse real client-path evidence.\n\nDo not infer PASS from NAT configuration alone.\n\nIf public egress is not proven:\nDEVELOPMENT GATE = FAIL\n\n==================================================\n4. DNS VALIDATION\n==================================================\n\nVerify from real Android client:\n\n- DNS through 10.60.0.1 works\n- hostname resolution works\n- no public WAN DNS exposure is required\n\nFor DEVELOPMENT:\na validated working protected DNS path is required.\n\nIf DNS is broken:\nDEVELOPMENT GATE = FAIL\n\n==================================================\n5. IPV6 DEVELOPMENT POLICY\n==================================================\n\nFor DEVELOPMENT, one of these is acceptable:\n\nA. IPv6 is properly tunneled and tested\n\nOR\n\nB. IPv6 is explicitly blocked for worm-os protected mode and there is\nevidence that direct IPv6 cannot bypass the VPN during test.\n\nIf IPv6 behavior is completely unknown:\nDEVELOPMENT GATE = FAIL\n\nProduction-grade exhaustive leak validation belongs to the production gate,\nbut the development design must already have a safe explicit policy.\n\n==================================================\n6. PRIVATE ROUTING\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nworm-os 10.60.0.10\n ->\nOPNsense\n ->\n10.90.0.0/16\n\nAt minimum verify one intended private destination is reachable.\n\nVerify:\n- no dependency on worm-robot forwarding\n- worm-robot ip_forward remains 0\n\n==================================================\n7. ADMIN ISOLATION\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n\n10.77.0.0/24 ADMIN remains isolated from normal worm-os peer.\n\nException allowed by frozen policy:\n\nworm-os -> OPNsense 10.60.0.1:\nTCP 22\nTCP 80\nTCP 443\n\nNo broad access to worm-robot SSH/admin must be introduced.\n\n==================================================\n8. PUBLIC EXPOSURE\n==================================================\n\nVerify OPNsense WAN:\n\n2.28.34.27:22  DENY\n2.28.34.27:80  DENY\n2.28.34.27:443 DENY\n\nUDP/51821 available.\n\nVerify worm-robot public web/OTA policy remains denied.\n\n==================================================\n9. ANDROID SOURCE PREREQUISITES\n==================================================\n\nAudit ex-graphene/Worm OS source READ-ONLY.\n\nDetermine whether development can proceed using existing platform pieces.\n\nAudit:\n\n- kernel WireGuard support\n- VPN framework\n- always-on VPN support\n- lockdown support\n- ConnectivityService\n- NetworkStack/netd\n- boot lifecycle\n- Wi-Fi/mobile handover hooks\n- Keystore\n- SELinux\n- backup exclusion\n- OTA integration points\n- existing Worm system services\n\nDo NOT require a completed system-WireGuard component.\nIts absence is the reason for this development phase.\n\n==================================================\n10. KEY MANAGEMENT DESIGN\n==================================================\n\nDevelopment is allowed only if the proposed design supports:\n\n- unique keypair per device\n- private key generated on device\n- no shared production private key\n- no private key in source\n- no private key in factory image\n- no private key in OTA\n- backup exclusion\n- per-device /32 address\n- public-key enrollment\n- independent peer revocation\n\nIf design requires a shared key:\nP0 FAIL.\n\n==================================================\n11. FAIL-CLOSED DESIGN\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT require native fail-closed implementation to already exist.\n\nInstead confirm a viable design exists for:\n\n- OTA\n- downloads\n- Apps\n- backup\n- private Worm APIs\n\nProduction requirement:\nno public fallback if WireGuard is unavailable.\n\nFor DEVELOPMENT:\ndesign identified = PASS\nno viable design = FAIL\n\n==================================================\n12. SELINUX / PLATFORM SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nConfirm implementation can proceed while preserving:\n\n- SELinux enforcing\n- AVB / Verified Boot\n- Android sandbox\n- Keystore\n- GrapheneOS security hardening\n\nAny proposal requiring:\nSELinux permissive\nroot shell scripts\ndisabled neverallows\nshared plaintext secrets\n\nis a DEVELOPMENT blocker.\n\n==================================================\n13. SECRET SCAN\n==================================================\n\nScan relevant audit/patch docs.\n\nNever print:\n- WireGuard private keys\n- PSKs\n- passwords\n- Hetzner tokens\n- SSH private keys\n- signing keys\n\n==================================================\n14. DEVELOPMENT BLOCKERS\n==================================================\n\nOnly these categories should block DEVELOPMENT:\n\nP0:\n- shared/private key design flaw\n- requirement to weaken Android core security\n- topology fundamentally incompatible\n\nP1:\n- no real WG handshake\n- full-tunnel egress not working\n- protected DNS not working\n- unsafe/unknown IPv6 behavior\n- no viable Android integration path\n- unresolved server networking failure\n\nThe following DO NOT block development by themselves:\n\n- native Worm system-WG not implemented yet\n- native fail-closed not implemented yet\n- hardware/device production tests not completed yet\n- production OTA integration not completed yet\n\nThose belong to PRODUCTION GATE.\n\n==================================================\n15. OUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/root/WORM-SYSTEM-WIREGUARD-DEVELOPMENT-GATE/\n\nFiles:\n\n00-SUMMARY.md\n01-INFRASTRUCTURE.md\n02-LIVE-WIREGUARD.md\n03-FULL-TUNNEL.md\n04-DNS.md\n05-IPV6.md\n06-PRIVATE-ROUTING.md\n07-ANDROID-PREREQUISITES.md\n08-KEY-MANAGEMENT.md\n09-FAIL-CLOSED-DESIGN.md\n10-SELINUX.md\n11-FINDINGS.md\n12-GATE.md\nfindings.json\n\n==================================================\nFINAL RESULT\n==================================================\n\nPrint exactly one:\n\nREADY FOR WORM-OS SYSTEM WIREGUARD DEVELOPMENT\n\nor\n\nNOT READY FOR WORM-OS SYSTEM WIREGUARD DEVELOPMENT\n\nIf NOT READY:\nlist only the exact P0/P1 blockers.\n\nDo not implement anything after the audit."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a078a3-c15e-7e81-9693-d9f877601739","create_time":1788730392.95305,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a078ab-b5b3-7bb0-a1fd-f5604cf24181","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Perform WORM WIREGUARD COMPLETE RECOVERY AND LIVE VALIDATION.\n\nGOAL:\nMake the existing Android test client successfully establish WireGuard\nwith OPNsense and validate full-tunnel networking.\n\nThis task MAY remediate WireGuard configuration after diagnosis.\n\nDO NOT change the frozen network architecture.\n\n==================================================\nFROZEN NETWORK\n==================================================\n\nOPNsense WAN:\n2.28.34.27\n\nOPNsense PRIVATE:\n10.90.10.1\n\nOPNsense WireGuard:\n10.60.0.1/24\n\nWireGuard UDP:\n51821\n\nAndroid test client:\n10.60.0.10/32\n\nAndroid public key:\njxZ2fEyoynXMrhNPZitfKY1kqMZBZ/6bYLbyZb6XCXM=\n\nworm-robot PRIVATE:\n10.90.20.10\n\nworm-robot PUBLIC:\n162.55.6.173\n\nADMIN:\n10.77.0.0/24\n\nExpected worm-os public egress:\n2.28.34.27\n\n==================================================\nPHASE 1 — COMPLETE READ-ONLY DIAGNOSIS\n==================================================\n\nUse private SSH:\nworm-robot -> OPNsense 10.90.10.1\n\nInspect LIVE WireGuard state.\n\nDetermine:\n\n- actual interface name\n- tunnel address\n- listen port\n- live public key\n- configured persistent public/private key relationship\n- Android peer\n- Android AllowedIP\n- number of WireGuard interfaces\n- number of UDP/51821 listeners\n- OPNsense WireGuard service state\n- PF rules for UDP/51821\n- interface assignment\n- NAT state\n- DNS state\n\nNEVER print private keys.\n\nVerify server private key derives to the live public key.\n\nReport only public-key result.\n\n==================================================\nPHASE 2 — CONFIGURATION CONSISTENCY\n==================================================\n\nCompare THREE states:\n\nA. OPNsense persistent config\nB. OPNsense generated/runtime WireGuard config\nC. live wg show state\n\nThey MUST agree on:\n\ninterface:\nwg0\n\naddress:\n10.60.0.1/24\n\nlisten:\n51821\n\nserver keypair:\nsame identity\n\nAndroid peer:\njxZ2fEyoynXMrhNPZitfKY1kqMZBZ/6bYLbyZb6XCXM=\n\nAndroid AllowedIP:\n10.60.0.10/32\n\nFind:\n- stale keys\n- duplicate instances\n- duplicate peers\n- stale generated config\n- config/runtime mismatch\n- service reload failure\n\n==================================================\nPHASE 3 — REPAIR SERVER IF NECESSARY\n==================================================\n\nIf persistent/runtime/live configuration differs:\n\nBACK UP OPNsense configuration first.\n\nThen make the MINIMUM correction required.\n\nDo NOT regenerate the OPNsense keypair unless the existing keypair is\nactually invalid/inconsistent and cannot safely be repaired.\n\nIf regeneration becomes absolutely necessary:\nSTOP before doing it and report why.\n\nDo not regenerate Android keys.\n\nAfter any correction:\napply/reload WireGuard safely.\n\nVerify:\n\nwg0 = 10.60.0.1/24\nUDP = 51821\npeer = correct Android public key\nAllowedIP = 10.60.0.10/32\n\n==================================================\nPHASE 4 — PRODUCE EXACT ANDROID CONFIG\n==================================================\n\nAfter determining the authoritative LIVE OPNsense public key, output\nan Android configuration checklist.\n\nDo NOT include Android PrivateKey.\n\nOutput:\n\nANDROID_ADDRESS=10.60.0.10/32\nANDROID_DNS=10.60.0.1\nOPNSENSE_PUBLIC_KEY=<AUTHORITATIVE LIVE KEY>\nENDPOINT=2.28.34.27:51821\nALLOWED_IPS=0.0.0.0/0\nKEEPALIVE=25\n\nAlso verify that the Android public key expected by OPNsense remains:\n\njxZ2fEyoynXMrhNPZitfKY1kqMZBZ/6bYLbyZb6XCXM=\n\n==================================================\nPHASE 5 — LIVE HANDSHAKE TEST\n==================================================\n\nStart simultaneous monitoring:\n\n- tcpdump WAN UDP/51821\n- wg show wg0\n- relevant PF counters/logs\n\nThen print clearly:\n\n========================================\nENABLE ANDROID WIREGUARD NOW\n========================================\n\nWait/monitor for 90 seconds.\n\nDo not change configuration during this window.\n\nRecord:\n\nWAN UDP packets\nPF pass/block\nlatest handshake\nRX\nTX\n\n==================================================\nPHASE 6 — IF PACKETS ARRIVE BUT NO HANDSHAKE\n==================================================\n\nIf WAN packets > 0 but handshake = NEVER:\n\nDo NOT touch NAT or DNS.\n\nInvestigate only WireGuard authentication/runtime:\n\n- server key identity\n- client public key\n- correct UDP socket\n- correct instance\n- peer lookup\n- persistent/runtime mismatch\n- WireGuard logs\n- PF delivery to local socket\n\nIdentify exact cause.\n\nApply a correction ONLY if evidence proves it.\n\nThen repeat the 90-second live test.\n\n==================================================\nPHASE 7 — HANDSHAKE PASS\n==================================================\n\nOnce handshake becomes RECENT:\n\nrequire:\n\nRX > 0\nTX > 0\n\nThen proceed downstream.\n\nDo not continue to NAT/DNS tests until handshake passes.\n\n==================================================\nPHASE 8 — FIREWALL / FULL-TUNNEL\n==================================================\n\nVerify OPNsense permits worm-os Internet egress.\n\nSource:\n10.60.0.0/24\n\nOutbound NAT:\nWAN address\n\nExpected:\n\n10.60.0.10\n ->\nwg0\n ->\nOPNsense\n ->\nWAN NAT\n ->\n2.28.34.27\n ->\nInternet\n\nPreserve explicit security denies.\n\n==================================================\nPHASE 9 — DNS\n==================================================\n\nVerify resolver:\n\n10.60.0.1:53\n\nfrom worm-os WireGuard network.\n\nVerify:\n- UDP DNS\n- TCP DNS where applicable\n- resolver response\n- no WAN resolver exposure\n\nIf DNS fails after handshake:\nrepair DNS/firewall only after identifying exact cause.\n\n==================================================\nPHASE 10 — INTERNET TEST\n==================================================\n\nWith Android WireGuard ENABLED:\n\nverify Internet connectivity.\n\nExpected public IPv4:\n\n2.28.34.27\n\nUse real client-path evidence where available.\n\nDo not infer PASS solely from NAT configuration.\n\n==================================================\nPHASE 11 — PRIVATE NETWORK\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nAndroid\n10.60.0.10\n ->\nOPNsense\n ->\n10.90.0.0/16\n\nTest intended private connectivity.\n\nPreserve:\n\nworm-robot ip_forward=0\n\nOPNsense remains the router.\n\n==================================================\nPHASE 12 — MANAGEMENT POLICY\n==================================================\n\nFrozen policy requires from worm-os:\n\n10.60.0.1:22  ALLOW\n10.60.0.1:80  ALLOW\n10.60.0.1:443 ALLOW\n\nWAN remains:\n\n2.28.34.27:22  DENY\n2.28.34.27:80  DENY\n2.28.34.27:443 DENY\n\nDo not accidentally expose management publicly.\n\n==================================================\nPHASE 13 — IPV6\n==================================================\n\nVerify Android IPv6 cannot bypass the protected path.\n\nUntil dedicated tunneled IPv6 is implemented:\nuse the existing explicit no-leak policy.\n\nDo not break the working IPv4 tunnel while investigating IPv6.\n\n==================================================\nPHASE 14 — REGRESSION\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nworm-robot:\n162.55.6.173 unchanged\n10.90.20.10 unchanged\nFireHOL active\nADMIN WG unchanged\nip_forward=0\n\nOPNsense:\n2.28.34.27 unchanged\n10.90.10.1 unchanged\n10.60.0.1 unchanged\nWAN management closed\n\nNo frozen topology changes.\n\n==================================================\nPHASE 15 — PERSISTENCE\n==================================================\n\nOnce working, verify the configuration is persistent.\n\nDo not leave a fix applied only through:\n\nwg set\n\nor another runtime-only command.\n\nThe authoritative OPNsense configuration must contain the working\nWireGuard state.\n\nDo not reboot merely to prove this unless necessary.\n\n==================================================\nPHASE 16 — SECRET SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nNever print/store:\n\n- OPNsense WireGuard private key\n- Android WireGuard private key\n- PSK\n- Hetzner API token\n- passwords\n- SSH private keys\n\nPublic keys are allowed.\n\nRun secret scan.\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/root/WORM-WIREGUARD-RECOVERY/\n\nInclude:\n\n00-SUMMARY.md\n01-DIAGNOSIS.md\n02-OPNSENSE-WG.md\n03-ANDROID-CONFIG.md\n04-HANDSHAKE.md\n05-FIREWALL.md\n06-NAT.md\n07-DNS.md\n08-INTERNET.md\n09-PRIVATE-ROUTING.md\n10-IPV6.md\n11-PERSISTENCE.md\n12-REGRESSION.md\n13-FINDINGS.md\n14-FINAL.md\nROLLBACK.md\nfindings.json\n\n==================================================\nFINAL GATE\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT claim success unless:\n\nPASS server key consistency\nPASS Android peer\nPASS AllowedIP 10.60.0.10/32\nPASS UDP/51821\nPASS WAN packets reach OPNsense\nPASS PF permits WireGuard\nPASS handshake RECENT\nPASS RX > 0\nPASS TX > 0\nPASS DNS\nPASS Internet through tunnel\nPASS public IPv4 = 2.28.34.27\nPASS private routing\nPASS OPNsense WG management policy\nPASS WAN management denied\nPASS IPv6 no-leak policy\nPASS persistent configuration\nPASS frozen topology\nPASS no secrets\n\nFinal output must be:\n\nWORM WIREGUARD: PASS\n\nor:\n\nWORM WIREGUARD: FAIL\n\nIf FAIL:\nstate the ONE CURRENT FAILING STAGE and exact evidence.\n\nDo not start system-WireGuard Android development automatically."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a078ab-b598-7153-bc4c-18858deaf5b8","create_time":1788730914.2276084,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a078b3-ceb3-7ee3-bd57-afd92f162b7a","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Implement PATCH-DIAG-WIREGUARD-OPNSENSE-MINIMAL.\n\nTEMPORARY DIAGNOSTIC PATCH ONLY.\n\nFROZEN ADDRESSES MUST NOT CHANGE:\n\nworm-robot PUBLIC:  162.55.6.173\nworm-robot PRIVATE: 10.90.20.10\n\nOPNsense WAN:       2.28.34.27\nOPNsense PRIVATE:   10.90.10.1\nOPNsense WG:        10.60.0.1/24\n\nworm-os test peer:  10.60.0.10/32\n\nADMIN WG:           10.77.0.0/24\n\nWireGuard port:     UDP/51821\n\n==================================================\n1. WORM-ROBOT: LEAVE NETWORKING ALONE\n==================================================\n\nDO NOT change:\n- 162.55.6.173\n- 10.90.20.10\n- VLAN 4000\n- MTU 1400\n- private route\n- ADMIN WireGuard\n- SSH configuration\n- default route\n\nnet.ipv4.ip_forward MUST remain 0.\n\nFireHOL:\nDO NOT disable the entire public firewall.\n\nTemporarily remove/disable ONLY rules that could interfere with\ntraffic on the PRIVATE interface enp9s0.4000 if evidence shows they\nblock the diagnostic private path.\n\nPreserve PUBLIC protection:\n- SSH policy\n- block/default-deny policy\n- no public Web/OTA/download exposure\n\nBefore any FireHOL change:\nbackup configuration and record current effective state.\n\n==================================================\n2. OPNsense BACKUP\n==================================================\n\nBack up the complete persistent OPNsense configuration before changes.\n\nRecord:\n- wg0\n- peers\n- PF rules\n- NAT\n- DNS\n- interface assignments\n\nNever print private keys.\n\n==================================================\n3. MINIMAL WIREGUARD SERVER\n==================================================\n\nEnsure exactly ONE worm-os WireGuard instance exists:\n\nwg0\n10.60.0.1/24\nUDP 51821\n\nEnsure exactly ONE Android test peer:\n\nPublicKey:\njxZ2fEyoynXMrhNPZitfKY1kqMZBZ/6bYLbyZb6XCXM=\n\nAllowedIP:\n10.60.0.10/32\n\nDo not regenerate either side's keys.\n\nDetermine authoritative OPNsense public key from LIVE wg0.\n\nNever print private key.\n\n==================================================\n4. TEMPORARY OPNsense DIAGNOSTIC PF POLICY\n==================================================\n\nKeep WAN default deny.\n\nWAN temporary explicit rule:\n\nALLOW UDP\nsource: any\ndestination: WAN address\nport: 51821\n\nDo NOT open publicly:\nTCP/22\nTCP/80\nTCP/443\n\nFor the worm-os WG interface, temporarily use a SIMPLE diagnostic IPv4\npolicy sufficient for:\n\n- client -> OPNsense WG address\n- client -> DNS\n- client -> Internet through NAT\n- client -> intended 10.90.0.0/16 private test path\n\nDo not create public management exposure.\n\nKeep 10.77.0.0/24 ADMIN isolated.\n\nDocument every temporary rule.\n\n==================================================\n5. NAT\n==================================================\n\nUse one clear outbound NAT rule:\n\nsource:\n10.60.0.0/24\n\ninterface:\nWAN\n\ntranslation:\nWAN address\n\nDo not add duplicate NAT rules.\n\nDo not NAT private traffic between:\n10.60.0.0/24\nand\n10.90.0.0/16\n\n==================================================\n6. DNS\n==================================================\n\nEnsure OPNsense resolver can answer:\n\n10.60.0.0/24 -> 10.60.0.1 TCP/UDP 53\n\nDo NOT expose DNS on WAN.\n\n==================================================\n7. LIVE HANDSHAKE TEST FIRST\n==================================================\n\nBefore testing DNS/NAT/private services:\n\nmonitor:\n- WAN UDP/51821\n- wg show wg0\n- PF pass/block\n\nPrint:\n\nENABLE ANDROID WIREGUARD NOW\n\nThen monitor for 90 seconds.\n\nPASS requires:\nWAN packets > 0\nHANDSHAKE RECENT\nRX > 0\nTX > 0\n\nIf handshake remains NEVER:\nSTOP.\n\nDo NOT blame FireHOL, NAT, DNS or worm-robot.\nReport the exact WireGuard authentication/runtime problem.\n\n==================================================\n8. AFTER HANDSHAKE ONLY\n==================================================\n\nOnly after handshake PASS test:\n\n1. 10.60.0.1 reachability\n2. DNS 10.60.0.1\n3. Internet\n4. public IPv4 = 2.28.34.27\n5. private route toward 10.90.0.0/16\n\n==================================================\n9. PUBLIC SECURITY REGRESSION\n==================================================\n\nMust remain:\n\nOPNsense:\n2.28.34.27:22  CLOSED/FILTERED\n2.28.34.27:80  CLOSED/FILTERED\n2.28.34.27:443 CLOSED/FILTERED\n\nworm-robot:\npublic Web/OTA/download remains denied.\n\nDo not expose additional services for diagnosis.\n\n==================================================\n10. ROLLBACK\n==================================================\n\nCreate exact rollback for every temporary OPNsense/FireHOL change.\n\nDo not leave diagnostic broad rules in production.\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nPATCH-DIAG-WIREGUARD-OPNSENSE-MINIMAL/\n\nInclude:\n\nREADME.md\nBEFORE.md\nOPNSENSE.md\nWIREGUARD.md\nPF.md\nNAT.md\nDNS.md\nFIREHOL.md\nTESTS.md\nROLLBACK.md\ntest-results.txt\nmodified-files.txt\n\nFinal output:\n\nDIAGNOSTIC WG HANDSHAKE:\nPASS / FAIL\n\nWAN PACKETS:\n<count>\n\nHANDSHAKE:\nRECENT / NEVER\n\nRX:\n<value>\n\nTX:\n<value>\n\nINTERNET:\nPASS / NOT TESTED / FAIL\n\nPUBLIC IPV4:\n<value or NOT TESTED>\n\nPRIVATE ROUTING:\nPASS / NOT TESTED / FAIL\n\nFIREHOL:\nUNCHANGED / PRIVATE-RULES-TEMPORARILY-RELAXED\n\nFROZEN IP TOPOLOGY:\nUNCHANGED / FAIL\n\nDo not start another patch."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a078b3-ce98-7a13-9544-44e5bcd2c9ef","create_time":1788731444.9155874,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a078b7-6d1d-7881-89c1-7dcd4ab29cf6","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Implement PATCH-NET-008-DEDICATED-OPNSENSE-PUBLIC-IP.\n\nGOAL:\nGive OPNsense/Worm-OS WireGuard its own dedicated NEW public IPv4,\nwhile leaving worm-robot and the complete private network unchanged.\n\nDO NOT invent an IPv4 address.\n\nFIRST inspect Hetzner resources and determine whether an additional\npublic IPv4/Floating IP/Primary IP suitable for this OPNsense VPS is\nalready allocated or can be correctly attached.\n\nCURRENT:\n\nworm-robot PUBLIC:\n162.55.6.173\n\nworm-robot PRIVATE:\n10.90.20.10\n\nOPNsense CURRENT PUBLIC:\n2.28.34.27\n\nOPNsense PRIVATE:\n10.90.10.1\n\nOPNsense WG:\n10.60.0.1/24\n\nworm-os:\n10.60.0.x/32\n\nPRIVATE NETWORK:\n10.90.0.0/16\n\n==================================================\nABSOLUTE REQUIREMENTS\n==================================================\n\nWORM-ROBOT MUST REMAIN UNCHANGED:\n\nPUBLIC:\n162.55.6.173\n\nPRIVATE:\n10.90.20.10\n\nFireHOL:\nKEEP ENABLED\n\nPreserve:\n- SSH policy\n- blocklists\n- ADMIN WireGuard\n- public default deny\n- ip_forward=0\n\nDo not route worm-os Internet through worm-robot.\n\n==================================================\nPRIVATE NETWORK MUST REMAIN UNCHANGED\n==================================================\n\nPreserve:\n\n10.90.0.0/16\n\nOPNsense PRIVATE:\n10.90.10.1\n\nworm-robot PRIVATE:\n10.90.20.10\n\nVLAN:\n4000\n\nMTU:\n1400\n\nDo not modify private addressing or routing unless required only to\nrepair an existing fault.\n\n==================================================\nNEW OPNsense PUBLIC IP\n==================================================\n\nDiscover/allocate the correct Hetzner-supported dedicated IPv4 for\nOPNsense.\n\nCall it:\n\nNEW_OPNSENSE_PUBLIC_IPV4\n\nDo not proceed with cutover until Hetzner confirms the address is\nassigned/routed correctly to OPNsense.\n\nThe new address becomes:\n\nworm-os dedicated public egress IP\nWireGuard public endpoint\n\nWireGuard endpoint:\n\nNEW_OPNSENSE_PUBLIC_IPV4:51821\n\nExpected worm-os Internet egress:\n\nNEW_OPNSENSE_PUBLIC_IPV4\n\n==================================================\nSAFE MIGRATION\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT immediately remove 2.28.34.27.\n\nUse staged migration:\n\n1. provision NEW_OPNSENSE_PUBLIC_IPV4\n2. verify OPNsense receives it\n3. verify routing/gateway\n4. allow UDP/51821 on NEW address\n5. keep TCP 22/80/443 publicly denied\n6. test WireGuard using NEW address\n7. verify handshake\n8. verify DNS\n9. verify NAT\n10. verify Internet egress equals NEW address\n11. verify private routing\n12. only then decide whether 2.28.34.27 can be retired\n\nNo destructive cutover before validation.\n\n==================================================\nOPNsense PUBLIC POLICY\n==================================================\n\nNEW_OPNSENSE_PUBLIC_IPV4:\n\nALLOW:\nUDP/51821 WireGuard\n\nDENY PUBLIC:\nTCP/22\nTCP/80\nTCP/443\nDNS\nWebGUI\nSSH\nall other unsolicited inbound traffic\n\nManagement remains through protected/private paths.\n\n==================================================\nWIREGUARD\n==================================================\n\nPreserve:\n\nOPNsense WG:\n10.60.0.1/24\n\nAndroid test peer:\n10.60.0.10/32\n\nDo NOT regenerate keys.\n\nOnly change endpoint after NEW public IP is confirmed operational.\n\n==================================================\nNAT\n==================================================\n\nAfter successful migration:\n\n10.60.0.0/24\n ->\nOPNsense WAN\n ->\nNEW_OPNSENSE_PUBLIC_IPV4\n\nExpected public IP from worm-os:\n\nNEW_OPNSENSE_PUBLIC_IPV4\n\nDo not NAT private traffic unnecessarily between:\n\n10.60.0.0/24\nand\n10.90.0.0/16\n\n==================================================\nTESTS\n==================================================\n\nPASS worm-robot 162.55.6.173 unchanged\nPASS FireHOL active\nPASS worm-robot 10.90.20.10 unchanged\nPASS OPNsense 10.90.10.1 unchanged\nPASS private 10.90.0.0/16 unchanged\nPASS OPNsense WG 10.60.0.1 unchanged\nPASS NEW public IPv4 actually assigned by Hetzner\nPASS NEW IPv4 routed to OPNsense\nPASS UDP/51821 reaches NEW IPv4\nPASS real WireGuard handshake\nPASS RX/TX\nPASS DNS\nPASS Internet through WG\nPASS public egress = NEW_OPNSENSE_PUBLIC_IPV4\nPASS NEW IP TCP/22 denied\nPASS NEW IP TCP/80 denied\nPASS NEW IP TCP/443 denied\nPASS no secrets\n\nIf no suitable additional IPv4 is currently available:\n\nSTOP.\n\nPrint:\nNEW OPNsense PUBLIC IPv4 REQUIRED\n\nDo not fabricate an address.\nDo not break the current 2.28.34.27 configuration.\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nPATCH-NET-008-DEDICATED-OPNSENSE-PUBLIC-IP/\n\nInclude:\nREADME.md\nHETZNER.md\nMIGRATION.md\nOPNSENSE.md\nWIREGUARD.md\nNAT.md\nFIREWALL.md\nTESTS.md\nROLLBACK.md\nmodified-files.txt\ntest-results.txt\n\nFinal output:\n\nPATCH-NET-008 STATUS:\nPASS / PENDING-IP / BLOCKED\n\nWORM-ROBOT PUBLIC:\n162.55.6.173\n\nWORM-ROBOT PRIVATE:\n10.90.20.10\n\nFIREHOL:\nACTIVE\n\nOPNSENSE PRIVATE:\n10.90.10.1\n\nOPNSENSE NEW PUBLIC:\n<actual address or REQUIRED>\n\nOPNSENSE WG:\n10.60.0.1\n\nWIREGUARD ENDPOINT:\n<NEW-IP>:51821\n\nFROZEN PRIVATE NETWORK:\nUNCHANGED\n\nDo not start another patch automatically."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a078b3-ce98-7a13-9544-44e5bcd2c9ef","create_time":1788731682.0779321,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a078bb-7585-71d2-8ef9-51889ab41667","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Implement PATCH-NET-BASE-PRIVATE-WORM.\n\nPURPOSE:\nBuild and certify the minimum stable private networking foundation\nbefore doing any additional Worm OS networking work.\n\nDO NOT:\n- change public IPs\n- add another public IP\n- modify OTA\n- modify WebUSB\n- modify Apps\n- modify Android/ex-graphene\n- redesign addressing\n- remove FireHOL\n- enable worm-robot forwarding\n- regenerate WireGuard keys\n\n==================================================\nFROZEN PRIVATE FOUNDATION\n==================================================\n\nWireGuard client / future worm-os:\n10.60.0.10/32\n\nWireGuard network:\n10.60.0.0/24\n\nOPNsense WireGuard:\n10.60.0.1/24\n\nOPNsense private:\n10.90.10.1\n\nHetzner private network:\n10.90.0.0/16\n\nworm-robot private:\n10.90.20.10\n\nworm-robot private interface:\nenp9s0.4000\n\nVLAN:\n4000\n\nMTU:\n1400\n\n==================================================\nTARGET CONNECTIVITY\n==================================================\n\nMust work:\n\n10.60.0.10 -> 10.60.0.1\n10.60.0.10 -> 10.90.10.1\n10.60.0.10 -> 10.90.20.10\n\nSSH must work:\n\n10.60.0.10 -> 10.90.20.10 TCP/22\n\nThis SSH path is PRIVATE ONLY.\n\nDo not require worm-os/client to use:\n\n162.55.6.173:22\n\nfor this private SSH path.\n\n==================================================\n1. WIREGUARD\n==================================================\n\nAudit existing OPNsense WireGuard.\n\nExpected:\n\nwg0:\n10.60.0.1/24\n\nlisten:\nUDP/51821\n\nreal test peer:\n10.60.0.10/32\n\nDo not regenerate keys.\n\nVerify:\n- peer present\n- correct /32\n- handshake\n- RX/TX\n\nNever print private keys.\n\n==================================================\n2. OPNsense PRIVATE ROUTING\n==================================================\n\nEnsure OPNsense routes:\n\n10.60.0.0/24\n<->\n10.90.0.0/16\n\nDo not NAT this private-to-private traffic unless technically required\nand explicitly justified.\n\nPreferred:\nROUTED PRIVATE TRAFFIC.\n\nOPNsense remains the router.\n\n==================================================\n3. WORM-ROBOT PRIVATE NETWORK\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nenp9s0.4000 UP\nVLAN 4000\nMTU 1400\n10.90.20.10/24\n\nExpected private route:\n10.90.0.0/16 via existing Hetzner private path.\n\nVerify return path for:\n10.60.0.0/24\n\nIf an explicit route via OPNsense/Hetzner private gateway is required,\nimplement the minimum persistent route.\n\nDo not change the public default route.\n\n==================================================\n4. FIREHOL\n==================================================\n\nFireHOL MUST remain active.\n\nPUBLIC policy remains unchanged.\n\nAdd/verify a PRIVATE rule permitting:\n\nSOURCE:\n10.60.0.0/24\n\nDESTINATION:\nworm-robot private address 10.90.20.10\n\nSERVICE:\nSSH TCP/22\n\nThis rule must apply to the PRIVATE path only.\n\nDo not create:\n10.60.0.0/24 -> any ACCEPT\n\nDo not make enp9s0.4000 trusted-any.\n\nKeep blocklist/public protection.\n\n==================================================\n5. SSH\n==================================================\n\nVerify sshd is able to accept connections on:\n\n10.90.20.10:22\n\nPrefer explicit private/admin bindings where compatible with the\nexisting recovery design.\n\nDo not disable the existing public recovery/admin SSH during this patch.\n\nDo not weaken:\n- authentication\n- root policy\n- key requirements\n- crypto policy\n\nThis patch changes NETWORK REACHABILITY, not SSH authentication policy.\n\n==================================================\n6. OPNsense FIREWALL\n==================================================\n\nAllow from:\n\n10.60.0.0/24\n\nto:\n\n10.90.20.10 TCP/22\n\nAllow required private routing traffic for testing.\n\nKeep ADMIN network:\n10.77.0.0/24\n\nseparate unless explicitly required.\n\nDo not open worm-robot SSH through OPNsense WAN.\n\n==================================================\n7. NO PUBLIC DEPENDENCY\n==================================================\n\nPrivate SSH test must succeed without connecting to:\n\n162.55.6.173\n\nExpected path:\n\nclient 10.60.0.10\n  ->\nWireGuard\n  ->\nOPNsense 10.60.0.1\n  ->\nOPNsense private routing\n  ->\nworm-robot 10.90.20.10:22\n\n==================================================\n8. LIVE TESTS\n==================================================\n\nWith real WireGuard client connected:\n\nTEST A:\nreach 10.60.0.1\n\nTEST B:\nreach 10.90.10.1\n\nTEST C:\nreach 10.90.20.10\n\nTEST D:\nTCP connect 10.90.20.10:22\n\nTEST E:\nreal SSH authentication to:\n\nssh <authorized-admin-user>@10.90.20.10\n\nDo not alter authentication credentials for the test.\n\nTEST F:\nverify WireGuard handshake remains RECENT.\n\nTEST G:\nverify RX/TX increase.\n\n==================================================\n9. RETURN PATH\n==================================================\n\nExplicitly verify return traffic:\n\nworm-robot 10.90.20.10\n ->\nOPNsense\n ->\n10.60.0.10\n\nDo not accept a one-way connectivity test as PASS.\n\nUse routing/firewall counters where useful.\n\n==================================================\n10. SECURITY TESTS\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n\n- worm-robot ip_forward = 0\n- FireHOL active\n- no broad PRIVATE allow\n- no new public SSH exposure\n- OPNsense WAN management unchanged\n- no private key leak\n- no public-IP dependency for private SSH\n\n==================================================\n11. PERSISTENCE\n==================================================\n\nEnsure all required configuration is persistent:\n\nOPNsense:\n- WG instance\n- peer\n- private route\n- PF rules\n\nworm-robot:\n- VLAN\n- private IP\n- private route\n- FireHOL rule\n- SSH private reachability\n\nDo not leave essential configuration as runtime-only commands.\n\n==================================================\n12. OUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nPATCH-NET-BASE-PRIVATE-WORM/\n\nInclude:\n\nREADME.md\nARCHITECTURE.md\nWIREGUARD.md\nOPNSENSE.md\nWORM-ROBOT.md\nFIREHOL.md\nSSH.md\nROUTING.md\nACL-MATRIX.md\nTESTS.md\nPERSISTENCE.md\nSECURITY.md\nROLLBACK.md\nmodified-files.txt\ntest-results.txt\n\n==================================================\nPASS GATE\n==================================================\n\nDo not mark PASS unless a REAL WireGuard client verifies:\n\nPASS 10.60.0.10 -> 10.60.0.1\nPASS 10.60.0.10 -> 10.90.10.1\nPASS 10.60.0.10 -> 10.90.20.10\nPASS 10.60.0.10 -> 10.90.20.10:22\nPASS real private SSH connection\nPASS WireGuard handshake RECENT\nPASS WireGuard RX/TX\nPASS bidirectional return path\nPASS FireHOL active\nPASS worm-robot ip_forward=0\nPASS no broad private allow\nPASS no new public exposure\nPASS persistent configuration\nPASS frozen private addressing\nPASS no secrets\n\nFinal output must be exactly:\n\nPRIVATE WORM FOUNDATION: PASS\n\nor:\n\nPRIVATE WORM FOUNDATION: FAIL\n\nIf FAIL:\nstate the exact failing hop:\n\nCLIENT -> WG\nWG -> OPNsense\nOPNsense -> PRIVATE\nPRIVATE -> WORM-ROBOT\nFIREHOL\nSSH\nRETURN PATH\n\nDo not start OTA/Web/Android work automatically."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a078b3-ce98-7a13-9544-44e5bcd2c9ef","create_time":1788731946.3732257,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a078c8-2b47-7d13-9380-096921e6e982","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Implement PATCH-WG-RESET-TEST-IDENTITY.\n\nPURPOSE:\nRepair ONLY the failing CLIENT -> WG hop.\n\nThe private Worm foundation already has the required server-side\nrouting/firewall rules.\n\nDO NOT modify:\n- 10.60.0.0/24\n- OPNsense 10.60.0.1\n- OPNsense private 10.90.10.1\n- worm-robot 10.90.20.10\n- VLAN 4000\n- private routing\n- FireHOL private rules\n- worm-robot SSH\n- worm-robot public IP\n- worm-robot ip_forward\n- NAT/DNS unless handshake succeeds first\n\n==================================================\n1. BACKUP\n==================================================\n\nBackup persistent OPNsense configuration.\n\nRecord current:\n- wg0\n- UDP/51821\n- current server public key\n- current Android peer\n- PF rules\n- private routing\n\nNever print private keys.\n\n==================================================\n2. REMOVE ONLY THE BROKEN TEST WG IDENTITY\n==================================================\n\nRemove the current Android test peer from the worm-os WG instance.\n\nDo NOT remove:\n- wg0 address\n- UDP/51821\n- PF rules\n- private routing\n\nGenerate a NEW OPNsense WireGuard keypair only if necessary to create\na clean known-good identity.\n\nIf regenerated:\n- store private key only in OPNsense persistent configuration\n- never print it\n- output ONLY the new public key\n\n==================================================\n3. CLEAN ANDROID TEST PEER\n==================================================\n\nWe will create a fresh Android WireGuard tunnel manually.\n\nReserve:\n\nCLIENT IP:\n10.60.0.10/32\n\nGenerate a NEW keypair ON THE ANDROID DEVICE.\n\nDo not generate or store the Android private key on worm-robot,\nOPNsense, Codex workspace or Git.\n\nSTOP after server preparation and print:\n\nOPNSENSE_WG_PUBLIC_KEY=<public key>\nENDPOINT=2.28.34.27:51821\nCLIENT_ADDRESS=10.60.0.10/32\nDNS=10.60.0.1\nALLOWED_IPS=10.60.0.0/24,10.90.0.0/16\nKEEPALIVE=25\n\nIMPORTANT:\nUse SPLIT TUNNEL for this recovery test.\n\nDo NOT use 0.0.0.0/0 yet.\n\nThen print:\n\nWAITING FOR NEW ANDROID PUBLIC KEY\n\nDo not continue until the new Android public key is supplied.\n\n==================================================\n4. AFTER ANDROID PUBLIC KEY IS SUPPLIED\n==================================================\n\nCreate exactly one peer:\n\nPublicKey:\n<NEW ANDROID PUBLIC KEY>\n\nAllowedIP:\n10.60.0.10/32\n\nPersist configuration.\n\nVerify:\n- exactly one test peer\n- exactly one AllowedIP\n- wg0 10.60.0.1/24\n- UDP/51821\n\n==================================================\n5. LIVE TEST\n==================================================\n\nStart:\n\ntcpdump WAN UDP/51821\nwg show wg0\n\nPrint:\n\nENABLE NEW ANDROID WIREGUARD TUNNEL NOW\n\nMonitor 90 seconds.\n\nPASS requires:\n\nWAN packets > 0\nlatest handshake RECENT\nRX > 0\nTX > 0\n\n==================================================\n6. ONLY AFTER HANDSHAKE\n==================================================\n\nTest in this exact order:\n\n10.60.0.10 -> 10.60.0.1\n10.60.0.10 -> 10.90.10.1\n10.60.0.10 -> 10.90.20.10\n10.60.0.10 -> 10.90.20.10:22\n\nThen real SSH:\n\nssh <authorized-user>@10.90.20.10\n\nDo not test full-tunnel Internet yet.\n\n==================================================\n7. PASS GATE\n==================================================\n\nPASS server identity consistent\nPASS new Android peer\nPASS UDP/51821\nPASS handshake RECENT\nPASS RX/TX\nPASS OPNsense WG reachable\nPASS OPNsense private reachable\nPASS worm-robot private reachable\nPASS private SSH reachable\nPASS FireHOL remains active\nPASS worm-robot ip_forward=0\nPASS frozen private network unchanged\nPASS persistence\nPASS no secrets\n\nFinal:\n\nPRIVATE WORM FOUNDATION: PASS\n\nor:\n\nPRIVATE WORM FOUNDATION: FAIL\n\nDo not modify OTA/Web/Android system integration."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a078c7-1d4b-7603-ad6b-ab6cf2605cc8","create_time":1788732779.3357832,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a078cf-6f3b-7502-aa3d-11021e5f55ca","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"IMPORTANT NEW LIVE EVIDENCE:\n\nThe Android WireGuard tunnel is currently working for Internet access\nafter changing Android DNS from 10.60.0.1 to 1.1.1.1.\n\nDO NOT reset or regenerate WireGuard keys.\nDO NOT recreate wg0.\nDO NOT recreate the Android peer.\n\nRe-evaluate the previous CLIENT -> WG failure.\n\nWhile Android WireGuard remains ENABLED:\n\n1. Run:\n   wg show wg0\n\nVerify:\n- latest handshake\n- RX\n- TX\n\n2. Verify the Android peer:\n   10.60.0.10/32\n\n3. Verify outbound NAT counters for 10.60.0.0/24.\n\n4. Determine actual client public IPv4.\nExpected:\n2.28.34.27\n\n5. Diagnose ONLY OPNsense DNS for the worm-os WG network.\n\nExpected resolver:\n10.60.0.1\n\nCheck:\n- Unbound listening interfaces\n- 10.60.0.1 UDP/53\n- 10.60.0.1 TCP/53\n- PF rules from 10.60.0.0/24\n- Unbound ACL for 10.60.0.0/24\n- resolver logs\n- DNSSEC/upstream resolution\n\nDo not expose DNS on WAN.\n\n6. If WireGuard handshake is RECENT and RX/TX > 0:\nreclassify CLIENT -> WG as PASS.\n\n7. If public IPv4 is 2.28.34.27:\nreclassify FULL TUNNEL as PASS.\n\n8. Keep 1.1.1.1 only as TEMPORARY diagnostic DNS.\n\nRepair 10.60.0.1 DNS only after identifying the exact failure.\n\nTarget final state:\n\nAndroid:\nAddress = 10.60.0.10/32\nDNS = 10.60.0.1\n\nWireGuard:\nEndpoint = 2.28.34.27:51821\nAllowedIPs = 0.0.0.0/0\n\nExpected:\nHANDSHAKE=RECENT\nRX>0\nTX>0\nPUBLIC_IPV4=2.28.34.27\nDNS_10.60.0.1=PASS\n\nDo not alter frozen private addressing.\nDo not modify FireHOL.\nDo not modify worm-robot networking."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a078cf-6efb-76d2-8316-b62caa101f69","create_time":1788733255.4832513,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a078d5-6139-7423-858f-8bc8b58306fd","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"TEMPORARILY STOP FULL-TUNNEL DEBUGGING.\n\nWe are establishing the PRIVATE WORM FOUNDATION first.\n\nAndroid test client configuration is now:\n\nAddress:\n10.60.0.10/32\n\nAllowedIPs:\n10.60.0.0/24,10.90.0.0/16\n\nDNS:\n1.1.1.1\n\nEndpoint:\n2.28.34.27:51821\n\nDo NOT modify:\n- WireGuard keys\n- public IPs\n- private addressing\n- NAT\n- DNS\n- FireHOL public policy\n\nGoal:\nmake split-tunnel private connectivity work first.\n\nWhile Android WireGuard is ENABLED, verify:\n\n1. wg show wg0\n\nRequired:\nHANDSHAKE=RECENT\nRX>0\nTX>0\n\nIf handshake is not RECENT:\nSTOP.\nDiagnose WireGuard only.\n\nIf handshake passes, test routing in this exact order:\n\nA:\nAndroid -> 10.60.0.1\nExpected PASS.\n\nB:\nAndroid -> 10.90.10.1\nExpected PASS.\n\nC:\nAndroid -> 10.90.20.10\nExpected PASS.\n\nD:\nAndroid -> 10.90.20.10 TCP/22\nExpected PASS.\n\nE:\nReal SSH:\nAndroid -> 10.90.20.10:22\nExpected PASS with existing authorized credentials.\n\nTrace failures using:\nOPNsense PF logs/counters\nrouting tables\npacket captures on wg0/private interface\nworm-robot FireHOL counters\n\nDo not create broad allow rules.\n\nRequired private policy:\n\n10.60.0.0/24 -> 10.90.20.10 TCP/22 ALLOW\n\nReturn traffic:\n10.90.20.10 -> 10.60.0.0/24\nmust have a valid route through OPNsense/private infrastructure.\n\nworm-robot:\nnet.ipv4.ip_forward=0\n\nOPNsense remains the router.\n\nDo not touch full-tunnel NAT until:\n\nPASS handshake\nPASS 10.60.0.1\nPASS 10.90.10.1\nPASS 10.90.20.10\nPASS 10.90.20.10:22\nPASS real private SSH\n\nFinal output:\n\nPRIVATE_WG_HANDSHAKE=\nOPNSENSE_WG=\nOPNSENSE_PRIVATE=\nWORM_ROBOT_PRIVATE=\nWORM_ROBOT_PRIVATE_SSH=\nRETURN_PATH=\nPRIVATE_WORM_FOUNDATION=\n\nDo not start another patch."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a078d5-60fa-7542-bdd5-ace16a98dae5","create_time":1788733645.1131108,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a078d8-52d0-7f00-a587-77cb93574485","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_tex