/root/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T18-02-21-01a07774-da5a-7751-beb8-16e2ba629dff.jsonl:18314:{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T17:12:00.476Z","ordinal":18312,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a08201-54dc-79d2-8772-2e14356ce65a","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"CREATE WORMOS IMPLEMENTATION CHECKPOINT TAG\n\nCurrent verified source state:\n\nSOURCE_STATE_READY=PASS\nBUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN\nBLOCKERS=None\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nThis task is GIT CHECKPOINT ONLY.\n\nDo NOT:\n- build\n- generate OTA\n- modify source implementation\n- add Bitwarden\n- add Proton Drive\n- change WireGuard\n- change Material 3\n- modify server/network infrastructure\n\n============================================================\n1. INSPECT CANONICAL GIT STATE\n============================================================\n\nWork from:\n\n/opt/worm\n\nIdentify the canonical WormOS Git repository and remote.\n\nVerify the remote belongs to the configured git.worm infrastructure.\n\nReport:\n\nGIT_ROOT=\nGIT_REMOTE=\nGIT_BRANCH=\nGIT_HEAD=\nGIT_STATUS=\n\nDo not change the remote.\n\n============================================================\n2. VERIFY CHECKPOINT CONTENT\n============================================================\n\nConfirm the checkpoint contains the recovered persistent state for:\n\n- WormOS base/product\n- Material 3\n- WormOS App Store\n- Proton\n- WormSystemWireGuard\n- official WireGuard Android backend\n- wireguard-go source/build integration\n- backend provenance\n- SELinux source changes\n- fail-closed source/design\n\nBitwarden and Proton Drive are explicitly NOT part of this checkpoint.\n\nDo not add generated build artifacts.\n\nEnsure .gitignore excludes at minimum appropriate generated content under:\n\n/opt/worm/build/\n/opt/worm/cache/\n\nand other disposable Android build outputs.\n\nDo not accidentally ignore persistent source, patches, manifests,\nprovenance or documentation.\n\n============================================================\n3. SECRET SCAN\n============================================================\n\nRun the existing WormOS secret scan over everything that will be committed.\n\nMust remain:\n\nNO_SECRETS=PASS\n\nIf a genuine secret is detected:\n\nSTOP\n\nDo not commit.\nDo not push.\n\n============================================================\n4. CREATE CHECKPOINT COMMIT\n============================================================\n\nStage only the persistent reconstructed project/source state.\n\nCreate a commit with message:\n\nWormOS: recover pre-build WireGuard backend source state\n\nReport:\n\nCHECKPOINT_COMMIT=\n\n============================================================\n5. CREATE ANNOTATED IMPLEMENTATION TAG\n============================================================\n\nCreate exactly:\n\nwormos-prebuild-wg-backend-recovered\n\nas an ANNOTATED Git tag pointing to CHECKPOINT_COMMIT.\n\nTag message:\n\nWormOS pre-build WireGuard backend recovered checkpoint.\n\nRecovered and verified source state:\n- WormOS base/product\n- Material 3\n- WormOS App Store\n- Proton\n- system-owned WormSystemWireGuard\n- official WireGuard Android backend\n- source-built wireguard-go integration\n- pinned backend provenance\n- SELinux source changes\n- fail-closed source/design\n\nBitwarden and Proton Drive are not part of this checkpoint.\nBuild not run.\nOTA not generated.\nRuntime tests not performed.\n\nVerify:\n\ngit rev-parse wormos-prebuild-wg-backend-recovered^{commit}\n\nmust equal CHECKPOINT_COMMIT.\n\n============================================================\n6. PUSH CHECKPOINT\n============================================================\n\nPush the checkpoint commit using the existing safe WormOS branch strategy.\n\nPush the tag:\n\nwormos-prebuild-wg-backend-recovered\n\nDo NOT force push.\n\nDo NOT move/replace an existing tag.\n\nIf that tag already exists remotely, compare its target first.\n\nIf it already points to the exact checkpoint:\nTAG_PUSH=ALREADY_PRESENT_VALID\n\nIf it points somewhere else:\nSTOP\nTAG_CONFLICT=YES\n\nNever overwrite it.\n\n============================================================\n7. ESTABLISH PER-IMPLEMENTATION TAG POLICY\n============================================================\n\nCreate/update:\n\n/opt/worm/docs/GIT-TAG-POLICY.md\n\nPolicy:\n\nEvery accepted WormOS implementation gets its own immutable annotated tag.\n\nFormat:\n\nwormos-<implementation>\n\nor, where state matters:\n\nwormos-<implementation>-<state>\n\nExamples:\n\nwormos-base-product\nwormos-material3\nwormos-appstore\nwormos-appstore-bitwarden\nwormos-appstore-proton-drive\nwormos-system-wg\nwormos-wg-backend\nwormos-wg-failclosed\nwormos-prebuild-wg-backend-recovered\n\nRules:\n\n- annotated tags only\n- one accepted implementation/checkpoint per tag\n- never move an existing published tag\n- never force-update a tag\n- secret scan before tagging\n- tag exact verified commit\n- build status documented separately from source status\n\nDo NOT create the example tags retroactively in this task.\n\nOnly create:\n\nwormos-prebuild-wg-backend-recovered\n\n============================================================\nFINAL REPORT\n============================================================\n\nGIT_ROOT=\nGIT_REMOTE=\nGIT_BRANCH=\nCHECKPOINT_COMMIT=\n\nNO_SECRETS=\n\nIMPLEMENTATION_TAG=wormos-prebuild-wg-backend-recovered\nTAG_TYPE=\nTAG_TARGET=\nTAG_VERIFIED=\nTAG_PUSH=\nTAG_CONFLICT=\n\nDEFAULT_BRANCH_CHANGED=\nTAG_POLICY_CREATED=\n\nBUILD=NOT_RUN\nOTA=NOT_RUN\nSOURCE_STATE_READY=PASS"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08201-54b6-7c92-8529-5b089e87e8d9","create_time":1788887520.4763577,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}}}
